u do not have to wait until you have perfectly analyzed the root cause. If you find an intervention that works, that restores your function, use it. The explanation can come later, or maybe it never comes at all. But survival and restoration are not gated by your ability to explain the machinery. It is an incredibly liberating realization. It frees you to act in a complex world without being paralyzed by a lack of total information. Okay, let's take a major step back and look at this massive journey we just went on. We covered an immense amount of ground, from physics, to biology, to AI. We really did. We started by looking at the geometry of systems, and we learned that boundaries aren't just passive walls where things geometrically stop. Boundaries are active computational objects. They are statistical screens forcing a system to minimize surprise. They are biological memory layers actively pursuing a target shape. And there are topological deletions that permanently refuse certain futures by zeroing them out of existence. And importantly, we established that those are distinctly different mechanisms that can actually mathematically conflict with one another if you force them together. Right. Then we moved into the brevity trap. We learned that the shortness of a description, or the compression of a neural network, absolutely does not guarantee deeper understanding. Because of superposed, tangled representations, a perfectly compressed model might have lost its ability to distinguish nuance entirely. We cannot use compression as a continuous proxy for understanding. Sometimes, shortness just means you are relying on a massive, hidden library of past work. And in complex environments, you actually have to widen the curriculum and deliberately increase entropy to keep learning. You cannot compress your way to genius. And finally, we looked at survival. We saw that functional restoration, getting a complex system to work again, is entirely logically decoupled from architectural transparency, being able to explain exactly how it works. From tweaking transformer layers to legacy code to kidney transplants, we constantly fix things without fully understanding the underlying mechanisms. Restoration before explanation. It is a complete inversion of how we are taught to approach problem solving. It is. So we always like to leave you with a final thought, something to mull over on your own time. And building on these three papers and this idea of restoration without explanation, I have a massive, provocative question for you. What is the question? Well, if boundaries actively dictate what a system can become through refusal, by permanently deleting options, and if a system can be perfectly repaired and restored without anyone understanding how it works, does that mean the most resilient systems of the future will be the ones that are deliberately designed to be unexplainable? That is a deeply provocative thought. Think about it. Look at our current trajectory with AI and even societal structures. We are obsessed with algorithmic transparency. We want to be able to open the black box and see exactly why the AI made a decision. But if true resilience, true functional adequacy comes from the ability to quickly restore function without the heavy, slow burden of architectural transparency, maybe our current obsession with making every AI completely explainable is exactly what will make those systems fragile. It is a valid fear. If you legally or architecturally force a system to maintain an explicit, inspectable explanation for everything it does, you are forcing it to use a very specific, rigid ontology. You might be severely limiting its ability to utilize those complex, distributed, superposed representations that actually allow it to adapt, learn, and restore itself quickly in a chaotic environment. Exactly. We might be building a glass jaw into our most advanced artificial intelligence or our most advanced bureaucracies just to satisfy our own psychological need for a neat, compressed explanation. We are forcing a coding deficit requirement onto a system that just needs to maximize its distinguishability. Something for you to mull over. It certainly recontextualizes our deep-seated need for control. We want the clean narrative, even if it makes the system weaker. It does. It goes right back to the beginning. We want the clean, jagged white line on the x-ray. We want to point at the broken bone and say, there it is. That is the exploration. But the reality of complex systems is muddy waters. It is active boundaries, tangled representations, and blind restoration. And maybe, just maybe, those muddy waters are exactly where the resilience lives. The muddy waters are where the system survives. Thank you so much for joining us on this deep dive. Keep questioning the boundaries, keep embracing the complexity, and keep exploring. See you next time. We'll see you next time.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 8.0, "text": " Imagine, it's 1954, you are standing in an operating room at the Peter Bent Brigham Hospital in Boston.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 11, 309, 311, 46590, 11, 291, 366, 4877, 294, 364, 7447, 1808, 412, 264, 6508, 28894, 1603, 910, 335, 15645, 294, 12333, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1360351528440203, "compression_ratio": 1.5084175084175084, "no_speech_prob": 1.129030896551697e-12}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 8.3, "end": 8.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50780, 1779, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1360351528440203, "compression_ratio": 1.5084175084175084, "no_speech_prob": 1.129030896551697e-12}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 8.96, "end": 16.72, "text": " And a surgeon named Dr. Joseph Murray is about to attempt something that honestly sounds like absolute science fiction for the era.", "tokens": [50813, 400, 257, 22913, 4926, 2491, 13, 11170, 27291, 307, 466, 281, 5217, 746, 300, 6095, 3263, 411, 8236, 3497, 13266, 337, 264, 4249, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1360351528440203, "compression_ratio": 1.5084175084175084, "no_speech_prob": 1.129030896551697e-12}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 16.84, "end": 17.6, "text": " Oh, completely.", "tokens": [51207, 876, 11, 2584, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1360351528440203, "compression_ratio": 1.5084175084175084, "no_speech_prob": 1.129030896551697e-12}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 17.88, "end": 26.3, "text": " He's taking a healthy kidney from one man and, you know, sewing it into the body of his identical twin who is actively dying of renal failure.", "tokens": [51259, 634, 311, 1940, 257, 4627, 19000, 490, 472, 587, 293, 11, 291, 458, 11, 19311, 309, 666, 264, 1772, 295, 702, 14800, 18397, 567, 307, 13022, 8639, 295, 319, 4660, 7763, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1360351528440203, "compression_ratio": 1.5084175084175084, "no_speech_prob": 1.129030896551697e-12}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 26.42, "end": 26.68, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51686, 865, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1360351528440203, "compression_ratio": 1.5084175084175084, "no_speech_prob": 1.129030896551697e-12}, {"id": 6, "seek": 0, "start": 26.68, "end": 28.98, "text": " And the surgery is this massive success.", "tokens": [51699, 400, 264, 7930, 307, 341, 5994, 2245, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1360351528440203, "compression_ratio": 1.5084175084175084, "no_speech_prob": 1.129030896551697e-12}, {"id": 7, "seek": 2898, "start": 28.98, "end": 31.44, "text": " The patient actually lives for eight more years.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4537, 767, 2909, 337, 3180, 544, 924, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09981757138682677, "compression_ratio": 1.609271523178808, "no_speech_prob": 8.037742021439753e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2898, "start": 31.78, "end": 36.02, "text": " But here is the catch, the part that should make your brain just freeze for a second.", "tokens": [50505, 583, 510, 307, 264, 3745, 11, 264, 644, 300, 820, 652, 428, 3567, 445, 15959, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09981757138682677, "compression_ratio": 1.609271523178808, "no_speech_prob": 8.037742021439753e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2898, "start": 36.06, "end": 37.18, "text": " This is the crazy part.", "tokens": [50719, 639, 307, 264, 3219, 644, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09981757138682677, "compression_ratio": 1.609271523178808, "no_speech_prob": 8.037742021439753e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2898, "start": 37.44, "end": 37.620000000000005, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50788, 1779, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09981757138682677, "compression_ratio": 1.609271523178808, "no_speech_prob": 8.037742021439753e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2898, "start": 37.96, "end": 53.260000000000005, "text": " Because in 1954, medical science did not actually understand the human immune system, the human leukocyte antigen system, like the actual mechanism that dictates whether a body will accept or reject a foreign organ that wouldn't even be discovered until four years later in 1958.", "tokens": [50814, 1436, 294, 46590, 11, 4625, 3497, 630, 406, 767, 1223, 264, 1952, 11992, 1185, 11, 264, 1952, 32665, 31078, 975, 2511, 3213, 1185, 11, 411, 264, 3539, 7513, 300, 12569, 1024, 1968, 257, 1772, 486, 3241, 420, 8248, 257, 5329, 1798, 300, 2759, 380, 754, 312, 6941, 1826, 1451, 924, 1780, 294, 45868, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09981757138682677, "compression_ratio": 1.609271523178808, "no_speech_prob": 8.037742021439753e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 2898, "start": 53.5, "end": 55.480000000000004, "text": " It's just a remarkable piece of history.", "tokens": [51591, 467, 311, 445, 257, 12802, 2522, 295, 2503, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09981757138682677, "compression_ratio": 1.609271523178808, "no_speech_prob": 8.037742021439753e-13}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5548, "start": 55.48, "end": 64.52, "text": " I mean, they intervened in this incredibly complex system and perfectly restored its function years before they could explicitly explain the biological architecture they were, you know, manipulating.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 436, 17104, 292, 294, 341, 6252, 3997, 1185, 293, 6239, 23143, 1080, 2445, 924, 949, 436, 727, 20803, 2903, 264, 13910, 9482, 436, 645, 11, 291, 458, 11, 40805, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.155705510834117, "compression_ratio": 1.5316455696202531, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048065011609823e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5548, "start": 64.94, "end": 65.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50838, 7587, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.155705510834117, "compression_ratio": 1.5316455696202531, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048065011609823e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5548, "start": 65.62, "end": 68.16, "text": " They fixed a system they didn't fundamentally understand.", "tokens": [50872, 814, 6806, 257, 1185, 436, 994, 380, 17879, 1223, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.155705510834117, "compression_ratio": 1.5316455696202531, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048065011609823e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 5548, "start": 69.0, "end": 73.08, "text": " And that paradox right there is the core of our deep dive today.", "tokens": [51041, 400, 300, 26221, 558, 456, 307, 264, 4965, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 965, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.155705510834117, "compression_ratio": 1.5316455696202531, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048065011609823e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 5548, "start": 73.16, "end": 73.36, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51249, 865, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.155705510834117, "compression_ratio": 1.5316455696202531, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048065011609823e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 5548, "start": 73.44, "end": 74.69999999999999, "text": " It really sets the stage.", "tokens": [51263, 467, 534, 6352, 264, 3233, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.155705510834117, "compression_ratio": 1.5316455696202531, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048065011609823e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 7470, "start": 74.7, "end": 80.18, "text": " Because if you look around, you realize we live in a culture that absolutely demands explanation.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 291, 574, 926, 11, 291, 4325, 321, 1621, 294, 257, 3713, 300, 3122, 15107, 10835, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10779316497571541, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837675359202773e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 7470, "start": 80.44, "end": 80.74000000000001, "text": " Always.", "tokens": [50652, 11270, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10779316497571541, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837675359202773e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 7470, "start": 81.16, "end": 92.62, "text": " We assume that because our technology is so advanced, because we map the genome, because we build these massive artificial neural networks, we must have a firm grip on the foundational rules of reality.", "tokens": [50688, 492, 6552, 300, 570, 527, 2899, 307, 370, 7339, 11, 570, 321, 4471, 264, 21953, 11, 570, 321, 1322, 613, 5994, 11677, 18161, 9590, 11, 321, 1633, 362, 257, 6174, 12007, 322, 264, 32195, 4474, 295, 4103, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10779316497571541, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837675359202773e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 9262, "start": 92.62, "end": 93.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16025345746208638, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607642352670869e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 9262, "start": 93.14, "end": 94.22, "text": " We think we have the blueprint.", "tokens": [50391, 492, 519, 321, 362, 264, 35868, 13, 50445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16025345746208638, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607642352670869e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 9262, "start": 94.7, "end": 95.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50469, 7587, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16025345746208638, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607642352670869e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 9262, "start": 95.46000000000001, "end": 105.80000000000001, "text": " We think that to control something, to fix it, or even to know what it is, we have to possess a perfect, compressed, explainable blueprint of its internals.", "tokens": [50507, 492, 519, 300, 281, 1969, 746, 11, 281, 3191, 309, 11, 420, 754, 281, 458, 437, 309, 307, 11, 321, 362, 281, 17490, 257, 2176, 11, 30353, 11, 2903, 712, 35868, 295, 1080, 2154, 1124, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16025345746208638, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607642352670869e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 9262, "start": 106.0, "end": 108.04, "text": " Which is an incredibly comforting illusion.", "tokens": [51034, 3013, 307, 364, 6252, 38439, 18854, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16025345746208638, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607642352670869e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 9262, "start": 108.34, "end": 111.38000000000001, "text": " I mean, it gives us a sense of mastery over the chaos of the world.", "tokens": [51151, 286, 914, 11, 309, 2709, 505, 257, 2020, 295, 37951, 670, 264, 14158, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16025345746208638, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607642352670869e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 11138, "start": 111.38, "end": 115.58, "text": " We believe that explanation is the strict prerequisite for survival.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1697, 300, 10835, 307, 264, 10910, 38333, 34152, 337, 12559, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12598151019495776, "compression_ratio": 1.7177914110429449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783439229726358e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 11138, "start": 115.86, "end": 130.84, "text": " But when you start pulling at the threads of how complex systems actually operate, I mean, from single biological cells all the way up to trillion parameter AI models, you discover that our obsession with explicit explanation is often exactly what blinds us to how the world truly works.", "tokens": [50589, 583, 562, 291, 722, 8407, 412, 264, 19314, 295, 577, 3997, 3652, 767, 9651, 11, 286, 914, 11, 490, 2167, 13910, 5438, 439, 264, 636, 493, 281, 18723, 13075, 7318, 5245, 11, 291, 4411, 300, 527, 30521, 365, 13691, 10835, 307, 2049, 2293, 437, 6865, 82, 505, 281, 577, 264, 1002, 4908, 1985, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12598151019495776, "compression_ratio": 1.7177914110429449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783439229726358e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 11138, "start": 131.32, "end": 135.07999999999998, "text": " And that realization is just, it's like the ground falling out from under you.", "tokens": [51362, 400, 300, 25138, 307, 445, 11, 309, 311, 411, 264, 2727, 7440, 484, 490, 833, 291, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12598151019495776, "compression_ratio": 1.7177914110429449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783439229726358e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 11138, "start": 135.14, "end": 140.32, "text": " When you realize the rules you thought governed the system are actually just the comforting stories you told yourself.", "tokens": [51553, 1133, 291, 4325, 264, 4474, 291, 1194, 35529, 264, 1185, 366, 767, 445, 264, 38439, 3676, 291, 1907, 1803, 13, 51812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12598151019495776, "compression_ratio": 1.7177914110429449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783439229726358e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 11138, "start": 140.32, "end": 140.72, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51812, 865, 13, 51832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12598151019495776, "compression_ratio": 1.7177914110429449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783439229726358e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 14072, "start": 140.72, "end": 141.78, "text": " Yeah, precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 13402, 13, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13832744994720855, "compression_ratio": 1.5571428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736815062866727e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 14072, "start": 142.16, "end": 143.9, "text": " So, welcome to the Deep Dive.", "tokens": [50437, 407, 11, 2928, 281, 264, 14895, 413, 488, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13832744994720855, "compression_ratio": 1.5571428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736815062866727e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 14072, "start": 144.16, "end": 151.0, "text": " Today, we are taking you on a mission to completely rewire how you think about complex systems.", "tokens": [50537, 2692, 11, 321, 366, 1940, 291, 322, 257, 4447, 281, 2584, 319, 42689, 577, 291, 519, 466, 3997, 3652, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13832744994720855, "compression_ratio": 1.5571428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736815062866727e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 14072, "start": 151.44, "end": 163.28, "text": " We are going to explore how systems define themselves, how we mistakenly measure their understanding, and why we can successfully fix them without actually having a clue how they work.", "tokens": [50901, 492, 366, 516, 281, 6839, 577, 3652, 6964, 2969, 11, 577, 321, 21333, 356, 3481, 641, 3701, 11, 293, 983, 321, 393, 10727, 3191, 552, 1553, 767, 1419, 257, 13602, 577, 436, 589, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13832744994720855, "compression_ratio": 1.5571428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736815062866727e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 16328, "start": 163.28, "end": 171.42000000000002, "text": " It is a profound shift in perspective, and one that requires us to look at three very specific, very disruptive pieces of research.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 5513, 294, 4585, 11, 293, 472, 300, 7029, 505, 281, 574, 412, 1045, 588, 2685, 11, 588, 37865, 3755, 295, 2132, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417893868905525, "compression_ratio": 1.4848484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251357034923307e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 16328, "start": 171.46, "end": 172.44, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [50774, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417893868905525, "compression_ratio": 1.4848484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251357034923307e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 16328, "start": 172.82, "end": 177.72, "text": " I've been buried in our source material for the last week, and I'm not going to lie, it is incredibly dense.", "tokens": [50842, 286, 600, 668, 14101, 294, 527, 4009, 2527, 337, 264, 1036, 1243, 11, 293, 286, 478, 406, 516, 281, 4544, 11, 309, 307, 6252, 18011, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417893868905525, "compression_ratio": 1.4848484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251357034923307e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 16328, "start": 177.8, "end": 178.22, "text": " Oh, it is.", "tokens": [51091, 876, 11, 309, 307, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417893868905525, "compression_ratio": 1.4848484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251357034923307e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 16328, "start": 178.3, "end": 178.96, "text": " It's heavy stuff.", "tokens": [51116, 467, 311, 4676, 1507, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417893868905525, "compression_ratio": 1.4848484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251357034923307e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 17896, "start": 178.96, "end": 185.64000000000001, "text": " We're looking at three groundbreaking papers, all published in July of 2026 by an author named Flixion.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 434, 1237, 412, 1045, 42491, 10577, 11, 439, 6572, 294, 7370, 295, 945, 10880, 538, 364, 3793, 4926, 3235, 970, 313, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16339492797851562, "compression_ratio": 1.331360946745562, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346922509542395e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 17896, "start": 186.34, "end": 191.08, "text": " And the titles alone, I mean, they sound like they belong in completely different university departments.", "tokens": [50734, 400, 264, 12992, 3312, 11, 286, 914, 11, 436, 1626, 411, 436, 5784, 294, 2584, 819, 5454, 15326, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16339492797851562, "compression_ratio": 1.331360946745562, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346922509542395e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 17896, "start": 191.28, "end": 191.66, "text": " They really do.", "tokens": [50981, 814, 534, 360, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16339492797851562, "compression_ratio": 1.331360946745562, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346922509542395e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 19166, "start": 191.66, "end": 196.44, "text": " We have boundaries or computational objects, which sounds like physics or biology.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 13180, 420, 28270, 6565, 11, 597, 3263, 411, 10649, 420, 14956, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135040650000939, "compression_ratio": 1.3984962406015038, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773449611745314e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 19166, "start": 196.84, "end": 202.06, "text": " Then we have the compression fallacy, which is straight out of computer science and information theory.", "tokens": [50624, 1396, 321, 362, 264, 19355, 2100, 2551, 11, 597, 307, 2997, 484, 295, 3820, 3497, 293, 1589, 5261, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135040650000939, "compression_ratio": 1.3984962406015038, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773449611745314e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 20206, "start": 202.06, "end": 210.46, "text": " And finally, we have restoration before explanation, which is this wild mix of engineering, clinical medicine, and artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 362, 23722, 949, 10835, 11, 597, 307, 341, 4868, 2890, 295, 7043, 11, 9115, 7195, 11, 293, 11677, 7599, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11514742885317121, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556549967822187e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 20206, "start": 210.58, "end": 214.52, "text": " And if you merely skimmed the abstracts, you would absolutely assume these were isolated arguments.", "tokens": [50791, 400, 498, 291, 17003, 1110, 332, 1912, 264, 12649, 82, 11, 291, 576, 3122, 6552, 613, 645, 14621, 12869, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11514742885317121, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556549967822187e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 20206, "start": 215.18, "end": 219.08, "text": " But Flixion has essentially built a Trojan horse here.", "tokens": [51021, 583, 3235, 970, 313, 575, 4476, 3094, 257, 19406, 14763, 6832, 510, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11514742885317121, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556549967822187e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 20206, "start": 219.2, "end": 220.04, "text": " Trojan horse.", "tokens": [51222, 19406, 14763, 6832, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11514742885317121, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556549967822187e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 20206, "start": 220.14000000000001, "end": 223.86, "text": " Yeah, because when you synthesize them, they are not three separate papers.", "tokens": [51269, 865, 11, 570, 562, 291, 26617, 1125, 552, 11, 436, 366, 406, 1045, 4994, 10577, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11514742885317121, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556549967822187e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 20206, "start": 224.1, "end": 229.16, "text": " They actually form a single, unified critique of our fundamental assumptions about reality.", "tokens": [51467, 814, 767, 1254, 257, 2167, 11, 26787, 25673, 295, 527, 8088, 17695, 466, 4103, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11514742885317121, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556549967822187e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 20206, "start": 229.32, "end": 229.74, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51728, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11514742885317121, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556549967822187e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 22974, "start": 229.74, "end": 239.16, "text": " They tell one massive, mind-bending story about the geometry of a system, the traps of measuring its intelligence, and the architecture of its survival.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 980, 472, 5994, 11, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 1657, 466, 264, 18426, 295, 257, 1185, 11, 264, 24173, 295, 13389, 1080, 7599, 11, 293, 264, 9482, 295, 1080, 12559, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588983504498592, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555029916376363e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 22974, "start": 239.5, "end": 244.54000000000002, "text": " And I am so incredibly excited to share this with you, because once you see this framework, you just cannot unsee it.", "tokens": [50853, 400, 286, 669, 370, 6252, 2919, 281, 2073, 341, 365, 291, 11, 570, 1564, 291, 536, 341, 8388, 11, 291, 445, 2644, 517, 17109, 309, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588983504498592, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555029916376363e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 22974, "start": 244.9, "end": 247.68, "text": " So our mission today is to walk you through this narrative.", "tokens": [51123, 407, 527, 4447, 965, 307, 281, 1792, 291, 807, 341, 9977, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588983504498592, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555029916376363e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 22974, "start": 248.02, "end": 249.18, "text": " We have a lot of ground to cover.", "tokens": [51279, 492, 362, 257, 688, 295, 2727, 281, 2060, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588983504498592, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555029916376363e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 22974, "start": 249.48000000000002, "end": 252.58, "text": " We should probably start where any system starts, with its geometry.", "tokens": [51352, 492, 820, 1391, 722, 689, 604, 1185, 3719, 11, 365, 1080, 18426, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588983504498592, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555029916376363e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 22974, "start": 253.02, "end": 253.28, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51529, 1779, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588983504498592, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555029916376363e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 22974, "start": 253.9, "end": 258.76, "text": " Part one, the geometry of boundaries, from fences to computers.", "tokens": [51573, 4100, 472, 11, 264, 18426, 295, 13180, 11, 490, 45796, 281, 10807, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588983504498592, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555029916376363e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 25876, "start": 258.76, "end": 266.0, "text": " Because before we can even talk about how a system learns or how it breaks or how we might go about fixing it, we have to know where the system begins and ends.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 949, 321, 393, 754, 751, 466, 577, 257, 1185, 27152, 420, 577, 309, 9857, 420, 577, 321, 1062, 352, 466, 19442, 309, 11, 321, 362, 281, 458, 689, 264, 1185, 7338, 293, 5314, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 25876, "start": 266.21999999999997, "end": 266.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50738, 1779, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 25876, "start": 266.59999999999997, "end": 268.9, "text": " Like what is inside the system and what is outside.", "tokens": [50757, 1743, 437, 307, 1854, 264, 1185, 293, 437, 307, 2380, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 25876, "start": 269.08, "end": 270.38, "text": " You have to draw a line somewhere.", "tokens": [50881, 509, 362, 281, 2642, 257, 1622, 4079, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 25876, "start": 270.74, "end": 270.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50964, 1079, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 25876, "start": 271.09999999999997, "end": 276.34, "text": " And the everyday assumption we all make about boundaries is that they are just passive geometric facts.", "tokens": [50982, 400, 264, 7429, 15302, 321, 439, 652, 466, 13180, 307, 300, 436, 366, 445, 14975, 33246, 9130, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 25876, "start": 276.74, "end": 278.24, "text": " Think about the physical world.", "tokens": [51264, 6557, 466, 264, 4001, 1002, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 25876, "start": 278.74, "end": 279.82, "text": " A fence around a yard.", "tokens": [51364, 316, 15422, 926, 257, 11682, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 25876, "start": 280.4, "end": 281.52, "text": " The walls of your house.", "tokens": [51447, 440, 7920, 295, 428, 1782, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 25876, "start": 281.96, "end": 282.92, "text": " The skin on your arm.", "tokens": [51525, 440, 3178, 322, 428, 3726, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1600923381867956, "compression_ratio": 1.697080291970803, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790965118678055e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 28292, "start": 282.92, "end": 286.38, "text": " We intuitively treat these as inert geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 46506, 2387, 613, 382, 25832, 18426, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 28292, "start": 287.2, "end": 291.68, "text": " They are simply the physical coordinates where one thing stops and another thing begins.", "tokens": [50579, 814, 366, 2935, 264, 4001, 21056, 689, 472, 551, 10094, 293, 1071, 551, 7338, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 28292, "start": 291.88, "end": 294.66, "text": " That is the common spatial intuition.", "tokens": [50813, 663, 307, 264, 2689, 23598, 24002, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 28292, "start": 295.06, "end": 296.54, "text": " The boundary is just a marker.", "tokens": [50972, 440, 12866, 307, 445, 257, 15247, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 28292, "start": 296.72, "end": 297.70000000000005, "text": " It doesn't actually do anything.", "tokens": [51055, 467, 1177, 380, 767, 360, 1340, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 28292, "start": 297.8, "end": 298.42, "text": " It just is.", "tokens": [51109, 467, 445, 307, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 28292, "start": 298.48, "end": 299.52000000000004, "text": " It's a spatial container.", "tokens": [51143, 467, 311, 257, 23598, 10129, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 28292, "start": 299.92, "end": 300.02000000000004, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51215, 1779, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22225315506393845, "compression_ratio": 1.518918918918919, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827560174626944e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 30002, "start": 300.02, "end": 307.02, "text": " But Fliction's first paper brings to light a paradigm shift happening across three completely independent research fields.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 4105, 311, 700, 3035, 5607, 281, 1442, 257, 24709, 5513, 2737, 2108, 1045, 2584, 6695, 2132, 7909, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15673823654651642, "compression_ratio": 1.5169082125603865, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893505687566202e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 30002, "start": 307.97999999999996, "end": 314.2, "text": " Physicists, biologists, and computer scientists are all independently discovering that boundaries are not passive containers.", "tokens": [50763, 15542, 299, 1751, 11, 3228, 12256, 11, 293, 3820, 7708, 366, 439, 21761, 24773, 300, 13180, 366, 406, 14975, 17089, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15673823654651642, "compression_ratio": 1.5169082125603865, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893505687566202e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 30002, "start": 314.56, "end": 317.14, "text": " They are active computational objects.", "tokens": [51092, 814, 366, 4967, 28270, 6565, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15673823654651642, "compression_ratio": 1.5169082125603865, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893505687566202e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 30002, "start": 317.26, "end": 318.0, "text": " Wait, what does that mean?", "tokens": [51227, 3802, 11, 437, 775, 300, 914, 30, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15673823654651642, "compression_ratio": 1.5169082125603865, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893505687566202e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 31800, "start": 318.0, "end": 323.52, "text": " It means they're actually doing mechanical work to determine what the system is permitted to become.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1355, 436, 434, 767, 884, 12070, 589, 281, 6997, 437, 264, 1185, 307, 28658, 281, 1813, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14917600722539992, "compression_ratio": 1.634453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.875918474378291e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 31800, "start": 323.92, "end": 325.2, "text": " A boundary that computes.", "tokens": [50661, 316, 12866, 300, 715, 1819, 13, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14917600722539992, "compression_ratio": 1.634453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.875918474378291e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 31800, "start": 325.64, "end": 331.42, "text": " It is such a wild concept because it immediately implies that the edge of a thing is like making decisions.", "tokens": [50747, 467, 307, 1270, 257, 4868, 3410, 570, 309, 4258, 18779, 300, 264, 4691, 295, 257, 551, 307, 411, 1455, 5327, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14917600722539992, "compression_ratio": 1.634453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.875918474378291e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 31800, "start": 331.56, "end": 332.24, "text": " Yes, exactly.", "tokens": [51043, 1079, 11, 2293, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14917600722539992, "compression_ratio": 1.634453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.875918474378291e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 31800, "start": 332.24, "end": 341.28, "text": " And the paper breaks this down into three distinct mechanisms, three completely different ways that a boundary does this computational work.", "tokens": [51077, 400, 264, 3035, 9857, 341, 760, 666, 1045, 10644, 15902, 11, 1045, 2584, 819, 2098, 300, 257, 12866, 775, 341, 28270, 589, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14917600722539992, "compression_ratio": 1.634453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.875918474378291e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 34128, "start": 341.28, "end": 349.61999999999995, "text": " So, let's start with the first one, which comes from the free energy principle formulated by the neuroscientist and theoretical biologist Carl Fristen.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 718, 311, 722, 365, 264, 700, 472, 11, 597, 1487, 490, 264, 1737, 2281, 8665, 48936, 538, 264, 28813, 5412, 468, 293, 20864, 3228, 9201, 14256, 1526, 4821, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 34128, "start": 349.78, "end": 350.09999999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50790, 1779, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 34128, "start": 350.32, "end": 352.53999999999996, "text": " He calls his boundary a Markov blanket.", "tokens": [50817, 634, 5498, 702, 12866, 257, 3934, 5179, 17907, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 34128, "start": 353.55999999999995, "end": 358.38, "text": " Now, when I first read this, I got completely lost in the Bayesian map, so I need you to help me anchor this.", "tokens": [50979, 823, 11, 562, 286, 700, 1401, 341, 11, 286, 658, 2584, 2731, 294, 264, 7840, 42434, 4471, 11, 370, 286, 643, 291, 281, 854, 385, 18487, 341, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 34128, "start": 358.5, "end": 359.41999999999996, "text": " I can certainly do that.", "tokens": [51226, 286, 393, 3297, 360, 300, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 34128, "start": 359.76, "end": 366.71999999999997, "text": " Fristen's framework requires you to completely abandon the idea of a boundary as a physical membrane or a spatial distance.", "tokens": [51289, 1526, 4821, 311, 8388, 7029, 291, 281, 2584, 9072, 264, 1558, 295, 257, 12866, 382, 257, 4001, 19651, 420, 257, 23598, 4560, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 34128, "start": 366.84, "end": 368.53999999999996, "text": " Okay, abandoning the fence idea.", "tokens": [51643, 1033, 11, 9072, 278, 264, 15422, 1558, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 34128, "start": 368.67999999999995, "end": 368.91999999999996, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51735, 1779, 13, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1512126321867695, "compression_ratio": 1.6456953642384107, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614331659238867e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 36892, "start": 368.92, "end": 372.36, "text": " In his math, you define a boundary purely statistically.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 702, 5221, 11, 291, 6964, 257, 12866, 17491, 36478, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 36892, "start": 372.90000000000003, "end": 374.34000000000003, "text": " It is a statistical screen.", "tokens": [50564, 467, 307, 257, 22820, 2568, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 36892, "start": 374.5, "end": 375.90000000000003, "text": " Okay, a statistical screen.", "tokens": [50644, 1033, 11, 257, 22820, 2568, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 36892, "start": 376.08000000000004, "end": 377.2, "text": " What are we screening exactly?", "tokens": [50723, 708, 366, 321, 17732, 2293, 30, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 36892, "start": 377.6, "end": 379.82, "text": " We are screening causal influences.", "tokens": [50799, 492, 366, 17732, 38755, 21222, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 36892, "start": 380.66, "end": 384.02000000000004, "text": " Think about it in terms of a network of interacting variables.", "tokens": [50952, 6557, 466, 309, 294, 2115, 295, 257, 3209, 295, 18017, 9102, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 36892, "start": 384.46000000000004, "end": 391.68, "text": " A Markov blanket partitions a system into internal states, external states, and the blanket states themselves.", "tokens": [51142, 316, 3934, 5179, 17907, 644, 2451, 257, 1185, 666, 6920, 4368, 11, 8320, 4368, 11, 293, 264, 17907, 4368, 2969, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 36892, "start": 391.86, "end": 392.20000000000005, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51512, 5803, 309, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 36892, "start": 392.34000000000003, "end": 397.04, "text": " And those blanket states are further divided into sensory states and active states.", "tokens": [51536, 400, 729, 17907, 4368, 366, 3052, 6666, 666, 27233, 4368, 293, 4967, 4368, 13, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17425061180478052, "compression_ratio": 1.8089430894308942, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609783651961528e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 39704, "start": 397.04, "end": 402.90000000000003, "text": " Okay, so I have my inside, my outside, and this blanket made of sensors and actors wrapped around the middle.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 286, 362, 452, 1854, 11, 452, 2380, 11, 293, 341, 17907, 1027, 295, 14840, 293, 10037, 14226, 926, 264, 2808, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15203800201416015, "compression_ratio": 1.5175879396984924, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832380336628591e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 39704, "start": 403.16, "end": 403.54, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [50671, 12753, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15203800201416015, "compression_ratio": 1.5175879396984924, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832380336628591e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 39704, "start": 404.06, "end": 406.26000000000005, "text": " But here is the crucial mechanical feature.", "tokens": [50716, 583, 510, 307, 264, 11462, 12070, 4111, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15203800201416015, "compression_ratio": 1.5175879396984924, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832380336628591e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 39704, "start": 406.98, "end": 410.84000000000003, "text": " The defining property of this blanket isn't what it physically blocks.", "tokens": [50862, 440, 17827, 4707, 295, 341, 17907, 1943, 380, 437, 309, 9762, 8474, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15203800201416015, "compression_ratio": 1.5175879396984924, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832380336628591e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 39704, "start": 411.02000000000004, "end": 414.44, "text": " It is defined by a mathematical absence of causal edges.", "tokens": [51064, 467, 307, 7642, 538, 257, 18894, 17145, 295, 38755, 8819, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15203800201416015, "compression_ratio": 1.5175879396984924, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832380336628591e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 39704, "start": 414.70000000000005, "end": 415.12, "text": " An absence.", "tokens": [51248, 1107, 17145, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15203800201416015, "compression_ratio": 1.5175879396984924, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832380336628591e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 41512, "start": 415.12, "end": 415.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16635877945843866, "compression_ratio": 1.710382513661202, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266180467861767e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 41512, "start": 415.5, "end": 423.82, "text": " Under this structure, the internal states do not directly cause the sensory states, and the external states do not directly cause the active states.", "tokens": [50384, 6974, 341, 3877, 11, 264, 6920, 4368, 360, 406, 3838, 3082, 264, 27233, 4368, 11, 293, 264, 8320, 4368, 360, 406, 3838, 3082, 264, 4967, 4368, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16635877945843866, "compression_ratio": 1.710382513661202, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266180467861767e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 41512, "start": 423.94, "end": 425.62, "text": " So they are severed from each other directly.", "tokens": [50806, 407, 436, 366, 2802, 292, 490, 1184, 661, 3838, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16635877945843866, "compression_ratio": 1.710382513661202, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266180467861767e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 41512, "start": 425.68, "end": 426.12, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50893, 7587, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16635877945843866, "compression_ratio": 1.710382513661202, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266180467861767e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 41512, "start": 426.62, "end": 432.2, "text": " This specific pattern of missing connections induces what statisticians call conditional independence.", "tokens": [50940, 639, 2685, 5102, 295, 5361, 9271, 13716, 887, 437, 29588, 2567, 818, 27708, 14640, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16635877945843866, "compression_ratio": 1.710382513661202, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266180467861767e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 43220, "start": 432.2, "end": 432.64, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13222025831540427, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 2.004712151490451e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 43220, "start": 432.82, "end": 436.47999999999996, "text": " The inside is conditionally independent of the outside, given the blanket.", "tokens": [50396, 440, 1854, 307, 4188, 379, 6695, 295, 264, 2380, 11, 2212, 264, 17907, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13222025831540427, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 2.004712151490451e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 43220, "start": 437.02, "end": 442.26, "text": " Any influence from the outside world has to pass through that sensory and active layer to affect the inside.", "tokens": [50606, 2639, 6503, 490, 264, 2380, 1002, 575, 281, 1320, 807, 300, 27233, 293, 4967, 4583, 281, 3345, 264, 1854, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13222025831540427, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 2.004712151490451e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 43220, "start": 442.62, "end": 446.7, "text": " Okay, in the original notes I read, there was a metaphor about a bouncer at a club.", "tokens": [50886, 1033, 11, 294, 264, 3380, 5570, 286, 1401, 11, 456, 390, 257, 19157, 466, 257, 272, 14296, 412, 257, 6482, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13222025831540427, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 2.004712151490451e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 43220, "start": 447.02, "end": 451.84, "text": " But I really want to push on that because I think it misses the real weirdness of Friston's theory.", "tokens": [51106, 583, 286, 534, 528, 281, 2944, 322, 300, 570, 286, 519, 309, 29394, 264, 957, 3657, 1287, 295, 1526, 47345, 311, 5261, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13222025831540427, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 2.004712151490451e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 43220, "start": 451.98, "end": 452.34, "text": " Ooh.", "tokens": [51354, 7951, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13222025831540427, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 2.004712151490451e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 45234, "start": 452.34, "end": 456.52, "text": " Yeah, because it's not just that a bouncer is standing at the door deciding who gets in.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 570, 309, 311, 406, 445, 300, 257, 272, 14296, 307, 4877, 412, 264, 2853, 17990, 567, 2170, 294, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 45234, "start": 457.15999999999997, "end": 459.73999999999995, "text": " That just sounds like a normal passive wall with a door.", "tokens": [50606, 663, 445, 3263, 411, 257, 2710, 14975, 2929, 365, 257, 2853, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 45234, "start": 459.94, "end": 460.41999999999996, "text": " You are right.", "tokens": [50745, 509, 366, 558, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 45234, "start": 460.5, "end": 462.9, "text": " The standard bouncer analogy is way too passive.", "tokens": [50773, 440, 3832, 272, 14296, 21663, 307, 636, 886, 14975, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 45234, "start": 463.26, "end": 463.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50911, 1779, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 45234, "start": 463.76, "end": 467.38, "text": " So if I am understanding active inference correctly, it's more like this.", "tokens": [50936, 407, 498, 286, 669, 3701, 4967, 38253, 8944, 11, 309, 311, 544, 411, 341, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 45234, "start": 467.9, "end": 472.47999999999996, "text": " The people inside the club, the internal states, are completely blind.", "tokens": [51143, 440, 561, 1854, 264, 6482, 11, 264, 6920, 4368, 11, 366, 2584, 6865, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 45234, "start": 472.67999999999995, "end": 473.5, "text": " There are no windows.", "tokens": [51382, 821, 366, 572, 9309, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 45234, "start": 473.88, "end": 475.41999999999996, "text": " They cannot see the street outside.", "tokens": [51442, 814, 2644, 536, 264, 4838, 2380, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 45234, "start": 475.55999999999995, "end": 475.94, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51526, 1079, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 45234, "start": 476.02, "end": 481.44, "text": " The only thing they can see is a live video feed of the bouncer's face, the sensory states.", "tokens": [51549, 440, 787, 551, 436, 393, 536, 307, 257, 1621, 960, 3154, 295, 264, 272, 14296, 311, 1851, 11, 264, 27233, 4368, 13, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853445688883463, "compression_ratio": 1.7731958762886597, "no_speech_prob": 1.790022232002475e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 48144, "start": 481.44, "end": 485.48, "text": " They have to constantly figure out what is happening out on the street.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 362, 281, 6460, 2573, 484, 437, 307, 2737, 484, 322, 264, 4838, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 48144, "start": 485.84, "end": 486.56, "text": " Is there a fight?", "tokens": [50585, 1119, 456, 257, 2092, 30, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 48144, "start": 486.7, "end": 487.28, "text": " Is it raining?", "tokens": [50628, 1119, 309, 18441, 30, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 48144, "start": 487.46, "end": 488.34, "text": " Are the police there?", "tokens": [50666, 2014, 264, 3804, 456, 30, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 48144, "start": 489.02, "end": 494.46, "text": " Based exclusively on the microexpressions on bouncer's face, they are inferring reality from a proxy.", "tokens": [50744, 18785, 20638, 322, 264, 4532, 3121, 11637, 626, 322, 272, 14296, 311, 1851, 11, 436, 366, 13596, 2937, 4103, 490, 257, 29690, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 48144, "start": 495.06, "end": 497.7, "text": " That is a much more accurate translation of the mathematics.", "tokens": [51046, 663, 307, 257, 709, 544, 8559, 12853, 295, 264, 18666, 13, 51178], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 48144, "start": 498.12, "end": 505.15999999999997, "text": " Because of this statistical screening, the system's internal dynamics are forced to act as an approximate Bayesian inference about the outside world.", "tokens": [51199, 1436, 295, 341, 22820, 17732, 11, 264, 1185, 311, 6920, 15679, 366, 7579, 281, 605, 382, 364, 30874, 7840, 42434, 38253, 466, 264, 2380, 1002, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 48144, "start": 505.3, "end": 510.08, "text": " The internal states are constantly generating hypotheses to explain the states of the blanket.", "tokens": [51558, 440, 6920, 4368, 366, 6460, 17746, 49969, 281, 2903, 264, 4368, 295, 264, 17907, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10944377489326414, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161631936571162e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 51008, "start": 510.08, "end": 513.14, "text": " And this leads to the prime directive of Friston's system, right?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 264, 5835, 45444, 295, 1526, 47345, 311, 1185, 11, 558, 30, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14302185419443492, "compression_ratio": 1.4974874371859297, "no_speech_prob": 2.307364802695e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 51008, "start": 513.36, "end": 514.26, "text": " Minimizing surprise.", "tokens": [50529, 2829, 332, 3319, 6365, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14302185419443492, "compression_ratio": 1.4974874371859297, "no_speech_prob": 2.307364802695e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 51008, "start": 514.48, "end": 515.04, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50585, 48746, 736, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14302185419443492, "compression_ratio": 1.4974874371859297, "no_speech_prob": 2.307364802695e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 51008, "start": 515.48, "end": 520.22, "text": " Variational free energy in this context is essentially an upper bound on surprise.", "tokens": [50635, 32511, 1478, 1737, 2281, 294, 341, 4319, 307, 4476, 364, 6597, 5472, 322, 6365, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14302185419443492, "compression_ratio": 1.4974874371859297, "no_speech_prob": 2.307364802695e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 51008, "start": 521.04, "end": 528.6, "text": " The system must minimize the discrepancy between what it expects the blanket states to be and what they actually are.", "tokens": [50913, 440, 1185, 1633, 17522, 264, 2983, 265, 6040, 1344, 1296, 437, 309, 33280, 264, 17907, 4368, 281, 312, 293, 437, 436, 767, 366, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14302185419443492, "compression_ratio": 1.4974874371859297, "no_speech_prob": 2.307364802695e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 52860, "start": 528.6, "end": 533.52, "text": " And because of the architecture of the Markov blanket, it can only do this in two ways.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 570, 295, 264, 9482, 295, 264, 3934, 5179, 17907, 11, 309, 393, 787, 360, 341, 294, 732, 2098, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09330162794693657, "compression_ratio": 1.7566371681415929, "no_speech_prob": 2.044256474167949e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 52860, "start": 533.72, "end": 534.5, "text": " Perception and action.", "tokens": [50621, 3026, 7311, 293, 3069, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09330162794693657, "compression_ratio": 1.7566371681415929, "no_speech_prob": 2.044256474167949e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 52860, "start": 534.7, "end": 534.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50670, 1079, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09330162794693657, "compression_ratio": 1.7566371681415929, "no_speech_prob": 2.044256474167949e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 52860, "start": 535.4200000000001, "end": 551.4200000000001, "text": " It can either update its internal beliefs to better fit the sensory evidence it is receiving, that is perception, or it can use its active states to reach out and change the external world, thereby altering the sensory evidence so that it fits its existing beliefs, that is action.", "tokens": [50706, 467, 393, 2139, 5623, 1080, 6920, 13585, 281, 1101, 3318, 264, 27233, 4467, 309, 307, 10040, 11, 300, 307, 12860, 11, 420, 309, 393, 764, 1080, 4967, 4368, 281, 2524, 484, 293, 1319, 264, 8320, 1002, 11, 28281, 11337, 278, 264, 27233, 4467, 370, 300, 309, 9001, 1080, 6741, 13585, 11, 300, 307, 3069, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09330162794693657, "compression_ratio": 1.7566371681415929, "no_speech_prob": 2.044256474167949e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 55142, "start": 551.42, "end": 561.66, "text": " So if I'm in the club, and I strongly believe it's a calm night, but the bouncer on the monitor looks stressed, I either change my belief and accept that there's a riot outside, or I take an action.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 286, 478, 294, 264, 6482, 11, 293, 286, 10613, 1697, 309, 311, 257, 7151, 1818, 11, 457, 264, 272, 14296, 322, 264, 6002, 1542, 14471, 11, 286, 2139, 1319, 452, 7107, 293, 3241, 300, 456, 311, 257, 32211, 2380, 11, 420, 286, 747, 364, 3069, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611832964551317, "compression_ratio": 1.5890410958904109, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903485547727694e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 55142, "start": 561.68, "end": 561.9599999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50878, 1779, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611832964551317, "compression_ratio": 1.5890410958904109, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903485547727694e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 55142, "start": 562.4799999999999, "end": 568.86, "text": " Like, I send the bouncer a cup of coffee to calm him down, changing his facial expression to match my belief that everything is fine.", "tokens": [50918, 1743, 11, 286, 2845, 264, 272, 14296, 257, 4414, 295, 4982, 281, 7151, 796, 760, 11, 4473, 702, 15642, 6114, 281, 2995, 452, 7107, 300, 1203, 307, 2489, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611832964551317, "compression_ratio": 1.5890410958904109, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903485547727694e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 55142, "start": 569.28, "end": 569.7199999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51258, 7587, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611832964551317, "compression_ratio": 1.5890410958904109, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903485547727694e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 56972, "start": 569.72, "end": 576.44, "text": " But I want to draw your attention to what is not happening in this mechanism, because it is vital for understanding the conflict we'll talk about later on.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 286, 528, 281, 2642, 428, 3202, 281, 437, 307, 406, 2737, 294, 341, 7513, 11, 570, 309, 307, 11707, 337, 3701, 264, 6596, 321, 603, 751, 466, 1780, 322, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 56972, "start": 576.6600000000001, "end": 577.38, "text": " Okay, what's not happening?", "tokens": [50712, 1033, 11, 437, 311, 406, 2737, 30, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 56972, "start": 577.5400000000001, "end": 587.6, "text": " The Markov blanket screens, it mediates, and it allows the system to minimize surprise by updating probabilities, reweighting its beliefs over a fixed model of the world.", "tokens": [50756, 440, 3934, 5179, 17907, 11171, 11, 309, 17269, 1024, 11, 293, 309, 4045, 264, 1185, 281, 17522, 6365, 538, 25113, 33783, 11, 319, 12329, 278, 1080, 13585, 670, 257, 6806, 2316, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 56972, "start": 588.02, "end": 590.5400000000001, "text": " But it never outright deletes possibilities.", "tokens": [51280, 583, 309, 1128, 35189, 1103, 37996, 12178, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 56972, "start": 590.98, "end": 591.4200000000001, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51428, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 56972, "start": 591.5, "end": 592.6800000000001, "text": " It just shifts the math around.", "tokens": [51454, 467, 445, 19201, 264, 5221, 926, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 56972, "start": 592.76, "end": 596.84, "text": " It says, this is highly unlikely now, but it doesn't say, this is impossible.", "tokens": [51517, 467, 1619, 11, 341, 307, 5405, 17518, 586, 11, 457, 309, 1177, 380, 584, 11, 341, 307, 6243, 13, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 56972, "start": 597.0400000000001, "end": 597.38, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51731, 12753, 13, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11109526952107747, "compression_ratio": 1.617737003058104, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149516398987097e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 59738, "start": 597.38, "end": 603.26, "text": " The space of available policies and the fundamental generative model remain entirely intact.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1901, 295, 2435, 7657, 293, 264, 8088, 1337, 1166, 2316, 6222, 7696, 23493, 13, 50659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687927807078642, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615844562941959e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 59738, "start": 603.58, "end": 609.06, "text": " The boundary is an active inferential screen, but it is conservative regarding the option space.", "tokens": [50675, 440, 12866, 307, 364, 4967, 13596, 2549, 2568, 11, 457, 309, 307, 13780, 8595, 264, 3614, 1901, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687927807078642, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615844562941959e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 59738, "start": 609.36, "end": 615.48, "text": " Okay, so Fristen's boundary is a statistical screen forcing the system to minimize surprise through inference.", "tokens": [50964, 1033, 11, 370, 1526, 4821, 311, 12866, 307, 257, 22820, 2568, 19030, 264, 1185, 281, 17522, 6365, 807, 38253, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687927807078642, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615844562941959e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 59738, "start": 616.2, "end": 617.18, "text": " That's mechanism one.", "tokens": [51306, 663, 311, 7513, 472, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687927807078642, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615844562941959e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 59738, "start": 617.28, "end": 617.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51360, 1779, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687927807078642, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615844562941959e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 59738, "start": 617.88, "end": 623.4, "text": " Let's move to mechanism two, which shifts us from theoretical neuroscience to developmental biology.", "tokens": [51390, 961, 311, 1286, 281, 7513, 732, 11, 597, 19201, 505, 490, 20864, 42762, 281, 30160, 14956, 13, 51666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687927807078642, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615844562941959e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 59738, "start": 623.74, "end": 625.6, "text": " This is the work of Michael Levin.", "tokens": [51683, 639, 307, 264, 589, 295, 5116, 1456, 4796, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687927807078642, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615844562941959e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 62560, "start": 625.6, "end": 628.64, "text": " And I have to tell you, this part absolutely blew my mind.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 286, 362, 281, 980, 291, 11, 341, 644, 3122, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12197465227361311, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.82504380531745e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 62560, "start": 628.98, "end": 630.26, "text": " Levin's work is revolutionary.", "tokens": [50534, 1456, 4796, 311, 589, 307, 22687, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12197465227361311, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.82504380531745e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 62560, "start": 630.6800000000001, "end": 635.82, "text": " I mean, if Fristen's boundary is a statistical screen, Levin's boundary is a stored pursuit.", "tokens": [50619, 286, 914, 11, 498, 1526, 4821, 311, 12866, 307, 257, 22820, 2568, 11, 1456, 4796, 311, 12866, 307, 257, 12187, 23365, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12197465227361311, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.82504380531745e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 62560, "start": 636.24, "end": 637.0, "text": " A stored pursuit.", "tokens": [50897, 316, 12187, 23365, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12197465227361311, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.82504380531745e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 62560, "start": 637.8000000000001, "end": 646.52, "text": " If Fristen's boundary is the blind club goers reading a bouncer's face, I look at Levin's boundary as an architect who is obsessively following a blueprint.", "tokens": [50975, 759, 1526, 4821, 311, 12866, 307, 264, 6865, 6482, 352, 433, 3760, 257, 272, 14296, 311, 1851, 11, 286, 574, 412, 1456, 4796, 311, 12866, 382, 364, 6331, 567, 307, 35803, 3413, 3480, 257, 35868, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12197465227361311, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.82504380531745e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 62560, "start": 646.88, "end": 648.82, "text": " That is a very apt framing.", "tokens": [51429, 663, 307, 257, 588, 29427, 28971, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12197465227361311, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.82504380531745e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 62560, "start": 649.22, "end": 651.5400000000001, "text": " Levin studies developmental bioelectricity.", "tokens": [51546, 1456, 4796, 5313, 30160, 12198, 33243, 507, 13, 51662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12197465227361311, "compression_ratio": 1.736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.82504380531745e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 65154, "start": 651.54, "end": 655.48, "text": " And we really need to clarify that this is not about the nervous system.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 534, 643, 281, 17594, 300, 341, 307, 406, 466, 264, 6296, 1185, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16127437740177303, "compression_ratio": 1.5487179487179488, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823999654692502e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 65154, "start": 656.0, "end": 659.56, "text": " We are not talking about neurons firing fast action potentials.", "tokens": [50588, 492, 366, 406, 1417, 466, 22027, 16045, 2370, 3069, 3995, 82, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16127437740177303, "compression_ratio": 1.5487179487179488, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823999654692502e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 65154, "start": 659.62, "end": 665.0799999999999, "text": " We are talking about slow endogenous voltage gradients across all somatic cells.", "tokens": [50769, 492, 366, 1417, 466, 2964, 917, 45519, 8352, 2771, 2448, 2108, 439, 3307, 2399, 5438, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16127437740177303, "compression_ratio": 1.5487179487179488, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823999654692502e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 65154, "start": 665.3399999999999, "end": 666.9599999999999, "text": " Okay, break that down for me mechanically.", "tokens": [51055, 1033, 11, 1821, 300, 760, 337, 385, 4236, 984, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16127437740177303, "compression_ratio": 1.5487179487179488, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823999654692502e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 65154, "start": 667.14, "end": 669.26, "text": " How does a non-nerve cell have a voltage?", "tokens": [51145, 1012, 775, 257, 2107, 12, 1193, 303, 2815, 362, 257, 8352, 30, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16127437740177303, "compression_ratio": 1.5487179487179488, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823999654692502e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 66926, "start": 669.26, "end": 677.66, "text": " Well, every cell has a membrane, and that membrane has ion channels and pumps that push charged particles like sodium, potassium, and chloride in and out.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 633, 2815, 575, 257, 19651, 11, 293, 300, 19651, 575, 17437, 9235, 293, 27648, 300, 2944, 11109, 10007, 411, 20265, 11, 29547, 11, 293, 35434, 294, 293, 484, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 66926, "start": 678.06, "end": 678.3199999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50805, 1033, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 66926, "start": 678.58, "end": 682.9, "text": " This creates an electrical potential difference between the inside and the outside of the cell.", "tokens": [50831, 639, 7829, 364, 12147, 3995, 2649, 1296, 264, 1854, 293, 264, 2380, 295, 264, 2815, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 66926, "start": 683.22, "end": 689.1, "text": " And what Levin's lab discovered is that these voltage gradients aren't just a metabolic byproduct of being alive.", "tokens": [51063, 400, 437, 1456, 4796, 311, 2715, 6941, 307, 300, 613, 8352, 2771, 2448, 3212, 380, 445, 257, 36464, 538, 33244, 295, 885, 5465, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 66926, "start": 689.22, "end": 690.4399999999999, "text": " They aren't just exhaust fumes.", "tokens": [51363, 814, 3212, 380, 445, 14687, 283, 10018, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 66926, "start": 690.72, "end": 691.2, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51438, 7587, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 66926, "start": 691.36, "end": 693.2, "text": " They are actually a communication network.", "tokens": [51470, 814, 366, 767, 257, 6101, 3209, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 66926, "start": 693.56, "end": 696.34, "text": " They function as a bioelectric pre-pattern.", "tokens": [51580, 814, 2445, 382, 257, 12198, 33243, 659, 12, 79, 1161, 77, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 66926, "start": 696.46, "end": 697.88, "text": " So they are passing messages to each other.", "tokens": [51725, 407, 436, 366, 8437, 7897, 281, 1184, 661, 13, 51796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13767964603336713, "compression_ratio": 1.6884735202492211, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039891853961152e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 69788, "start": 697.88, "end": 699.74, "text": " More than just messages, actually.", "tokens": [50365, 5048, 813, 445, 7897, 11, 767, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15267615982248814, "compression_ratio": 1.5128205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.782381967713187e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 69788, "start": 700.38, "end": 708.0, "text": " This bioelectric network literally instructs cell behavior during embryo development, regeneration, and tissue maintenance.", "tokens": [50490, 639, 12198, 33243, 3209, 3736, 7232, 82, 2815, 5223, 1830, 31588, 78, 3250, 11, 43813, 11, 293, 12404, 11258, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15267615982248814, "compression_ratio": 1.5128205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.782381967713187e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 69788, "start": 708.3, "end": 708.5, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50886, 3153, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15267615982248814, "compression_ratio": 1.5128205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.782381967713187e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 69788, "start": 708.66, "end": 711.12, "text": " It acts as a pattern memory layer.", "tokens": [50904, 467, 10672, 382, 257, 5102, 4675, 4583, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15267615982248814, "compression_ratio": 1.5128205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.782381967713187e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 69788, "start": 711.54, "end": 721.84, "text": " It encodes a target morphology, a specific large-scale anatomical configuration that the collective intelligence of the cells can read and actively pursue.", "tokens": [51048, 467, 2058, 4789, 257, 3779, 25778, 1793, 11, 257, 2685, 2416, 12, 20033, 21618, 298, 804, 11694, 300, 264, 12590, 7599, 295, 264, 5438, 393, 1401, 293, 13022, 12392, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15267615982248814, "compression_ratio": 1.5128205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.782381967713187e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 72184, "start": 721.84, "end": 729.36, "text": " So, wait, the electrical state of the tissue is literally holding a memory of what the tissue is supposed to look like in the future.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 1699, 11, 264, 12147, 1785, 295, 264, 12404, 307, 3736, 5061, 257, 4675, 295, 437, 264, 12404, 307, 3442, 281, 574, 411, 294, 264, 2027, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11768461709999177, "compression_ratio": 1.658878504672897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362209981010678e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 72184, "start": 729.5600000000001, "end": 729.9200000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50751, 1079, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11768461709999177, "compression_ratio": 1.658878504672897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362209981010678e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 72184, "start": 730.1600000000001, "end": 735.86, "text": " So the boundary of a regenerating arm isn't just the place where the cells ran out of energy and stopped growing.", "tokens": [50781, 407, 264, 12866, 295, 257, 26358, 990, 3726, 1943, 380, 445, 264, 1081, 689, 264, 5438, 5872, 484, 295, 2281, 293, 5936, 4194, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11768461709999177, "compression_ratio": 1.658878504672897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362209981010678e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 72184, "start": 736.2, "end": 742.5400000000001, "text": " The boundary is the visible outcome of a target shape that the tissue is constantly striving to match.", "tokens": [51083, 440, 12866, 307, 264, 8974, 9700, 295, 257, 3779, 3909, 300, 264, 12404, 307, 6460, 36582, 281, 2995, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11768461709999177, "compression_ratio": 1.658878504672897, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362209981010678e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 74254, "start": 742.54, "end": 742.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19120098114013673, "compression_ratio": 1.4263157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823915086923048e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 74254, "start": 743.04, "end": 746.7199999999999, "text": " The boundary is evaluated against a state the system does not your occupy.", "tokens": [50390, 440, 12866, 307, 25509, 1970, 257, 1785, 264, 1185, 775, 406, 428, 30645, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19120098114013673, "compression_ratio": 1.4263157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823915086923048e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 74254, "start": 747.1999999999999, "end": 749.78, "text": " And the empirical proof of this is astonishing.", "tokens": [50598, 400, 264, 31886, 8177, 295, 341, 307, 35264, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19120098114013673, "compression_ratio": 1.4263157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823915086923048e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 74254, "start": 750.14, "end": 751.18, "text": " Tell me about the flatworms.", "tokens": [50745, 5115, 385, 466, 264, 4962, 30917, 82, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19120098114013673, "compression_ratio": 1.4263157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823915086923048e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 74254, "start": 751.4, "end": 751.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50808, 1779, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19120098114013673, "compression_ratio": 1.4263157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823915086923048e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 74254, "start": 751.8399999999999, "end": 756.9, "text": " So in Levin's lab, they work with planaria, these flatworms that can regenerate from almost any injury.", "tokens": [50830, 407, 294, 1456, 4796, 311, 2715, 11, 436, 589, 365, 1393, 9831, 11, 613, 4962, 30917, 82, 300, 393, 26358, 473, 490, 1920, 604, 10454, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19120098114013673, "compression_ratio": 1.4263157894736842, "no_speech_prob": 1.7823915086923048e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 75690, "start": 756.9, "end": 764.02, "text": " If you cut off a flatworm's head, the cells at the wound site communicate bioelectrically to say, hey, we need a head here, and they build one.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1723, 766, 257, 4962, 30917, 311, 1378, 11, 264, 5438, 412, 264, 10999, 3621, 7890, 12198, 14664, 81, 984, 281, 584, 11, 4177, 11, 321, 643, 257, 1378, 510, 11, 293, 436, 1322, 472, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0837405019526859, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619832680225821e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 75690, "start": 764.18, "end": 766.28, "text": " Which is already amazing, but it goes further than that, right?", "tokens": [50729, 3013, 307, 1217, 2243, 11, 457, 309, 1709, 3052, 813, 300, 11, 558, 30, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0837405019526859, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619832680225821e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 75690, "start": 766.48, "end": 767.04, "text": " Much further.", "tokens": [50844, 12313, 3052, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0837405019526859, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619832680225821e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 75690, "start": 767.88, "end": 779.1, "text": " Levin's team found that by briefly altering the bioelectric gradient at the wound site, just changing the voltage, without touching the DNA at all, they could rewrite the stored target morphology.", "tokens": [50914, 1456, 4796, 311, 1469, 1352, 300, 538, 10515, 11337, 278, 264, 12198, 33243, 16235, 412, 264, 10999, 3621, 11, 445, 4473, 264, 8352, 11, 1553, 11175, 264, 8272, 412, 439, 11, 436, 727, 28132, 264, 12187, 3779, 25778, 1793, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0837405019526859, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619832680225821e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 75690, "start": 779.3, "end": 780.42, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [51485, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0837405019526859, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619832680225821e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 75690, "start": 780.42, "end": 786.66, "text": " They could tell the tissue, the target shape is now two heads, and the worm would grow a second head at the tail end.", "tokens": [51541, 814, 727, 980, 264, 12404, 11, 264, 3779, 3909, 307, 586, 732, 8050, 11, 293, 264, 23835, 576, 1852, 257, 1150, 1378, 412, 264, 6838, 917, 13, 51853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0837405019526859, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619832680225821e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 78666, "start": 786.66, "end": 787.8199999999999, "text": " They hacked the blueprint.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 36218, 264, 35868, 13, 50423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991427220335794, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 78666, "start": 788.0799999999999, "end": 788.66, "text": " They did.", "tokens": [50436, 814, 630, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991427220335794, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 78666, "start": 789.24, "end": 798.9399999999999, "text": " And perhaps even more profoundly, if you then take that two-headed worm, leave its bioelectricity alone, and cut off both heads, it will regenerate into a two-headed worm again.", "tokens": [50494, 400, 4317, 754, 544, 39954, 11, 498, 291, 550, 747, 300, 732, 12, 28409, 23835, 11, 1856, 1080, 12198, 33243, 507, 3312, 11, 293, 1723, 766, 1293, 8050, 11, 309, 486, 26358, 473, 666, 257, 732, 12, 28409, 23835, 797, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991427220335794, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 78666, "start": 799.1, "end": 799.8399999999999, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [50987, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991427220335794, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 78666, "start": 800.48, "end": 802.0799999999999, "text": " Even though the DNA hasn't changed?", "tokens": [51056, 2754, 1673, 264, 8272, 6132, 380, 3105, 30, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991427220335794, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 78666, "start": 802.24, "end": 812.88, "text": " The genetic code is completely normal, wild-type DNA, but the bioelectric memory layer is intact and actively pulling the cells toward the new, altered target morphology.", "tokens": [51144, 440, 12462, 3089, 307, 2584, 2710, 11, 4868, 12, 20467, 8272, 11, 457, 264, 12198, 33243, 4675, 4583, 307, 23493, 293, 13022, 8407, 264, 5438, 7361, 264, 777, 11, 28783, 3779, 25778, 1793, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10991427220335794, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 81288, "start": 812.88, "end": 820.58, "text": " So the DNA is just the hardware providing the proteins, but the bioelectric boundary is the software actually running the geometric pursuit.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 8272, 307, 445, 264, 8837, 6530, 264, 15577, 11, 457, 264, 12198, 33243, 12866, 307, 264, 4722, 767, 2614, 264, 33246, 23365, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10318545760395371, "compression_ratio": 1.6703703703703703, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759147880909044e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 81288, "start": 820.8, "end": 821.6, "text": " That's exactly right.", "tokens": [50761, 663, 311, 2293, 558, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10318545760395371, "compression_ratio": 1.6703703703703703, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759147880909044e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 81288, "start": 821.9, "end": 825.08, "text": " So Levin's boundary is defined by what the system is trying to become.", "tokens": [50816, 407, 1456, 4796, 311, 12866, 307, 7642, 538, 437, 264, 1185, 307, 1382, 281, 1813, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10318545760395371, "compression_ratio": 1.6703703703703703, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759147880909044e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 81288, "start": 825.36, "end": 828.2, "text": " It's a computational object driving a physical pursuit.", "tokens": [50989, 467, 311, 257, 28270, 2657, 4840, 257, 4001, 23365, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10318545760395371, "compression_ratio": 1.6703703703703703, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759147880909044e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 81288, "start": 828.56, "end": 833.06, "text": " Okay, so we have Fristen's statistical screen and Levin's stored pursuit.", "tokens": [51149, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 362, 1526, 4821, 311, 22820, 2568, 293, 1456, 4796, 311, 12187, 23365, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10318545760395371, "compression_ratio": 1.6703703703703703, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759147880909044e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 81288, "start": 833.4399999999999, "end": 837.04, "text": " Now we hit the third mechanism, and I really need you to hold my hand through this one,", "tokens": [51393, 823, 321, 2045, 264, 2636, 7513, 11, 293, 286, 534, 643, 291, 281, 1797, 452, 1011, 807, 341, 472, 11, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10318545760395371, "compression_ratio": 1.6703703703703703, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759147880909044e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 83704, "start": 837.04, "end": 841.3399999999999, "text": " because this is where the paper gets incredibly abstract, but also where it hits the hardest.", "tokens": [50365, 570, 341, 307, 689, 264, 3035, 2170, 6252, 12649, 11, 457, 611, 689, 309, 8664, 264, 13158, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12436251867385138, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338403933073177e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 83704, "start": 841.5, "end": 842.7199999999999, "text": " Yeah, this one is deep.", "tokens": [50588, 865, 11, 341, 472, 307, 2452, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12436251867385138, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338403933073177e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 83704, "start": 843.0999999999999, "end": 848.88, "text": " This comes from an admissibility theoretic account of irreversible computation, known as RSVP theory.", "tokens": [50668, 639, 1487, 490, 364, 5910, 891, 2841, 14308, 299, 2696, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 24903, 11, 2570, 382, 25855, 53, 47, 5261, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12436251867385138, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338403933073177e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 83704, "start": 849.04, "end": 849.3399999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50965, 1079, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12436251867385138, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338403933073177e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 83704, "start": 849.8, "end": 854.3399999999999, "text": " And where Fristen looks at missing causal edges, and Levin looks at a stored target,", "tokens": [51003, 400, 689, 1526, 4821, 1542, 412, 5361, 38755, 8819, 11, 293, 1456, 4796, 1542, 412, 257, 12187, 3779, 11, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12436251867385138, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338403933073177e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 83704, "start": 855.02, "end": 861.5799999999999, "text": " RSVP theory locates the boundary in what has been permanently deleted from a system space of possible futures.", "tokens": [51264, 25855, 53, 47, 5261, 1628, 1024, 264, 12866, 294, 437, 575, 668, 24042, 22981, 490, 257, 1185, 1901, 295, 1944, 26071, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12436251867385138, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338403933073177e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 86158, "start": 862.08, "end": 863.1600000000001, "text": " Admissibility deletion.", "tokens": [50390, 46292, 891, 2841, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 50444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120532852035385, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 86158, "start": 863.74, "end": 868.0200000000001, "text": " Okay, let's really take our time here, because the paper looks at this across three different scales,", "tokens": [50473, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 534, 747, 527, 565, 510, 11, 570, 264, 3035, 1542, 412, 341, 2108, 1045, 819, 17408, 11, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120532852035385, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 86158, "start": 868.12, "end": 870.2800000000001, "text": " and I want to make sure I understand the mechanics of each one.", "tokens": [50692, 293, 286, 528, 281, 652, 988, 286, 1223, 264, 12939, 295, 1184, 472, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120532852035385, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 86158, "start": 870.36, "end": 873.62, "text": " Let's start at the macroscopic level, what they call the continuum scale.", "tokens": [50804, 961, 311, 722, 412, 264, 7912, 38006, 299, 1496, 11, 437, 436, 818, 264, 36120, 4373, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120532852035385, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 86158, "start": 874.24, "end": 881.96, "text": " At this scale, RSVP theory formalizes the boundary as an entropy field over a system's entire configuration space.", "tokens": [50998, 1711, 341, 4373, 11, 25855, 53, 47, 5261, 9860, 5660, 264, 12866, 382, 364, 30867, 2519, 670, 257, 1185, 311, 2302, 11694, 1901, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120532852035385, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 86158, "start": 882.22, "end": 886.6400000000001, "text": " Meaning the space of all possible physical arrangements the system could possibly take.", "tokens": [51397, 19948, 264, 1901, 295, 439, 1944, 4001, 22435, 264, 1185, 727, 6264, 747, 13, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120532852035385, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 88664, "start": 886.64, "end": 892.52, "text": " Correct. As a system undergoes changes, makes physical commitments, or expends energy,", "tokens": [50365, 12753, 13, 1018, 257, 1185, 26426, 279, 2962, 11, 1669, 4001, 26230, 11, 420, 1278, 2581, 2281, 11, 50659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 88664, "start": 892.86, "end": 895.4, "text": " it approaches a maximal admissible limit.", "tokens": [50676, 309, 11587, 257, 49336, 5910, 41073, 4948, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 88664, "start": 895.98, "end": 899.06, "text": " These regions act as hard barriers to further change.", "tokens": [50832, 1981, 10682, 605, 382, 1152, 13565, 281, 3052, 1319, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 88664, "start": 899.46, "end": 902.9, "text": " The theory calls them structural placos, or frozen domains.", "tokens": [51006, 440, 5261, 5498, 552, 15067, 20831, 329, 11, 420, 12496, 25514, 13, 51178], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 88664, "start": 903.1999999999999, "end": 906.72, "text": " Okay, so at this scale, it's kind of like a car driving into a dead end.", "tokens": [51193, 1033, 11, 370, 412, 341, 4373, 11, 309, 311, 733, 295, 411, 257, 1032, 4840, 666, 257, 3116, 917, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 88664, "start": 906.8, "end": 906.96, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51373, 1033, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 88664, "start": 907.06, "end": 912.78, "text": " The boundary is just the place where the system has completely run out of room to keep moving or changing.", "tokens": [51386, 440, 12866, 307, 445, 264, 1081, 689, 264, 1185, 575, 2584, 1190, 484, 295, 1808, 281, 1066, 2684, 420, 4473, 13, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 88664, "start": 912.9, "end": 914.48, "text": " It's a global saturation point.", "tokens": [51678, 467, 311, 257, 4338, 27090, 935, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10362911224365234, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617880694621887e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 91448, "start": 914.48, "end": 917.76, "text": " Yes. Now let's zoom in to the discrete event scale.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 823, 718, 311, 8863, 294, 281, 264, 27706, 2280, 4373, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 91448, "start": 917.96, "end": 919.22, "text": " This is where it gets more dynamic.", "tokens": [50539, 639, 307, 689, 309, 2170, 544, 8546, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 91448, "start": 919.84, "end": 926.1800000000001, "text": " At this scale, the theory formalizes the boundary as the elimination of a specific region of an option space.", "tokens": [50633, 1711, 341, 4373, 11, 264, 5261, 9860, 5660, 264, 12866, 382, 264, 29224, 295, 257, 2685, 4458, 295, 364, 3614, 1901, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 91448, "start": 926.34, "end": 926.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50958, 1033, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 91448, "start": 926.8000000000001, "end": 929.22, "text": " And what is crucial here is the thermodynamics.", "tokens": [50981, 400, 437, 307, 11462, 510, 307, 264, 8810, 35483, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 91448, "start": 929.94, "end": 935.32, "text": " The entropy cost of eliminating that option is concentrated right near the boundary of the region being eliminated,", "tokens": [51138, 440, 30867, 2063, 295, 31203, 300, 3614, 307, 21321, 558, 2651, 264, 12866, 295, 264, 4458, 885, 20308, 11, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 91448, "start": 935.76, "end": 937.8000000000001, "text": " what they call boundary sharpening slack.", "tokens": [51429, 437, 436, 818, 12866, 8199, 4559, 29767, 13, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 91448, "start": 937.9200000000001, "end": 940.0, "text": " Wait, explain that. What is boundary sharpening slack?", "tokens": [51537, 3802, 11, 2903, 300, 13, 708, 307, 12866, 8199, 4559, 29767, 30, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661606516156877, "compression_ratio": 1.7915057915057915, "no_speech_prob": 1.825485726122955e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 94000, "start": 940.0, "end": 942.66, "text": " Think about making a hard, irreversible decision.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 1455, 257, 1152, 11, 16014, 840, 964, 3537, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309359049059681, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5159934939334985e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 94000, "start": 942.78, "end": 946.36, "text": " Before you decide, there is a lot of fluctuation, a lot of back and forth, high entropy.", "tokens": [50504, 4546, 291, 4536, 11, 456, 307, 257, 688, 295, 23448, 16073, 11, 257, 688, 295, 646, 293, 5220, 11, 1090, 30867, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309359049059681, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5159934939334985e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 94000, "start": 946.48, "end": 946.68, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50689, 1779, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309359049059681, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5159934939334985e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 94000, "start": 946.84, "end": 951.04, "text": " The moment you make the irreversible choice and eliminate an entire set of options,", "tokens": [50707, 440, 1623, 291, 652, 264, 16014, 840, 964, 3922, 293, 13819, 364, 2302, 992, 295, 3956, 11, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309359049059681, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5159934939334985e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 94000, "start": 951.28, "end": 956.34, "text": " there is a sharp spike in energy dissipation right at the edge of that decision space.", "tokens": [50929, 456, 307, 257, 8199, 21053, 294, 2281, 29544, 399, 558, 412, 264, 4691, 295, 300, 3537, 1901, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309359049059681, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5159934939334985e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 94000, "start": 956.48, "end": 960.82, "text": " The boundary is defined by that localized burst of irreversibility.", "tokens": [51189, 440, 12866, 307, 7642, 538, 300, 44574, 12712, 295, 16014, 840, 2841, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309359049059681, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5159934939334985e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 96082, "start": 960.82, "end": 971.0600000000001, "text": " Okay. So instead of a gradual approach to a wall, this is the exact moment a single irreversible choice is crystallized and a whole set of futures is just snapped off.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 407, 2602, 295, 257, 32890, 3109, 281, 257, 2929, 11, 341, 307, 264, 1900, 1623, 257, 2167, 16014, 840, 964, 3922, 307, 31924, 1602, 293, 257, 1379, 992, 295, 26071, 307, 445, 41396, 766, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09977179357450303, "compression_ratio": 1.4615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732952050526161e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 96082, "start": 971.24, "end": 979.12, "text": " Exactly. And finally, at the smallest scale, looking at just pairs of individual states, they define an exclusion distance.", "tokens": [50886, 7587, 13, 400, 2721, 11, 412, 264, 16998, 4373, 11, 1237, 412, 445, 15494, 295, 2609, 4368, 11, 436, 6964, 364, 33049, 4560, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09977179357450303, "compression_ratio": 1.4615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732952050526161e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 96082, "start": 979.34, "end": 979.6800000000001, "text": " What's that?", "tokens": [51291, 708, 311, 300, 30, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09977179357450303, "compression_ratio": 1.4615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.5732952050526161e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 97968, "start": 979.68, "end": 984.4, "text": " This is the minimum admissibility barrier separating state A from state B.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 7285, 5910, 891, 2841, 13357, 29279, 1785, 316, 490, 1785, 363, 13, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12159421596121281, "compression_ratio": 1.6943231441048034, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776347684152368e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 97968, "start": 984.9399999999999, "end": 988.9, "text": " If that barrier is greater than zero, a boundary exists between them.", "tokens": [50628, 759, 300, 13357, 307, 5044, 813, 4018, 11, 257, 12866, 8198, 1296, 552, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12159421596121281, "compression_ratio": 1.6943231441048034, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776347684152368e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 97968, "start": 989.16, "end": 995.8599999999999, "text": " And the theory argues that identity itself, what makes a thing that thing, is defined as what persists because of that obstruction.", "tokens": [50839, 400, 264, 5261, 38218, 300, 6575, 2564, 11, 437, 1669, 257, 551, 300, 551, 11, 307, 7642, 382, 437, 868, 1751, 570, 295, 300, 49711, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12159421596121281, "compression_ratio": 1.6943231441048034, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776347684152368e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 97968, "start": 996.3199999999999, "end": 999.66, "text": " I am what I am because of the things I am obstructed from becoming.", "tokens": [51197, 286, 669, 437, 286, 669, 570, 295, 264, 721, 286, 669, 45579, 292, 490, 5617, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12159421596121281, "compression_ratio": 1.6943231441048034, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776347684152368e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 97968, "start": 999.9399999999999, "end": 1001.26, "text": " That is deeply philosophical.", "tokens": [51378, 663, 307, 8760, 25066, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12159421596121281, "compression_ratio": 1.6943231441048034, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776347684152368e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 97968, "start": 1001.4599999999999, "end": 1002.0799999999999, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51454, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12159421596121281, "compression_ratio": 1.6943231441048034, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776347684152368e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 100208, "start": 1002.08, "end": 1010.1800000000001, "text": " But the paper dives into one specific application of this RSVP framework that I think is the most profound part of this whole first section, and that's the concept of refusal.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 3035, 274, 1539, 666, 472, 2685, 3861, 295, 341, 25855, 53, 47, 8388, 300, 286, 519, 307, 264, 881, 14382, 644, 295, 341, 1379, 700, 3541, 11, 293, 300, 311, 264, 3410, 295, 48948, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09539269386453832, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983200006564058e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 100208, "start": 1010.58, "end": 1010.9000000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50790, 1079, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09539269386453832, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983200006564058e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 100208, "start": 1011.5400000000001, "end": 1018.26, "text": " The formal theory of refusal is the sharpest, most controversial instance of this admissibility dilution.", "tokens": [50838, 440, 9860, 5261, 295, 48948, 307, 264, 8199, 377, 11, 881, 17323, 5197, 295, 341, 5910, 891, 2841, 11504, 1448, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09539269386453832, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983200006564058e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 100208, "start": 1018.26, "end": 1025.42, "text": " I really want you, the listener, to pay attention to this because reading this completely changed how I think about choice.", "tokens": [51174, 286, 534, 528, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 281, 1689, 3202, 281, 341, 570, 3760, 341, 2584, 3105, 577, 286, 519, 466, 3922, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09539269386453832, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983200006564058e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 102542, "start": 1025.42, "end": 1033.5, "text": " Normally, in economics or psychology, if I offer you a piece of cake and you say no, we just assume you have a low preference for cake.", "tokens": [50365, 17424, 11, 294, 14564, 420, 15105, 11, 498, 286, 2626, 291, 257, 2522, 295, 5908, 293, 291, 584, 572, 11, 321, 445, 6552, 291, 362, 257, 2295, 17502, 337, 5908, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11547157551982615, "compression_ratio": 1.541501976284585, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617924062708786e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 102542, "start": 1033.68, "end": 1033.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50778, 1779, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11547157551982615, "compression_ratio": 1.541501976284585, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617924062708786e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 102542, "start": 1034.1000000000001, "end": 1039.16, "text": " You ran a quick utility calculation in your head, the cake scored low, maybe you're on a diet, so you passed.", "tokens": [50799, 509, 5872, 257, 1702, 14877, 17108, 294, 428, 1378, 11, 264, 5908, 18139, 2295, 11, 1310, 291, 434, 322, 257, 6339, 11, 370, 291, 4678, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11547157551982615, "compression_ratio": 1.541501976284585, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617924062708786e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 102542, "start": 1039.78, "end": 1045.2, "text": " But Percusion points out that RSVP theory says genuine refusal is not a preference.", "tokens": [51083, 583, 3026, 1149, 313, 2793, 484, 300, 25855, 53, 47, 5261, 1619, 16699, 48948, 307, 406, 257, 17502, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11547157551982615, "compression_ratio": 1.541501976284585, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617924062708786e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 102542, "start": 1045.7, "end": 1049.64, "text": " It is emphatically not ordinary utility maximization.", "tokens": [51379, 467, 307, 846, 950, 5030, 406, 10547, 14877, 5138, 2144, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11547157551982615, "compression_ratio": 1.541501976284585, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617924062708786e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 104964, "start": 1049.64, "end": 1058.8600000000001, "text": " The source theory provides a rigorous formal proof that true refusal cannot be represented as just having a low utility function over a fixed space of options.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4009, 5261, 6417, 257, 29882, 9860, 8177, 300, 2074, 48948, 2644, 312, 10379, 382, 445, 1419, 257, 2295, 14877, 2445, 670, 257, 6806, 1901, 295, 3956, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07810281452379729, "compression_ratio": 1.6769759450171822, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254779198673132e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 104964, "start": 1059.0, "end": 1059.6000000000001, "text": " I don't get that.", "tokens": [50833, 286, 500, 380, 483, 300, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07810281452379729, "compression_ratio": 1.6769759450171822, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254779198673132e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 104964, "start": 1059.72, "end": 1063.98, "text": " I mean, if I assign a value of negative 10 to eating the cake, isn't that a refusal?", "tokens": [50869, 286, 914, 11, 498, 286, 6269, 257, 2158, 295, 3671, 1266, 281, 3936, 264, 5908, 11, 1943, 380, 300, 257, 48948, 30, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07810281452379729, "compression_ratio": 1.6769759450171822, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254779198673132e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 104964, "start": 1064.38, "end": 1066.3000000000002, "text": " Why doesn't the standard utility model work?", "tokens": [51102, 1545, 1177, 380, 264, 3832, 14877, 2316, 589, 30, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07810281452379729, "compression_ratio": 1.6769759450171822, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254779198673132e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 104964, "start": 1066.48, "end": 1074.7, "text": " Because merely discovering that an option is worthless or has negative utility is behaviorally indistinguishable from refusing an option that you know has high value.", "tokens": [51207, 1436, 17003, 24773, 300, 364, 3614, 307, 34857, 420, 575, 3671, 14877, 307, 5223, 379, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 490, 37289, 364, 3614, 300, 291, 458, 575, 1090, 2158, 13, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07810281452379729, "compression_ratio": 1.6769759450171822, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254779198673132e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 104964, "start": 1074.94, "end": 1075.48, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [51630, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07810281452379729, "compression_ratio": 1.6769759450171822, "no_speech_prob": 1.8254779198673132e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 107548, "start": 1075.48, "end": 1086.06, "text": " Yeah. If we only look at a standard utility function, we can't tell the difference between an agent who simply doesn't want to win a game and an agent who actively refuses to win out of moral protest.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 759, 321, 787, 574, 412, 257, 3832, 14877, 2445, 11, 321, 393, 380, 980, 264, 2649, 1296, 364, 9461, 567, 2935, 1177, 380, 528, 281, 1942, 257, 1216, 293, 364, 9461, 567, 13022, 33222, 281, 1942, 484, 295, 9723, 11281, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405252062584743, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615851068154994e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 107548, "start": 1086.3600000000001, "end": 1086.98, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50909, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405252062584743, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615851068154994e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 107548, "start": 1087.28, "end": 1090.38, "text": " The utility function just sees the outcome. Did not win.", "tokens": [50955, 440, 14877, 2445, 445, 8194, 264, 9700, 13, 2589, 406, 1942, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405252062584743, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615851068154994e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 107548, "start": 1091.04, "end": 1095.54, "text": " To represent true refusal, you have to track the event history as a mathematical primitive.", "tokens": [51143, 1407, 2906, 2074, 48948, 11, 291, 362, 281, 2837, 264, 2280, 2503, 382, 257, 18894, 28540, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405252062584743, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615851068154994e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 107548, "start": 1096.02, "end": 1098.48, "text": " You have to know what was on the table and was actively rejected.", "tokens": [51392, 509, 362, 281, 458, 437, 390, 322, 264, 3199, 293, 390, 13022, 15749, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405252062584743, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615851068154994e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 107548, "start": 1098.9, "end": 1102.58, "text": " So what is refusal mechanically if it isn't just a low preference score?", "tokens": [51536, 407, 437, 307, 48948, 4236, 984, 498, 309, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 2295, 17502, 6175, 30, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12405252062584743, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3615851068154994e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 110258, "start": 1102.58, "end": 1105.96, "text": " Mechanically, it is an inadmissibility prior.", "tokens": [50365, 30175, 984, 11, 309, 307, 364, 42148, 76, 891, 2841, 4059, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11221186022892177, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071332853597297e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 110258, "start": 1106.62, "end": 1113.26, "text": " It is a structural constraint that sets the probability of an entire class of future trajectories permanently to zero.", "tokens": [50567, 467, 307, 257, 15067, 25534, 300, 6352, 264, 8482, 295, 364, 2302, 1508, 295, 2027, 18257, 2083, 24042, 281, 4018, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11221186022892177, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071332853597297e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 110258, "start": 1113.5, "end": 1115.3, "text": " It is a topological deletion.", "tokens": [50911, 467, 307, 257, 1192, 4383, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11221186022892177, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071332853597297e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 110258, "start": 1115.5, "end": 1118.08, "text": " A topological deletion. It deletes the future.", "tokens": [51011, 316, 1192, 4383, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 467, 1103, 37996, 264, 2027, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11221186022892177, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071332853597297e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 110258, "start": 1118.56, "end": 1121.76, "text": " It doesn't just say, I'd rather not take this path because it costs too much.", "tokens": [51164, 467, 1177, 380, 445, 584, 11, 286, 1116, 2831, 406, 747, 341, 3100, 570, 309, 5497, 886, 709, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11221186022892177, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071332853597297e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 110258, "start": 1121.84, "end": 1125.8999999999999, "text": " It says, this path no longer exists in my universe. I have severed the bridge.", "tokens": [51328, 467, 1619, 11, 341, 3100, 572, 2854, 8198, 294, 452, 6445, 13, 286, 362, 2802, 292, 264, 7283, 13, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11221186022892177, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071332853597297e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 112590, "start": 1125.9, "end": 1131.5800000000002, "text": " Exactly. It contracts the trajectory space permanently at the boundary that the refusal draws.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 467, 13952, 264, 21512, 1901, 24042, 412, 264, 12866, 300, 264, 48948, 20045, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09592793538020207, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977281042475e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 112590, "start": 1131.98, "end": 1138.92, "text": " It is constitutive. It changes the geometry of what the system is. It is not just a Bayesian update of beliefs based on new evidence.", "tokens": [50669, 467, 307, 23079, 17254, 13, 467, 2962, 264, 18426, 295, 437, 264, 1185, 307, 13, 467, 307, 406, 445, 257, 7840, 42434, 5623, 295, 13585, 2361, 322, 777, 4467, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09592793538020207, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977281042475e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 113892, "start": 1138.92, "end": 1143.22, "text": " Okay, so let's synthesize this. We have these three incredible mechanisms.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 718, 311, 26617, 1125, 341, 13, 492, 362, 613, 1045, 4651, 15902, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19831096592234143, "compression_ratio": 1.3730569948186528, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214524077047155e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 113892, "start": 1143.88, "end": 1146.8600000000001, "text": " Friston's statistical screen forcing blind inference.", "tokens": [50613, 1526, 47345, 311, 22820, 2568, 19030, 6865, 38253, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19831096592234143, "compression_ratio": 1.3730569948186528, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214524077047155e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 113892, "start": 1147.48, "end": 1151.8600000000001, "text": " Levin's stored bioelectric pursuit dragging cells toward a target.", "tokens": [50793, 1456, 4796, 311, 12187, 12198, 33243, 23365, 24385, 5438, 7361, 257, 3779, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19831096592234143, "compression_ratio": 1.3730569948186528, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214524077047155e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 113892, "start": 1152.26, "end": 1157.2, "text": " And RSVP's topological dilution permanently zeroing out futures.", "tokens": [51032, 400, 25855, 53, 47, 311, 1192, 4383, 11504, 1448, 24042, 4018, 278, 484, 26071, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19831096592234143, "compression_ratio": 1.3730569948186528, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214524077047155e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 113892, "start": 1157.44, "end": 1157.8200000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51291, 1079, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19831096592234143, "compression_ratio": 1.3730569948186528, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214524077047155e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 115782, "start": 1157.82, "end": 1164.12, "text": " Now, I have to play the skeptic here because my immediate reaction when reading this sack of papers was, well, wait a minute.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 286, 362, 281, 862, 264, 19128, 299, 510, 570, 452, 11629, 5480, 562, 3760, 341, 33209, 295, 10577, 390, 11, 731, 11, 1699, 257, 3456, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 115782, "start": 1164.4399999999998, "end": 1169.0, "text": " Aren't these just three different overly complex academic metaphors for the exact same thing?", "tokens": [50696, 15464, 380, 613, 445, 1045, 819, 24324, 3997, 7778, 30946, 830, 337, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 30, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 115782, "start": 1169.06, "end": 1170.1599999999999, "text": " It's a common reaction.", "tokens": [50927, 467, 311, 257, 2689, 5480, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 115782, "start": 1170.5, "end": 1173.46, "text": " Right. Aren't they all just saying, hey, boundaries are active instead of passive?", "tokens": [50999, 1779, 13, 15464, 380, 436, 439, 445, 1566, 11, 4177, 11, 13180, 366, 4967, 2602, 295, 14975, 30, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 115782, "start": 1173.6, "end": 1175.06, "text": " Or are we just arguing over semantics?", "tokens": [51154, 1610, 366, 321, 445, 19697, 670, 4361, 45298, 30, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 115782, "start": 1175.3799999999999, "end": 1177.4199999999998, "text": " It is a very tempting move to make.", "tokens": [51243, 467, 307, 257, 588, 37900, 1286, 281, 652, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 115782, "start": 1177.8799999999999, "end": 1180.22, "text": " In academia, we call that a flattening move.", "tokens": [51368, 682, 28937, 11, 321, 818, 300, 257, 24183, 278, 1286, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 115782, "start": 1180.46, "end": 1181.9199999999998, "text": " You look at three different fields.", "tokens": [51497, 509, 574, 412, 1045, 819, 7909, 13, 51570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14077006704438993, "compression_ratio": 1.6450511945392492, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047210419482653e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 118192, "start": 1181.92, "end": 1183.8200000000002, "text": " Notice they all agree that boundaries are active.", "tokens": [50365, 13428, 436, 439, 3986, 300, 13180, 366, 4967, 13, 50460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 118192, "start": 1183.98, "end": 1188.42, "text": " And you say, look, they must all be pointing to the same underlying universal mechanism.", "tokens": [50468, 400, 291, 584, 11, 574, 11, 436, 1633, 439, 312, 12166, 281, 264, 912, 14217, 11455, 7513, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 118192, "start": 1188.74, "end": 1190.8600000000001, "text": " Let's just call it an active boundary and move on.", "tokens": [50706, 961, 311, 445, 818, 309, 364, 4967, 12866, 293, 1286, 322, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 118192, "start": 1190.98, "end": 1192.2, "text": " Exactly. Why not just do that?", "tokens": [50818, 7587, 13, 1545, 406, 445, 360, 300, 30, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 118192, "start": 1192.38, "end": 1196.02, "text": " But Flicksheen's paper argues vehemently against this.", "tokens": [50888, 583, 3235, 618, 9611, 268, 311, 3035, 38218, 4221, 1712, 356, 1970, 341, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 118192, "start": 1196.0800000000002, "end": 1196.22, "text": " What?", "tokens": [51073, 708, 30, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 118192, "start": 1196.44, "end": 1202.3000000000002, "text": " Because they are a category of computational objects, but they have non-interchangeable implementations.", "tokens": [51091, 1436, 436, 366, 257, 7719, 295, 28270, 6565, 11, 457, 436, 362, 2107, 12, 5106, 15431, 712, 4445, 763, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 118192, "start": 1202.72, "end": 1204.96, "text": " They are not the same operation under the hood.", "tokens": [51405, 814, 366, 406, 264, 912, 6916, 833, 264, 13376, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 118192, "start": 1205.14, "end": 1205.8200000000002, "text": " Prove it to me.", "tokens": [51526, 1705, 303, 309, 281, 385, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 118192, "start": 1206.66, "end": 1208.0800000000002, "text": " Mechanically, how do they differ?", "tokens": [51602, 30175, 984, 11, 577, 360, 436, 743, 30, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694473000459893, "compression_ratio": 1.635135135135135, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130242978639297e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 120808, "start": 1208.08, "end": 1213.4399999999998, "text": " The easiest way to see the difference is to look at how each boundary is evaluated against time.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 12889, 636, 281, 536, 264, 2649, 307, 281, 574, 412, 577, 1184, 12866, 307, 25509, 1970, 565, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833904770185361, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 120808, "start": 1214.32, "end": 1217.36, "text": " Fristin's Markov blanket is evaluated synchronically.", "tokens": [50677, 1526, 468, 259, 311, 3934, 5179, 17907, 307, 25509, 19331, 984, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833904770185361, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 120808, "start": 1217.4199999999998, "end": 1219.22, "text": " Meaning at a single snapshot in time?", "tokens": [50832, 19948, 412, 257, 2167, 30163, 294, 565, 30, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833904770185361, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 120808, "start": 1219.46, "end": 1219.8, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [50934, 12753, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833904770185361, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 120808, "start": 1220.1, "end": 1228.02, "text": " It looks at the current joint state of the system right now and asks what variables are screened off from what other variables right now.", "tokens": [50966, 467, 1542, 412, 264, 2190, 7225, 1785, 295, 264, 1185, 558, 586, 293, 8962, 437, 9102, 366, 2568, 292, 766, 490, 437, 661, 9102, 558, 586, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833904770185361, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 120808, "start": 1228.24, "end": 1234.3799999999999, "text": " It assumes absolutely nothing about where the system came from, and it has no stored target of where the system is going.", "tokens": [51373, 467, 37808, 3122, 1825, 466, 689, 264, 1185, 1361, 490, 11, 293, 309, 575, 572, 12187, 3779, 295, 689, 264, 1185, 307, 516, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12833904770185361, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 123438, "start": 1234.38, "end": 1239.6200000000001, "text": " Right. The blind club goers only care about the bouncer's face in this exact millisecond.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 440, 6865, 6482, 352, 433, 787, 1127, 466, 264, 272, 14296, 311, 1851, 294, 341, 1900, 27940, 18882, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14855227532324852, "compression_ratio": 1.4528301886792452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132590276342728e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 123438, "start": 1240.0400000000002, "end": 1245.68, "text": " Levin's bioelectric boundary, on the other hand, is evaluated against a state the system does not yet occupy.", "tokens": [50648, 1456, 4796, 311, 12198, 33243, 12866, 11, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 307, 25509, 1970, 257, 1785, 264, 1185, 775, 406, 1939, 30645, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14855227532324852, "compression_ratio": 1.4528301886792452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132590276342728e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 123438, "start": 1245.8400000000001, "end": 1246.5600000000002, "text": " Because of the blueprint.", "tokens": [50938, 1436, 295, 264, 35868, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14855227532324852, "compression_ratio": 1.4528301886792452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132590276342728e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 123438, "start": 1246.8400000000001, "end": 1252.4, "text": " Exactly. It inherently requires a stored target morphology. It is future-oriented.", "tokens": [50988, 7587, 13, 467, 27993, 7029, 257, 12187, 3779, 25778, 1793, 13, 467, 307, 2027, 12, 27414, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14855227532324852, "compression_ratio": 1.4528301886792452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132590276342728e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 125240, "start": 1252.4, "end": 1261.2, "text": " And the RSVP admissibility deletion is evaluated diachronically over a historical timeline of accumulated irreversible commitments.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 5910, 891, 2841, 1103, 302, 313, 307, 25509, 1026, 608, 2044, 984, 670, 257, 8584, 12933, 295, 31346, 16014, 840, 964, 26230, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12192110220591228, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604513345201076e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 125240, "start": 1261.68, "end": 1261.72, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50829, 1033, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12192110220591228, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604513345201076e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 125240, "start": 1261.8600000000001, "end": 1268.74, "text": " It requires no stored target and no current joint state, only a strict record of what has been permanently removed from the option space.", "tokens": [50838, 467, 7029, 572, 12187, 3779, 293, 572, 2190, 7225, 1785, 11, 787, 257, 10910, 2136, 295, 437, 575, 668, 24042, 7261, 490, 264, 3614, 1901, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12192110220591228, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604513345201076e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 125240, "start": 1269.0600000000002, "end": 1273.1200000000001, "text": " Okay, so they are operating on completely different axes of time and purpose.", "tokens": [51198, 1033, 11, 370, 436, 366, 7447, 322, 2584, 819, 35387, 295, 565, 293, 4334, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12192110220591228, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604513345201076e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 125240, "start": 1273.8400000000001, "end": 1276.8400000000001, "text": " Snapshot, future target, and historical deletion.", "tokens": [51437, 9264, 2382, 12194, 11, 2027, 3779, 11, 293, 8584, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12192110220591228, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604513345201076e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 127684, "start": 1276.84, "end": 1280.54, "text": " But in your notes, you said they actually conflict with each other.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 428, 5570, 11, 291, 848, 436, 767, 6596, 365, 1184, 661, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11722501118977864, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281900736854094e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 127684, "start": 1280.72, "end": 1284.76, "text": " If they're just different tools in a toolbox, why would they conflict? Where is the friction?", "tokens": [50559, 759, 436, 434, 445, 819, 3873, 294, 257, 44593, 11, 983, 576, 436, 6596, 30, 2305, 307, 264, 17710, 30, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11722501118977864, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281900736854094e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 127684, "start": 1285.24, "end": 1291.72, "text": " The friction is explicitly stated in the source theory between RSVP refusal and Friston's free energy minimization.", "tokens": [50785, 440, 17710, 307, 20803, 11323, 294, 264, 4009, 5261, 1296, 25855, 53, 47, 48948, 293, 1526, 47345, 311, 1737, 2281, 4464, 2144, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11722501118977864, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281900736854094e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 127684, "start": 1292.5, "end": 1298.6, "text": " They are formally, mathematically incompatible if you try to run them in the same system simultaneously.", "tokens": [51148, 814, 366, 25983, 11, 44003, 40393, 267, 964, 498, 291, 853, 281, 1190, 552, 294, 264, 912, 1185, 16561, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11722501118977864, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281900736854094e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 127684, "start": 1298.8999999999999, "end": 1301.6, "text": " How can they be incompatible? Walk me through a scenario.", "tokens": [51468, 1012, 393, 436, 312, 40393, 267, 964, 30, 10818, 385, 807, 257, 9005, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11722501118977864, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281900736854094e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 127684, "start": 1301.74, "end": 1303.22, "text": " Let's go back to what refusal does.", "tokens": [51610, 961, 311, 352, 646, 281, 437, 48948, 775, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11722501118977864, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281900736854094e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 130322, "start": 1303.22, "end": 1308.1200000000001, "text": " It permanently excludes a trajectory by setting its probability to absolute zero.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 24042, 16269, 279, 257, 21512, 538, 3287, 1080, 8482, 281, 8236, 4018, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1233659553527832, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735415357862048e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 130322, "start": 1309.0, "end": 1313.94, "text": " Now, imagine a system operating under Friston's rules trying to minimize surprise.", "tokens": [50654, 823, 11, 3811, 257, 1185, 7447, 833, 1526, 47345, 311, 4474, 1382, 281, 17522, 6365, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1233659553527832, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735415357862048e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 130322, "start": 1314.78, "end": 1323.4, "text": " And imagine there is a specific trajectory that has a very high prior probability and represents a very low expected surprise under the agent's generative model.", "tokens": [50943, 400, 3811, 456, 307, 257, 2685, 21512, 300, 575, 257, 588, 1090, 4059, 8482, 293, 8855, 257, 588, 2295, 5176, 6365, 833, 264, 9461, 311, 1337, 1166, 2316, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1233659553527832, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735415357862048e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 130322, "start": 1323.58, "end": 1331.4, "text": " Like a deeply ingrained habit, an action that makes total sense, is highly rewarding, and would be very predictable and safe for the agent to take.", "tokens": [51383, 1743, 257, 8760, 3957, 31774, 7164, 11, 364, 3069, 300, 1669, 3217, 2020, 11, 307, 5405, 20063, 11, 293, 576, 312, 588, 27737, 293, 3273, 337, 264, 9461, 281, 747, 13, 51774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1233659553527832, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735415357862048e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 133140, "start": 1331.4, "end": 1335.46, "text": " Let's say a smoker reaching for a cigarette when they're stressed.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 257, 899, 16722, 9906, 337, 257, 26184, 562, 436, 434, 14471, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 133140, "start": 1335.7, "end": 1336.48, "text": " Perfect example.", "tokens": [50580, 10246, 1365, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 133140, "start": 1337.38, "end": 1343.1000000000001, "text": " Under Friston's free energy principle, reaching for that cigarette minimizes surprise.", "tokens": [50664, 6974, 1526, 47345, 311, 1737, 2281, 8665, 11, 9906, 337, 300, 26184, 4464, 5660, 6365, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 133140, "start": 1343.94, "end": 1347.8200000000002, "text": " It returns the system to an expected stable internal state.", "tokens": [50992, 467, 11247, 264, 1185, 281, 364, 5176, 8351, 6920, 1785, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 133140, "start": 1347.98, "end": 1348.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51194, 1779, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 133140, "start": 1348.4, "end": 1351.38, "text": " Now, imagine the agent exercises RSVP refusal.", "tokens": [51215, 823, 11, 3811, 264, 9461, 11900, 25855, 53, 47, 48948, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 133140, "start": 1351.8600000000001, "end": 1354.74, "text": " They decide to permanently delete that option.", "tokens": [51388, 814, 4536, 281, 24042, 12097, 300, 3614, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 133140, "start": 1355.26, "end": 1358.1000000000001, "text": " I am a non-smoker now. That path is zeroed out.", "tokens": [51558, 286, 669, 257, 2107, 12, 10817, 16722, 586, 13, 663, 3100, 307, 4018, 292, 484, 13, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 133140, "start": 1358.3000000000002, "end": 1359.9, "text": " Okay. What happens to the math?", "tokens": [51710, 1033, 13, 708, 2314, 281, 264, 5221, 30, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20229325727982955, "compression_ratio": 1.5451127819548873, "no_speech_prob": 1.661735419405952e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 135990, "start": 1359.9, "end": 1363.02, "text": " According to Friston's model, doing that is catastrophic.", "tokens": [50365, 7328, 281, 1526, 47345, 311, 2316, 11, 884, 300, 307, 34915, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10339883300993177, "compression_ratio": 1.5753424657534247, "no_speech_prob": 1.2439865760757729e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 135990, "start": 1363.76, "end": 1374.4, "text": " By deleting a low surprise option, you dramatically increase the expected free energy of the system, because you are removing a perfectly good, mathematically optimal way to minimize surprise.", "tokens": [50558, 3146, 48946, 257, 2295, 6365, 3614, 11, 291, 17548, 3488, 264, 5176, 1737, 2281, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 570, 291, 366, 12720, 257, 6239, 665, 11, 44003, 16252, 636, 281, 17522, 6365, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10339883300993177, "compression_ratio": 1.5753424657534247, "no_speech_prob": 1.2439865760757729e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 135990, "start": 1374.74, "end": 1378.74, "text": " And the bouncer isn't giving you any new information that says cigarettes don't exist anymore.", "tokens": [51107, 400, 264, 272, 14296, 1943, 380, 2902, 291, 604, 777, 1589, 300, 1619, 29244, 500, 380, 2514, 3602, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10339883300993177, "compression_ratio": 1.5753424657534247, "no_speech_prob": 1.2439865760757729e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 137874, "start": 1378.74, "end": 1389.68, "text": " Exactly. A specific operation that zeroes out support-like refusal is fundamentally different from an operation that merely reweights probabilities over a fixed model, which is inference.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 316, 2685, 6916, 300, 4018, 279, 484, 1406, 12, 4092, 48948, 307, 17879, 819, 490, 364, 6916, 300, 17003, 319, 826, 5761, 33783, 670, 257, 6806, 2316, 11, 597, 307, 38253, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10953840716131802, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 1.66787948469721e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 137874, "start": 1390.2, "end": 1391.3, "text": " The math literally breaks.", "tokens": [50938, 440, 5221, 3736, 9857, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10953840716131802, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 1.66787948469721e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 137874, "start": 1391.56, "end": 1391.72, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51006, 876, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10953840716131802, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 1.66787948469721e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 137874, "start": 1391.84, "end": 1398.52, "text": " The only way you can make them compatible on paper is if you force the free energy model to include what are called latent commitment variable.", "tokens": [51020, 440, 787, 636, 291, 393, 652, 552, 18218, 322, 3035, 307, 498, 291, 3464, 264, 1737, 2281, 2316, 281, 4090, 437, 366, 1219, 48994, 8371, 7006, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10953840716131802, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 1.66787948469721e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 137874, "start": 1398.64, "end": 1400.02, "text": " What is a latent commitment variable?", "tokens": [51360, 708, 307, 257, 48994, 8371, 7006, 30, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10953840716131802, "compression_ratio": 1.639344262295082, "no_speech_prob": 1.66787948469721e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 140002, "start": 1400.02, "end": 1408.58, "text": " You have to artificially inject hidden variables into the Bayesian model, things like my identity as a non-smoker or social role stability.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 281, 39905, 2270, 10711, 7633, 9102, 666, 264, 7840, 42434, 2316, 11, 721, 411, 452, 6575, 382, 257, 2107, 12, 10817, 16722, 420, 2093, 3090, 11826, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12584698416969992, "compression_ratio": 1.5029585798816567, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756374491751826e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 140002, "start": 1408.58, "end": 1415.56, "text": " You have to rig the math so that the previously low surprise trajectory of smoking suddenly becomes high surprise.", "tokens": [50793, 509, 362, 281, 8329, 264, 5221, 370, 300, 264, 8046, 2295, 6365, 21512, 295, 14055, 5800, 3643, 1090, 6365, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12584698416969992, "compression_ratio": 1.5029585798816567, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756374491751826e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 141556, "start": 1415.56, "end": 1419.28, "text": " Because taking it would destabilize those new hidden invariants.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 1940, 309, 576, 2677, 5177, 1125, 729, 777, 7633, 33270, 1719, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08961244190440458, "compression_ratio": 1.4752475247524752, "no_speech_prob": 1.911693459782926e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 141556, "start": 1419.44, "end": 1430.3799999999999, "text": " Right. But doing that requires extending the generative model with exactly the kind of diachronic history tracking structure that a Markov blanket simply does not possess on its own.", "tokens": [50559, 1779, 13, 583, 884, 300, 7029, 24360, 264, 1337, 1166, 2316, 365, 2293, 264, 733, 295, 1026, 608, 10011, 2503, 11603, 3877, 300, 257, 3934, 5179, 17907, 2935, 775, 406, 17490, 322, 1080, 1065, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08961244190440458, "compression_ratio": 1.4752475247524752, "no_speech_prob": 1.911693459782926e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 141556, "start": 1430.7, "end": 1433.1399999999999, "text": " You have to cheat the math to make them play nice.", "tokens": [51122, 509, 362, 281, 17470, 264, 5221, 281, 652, 552, 862, 1481, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08961244190440458, "compression_ratio": 1.4752475247524752, "no_speech_prob": 1.911693459782926e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 143314, "start": 1433.14, "end": 1437.0800000000002, "text": " You do. Which proves they really are fundamentally different mechanics.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 360, 13, 3013, 25019, 436, 534, 366, 17879, 819, 12939, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238870584739829, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491447100807187e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 143314, "start": 1437.5800000000002, "end": 1439.76, "text": " They are a category, not a single metaphor.", "tokens": [50587, 814, 366, 257, 7719, 11, 406, 257, 2167, 19157, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238870584739829, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491447100807187e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 143314, "start": 1440.5800000000002, "end": 1448.38, "text": " A system could exhibit statistical screening without any bioelectric pursuit, or it could pursue a target without topological deletion.", "tokens": [50737, 316, 1185, 727, 20487, 22820, 17732, 1553, 604, 12198, 33243, 23365, 11, 420, 309, 727, 12392, 257, 3779, 1553, 1192, 4383, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238870584739829, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491447100807187e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 143314, "start": 1448.92, "end": 1456.5200000000002, "text": " Treating them all as just one vague idea of an active boundary completely fails to predict how these systems will actually behave under stress.", "tokens": [51154, 20298, 278, 552, 439, 382, 445, 472, 24247, 1558, 295, 364, 4967, 12866, 2584, 18199, 281, 6069, 577, 613, 3652, 486, 767, 15158, 833, 4244, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238870584739829, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491447100807187e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 143314, "start": 1456.7, "end": 1459.96, "text": " So let's bring this down to earth. What does this all mean for you, listening to this?", "tokens": [51543, 407, 718, 311, 1565, 341, 760, 281, 4120, 13, 708, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 291, 11, 4764, 281, 341, 30, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238870584739829, "compression_ratio": 1.6174496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491447100807187e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 145996, "start": 1459.96, "end": 1463.16, "text": " Why should you care about Markov blankets and RSVP theory?", "tokens": [50365, 1545, 820, 291, 1127, 466, 3934, 5179, 38710, 293, 25855, 53, 47, 5261, 30, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1046417470563922, "compression_ratio": 1.6437908496732025, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622631869398941e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 145996, "start": 1463.3, "end": 1464.24, "text": " It's a fair question.", "tokens": [50532, 467, 311, 257, 3143, 1168, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1046417470563922, "compression_ratio": 1.6437908496732025, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622631869398941e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 145996, "start": 1464.52, "end": 1478.68, "text": " Because whether you are a doctor looking at a cell trying to repair itself, or an engineer prompting an AI model, or just a person examining your own psychological boundaries, treating a boundary as inert geometry, is going to fail you.", "tokens": [50593, 1436, 1968, 291, 366, 257, 4631, 1237, 412, 257, 2815, 1382, 281, 10535, 2564, 11, 420, 364, 11403, 12391, 278, 364, 7318, 2316, 11, 420, 445, 257, 954, 34662, 428, 1065, 14346, 13180, 11, 15083, 257, 12866, 382, 25832, 18426, 11, 307, 516, 281, 3061, 291, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1046417470563922, "compression_ratio": 1.6437908496732025, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622631869398941e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 145996, "start": 1478.78, "end": 1479.22, "text": " Absolutely.", "tokens": [51306, 7021, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1046417470563922, "compression_ratio": 1.6437908496732025, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622631869398941e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 145996, "start": 1479.6200000000001, "end": 1488.1200000000001, "text": " If you think your boundaries are just passive walls you put up to keep the bad stuff out, you are completely missing the computational work they are doing behind the scenes.", "tokens": [51348, 759, 291, 519, 428, 13180, 366, 445, 14975, 7920, 291, 829, 493, 281, 1066, 264, 1578, 1507, 484, 11, 291, 366, 2584, 5361, 264, 28270, 589, 436, 366, 884, 2261, 264, 8026, 13, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1046417470563922, "compression_ratio": 1.6437908496732025, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622631869398941e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 148812, "start": 1488.12, "end": 1492.9399999999998, "text": " Are your boundaries just screening out noise to minimize your daily surprise?", "tokens": [50365, 2014, 428, 13180, 445, 17732, 484, 5658, 281, 17522, 428, 5212, 6365, 30, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969197470566322, "compression_ratio": 1.61198738170347, "no_speech_prob": 1.2645016327431091e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 148812, "start": 1493.36, "end": 1498.3999999999999, "text": " Are they actively pulling you toward a target morphology of who you want to be five years from now?", "tokens": [50627, 2014, 436, 13022, 8407, 291, 7361, 257, 3779, 25778, 1793, 295, 567, 291, 528, 281, 312, 1732, 924, 490, 586, 30, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969197470566322, "compression_ratio": 1.61198738170347, "no_speech_prob": 1.2645016327431091e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 148812, "start": 1498.6599999999999, "end": 1505.2199999999998, "text": " Or are they topological deletions, permanently refusing certain futures so you can force yourself down a narrower path?", "tokens": [50892, 1610, 366, 436, 1192, 4383, 1103, 302, 626, 11, 24042, 37289, 1629, 26071, 370, 291, 393, 3464, 1803, 760, 257, 46751, 3100, 30, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969197470566322, "compression_ratio": 1.61198738170347, "no_speech_prob": 1.2645016327431091e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 148812, "start": 1505.6399999999999, "end": 1508.82, "text": " That is a very powerful, practical way to apply the framework.", "tokens": [51241, 663, 307, 257, 588, 4005, 11, 8496, 636, 281, 3079, 264, 8388, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969197470566322, "compression_ratio": 1.61198738170347, "no_speech_prob": 1.2645016327431091e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 148812, "start": 1508.9599999999998, "end": 1510.6, "text": " You have to identify the computation.", "tokens": [51407, 509, 362, 281, 5876, 264, 24903, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969197470566322, "compression_ratio": 1.61198738170347, "no_speech_prob": 1.2645016327431091e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 148812, "start": 1510.82, "end": 1515.06, "text": " If you don't know which mechanism your system is running, you do not actually understand your own system.", "tokens": [51500, 759, 291, 500, 380, 458, 597, 7513, 428, 1185, 307, 2614, 11, 291, 360, 406, 767, 1223, 428, 1065, 1185, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969197470566322, "compression_ratio": 1.61198738170347, "no_speech_prob": 1.2645016327431091e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 148812, "start": 1515.1, "end": 1515.4399999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51714, 1779, 13, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09969197470566322, "compression_ratio": 1.61198738170347, "no_speech_prob": 1.2645016327431091e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 151544, "start": 1515.44, "end": 1526.0800000000002, "text": " That is a massive paradigm shift, but it provides the perfect transition into part two of our deep dive, the brevity trap or the compression fallacy.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 5994, 24709, 5513, 11, 457, 309, 6417, 264, 2176, 6034, 666, 644, 732, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 11, 264, 1403, 23110, 11487, 420, 264, 19355, 2100, 2551, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054035005115327, "compression_ratio": 1.6968641114982579, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273210434748163e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 151544, "start": 1526.54, "end": 1528.5, "text": " This is where things get really controversial.", "tokens": [50920, 639, 307, 689, 721, 483, 534, 17323, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054035005115327, "compression_ratio": 1.6968641114982579, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273210434748163e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 151544, "start": 1528.88, "end": 1542.18, "text": " Because if we accept that boundaries are active computers, defining what a system is and what it is permitted to become, the very next logical question has to be, how do we measure the information that actually makes it inside that boundary?", "tokens": [51037, 1436, 498, 321, 3241, 300, 13180, 366, 4967, 10807, 11, 17827, 437, 257, 1185, 307, 293, 437, 309, 307, 28658, 281, 1813, 11, 264, 588, 958, 14978, 1168, 575, 281, 312, 11, 577, 360, 321, 3481, 264, 1589, 300, 767, 1669, 309, 1854, 300, 12866, 30, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054035005115327, "compression_ratio": 1.6968641114982579, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273210434748163e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 151544, "start": 1542.4, "end": 1544.7, "text": " How do we evaluate what a system actually knows?", "tokens": [51713, 1012, 360, 321, 13059, 437, 257, 1185, 767, 3255, 30, 51828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054035005115327, "compression_ratio": 1.6968641114982579, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273210434748163e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 154470, "start": 1544.7, "end": 1550.04, "text": " And this is where we run into perhaps the most pervasive cognitive bias in modern science and engineering.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 689, 321, 1190, 666, 4317, 264, 881, 680, 39211, 15605, 12577, 294, 4363, 3497, 293, 7043, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18648718021534108, "compression_ratio": 1.3860759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879056746049725e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 154470, "start": 1550.26, "end": 1550.3600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50643, 1779, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18648718021534108, "compression_ratio": 1.3860759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879056746049725e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 154470, "start": 1550.5800000000002, "end": 1555.6200000000001, "text": " My instinct, and I think the instinct of almost everyone listening, is to look for simplicity.", "tokens": [50659, 1222, 16556, 11, 293, 286, 519, 264, 16556, 295, 1920, 1518, 4764, 11, 307, 281, 574, 337, 25632, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18648718021534108, "compression_ratio": 1.3860759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879056746049725e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 154470, "start": 1555.88, "end": 1556.3600000000001, "text": " Of course.", "tokens": [50924, 2720, 1164, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18648718021534108, "compression_ratio": 1.3860759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879056746049725e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 155636, "start": 1556.36, "end": 1563.6999999999998, "text": " If a system produces a massive, sprawling, chaotic explanation for something, we assume it's confused.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 1185, 14725, 257, 5994, 11, 22734, 1688, 11, 27013, 10835, 337, 746, 11, 321, 6552, 309, 311, 9019, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11870133876800537, "compression_ratio": 1.7564102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920900665530868e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 155636, "start": 1564.1399999999999, "end": 1572.6599999999999, "text": " But if we look at the smallest, tightest, most elegant piece of code or explanation the system produces, we say, ah, it truly understands.", "tokens": [50754, 583, 498, 321, 574, 412, 264, 16998, 11, 4524, 377, 11, 881, 21117, 2522, 295, 3089, 420, 10835, 264, 1185, 14725, 11, 321, 584, 11, 3716, 11, 309, 4908, 15146, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11870133876800537, "compression_ratio": 1.7564102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920900665530868e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 155636, "start": 1573.12, "end": 1576.82, "text": " We assume that if you can explain something simply, you understand it perfectly.", "tokens": [51203, 492, 6552, 300, 498, 291, 393, 2903, 746, 2935, 11, 291, 1223, 309, 6239, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11870133876800537, "compression_ratio": 1.7564102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920900665530868e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 155636, "start": 1576.9799999999998, "end": 1578.28, "text": " Keep it simple, stupid.", "tokens": [51396, 5527, 309, 2199, 11, 6631, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11870133876800537, "compression_ratio": 1.7564102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920900665530868e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 155636, "start": 1578.56, "end": 1581.4799999999998, "text": " If you can't explain to a six-year-old, you don't understand it.", "tokens": [51475, 759, 291, 393, 380, 2903, 281, 257, 2309, 12, 5294, 12, 2641, 11, 291, 500, 380, 1223, 309, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11870133876800537, "compression_ratio": 1.7564102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920900665530868e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 158148, "start": 1581.48, "end": 1583.68, "text": " We hear these platitudes constantly.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1568, 613, 3403, 16451, 6460, 13, 50475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14300185203552246, "compression_ratio": 1.3836477987421383, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279235767914125e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 158148, "start": 1583.88, "end": 1586.44, "text": " We have deeply conflated compression with understanding.", "tokens": [50485, 492, 362, 8760, 1497, 38539, 19355, 365, 3701, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14300185203552246, "compression_ratio": 1.3836477987421383, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279235767914125e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 158148, "start": 1586.94, "end": 1594.42, "text": " And the second paper in Flyxion's stack proves, with rigorous mathematics, exactly why that assumption is a dangerous fallacy.", "tokens": [50638, 400, 264, 1150, 3035, 11, 682, 3423, 4105, 37649, 11, 25019, 11, 365, 29882, 18666, 11, 2293, 983, 300, 15302, 307, 257, 5795, 2100, 2551, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14300185203552246, "compression_ratio": 1.3836477987421383, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279235767914125e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 159442, "start": 1594.42, "end": 1602.76, "text": " The paper starts by referencing an older, very famous idea from computer science, Daniel Hillis' definition of information content.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 3719, 538, 40582, 364, 4906, 11, 588, 4618, 1558, 490, 3820, 3497, 11, 8033, 9109, 271, 6, 7123, 295, 1589, 2701, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803192016926218, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547506416665248e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 159442, "start": 1603.0600000000002, "end": 1603.78, "text": " Yes, Hillis.", "tokens": [50797, 1079, 11, 9109, 271, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803192016926218, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547506416665248e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 159442, "start": 1604.0600000000002, "end": 1606.64, "text": " Echoing the earlier work of Andrei Kolmogorov.", "tokens": [50847, 31887, 278, 264, 3071, 589, 295, 400, 10271, 26137, 76, 664, 284, 5179, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803192016926218, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547506416665248e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 159442, "start": 1607.0, "end": 1612.02, "text": " In the 1960s, Kolmogorov formulated what we now call Kolmogorov complexity.", "tokens": [50994, 682, 264, 16157, 82, 11, 26137, 76, 664, 284, 5179, 48936, 437, 321, 586, 818, 26137, 76, 664, 284, 5179, 14024, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803192016926218, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547506416665248e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 159442, "start": 1612.5600000000002, "end": 1615.5600000000002, "text": " It's a measure of the algorithmic complexity of an object.", "tokens": [51272, 467, 311, 257, 3481, 295, 264, 9284, 299, 14024, 295, 364, 2657, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803192016926218, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547506416665248e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 159442, "start": 1615.76, "end": 1615.88, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51432, 1033, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15803192016926218, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547506416665248e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 161588, "start": 1615.88, "end": 1617.44, "text": " Hillis summarized it beautifully.", "tokens": [50365, 9109, 271, 14611, 1602, 309, 16525, 13, 50443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 161588, "start": 1617.9, "end": 1624.94, "text": " He said the amount of information in a pattern of bits is equal to the length of the shortest computer program capable of generating those bits.", "tokens": [50466, 634, 848, 264, 2372, 295, 1589, 294, 257, 5102, 295, 9239, 307, 2681, 281, 264, 4641, 295, 264, 31875, 3820, 1461, 8189, 295, 17746, 729, 9239, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 161588, "start": 1625.24, "end": 1628.6200000000001, "text": " Okay, let's give an example of Kolmogorov complexity, just so we're all on the same page.", "tokens": [50833, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 976, 364, 1365, 295, 26137, 76, 664, 284, 5179, 14024, 11, 445, 370, 321, 434, 439, 322, 264, 912, 3028, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 161588, "start": 1629.66, "end": 1635.44, "text": " If I have a string of a million alternating ones, and zeros, one, zero, one, zero, we owe ten, what about a ten?", "tokens": [51054, 759, 286, 362, 257, 6798, 295, 257, 2459, 40062, 2306, 11, 293, 35193, 11, 472, 11, 4018, 11, 472, 11, 4018, 11, 321, 16655, 2064, 11, 437, 466, 257, 2064, 30, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 161588, "start": 1635.6000000000001, "end": 1637.6200000000001, "text": " I don't need a million characters to describe it.", "tokens": [51351, 286, 500, 380, 643, 257, 2459, 4342, 281, 6786, 309, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 161588, "start": 1637.7, "end": 1637.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51456, 1779, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 161588, "start": 1638.0600000000002, "end": 1641.8000000000002, "text": " I could just write a tiny program that says, print ten 500,000 times.", "tokens": [51474, 286, 727, 445, 2464, 257, 5870, 1461, 300, 1619, 11, 4482, 2064, 5923, 11, 1360, 1413, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 161588, "start": 1641.92, "end": 1642.18, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51667, 865, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 161588, "start": 1642.5400000000002, "end": 1643.94, "text": " The string is highly compressible.", "tokens": [51698, 440, 6798, 307, 5405, 14778, 964, 13, 51768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14870463121657404, "compression_ratio": 1.6194690265486726, "no_speech_prob": 1.4957626066555707e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 164394, "start": 1643.94, "end": 1649.6200000000001, "text": " Exactly. Because it has a regular, predictable pattern, its Kolmogorov complexity is very low.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 1436, 309, 575, 257, 3890, 11, 27737, 5102, 11, 1080, 26137, 76, 664, 284, 5179, 14024, 307, 588, 2295, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08128211281516336, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028173816859943e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 164394, "start": 1650.0, "end": 1655.44, "text": " But if you have a string of a million completely random, unpatterned coin flips, there is no shortcut.", "tokens": [50668, 583, 498, 291, 362, 257, 6798, 295, 257, 2459, 2584, 4974, 11, 20994, 1161, 9232, 11464, 40249, 11, 456, 307, 572, 24822, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08128211281516336, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028173816859943e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 164394, "start": 1655.64, "end": 1656.5800000000002, "text": " You just have to list them all.", "tokens": [50950, 509, 445, 362, 281, 1329, 552, 439, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08128211281516336, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028173816859943e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 164394, "start": 1656.74, "end": 1663.44, "text": " Right. The shortest program to generate that string is essentially just a giant print statement containing the string itself.", "tokens": [51005, 1779, 13, 440, 31875, 1461, 281, 8460, 300, 6798, 307, 4476, 445, 257, 7410, 4482, 5629, 19273, 264, 6798, 2564, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08128211281516336, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028173816859943e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 164394, "start": 1663.92, "end": 1666.54, "text": " It is incompressible. Its complexity is high.", "tokens": [51364, 467, 307, 40393, 735, 964, 13, 6953, 14024, 307, 1090, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08128211281516336, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028173816859943e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 164394, "start": 1666.6200000000001, "end": 1668.88, "text": " That makes total sense as a way to measure data.", "tokens": [51499, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 382, 257, 636, 281, 3481, 1412, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08128211281516336, "compression_ratio": 1.6245487364620939, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028173816859943e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 166888, "start": 1668.88, "end": 1677.5, "text": " But the paper points out that the broader culture took this mathematical definition and, well, twisted it into an epistemology.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 3035, 2793, 484, 300, 264, 13227, 3713, 1890, 341, 18894, 7123, 293, 11, 731, 11, 23057, 309, 666, 364, 2388, 43958, 1793, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10422205650943449, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667012179434002e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 166888, "start": 1677.88, "end": 1680.2800000000002, "text": " They took a massive, unjustified step further.", "tokens": [50815, 814, 1890, 257, 5994, 11, 37046, 2587, 1823, 3052, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10422205650943449, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667012179434002e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 166888, "start": 1680.8200000000002, "end": 1686.44, "text": " Especially in computer science, machine learning, and even physics, there arose this implicit assumption.", "tokens": [50962, 8545, 294, 3820, 3497, 11, 3479, 2539, 11, 293, 754, 10649, 11, 456, 37192, 341, 26947, 15302, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10422205650943449, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667012179434002e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 166888, "start": 1687.0, "end": 1694.72, "text": " A system which produces a shorter description of a domain has thereby understood that domain better than a system producing a longer description.", "tokens": [51271, 316, 1185, 597, 14725, 257, 11639, 3855, 295, 257, 9274, 575, 28281, 7320, 300, 9274, 1101, 813, 257, 1185, 10501, 257, 2854, 3855, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10422205650943449, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667012179434002e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 169472, "start": 1694.72, "end": 1698.1000000000001, "text": " A compressed model is presumed to be a deeper, truer model.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 30353, 2316, 307, 18028, 292, 281, 312, 257, 7731, 11, 504, 5486, 2316, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11995235933076351, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735435957703325e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 169472, "start": 1698.34, "end": 1701.42, "text": " Yes. And the paper sets out to dismantle this mathematically.", "tokens": [50546, 1079, 13, 400, 264, 3035, 6352, 484, 281, 30506, 306, 341, 44003, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11995235933076351, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735435957703325e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 169472, "start": 1701.92, "end": 1705.4, "text": " To do this, it introduces a framework called the ontological triple.", "tokens": [50725, 1407, 360, 341, 11, 309, 31472, 257, 8388, 1219, 264, 6592, 4383, 15508, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11995235933076351, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735435957703325e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 169472, "start": 1705.64, "end": 1708.7, "text": " Okay. I'm going to need you to walk us through the math of misunderstanding here.", "tokens": [50911, 1033, 13, 286, 478, 516, 281, 643, 291, 281, 1792, 505, 807, 264, 5221, 295, 29227, 510, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11995235933076351, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735435957703325e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 169472, "start": 1709.0, "end": 1710.46, "text": " What is an ontological triple?", "tokens": [51079, 708, 307, 364, 6592, 4383, 15508, 30, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11995235933076351, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735435957703325e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 169472, "start": 1710.6000000000001, "end": 1715.24, "text": " An ontological triple is a formal way of defining how any system represents the world.", "tokens": [51159, 1107, 6592, 4383, 15508, 307, 257, 9860, 636, 295, 17827, 577, 604, 1185, 8855, 264, 1002, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11995235933076351, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735435957703325e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 169472, "start": 1715.72, "end": 1717.7, "text": " It consists of three interlocking elements.", "tokens": [51415, 467, 14689, 295, 1045, 728, 4102, 278, 4959, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11995235933076351, "compression_ratio": 1.688715953307393, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735435957703325e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 171770, "start": 1717.7, "end": 1720.32, "text": " First, you have the domain. Let's call it X.", "tokens": [50365, 2386, 11, 291, 362, 264, 9274, 13, 961, 311, 818, 309, 1783, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 171770, "start": 1720.6200000000001, "end": 1724.16, "text": " This is the raw set of objects, items, or phenomena you are trying to describe.", "tokens": [50511, 639, 307, 264, 8936, 992, 295, 6565, 11, 4754, 11, 420, 22004, 291, 366, 1382, 281, 6786, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 171770, "start": 1724.48, "end": 1725.76, "text": " Let's use a tangible example.", "tokens": [50704, 961, 311, 764, 257, 27094, 1365, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 171770, "start": 1726.0800000000002, "end": 1730.9, "text": " Let's say my domain is my massive, disorganized collection of vintage vinyl records.", "tokens": [50784, 961, 311, 584, 452, 9274, 307, 452, 5994, 11, 717, 12372, 1602, 5765, 295, 23050, 25226, 7724, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 171770, "start": 1731.02, "end": 1733.16, "text": " Perfect. So X is the physical records.", "tokens": [51031, 10246, 13, 407, 1783, 307, 264, 4001, 7724, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 171770, "start": 1733.52, "end": 1736.28, "text": " The second element is the indistinguishability relation.", "tokens": [51156, 440, 1150, 4478, 307, 264, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 2310, 9721, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 171770, "start": 1736.78, "end": 1737.2, "text": " The what?", "tokens": [51319, 440, 437, 30, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 171770, "start": 1738.2, "end": 1739.1200000000001, "text": " Indistinguishability relation.", "tokens": [51390, 2333, 468, 7050, 742, 2310, 9721, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1718852815173921, "compression_ratio": 1.6347826086956523, "no_speech_prob": 2.0515054498931873e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 173912, "start": 1739.12, "end": 1746.58, "text": " This is the logical rule that specifies when two items in your domain count as being the same for your current purposes.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 14978, 4978, 300, 1608, 11221, 562, 732, 4754, 294, 428, 9274, 1207, 382, 885, 264, 912, 337, 428, 2190, 9932, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12586321272291578, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214443846086391e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 173912, "start": 1747.3, "end": 1749.58, "text": " When are they observationally indistinguishable?", "tokens": [50774, 1133, 366, 436, 14816, 379, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 30, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12586321272291578, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214443846086391e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 173912, "start": 1749.9599999999998, "end": 1753.4199999999998, "text": " So, if I only care about the band name and the album title,", "tokens": [50907, 407, 11, 498, 286, 787, 1127, 466, 264, 4116, 1315, 293, 264, 6030, 4876, 11, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12586321272291578, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214443846086391e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 173912, "start": 1753.7199999999998, "end": 1758.4599999999998, "text": " my indistinguishability relation says that a 1969 UK pressing of Abbey Road", "tokens": [51095, 452, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 2310, 9721, 1619, 300, 257, 32090, 7051, 12417, 295, 2847, 13502, 11507, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12586321272291578, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214443846086391e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 173912, "start": 1758.4599999999998, "end": 1763.78, "text": " and a 2012 remastered reissue of Abbey Road are identical.", "tokens": [51332, 293, 257, 9125, 890, 1727, 292, 319, 891, 622, 295, 2847, 13502, 11507, 366, 14800, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12586321272291578, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214443846086391e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 173912, "start": 1764.08, "end": 1765.7399999999998, "text": " I can't distinguish them based on my rule.", "tokens": [51613, 286, 393, 380, 20206, 552, 2361, 322, 452, 4978, 13, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12586321272291578, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214443846086391e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 173912, "start": 1765.86, "end": 1766.4199999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51702, 7587, 13, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12586321272291578, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214443846086391e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 176642, "start": 1766.42, "end": 1769.52, "text": " But if my rule includes the catalog number etched in the runout groove,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 452, 4978, 5974, 264, 19746, 1230, 1030, 19318, 294, 264, 1190, 346, 26910, 11, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 176642, "start": 1769.96, "end": 1771.5800000000002, "text": " suddenly they are highly distinguishable.", "tokens": [50542, 5800, 436, 366, 5405, 20206, 712, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 176642, "start": 1771.72, "end": 1774.72, "text": " Exactly. The relation defines the resolution of your reality.", "tokens": [50630, 7587, 13, 440, 9721, 23122, 264, 8669, 295, 428, 4103, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 176642, "start": 1774.88, "end": 1776.5, "text": " And the third element is the ontology.", "tokens": [50788, 400, 264, 2636, 4478, 307, 264, 6592, 1793, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 176642, "start": 1776.9, "end": 1780.8000000000002, "text": " This is the actual description language, the vocabulary, or the database schema", "tokens": [50889, 639, 307, 264, 3539, 3855, 2856, 11, 264, 19864, 11, 420, 264, 8149, 34078, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 176642, "start": 1780.8000000000002, "end": 1783.66, "text": " that you are forced to use to describe the objects.", "tokens": [51084, 300, 291, 366, 7579, 281, 764, 281, 6786, 264, 6565, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 176642, "start": 1783.74, "end": 1783.92, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51231, 1033, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 176642, "start": 1784.18, "end": 1788.68, "text": " It determines which descriptions are actually reachable by you in practice, given your constraints.", "tokens": [51253, 467, 24799, 597, 24406, 366, 767, 2524, 712, 538, 291, 294, 3124, 11, 2212, 428, 18491, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 176642, "start": 1788.92, "end": 1792.0800000000002, "text": " Okay. So the triple is the stuff, the records,", "tokens": [51490, 1033, 13, 407, 264, 15508, 307, 264, 1507, 11, 264, 7724, 11, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 176642, "start": 1792.4, "end": 1795.8200000000002, "text": " the rule for when the stuff looks identical, the resolution.", "tokens": [51664, 264, 4978, 337, 562, 264, 1507, 1542, 14800, 11, 264, 8669, 13, 51835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399935953544848, "compression_ratio": 1.7721518987341771, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760850078319846e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 179642, "start": 1796.42, "end": 1800.7, "text": " And the language I use to describe the stuff, my database.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 2856, 286, 764, 281, 6786, 264, 1507, 11, 452, 8149, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1613927168004653, "compression_ratio": 1.5248868778280542, "no_speech_prob": 2.533778742375148e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 179642, "start": 1800.96, "end": 1801.46, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50592, 48746, 736, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1613927168004653, "compression_ratio": 1.5248868778280542, "no_speech_prob": 2.533778742375148e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 179642, "start": 1801.76, "end": 1803.3600000000001, "text": " Now, over this tripartite structure,", "tokens": [50632, 823, 11, 670, 341, 4931, 446, 642, 3877, 11, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1613927168004653, "compression_ratio": 1.5248868778280542, "no_speech_prob": 2.533778742375148e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 179642, "start": 1803.9, "end": 1808.18, "text": " the paper defines two completely different metrics of failure, or deficits.", "tokens": [50739, 264, 3035, 23122, 732, 2584, 819, 16367, 295, 7763, 11, 420, 49616, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1613927168004653, "compression_ratio": 1.5248868778280542, "no_speech_prob": 2.533778742375148e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 179642, "start": 1808.46, "end": 1809.28, "text": " Okay. What's the first one?", "tokens": [50967, 1033, 13, 708, 311, 264, 700, 472, 30, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1613927168004653, "compression_ratio": 1.5248868778280542, "no_speech_prob": 2.533778742375148e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 179642, "start": 1809.4, "end": 1810.8400000000001, "text": " The first is the coding deficit.", "tokens": [51014, 440, 700, 307, 264, 17720, 22132, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1613927168004653, "compression_ratio": 1.5248868778280542, "no_speech_prob": 2.533778742375148e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 179642, "start": 1811.02, "end": 1816.14, "text": " This measures how much longer a description is than it absolutely mathematically needs to be.", "tokens": [51095, 639, 8000, 577, 709, 2854, 257, 3855, 307, 813, 309, 3122, 44003, 2203, 281, 312, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1613927168004653, "compression_ratio": 1.5248868778280542, "no_speech_prob": 2.533778742375148e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 181614, "start": 1816.14, "end": 1822.94, "text": " It is the gap between the description your clumsy ontology actually produces and the absolute mathematical floor,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 7417, 1296, 264, 3855, 428, 44640, 6592, 1793, 767, 14725, 293, 264, 8236, 18894, 4123, 11, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436418824725681, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.825053779977437e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 181614, "start": 1823.2800000000002, "end": 1825.4, "text": " the Kolmogorov optimal description length.", "tokens": [50722, 264, 26137, 76, 664, 284, 5179, 16252, 3855, 4641, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436418824725681, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.825053779977437e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 181614, "start": 1825.5800000000002, "end": 1826.92, "text": " It's a measure of inefficiency.", "tokens": [50837, 467, 311, 257, 3481, 295, 7167, 49086, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436418824725681, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.825053779977437e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 181614, "start": 1827.26, "end": 1834.3000000000002, "text": " Like, if I describe a record in my database as a circular disk of black polyvinyl chloride containing analog sound recordings,", "tokens": [50921, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 6786, 257, 2136, 294, 452, 8149, 382, 257, 16476, 12355, 295, 2211, 6754, 85, 22946, 35434, 19273, 16660, 1626, 25162, 11, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436418824725681, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.825053779977437e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 183430, "start": 1834.3, "end": 1840.7, "text": " specifically the 11th studio album by the English rock band The Beatles, featuring a zebra crossing on the cover,", "tokens": [50365, 4682, 264, 2975, 392, 6811, 6030, 538, 264, 3669, 3727, 4116, 440, 38376, 11, 19742, 257, 47060, 14712, 322, 264, 2060, 11, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17721977481594334, "compression_ratio": 1.4759615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.142031994487037e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 183430, "start": 1840.8999999999999, "end": 1842.84, "text": " I have a massive coding deficit.", "tokens": [50695, 286, 362, 257, 5994, 17720, 22132, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17721977481594334, "compression_ratio": 1.4759615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.142031994487037e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 183430, "start": 1842.98, "end": 1844.12, "text": " Yes. Very massive.", "tokens": [50799, 1079, 13, 4372, 5994, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17721977481594334, "compression_ratio": 1.4759615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.142031994487037e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 183430, "start": 1844.28, "end": 1846.3999999999999, "text": " The optimal description might just be unique barcode.", "tokens": [50864, 440, 16252, 3855, 1062, 445, 312, 3845, 2159, 22332, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17721977481594334, "compression_ratio": 1.4759615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.142031994487037e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 183430, "start": 1846.48, "end": 1847.8999999999999, "text": " The extra words are the deficit.", "tokens": [50974, 440, 2857, 2283, 366, 264, 22132, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17721977481594334, "compression_ratio": 1.4759615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.142031994487037e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 183430, "start": 1848.0, "end": 1850.68, "text": " Exactly. Coding deficit is about length and verbosity.", "tokens": [51050, 7587, 13, 383, 8616, 22132, 307, 466, 4641, 293, 9595, 20373, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17721977481594334, "compression_ratio": 1.4759615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.142031994487037e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 185068, "start": 1850.68, "end": 1851.16, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 185068, "start": 1851.38, "end": 1853.6200000000001, "text": " Now, the second deficit is the distinguishability deficit.", "tokens": [50400, 823, 11, 264, 1150, 22132, 307, 264, 20206, 2310, 22132, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 185068, "start": 1853.88, "end": 1855.52, "text": " This measures something entirely different.", "tokens": [50525, 639, 8000, 746, 7696, 819, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 185068, "start": 1855.92, "end": 1860.88, "text": " It measures how much power to separate or distinguish objects has been lost by your system.", "tokens": [50627, 467, 8000, 577, 709, 1347, 281, 4994, 420, 20206, 6565, 575, 668, 2731, 538, 428, 1185, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 185068, "start": 1861.46, "end": 1866.16, "text": " It is the gap between the number of things your specific ontology can successfully tell apart", "tokens": [50904, 467, 307, 264, 7417, 1296, 264, 1230, 295, 721, 428, 2685, 6592, 1793, 393, 10727, 980, 4936, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 185068, "start": 1866.16, "end": 1870.88, "text": " and the maximum number of things the best possible ontology could tell apart,", "tokens": [51139, 293, 264, 6674, 1230, 295, 721, 264, 1151, 1944, 6592, 1793, 727, 980, 4936, 11, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 185068, "start": 1871.24, "end": 1873.6200000000001, "text": " given the indistinguishability relation.", "tokens": [51393, 2212, 264, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 2310, 9721, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 185068, "start": 1873.88, "end": 1875.8400000000001, "text": " So coding deficit is about length.", "tokens": [51525, 407, 17720, 22132, 307, 466, 4641, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 185068, "start": 1876.5600000000002, "end": 1878.98, "text": " Distinguishability deficit is about clarity and resolution.", "tokens": [51659, 9840, 7050, 742, 2310, 22132, 307, 466, 16992, 293, 8669, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1702982695206352, "compression_ratio": 1.8884758364312269, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171618081109451e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 187898, "start": 1878.98, "end": 1881.82, "text": " Can I still tell the difference between object A and object B?", "tokens": [50365, 1664, 286, 920, 980, 264, 2649, 1296, 2657, 316, 293, 2657, 363, 30, 50507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 187898, "start": 1881.94, "end": 1885.4, "text": " Right. And here is where the cognitive trap springs shut on us.", "tokens": [50513, 1779, 13, 400, 510, 307, 689, 264, 15605, 11487, 24647, 5309, 322, 505, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 187898, "start": 1886.18, "end": 1889.26, "text": " The assumption everyone makes, from software engineers to philosophers,", "tokens": [50725, 440, 15302, 1518, 1669, 11, 490, 4722, 11955, 281, 36839, 11, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 187898, "start": 1889.6, "end": 1892.4, "text": " is that these two deficits are tightly coupled.", "tokens": [50896, 307, 300, 613, 732, 49616, 366, 21952, 29482, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 187898, "start": 1892.74, "end": 1895.1, "text": " We assume that if you lower the coding deficit,", "tokens": [51053, 492, 6552, 300, 498, 291, 3126, 264, 17720, 22132, 11, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 187898, "start": 1895.52, "end": 1898.42, "text": " if you make the description shorter, tighter, more elegant,", "tokens": [51192, 498, 291, 652, 264, 3855, 11639, 11, 30443, 11, 544, 21117, 11, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 187898, "start": 1898.72, "end": 1904.0, "text": " you must be simultaneously improving or at least maintaining the distinguishability deficit.", "tokens": [51352, 291, 1633, 312, 16561, 11470, 420, 412, 1935, 14916, 264, 20206, 2310, 22132, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 187898, "start": 1904.14, "end": 1905.98, "text": " We assume brevity equals clarity.", "tokens": [51623, 492, 6552, 1403, 23110, 6915, 16992, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 187898, "start": 1906.48, "end": 1908.16, "text": " Shorter equals better understanding.", "tokens": [51740, 1160, 6122, 6915, 1101, 3701, 13, 51824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16135736991619243, "compression_ratio": 1.7039473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465496059300035e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 190816, "start": 1908.16, "end": 1912.92, "text": " But the paper introduces a formal proof called the deficit proxy theorem,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 3035, 31472, 257, 9860, 8177, 1219, 264, 22132, 29690, 20904, 11, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 190816, "start": 1913.24, "end": 1915.8200000000002, "text": " and it proves that this relationship is a one-way street,", "tokens": [50619, 293, 309, 25019, 300, 341, 2480, 307, 257, 472, 12, 676, 4838, 11, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 190816, "start": 1916.02, "end": 1918.6200000000001, "text": " and it only works at the absolute theoretical limit.", "tokens": [50758, 293, 309, 787, 1985, 412, 264, 8236, 20864, 4948, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 190816, "start": 1918.76, "end": 1919.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50895, 1079, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 190816, "start": 1919.1200000000001, "end": 1920.68, "text": " Okay, what does the theorem actually state?", "tokens": [50913, 1033, 11, 437, 775, 264, 20904, 767, 1785, 30, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 190816, "start": 1920.88, "end": 1923.16, "text": " Let's get into the mechanics of why the assumption fails.", "tokens": [51001, 961, 311, 483, 666, 264, 12939, 295, 983, 264, 15302, 18199, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 190816, "start": 1923.3200000000002, "end": 1927.2, "text": " The theorem states that assuming something called faithful encoding,", "tokens": [51123, 440, 20904, 4368, 300, 11926, 746, 1219, 17808, 43430, 11, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 190816, "start": 1927.68, "end": 1931.5, "text": " which means every distinction costs at least one bit of information to express,", "tokens": [51341, 597, 1355, 633, 16844, 5497, 412, 1935, 472, 857, 295, 1589, 281, 5109, 11, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14562248947596787, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778479225623474e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 193150, "start": 1931.5, "end": 1937.66, "text": " the distinguishability deficit is bounded above by a constant multiple of the coding deficit.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 20206, 2310, 22132, 307, 37498, 3673, 538, 257, 5754, 3866, 295, 264, 17720, 22132, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19498404264450073, "compression_ratio": 1.1625, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897569277308678e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 193766, "start": 1937.66, "end": 1940.28, "text": " Okay. Translate the math into reality for me.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 6531, 17593, 264, 5221, 666, 4103, 337, 385, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20487121686543505, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547612246784691e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 193766, "start": 1940.38, "end": 1942.5600000000002, "text": " The direct mathematical consequence is this.", "tokens": [50501, 440, 2047, 18894, 18326, 307, 341, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20487121686543505, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547612246784691e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 193766, "start": 1943.1200000000001, "end": 1945.78, "text": " If your coding deficit is exactly zero,", "tokens": [50638, 759, 428, 17720, 22132, 307, 2293, 4018, 11, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20487121686543505, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547612246784691e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 193766, "start": 1946.5400000000002, "end": 1952.0800000000002, "text": " meaning you have achieved the absolute, theoretically shortest possible description of an object,", "tokens": [50809, 3620, 291, 362, 11042, 264, 8236, 11, 29400, 31875, 1944, 3855, 295, 364, 2657, 11, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20487121686543505, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547612246784691e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 193766, "start": 1952.3200000000002, "end": 1955.5800000000002, "text": " then your distinguishability deficit must also be zero.", "tokens": [51098, 550, 428, 20206, 2310, 22132, 1633, 611, 312, 4018, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20487121686543505, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547612246784691e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 193766, "start": 1956.26, "end": 1959.52, "text": " Perfect compression guarantees perfect distinguishing capacity.", "tokens": [51295, 10246, 19355, 32567, 2176, 11365, 3807, 6042, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20487121686543505, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547612246784691e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 195952, "start": 1959.52, "end": 1964.76, "text": " Okay, so if I use a perfect, lossless compression algorithm on a high-resolution photo,", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 286, 764, 257, 2176, 11, 4470, 1832, 19355, 9284, 322, 257, 1090, 12, 495, 3386, 5052, 11, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 195952, "start": 1965.02, "end": 1968.56, "text": " and I reach the absolute mathematical floor of how small that file can be,", "tokens": [50640, 293, 286, 2524, 264, 8236, 18894, 4123, 295, 577, 1359, 300, 3991, 393, 312, 11, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 195952, "start": 1968.7, "end": 1969.86, "text": " I haven't lost any data.", "tokens": [50824, 286, 2378, 380, 2731, 604, 1412, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 195952, "start": 1970.12, "end": 1973.54, "text": " When I unzip it, I can still distinguish every single pixel perfectly.", "tokens": [50895, 1133, 286, 517, 27268, 309, 11, 286, 393, 920, 20206, 633, 2167, 19261, 6239, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 195952, "start": 1973.7, "end": 1976.06, "text": " Yes, that is the one direction the theorem proves.", "tokens": [51074, 1079, 11, 300, 307, 264, 472, 3513, 264, 20904, 25019, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 195952, "start": 1976.4, "end": 1979.92, "text": " But, and this is the massive flashing red warning light of the paper,", "tokens": [51209, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 5994, 31049, 2182, 9164, 1442, 295, 264, 3035, 11, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 195952, "start": 1980.5, "end": 1983.04, "text": " the theorem explicitly does not prove the converse.", "tokens": [51414, 264, 20904, 20803, 775, 406, 7081, 264, 416, 4308, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 195952, "start": 1983.18, "end": 1983.82, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [51548, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 195952, "start": 1983.9, "end": 1987.8, "text": " A distinguishability deficit of zero does not force a coding deficit of zero.", "tokens": [51584, 316, 20206, 2310, 22132, 295, 4018, 775, 406, 3464, 257, 17720, 22132, 295, 4018, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0942324229649135, "compression_ratio": 1.703583061889251, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947689996174575e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 198780, "start": 1987.8, "end": 1989.46, "text": " Let me make sure I'm grasping this.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 29444, 3381, 341, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 198780, "start": 1989.76, "end": 1991.04, "text": " Let's go back to your record collection.", "tokens": [50463, 961, 311, 352, 646, 281, 428, 2136, 5765, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 198780, "start": 1992.04, "end": 1994.6399999999999, "text": " You can have a system with zero distinguishability.", "tokens": [50577, 509, 393, 362, 257, 1185, 365, 4018, 20206, 2310, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 198780, "start": 1995.54, "end": 1997.74, "text": " Deficit, meaning your database,", "tokens": [50752, 1346, 1786, 270, 11, 3620, 428, 8149, 11, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 198780, "start": 1998.1599999999999, "end": 2003.94, "text": " perfectly captures the difference between every single pressing label variant and scratch in your collection.", "tokens": [50883, 6239, 27986, 264, 2649, 1296, 633, 2167, 12417, 7645, 17501, 293, 8459, 294, 428, 5765, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 198780, "start": 2004.26, "end": 2006.34, "text": " You understand the domain perfectly.", "tokens": [51188, 509, 1223, 264, 9274, 6239, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 198780, "start": 2006.72, "end": 2007.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51311, 1779, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 198780, "start": 2007.2, "end": 2009.6599999999999, "text": " But your ontology might be incredibly inefficient.", "tokens": [51335, 583, 428, 6592, 1793, 1062, 312, 6252, 43495, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 198780, "start": 2009.9199999999998, "end": 2012.6, "text": " You might be writing out a paragraph of text for every record.", "tokens": [51471, 509, 1062, 312, 3579, 484, 257, 18865, 295, 2487, 337, 633, 2136, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 198780, "start": 2012.78, "end": 2015.1, "text": " You carry a massive coding deficit.", "tokens": [51614, 509, 3985, 257, 5994, 17720, 22132, 13, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1923990249633789, "compression_ratio": 1.6395759717314489, "no_speech_prob": 1.839629360303463e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 201510, "start": 2015.1, "end": 2018.5, "text": " Okay, so verbosity does not mean ignorance.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 9595, 20373, 775, 406, 914, 25390, 13, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 201510, "start": 2019.76, "end": 2021.82, "text": " I can be long-winded and chaotic in my description,", "tokens": [50598, 286, 393, 312, 938, 12, 12199, 292, 293, 27013, 294, 452, 3855, 11, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 201510, "start": 2021.9599999999998, "end": 2024.62, "text": " but still perfectly understand the nuances of the domain.", "tokens": [50708, 457, 920, 6239, 1223, 264, 38775, 295, 264, 9274, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 201510, "start": 2025.04, "end": 2025.4399999999998, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50862, 48746, 736, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 201510, "start": 2025.62, "end": 2027.9399999999998, "text": " But the trap is even more insidious than that.", "tokens": [50891, 583, 264, 11487, 307, 754, 544, 1028, 327, 851, 813, 300, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 201510, "start": 2028.4599999999998, "end": 2030.82, "text": " Because the theorem is only an upper bound,", "tokens": [51033, 1436, 264, 20904, 307, 787, 364, 6597, 5472, 11, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 201510, "start": 2031.12, "end": 2033.7199999999998, "text": " if you have an already imperfect coding deficit,", "tokens": [51166, 498, 291, 362, 364, 1217, 26714, 17720, 22132, 11, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 201510, "start": 2033.9599999999998, "end": 2035.36, "text": " say your database is kind of messy,", "tokens": [51308, 584, 428, 8149, 307, 733, 295, 16191, 11, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 201510, "start": 2035.52, "end": 2039.1, "text": " and you hire a consultant to optimize it and make the descriptions a little bit shorter,", "tokens": [51386, 293, 291, 11158, 257, 24676, 281, 19719, 309, 293, 652, 264, 24406, 257, 707, 857, 11639, 11, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 201510, "start": 2039.52, "end": 2042.4399999999998, "text": " that reduction in length is not mathematical evidence", "tokens": [51586, 300, 11004, 294, 4641, 307, 406, 18894, 4467, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 201510, "start": 2042.4399999999998, "end": 2044.86, "text": " that you have improved your distinguishing capacity.", "tokens": [51732, 300, 291, 362, 9689, 428, 11365, 3807, 6042, 13, 51853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17076285680135092, "compression_ratio": 1.6697819314641744, "no_speech_prob": 1.2693332713045735e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 204486, "start": 2044.86, "end": 2045.8, "text": " Oh, I see it now.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 286, 536, 309, 586, 13, 50412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18509823935372488, "compression_ratio": 1.5662100456621004, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383331765205343e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 204486, "start": 2046.26, "end": 2049.8599999999997, "text": " If my consultant just starts aggressively deleting words to save space,", "tokens": [50435, 759, 452, 24676, 445, 3719, 32024, 48946, 2283, 281, 3155, 1901, 11, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18509823935372488, "compression_ratio": 1.5662100456621004, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383331765205343e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 204486, "start": 2050.4, "end": 2054.58, "text": " eventually my database just says Beatles album for both Abbey Road and the White Album.", "tokens": [50642, 4728, 452, 8149, 445, 1619, 38376, 6030, 337, 1293, 2847, 13502, 11507, 293, 264, 5552, 967, 5559, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18509823935372488, "compression_ratio": 1.5662100456621004, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383331765205343e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 204486, "start": 2055.12, "end": 2057.16, "text": " I radically improved the coding deficit.", "tokens": [50878, 286, 35508, 9689, 264, 17720, 22132, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18509823935372488, "compression_ratio": 1.5662100456621004, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383331765205343e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 204486, "start": 2057.44, "end": 2059.24, "text": " My database is so small and efficient,", "tokens": [50994, 1222, 8149, 307, 370, 1359, 293, 7148, 11, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18509823935372488, "compression_ratio": 1.5662100456621004, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383331765205343e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 204486, "start": 2059.7999999999997, "end": 2063.14, "text": " but I completely ruined the distinguishability deficit.", "tokens": [51112, 457, 286, 2584, 17013, 264, 20206, 2310, 22132, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18509823935372488, "compression_ratio": 1.5662100456621004, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383331765205343e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 204486, "start": 2063.52, "end": 2065.5, "text": " I am blind to the difference.", "tokens": [51298, 286, 669, 6865, 281, 264, 2649, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18509823935372488, "compression_ratio": 1.5662100456621004, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383331765205343e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 206550, "start": 2065.5, "end": 2065.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 206550, "start": 2065.94, "end": 2067.58, "text": " You compressed your way into ignorance.", "tokens": [50387, 509, 30353, 428, 636, 666, 25390, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 206550, "start": 2068.06, "end": 2072.42, "text": " Treating description length as a continuous sliding scale proxy for understanding", "tokens": [50493, 20298, 278, 3855, 4641, 382, 257, 10957, 21169, 4373, 29690, 337, 3701, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 206550, "start": 2072.42, "end": 2074.58, "text": " is totally unsupported by the math.", "tokens": [50711, 307, 3879, 2693, 10504, 14813, 538, 264, 5221, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 206550, "start": 2074.88, "end": 2075.88, "text": " You cannot say,", "tokens": [50834, 509, 2644, 584, 11, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 206550, "start": 2076.24, "end": 2077.6, "text": " my model is 10% smaller,", "tokens": [50902, 452, 2316, 307, 1266, 4, 4356, 11, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 206550, "start": 2077.74, "end": 2081.36, "text": " therefore it has captured the true essence of the data 10% better.", "tokens": [50977, 4412, 309, 575, 11828, 264, 2074, 12801, 295, 264, 1412, 1266, 4, 1101, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 206550, "start": 2081.52, "end": 2084.04, "text": " It might have just thrown away the most important nuances.", "tokens": [51166, 467, 1062, 362, 445, 11732, 1314, 264, 881, 1021, 38775, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19687816074916295, "compression_ratio": 1.506787330316742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796945999554945e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 208404, "start": 2084.04, "end": 2085.3, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18430635788861444, "compression_ratio": 1.5491071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813233747955958e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 208404, "start": 2085.74, "end": 2088.22, "text": " It completely upends the keep it simple mandate.", "tokens": [50450, 467, 2584, 493, 2581, 264, 1066, 309, 2199, 23885, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18430635788861444, "compression_ratio": 1.5491071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813233747955958e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 208404, "start": 2089.12, "end": 2091.5, "text": " And Fluxian doesn't just leave this as abstract math.", "tokens": [50619, 400, 3235, 2449, 952, 1177, 380, 445, 1856, 341, 382, 12649, 5221, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18430635788861444, "compression_ratio": 1.5491071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813233747955958e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 208404, "start": 2091.98, "end": 2094.7599999999998, "text": " The paper applies this to real world scenarios to ground it,", "tokens": [50762, 440, 3035, 13165, 341, 281, 957, 1002, 15077, 281, 2727, 309, 11, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18430635788861444, "compression_ratio": 1.5491071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813233747955958e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 208404, "start": 2094.88, "end": 2096.54, "text": " starting with the history of programming languages.", "tokens": [50907, 2891, 365, 264, 2503, 295, 9410, 8650, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18430635788861444, "compression_ratio": 1.5491071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813233747955958e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 208404, "start": 2097.04, "end": 2099.22, "text": " Specifically, they look at the fourth programming language.", "tokens": [51015, 26058, 11, 436, 574, 412, 264, 6409, 9410, 2856, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18430635788861444, "compression_ratio": 1.5491071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813233747955958e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 208404, "start": 2099.44, "end": 2102.34, "text": " Fourth is a fascinating case study in this exact fallacy.", "tokens": [51135, 23773, 307, 257, 10343, 1389, 2979, 294, 341, 1900, 2100, 2551, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18430635788861444, "compression_ratio": 1.5491071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813233747955958e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 210234, "start": 2102.34, "end": 2105.1600000000003, "text": " It was created in the 1970s by Charles Moore,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 390, 2942, 294, 264, 14577, 82, 538, 10523, 21644, 11, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 210234, "start": 2105.36, "end": 2107.3, "text": " originally to control radio telescopes.", "tokens": [50516, 7993, 281, 1969, 6477, 46051, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 210234, "start": 2107.7200000000003, "end": 2110.92, "text": " And it is famous among its devotees for being incredibly cursed.", "tokens": [50634, 400, 309, 307, 4618, 3654, 1080, 46960, 337, 885, 6252, 29498, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 210234, "start": 2111.42, "end": 2112.9, "text": " Fourth code is unusually short.", "tokens": [50819, 23773, 3089, 307, 10054, 671, 2099, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 210234, "start": 2113.28, "end": 2116.42, "text": " And for decades, programmers have pointed to this brevity,", "tokens": [50912, 400, 337, 7878, 11, 41504, 362, 10932, 281, 341, 1403, 23110, 11, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 210234, "start": 2117.1800000000003, "end": 2119.2200000000003, "text": " cited Hillis' definition of information,", "tokens": [51107, 30134, 9109, 271, 6, 7123, 295, 1589, 11, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 210234, "start": 2119.76, "end": 2122.36, "text": " and claimed that because fourth code is so short,", "tokens": [51236, 293, 12941, 300, 570, 6409, 3089, 307, 370, 2099, 11, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 210234, "start": 2122.7000000000003, "end": 2126.82, "text": " it must be sitting right on top of the Kolmogorov optimal floor of the problem.", "tokens": [51383, 309, 1633, 312, 3798, 558, 322, 1192, 295, 264, 26137, 76, 664, 284, 5179, 16252, 4123, 295, 264, 1154, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 210234, "start": 2127.46, "end": 2130.3, "text": " They argue it is a pure expression of logic.", "tokens": [51621, 814, 9695, 309, 307, 257, 6075, 6114, 295, 9952, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 210234, "start": 2130.3, "end": 2132.06, "text": " It's the ultimate compressed language.", "tokens": [51763, 467, 311, 264, 9705, 30353, 2856, 13, 51851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481921349802324, "compression_ratio": 1.5796178343949046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 213234, "start": 2132.34, "end": 2134.46, "text": " But the paper says that's a mirage.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 3035, 1619, 300, 311, 257, 3149, 609, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 213234, "start": 2134.76, "end": 2135.1800000000003, "text": " Completely.", "tokens": [50486, 39978, 13, 50507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 213234, "start": 2135.8, "end": 2138.48, "text": " Fourth code isn't short because it magically approaches", "tokens": [50538, 23773, 3089, 1943, 380, 2099, 570, 309, 39763, 11587, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 213234, "start": 2138.48, "end": 2140.56, "text": " pure mathematical perfection on the fly.", "tokens": [50672, 6075, 18894, 19708, 322, 264, 3603, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 213234, "start": 2141.08, "end": 2145.4, "text": " It is short because of a concept the framework calls reachable complexity.", "tokens": [50802, 467, 307, 2099, 570, 295, 257, 3410, 264, 8388, 5498, 2524, 712, 14024, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 213234, "start": 2145.6800000000003, "end": 2146.58, "text": " Reachable complexity.", "tokens": [51032, 35904, 712, 14024, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 213234, "start": 2146.7400000000002, "end": 2148.4, "text": " How does that work mechanically in fourth?", "tokens": [51085, 1012, 775, 300, 589, 4236, 984, 294, 6409, 30, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 213234, "start": 2148.6200000000003, "end": 2150.5, "text": " Fourth is a stack-based language.", "tokens": [51179, 23773, 307, 257, 8630, 12, 6032, 2856, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 213234, "start": 2150.88, "end": 2152.9, "text": " A programmer doesn't write everything from scratch.", "tokens": [51292, 316, 32116, 1177, 380, 2464, 1203, 490, 8459, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 213234, "start": 2153.44, "end": 2156.96, "text": " They build a massive, personalized library of named operations,", "tokens": [51420, 814, 1322, 257, 5994, 11, 28415, 6405, 295, 4926, 7705, 11, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 213234, "start": 2157.1800000000003, "end": 2158.08, "text": " which they call words.", "tokens": [51607, 597, 436, 818, 2283, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 213234, "start": 2158.08, "end": 2160.56, "text": " These words are built from tiny, primitive operations,", "tokens": [51652, 1981, 2283, 366, 3094, 490, 5870, 11, 28540, 7705, 11, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16886254279844223, "compression_ratio": 1.7009966777408638, "no_speech_prob": 1.981359304056851e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 216056, "start": 2160.56, "end": 2165.4, "text": " and they capture specific, highly complex functions the programmer knows they will need again.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 436, 7983, 2685, 11, 5405, 3997, 6828, 264, 32116, 3255, 436, 486, 643, 797, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.132999164717538, "compression_ratio": 1.5060240963855422, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047688773476956e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 216056, "start": 2166.04, "end": 2170.06, "text": " When the programmer finally sits down to write the top-level script to solve a new task,", "tokens": [50639, 1133, 264, 32116, 2721, 12696, 760, 281, 2464, 264, 1192, 12, 12418, 5755, 281, 5039, 257, 777, 5633, 11, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.132999164717538, "compression_ratio": 1.5060240963855422, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047688773476956e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 216056, "start": 2170.42, "end": 2173.94, "text": " the script looks incredibly short, maybe just three or four words.", "tokens": [50858, 264, 5755, 1542, 6252, 2099, 11, 1310, 445, 1045, 420, 1451, 2283, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.132999164717538, "compression_ratio": 1.5060240963855422, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047688773476956e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 217394, "start": 2173.94, "end": 2177.34, "text": " But it's only short because it is calling upon this massive,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 311, 787, 2099, 570, 309, 307, 5141, 3564, 341, 5994, 11, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 217394, "start": 2177.62, "end": 2181.06, "text": " hidden, pre-existing library of already accumulated knowledge.", "tokens": [50549, 7633, 11, 659, 12, 36447, 6405, 295, 1217, 31346, 3601, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 217394, "start": 2181.4, "end": 2181.84, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50738, 865, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 217394, "start": 2182.36, "end": 2184.1, "text": " It's like writing a recipe that just says,", "tokens": [50786, 467, 311, 411, 3579, 257, 6782, 300, 445, 1619, 11, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 217394, "start": 2184.52, "end": 2185.48, "text": " make beef Wellington.", "tokens": [50894, 652, 9256, 45812, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 217394, "start": 2186.32, "end": 2187.36, "text": " It looks short,", "tokens": [50984, 467, 1542, 2099, 11, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 217394, "start": 2187.52, "end": 2190.32, "text": " but only because you already spent 10 years in culinary school", "tokens": [51044, 457, 787, 570, 291, 1217, 4418, 1266, 924, 294, 39273, 1395, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 217394, "start": 2190.32, "end": 2193.36, "text": " learning the 50 sub-steps of making the pastry and the ducksels.", "tokens": [51184, 2539, 264, 2625, 1422, 12, 20413, 295, 1455, 264, 29198, 293, 264, 12482, 26604, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24839162826538086, "compression_ratio": 1.5089285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845651593770498e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 219336, "start": 2193.36, "end": 2193.92, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 219336, "start": 2194.86, "end": 2197.86, "text": " The shortness of the code is not a symptom of some raw,", "tokens": [50440, 440, 2099, 1287, 295, 264, 3089, 307, 406, 257, 29370, 295, 512, 8936, 11, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 219336, "start": 2198.04, "end": 2201.1200000000003, "text": " brilliant mathematical compression of the immediate problem.", "tokens": [50599, 10248, 18894, 19355, 295, 264, 11629, 1154, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 219336, "start": 2201.54, "end": 2204.38, "text": " It is a symptom of past exploration and expansion.", "tokens": [50774, 467, 307, 257, 29370, 295, 1791, 16197, 293, 11260, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 219336, "start": 2205.08, "end": 2209.26, "text": " The hard work, the verbosity, was already done and stored in the dictionary.", "tokens": [50951, 440, 1152, 589, 11, 264, 9595, 20373, 11, 390, 1217, 1096, 293, 12187, 294, 264, 25890, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 219336, "start": 2209.6400000000003, "end": 2212.2400000000002, "text": " If two programmers solve the same task in fourth,", "tokens": [51179, 759, 732, 41504, 5039, 264, 912, 5633, 294, 6409, 11, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 219336, "start": 2212.6200000000003, "end": 2214.44, "text": " and one uses much shorter code,", "tokens": [51328, 293, 472, 4960, 709, 11639, 3089, 11, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 219336, "start": 2214.6400000000003, "end": 2218.2000000000003, "text": " it doesn't mean they understood the fundamental mathematics of the task better.", "tokens": [51429, 309, 1177, 380, 914, 436, 7320, 264, 8088, 18666, 295, 264, 5633, 1101, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 219336, "start": 2218.6200000000003, "end": 2222.6800000000003, "text": " It just means they had a vastly superior library available to reuse.", "tokens": [51628, 467, 445, 1355, 436, 632, 257, 41426, 13028, 6405, 2435, 281, 26225, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19678251846976902, "compression_ratio": 1.704225352112676, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179334990500728e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 222268, "start": 2222.68, "end": 2225.8199999999997, "text": " The brevity is a downstream effect of prior expansion,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1403, 23110, 307, 257, 30621, 1802, 295, 4059, 11260, 11, 50522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 222268, "start": 2226.16, "end": 2228.2, "text": " not a measure of immediate intelligence.", "tokens": [50539, 406, 257, 3481, 295, 11629, 7599, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 222268, "start": 2228.62, "end": 2229.44, "text": " I love that framing.", "tokens": [50662, 286, 959, 300, 28971, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 222268, "start": 2230.2, "end": 2232.4199999999996, "text": " The brevity reports the existence of the library,", "tokens": [50741, 440, 1403, 23110, 7122, 264, 9123, 295, 264, 6405, 11, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 222268, "start": 2232.64, "end": 2235.14, "text": " not the absolute informational floor of the task.", "tokens": [50863, 406, 264, 8236, 49391, 4123, 295, 264, 5633, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 222268, "start": 2235.56, "end": 2238.8799999999997, "text": " We mistake the convenience of the interface for the simplicity of the domain.", "tokens": [51009, 492, 6146, 264, 19283, 295, 264, 9226, 337, 264, 25632, 295, 264, 9274, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 222268, "start": 2239.44, "end": 2242.8199999999997, "text": " But this doesn't just apply to old 1970s programming languages.", "tokens": [51203, 583, 341, 1177, 380, 445, 3079, 281, 1331, 14577, 82, 9410, 8650, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 222268, "start": 2243.18, "end": 2244.7799999999997, "text": " Here's where this paper gets incredibly relevant,", "tokens": [51390, 1692, 311, 689, 341, 3035, 2170, 6252, 7340, 11, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 222268, "start": 2244.8799999999997, "end": 2247.3999999999996, "text": " because it applies this exact same mathematical logic", "tokens": [51475, 570, 309, 13165, 341, 1900, 912, 18894, 9952, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 222268, "start": 2247.3999999999996, "end": 2249.74, "text": " to modern machine learning and AI.", "tokens": [51601, 281, 4363, 3479, 2539, 293, 7318, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369873378587805, "compression_ratio": 1.6188925081433225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614907792285917e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 224974, "start": 2249.74, "end": 2253.3599999999997, "text": " And this is where the cultural assumption is most dangerous right now.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 6988, 15302, 307, 881, 5795, 558, 586, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14279329658734916, "compression_ratio": 1.5298507462686568, "no_speech_prob": 1.636370292740219e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 224974, "start": 2254.16, "end": 2258.3799999999997, "text": " In modern AI research, there is a massive industry-wide obsession", "tokens": [50586, 682, 4363, 7318, 2132, 11, 456, 307, 257, 5994, 3518, 12, 7990, 30521, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14279329658734916, "compression_ratio": 1.5298507462686568, "no_speech_prob": 1.636370292740219e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 224974, "start": 2258.3799999999997, "end": 2263.06, "text": " with sparse coding, disentanglement, and description length reduction.", "tokens": [50797, 365, 637, 11668, 17720, 11, 37313, 656, 3054, 11, 293, 3855, 4641, 11004, 13, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14279329658734916, "compression_ratio": 1.5298507462686568, "no_speech_prob": 1.636370292740219e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 224974, "start": 2263.2999999999997, "end": 2264.9399999999996, "text": " Yes, if you read any AI paper,", "tokens": [51043, 1079, 11, 498, 291, 1401, 604, 7318, 3035, 11, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14279329658734916, "compression_ratio": 1.5298507462686568, "no_speech_prob": 1.636370292740219e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 224974, "start": 2265.2799999999997, "end": 2269.8799999999997, "text": " researchers love talking about a small, highly compressed, latent space.", "tokens": [51142, 10309, 959, 1417, 466, 257, 1359, 11, 5405, 30353, 11, 48994, 1901, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14279329658734916, "compression_ratio": 1.5298507462686568, "no_speech_prob": 1.636370292740219e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 224974, "start": 2270.2, "end": 2273.12, "text": " They use architectures like beta VAEs,", "tokens": [51388, 814, 764, 6331, 1303, 411, 9861, 18527, 20442, 11, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14279329658734916, "compression_ratio": 1.5298507462686568, "no_speech_prob": 1.636370292740219e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 224974, "start": 2273.2599999999998, "end": 2275.74, "text": " variational autoencoders with an adjustable hyperparameter.", "tokens": [51541, 3034, 1478, 8399, 22660, 378, 433, 365, 364, 27804, 9848, 2181, 335, 2398, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14279329658734916, "compression_ratio": 1.5298507462686568, "no_speech_prob": 1.636370292740219e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 227574, "start": 2275.74, "end": 2277.18, "text": " Okay, pause.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 10465, 13, 50437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 227574, "start": 2277.4399999999996, "end": 2279.12, "text": " Let's unpack that jargon for the listener.", "tokens": [50450, 961, 311, 26699, 300, 15181, 10660, 337, 264, 31569, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 227574, "start": 2279.8199999999997, "end": 2284.12, "text": " What is an autoencoder, and why is a beta VAE pushing for compression?", "tokens": [50569, 708, 307, 364, 8399, 22660, 19866, 11, 293, 983, 307, 257, 9861, 18527, 36, 7380, 337, 19355, 30, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 227574, "start": 2284.66, "end": 2288.8399999999997, "text": " An autoencoder is a type of neural network designed to learn efficient data codings.", "tokens": [50811, 1107, 8399, 22660, 19866, 307, 257, 2010, 295, 18161, 3209, 4761, 281, 1466, 7148, 1412, 17656, 1109, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 227574, "start": 2289.4599999999996, "end": 2291.7999999999997, "text": " It has two parts, an encoder and a decoder.", "tokens": [51051, 467, 575, 732, 3166, 11, 364, 2058, 19866, 293, 257, 979, 19866, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 227574, "start": 2292.24, "end": 2293.72, "text": " You feed an image to the encoder,", "tokens": [51190, 509, 3154, 364, 3256, 281, 264, 2058, 19866, 11, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 227574, "start": 2293.8399999999997, "end": 2297.8199999999997, "text": " and it squashes it down into a tiny bottleneck of numbers, the latent space.", "tokens": [51270, 293, 309, 2339, 12808, 309, 760, 666, 257, 5870, 44641, 547, 295, 3547, 11, 264, 48994, 1901, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 227574, "start": 2298.02, "end": 2298.24, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51479, 5803, 309, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15562609079721812, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351781462007e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 229824, "start": 2298.24, "end": 2302.8799999999997, "text": " Then the decoder tries to reconstruct the original image from that tiny bottleneck.", "tokens": [50365, 1396, 264, 979, 19866, 9898, 281, 31499, 264, 3380, 3256, 490, 300, 5870, 44641, 547, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897990245445102, "compression_ratio": 1.611764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.935176845158093e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 229824, "start": 2303.18, "end": 2307.2, "text": " It's literally forcing the network to play a game of telephone through a very narrow pipe.", "tokens": [50612, 467, 311, 3736, 19030, 264, 3209, 281, 862, 257, 1216, 295, 19800, 807, 257, 588, 9432, 11240, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897990245445102, "compression_ratio": 1.611764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.935176845158093e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 229824, "start": 2307.4199999999996, "end": 2307.8199999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50824, 7587, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897990245445102, "compression_ratio": 1.611764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.935176845158093e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 229824, "start": 2308.3999999999996, "end": 2311.14, "text": " And a beta VAE turns up the pressure on that pipe.", "tokens": [50873, 400, 257, 9861, 18527, 36, 4523, 493, 264, 3321, 322, 300, 11240, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897990245445102, "compression_ratio": 1.611764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.935176845158093e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 229824, "start": 2311.58, "end": 2315.8799999999997, "text": " It explicitly penalizes the network for using too much information in the bottleneck.", "tokens": [51032, 467, 20803, 13661, 5660, 264, 3209, 337, 1228, 886, 709, 1589, 294, 264, 44641, 547, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897990245445102, "compression_ratio": 1.611764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.935176845158093e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 229824, "start": 2316.14, "end": 2319.58, "text": " It forces the latent code to be as sparse and compressed as possible.", "tokens": [51260, 467, 5874, 264, 48994, 3089, 281, 312, 382, 637, 11668, 293, 30353, 382, 1944, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897990245445102, "compression_ratio": 1.611764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.935176845158093e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 229824, "start": 2319.72, "end": 2320.3799999999997, "text": " Why do they do that?", "tokens": [51439, 1545, 360, 436, 360, 300, 30, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897990245445102, "compression_ratio": 1.611764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.935176845158093e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 232038, "start": 2320.38, "end": 2325.46, "text": " Well, researchers also use sparse autoencoders to probe large language models,", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 10309, 611, 764, 637, 11668, 8399, 22660, 378, 433, 281, 22715, 2416, 2856, 5245, 11, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12687953880855016, "compression_ratio": 1.613240418118467, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370733115124824e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 232038, "start": 2325.88, "end": 2331.38, "text": " trying to force the model to represent its knowledge with only a few active neurons at a time.", "tokens": [50640, 1382, 281, 3464, 264, 2316, 281, 2906, 1080, 3601, 365, 787, 257, 1326, 4967, 22027, 412, 257, 565, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12687953880855016, "compression_ratio": 1.613240418118467, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370733115124824e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 232038, "start": 2332.1400000000003, "end": 2336.04, "text": " The stated, explicit motivation for all this is almost always.", "tokens": [50953, 440, 11323, 11, 13691, 12335, 337, 439, 341, 307, 1920, 1009, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12687953880855016, "compression_ratio": 1.613240418118467, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370733115124824e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 232038, "start": 2336.56, "end": 2342.3, "text": " Compression is a proxy for finding the true, underlying, causal generative factors of a domain.", "tokens": [51174, 6620, 2775, 307, 257, 29690, 337, 5006, 264, 2074, 11, 14217, 11, 38755, 1337, 1166, 6771, 295, 257, 9274, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12687953880855016, "compression_ratio": 1.613240418118467, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370733115124824e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 232038, "start": 2342.6, "end": 2345.96, "text": " The belief is that if you squeeze the data hard enough, the noise falls away,", "tokens": [51476, 440, 7107, 307, 300, 498, 291, 13578, 264, 1412, 1152, 1547, 11, 264, 5658, 8804, 1314, 11, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12687953880855016, "compression_ratio": 1.613240418118467, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370733115124824e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 232038, "start": 2346.2200000000003, "end": 2348.62, "text": " and only the pure, fundamental truth remains.", "tokens": [51657, 293, 787, 264, 6075, 11, 8088, 3494, 7023, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12687953880855016, "compression_ratio": 1.613240418118467, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370733115124824e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 232038, "start": 2348.86, "end": 2349.1, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51789, 1779, 13, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12687953880855016, "compression_ratio": 1.613240418118467, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370733115124824e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 234910, "start": 2349.1, "end": 2352.66, "text": " It's like trying to pack a suitcase by blindly throwing out half your clothes,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 2844, 257, 34545, 538, 47744, 10238, 484, 1922, 428, 5534, 11, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12060394287109374, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426213687859015e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 234910, "start": 2352.8199999999997, "end": 2356.66, "text": " cramming the rest into a tiny bag, and then confidently claiming to the world", "tokens": [50551, 941, 335, 2810, 264, 1472, 666, 257, 5870, 3411, 11, 293, 550, 41956, 19232, 281, 264, 1002, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12060394287109374, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426213687859015e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 234910, "start": 2356.66, "end": 2360.74, "text": " that because your suitcase is lighter, you fundamentally understand travel better.", "tokens": [50743, 300, 570, 428, 34545, 307, 11546, 11, 291, 17879, 1223, 3147, 1101, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12060394287109374, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426213687859015e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 234910, "start": 2360.94, "end": 2362.3399999999997, "text": " That is a brilliant analogy.", "tokens": [50957, 663, 307, 257, 10248, 21663, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12060394287109374, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426213687859015e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 234910, "start": 2362.74, "end": 2368.16, "text": " And the math from the ontological triple shows exactly why that AI methodology is standing on thin air.", "tokens": [51047, 400, 264, 5221, 490, 264, 6592, 4383, 15508, 3110, 2293, 983, 300, 7318, 24850, 307, 4877, 322, 5862, 1988, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12060394287109374, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426213687859015e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 234910, "start": 2368.68, "end": 2370.3399999999997, "text": " Remember the deficit proxy theorem.", "tokens": [51344, 5459, 264, 22132, 29690, 20904, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12060394287109374, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426213687859015e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 234910, "start": 2370.7, "end": 2375.8399999999997, "text": " The one direction it does prove, that perfect compression guarantees perfect distinguishing capacity,", "tokens": [51445, 440, 472, 3513, 309, 775, 7081, 11, 300, 2176, 19355, 32567, 2176, 11365, 3807, 6042, 11, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12060394287109374, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426213687859015e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 237584, "start": 2375.84, "end": 2380.6800000000003, "text": " relies on a very specific mathematical assumption called faithful encoding.", "tokens": [50365, 30910, 322, 257, 588, 2685, 18894, 15302, 1219, 17808, 43430, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21184648226385247, "compression_ratio": 1.6683937823834196, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428724920926729e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 237584, "start": 2380.6800000000003, "end": 2382.04, "text": " Right, faithful encoding.", "tokens": [50607, 1779, 11, 17808, 43430, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21184648226385247, "compression_ratio": 1.6683937823834196, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428724920926729e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 237584, "start": 2382.4, "end": 2386.06, "text": " The assumption that every distinct feature costs exactly one bit to express.", "tokens": [50693, 440, 15302, 300, 633, 10644, 4111, 5497, 2293, 472, 857, 281, 5109, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21184648226385247, "compression_ratio": 1.6683937823834196, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428724920926729e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 237584, "start": 2386.3, "end": 2387.32, "text": " One bit, one feature.", "tokens": [50888, 1485, 857, 11, 472, 4111, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21184648226385247, "compression_ratio": 1.6683937823834196, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428724920926729e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 237584, "start": 2387.6800000000003, "end": 2392.28, "text": " But neural networks, by their very nature, do not use faithful encoding.", "tokens": [50957, 583, 18161, 9590, 11, 538, 641, 588, 3687, 11, 360, 406, 764, 17808, 43430, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21184648226385247, "compression_ratio": 1.6683937823834196, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428724920926729e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 237584, "start": 2392.7200000000003, "end": 2395.4, "text": " They use distributed, superposed representation.", "tokens": [51209, 814, 764, 12631, 11, 1687, 79, 1744, 10290, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21184648226385247, "compression_ratio": 1.6683937823834196, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428724920926729e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 239540, "start": 2395.4, "end": 2398.96, "text": " Superposition, meaning things are tangled up.", "tokens": [50365, 4548, 38078, 11, 3620, 721, 366, 47192, 493, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2104899247487386, "compression_ratio": 1.6057142857142856, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503496040407242e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 239540, "start": 2398.96, "end": 2399.6800000000003, "text": " Highly tangled.", "tokens": [50543, 5229, 356, 47192, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2104899247487386, "compression_ratio": 1.6057142857142856, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503496040407242e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 239540, "start": 2400.28, "end": 2406.4, "text": " In a neural network, a single direction or vector in an activation space might participate in encoding multiple,", "tokens": [50609, 682, 257, 18161, 3209, 11, 257, 2167, 3513, 420, 8062, 294, 364, 24433, 1901, 1062, 8197, 294, 43430, 3866, 11, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2104899247487386, "compression_ratio": 1.6057142857142856, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503496040407242e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 239540, "start": 2406.58, "end": 2412.64, "text": " completely unrelated features, and a single feature might be encoded across multiple scattered directions.", "tokens": [50924, 2584, 38967, 4122, 11, 293, 257, 2167, 4111, 1062, 312, 2058, 12340, 2108, 3866, 21986, 11095, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2104899247487386, "compression_ratio": 1.6057142857142856, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503496040407242e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 241264, "start": 2412.64, "end": 2415.5, "text": " So the bits are doing double, triple, quadruple duty.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 9239, 366, 884, 3834, 11, 15508, 11, 10787, 894, 781, 9776, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14365242373558781, "compression_ratio": 1.5418326693227091, "no_speech_prob": 2.020441973449305e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 241264, "start": 2416.02, "end": 2418.48, "text": " The redness of an apple isn't stored in one neuron.", "tokens": [50534, 440, 2182, 1287, 295, 364, 10606, 1943, 380, 12187, 294, 472, 34090, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14365242373558781, "compression_ratio": 1.5418326693227091, "no_speech_prob": 2.020441973449305e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 241264, "start": 2418.64, "end": 2424.64, "text": " It's smeared across a thousand neurons, which are also simultaneously storing the roundness of a baseball.", "tokens": [50665, 467, 311, 41818, 1642, 2108, 257, 4714, 22027, 11, 597, 366, 611, 16561, 26085, 264, 3098, 1287, 295, 257, 14323, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14365242373558781, "compression_ratio": 1.5418326693227091, "no_speech_prob": 2.020441973449305e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 241264, "start": 2425.02, "end": 2425.5, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50984, 7587, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14365242373558781, "compression_ratio": 1.5418326693227091, "no_speech_prob": 2.020441973449305e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 241264, "start": 2426.18, "end": 2431.04, "text": " And because superposed representations violate the foundational assumption of faithful encoding,", "tokens": [51042, 400, 570, 1687, 79, 1744, 33358, 37478, 264, 32195, 15302, 295, 17808, 43430, 11, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14365242373558781, "compression_ratio": 1.5418326693227091, "no_speech_prob": 2.020441973449305e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 241264, "start": 2431.58, "end": 2435.16, "text": " the deficit proxy theorem breaks down entirely in this setting.", "tokens": [51312, 264, 22132, 29690, 20904, 9857, 760, 7696, 294, 341, 3287, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14365242373558781, "compression_ratio": 1.5418326693227091, "no_speech_prob": 2.020441973449305e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 241264, "start": 2435.42, "end": 2435.66, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51504, 3153, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14365242373558781, "compression_ratio": 1.5418326693227091, "no_speech_prob": 2.020441973449305e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 243566, "start": 2435.66, "end": 2443.64, "text": " In a superposed system, making an AI model's latent representation smaller carries absolutely no mathematically guaranteed relationship", "tokens": [50365, 682, 257, 1687, 79, 1744, 1185, 11, 1455, 364, 7318, 2316, 311, 48994, 10290, 4356, 16402, 3122, 572, 44003, 18031, 2480, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12737390854779412, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969037274442103e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 243566, "start": 2443.64, "end": 2447.2999999999997, "text": " to its actual distinguishing capacity or its understanding of the data.", "tokens": [50764, 281, 1080, 3539, 11365, 3807, 6042, 420, 1080, 3701, 295, 264, 1412, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12737390854779412, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969037274442103e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 243566, "start": 2447.46, "end": 2447.7599999999998, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50955, 3153, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12737390854779412, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969037274442103e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 243566, "start": 2448.3199999999997, "end": 2449.3199999999997, "text": " Let me just sit with that.", "tokens": [50998, 961, 385, 445, 1394, 365, 300, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12737390854779412, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969037274442103e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 243566, "start": 2449.74, "end": 2454.6, "text": " So when AI researchers force a model to brutally compress its representation,", "tokens": [51069, 407, 562, 7318, 10309, 3464, 257, 2316, 281, 48476, 14778, 1080, 10290, 11, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12737390854779412, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969037274442103e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 243566, "start": 2455.1, "end": 2459.74, "text": " and then they publish a paper pointing to that smaller, sparser representation", "tokens": [51337, 293, 550, 436, 11374, 257, 3035, 12166, 281, 300, 4356, 11, 637, 685, 260, 10290, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12737390854779412, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969037274442103e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 245974, "start": 2459.74, "end": 2466.0, "text": " as empirical evidence that the model has finally learned the true disentangled structure of the data,", "tokens": [50365, 382, 31886, 4467, 300, 264, 2316, 575, 2721, 3264, 264, 2074, 37313, 39101, 3877, 295, 264, 1412, 11, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 245974, "start": 2466.3199999999997, "end": 2468.24, "text": " they were scientifically unjustified.", "tokens": [50694, 436, 645, 39719, 37046, 2587, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 245974, "start": 2468.3199999999997, "end": 2470.64, "text": " They are using a heuristic as if it were a theorem.", "tokens": [50794, 814, 366, 1228, 257, 415, 374, 3142, 382, 498, 309, 645, 257, 20904, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 245974, "start": 2471.14, "end": 2475.54, "text": " They are confusing a smaller coding deficit with a smaller distinguishability deficit.", "tokens": [50935, 814, 366, 13181, 257, 4356, 17720, 22132, 365, 257, 4356, 20206, 2310, 22132, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 245974, "start": 2476.16, "end": 2479.64, "text": " Now, to be fair, the paper isn't saying compression is practically useless.", "tokens": [51186, 823, 11, 281, 312, 3143, 11, 264, 3035, 1943, 380, 1566, 19355, 307, 15667, 14115, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 245974, "start": 2480.0, "end": 2481.22, "text": " Right, like efficiency matters.", "tokens": [51378, 1779, 11, 411, 10493, 7001, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 245974, "start": 2481.4199999999996, "end": 2484.1, "text": " Efficiency is a highly valid engineering goal.", "tokens": [51449, 462, 49086, 307, 257, 5405, 7363, 7043, 3387, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 245974, "start": 2484.1, "end": 2487.4599999999996, "text": " If you want the model to run faster on a cheaper chip, compress it.", "tokens": [51583, 759, 291, 528, 264, 2316, 281, 1190, 4663, 322, 257, 12284, 11409, 11, 14778, 309, 13, 51751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15827447940141726, "compression_ratio": 1.7335640138408304, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924126147015e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 248746, "start": 2487.46, "end": 2493.18, "text": " But we cannot treat a reduction in apparent size as epistemic evidence of deeper understanding.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 321, 2644, 2387, 257, 11004, 294, 18335, 2744, 382, 2388, 468, 3438, 4467, 295, 7731, 3701, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14070947391470684, "compression_ratio": 1.6330935251798562, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009177470637797e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 248746, "start": 2493.6, "end": 2497.42, "text": " That is a devastating critique of how we measure AI intelligence right now.", "tokens": [50672, 663, 307, 257, 21280, 25673, 295, 577, 321, 3481, 7318, 7599, 558, 586, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14070947391470684, "compression_ratio": 1.6330935251798562, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009177470637797e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 248746, "start": 2497.96, "end": 2500.26, "text": " But flixion doesn't stop at artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [50890, 583, 932, 970, 313, 1177, 380, 1590, 412, 11677, 7599, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14070947391470684, "compression_ratio": 1.6330935251798562, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009177470637797e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 248746, "start": 2500.68, "end": 2505.44, "text": " The paper looks for biological proof to show that compression isn't the ultimate goal of learning in nature either.", "tokens": [51026, 440, 3035, 1542, 337, 13910, 8177, 281, 855, 300, 19355, 1943, 380, 264, 9705, 3387, 295, 2539, 294, 3687, 2139, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14070947391470684, "compression_ratio": 1.6330935251798562, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009177470637797e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 248746, "start": 2505.98, "end": 2507.7, "text": " It looks at human childhood development.", "tokens": [51291, 467, 1542, 412, 1952, 9278, 3250, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14070947391470684, "compression_ratio": 1.6330935251798562, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009177470637797e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 248746, "start": 2508.0, "end": 2511.7400000000002, "text": " This is such a beautiful convergence of evidence from cognitive science.", "tokens": [51392, 639, 307, 1270, 257, 2238, 32181, 295, 4467, 490, 15605, 3497, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14070947391470684, "compression_ratio": 1.6330935251798562, "no_speech_prob": 2.1009177470637797e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 251174, "start": 2511.74, "end": 2519.7799999999997, "text": " The developmental research on the explore-exploit trade-off shows that human childhood is uniquely evolutionarily long for a reason.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 30160, 2132, 322, 264, 6839, 12, 3121, 21132, 270, 4923, 12, 4506, 3110, 300, 1952, 9278, 307, 31474, 9303, 3289, 938, 337, 257, 1778, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15173814326156804, "compression_ratio": 1.554054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.981066135789411e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 251174, "start": 2520.7, "end": 2524.2, "text": " Young children operate in a mode of pure exploration.", "tokens": [50813, 8160, 2227, 9651, 294, 257, 4391, 295, 6075, 16197, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15173814326156804, "compression_ratio": 1.554054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.981066135789411e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 251174, "start": 2524.7, "end": 2528.3799999999997, "text": " They explore broadly, wildly, and incredibly inefficiently.", "tokens": [51013, 814, 6839, 19511, 11, 34731, 11, 293, 6252, 43495, 356, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15173814326156804, "compression_ratio": 1.554054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.981066135789411e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 251174, "start": 2528.68, "end": 2533.2, "text": " They generate high entropy, complex hypotheses about how the world works.", "tokens": [51212, 814, 8460, 1090, 30867, 11, 3997, 49969, 466, 577, 264, 1002, 1985, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15173814326156804, "compression_ratio": 1.554054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.981066135789411e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 251174, "start": 2533.2999999999997, "end": 2534.08, "text": " They make a mess.", "tokens": [51443, 814, 652, 257, 2082, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15173814326156804, "compression_ratio": 1.554054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.981066135789411e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 251174, "start": 2534.2, "end": 2534.3399999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51488, 1779, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15173814326156804, "compression_ratio": 1.554054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.981066135789411e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 253434, "start": 2534.34, "end": 2539.2200000000003, "text": " If a kid is trying to figure out how a toy works, they don't look for the shortest, most logical path.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 1636, 307, 1382, 281, 2573, 484, 577, 257, 12058, 1985, 11, 436, 500, 380, 574, 337, 264, 31875, 11, 881, 14978, 3100, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 253434, "start": 2539.48, "end": 2540.54, "text": " They bang it on the table.", "tokens": [50622, 814, 8550, 309, 322, 264, 3199, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 253434, "start": 2540.6400000000003, "end": 2541.32, "text": " They put it in their mouth.", "tokens": [50680, 814, 829, 309, 294, 641, 4525, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 253434, "start": 2541.38, "end": 2542.3, "text": " They throw it across the room.", "tokens": [50717, 814, 3507, 309, 2108, 264, 1808, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 253434, "start": 2542.36, "end": 2544.6400000000003, "text": " They try everything, even when it doesn't make sense.", "tokens": [50766, 814, 853, 1203, 11, 754, 562, 309, 1177, 380, 652, 2020, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 253434, "start": 2544.98, "end": 2545.2400000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50897, 1779, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 253434, "start": 2545.6200000000003, "end": 2550.78, "text": " And if human cognition were fundamentally driven by a primary desire for rapid compression,", "tokens": [50929, 400, 498, 1952, 46905, 645, 17879, 9555, 538, 257, 6194, 7516, 337, 7558, 19355, 11, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 253434, "start": 2551.2200000000003, "end": 2555.1200000000003, "text": " if understanding simply meant finding the shortest description as quickly as possible,", "tokens": [51209, 498, 3701, 2935, 4140, 5006, 264, 31875, 3855, 382, 2661, 382, 1944, 11, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 253434, "start": 2555.6400000000003, "end": 2559.96, "text": " children would lock into narrow, highly compressed hypotheses way too early.", "tokens": [51430, 2227, 576, 4017, 666, 9432, 11, 5405, 30353, 49969, 636, 886, 2440, 13, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13243355238733212, "compression_ratio": 1.6503267973856208, "no_speech_prob": 1.454759381534776e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 255996, "start": 2559.96, "end": 2563.86, "text": " They would converge on the first local efficiency gain they found.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 576, 41881, 322, 264, 700, 2654, 10493, 6052, 436, 1352, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1818272192266923, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 2.175755886221764e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 255996, "start": 2564.2200000000003, "end": 2565.64, "text": " Like, if I cry, I get milk.", "tokens": [50578, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 3305, 11, 286, 483, 5392, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1818272192266923, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 2.175755886221764e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 255996, "start": 2565.94, "end": 2567.12, "text": " I understand the universe.", "tokens": [50664, 286, 1223, 264, 6445, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1818272192266923, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 2.175755886221764e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 255996, "start": 2567.28, "end": 2568.7, "text": " I will now only ever cry.", "tokens": [50731, 286, 486, 586, 787, 1562, 3305, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1818272192266923, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 2.175755886221764e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 255996, "start": 2569.62, "end": 2576.8, "text": " If they were purely compressing, they'd never learn anything complex because they'd stop exploring the minute they found a simple rule that technically works.", "tokens": [50848, 759, 436, 645, 17491, 14778, 278, 11, 436, 1116, 1128, 1466, 1340, 3997, 570, 436, 1116, 1590, 12736, 264, 3456, 436, 1352, 257, 2199, 4978, 300, 12120, 1985, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1818272192266923, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 2.175755886221764e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 255996, "start": 2576.9, "end": 2577.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51212, 7587, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1818272192266923, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 2.175755886221764e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 257728, "start": 2577.28, "end": 2584.0800000000004, "text": " True skilled performance later in life, whether it's playing a violin, navigating social politics, or doing advanced mathematics,", "tokens": [50365, 13587, 19690, 3389, 1780, 294, 993, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 2433, 257, 22878, 11, 32054, 2093, 7341, 11, 420, 884, 7339, 18666, 11, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09573481393897015, "compression_ratio": 1.539568345323741, "no_speech_prob": 1.708053945677357e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 257728, "start": 2584.34, "end": 2594.1400000000003, "text": " depends on preserving subtle distinctions that a purely exploitative, compression-driven learner would have aggressively discarded as useless noise early on.", "tokens": [50718, 5946, 322, 33173, 13743, 1483, 49798, 300, 257, 17491, 12382, 14275, 11, 19355, 12, 25456, 33347, 576, 362, 32024, 45469, 382, 14115, 5658, 2440, 322, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09573481393897015, "compression_ratio": 1.539568345323741, "no_speech_prob": 1.708053945677357e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 257728, "start": 2594.3, "end": 2597.8, "text": " The paper also talks about environmental scaffolding, which I found fascinating.", "tokens": [51216, 440, 3035, 611, 6686, 466, 8303, 44094, 278, 11, 597, 286, 1352, 10343, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09573481393897015, "compression_ratio": 1.539568345323741, "no_speech_prob": 1.708053945677357e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 257728, "start": 2597.98, "end": 2598.1800000000003, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51400, 865, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09573481393897015, "compression_ratio": 1.539568345323741, "no_speech_prob": 1.708053945677357e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 257728, "start": 2598.26, "end": 2600.1200000000003, "text": " Because we do simplify things for kids, right?", "tokens": [51414, 1436, 321, 360, 20460, 721, 337, 2301, 11, 558, 30, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09573481393897015, "compression_ratio": 1.539568345323741, "no_speech_prob": 1.708053945677357e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 257728, "start": 2600.1600000000003, "end": 2600.6600000000003, "text": " We do.", "tokens": [51509, 492, 360, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09573481393897015, "compression_ratio": 1.539568345323741, "no_speech_prob": 1.708053945677357e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 260066, "start": 2600.66, "end": 2606.48, "text": " We build scaffolds, simple, low-entropy environments like pleapens or basic preschool curriculums.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1322, 40889, 31518, 11, 2199, 11, 2295, 12, 317, 27514, 12388, 411, 3362, 569, 694, 420, 3875, 39809, 13179, 425, 8099, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15262387706115182, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485650514320605e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 260066, "start": 2606.6, "end": 2609.1, "text": " But we don't do this because reality is simple.", "tokens": [50662, 583, 321, 500, 380, 360, 341, 570, 4103, 307, 2199, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15262387706115182, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485650514320605e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 260066, "start": 2609.24, "end": 2615.3999999999996, "text": " We do it because a learner who hasn't built up any internal models yet will just fail if you throw them into full chaos.", "tokens": [50794, 492, 360, 309, 570, 257, 33347, 567, 6132, 380, 3094, 493, 604, 6920, 5245, 1939, 486, 445, 3061, 498, 291, 3507, 552, 666, 1577, 14158, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15262387706115182, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485650514320605e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 260066, "start": 2615.64, "end": 2615.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51114, 1779, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15262387706115182, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485650514320605e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 260066, "start": 2615.94, "end": 2618.2999999999997, "text": " The paper uses a great geometric analogy.", "tokens": [51129, 440, 3035, 4960, 257, 869, 33246, 21663, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15262387706115182, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485650514320605e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 260066, "start": 2619.06, "end": 2626.62, "text": " We build roads straight and flat, not because the surface of the earth is naturally straight and flat, but because our cars have bad suspensions.", "tokens": [51285, 492, 1322, 11344, 2997, 293, 4962, 11, 406, 570, 264, 3753, 295, 264, 4120, 307, 8195, 2997, 293, 4962, 11, 457, 570, 527, 5163, 362, 1578, 6535, 8302, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15262387706115182, "compression_ratio": 1.65, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485650514320605e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 262662, "start": 2626.62, "end": 2633.62, "text": " The low geometric entropy of the road, the simplicity compensates for the narrow tolerance of the vehicle.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2295, 33246, 30867, 295, 264, 3060, 11, 264, 25632, 11598, 1024, 337, 264, 9432, 23368, 295, 264, 5864, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15651066104571024, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324744933267967e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 262662, "start": 2633.94, "end": 2637.14, "text": " Okay, so we artificially compress the environment for the beginner.", "tokens": [50731, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 39905, 2270, 14778, 264, 2823, 337, 264, 22080, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15651066104571024, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324744933267967e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 262662, "start": 2637.7, "end": 2638.74, "text": " We give them training wheels.", "tokens": [50919, 492, 976, 552, 3097, 10046, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15651066104571024, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324744933267967e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 262662, "start": 2639.08, "end": 2646.02, "text": " But to actually achieve true expert understanding, what has to happen to that scaffold?", "tokens": [50988, 583, 281, 767, 4584, 2074, 5844, 3701, 11, 437, 575, 281, 1051, 281, 300, 44094, 30, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15651066104571024, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324744933267967e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 262662, "start": 2646.3399999999997, "end": 2647.58, "text": " The curriculum must widen.", "tokens": [51351, 440, 14302, 1633, 32552, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15651066104571024, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324744933267967e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 262662, "start": 2648.08, "end": 2653.8599999999997, "text": " Once a learner has mastered a scaffold, further progress doesn't come from compressing that simple environment even more.", "tokens": [51438, 3443, 257, 33347, 575, 38686, 257, 44094, 11, 3052, 4205, 1177, 380, 808, 490, 14778, 278, 300, 2199, 2823, 754, 544, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15651066104571024, "compression_ratio": 1.6455223880597014, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324744933267967e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 265386, "start": 2653.86, "end": 2657.7000000000003, "text": " It doesn't come from finding a shorter way to ride a bike with training wheels.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 808, 490, 5006, 257, 11639, 636, 281, 5077, 257, 5656, 365, 3097, 10046, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 265386, "start": 2658.0, "end": 2661.08, "text": " It comes from deliberately increasing the entropy of the environment.", "tokens": [50572, 467, 1487, 490, 23506, 5662, 264, 30867, 295, 264, 2823, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 265386, "start": 2661.56, "end": 2665.52, "text": " You have to reintroduce the messy complexity that the scaffold was originally hiding.", "tokens": [50750, 509, 362, 281, 319, 38132, 384, 264, 16191, 14024, 300, 264, 44094, 390, 7993, 10596, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 265386, "start": 2665.6800000000003, "end": 2666.84, "text": " You have to take the training wheels off.", "tokens": [50956, 509, 362, 281, 747, 264, 3097, 10046, 766, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 265386, "start": 2667.1200000000003, "end": 2670.08, "text": " You have to introduce the curves, the potholes, and the traffic into the road.", "tokens": [51028, 509, 362, 281, 5366, 264, 19490, 11, 264, 280, 900, 7456, 11, 293, 264, 6419, 666, 264, 3060, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 265386, "start": 2670.26, "end": 2670.52, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51185, 1079, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 265386, "start": 2671.04, "end": 2676.58, "text": " A curriculum that only simplifies and never widens terminates in a plateau, not in understanding.", "tokens": [51224, 316, 14302, 300, 787, 6883, 11221, 293, 1128, 5274, 694, 10761, 1024, 294, 257, 39885, 11, 406, 294, 3701, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 265386, "start": 2677.3, "end": 2683.04, "text": " Productive problem solving, true mastery, inevitably requires a deliberate detour into greater complexity.", "tokens": [51537, 22005, 488, 1154, 12606, 11, 2074, 37951, 11, 28171, 7029, 257, 30515, 1141, 396, 666, 5044, 14024, 13, 51824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500214209923377, "compression_ratio": 1.8258064516129033, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077903761292257e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 268304, "start": 2683.04, "end": 2692.2599999999998, "text": " So connecting this back to you, the listener, trying to navigate your own work or life, we are constantly bombarded with this messaging to optimize.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11015, 341, 646, 281, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 1382, 281, 12350, 428, 1065, 589, 420, 993, 11, 321, 366, 6460, 7851, 22803, 365, 341, 21812, 281, 19719, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13105383412591343, "compression_ratio": 1.6761565836298933, "no_speech_prob": 1.973636965663106e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 268304, "start": 2692.98, "end": 2696.96, "text": " Find the hack that compresses the problem down to a one-liner, automate this, shrink that.", "tokens": [50862, 11809, 264, 10339, 300, 14778, 279, 264, 1154, 760, 281, 257, 472, 12, 36849, 11, 31605, 341, 11, 23060, 300, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13105383412591343, "compression_ratio": 1.6761565836298933, "no_speech_prob": 1.973636965663106e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 268304, "start": 2697.52, "end": 2703.38, "text": " But this paper proves that productive problem solving requires a detour through greater complexity.", "tokens": [51089, 583, 341, 3035, 25019, 300, 13304, 1154, 12606, 7029, 257, 1141, 396, 807, 5044, 14024, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13105383412591343, "compression_ratio": 1.6761565836298933, "no_speech_prob": 1.973636965663106e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 268304, "start": 2704.06, "end": 2706.18, "text": " You cannot compress your way to genius.", "tokens": [51416, 509, 2644, 14778, 428, 636, 281, 14017, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13105383412591343, "compression_ratio": 1.6761565836298933, "no_speech_prob": 1.973636965663106e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 268304, "start": 2706.34, "end": 2707.36, "text": " It's so true.", "tokens": [51530, 467, 311, 370, 2074, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13105383412591343, "compression_ratio": 1.6761565836298933, "no_speech_prob": 1.973636965663106e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 268304, "start": 2707.7, "end": 2708.66, "text": " I think about my own life.", "tokens": [51598, 286, 519, 466, 452, 1065, 993, 13, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13105383412591343, "compression_ratio": 1.6761565836298933, "no_speech_prob": 1.973636965663106e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 268304, "start": 2708.7599999999998, "end": 2711.3, "text": " I used to try to over-optimize my morning routine.", "tokens": [51651, 286, 1143, 281, 853, 281, 670, 12, 5747, 43890, 452, 2446, 9927, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13105383412591343, "compression_ratio": 1.6761565836298933, "no_speech_prob": 1.973636965663106e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 271130, "start": 2711.3, "end": 2716.98, "text": " I wanted the shortest, most compressed sequence of events, from waking up to sitting at my desk.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 1415, 264, 31875, 11, 881, 30353, 8310, 295, 3931, 11, 490, 20447, 493, 281, 3798, 412, 452, 10026, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09214524242365471, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555081958080642e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 271130, "start": 2717.44, "end": 2718.2200000000003, "text": " And it was a disaster.", "tokens": [50672, 400, 309, 390, 257, 11293, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09214524242365471, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555081958080642e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 271130, "start": 2718.6000000000004, "end": 2723.42, "text": " If one tiny thing went wrong, if I spilled the coffee, the whole highly compressed system shattered.", "tokens": [50730, 759, 472, 5870, 551, 1437, 2085, 11, 498, 286, 37833, 264, 4982, 11, 264, 1379, 5405, 30353, 1185, 35209, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09214524242365471, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555081958080642e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 271130, "start": 2723.6400000000003, "end": 2728.1600000000003, "text": " Because I had stripped out all the slack, all the messy redundancies that actually make a morning robust.", "tokens": [50982, 1436, 286, 632, 33221, 484, 439, 264, 29767, 11, 439, 264, 16191, 27830, 32286, 300, 767, 652, 257, 2446, 13956, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09214524242365471, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555081958080642e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 271130, "start": 2728.26, "end": 2729.6400000000003, "text": " You fell into the brevity trap.", "tokens": [51213, 509, 5696, 666, 264, 1403, 23110, 11487, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09214524242365471, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555081958080642e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 271130, "start": 2729.76, "end": 2735.0, "text": " You sacrificed distinguishing capacity, the ability to handle different contextual states, for coding efficiency.", "tokens": [51288, 509, 32021, 11365, 3807, 6042, 11, 264, 3485, 281, 4813, 819, 35526, 4368, 11, 337, 17720, 10493, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09214524242365471, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555081958080642e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 273500, "start": 2735.0, "end": 2736.08, "text": " I absolutely did.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 3122, 630, 13, 50419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18317709340677632, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617353109857347e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 273500, "start": 2736.32, "end": 2742.38, "text": " If you are always trying to find the shortest answer, you're probably sacrificing the very distinctions that make the answer meaningful.", "tokens": [50431, 759, 291, 366, 1009, 1382, 281, 915, 264, 31875, 1867, 11, 291, 434, 1391, 42294, 264, 588, 1483, 49798, 300, 652, 264, 1867, 10995, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18317709340677632, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617353109857347e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 273500, "start": 2743.02, "end": 2744.12, "text": " Which is a perfect segue.", "tokens": [50766, 3013, 307, 257, 2176, 33850, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18317709340677632, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617353109857347e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 273500, "start": 2744.62, "end": 2750.18, "text": " Because what happens when those highly compressed, fragile systems inevitably shatter?", "tokens": [50846, 1436, 437, 2314, 562, 729, 5405, 30353, 11, 23847, 3652, 28171, 402, 1161, 30, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18317709340677632, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617353109857347e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 273500, "start": 2750.46, "end": 2750.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51138, 1779, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18317709340677632, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617353109857347e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 273500, "start": 2750.96, "end": 2753.64, "text": " That leads us perfectly into part three of our deep dive.", "tokens": [51163, 663, 6689, 505, 6239, 666, 644, 1045, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18317709340677632, "compression_ratio": 1.4887892376681615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617353109857347e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 275364, "start": 2753.64, "end": 2758.06, "text": " The architecture of survival, or restoration before explanation.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 9482, 295, 12559, 11, 420, 23722, 949, 10835, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15620877021966978, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.661977955431937e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 275364, "start": 2758.7799999999997, "end": 2767.62, "text": " Because if we agree that true understanding requires messy complexity rather than neat compression, how do we fix these complex systems when they go wrong?", "tokens": [50622, 1436, 498, 321, 3986, 300, 2074, 3701, 7029, 16191, 14024, 2831, 813, 10654, 19355, 11, 577, 360, 321, 3191, 613, 3997, 3652, 562, 436, 352, 2085, 30, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15620877021966978, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.661977955431937e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 275364, "start": 2767.62, "end": 2773.16, "text": " The prevailing cultural assumption is, well, to fix it, you have to fully understand it.", "tokens": [51064, 440, 12642, 23315, 6988, 15302, 307, 11, 731, 11, 281, 3191, 309, 11, 291, 362, 281, 4498, 1223, 309, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15620877021966978, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.661977955431937e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 275364, "start": 2773.24, "end": 2774.22, "text": " You have to have the blueprint.", "tokens": [51345, 509, 362, 281, 362, 264, 35868, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15620877021966978, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.661977955431937e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 275364, "start": 2774.7799999999997, "end": 2777.2799999999997, "text": " You need a complete explanation of the root cause.", "tokens": [51422, 509, 643, 257, 3566, 10835, 295, 264, 5593, 3082, 13, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15620877021966978, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.661977955431937e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 277728, "start": 2777.28, "end": 2787.84, "text": " But the third paper in Flyxion's stack brings us to a radical, counterintuitive conclusion that completely validates that 1954 kidney transplant story we started with.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 2636, 3035, 11, 682, 3423, 4105, 37649, 11, 5607, 505, 281, 257, 12001, 11, 5682, 686, 48314, 10063, 300, 2584, 7363, 1024, 300, 46590, 19000, 20662, 1657, 321, 1409, 365, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08812394768300683, "compression_ratio": 1.58843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213638946380946e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 277728, "start": 2788.6200000000003, "end": 2797.2400000000002, "text": " The pager argues that functional restoration routinely precedes, and fundamentally does not require, an explicit explanation of how that restoration works.", "tokens": [50932, 440, 280, 3557, 38218, 300, 11745, 23722, 40443, 16969, 279, 11, 293, 17879, 775, 406, 3651, 11, 364, 13691, 10835, 295, 577, 300, 23722, 1985, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08812394768300683, "compression_ratio": 1.58843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213638946380946e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 277728, "start": 2797.36, "end": 2801.0, "text": " You can fix it reliably and repeatedly without knowing how you fixed it.", "tokens": [51369, 509, 393, 3191, 309, 49927, 293, 18227, 1553, 5276, 577, 291, 6806, 309, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08812394768300683, "compression_ratio": 1.58843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213638946380946e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 277728, "start": 2801.0800000000004, "end": 2804.0800000000004, "text": " And the paper arrives at this through what it calls a dual decoupling.", "tokens": [51555, 400, 264, 3035, 20116, 412, 341, 807, 437, 309, 5498, 257, 11848, 979, 263, 11970, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08812394768300683, "compression_ratio": 1.58843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213638946380946e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 280408, "start": 2804.08, "end": 2810.7, "text": " It points out that two completely separate theoretical frameworks arrived at this exact same conclusion simultaneously.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2793, 484, 300, 732, 2584, 4994, 20864, 29834, 6678, 412, 341, 1900, 912, 10063, 16561, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13853171238532433, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760829699314806e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 280408, "start": 2811.1, "end": 2812.38, "text": " Let's look at the first decoupling.", "tokens": [50716, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 700, 979, 263, 11970, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13853171238532433, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760829699314806e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 280408, "start": 2812.64, "end": 2816.56, "text": " The first decoupling comes from a general theory of recoverable persistence.", "tokens": [50793, 440, 700, 979, 263, 11970, 1487, 490, 257, 2674, 5261, 295, 8114, 712, 37617, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13853171238532433, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760829699314806e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 280408, "start": 2817.4, "end": 2821.52, "text": " This theory formally states that prediction is totally separate from explanation.", "tokens": [51031, 639, 5261, 25983, 4368, 300, 17630, 307, 3879, 4994, 490, 10835, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13853171238532433, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760829699314806e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 280408, "start": 2821.96, "end": 2823.4, "text": " Prediction versus explanation.", "tokens": [51259, 32969, 4105, 5717, 10835, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13853171238532433, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760829699314806e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 280408, "start": 2824.06, "end": 2828.12, "text": " Let's make sure we have this logically clear, because we often use those words interchangeably.", "tokens": [51364, 961, 311, 652, 988, 321, 362, 341, 38887, 1850, 11, 570, 321, 2049, 764, 729, 2283, 30358, 1188, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13853171238532433, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760829699314806e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 280408, "start": 2828.2999999999997, "end": 2831.88, "text": " Prediction in this framework means successful extrapolation.", "tokens": [51576, 32969, 4105, 294, 341, 8388, 1355, 4406, 48224, 399, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13853171238532433, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760829699314806e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 283188, "start": 2831.88, "end": 2834.8, "text": " A system can accurately extend a pattern.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1185, 393, 20095, 10101, 257, 5102, 13, 50511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15553103671984725, "compression_ratio": 1.5809128630705394, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884409030481826e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 283188, "start": 2835.32, "end": 2838.6, "text": " It can tell you what state will happen next, given the current state.", "tokens": [50537, 467, 393, 980, 291, 437, 1785, 486, 1051, 958, 11, 2212, 264, 2190, 1785, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15553103671984725, "compression_ratio": 1.5809128630705394, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884409030481826e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 283188, "start": 2839.48, "end": 2842.9, "text": " Explanation, however, is defined as distinction repair.", "tokens": [50745, 12514, 282, 399, 11, 4461, 11, 307, 7642, 382, 16844, 10535, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15553103671984725, "compression_ratio": 1.5809128630705394, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884409030481826e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 283188, "start": 2843.2400000000002, "end": 2844.08, "text": " Distinction repair?", "tokens": [50933, 9840, 12987, 10535, 30, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15553103671984725, "compression_ratio": 1.5809128630705394, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884409030481826e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 283188, "start": 2844.34, "end": 2844.62, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50988, 1079, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15553103671984725, "compression_ratio": 1.5809128630705394, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884409030481826e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 283188, "start": 2845.2000000000003, "end": 2853.5, "text": " A theory explains something when it takes disconnected data points or fragmented observations and reconstructs the underlying causal structure connecting them.", "tokens": [51031, 316, 5261, 13948, 746, 562, 309, 2516, 29426, 1412, 2793, 420, 9241, 14684, 18163, 293, 31499, 82, 264, 14217, 38755, 3877, 11015, 552, 13, 51446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15553103671984725, "compression_ratio": 1.5809128630705394, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884409030481826e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 283188, "start": 2853.56, "end": 2854.54, "text": " Okay, let me try an analogy.", "tokens": [51449, 1033, 11, 718, 385, 853, 364, 21663, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15553103671984725, "compression_ratio": 1.5809128630705394, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884409030481826e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 285454, "start": 2854.54, "end": 2861.46, "text": " If I observe that the sun rises in the east every single morning, I can predict with 100% accuracy that it will rise in the east tomorrow.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 11441, 300, 264, 3295, 21373, 294, 264, 10648, 633, 2167, 2446, 11, 286, 393, 6069, 365, 2319, 4, 14170, 300, 309, 486, 6272, 294, 264, 10648, 4153, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566614027946226, "compression_ratio": 1.567099567099567, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552549261805716e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 285454, "start": 2861.8, "end": 2863.74, "text": " That is successful extrapolation.", "tokens": [50728, 663, 307, 4406, 48224, 399, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566614027946226, "compression_ratio": 1.567099567099567, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552549261805716e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 285454, "start": 2864.02, "end": 2864.42, "text": " Prediction.", "tokens": [50839, 32969, 4105, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566614027946226, "compression_ratio": 1.567099567099567, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552549261805716e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 285454, "start": 2864.62, "end": 2864.82, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50869, 1779, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566614027946226, "compression_ratio": 1.567099567099567, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552549261805716e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 285454, "start": 2865.06, "end": 2872.0, "text": " But if you ask me why it happens, and I have to explain orbital mechanics, the rotation of the earth in gravity, that is distinction repair.", "tokens": [50891, 583, 498, 291, 1029, 385, 983, 309, 2314, 11, 293, 286, 362, 281, 2903, 27677, 12939, 11, 264, 12447, 295, 264, 4120, 294, 12110, 11, 300, 307, 16844, 10535, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566614027946226, "compression_ratio": 1.567099567099567, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552549261805716e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 285454, "start": 2872.24, "end": 2873.24, "text": " That is explanation.", "tokens": [51250, 663, 307, 10835, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566614027946226, "compression_ratio": 1.567099567099567, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552549261805716e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 285454, "start": 2873.88, "end": 2874.36, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51332, 7587, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1566614027946226, "compression_ratio": 1.567099567099567, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552549261805716e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 287436, "start": 2874.36, "end": 2878.2400000000002, "text": " And the theory proves mathematically that these are independent operations.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 5261, 25019, 44003, 300, 613, 366, 6695, 7705, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19024511662925161, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941661631238333e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 287436, "start": 2879.1, "end": 2883.5, "text": " A system can achieve perfect prediction without possessing any explanation whatsoever.", "tokens": [50602, 316, 1185, 393, 4584, 2176, 17630, 1553, 17490, 278, 604, 10835, 17076, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19024511662925161, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941661631238333e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 287436, "start": 2884.48, "end": 2890.36, "text": " Early humans predicted the sunrise perfectly for millennia without knowing a single thing about orbital mechanics.", "tokens": [50871, 18344, 6255, 19147, 264, 33675, 6239, 337, 21362, 654, 1553, 5276, 257, 2167, 551, 466, 27677, 12939, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19024511662925161, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941661631238333e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 287436, "start": 2891.1600000000003, "end": 2892.6400000000003, "text": " Okay, so that's the first decoupling.", "tokens": [51205, 1033, 11, 370, 300, 311, 264, 700, 979, 263, 11970, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19024511662925161, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941661631238333e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 287436, "start": 2893.06, "end": 2894.84, "text": " Prediction does not require explanation.", "tokens": [51300, 32969, 4105, 775, 406, 3651, 10835, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19024511662925161, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941661631238333e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 287436, "start": 2895.42, "end": 2896.6600000000003, "text": " What's the second decoupling?", "tokens": [51418, 708, 311, 264, 1150, 979, 263, 11970, 30, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19024511662925161, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941661631238333e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 289666, "start": 2896.66, "end": 2901.2799999999997, "text": " The second comes from a formal architecture for admissibility tracking.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1150, 1487, 490, 257, 9860, 9482, 337, 5910, 891, 2841, 11603, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 289666, "start": 2901.8799999999997, "end": 2905.66, "text": " This one separates functional adequacy from architectural transparency.", "tokens": [50626, 639, 472, 34149, 11745, 15747, 2551, 490, 26621, 17131, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 289666, "start": 2906.52, "end": 2907.62, "text": " Those are heavy terms.", "tokens": [50858, 3950, 366, 4676, 2115, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 289666, "start": 2908.16, "end": 2909.42, "text": " Let's break them down mechanically.", "tokens": [50940, 961, 311, 1821, 552, 760, 4236, 984, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 289666, "start": 2909.6, "end": 2914.48, "text": " Functional adequacy simply means the system's behavior correctly tracks the truth of its environment.", "tokens": [51012, 11166, 41048, 15747, 2551, 2935, 1355, 264, 1185, 311, 5223, 8944, 10218, 264, 3494, 295, 1080, 2823, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 289666, "start": 2915.12, "end": 2922.48, "text": " It gives the right answers, it performs the right actions, and it achieves its goals regardless of what internal hidden mechanism is producing that behavior.", "tokens": [51288, 467, 2709, 264, 558, 6338, 11, 309, 26213, 264, 558, 5909, 11, 293, 309, 3538, 977, 1080, 5493, 10060, 295, 437, 6920, 7633, 7513, 307, 10501, 300, 5223, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 289666, "start": 2922.62, "end": 2923.14, "text": " It works.", "tokens": [51663, 467, 1985, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 289666, "start": 2923.2599999999998, "end": 2924.14, "text": " It gets the job done.", "tokens": [51695, 467, 2170, 264, 1691, 1096, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14598059220747514, "compression_ratio": 1.7272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610217533687745e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 292414, "start": 2924.14, "end": 2927.8399999999997, "text": " That's functional adequacy and architectural transparency.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 11745, 15747, 2551, 293, 26621, 17131, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11487029297183259, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106087817602255e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 292414, "start": 2928.42, "end": 2938.64, "text": " Architectural transparency means that you can open the system up, inspect its internals, and explicitly point to a localized object, a mechanism, or a line of code that is tracking that truth.", "tokens": [50579, 29306, 1807, 17131, 1355, 300, 291, 393, 1269, 264, 1185, 493, 11, 15018, 1080, 2154, 1124, 11, 293, 20803, 935, 281, 257, 44574, 2657, 11, 257, 7513, 11, 420, 257, 1622, 295, 3089, 300, 307, 11603, 300, 3494, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11487029297183259, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106087817602255e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 292414, "start": 2938.94, "end": 2942.2799999999997, "text": " You can point to the exact gear in the clock that is doing the work.", "tokens": [51105, 509, 393, 935, 281, 264, 1900, 7394, 294, 264, 7830, 300, 307, 884, 264, 589, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11487029297183259, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106087817602255e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 292414, "start": 2942.4, "end": 2942.64, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51278, 1779, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11487029297183259, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106087817602255e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 292414, "start": 2942.94, "end": 2950.8599999999997, "text": " And the architectural theory proves that a system can achieve perfect functional adequacy while remaining completely architecturally opaque.", "tokens": [51305, 400, 264, 26621, 5261, 25019, 300, 257, 1185, 393, 4584, 2176, 11745, 15747, 2551, 1339, 8877, 2584, 6331, 6512, 42687, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11487029297183259, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106087817602255e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 295086, "start": 2950.86, "end": 2959.1200000000003, "text": " You can have a system that behaves perfectly, and no amount of probing its internals will reveal an explicit representation of how it's doing it.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 362, 257, 1185, 300, 36896, 6239, 11, 293, 572, 2372, 295, 1239, 278, 1080, 2154, 1124, 486, 10658, 364, 13691, 10290, 295, 577, 309, 311, 884, 309, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11499007124649852, "compression_ratio": 1.5406698564593302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 295086, "start": 2959.48, "end": 2965.52, "text": " Because, tying it back to our earlier discussion, the mechanism might be a superposed, distributed representation.", "tokens": [50796, 1436, 11, 32405, 309, 646, 281, 527, 3071, 5017, 11, 264, 7513, 1062, 312, 257, 1687, 79, 1744, 11, 12631, 10290, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11499007124649852, "compression_ratio": 1.5406698564593302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 295086, "start": 2965.6600000000003, "end": 2968.36, "text": " It's smeared everywhere, so you can't point to a single gear.", "tokens": [51105, 467, 311, 41818, 1642, 5315, 11, 370, 291, 393, 380, 935, 281, 257, 2167, 7394, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11499007124649852, "compression_ratio": 1.5406698564593302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 296836, "start": 2968.36, "end": 2968.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1617485951569121, "compression_ratio": 1.46875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875396479515414e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 296836, "start": 2968.86, "end": 2981.7200000000003, "text": " So, combining these two frameworks, you can perfectly restore a system's functional adequacy, make it predict correctly, and survive, without ever achieving architectural transparency, having a localized explanation of the repair.", "tokens": [50390, 407, 11, 21928, 613, 732, 29834, 11, 291, 393, 6239, 15227, 257, 1185, 311, 11745, 15747, 2551, 11, 652, 309, 6069, 8944, 11, 293, 7867, 11, 1553, 1562, 19626, 26621, 17131, 11, 1419, 257, 44574, 10835, 295, 264, 10535, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1617485951569121, "compression_ratio": 1.46875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875396479515414e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 296836, "start": 2982.48, "end": 2984.92, "text": " Restoration and explanation are decoupled.", "tokens": [51071, 13094, 9357, 293, 10835, 366, 979, 263, 15551, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1617485951569121, "compression_ratio": 1.46875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875396479515414e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 298492, "start": 2984.92, "end": 2987.44, "text": " Infliction doesn't just leave this as a theory.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 3423, 4105, 1177, 380, 445, 1856, 341, 382, 257, 5261, 13, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396815726097594, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.708208878167805e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 298492, "start": 2988.16, "end": 2994.66, "text": " To prove this, the paper lays out four distinct pillars of proof across completely different domains of science.", "tokens": [50527, 1407, 7081, 341, 11, 264, 3035, 32714, 484, 1451, 10644, 26729, 295, 8177, 2108, 2584, 819, 25514, 295, 3497, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396815726097594, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.708208878167805e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 298492, "start": 2995.34, "end": 3000.14, "text": " I am so excited to walk through these because it shows how universal this principle of survival is.", "tokens": [50886, 286, 669, 370, 2919, 281, 1792, 807, 613, 570, 309, 3110, 577, 11455, 341, 8665, 295, 12559, 307, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396815726097594, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.708208878167805e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 298492, "start": 3000.56, "end": 3004.52, "text": " Let's start with Pillar 1, Artificial Intelligence and Reinforcement Learning.", "tokens": [51147, 961, 311, 722, 365, 430, 30635, 502, 11, 5735, 10371, 27274, 293, 42116, 9382, 15205, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396815726097594, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.708208878167805e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 298492, "start": 3004.76, "end": 3009.96, "text": " There was a highly discussed empirical result in 2026 involving large language models.", "tokens": [51357, 821, 390, 257, 5405, 7152, 31886, 1874, 294, 945, 10880, 17030, 2416, 2856, 5245, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396815726097594, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.708208878167805e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 300996, "start": 3009.96, "end": 3019.14, "text": " Researchers found that if you take a massive transformer model, and you train just a single middle layer using reinforcement learning, leaving all the other layers completely frozen,", "tokens": [50365, 43555, 1352, 300, 498, 291, 747, 257, 5994, 31782, 2316, 11, 293, 291, 3847, 445, 257, 2167, 2808, 4583, 1228, 29280, 2539, 11, 5012, 439, 264, 661, 7914, 2584, 12496, 11, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276694177423866, "compression_ratio": 1.702054794520548, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016210930945961e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 300996, "start": 3019.52, "end": 3025.48, "text": " you can match or even exceed the performance gain by updating every single parameter in the entire network.", "tokens": [50843, 291, 393, 2995, 420, 754, 14048, 264, 3389, 6052, 538, 25113, 633, 2167, 13075, 294, 264, 2302, 3209, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276694177423866, "compression_ratio": 1.702054794520548, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016210930945961e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 300996, "start": 3025.92, "end": 3026.2, "text": " Wait.", "tokens": [51163, 3802, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276694177423866, "compression_ratio": 1.702054794520548, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016210930945961e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 300996, "start": 3026.8, "end": 3030.88, "text": " A model has billions of parameters across dozens of layers.", "tokens": [51207, 316, 2316, 575, 17375, 295, 9834, 2108, 18431, 295, 7914, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276694177423866, "compression_ratio": 1.702054794520548, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016210930945961e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 300996, "start": 3031.3, "end": 3039.2, "text": " You are saying you ignore 95% of the massive neural network, you just violently tweak one single layer somewhere in the middle of the stack,", "tokens": [51432, 509, 366, 1566, 291, 11200, 13420, 4, 295, 264, 5994, 18161, 3209, 11, 291, 445, 46728, 29879, 472, 2167, 4583, 4079, 294, 264, 2808, 295, 264, 8630, 11, 51827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276694177423866, "compression_ratio": 1.702054794520548, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016210930945961e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 303920, "start": 3039.2, "end": 3041.64, "text": " and it works just as well as carefully retraining the whole thing.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 309, 1985, 445, 382, 731, 382, 7500, 49356, 1760, 264, 1379, 551, 13, 50487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 303920, "start": 3041.72, "end": 3042.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50491, 1079, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 303920, "start": 3042.2999999999997, "end": 3044.58, "text": " It is a very clean instance of functional restoration.", "tokens": [50520, 467, 307, 257, 588, 2541, 5197, 295, 11745, 23722, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 303920, "start": 3044.98, "end": 3048.2799999999997, "text": " The model's task performance measurably, undeniably improves.", "tokens": [50654, 440, 2316, 311, 5633, 3389, 5731, 374, 1188, 11, 674, 15711, 1188, 24771, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 303920, "start": 3048.54, "end": 3050.54, "text": " But here's the catch that proves the theory.", "tokens": [50832, 583, 510, 311, 264, 3745, 300, 25019, 264, 5261, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 303920, "start": 3051.14, "end": 3055.6, "text": " Nobody in the AI community actually knows why the middle depth is the magic spot.", "tokens": [50962, 9297, 294, 264, 7318, 1768, 767, 3255, 983, 264, 2808, 7161, 307, 264, 5585, 4008, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 303920, "start": 3055.7, "end": 3056.54, "text": " There is no explanation.", "tokens": [51190, 821, 307, 572, 10835, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 303920, "start": 3056.9399999999996, "end": 3058.62, "text": " None that is universally accepted.", "tokens": [51252, 14492, 300, 307, 43995, 9035, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 303920, "start": 3059.4199999999996, "end": 3060.6, "text": " There are candidate theories.", "tokens": [51376, 821, 366, 11532, 13667, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 303920, "start": 3061.08, "end": 3063.4399999999996, "text": " Some argue it has to do with residual computation.", "tokens": [51459, 2188, 9695, 309, 575, 281, 360, 365, 27980, 24903, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568722641258909, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383301407544513e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 306344, "start": 3063.44, "end": 3069.66, "text": " Others think it's because the middle layers handle the most semantic abstraction before the model decodes back into syntax.", "tokens": [50365, 20277, 519, 309, 311, 570, 264, 2808, 7914, 4813, 264, 881, 47982, 37765, 949, 264, 2316, 979, 4789, 646, 666, 28431, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973825878567165, "compression_ratio": 1.5907473309608542, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139180649639e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 306344, "start": 3070.42, "end": 3078.6, "text": " But no localized, architecturally transparent mechanism accounts for why this specific isolated intervention works so perfectly.", "tokens": [50714, 583, 572, 44574, 11, 6331, 6512, 12737, 7513, 9402, 337, 983, 341, 2685, 14621, 13176, 1985, 370, 6239, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973825878567165, "compression_ratio": 1.5907473309608542, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139180649639e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 306344, "start": 3078.88, "end": 3079.7200000000003, "text": " But they do it anyway.", "tokens": [51137, 583, 436, 360, 309, 4033, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973825878567165, "compression_ratio": 1.5907473309608542, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139180649639e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 306344, "start": 3080.36, "end": 3086.76, "text": " The restoration is complete and available right now, so engineers use a trick to save millions of dollars in compute costs,", "tokens": [51211, 440, 23722, 307, 3566, 293, 2435, 558, 586, 11, 370, 11955, 764, 257, 4282, 281, 3155, 6803, 295, 3808, 294, 14722, 5497, 11, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973825878567165, "compression_ratio": 1.5907473309608542, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139180649639e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 306344, "start": 3087.26, "end": 3089.14, "text": " even though the explanation might never arrive.", "tokens": [51556, 754, 1673, 264, 10835, 1062, 1128, 8881, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973825878567165, "compression_ratio": 1.5907473309608542, "no_speech_prob": 1.549139180649639e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 308914, "start": 3089.14, "end": 3093.6, "text": " We are building and repairing AI that we fundamentally cannot explain.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 2390, 293, 46158, 7318, 300, 321, 17879, 2644, 2903, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1317017328171503, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.938967432793537e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 308914, "start": 3094.1, "end": 3096.68, "text": " Okay, pillar two, infrastructure and software.", "tokens": [50613, 1033, 11, 27592, 732, 11, 6896, 293, 4722, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1317017328171503, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.938967432793537e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 308914, "start": 3097.0, "end": 3103.3799999999997, "text": " If you look at spacecraft instrumentation or old embedded systems deep in banking mainframes or municipal transit networks,", "tokens": [50758, 759, 291, 574, 412, 22910, 7198, 399, 420, 1331, 16741, 3652, 2452, 294, 18261, 2135, 43277, 420, 27177, 17976, 9590, 11, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1317017328171503, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.938967432793537e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 308914, "start": 3103.58, "end": 3106.14, "text": " you see this principle baked into the design philosophy.", "tokens": [51087, 291, 536, 341, 8665, 19453, 666, 264, 1715, 10675, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1317017328171503, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.938967432793537e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 308914, "start": 3106.7, "end": 3113.72, "text": " These systems are literally designed on purpose to outlast their own documentation and the lifetimes of the engineers who built them.", "tokens": [51243, 1981, 3652, 366, 3736, 4761, 322, 4334, 281, 484, 15459, 641, 1065, 14333, 293, 264, 4545, 302, 1532, 295, 264, 11955, 567, 3094, 552, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1317017328171503, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.938967432793537e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 308914, "start": 3113.92, "end": 3116.58, "text": " They are built to survive the loss of their own blueprints.", "tokens": [51604, 814, 366, 3094, 281, 7867, 264, 4470, 295, 641, 1065, 888, 23547, 47523, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1317017328171503, "compression_ratio": 1.6734693877551021, "no_speech_prob": 1.938967432793537e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 311658, "start": 3116.58, "end": 3119.36, "text": " I experienced this.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 6751, 341, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12128241278908469, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.219218515550625e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 311658, "start": 3119.96, "end": 3125.12, "text": " I bought an old house built in the 1920s, and the electrical wiring is a nightmare of different eras.", "tokens": [50534, 286, 4243, 364, 1331, 1782, 3094, 294, 264, 22003, 82, 11, 293, 264, 12147, 27520, 307, 257, 18724, 295, 819, 1189, 296, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12128241278908469, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.219218515550625e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 311658, "start": 3125.86, "end": 3133.1, "text": " When an outlet failed, the electrician didn't rip open all the walls to understand the grand architectural intent of the 1920s builder.", "tokens": [50829, 1133, 364, 20656, 7612, 11, 264, 5210, 952, 994, 380, 12782, 1269, 439, 264, 7920, 281, 1223, 264, 2697, 26621, 8446, 295, 264, 22003, 82, 27377, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12128241278908469, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.219218515550625e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 311658, "start": 3133.48, "end": 3138.7799999999997, "text": " He just isolated the local fault, bypassed a weird dead-end wire, and restored power to the room.", "tokens": [51210, 634, 445, 14621, 264, 2654, 7441, 11, 24996, 292, 257, 3657, 3116, 12, 521, 6234, 11, 293, 23143, 1347, 281, 264, 1808, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12128241278908469, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.219218515550625e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 311658, "start": 3139.1, "end": 3141.3199999999997, "text": " He fixed it without explaining the whole system.", "tokens": [51491, 634, 6806, 309, 1553, 13468, 264, 1379, 1185, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12128241278908469, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.219218515550625e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 311658, "start": 3141.62, "end": 3144.88, "text": " And that is exactly how critical software infrastructure operates.", "tokens": [51617, 400, 300, 307, 2293, 577, 4924, 4722, 6896, 22577, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12128241278908469, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.219218515550625e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 314488, "start": 3144.88, "end": 3148.1600000000003, "text": " They minimize internal complexity not to make the system elegant,", "tokens": [50365, 814, 17522, 6920, 14024, 406, 281, 652, 264, 1185, 21117, 11, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685560774529118, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881620884187654e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 314488, "start": 3148.6, "end": 3153.98, "text": " but to enlarge the population of future operators who can restore the system without first having to explain it.", "tokens": [50551, 457, 281, 31976, 432, 264, 4415, 295, 2027, 19077, 567, 393, 15227, 264, 1185, 1553, 700, 1419, 281, 2903, 309, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685560774529118, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881620884187654e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 314488, "start": 3154.4, "end": 3157.6600000000003, "text": " In those environments, restorability is the primary design variable.", "tokens": [50841, 682, 729, 12388, 11, 46594, 2310, 307, 264, 6194, 1715, 7006, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685560774529118, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881620884187654e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 314488, "start": 3158.1600000000003, "end": 3161.1600000000003, "text": " Explicability is a secondary luxury or ignored entirely.", "tokens": [51029, 2111, 4770, 2310, 307, 257, 11396, 15558, 420, 19735, 7696, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685560774529118, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881620884187654e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 314488, "start": 3161.7000000000003, "end": 3166.82, "text": " If a software patch fixes the symptom and keeps the satellite in orbit, you deploy the patch immediately.", "tokens": [51206, 759, 257, 4722, 9972, 32539, 264, 29370, 293, 5965, 264, 16016, 294, 13991, 11, 291, 7274, 264, 9972, 4258, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685560774529118, "compression_ratio": 1.626984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881620884187654e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 316682, "start": 3166.82, "end": 3170.88, "text": " You do not wait for a three-month root cause analysis if the ship is going down.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 360, 406, 1699, 337, 257, 1045, 12, 23534, 5593, 3082, 5215, 498, 264, 5374, 307, 516, 760, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15606326406652277, "compression_ratio": 1.4943396226415093, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842578964813674e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 316682, "start": 3171.1000000000004, "end": 3173.28, "text": " Exactly. Restoration before explanation.", "tokens": [50579, 7587, 13, 13094, 9357, 949, 10835, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15606326406652277, "compression_ratio": 1.4943396226415093, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842578964813674e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 316682, "start": 3173.86, "end": 3178.3, "text": " Which brings us to Pillar 3, which is the ultimate example of this, biological repair.", "tokens": [50717, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 430, 30635, 805, 11, 597, 307, 264, 9705, 1365, 295, 341, 11, 13910, 10535, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15606326406652277, "compression_ratio": 1.4943396226415093, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842578964813674e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 316682, "start": 3178.6800000000003, "end": 3187.04, "text": " Clinical medicine has a long, exhaustively documented history of restoring function decades before a settled mechanistic account was available.", "tokens": [50958, 47942, 7195, 575, 257, 938, 11, 14687, 3413, 23007, 2503, 295, 36349, 2445, 7878, 949, 257, 14819, 4236, 3142, 2696, 390, 2435, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15606326406652277, "compression_ratio": 1.4943396226415093, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842578964813674e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 316682, "start": 3187.42, "end": 3189.84, "text": " Right. The Joseph Murray kidney transplant.", "tokens": [51395, 1779, 13, 440, 11170, 27291, 19000, 20662, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15606326406652277, "compression_ratio": 1.4943396226415093, "no_speech_prob": 2.0842578964813674e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 318984, "start": 3189.84, "end": 3195.56, "text": " Let's go deeper into that story from 1954, because it is the anchor of this whole idea.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 352, 7731, 666, 300, 1657, 490, 46590, 11, 570, 309, 307, 264, 18487, 295, 341, 1379, 1558, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12997924259730748, "compression_ratio": 1.6123188405797102, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186690418896093e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 318984, "start": 3195.56, "end": 3200.2000000000003, "text": " Dr. Joseph Murray was presented with Richard and Ronald Herrick, identical twins.", "tokens": [50651, 2491, 13, 11170, 27291, 390, 8212, 365, 9809, 293, 27397, 3204, 9323, 11, 14800, 22555, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12997924259730748, "compression_ratio": 1.6123188405797102, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186690418896093e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 318984, "start": 3200.7200000000003, "end": 3202.76, "text": " Richard was dying of severe kidney disease.", "tokens": [50909, 9809, 390, 8639, 295, 8922, 19000, 4752, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12997924259730748, "compression_ratio": 1.6123188405797102, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186690418896093e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 318984, "start": 3203.52, "end": 3209.76, "text": " Murray theorized that because they were identical twins, a transplanted organ might not be destroyed by the body's defenses.", "tokens": [51049, 27291, 27423, 1602, 300, 570, 436, 645, 14800, 22555, 11, 257, 20662, 292, 1798, 1062, 406, 312, 8937, 538, 264, 1772, 311, 35989, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12997924259730748, "compression_ratio": 1.6123188405797102, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186690418896093e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 318984, "start": 3210.2200000000003, "end": 3213.38, "text": " It was a massive surgical risk, but it was a clinical success.", "tokens": [51384, 467, 390, 257, 5994, 26646, 3148, 11, 457, 309, 390, 257, 9115, 2245, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12997924259730748, "compression_ratio": 1.6123188405797102, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186690418896093e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 318984, "start": 3213.7000000000003, "end": 3216.02, "text": " It kept Richard alive for eight more years.", "tokens": [51558, 467, 4305, 9809, 5465, 337, 3180, 544, 924, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12997924259730748, "compression_ratio": 1.6123188405797102, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186690418896093e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 321602, "start": 3216.02, "end": 3219.44, "text": " He restored a failing organ system. Functional adequacy achieved.", "tokens": [50365, 634, 23143, 257, 18223, 1798, 1185, 13, 11166, 41048, 15747, 2551, 11042, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08544813138302242, "compression_ratio": 1.5928338762214984, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109973598188443e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 321602, "start": 3219.52, "end": 3224.74, "text": " Yes. But in 1954, the immunological mechanisms governing graft rejection were a black box.", "tokens": [50540, 1079, 13, 583, 294, 46590, 11, 264, 13154, 4383, 15902, 30054, 44767, 26044, 645, 257, 2211, 2424, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08544813138302242, "compression_ratio": 1.5928338762214984, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109973598188443e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 321602, "start": 3225.24, "end": 3227.98, "text": " The concept of immunological tolerance was just a theory.", "tokens": [50826, 440, 3410, 295, 13154, 4383, 23368, 390, 445, 257, 5261, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08544813138302242, "compression_ratio": 1.5928338762214984, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109973598188443e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 321602, "start": 3228.42, "end": 3238.02, "text": " Murray restored function four full years before the human leukocyte antigen, the HLA system, which is the actual genetic architecture of tissue compatibility, was discovered in 1958.", "tokens": [50985, 27291, 23143, 2445, 1451, 1577, 924, 949, 264, 1952, 32665, 31078, 975, 2511, 3213, 11, 264, 389, 11435, 1185, 11, 597, 307, 264, 3539, 12462, 9482, 295, 12404, 34237, 11, 390, 6941, 294, 45868, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08544813138302242, "compression_ratio": 1.5928338762214984, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109973598188443e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 321602, "start": 3238.24, "end": 3242.5, "text": " So the surgeons didn't sit around waiting for the immunological explanation to save a life.", "tokens": [51476, 407, 264, 42354, 994, 380, 1394, 926, 3806, 337, 264, 13154, 4383, 10835, 281, 3155, 257, 993, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08544813138302242, "compression_ratio": 1.5928338762214984, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109973598188443e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 324250, "start": 3242.5, "end": 3249.74, "text": " But they didn't say, well, ethically, we can't do this transplant because we lack architectural transparency regarding the patient's immune system.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 436, 994, 380, 584, 11, 731, 11, 6468, 984, 11, 321, 393, 380, 360, 341, 20662, 570, 321, 5011, 26621, 17131, 8595, 264, 4537, 311, 11992, 1185, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 324250, "start": 3249.82, "end": 3250.54, "text": " We don't have the blueprint.", "tokens": [50731, 492, 500, 380, 362, 264, 35868, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 324250, "start": 3250.96, "end": 3251.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50788, 7587, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 324250, "start": 3252.02, "end": 3258.36, "text": " They saw that autographed skin from your own body and allografted skin from someone else had different survival rates.", "tokens": [50841, 814, 1866, 300, 36660, 292, 3178, 490, 428, 1065, 1772, 293, 439, 664, 4469, 292, 3178, 490, 1580, 1646, 632, 819, 12559, 6846, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 324250, "start": 3259.0, "end": 3260.82, "text": " They recognized the empirical pattern.", "tokens": [51190, 814, 9823, 264, 31886, 5102, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 324250, "start": 3261.06, "end": 3264.02, "text": " They extrapolated a prediction for identical twins.", "tokens": [51293, 814, 48224, 770, 257, 17630, 337, 14800, 22555, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 324250, "start": 3264.34, "end": 3266.08, "text": " And they intervened successfully.", "tokens": [51457, 400, 436, 17104, 292, 10727, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 324250, "start": 3266.74, "end": 3270.2, "text": " Explanation is not the gate through which restoration must pass.", "tokens": [51577, 12514, 282, 399, 307, 406, 264, 8539, 807, 597, 23722, 1633, 1320, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18853738015158134, "compression_ratio": 1.619672131147541, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396477917403953e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 327020, "start": 3270.2, "end": 3275.46, "text": " It is a separate, entirely different scientific achievement that comes much later.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 4994, 11, 7696, 819, 8134, 15838, 300, 1487, 709, 1780, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11117751623994561, "compression_ratio": 1.5944055944055944, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688941674268155e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 327020, "start": 3275.7599999999998, "end": 3281.22, "text": " OK, that brings us to pillar four, which loops us back to modern AI transformer audits.", "tokens": [50643, 2264, 11, 300, 5607, 505, 281, 27592, 1451, 11, 597, 16121, 505, 646, 281, 4363, 7318, 31782, 2379, 1208, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11117751623994561, "compression_ratio": 1.5944055944055944, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688941674268155e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 327020, "start": 3281.68, "end": 3288.3799999999997, "text": " This is perhaps the clearest modern illustration of the decoupling between functional adequacy and architectural transparency.", "tokens": [50939, 639, 307, 4317, 264, 1233, 17363, 4363, 22645, 295, 264, 979, 263, 11970, 1296, 11745, 15747, 2551, 293, 26621, 17131, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11117751623994561, "compression_ratio": 1.5944055944055944, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688941674268155e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 327020, "start": 3289.16, "end": 3297.62, "text": " Researchers can take a large language model and test it on an ambiguous sentence, a sentence that requires earlier, subtle context to be understood correctly.", "tokens": [51313, 43555, 393, 747, 257, 2416, 2856, 2316, 293, 1500, 309, 322, 364, 39465, 8174, 11, 257, 8174, 300, 7029, 3071, 11, 13743, 4319, 281, 312, 7320, 8944, 13, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11117751623994561, "compression_ratio": 1.5944055944055944, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688941674268155e-12}, {"id": 873, "seek": 329762, "start": 3297.62, "end": 3303.46, "text": " For example, if I give the AI the sentence, the trophy didn't fit into the brown suitcase because it was too large.", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 1365, 11, 498, 286, 976, 264, 7318, 264, 8174, 11, 264, 28639, 994, 380, 3318, 666, 264, 6292, 34545, 570, 309, 390, 886, 2416, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 874, "seek": 329762, "start": 3303.56, "end": 3306.44, "text": " And then I asked, what was too large, the trophy or the suitcase?", "tokens": [50662, 400, 550, 286, 2351, 11, 437, 390, 886, 2416, 11, 264, 28639, 420, 264, 34545, 30, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 875, "seek": 329762, "start": 3307.1, "end": 3307.54, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50839, 7587, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 876, "seek": 329762, "start": 3307.8199999999997, "end": 3309.16, "text": " That is a Winograd schema.", "tokens": [50875, 663, 307, 257, 10427, 664, 6206, 34078, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 877, "seek": 329762, "start": 3309.5, "end": 3314.44, "text": " We hold the question fixed and we see if the model gets the right answer based on context.", "tokens": [50959, 492, 1797, 264, 1168, 6806, 293, 321, 536, 498, 264, 2316, 2170, 264, 558, 1867, 2361, 322, 4319, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 878, "seek": 329762, "start": 3314.68, "end": 3320.56, "text": " And if it consistently gets the right answer, if it says the trophy, we have established functional adequacy.", "tokens": [51218, 400, 498, 309, 14961, 2170, 264, 558, 1867, 11, 498, 309, 1619, 264, 28639, 11, 321, 362, 7545, 11745, 15747, 2551, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 879, "seek": 329762, "start": 3320.88, "end": 3322.24, "text": " It behaves correctly.", "tokens": [51528, 467, 36896, 8944, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 880, "seek": 329762, "start": 3322.58, "end": 3323.74, "text": " It tracks the truth.", "tokens": [51613, 467, 10218, 264, 3494, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 881, "seek": 329762, "start": 3323.8399999999997, "end": 3324.96, "text": " But then comes the hard part.", "tokens": [51676, 583, 550, 1487, 264, 1152, 644, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11667383179184078, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346888899275048e-12}, {"id": 882, "seek": 332496, "start": 3324.96, "end": 3341.1, "text": " Right. If you then try to find the exact localized intervention point, if you search the billions of parameters to find the specific neurons or attention heads that hold that specific understanding of the word it, you are attempting an architectural transparency test.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 759, 291, 550, 853, 281, 915, 264, 1900, 44574, 13176, 935, 11, 498, 291, 3164, 264, 17375, 295, 9834, 281, 915, 264, 2685, 22027, 420, 3202, 8050, 300, 1797, 300, 2685, 3701, 295, 264, 1349, 309, 11, 291, 366, 22001, 364, 26621, 17131, 1500, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0810514460788684, "compression_ratio": 1.6728624535315986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830431141979686e-12}, {"id": 883, "seek": 332496, "start": 3341.48, "end": 3343.62, "text": " You are asking the model to explain itself.", "tokens": [51191, 509, 366, 3365, 264, 2316, 281, 2903, 2564, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0810514460788684, "compression_ratio": 1.6728624535315986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830431141979686e-12}, {"id": 884, "seek": 332496, "start": 3343.7400000000002, "end": 3346.5, "text": " And how often does that transparency test actually succeed?", "tokens": [51304, 400, 577, 2049, 775, 300, 17131, 1500, 767, 7754, 30, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0810514460788684, "compression_ratio": 1.6728624535315986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830431141979686e-12}, {"id": 885, "seek": 332496, "start": 3346.7400000000002, "end": 3351.18, "text": " It is notoriously difficult, heavily debated and frequently fails completely.", "tokens": [51454, 467, 307, 46772, 8994, 2252, 11, 10950, 42212, 293, 10374, 18199, 2584, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0810514460788684, "compression_ratio": 1.6728624535315986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830431141979686e-12}, {"id": 886, "seek": 335118, "start": 3351.18, "end": 3359.0, "text": " The practical reality of AI right now is that the functional adequacy test is passed constantly, millions of times a day, every time you use a good model.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8496, 4103, 295, 7318, 558, 586, 307, 300, 264, 11745, 15747, 2551, 1500, 307, 4678, 6460, 11, 6803, 295, 1413, 257, 786, 11, 633, 565, 291, 764, 257, 665, 2316, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07045310408204467, "compression_ratio": 1.6283783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312227397493161e-12}, {"id": 887, "seek": 335118, "start": 3359.3999999999996, "end": 3367.9199999999996, "text": " The architectural transparency test, finding the explicit localized explanation inside the black box, remains largely an unsolved problem in interpretability research.", "tokens": [50776, 440, 26621, 17131, 1500, 11, 5006, 264, 13691, 44574, 10835, 1854, 264, 2211, 2424, 11, 7023, 11611, 364, 2693, 29110, 1154, 294, 7302, 2310, 2132, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07045310408204467, "compression_ratio": 1.6283783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312227397493161e-12}, {"id": 888, "seek": 335118, "start": 3368.3199999999997, "end": 3377.62, "text": " We have successfully restored, trained and optimized these incredible models without being able to explain how their internals actually represent that success.", "tokens": [51222, 492, 362, 10727, 23143, 11, 8895, 293, 26941, 613, 4651, 5245, 1553, 885, 1075, 281, 2903, 577, 641, 2154, 1124, 767, 2906, 300, 2245, 13, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07045310408204467, "compression_ratio": 1.6283783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312227397493161e-12}, {"id": 889, "seek": 337762, "start": 3377.62, "end": 3381.02, "text": " Exactly. So what does this mean for our practice across all fields?", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 407, 437, 775, 341, 914, 337, 527, 3124, 2108, 439, 7909, 30, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287979099848499, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899370799625888e-12}, {"id": 890, "seek": 337762, "start": 3381.22, "end": 3386.16, "text": " It means we have to radically abandon the habit of expecting that intervention must wait on understanding.", "tokens": [50545, 467, 1355, 321, 362, 281, 35508, 9072, 264, 7164, 295, 9650, 300, 13176, 1633, 1699, 322, 3701, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287979099848499, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899370799625888e-12}, {"id": 891, "seek": 337762, "start": 3387.18, "end": 3395.88, "text": " A repair's reliability is based on whether it repeats under the right conditions, not whether you have a pristine, peer-reviewed academic explanation for it.", "tokens": [50843, 316, 10535, 311, 24550, 307, 2361, 322, 1968, 309, 35038, 833, 264, 558, 4487, 11, 406, 1968, 291, 362, 257, 582, 42745, 11, 15108, 12, 265, 1759, 292, 7778, 10835, 337, 309, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287979099848499, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899370799625888e-12}, {"id": 892, "seek": 339588, "start": 3395.88, "end": 3404.88, "text": " So, connecting this back to you, in your own life, in your own work, in your own body, you don't need a perfect causal map to take action.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 11015, 341, 646, 281, 291, 11, 294, 428, 1065, 993, 11, 294, 428, 1065, 589, 11, 294, 428, 1065, 1772, 11, 291, 500, 380, 643, 257, 2176, 38755, 4471, 281, 747, 3069, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07250837613177556, "compression_ratio": 1.672340425531915, "no_speech_prob": 1.6300440814839834e-12}, {"id": 893, "seek": 339588, "start": 3405.46, "end": 3417.4, "text": " Whether you are patching a bizarre software bug, treating a chronic symptom with a weird diet tweak that just happens to work, or trying to fix a bad habit through trial and error, you do not have to wait until you have perfectly analyzed the root cause.", "tokens": [50844, 8503, 291, 366, 9972, 278, 257, 18265, 4722, 7426, 11, 15083, 257, 14493, 29370, 365, 257, 3657, 6339, 29879, 300, 445, 2314, 281, 589, 11, 420, 1382, 281, 3191, 257, 1578, 7164, 807, 7308, 293, 6713, 11, 291, 360, 406, 362, 281, 1699, 1826, 291, 362, 6239, 28181, 264, 5593, 3082, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07250837613177556, "compression_ratio": 1.672340425531915, "no_speech_prob": 1.6300440814839834e-12}, {"id": 894, "seek": 341740, "start": 3417.4, "end": 3424.76, "text": " If you find an intervention that works, that restores your function, use it. The explanation can come later, or maybe it never comes at all.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 915, 364, 13176, 300, 1985, 11, 300, 1472, 2706, 428, 2445, 11, 764, 309, 13, 440, 10835, 393, 808, 1780, 11, 420, 1310, 309, 1128, 1487, 412, 439, 13, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516749064127604, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7418998101564886e-12}, {"id": 895, "seek": 341740, "start": 3425.0, "end": 3429.42, "text": " But survival and restoration are not gated by your ability to explain the machinery.", "tokens": [50745, 583, 12559, 293, 23722, 366, 406, 290, 770, 538, 428, 3485, 281, 2903, 264, 27302, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516749064127604, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7418998101564886e-12}, {"id": 896, "seek": 341740, "start": 3429.82, "end": 3439.2000000000003, "text": " It is an incredibly liberating realization. It frees you to act in a complex world without being paralyzed by a lack of total information.", "tokens": [50986, 467, 307, 364, 6252, 6774, 990, 25138, 13, 467, 2130, 279, 291, 281, 605, 294, 257, 3997, 1002, 1553, 885, 41919, 538, 257, 5011, 295, 3217, 1589, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516749064127604, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7418998101564886e-12}, {"id": 897, "seek": 341740, "start": 3439.46, "end": 3443.14, "text": " Okay, let's take a major step back and look at this massive journey we just went on.", "tokens": [51468, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 2563, 1823, 646, 293, 574, 412, 341, 5994, 4671, 321, 445, 1437, 322, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06516749064127604, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7418998101564886e-12}, {"id": 898, "seek": 344314, "start": 3443.14, "end": 3447.92, "text": " We covered an immense amount of ground, from physics, to biology, to AI.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 5343, 364, 22920, 2372, 295, 2727, 11, 490, 10649, 11, 281, 14956, 11, 281, 7318, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11509189822457054, "compression_ratio": 1.6254980079681276, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013966190776442e-12}, {"id": 899, "seek": 344314, "start": 3448.42, "end": 3456.2799999999997, "text": " We really did. We started by looking at the geometry of systems, and we learned that boundaries aren't just passive walls where things geometrically stop.", "tokens": [50629, 492, 534, 630, 13, 492, 1409, 538, 1237, 412, 264, 18426, 295, 3652, 11, 293, 321, 3264, 300, 13180, 3212, 380, 445, 14975, 7920, 689, 721, 12956, 81, 984, 1590, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11509189822457054, "compression_ratio": 1.6254980079681276, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013966190776442e-12}, {"id": 900, "seek": 344314, "start": 3456.68, "end": 3462.98, "text": " Boundaries are active computational objects. They are statistical screens forcing a system to minimize surprise.", "tokens": [51042, 363, 554, 4889, 366, 4967, 28270, 6565, 13, 814, 366, 22820, 11171, 19030, 257, 1185, 281, 17522, 6365, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11509189822457054, "compression_ratio": 1.6254980079681276, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013966190776442e-12}, {"id": 901, "seek": 344314, "start": 3463.7, "end": 3467.3599999999997, "text": " They are biological memory layers actively pursuing a target shape.", "tokens": [51393, 814, 366, 13910, 4675, 7914, 13022, 20222, 257, 3779, 3909, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11509189822457054, "compression_ratio": 1.6254980079681276, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013966190776442e-12}, {"id": 902, "seek": 346736, "start": 3467.36, "end": 3473.7200000000003, "text": " And there are topological deletions that permanently refuse certain futures by zeroing them out of existence.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 456, 366, 1192, 4383, 1103, 302, 626, 300, 24042, 16791, 1629, 26071, 538, 4018, 278, 552, 484, 295, 9123, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11819457285331958, "compression_ratio": 1.519047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.531093177589704e-12}, {"id": 903, "seek": 346736, "start": 3473.92, "end": 3481.04, "text": " And importantly, we established that those are distinctly different mechanisms that can actually mathematically conflict with one another if you force them together.", "tokens": [50693, 400, 8906, 11, 321, 7545, 300, 729, 366, 10644, 356, 819, 15902, 300, 393, 767, 44003, 6596, 365, 472, 1071, 498, 291, 3464, 552, 1214, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11819457285331958, "compression_ratio": 1.519047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.531093177589704e-12}, {"id": 904, "seek": 346736, "start": 3481.3, "end": 3483.82, "text": " Right. Then we moved into the brevity trap.", "tokens": [51062, 1779, 13, 1396, 321, 4259, 666, 264, 1403, 23110, 11487, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11819457285331958, "compression_ratio": 1.519047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.531093177589704e-12}, {"id": 905, "seek": 348382, "start": 3483.82, "end": 3491.4, "text": " We learned that the shortness of a description, or the compression of a neural network, absolutely does not guarantee deeper understanding.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 3264, 300, 264, 2099, 1287, 295, 257, 3855, 11, 420, 264, 19355, 295, 257, 18161, 3209, 11, 3122, 775, 406, 10815, 7731, 3701, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12569745381673178, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553465633477703e-12}, {"id": 906, "seek": 348382, "start": 3492.1200000000003, "end": 3499.7000000000003, "text": " Because of superposed, tangled representations, a perfectly compressed model might have lost its ability to distinguish nuance entirely.", "tokens": [50780, 1436, 295, 1687, 79, 1744, 11, 47192, 33358, 11, 257, 6239, 30353, 2316, 1062, 362, 2731, 1080, 3485, 281, 20206, 42625, 7696, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12569745381673178, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553465633477703e-12}, {"id": 907, "seek": 349970, "start": 3499.7, "end": 3504.3599999999997, "text": " We cannot use compression as a continuous proxy for understanding.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 2644, 764, 19355, 382, 257, 10957, 29690, 337, 3701, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17343736306214944, "compression_ratio": 1.5411255411255411, "no_speech_prob": 1.611001588207317e-12}, {"id": 908, "seek": 349970, "start": 3505.08, "end": 3510.12, "text": " Sometimes, shortness just means you are relying on a massive, hidden library of past work.", "tokens": [50634, 4803, 11, 2099, 1287, 445, 1355, 291, 366, 24140, 322, 257, 5994, 11, 7633, 6405, 295, 1791, 589, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17343736306214944, "compression_ratio": 1.5411255411255411, "no_speech_prob": 1.611001588207317e-12}, {"id": 909, "seek": 349970, "start": 3510.62, "end": 3516.68, "text": " And in complex environments, you actually have to widen the curriculum and deliberately increase entropy to keep learning.", "tokens": [50911, 400, 294, 3997, 12388, 11, 291, 767, 362, 281, 32552, 264, 14302, 293, 23506, 3488, 30867, 281, 1066, 2539, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17343736306214944, "compression_ratio": 1.5411255411255411, "no_speech_prob": 1.611001588207317e-12}, {"id": 910, "seek": 349970, "start": 3517.14, "end": 3518.98, "text": " You cannot compress your way to genius.", "tokens": [51237, 509, 2644, 14778, 428, 636, 281, 14017, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17343736306214944, "compression_ratio": 1.5411255411255411, "no_speech_prob": 1.611001588207317e-12}, {"id": 911, "seek": 349970, "start": 3519.54, "end": 3521.2799999999997, "text": " And finally, we looked at survival.", "tokens": [51357, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 2956, 412, 12559, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17343736306214944, "compression_ratio": 1.5411255411255411, "no_speech_prob": 1.611001588207317e-12}, {"id": 912, "seek": 352128, "start": 3521.28, "end": 3531.5, "text": " We saw that functional restoration, getting a complex system to work again, is entirely logically decoupled from architectural transparency, being able to explain exactly how it works.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1866, 300, 11745, 23722, 11, 1242, 257, 3997, 1185, 281, 589, 797, 11, 307, 7696, 38887, 979, 263, 15551, 490, 26621, 17131, 11, 885, 1075, 281, 2903, 2293, 577, 309, 1985, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221196602130759, "compression_ratio": 1.6925465838509317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900214730609543e-12}, {"id": 913, "seek": 352128, "start": 3531.86, "end": 3538.98, "text": " From tweaking transformer layers to legacy code to kidney transplants, we constantly fix things without fully understanding the underlying mechanisms.", "tokens": [50894, 3358, 6986, 2456, 31782, 7914, 281, 11711, 3089, 281, 19000, 1145, 42433, 11, 321, 6460, 3191, 721, 1553, 4498, 3701, 264, 14217, 15902, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221196602130759, "compression_ratio": 1.6925465838509317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900214730609543e-12}, {"id": 914, "seek": 352128, "start": 3539.46, "end": 3540.76, "text": " Restoration before explanation.", "tokens": [51274, 13094, 9357, 949, 10835, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221196602130759, "compression_ratio": 1.6925465838509317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900214730609543e-12}, {"id": 915, "seek": 352128, "start": 3541.1400000000003, "end": 3544.36, "text": " It is a complete inversion of how we are taught to approach problem solving.", "tokens": [51358, 467, 307, 257, 3566, 43576, 295, 577, 321, 366, 5928, 281, 3109, 1154, 12606, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221196602130759, "compression_ratio": 1.6925465838509317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900214730609543e-12}, {"id": 916, "seek": 352128, "start": 3544.6200000000003, "end": 3545.02, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51532, 467, 307, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221196602130759, "compression_ratio": 1.6925465838509317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900214730609543e-12}, {"id": 917, "seek": 352128, "start": 3545.46, "end": 3549.6800000000003, "text": " So we always like to leave you with a final thought, something to mull over on your own time.", "tokens": [51574, 407, 321, 1009, 411, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 257, 2572, 1194, 11, 746, 281, 275, 858, 670, 322, 428, 1065, 565, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221196602130759, "compression_ratio": 1.6925465838509317, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900214730609543e-12}, {"id": 918, "seek": 354968, "start": 3549.68, "end": 3557.2, "text": " And building on these three papers and this idea of restoration without explanation, I have a massive, provocative question for you.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2390, 322, 613, 1045, 10577, 293, 341, 1558, 295, 23722, 1553, 10835, 11, 286, 362, 257, 5994, 11, 47663, 1168, 337, 291, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10257631458648264, "compression_ratio": 1.6106194690265487, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 919, "seek": 354968, "start": 3557.3999999999996, "end": 3558.04, "text": " What is the question?", "tokens": [50751, 708, 307, 264, 1168, 30, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10257631458648264, "compression_ratio": 1.6106194690265487, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 920, "seek": 354968, "start": 3558.3599999999997, "end": 3572.66, "text": " Well, if boundaries actively dictate what a system can become through refusal, by permanently deleting options, and if a system can be perfectly repaired and restored without anyone understanding how it works,", "tokens": [50799, 1042, 11, 498, 13180, 13022, 36071, 437, 257, 1185, 393, 1813, 807, 48948, 11, 538, 24042, 48946, 3956, 11, 293, 498, 257, 1185, 393, 312, 6239, 36551, 293, 23143, 1553, 2878, 3701, 577, 309, 1985, 11, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10257631458648264, "compression_ratio": 1.6106194690265487, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 921, "seek": 357266, "start": 3572.66, "end": 3579.8599999999997, "text": " does that mean the most resilient systems of the future will be the ones that are deliberately designed to be unexplainable?", "tokens": [50365, 775, 300, 914, 264, 881, 23699, 3652, 295, 264, 2027, 486, 312, 264, 2306, 300, 366, 23506, 4761, 281, 312, 11572, 34821, 712, 30, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1698964579721515, "compression_ratio": 1.5924369747899159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492841384801004e-12}, {"id": 922, "seek": 357266, "start": 3579.98, "end": 3581.8799999999997, "text": " That is a deeply provocative thought.", "tokens": [50731, 663, 307, 257, 8760, 47663, 1194, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1698964579721515, "compression_ratio": 1.5924369747899159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492841384801004e-12}, {"id": 923, "seek": 357266, "start": 3581.8799999999997, "end": 3582.68, "text": " Think about it.", "tokens": [50826, 6557, 466, 309, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1698964579721515, "compression_ratio": 1.5924369747899159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492841384801004e-12}, {"id": 924, "seek": 357266, "start": 3582.7799999999997, "end": 3586.0, "text": " Look at our current trajectory with AI and even societal structures.", "tokens": [50871, 2053, 412, 527, 2190, 21512, 365, 7318, 293, 754, 33472, 9227, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1698964579721515, "compression_ratio": 1.5924369747899159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492841384801004e-12}, {"id": 925, "seek": 357266, "start": 3586.72, "end": 3588.96, "text": " We are obsessed with algorithmic transparency.", "tokens": [51068, 492, 366, 16923, 365, 9284, 299, 17131, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1698964579721515, "compression_ratio": 1.5924369747899159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492841384801004e-12}, {"id": 926, "seek": 357266, "start": 3589.7, "end": 3593.52, "text": " We want to be able to open the black box and see exactly why the AI made a decision.", "tokens": [51217, 492, 528, 281, 312, 1075, 281, 1269, 264, 2211, 2424, 293, 536, 2293, 983, 264, 7318, 1027, 257, 3537, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1698964579721515, "compression_ratio": 1.5924369747899159, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492841384801004e-12}, {"id": 927, "seek": 359352, "start": 3593.52, "end": 3602.28, "text": " But if true resilience, true functional adequacy comes from the ability to quickly restore function without the heavy, slow burden of architectural transparency,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 2074, 19980, 11, 2074, 11745, 15747, 2551, 1487, 490, 264, 3485, 281, 2661, 15227, 2445, 1553, 264, 4676, 11, 2964, 12578, 295, 26621, 17131, 11, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08300501757329053, "compression_ratio": 1.6888111888111887, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493959418077074e-12}, {"id": 928, "seek": 359352, "start": 3602.84, "end": 3609.0, "text": " maybe our current obsession with making every AI completely explainable is exactly what will make those systems fragile.", "tokens": [50831, 1310, 527, 2190, 30521, 365, 1455, 633, 7318, 2584, 2903, 712, 307, 2293, 437, 486, 652, 729, 3652, 23847, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08300501757329053, "compression_ratio": 1.6888111888111887, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493959418077074e-12}, {"id": 929, "seek": 359352, "start": 3609.2599999999998, "end": 3610.62, "text": " It is a valid fear.", "tokens": [51152, 467, 307, 257, 7363, 4240, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08300501757329053, "compression_ratio": 1.6888111888111887, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493959418077074e-12}, {"id": 930, "seek": 359352, "start": 3610.88, "end": 3618.28, "text": " If you legally or architecturally force a system to maintain an explicit, inspectable explanation for everything it does,", "tokens": [51233, 759, 291, 21106, 420, 6331, 6512, 3464, 257, 1185, 281, 6909, 364, 13691, 11, 15018, 712, 10835, 337, 1203, 309, 775, 11, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08300501757329053, "compression_ratio": 1.6888111888111887, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493959418077074e-12}, {"id": 931, "seek": 359352, "start": 3618.58, "end": 3621.98, "text": " you are forcing it to use a very specific, rigid ontology.", "tokens": [51618, 291, 366, 19030, 309, 281, 764, 257, 588, 2685, 11, 22195, 6592, 1793, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08300501757329053, "compression_ratio": 1.6888111888111887, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493959418077074e-12}, {"id": 932, "seek": 362198, "start": 3621.98, "end": 3632.94, "text": " You might be severely limiting its ability to utilize those complex, distributed, superposed representations that actually allow it to adapt, learn, and restore itself quickly in a chaotic environment.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1062, 312, 26271, 22083, 1080, 3485, 281, 16117, 729, 3997, 11, 12631, 11, 1687, 79, 1744, 33358, 300, 767, 2089, 309, 281, 6231, 11, 1466, 11, 293, 15227, 2564, 2661, 294, 257, 27013, 2823, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09495484946977974, "compression_ratio": 1.6688311688311688, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126328125451675e-12}, {"id": 933, "seek": 362198, "start": 3633.18, "end": 3633.58, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50925, 7587, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09495484946977974, "compression_ratio": 1.6688311688311688, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126328125451675e-12}, {"id": 934, "seek": 362198, "start": 3633.78, "end": 3643.9, "text": " We might be building a glass jaw into our most advanced artificial intelligence or our most advanced bureaucracies just to satisfy our own psychological need for a neat, compressed explanation.", "tokens": [50955, 492, 1062, 312, 2390, 257, 4276, 18162, 666, 527, 881, 7339, 11677, 7599, 420, 527, 881, 7339, 26360, 12080, 530, 445, 281, 19319, 527, 1065, 14346, 643, 337, 257, 10654, 11, 30353, 10835, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09495484946977974, "compression_ratio": 1.6688311688311688, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126328125451675e-12}, {"id": 935, "seek": 362198, "start": 3644.46, "end": 3650.44, "text": " We are forcing a coding deficit requirement onto a system that just needs to maximize its distinguishability.", "tokens": [51489, 492, 366, 19030, 257, 17720, 22132, 11695, 3911, 257, 1185, 300, 445, 2203, 281, 19874, 1080, 20206, 2310, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09495484946977974, "compression_ratio": 1.6688311688311688, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126328125451675e-12}, {"id": 936, "seek": 365044, "start": 3650.44, "end": 3652.02, "text": " Something for you to mull over.", "tokens": [50365, 6595, 337, 291, 281, 275, 858, 670, 13, 50444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 937, "seek": 365044, "start": 3652.36, "end": 3655.7400000000002, "text": " It certainly recontextualizes our deep-seated need for control.", "tokens": [50461, 467, 3297, 850, 896, 3828, 901, 5660, 527, 2452, 12, 405, 770, 643, 337, 1969, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 938, "seek": 365044, "start": 3655.98, "end": 3658.64, "text": " We want the clean narrative, even if it makes the system weaker.", "tokens": [50642, 492, 528, 264, 2541, 9977, 11, 754, 498, 309, 1669, 264, 1185, 24286, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 939, "seek": 365044, "start": 3658.98, "end": 3659.48, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50792, 467, 775, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 940, "seek": 365044, "start": 3659.58, "end": 3660.8, "text": " It goes right back to the beginning.", "tokens": [50822, 467, 1709, 558, 646, 281, 264, 2863, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 941, "seek": 365044, "start": 3661.2200000000003, "end": 3664.52, "text": " We want the clean, jagged white line on the x-ray.", "tokens": [50904, 492, 528, 264, 2541, 11, 6368, 3004, 2418, 1622, 322, 264, 2031, 12, 3458, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 942, "seek": 365044, "start": 3664.7200000000003, "end": 3667.38, "text": " We want to point at the broken bone and say, there it is.", "tokens": [51079, 492, 528, 281, 935, 412, 264, 5463, 9026, 293, 584, 11, 456, 309, 307, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 943, "seek": 365044, "start": 3667.48, "end": 3668.34, "text": " That is the exploration.", "tokens": [51217, 663, 307, 264, 16197, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 944, "seek": 365044, "start": 3669.2000000000003, "end": 3672.0, "text": " But the reality of complex systems is muddy waters.", "tokens": [51303, 583, 264, 4103, 295, 3997, 3652, 307, 38540, 12975, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 945, "seek": 365044, "start": 3672.48, "end": 3676.28, "text": " It is active boundaries, tangled representations, and blind restoration.", "tokens": [51467, 467, 307, 4967, 13180, 11, 47192, 33358, 11, 293, 6865, 23722, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881607353687286, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686113854166075e-12}, {"id": 946, "seek": 367628, "start": 3676.28, "end": 3682.2000000000003, "text": " And maybe, just maybe, those muddy waters are exactly where the resilience lives.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1310, 11, 445, 1310, 11, 729, 38540, 12975, 366, 2293, 689, 264, 19980, 2909, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16015086454503677, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.227345911876011e-12}, {"id": 947, "seek": 367628, "start": 3682.4, "end": 3684.44, "text": " The muddy waters are where the system survives.", "tokens": [50671, 440, 38540, 12975, 366, 689, 264, 1185, 46231, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16015086454503677, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.227345911876011e-12}, {"id": 948, "seek": 367628, "start": 3684.6000000000004, "end": 3686.92, "text": " Thank you so much for joining us on this deep dive.", "tokens": [50781, 1044, 291, 370, 709, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16015086454503677, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.227345911876011e-12}, {"id": 949, "seek": 367628, "start": 3687.2400000000002, "end": 3691.36, "text": " Keep questioning the boundaries, keep embracing the complexity, and keep exploring.", "tokens": [50913, 5527, 21257, 264, 13180, 11, 1066, 31596, 264, 14024, 11, 293, 1066, 12736, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16015086454503677, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.227345911876011e-12}, {"id": 950, "seek": 367628, "start": 3691.78, "end": 3692.38, "text": " See you next time.", "tokens": [51140, 3008, 291, 958, 565, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16015086454503677, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.227345911876011e-12}, {"id": 951, "seek": 369238, "start": 3692.38, "end": 3722.36, "text": " We'll see you next time.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 603, 536, 291, 958, 565, 13, 51864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.7767936706542968, "compression_ratio": 0.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.646791036868933e-11}], "language": "en"}
