er, almost.", "tokens": [50770, 1743, 257, 3233, 26018, 11, 1920, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08484404694800284, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169092974249732e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 7556, "start": 85.34, "end": 93.74000000000001, "text": " Exactly. Treating those words as a whisper to side. But when you encountered the dashes, your internal voice likely stayed at full volume.", "tokens": [50854, 7587, 13, 20298, 278, 729, 2283, 382, 257, 26018, 281, 1252, 13, 583, 562, 291, 20381, 264, 8240, 279, 11, 428, 6920, 3177, 3700, 9181, 412, 1577, 5523, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08484404694800284, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169092974249732e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 7556, "start": 93.86, "end": 95.38, "text": " Because it feels more urgent.", "tokens": [51280, 1436, 309, 3417, 544, 19022, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08484404694800284, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169092974249732e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 7556, "start": 95.58, "end": 99.04, "text": " Right. The momentum of the sentence just didn't drop. It plowed straight forward.", "tokens": [51366, 1779, 13, 440, 11244, 295, 264, 8174, 445, 994, 380, 3270, 13, 467, 499, 24347, 2997, 2128, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08484404694800284, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169092974249732e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 9904, "start": 99.04, "end": 106.92, "text": " And that almost imperceptible difference in how our brains render punctuation, that's the starting point for our deep dive today.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 1920, 10100, 1336, 964, 2649, 294, 577, 527, 15442, 15529, 27006, 16073, 11, 300, 311, 264, 2891, 935, 337, 527, 2452, 9192, 965, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1261218732541746, "compression_ratio": 1.5516014234875444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8968179891359904e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 9904, "start": 107.02000000000001, "end": 108.02000000000001, "text": " It's a great starting point.", "tokens": [50764, 467, 311, 257, 869, 2891, 935, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1261218732541746, "compression_ratio": 1.5516014234875444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8968179891359904e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 9904, "start": 108.16000000000001, "end": 115.76, "text": " We are looking at this truly fascinating paper from July 2026. It's by an independent researcher named Flixen.", "tokens": [50821, 492, 366, 1237, 412, 341, 4908, 10343, 3035, 490, 7370, 945, 10880, 13, 467, 311, 538, 364, 6695, 21751, 4926, 3235, 970, 268, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1261218732541746, "compression_ratio": 1.5516014234875444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8968179891359904e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 9904, "start": 115.96000000000001, "end": 117.98, "text": " Yeah, a really dense but amazing paper.", "tokens": [51211, 865, 11, 257, 534, 18011, 457, 2243, 3035, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1261218732541746, "compression_ratio": 1.5516014234875444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8968179891359904e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 9904, "start": 118.12, "end": 123.66000000000001, "text": " Super dense. It's titled Parenthetical Asides, Nested Scoping Conversation, Games, Stories, and Music.", "tokens": [51319, 4548, 18011, 13, 467, 311, 19841, 430, 20616, 27800, 1018, 1875, 11, 426, 21885, 2747, 26125, 33247, 399, 11, 12761, 11, 31797, 11, 293, 7609, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1261218732541746, "compression_ratio": 1.5516014234875444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8968179891359904e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 9904, "start": 123.88000000000001, "end": 124.92, "text": " A very ambitious title.", "tokens": [51607, 316, 588, 20239, 4876, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1261218732541746, "compression_ratio": 1.5516014234875444, "no_speech_prob": 1.8968179891359904e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 12492, "start": 124.92, "end": 133.28, "text": " Seriously. But the mission today is to show you how punctuation isn't just a style choice. It's not just grammar rules.", "tokens": [50365, 14063, 13, 583, 264, 4447, 965, 307, 281, 855, 291, 577, 27006, 16073, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 3758, 3922, 13, 467, 311, 406, 445, 22317, 4474, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11059146974144912, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 12492, "start": 133.52, "end": 134.42000000000002, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [50795, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11059146974144912, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 12492, "start": 134.46, "end": 145.9, "text": " It's actually a clumsy, low-resolution residue of a massive, invisible cognitive operation that you and I perform every single day without even realizing it.", "tokens": [50842, 467, 311, 767, 257, 44640, 11, 2295, 12, 495, 3386, 34799, 295, 257, 5994, 11, 14603, 15605, 6916, 300, 291, 293, 286, 2042, 633, 2167, 786, 1553, 754, 16734, 309, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11059146974144912, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 12492, "start": 146.06, "end": 147.94, "text": " An operation called Nested Scope.", "tokens": [51422, 1107, 6916, 1219, 426, 21885, 2747, 1114, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11059146974144912, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 14794, "start": 147.94, "end": 157.38, "text": " Nested Scope. So we're going to trace this specific mental architecture across domains that honestly seem completely unrelated on the surface.", "tokens": [50365, 426, 21885, 2747, 1114, 13, 407, 321, 434, 516, 281, 13508, 341, 2685, 4973, 9482, 2108, 25514, 300, 6095, 1643, 2584, 38967, 322, 264, 3753, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08858888707262405, "compression_ratio": 1.6642335766423357, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213593409889702e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 14794, "start": 157.48, "end": 161.4, "text": " Because once you understand the mechanics of Nested Scope, you literally start seeing it everywhere.", "tokens": [50842, 1436, 1564, 291, 1223, 264, 12939, 295, 426, 21885, 2747, 1114, 11, 291, 3736, 722, 2577, 309, 5315, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08858888707262405, "compression_ratio": 1.6642335766423357, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213593409889702e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 14794, "start": 161.66, "end": 165.28, "text": " Everywhere. We're going to dissect the architecture of everyday unscripted conversation.", "tokens": [51051, 37322, 13, 492, 434, 516, 281, 48332, 264, 9482, 295, 7429, 2693, 5944, 292, 3761, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08858888707262405, "compression_ratio": 1.6642335766423357, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213593409889702e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 14794, "start": 165.92, "end": 172.78, "text": " And then from there, look at how video game designers in the 1990s independently reinvented this exact cognitive structure.", "tokens": [51264, 400, 550, 490, 456, 11, 574, 412, 577, 960, 1216, 16196, 294, 264, 13384, 82, 21761, 33477, 292, 341, 1900, 15605, 3877, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08858888707262405, "compression_ratio": 1.6642335766423357, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213593409889702e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 17278, "start": 172.78, "end": 176.82, "text": " Just to make their levels function under those old, strict memory constraints.", "tokens": [50365, 1449, 281, 652, 641, 4358, 2445, 833, 729, 1331, 11, 10910, 4675, 18491, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13626417432512555, "compression_ratio": 1.5809859154929577, "no_speech_prob": 1.42662303411617e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 17278, "start": 176.94, "end": 178.38, "text": " Right, the old hardware limitations.", "tokens": [50573, 1779, 11, 264, 1331, 8837, 15705, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13626417432512555, "compression_ratio": 1.5809859154929577, "no_speech_prob": 1.42662303411617e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 17278, "start": 179.14000000000001, "end": 185.76, "text": " We'll also break down the underlying logic of computer terminal windows, dissect the structural mechanics of conversational hypnosis.", "tokens": [50683, 492, 603, 611, 1821, 760, 264, 14217, 9952, 295, 3820, 14709, 9309, 11, 48332, 264, 15067, 12939, 295, 2615, 1478, 7420, 46080, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13626417432512555, "compression_ratio": 1.5809859154929577, "no_speech_prob": 1.42662303411617e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 17278, "start": 185.86, "end": 187.12, "text": " Which is my favorite part, honestly.", "tokens": [51019, 3013, 307, 452, 2954, 644, 11, 6095, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13626417432512555, "compression_ratio": 1.5809859154929577, "no_speech_prob": 1.42662303411617e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 17278, "start": 187.68, "end": 188.76, "text": " Oh, it's so good.", "tokens": [51110, 876, 11, 309, 311, 370, 665, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13626417432512555, "compression_ratio": 1.5809859154929577, "no_speech_prob": 1.42662303411617e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 17278, "start": 189.26, "end": 196.44, "text": " We'll explore the physics of musical tension, and finally, look at the split audience logic of forced subtitles in film.", "tokens": [51189, 492, 603, 6839, 264, 10649, 295, 9165, 8980, 11, 293, 2721, 11, 574, 412, 264, 7472, 4034, 9952, 295, 7579, 42045, 294, 2007, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13626417432512555, "compression_ratio": 1.5809859154929577, "no_speech_prob": 1.42662303411617e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 17278, "start": 196.88, "end": 198.06, "text": " It's a massive journey.", "tokens": [51570, 467, 311, 257, 5994, 4671, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13626417432512555, "compression_ratio": 1.5809859154929577, "no_speech_prob": 1.42662303411617e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 19806, "start": 198.06, "end": 204.02, "text": " It is. So let's just unpack this from the ground up. Let's start with those two sentences about the delayed experiment.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 13, 407, 718, 311, 445, 26699, 341, 490, 264, 2727, 493, 13, 961, 311, 722, 365, 729, 732, 16579, 466, 264, 20268, 5120, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08539020538330078, "compression_ratio": 1.6424050632911393, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281864958182402e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 19806, "start": 204.3, "end": 206.22, "text": " Right, the parentheses versus the dashes.", "tokens": [50677, 1779, 11, 264, 34153, 5717, 264, 8240, 279, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08539020538330078, "compression_ratio": 1.6424050632911393, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281864958182402e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 19806, "start": 206.34, "end": 215.54, "text": " Yeah. Because if you look at standard style guides, like, you know, those heavy manuals that dictate proper writing, they categorize punctuation by tone.", "tokens": [50779, 865, 13, 1436, 498, 291, 574, 412, 3832, 3758, 17007, 11, 411, 11, 291, 458, 11, 729, 4676, 9688, 82, 300, 36071, 2296, 3579, 11, 436, 19250, 1125, 27006, 16073, 538, 8027, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08539020538330078, "compression_ratio": 1.6424050632911393, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281864958182402e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 19806, "start": 215.9, "end": 218.08, "text": " Which is kind of missing the forest for the trees.", "tokens": [51257, 3013, 307, 733, 295, 5361, 264, 6719, 337, 264, 5852, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08539020538330078, "compression_ratio": 1.6424050632911393, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281864958182402e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 19806, "start": 218.36, "end": 222.7, "text": " Totally. They claim parentheses are quiet, clinical, and meant for whispering.", "tokens": [51380, 22837, 13, 814, 3932, 34153, 366, 5677, 11, 9115, 11, 293, 4140, 337, 42445, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08539020538330078, "compression_ratio": 1.6424050632911393, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281864958182402e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 19806, "start": 222.7, "end": 227.84, "text": " And dash usage, they say, is loose, conversational, and meant for impact.", "tokens": [51597, 400, 8240, 14924, 11, 436, 584, 11, 307, 9612, 11, 2615, 1478, 11, 293, 4140, 337, 2712, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08539020538330078, "compression_ratio": 1.6424050632911393, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281864958182402e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 22806, "start": 228.06, "end": 236.7, "text": " But Fliction argues that this traditional stylistic interpretation just completely misses what is mechanically happening in the reader's brain.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 341, 5164, 23736, 3142, 14174, 445, 2584, 29394, 437, 307, 4236, 984, 2737, 294, 264, 15149, 311, 3567, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 22806, "start": 236.76, "end": 237.82, "text": " It's not about tone at all.", "tokens": [50800, 467, 311, 406, 466, 8027, 412, 439, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 22806, "start": 237.9, "end": 238.22, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50857, 883, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 22806, "start": 238.32, "end": 242.06, "text": " The paper suggests that parentheses act as stage directions in advance.", "tokens": [50878, 440, 3035, 13409, 300, 34153, 605, 382, 3233, 11095, 294, 7295, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 22806, "start": 242.38, "end": 244.76, "text": " Stage directions in advance. I love that phrasing.", "tokens": [51081, 25907, 11095, 294, 7295, 13, 286, 959, 300, 7636, 3349, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 22806, "start": 244.82, "end": 247.52, "text": " Right. Think about the sequential experience of reading.", "tokens": [51203, 1779, 13, 6557, 466, 264, 42881, 1752, 295, 3760, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 22806, "start": 247.52, "end": 255.12, "text": " When your eyes hit an opening parentheses before you've even processed the first word inside it, your brain receives a structural command.", "tokens": [51338, 1133, 428, 2575, 2045, 364, 5193, 34153, 949, 291, 600, 754, 18846, 264, 700, 1349, 1854, 309, 11, 428, 3567, 20717, 257, 15067, 5622, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 22806, "start": 255.4, "end": 256.56, "text": " It's bracing itself.", "tokens": [51732, 467, 311, 738, 5615, 2564, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14131005056973162, "compression_ratio": 1.6996699669966997, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485509568038182e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 25656, "start": 256.56, "end": 265.86, "text": " Exactly. It's being told, the main thread of this sentence is going on pause. Whatever comes next is subordinate. It's safe to skim.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 467, 311, 885, 1907, 11, 264, 2135, 7207, 295, 341, 8174, 307, 516, 322, 10465, 13, 8541, 1487, 958, 307, 1422, 37326, 13, 467, 311, 3273, 281, 1110, 332, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1024544986326303, "compression_ratio": 1.5164835164835164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609876893348361e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 25656, "start": 265.96, "end": 273.44, "text": " Safe to stim. So the parentheses actively downgrades the importance of the information before you even know what the information is.", "tokens": [50835, 27030, 281, 8983, 13, 407, 264, 34153, 13022, 760, 22626, 264, 7379, 295, 264, 1589, 949, 291, 754, 458, 437, 264, 1589, 307, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1024544986326303, "compression_ratio": 1.5164835164835164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609876893348361e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 25656, "start": 273.56, "end": 274.0, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51215, 48746, 736, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1024544986326303, "compression_ratio": 1.5164835164835164, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609876893348361e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 27400, "start": 274.0, "end": 283.94, "text": " It's a structural signpost saying, hey, feel free to ignore this part, which probably explains why we, you know, so often do skip right over them to get to the closing bracket.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 15067, 1465, 23744, 1566, 11, 4177, 11, 841, 1737, 281, 11200, 341, 644, 11, 597, 1391, 13948, 983, 321, 11, 291, 458, 11, 370, 2049, 360, 10023, 558, 670, 552, 281, 483, 281, 264, 10377, 16904, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08143319335638308, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204421902897396e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 27400, "start": 284.3, "end": 287.48, "text": " We just jump straight to the end of the parentheses to get back to the real sentence.", "tokens": [50880, 492, 445, 3012, 2997, 281, 264, 917, 295, 264, 34153, 281, 483, 646, 281, 264, 957, 8174, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08143319335638308, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204421902897396e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 27400, "start": 287.62, "end": 290.8, "text": " Yeah, exactly. But the dash behaves entirely differently.", "tokens": [51046, 865, 11, 2293, 13, 583, 264, 8240, 36896, 7696, 7614, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08143319335638308, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204421902897396e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 27400, "start": 291.0, "end": 297.1, "text": " Entirely differently. It opens a clause at full volume. It preserves the forward momentum of the thought.", "tokens": [51215, 3951, 621, 356, 7614, 13, 467, 9870, 257, 25925, 412, 1577, 5523, 13, 467, 1183, 9054, 264, 2128, 11244, 295, 264, 1194, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08143319335638308, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204421902897396e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 29710, "start": 297.1, "end": 298.32000000000005, "text": " It doesn't let you relax.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 718, 291, 5789, 13, 50426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.125989933013916, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.513033622002613e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 29710, "start": 298.32000000000005, "end": 305.02000000000004, "text": " No. And crucially, it provides zero structural warning about the hierarchy of the information that follows.", "tokens": [50426, 883, 13, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 309, 6417, 4018, 15067, 9164, 466, 264, 22333, 295, 264, 1589, 300, 10002, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.125989933013916, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.513033622002613e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 29710, "start": 305.14000000000004, "end": 314.14000000000004, "text": " So when you hit a dash, you don't know if the upcoming words are a minor interruption or a quick correction or literally the absolute climax of the entire sentence.", "tokens": [50767, 407, 562, 291, 2045, 257, 8240, 11, 291, 500, 380, 458, 498, 264, 11500, 2283, 366, 257, 6696, 728, 11266, 420, 257, 1702, 19984, 420, 3736, 264, 8236, 41329, 295, 264, 2302, 8174, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.125989933013916, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.513033622002613e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 29710, "start": 314.34000000000003, "end": 315.34000000000003, "text": " You're completely in the dark.", "tokens": [51227, 509, 434, 2584, 294, 264, 2877, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.125989933013916, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.513033622002613e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 29710, "start": 315.62, "end": 315.76000000000005, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51291, 865, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.125989933013916, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.513033622002613e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 29710, "start": 315.84000000000003, "end": 318.46000000000004, "text": " The dash forces ambiguity onto the reader.", "tokens": [51302, 440, 8240, 5874, 46519, 3911, 264, 15149, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.125989933013916, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.513033622002613e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 29710, "start": 318.52000000000004, "end": 319.20000000000005, "text": " Oh, that's interesting.", "tokens": [51436, 876, 11, 300, 311, 1880, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.125989933013916, "compression_ratio": 1.5703125, "no_speech_prob": 1.513033622002613e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 31920, "start": 319.2, "end": 327.0, "text": " Yeah. Like if I write, there was only one solution, repair the system. The text after the dash isn't a secondary thought.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 1743, 498, 286, 2464, 11, 456, 390, 787, 472, 3827, 11, 10535, 264, 1185, 13, 440, 2487, 934, 264, 8240, 1943, 380, 257, 11396, 1194, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08687430672023608, "compression_ratio": 1.684782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678043474887554e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 31920, "start": 327.12, "end": 329.38, "text": " Right. It's the main point. It's resolution.", "tokens": [50761, 1779, 13, 467, 311, 264, 2135, 935, 13, 467, 311, 8669, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08687430672023608, "compression_ratio": 1.684782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678043474887554e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 31920, "start": 329.65999999999997, "end": 336.62, "text": " Exactly. It's the resolution of the thought. So to understand why writers use dashes, we really have to look at what writing actually is.", "tokens": [50888, 7587, 13, 467, 311, 264, 8669, 295, 264, 1194, 13, 407, 281, 1223, 983, 13491, 764, 8240, 279, 11, 321, 534, 362, 281, 574, 412, 437, 3579, 767, 307, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08687430672023608, "compression_ratio": 1.684782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678043474887554e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 31920, "start": 336.7, "end": 337.94, "text": " Okay. What is writing then?", "tokens": [51240, 1033, 13, 708, 307, 3579, 550, 30, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08687430672023608, "compression_ratio": 1.684782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678043474887554e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 31920, "start": 338.03999999999996, "end": 346.28, "text": " Well, writing is a process of severe data compression. It takes the incredibly high resolution, multi-channel signal of human speech", "tokens": [51307, 1042, 11, 3579, 307, 257, 1399, 295, 8922, 1412, 19355, 13, 467, 2516, 264, 6252, 1090, 8669, 11, 4825, 12, 339, 11444, 6358, 295, 1952, 6218, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08687430672023608, "compression_ratio": 1.684782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678043474887554e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 34628, "start": 346.28, "end": 350.97999999999996, "text": " and compresses it down into a handful of lossy static symbols.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 14778, 279, 309, 760, 666, 257, 16458, 295, 4470, 88, 13437, 16944, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 34628, "start": 351.15999999999997, "end": 353.85999999999996, "text": " Lossy, like a low quality JPEG or something.", "tokens": [50609, 441, 772, 88, 11, 411, 257, 2295, 3125, 508, 5208, 38, 420, 746, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 34628, "start": 354.05999999999995, "end": 361.73999999999995, "text": " Exactly like that. When we speak in real life, we use pitch modulation, we use micropauses, changes in speaking pace, and register shifts.", "tokens": [50754, 7587, 411, 300, 13, 1133, 321, 1710, 294, 957, 993, 11, 321, 764, 7293, 42288, 11, 321, 764, 3123, 1513, 64, 8355, 11, 2962, 294, 4124, 11638, 11, 293, 7280, 19201, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 34628, "start": 361.88, "end": 363.94, "text": " We use our hands, our eyebrows.", "tokens": [51145, 492, 764, 527, 2377, 11, 527, 19916, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 34628, "start": 364.17999999999995, "end": 364.76, "text": " All of it.", "tokens": [51260, 1057, 295, 309, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 34628, "start": 364.78, "end": 364.97999999999996, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51290, 865, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 34628, "start": 365.03999999999996, "end": 367.73999999999995, "text": " And all of those biological signals carry structural meaning.", "tokens": [51303, 400, 439, 295, 729, 13910, 12354, 3985, 15067, 3620, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 34628, "start": 367.73999999999995, "end": 370.96, "text": " I've actually been thinking a lot about this compression problem.", "tokens": [51438, 286, 600, 767, 668, 1953, 257, 688, 466, 341, 19355, 1154, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13073531368322538, "compression_ratio": 1.5608856088560885, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779802815639842e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 37096, "start": 370.96, "end": 380.84, "text": " Writing with punctuation feels like trying to paint a highly detailed three-dimensional landscape using only a five-pack of chunky crayons.", "tokens": [50365, 32774, 365, 27006, 16073, 3417, 411, 1382, 281, 4225, 257, 5405, 9942, 1045, 12, 18759, 9661, 1228, 787, 257, 1732, 12, 9539, 295, 45392, 33073, 892, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08724265513212784, "compression_ratio": 1.4747899159663866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941646452407918e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 37096, "start": 380.96, "end": 383.38, "text": " That is a perfect analogy. You just don't have the colors.", "tokens": [50865, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 21663, 13, 509, 445, 500, 380, 362, 264, 4577, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08724265513212784, "compression_ratio": 1.4747899159663866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941646452407918e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 37096, "start": 383.79999999999995, "end": 389.46, "text": " Right. You get a comma, a period, a dash, a parenthesis, maybe a semicolon if you're feeling fancy.", "tokens": [51007, 1779, 13, 509, 483, 257, 22117, 11, 257, 2896, 11, 257, 8240, 11, 257, 23350, 9374, 11, 1310, 257, 27515, 38780, 498, 291, 434, 2633, 10247, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08724265513212784, "compression_ratio": 1.4747899159663866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941646452407918e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 37096, "start": 389.96, "end": 393.74, "text": " But human speech is a high-definition 3D photograph.", "tokens": [51315, 583, 1952, 6218, 307, 257, 1090, 12, 1479, 5194, 849, 805, 35, 8348, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08724265513212784, "compression_ratio": 1.4747899159663866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2941646452407918e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 39374, "start": 393.74, "end": 395.66, "text": " There's so much nuance in speech.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 311, 370, 709, 42625, 294, 6218, 13, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11229037394565819, "compression_ratio": 1.5880398671096345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189424154224418e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 39374, "start": 395.78000000000003, "end": 403.22, "text": " Yeah, like a quarter-second pause with a level pitch means something entirely different than a half-second pause where your voice drops a full octave.", "tokens": [50467, 865, 11, 411, 257, 6555, 12, 27375, 10465, 365, 257, 1496, 7293, 1355, 746, 7696, 819, 813, 257, 1922, 12, 27375, 10465, 689, 428, 3177, 11438, 257, 1577, 44441, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11229037394565819, "compression_ratio": 1.5880398671096345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189424154224418e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 39374, "start": 403.42, "end": 404.14, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [50849, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11229037394565819, "compression_ratio": 1.5880398671096345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189424154224418e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 39374, "start": 404.72, "end": 411.88, "text": " But on the printed page, both of those rich vocal events are flattened into the exact same symbol, usually just a comma.", "tokens": [50914, 583, 322, 264, 13567, 3028, 11, 1293, 295, 729, 4593, 11657, 3931, 366, 24183, 292, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 5986, 11, 2673, 445, 257, 22117, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11229037394565819, "compression_ratio": 1.5880398671096345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189424154224418e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 39374, "start": 412.36, "end": 418.66, "text": " Which is why the chunky crayon analogy works so well. It captures the structural lossiness of text perfectly.", "tokens": [51296, 3013, 307, 983, 264, 45392, 33073, 266, 21663, 1985, 370, 731, 13, 467, 27986, 264, 15067, 4470, 1324, 295, 2487, 6239, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11229037394565819, "compression_ratio": 1.5880398671096345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189424154224418e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 39374, "start": 419.38, "end": 422.08, "text": " The punctuation marks are just coarse buckets.", "tokens": [51647, 440, 27006, 16073, 10640, 366, 445, 39312, 32191, 13, 51782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11229037394565819, "compression_ratio": 1.5880398671096345, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189424154224418e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 42208, "start": 422.08, "end": 426.91999999999996, "text": " Coarse buckets attempting to catch a continuous, highly nuanced stream of vocal data.", "tokens": [50365, 3066, 11668, 32191, 22001, 281, 3745, 257, 10957, 11, 5405, 45115, 4309, 295, 11657, 1412, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08669799566268921, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.721172575123997e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 42208, "start": 427.06, "end": 430.14, "text": " Right. And this explains a massive paradox in modern writing.", "tokens": [50614, 1779, 13, 400, 341, 13948, 257, 5994, 26221, 294, 4363, 3579, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08669799566268921, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.721172575123997e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 42208, "start": 431.08, "end": 434.62, "text": " Grammar purists constantly complain that writers overuse the M-dash.", "tokens": [50815, 22130, 6209, 1864, 1751, 6460, 11024, 300, 13491, 670, 438, 264, 376, 12, 67, 1299, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08669799566268921, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.721172575123997e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 42208, "start": 434.68, "end": 437.62, "text": " Oh yeah, they hate it. They say it shouldn't be used in formal context.", "tokens": [50995, 876, 1338, 11, 436, 4700, 309, 13, 814, 584, 309, 4659, 380, 312, 1143, 294, 9860, 4319, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08669799566268921, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.721172575123997e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 42208, "start": 437.78, "end": 439.26, "text": " Right. But it is everywhere.", "tokens": [51150, 1779, 13, 583, 309, 307, 5315, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08669799566268921, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.721172575123997e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 42208, "start": 439.5, "end": 444.21999999999997, "text": " So if the dash is such a coarse bucket, why is it the favorite tool of so many writers?", "tokens": [51236, 407, 498, 264, 8240, 307, 1270, 257, 39312, 13058, 11, 983, 307, 309, 264, 2954, 2290, 295, 370, 867, 13491, 30, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08669799566268921, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.721172575123997e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 42208, "start": 444.52, "end": 448.88, "text": " I mean, why risk the ambiguity if a parenthesis or a comma could offer more grammatical precision?", "tokens": [51487, 286, 914, 11, 983, 3148, 264, 46519, 498, 257, 23350, 9374, 420, 257, 22117, 727, 2626, 544, 17570, 267, 804, 18356, 30, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08669799566268921, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.721172575123997e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 44888, "start": 448.88, "end": 453.32, "text": " Well, affliction suggests the dash is the bucket that loses the least amount of life.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 2096, 75, 4105, 13409, 264, 8240, 307, 264, 13058, 300, 18293, 264, 1935, 2372, 295, 993, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10929227678963307, "compression_ratio": 1.6941747572815533, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794550996955925e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 44888, "start": 453.62, "end": 455.12, "text": " The bucket that loses the least.", "tokens": [50602, 440, 13058, 300, 18293, 264, 1935, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10929227678963307, "compression_ratio": 1.6941747572815533, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794550996955925e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 44888, "start": 455.21999999999997, "end": 458.8, "text": " Yeah, because it refuses to warn the reader how to interpret the clause in advance.", "tokens": [50682, 865, 11, 570, 309, 33222, 281, 12286, 264, 15149, 577, 281, 7302, 264, 25925, 294, 7295, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10929227678963307, "compression_ratio": 1.6941747572815533, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794550996955925e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 44888, "start": 459.74, "end": 466.78, "text": " The dash forces the reader's brain to do the interpretive heavy lifting that a listener normally does by ear.", "tokens": [50908, 440, 8240, 5874, 264, 15149, 311, 3567, 281, 360, 264, 7302, 488, 4676, 15798, 300, 257, 31569, 5646, 775, 538, 1273, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10929227678963307, "compression_ratio": 1.6941747572815533, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794550996955925e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 44888, "start": 467.1, "end": 469.08, "text": " Oh, wow. So you have to work for it.", "tokens": [51276, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 407, 291, 362, 281, 589, 337, 309, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10929227678963307, "compression_ratio": 1.6941747572815533, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794550996955925e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 46908, "start": 469.08, "end": 471.96, "text": " You do. It preserves the ambiguity of emphasis.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 360, 13, 467, 1183, 9054, 264, 46519, 295, 16271, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1533908596286526, "compression_ratio": 1.5048543689320388, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 46908, "start": 471.96, "end": 478.38, "text": " It requires you to actively parse the sentence's structure on the fly, which makes the writing feel spoken.", "tokens": [50509, 467, 7029, 291, 281, 13022, 48377, 264, 8174, 311, 3877, 322, 264, 3603, 11, 597, 1669, 264, 3579, 841, 10759, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1533908596286526, "compression_ratio": 1.5048543689320388, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 46908, "start": 478.85999999999996, "end": 480.82, "text": " It feels alive and in motion.", "tokens": [50854, 467, 3417, 5465, 293, 294, 5394, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1533908596286526, "compression_ratio": 1.5048543689320388, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 46908, "start": 481.41999999999996, "end": 486.7, "text": " That makes total sense. It's the closest typographical equivalent to the dynamic, unresolved flow of human thought.", "tokens": [50982, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 467, 311, 264, 13699, 2125, 48434, 10344, 281, 264, 8546, 11, 517, 495, 29110, 3095, 295, 1952, 1194, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1533908596286526, "compression_ratio": 1.5048543689320388, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 46908, "start": 486.86, "end": 487.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51254, 7587, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1533908596286526, "compression_ratio": 1.5048543689320388, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 48724, "start": 487.24, "end": 495.84000000000003, "text": " Okay, so since punctuation is just the low-resolution residue of speech, we really should look at raw, unscripted human conversation.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 1670, 27006, 16073, 307, 445, 264, 2295, 12, 495, 3386, 34799, 295, 6218, 11, 321, 534, 820, 574, 412, 8936, 11, 2693, 5944, 292, 1952, 3761, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09622552477080247, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014816646952145e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 48724, "start": 496.18, "end": 500.24, "text": " Like, to see what this nested scope concept actually looks like in the wild.", "tokens": [50812, 1743, 11, 281, 536, 437, 341, 15646, 292, 11923, 3410, 767, 1542, 411, 294, 264, 4868, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09622552477080247, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014816646952145e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 48724, "start": 500.42, "end": 504.22, "text": " Because we nest scopes constantly when we talk, usually without even noticing.", "tokens": [51024, 1436, 321, 15646, 795, 30545, 6460, 562, 321, 751, 11, 2673, 1553, 754, 21814, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09622552477080247, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014816646952145e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 48724, "start": 504.44, "end": 507.54, "text": " Yeah, casual conversation is entirely built on nested scopes.", "tokens": [51225, 865, 11, 13052, 3761, 307, 7696, 3094, 322, 15646, 292, 795, 30545, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09622552477080247, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014816646952145e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 48724, "start": 507.64, "end": 508.3, "text": " Oh, 100%.", "tokens": [51385, 876, 11, 2319, 6856, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09622552477080247, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014816646952145e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 48724, "start": 508.3, "end": 512.24, "text": " Consider the mechanics of someone telling a mundane story about their weekend.", "tokens": [51418, 17416, 264, 12939, 295, 1580, 3585, 257, 43497, 1657, 466, 641, 6711, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09622552477080247, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014816646952145e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 48724, "start": 512.66, "end": 514.14, "text": " Like a co-worker on Monday morning.", "tokens": [51636, 1743, 257, 598, 12, 49402, 322, 8138, 2446, 13, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09622552477080247, "compression_ratio": 1.6527777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014816646952145e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 51724, "start": 517.24, "end": 518.62, "text": " The chronological thread of the story.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 19393, 4383, 7207, 295, 264, 1657, 13, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15646768730377483, "compression_ratio": 1.718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.091953780342104e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 51724, "start": 519.4, "end": 524.78, "text": " Then suddenly, they pause mid-sentence to explain some crucial context from the prior week.", "tokens": [50473, 1396, 5800, 11, 436, 10465, 2062, 12, 49315, 655, 281, 2903, 512, 11462, 4319, 490, 264, 4059, 1243, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15646768730377483, "compression_ratio": 1.718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.091953780342104e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 51724, "start": 524.96, "end": 529.12, "text": " Because you, the listener, need that context to understand the upcoming point.", "tokens": [50751, 1436, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 643, 300, 4319, 281, 1223, 264, 11500, 935, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15646768730377483, "compression_ratio": 1.718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.091953780342104e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 51724, "start": 529.24, "end": 535.26, "text": " Right, so they have opened a side context, they deliver the necessary backstory, and then they have to return to the main thread.", "tokens": [50965, 1779, 11, 370, 436, 362, 5625, 257, 1252, 4319, 11, 436, 4239, 264, 4818, 36899, 11, 293, 550, 436, 362, 281, 2736, 281, 264, 2135, 7207, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15646768730377483, "compression_ratio": 1.718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.091953780342104e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 51724, "start": 535.6, "end": 539.7, "text": " And to do this, they almost universally deploy a return marker.", "tokens": [51283, 400, 281, 360, 341, 11, 436, 1920, 43995, 7274, 257, 2736, 15247, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15646768730377483, "compression_ratio": 1.718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.091953780342104e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 51724, "start": 539.86, "end": 542.0, "text": " A return marker. Like the word A, anyway.", "tokens": [51496, 316, 2736, 15247, 13, 1743, 264, 1349, 316, 11, 4033, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15646768730377483, "compression_ratio": 1.718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.091953780342104e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 54200, "start": 542.0, "end": 549.86, "text": " Exactly. Anyway, or, so, as I was saying, which acts as a localized command to close the inner scope and resume the outer one.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 5684, 11, 420, 11, 370, 11, 382, 286, 390, 1566, 11, 597, 10672, 382, 257, 44574, 5622, 281, 1998, 264, 7284, 11923, 293, 15358, 264, 10847, 472, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783445863642245, "compression_ratio": 1.5938697318007662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427791202019981e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 54200, "start": 550.46, "end": 555.54, "text": " It's like, so, I was at the grocery store. Oh, which reminds me, I ran into your sister last week. She says, hi.", "tokens": [50788, 467, 311, 411, 11, 370, 11, 286, 390, 412, 264, 14410, 3531, 13, 876, 11, 597, 12025, 385, 11, 286, 5872, 666, 428, 4892, 1036, 1243, 13, 1240, 1619, 11, 4879, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783445863642245, "compression_ratio": 1.5938697318007662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427791202019981e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 54200, "start": 555.62, "end": 558.02, "text": " Anyway, I was at the store, and I saw this weird fruit.", "tokens": [51046, 5684, 11, 286, 390, 412, 264, 3531, 11, 293, 286, 1866, 341, 3657, 6773, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783445863642245, "compression_ratio": 1.5938697318007662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427791202019981e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 54200, "start": 558.28, "end": 559.12, "text": " Perfect example.", "tokens": [51179, 10246, 1365, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783445863642245, "compression_ratio": 1.5938697318007662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427791202019981e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 54200, "start": 559.34, "end": 563.14, "text": " And we do this effortlessly. But imagine trying to transcribe that faithfully.", "tokens": [51232, 400, 321, 360, 341, 4630, 12048, 13, 583, 3811, 1382, 281, 1145, 8056, 300, 4522, 2277, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783445863642245, "compression_ratio": 1.5938697318007662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427791202019981e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 54200, "start": 563.28, "end": 563.98, "text": " It would be a nightmare.", "tokens": [51429, 467, 576, 312, 257, 18724, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783445863642245, "compression_ratio": 1.5938697318007662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427791202019981e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 56398, "start": 563.98, "end": 570.48, "text": " You'd have to record not just the fact that a digression happened, but the depth of the digression, the urgency, and the tone.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1116, 362, 281, 2136, 406, 445, 264, 1186, 300, 257, 2528, 2775, 2011, 11, 457, 264, 7161, 295, 264, 2528, 2775, 11, 264, 29734, 11, 293, 264, 8027, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09561808474429019, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.567162523884169e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 56398, "start": 570.88, "end": 578.46, "text": " And whether the speaker assumed you still held the grocery store context in your active memory by the time they finally said, anyway.", "tokens": [50710, 400, 1968, 264, 8145, 15895, 291, 920, 5167, 264, 14410, 3531, 4319, 294, 428, 4967, 4675, 538, 264, 565, 436, 2721, 848, 11, 4033, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09561808474429019, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.567162523884169e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 56398, "start": 578.88, "end": 587.74, "text": " A completely honest transcript of everyday speech would just be an unreadable mess of false starts, dashed interruptions, and complex re-entries.", "tokens": [51110, 316, 2584, 3245, 24444, 295, 7429, 6218, 576, 445, 312, 364, 517, 2538, 712, 2082, 295, 7908, 3719, 11, 8240, 292, 12729, 626, 11, 293, 3997, 319, 12, 317, 2244, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09561808474429019, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.567162523884169e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 56398, "start": 587.94, "end": 590.32, "text": " It would look like broken computer code on the page.", "tokens": [51563, 467, 576, 574, 411, 5463, 3820, 3089, 322, 264, 3028, 13, 51682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09561808474429019, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.567162523884169e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 56398, "start": 590.58, "end": 591.02, "text": " Literally.", "tokens": [51695, 23768, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09561808474429019, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.567162523884169e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 59102, "start": 591.02, "end": 599.56, "text": " Yet our brains compile and execute that messy code seamlessly in real time, which raises a really fundamental biological question.", "tokens": [50365, 10890, 527, 15442, 31413, 293, 14483, 300, 16191, 3089, 38083, 294, 957, 565, 11, 597, 19658, 257, 534, 8088, 13910, 1168, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13402804961571327, "compression_ratio": 1.558303886925795, "no_speech_prob": 1.655505485302633e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 59102, "start": 599.6999999999999, "end": 600.14, "text": " What's that?", "tokens": [50799, 708, 311, 300, 30, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13402804961571327, "compression_ratio": 1.558303886925795, "no_speech_prob": 1.655505485302633e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 59102, "start": 600.42, "end": 604.54, "text": " Well, what is physically happening in the brain when we track these conversational detours?", "tokens": [50835, 1042, 11, 437, 307, 9762, 2737, 294, 264, 3567, 562, 321, 2837, 613, 2615, 1478, 1141, 5067, 30, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13402804961571327, "compression_ratio": 1.558303886925795, "no_speech_prob": 1.655505485302633e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 59102, "start": 605.46, "end": 610.6999999999999, "text": " Fliction brings in cognitive science in Appendix D of the paper to ground this.", "tokens": [51087, 3235, 4105, 5607, 294, 15605, 3497, 294, 3132, 521, 970, 413, 295, 264, 3035, 281, 2727, 341, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13402804961571327, "compression_ratio": 1.558303886925795, "no_speech_prob": 1.655505485302633e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 59102, "start": 610.74, "end": 612.24, "text": " Right, the cognitive load aspect.", "tokens": [51351, 1779, 11, 264, 15605, 3677, 4171, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13402804961571327, "compression_ratio": 1.558303886925795, "no_speech_prob": 1.655505485302633e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 59102, "start": 612.42, "end": 612.6, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51435, 865, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13402804961571327, "compression_ratio": 1.558303886925795, "no_speech_prob": 1.655505485302633e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 59102, "start": 613.28, "end": 617.96, "text": " Tracking these nested rules and hierarchical tasks is not just a linguistic metaphor.", "tokens": [51478, 1765, 14134, 613, 15646, 292, 4474, 293, 35250, 804, 9608, 307, 406, 445, 257, 43002, 19157, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13402804961571327, "compression_ratio": 1.558303886925795, "no_speech_prob": 1.655505485302633e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 61796, "start": 617.96, "end": 622.2, "text": " It imposes a measurable physical load on our working memory.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 704, 4201, 257, 43615, 4001, 3677, 322, 527, 1364, 4675, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557496706644694, "compression_ratio": 1.6822742474916388, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689041420868024e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 61796, "start": 622.36, "end": 623.34, "text": " Wait, break that down for me.", "tokens": [50585, 3802, 11, 1821, 300, 760, 337, 385, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557496706644694, "compression_ratio": 1.6822742474916388, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689041420868024e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 61796, "start": 623.38, "end": 631.9200000000001, "text": " When you say measurable physical load, are you saying my brain is burning more calories to listen to a story with a digression than a story told in a straight line?", "tokens": [50636, 1133, 291, 584, 43615, 4001, 3677, 11, 366, 291, 1566, 452, 3567, 307, 9488, 544, 14904, 281, 2140, 281, 257, 1657, 365, 257, 2528, 2775, 813, 257, 1657, 1907, 294, 257, 2997, 1622, 30, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557496706644694, "compression_ratio": 1.6822742474916388, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689041420868024e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 61796, "start": 632.0, "end": 633.3000000000001, "text": " In a very real sense, yes.", "tokens": [51067, 682, 257, 588, 957, 2020, 11, 2086, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557496706644694, "compression_ratio": 1.6822742474916388, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689041420868024e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 61796, "start": 633.86, "end": 641.72, "text": " The psychologist Alan Baddeley's foundational models of working memory show that we have a strict limit on how many active chunks of information we can hold simultaneously.", "tokens": [51160, 440, 29514, 16442, 11523, 1479, 3420, 311, 32195, 5245, 295, 1364, 4675, 855, 300, 321, 362, 257, 10910, 4948, 322, 577, 867, 4967, 24004, 295, 1589, 321, 393, 1797, 16561, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557496706644694, "compression_ratio": 1.6822742474916388, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689041420868024e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 61796, "start": 641.9200000000001, "end": 643.84, "text": " Okay, so we only have so much RAM in our heads.", "tokens": [51563, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 787, 362, 370, 709, 14561, 294, 527, 8050, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557496706644694, "compression_ratio": 1.6822742474916388, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689041420868024e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 64384, "start": 643.84, "end": 654.86, "text": " Exactly. When a speaker opens a conversational scope-like, a digression, your brain must dedicate active cognitive resources to holding the outer context.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 1133, 257, 8145, 9870, 257, 2615, 1478, 11923, 12, 4092, 11, 257, 2528, 2775, 11, 428, 3567, 1633, 30718, 4967, 15605, 3593, 281, 5061, 264, 10847, 4319, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11766496924466865, "compression_ratio": 1.5707762557077625, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884412283088343e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 64384, "start": 655.02, "end": 656.9200000000001, "text": " The grocery store, in my example.", "tokens": [50924, 440, 14410, 3531, 11, 294, 452, 1365, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11766496924466865, "compression_ratio": 1.5707762557077625, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884412283088343e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 64384, "start": 657.0400000000001, "end": 663.72, "text": " Right. It has to hold the grocery store in a suspended state while it processes the inner context, which is your sister saying hi.", "tokens": [51025, 1779, 13, 467, 575, 281, 1797, 264, 14410, 3531, 294, 257, 23437, 1785, 1339, 309, 7555, 264, 7284, 4319, 11, 597, 307, 428, 4892, 1566, 4879, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11766496924466865, "compression_ratio": 1.5707762557077625, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884412283088343e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 64384, "start": 664.08, "end": 664.9200000000001, "text": " So it's juggling.", "tokens": [51377, 407, 309, 311, 361, 29921, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11766496924466865, "compression_ratio": 1.5707762557077625, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884412283088343e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 64384, "start": 665.3000000000001, "end": 665.76, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51438, 467, 307, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11766496924466865, "compression_ratio": 1.5707762557077625, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884412283088343e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 66576, "start": 665.76, "end": 672.96, "text": " Brain imaging studies, particularly the work of Angela Friederici on sentence processing that Feliciano references, show this beautifully.", "tokens": [50365, 29783, 25036, 5313, 11, 4098, 264, 589, 295, 20848, 17605, 260, 8787, 322, 8174, 9007, 300, 13298, 299, 6254, 15400, 11, 855, 341, 16525, 13, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10741097710349343, "compression_ratio": 1.6612377850162867, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 66576, "start": 673.06, "end": 674.02, "text": " What do the scans show?", "tokens": [50730, 708, 360, 264, 35116, 855, 30, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10741097710349343, "compression_ratio": 1.6612377850162867, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 66576, "start": 674.28, "end": 686.22, "text": " They show that parsing these hierarchical embedded sequences engages specific neural regions, notably Broca's area, far more intensely than processing simple linear sequences.", "tokens": [50791, 814, 855, 300, 21156, 278, 613, 35250, 804, 16741, 22978, 45576, 2685, 18161, 10682, 11, 31357, 5425, 496, 311, 1859, 11, 1400, 544, 43235, 813, 9007, 2199, 8213, 22978, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10741097710349343, "compression_ratio": 1.6612377850162867, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 66576, "start": 686.4, "end": 692.24, "text": " Hold on. I thought Broca's area was just the part of the brain that controlled the physical muscles of your mouth for speech production.", "tokens": [51397, 6962, 322, 13, 286, 1194, 5425, 496, 311, 1859, 390, 445, 264, 644, 295, 264, 3567, 300, 10164, 264, 4001, 9530, 295, 428, 4525, 337, 6218, 4265, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10741097710349343, "compression_ratio": 1.6612377850162867, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 66576, "start": 692.66, "end": 693.84, "text": " That's what a lot of people think.", "tokens": [51710, 663, 311, 437, 257, 688, 295, 561, 519, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10741097710349343, "compression_ratio": 1.6612377850162867, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 69384, "start": 693.84, "end": 697.34, "text": " But you're saying it's actually doing the architectural math of holding sentences open.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 291, 434, 1566, 309, 311, 767, 884, 264, 26621, 5221, 295, 5061, 16579, 1269, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13030065072549357, "compression_ratio": 1.7247386759581882, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414788144529125e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 69384, "start": 697.46, "end": 699.46, "text": " That was the classical understanding for a long time.", "tokens": [50546, 663, 390, 264, 13735, 3701, 337, 257, 938, 565, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13030065072549357, "compression_ratio": 1.7247386759581882, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414788144529125e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 69384, "start": 699.64, "end": 702.0, "text": " The Broca's area was primarily for motor control.", "tokens": [50655, 440, 5425, 496, 311, 1859, 390, 10029, 337, 5932, 1969, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13030065072549357, "compression_ratio": 1.7247386759581882, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414788144529125e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 69384, "start": 702.94, "end": 709.96, "text": " But modern neuroimaging reveals it acts as a critical hub for syntactic processing and hierarchical sequencing.", "tokens": [50820, 583, 4363, 16499, 332, 3568, 20893, 309, 10672, 382, 257, 4924, 11838, 337, 23980, 19892, 9007, 293, 35250, 804, 32693, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13030065072549357, "compression_ratio": 1.7247386759581882, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414788144529125e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 69384, "start": 710.4200000000001, "end": 712.94, "text": " It manages the structural relationships of language.", "tokens": [51194, 467, 22489, 264, 15067, 6159, 295, 2856, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13030065072549357, "compression_ratio": 1.7247386759581882, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414788144529125e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 69384, "start": 713.36, "end": 719.38, "text": " The deeper the nesting, the harder Broca's area and the surrounding network have to work to maintain the scaffolding.", "tokens": [51341, 440, 7731, 264, 297, 8714, 11, 264, 6081, 5425, 496, 311, 1859, 293, 264, 11498, 3209, 362, 281, 589, 281, 6909, 264, 44094, 278, 13, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13030065072549357, "compression_ratio": 1.7247386759581882, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414788144529125e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 69384, "start": 719.5, "end": 720.44, "text": " That is fascinating.", "tokens": [51648, 663, 307, 10343, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13030065072549357, "compression_ratio": 1.7247386759581882, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414788144529125e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 72044, "start": 720.44, "end": 722.9000000000001, "text": " And it's not just polite digressions either, right?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 311, 406, 445, 25171, 2528, 735, 626, 2139, 11, 558, 30, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13886749869898746, "compression_ratio": 1.502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758303508252915e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 72044, "start": 723.2800000000001, "end": 726.3000000000001, "text": " Self-correction is a form of nested scope, isn't it?", "tokens": [50507, 16348, 12, 19558, 11417, 307, 257, 1254, 295, 15646, 292, 11923, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13886749869898746, "compression_ratio": 1.502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758303508252915e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 72044, "start": 726.44, "end": 726.86, "text": " Absolutely.", "tokens": [50665, 7021, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13886749869898746, "compression_ratio": 1.502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758303508252915e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 72044, "start": 727.1800000000001, "end": 731.5600000000001, "text": " Where the original plan for a sentence is just abandon mid-flight for an interruption.", "tokens": [50702, 2305, 264, 3380, 1393, 337, 257, 8174, 307, 445, 9072, 2062, 12, 43636, 337, 364, 728, 11266, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13886749869898746, "compression_ratio": 1.502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758303508252915e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 72044, "start": 731.9200000000001, "end": 738.82, "text": " You start saying something, realize you have the facts wrong, and bulldoze over your own sentence with a new thought.", "tokens": [50939, 509, 722, 1566, 746, 11, 4325, 291, 362, 264, 9130, 2085, 11, 293, 4693, 2595, 1381, 670, 428, 1065, 8174, 365, 257, 777, 1194, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13886749869898746, "compression_ratio": 1.502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758303508252915e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 72044, "start": 738.98, "end": 739.84, "text": " We do it all the time.", "tokens": [51292, 492, 360, 309, 439, 264, 565, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13886749869898746, "compression_ratio": 1.502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758303508252915e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 73984, "start": 739.84, "end": 742.9200000000001, "text": " The inner scope doesn't neatly return to the outer scope.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7284, 11923, 1177, 380, 36634, 2736, 281, 264, 10847, 11923, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 73984, "start": 743.0, "end": 744.96, "text": " It just annihilates it entirely.", "tokens": [50523, 467, 445, 40430, 388, 1024, 309, 7696, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 73984, "start": 745.12, "end": 745.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50629, 1779, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 73984, "start": 745.26, "end": 746.36, "text": " It's a destructive edit.", "tokens": [50636, 467, 311, 257, 26960, 8129, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 73984, "start": 747.46, "end": 751.62, "text": " And, you know, jokes manipulate this structural expectation deliberately.", "tokens": [50746, 400, 11, 291, 458, 11, 14439, 20459, 341, 15067, 14334, 23506, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 73984, "start": 751.9200000000001, "end": 753.64, "text": " Oh, I hadn't even thought about jokes.", "tokens": [50969, 876, 11, 286, 8782, 380, 754, 1194, 466, 14439, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 73984, "start": 753.76, "end": 753.96, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51061, 865, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 73984, "start": 754.12, "end": 758.0400000000001, "text": " The architecture of a joke is entirely dependent on nested scope manipulation.", "tokens": [51079, 440, 9482, 295, 257, 7647, 307, 7696, 12334, 322, 15646, 292, 11923, 26475, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943145025344122, "compression_ratio": 1.5238095238095237, "no_speech_prob": 2.2186748965813408e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 75804, "start": 758.04, "end": 764.1999999999999, "text": " The setup of the joke creates the outer scope, establishing a firm context and a set of assumptions.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8657, 295, 264, 7647, 7829, 264, 10847, 11923, 11, 22494, 257, 6174, 4319, 293, 257, 992, 295, 17695, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 75804, "start": 764.42, "end": 764.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50684, 1779, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 75804, "start": 764.92, "end": 770.9399999999999, "text": " Then the comedian introduces a digression or a secondary detail that seems entirely unrelated.", "tokens": [50709, 1396, 264, 30212, 31472, 257, 2528, 2775, 420, 257, 11396, 2607, 300, 2544, 7696, 38967, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 75804, "start": 771.3, "end": 774.06, "text": " Your brain opens an inner scope to hold it.", "tokens": [51028, 2260, 3567, 9870, 364, 7284, 11923, 281, 1797, 309, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 75804, "start": 774.14, "end": 776.74, "text": " Because you trust the comedian is going somewhere with it.", "tokens": [51170, 1436, 291, 3361, 264, 30212, 307, 516, 4079, 365, 309, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 75804, "start": 777.0, "end": 777.54, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51313, 7587, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 75804, "start": 777.74, "end": 777.9, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51350, 865, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 75804, "start": 778.0999999999999, "end": 783.74, "text": " And the punchline is the moment that magically resolves both the inner and outer scope simultaneously.", "tokens": [51368, 400, 264, 8135, 1889, 307, 264, 1623, 300, 39763, 7923, 977, 1293, 264, 7284, 293, 10847, 11923, 16561, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 75804, "start": 783.92, "end": 786.4, "text": " Revealing they were actually the same scope all along.", "tokens": [51659, 1300, 303, 4270, 436, 645, 767, 264, 912, 11923, 439, 2051, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15473738887853788, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346846615390321e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 78640, "start": 786.4, "end": 787.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 78640, "start": 787.74, "end": 794.72, "text": " The physical sensation of laughter is, in part, the sudden cognitive release of that working memory load.", "tokens": [50432, 440, 4001, 20069, 295, 13092, 307, 11, 294, 644, 11, 264, 3990, 15605, 4374, 295, 300, 1364, 4675, 3677, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 78640, "start": 794.88, "end": 796.76, "text": " It's a magic trick for your working memory.", "tokens": [50789, 467, 311, 257, 5585, 4282, 337, 428, 1364, 4675, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 78640, "start": 796.92, "end": 797.62, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50891, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 78640, "start": 797.78, "end": 805.56, "text": " The comedian creates tension by forcing you to hold multiple unresolved threads, and the punchline is the release of dropping them all at once.", "tokens": [50934, 440, 30212, 7829, 8980, 538, 19030, 291, 281, 1797, 3866, 517, 495, 29110, 19314, 11, 293, 264, 8135, 1889, 307, 264, 4374, 295, 13601, 552, 439, 412, 1564, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 78640, "start": 805.62, "end": 807.4599999999999, "text": " You can physically feel the relief.", "tokens": [51326, 509, 393, 9762, 841, 264, 10915, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 78640, "start": 807.56, "end": 808.5, "text": " You really can.", "tokens": [51423, 509, 534, 393, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 78640, "start": 809.0, "end": 812.22, "text": " But language hides these structural boundaries so well.", "tokens": [51495, 583, 2856, 35953, 613, 15067, 13180, 370, 731, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1247910805118894, "compression_ratio": 1.6370656370656371, "no_speech_prob": 1.87563202816432e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 81222, "start": 812.22, "end": 816.44, "text": " We do it so intuitively that it's hard to study just by listening to people talk.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 360, 309, 370, 46506, 300, 309, 311, 1152, 281, 2979, 445, 538, 4764, 281, 561, 751, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 81222, "start": 816.5600000000001, "end": 817.1800000000001, "text": " It's too fluid.", "tokens": [50582, 467, 311, 886, 9113, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 81222, "start": 817.44, "end": 817.64, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50626, 1779, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 81222, "start": 817.9, "end": 824.4200000000001, "text": " If we want to understand the pure mechanics of nested scope, we have to look at systems where the boundaries are drawn explicitly.", "tokens": [50649, 759, 321, 528, 281, 1223, 264, 6075, 12939, 295, 15646, 292, 11923, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 3652, 689, 264, 13180, 366, 10117, 20803, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 81222, "start": 824.9, "end": 826.28, "text": " Which brings us to computers.", "tokens": [50999, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 10807, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 81222, "start": 826.5600000000001, "end": 826.88, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51082, 1079, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 81222, "start": 827.0, "end": 828.4200000000001, "text": " Because computers don't have intuition.", "tokens": [51104, 1436, 10807, 500, 380, 362, 24002, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 81222, "start": 828.6600000000001, "end": 830.74, "text": " So how did early programmers deal with this?", "tokens": [51187, 407, 577, 630, 2440, 41504, 2028, 365, 341, 30, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 81222, "start": 830.8000000000001, "end": 832.78, "text": " They had to build the boundaries by hand.", "tokens": [51294, 814, 632, 281, 1322, 264, 13180, 538, 1011, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13150177552149847, "compression_ratio": 1.55078125, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053790623345677e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 83278, "start": 832.78, "end": 838.6999999999999, "text": " And this is where Flixian's analysis of 1990s video game design is so illuminating.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 689, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 5215, 295, 13384, 82, 960, 1216, 1715, 307, 370, 28593, 990, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572204474246863, "compression_ratio": 1.4901960784313726, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733227638735196e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 83278, "start": 838.9399999999999, "end": 840.06, "text": " I love this part of the paper.", "tokens": [50673, 286, 959, 341, 644, 295, 264, 3035, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572204474246863, "compression_ratio": 1.4901960784313726, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733227638735196e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 83278, "start": 840.3399999999999, "end": 841.06, "text": " It's brilliant.", "tokens": [50743, 467, 311, 10248, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572204474246863, "compression_ratio": 1.4901960784313726, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733227638735196e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 83278, "start": 842.02, "end": 846.48, "text": " Game designers in the early 90s weren't consulting linguists or neuroscientists.", "tokens": [50827, 7522, 16196, 294, 264, 2440, 4289, 82, 4999, 380, 23682, 21766, 1751, 420, 28813, 5412, 1751, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572204474246863, "compression_ratio": 1.4901960784313726, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733227638735196e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 83278, "start": 846.5799999999999, "end": 849.6999999999999, "text": " They were trying to solve a brutal engineering problem.", "tokens": [51055, 814, 645, 1382, 281, 5039, 257, 17878, 7043, 1154, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572204474246863, "compression_ratio": 1.4901960784313726, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733227638735196e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 83278, "start": 849.76, "end": 856.66, "text": " Which was, how do you build a massive, complex digital world on a machine that has maybe a few megabytes of RAM?", "tokens": [51214, 3013, 390, 11, 577, 360, 291, 1322, 257, 5994, 11, 3997, 4562, 1002, 322, 257, 3479, 300, 575, 1310, 257, 1326, 10816, 24538, 295, 14561, 30, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572204474246863, "compression_ratio": 1.4901960784313726, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733227638735196e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 85666, "start": 856.9399999999999, "end": 857.36, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50379, 7587, 13, 50400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 85666, "start": 857.88, "end": 862.28, "text": " To solve this, they independently reinvented the exact same logic of nested scope.", "tokens": [50426, 1407, 5039, 341, 11, 436, 21761, 33477, 292, 264, 1900, 912, 9952, 295, 15646, 292, 11923, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 85666, "start": 862.68, "end": 863.28, "text": " It's convergence.", "tokens": [50666, 467, 311, 32181, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 85666, "start": 863.54, "end": 864.76, "text": " Total convergent evolution.", "tokens": [50709, 23170, 9652, 6930, 9303, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 85666, "start": 864.98, "end": 865.16, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50781, 865, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 85666, "start": 865.52, "end": 870.9599999999999, "text": " Flixian uses the 1990 DOS game Commander Keen as the archetypal example.", "tokens": [50808, 3235, 970, 952, 4960, 264, 13384, 413, 4367, 1216, 20857, 3189, 268, 382, 264, 41852, 31862, 1365, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 85666, "start": 871.04, "end": 871.92, "text": " Commander Keen.", "tokens": [51084, 20857, 3189, 268, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 85666, "start": 872.04, "end": 872.24, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51134, 1033, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 85666, "start": 872.36, "end": 878.24, "text": " For anyone who didn't play 90s shareware games, Commander Keen uses a very distinct two-layer design.", "tokens": [51150, 1171, 2878, 567, 994, 380, 862, 4289, 82, 2073, 3039, 2813, 11, 20857, 3189, 268, 4960, 257, 588, 10644, 732, 12, 8376, 260, 1715, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 85666, "start": 878.62, "end": 880.16, "text": " It's perfect visual metaphor.", "tokens": [51463, 467, 311, 2176, 5056, 19157, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 85666, "start": 880.16, "end": 884.3, "text": " You start on an overworld map, which is this persistent outer scope.", "tokens": [51540, 509, 722, 322, 364, 670, 13217, 4471, 11, 597, 307, 341, 24315, 10847, 11923, 13, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17065752706220072, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938672265012553e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 88430, "start": 884.3, "end": 888.02, "text": " You walk your little guy around, looking at mountains and cities, deciding where to go.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1792, 428, 707, 2146, 926, 11, 1237, 412, 10233, 293, 6486, 11, 17990, 689, 281, 352, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 88430, "start": 888.14, "end": 889.62, "text": " You're just exploring the main thread.", "tokens": [50557, 509, 434, 445, 12736, 264, 2135, 7207, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 88430, "start": 889.78, "end": 890.02, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50639, 1779, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 88430, "start": 890.3599999999999, "end": 896.18, "text": " But when you walk into a specific city, the screen goes black, and you drop into a side-scrolling level.", "tokens": [50668, 583, 562, 291, 1792, 666, 257, 2685, 2307, 11, 264, 2568, 1709, 2211, 11, 293, 291, 3270, 666, 257, 1252, 12, 4417, 18688, 1496, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 88430, "start": 896.3399999999999, "end": 898.38, "text": " You have literally entered an inner scope.", "tokens": [50967, 509, 362, 3736, 9065, 364, 7284, 11923, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 88430, "start": 898.5, "end": 899.64, "text": " Completely new set of rules.", "tokens": [51075, 39978, 777, 992, 295, 4474, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 88430, "start": 899.92, "end": 900.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51146, 1079, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 88430, "start": 900.8599999999999, "end": 905.8399999999999, "text": " And the absolute rule of this game is what happens in the level stays in the level.", "tokens": [51193, 400, 264, 8236, 4978, 295, 341, 1216, 307, 437, 2314, 294, 264, 1496, 10834, 294, 264, 1496, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 88430, "start": 906.26, "end": 910.66, "text": " The enemies you alert, the platforms you move, the specific local score,", "tokens": [51463, 440, 7805, 291, 9615, 11, 264, 9473, 291, 1286, 11, 264, 2685, 2654, 6175, 11, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14099857455394307, "compression_ratio": 1.6619718309859155, "no_speech_prob": 1.965646612492322e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 91066, "start": 910.66, "end": 914.7199999999999, "text": " they exist only as long as you are actively inside that scope.", "tokens": [50365, 436, 2514, 787, 382, 938, 382, 291, 366, 13022, 1854, 300, 11923, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860374922163031, "compression_ratio": 1.5041666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 91066, "start": 915.38, "end": 916.1999999999999, "text": " They're highly localized.", "tokens": [50601, 814, 434, 5405, 44574, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860374922163031, "compression_ratio": 1.5041666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 91066, "start": 916.56, "end": 920.64, "text": " When you exit back to the map, all of those local variables just vanish.", "tokens": [50660, 1133, 291, 11043, 646, 281, 264, 4471, 11, 439, 295, 729, 2654, 9102, 445, 43584, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860374922163031, "compression_ratio": 1.5041666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 91066, "start": 921.06, "end": 927.76, "text": " They vanish because the computer literally clears them from memory to make room for the overworld map again.", "tokens": [50885, 814, 43584, 570, 264, 3820, 3736, 47033, 552, 490, 4675, 281, 652, 1808, 337, 264, 670, 13217, 4471, 797, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860374922163031, "compression_ratio": 1.5041666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 91066, "start": 927.98, "end": 928.88, "text": " It dumps the RAM.", "tokens": [51231, 467, 11430, 82, 264, 14561, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860374922163031, "compression_ratio": 1.5041666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 91066, "start": 929.04, "end": 929.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51284, 7587, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860374922163031, "compression_ratio": 1.5041666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 91066, "start": 930.12, "end": 932.8399999999999, "text": " The boundary conditions are what make the entire game possible.", "tokens": [51338, 440, 12866, 4487, 366, 437, 652, 264, 2302, 1216, 1944, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860374922163031, "compression_ratio": 1.5041666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 93284, "start": 932.84, "end": 937.64, "text": " If everything you did inside a level, like every enemy you killed, every block you moved,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 1203, 291, 630, 1854, 257, 1496, 11, 411, 633, 5945, 291, 4652, 11, 633, 3461, 291, 4259, 11, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 93284, "start": 938.0600000000001, "end": 941.02, "text": " permanently altered the overworld map in complex ways,", "tokens": [50626, 24042, 28783, 264, 670, 13217, 4471, 294, 3997, 2098, 11, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 93284, "start": 941.2, "end": 943.8000000000001, "text": " well, the computer would have to track all that data forever.", "tokens": [50783, 731, 11, 264, 3820, 576, 362, 281, 2837, 439, 300, 1412, 5680, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 93284, "start": 943.96, "end": 944.72, "text": " It would explode.", "tokens": [50921, 467, 576, 21411, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 93284, "start": 944.86, "end": 950.0, "text": " It would run out of memory instantly, and the game's logic would collapse into a tangled mess of dependencies.", "tokens": [50966, 467, 576, 1190, 484, 295, 4675, 13518, 11, 293, 264, 1216, 311, 9952, 576, 15584, 666, 257, 47192, 2082, 295, 36606, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 93284, "start": 950.5600000000001, "end": 954.38, "text": " But on the flip side, if nothing you did in the level mattered to the overworld,", "tokens": [51251, 583, 322, 264, 7929, 1252, 11, 498, 1825, 291, 630, 294, 264, 1496, 44282, 281, 264, 670, 13217, 11, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 93284, "start": 954.74, "end": 956.02, "text": " the game would have no progression.", "tokens": [51460, 264, 1216, 576, 362, 572, 18733, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 93284, "start": 956.2800000000001, "end": 957.64, "text": " It would be entirely pointless.", "tokens": [51537, 467, 576, 312, 7696, 32824, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 93284, "start": 957.82, "end": 957.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51614, 1779, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 93284, "start": 958.0, "end": 959.7800000000001, "text": " There has to be some communication between the two.", "tokens": [51623, 821, 575, 281, 312, 512, 6101, 1296, 264, 732, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.090554813840496, "compression_ratio": 1.7920792079207921, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796846252955077e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 95978, "start": 959.78, "end": 964.48, "text": " So they needed a way for the inner scope to talk to the outer scope, but only very specifically,", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 2978, 257, 636, 337, 264, 7284, 11923, 281, 751, 281, 264, 10847, 11923, 11, 457, 787, 588, 4682, 11, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 95978, "start": 965.02, "end": 966.22, "text": " which is why you have keys.", "tokens": [50627, 597, 307, 983, 291, 362, 9317, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 95978, "start": 966.6, "end": 967.54, "text": " The keys are everything.", "tokens": [50706, 440, 9317, 366, 1203, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 95978, "start": 967.8399999999999, "end": 971.8199999999999, "text": " You drop into a level, you navigate the hazards, and you find a red key card.", "tokens": [50768, 509, 3270, 666, 257, 1496, 11, 291, 12350, 264, 34516, 11, 293, 291, 915, 257, 2182, 2141, 2920, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 95978, "start": 972.3199999999999, "end": 975.64, "text": " When you exit the level, the enemies vanish, the hazards reset,", "tokens": [50992, 1133, 291, 11043, 264, 1496, 11, 264, 7805, 43584, 11, 264, 34516, 14322, 11, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 95978, "start": 976.1, "end": 980.48, "text": " but you bring that red key card back out to the overworld map to unlock a new path.", "tokens": [51181, 457, 291, 1565, 300, 2182, 2141, 2920, 646, 484, 281, 264, 670, 13217, 4471, 281, 11634, 257, 777, 3100, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 95978, "start": 980.68, "end": 984.76, "text": " The key is explicitly exported from the inner scope to the outer scope.", "tokens": [51410, 440, 2141, 307, 20803, 42055, 490, 264, 7284, 11923, 281, 264, 10847, 11923, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 95978, "start": 985.4599999999999, "end": 988.0799999999999, "text": " Exported. That's the exact technical term, isn't it?", "tokens": [51649, 50130, 292, 13, 663, 311, 264, 1900, 6191, 1433, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 95978, "start": 988.16, "end": 988.54, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51784, 467, 307, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13157710889830207, "compression_ratio": 1.7665505226480835, "no_speech_prob": 2.236392928484099e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 98854, "start": 988.54, "end": 991.4, "text": " The design is highly selective about state preservation.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1715, 307, 5405, 33930, 466, 1785, 27257, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 98854, "start": 992.1999999999999, "end": 996.42, "text": " Most things stay local, but a small, explicitly defined set of data,", "tokens": [50548, 4534, 721, 1754, 2654, 11, 457, 257, 1359, 11, 20803, 7642, 992, 295, 1412, 11, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 98854, "start": 996.66, "end": 1000.8199999999999, "text": " like the key or your total ammunition, gets exported back up the hierarchy.", "tokens": [50771, 411, 264, 2141, 420, 428, 3217, 32251, 11, 2170, 42055, 646, 493, 264, 22333, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 98854, "start": 1001.18, "end": 1004.26, "text": " And this logic also dictates how save points function, doesn't it?", "tokens": [50997, 400, 341, 9952, 611, 12569, 1024, 577, 3155, 2793, 2445, 11, 1177, 380, 309, 30, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 98854, "start": 1004.3, "end": 1004.9, "text": " Oh, perfectly.", "tokens": [51153, 876, 11, 6239, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 98854, "start": 1005.06, "end": 1009.3199999999999, "text": " A save point in a game like this is not a recording of your moment-to-moment actions.", "tokens": [51191, 316, 3155, 935, 294, 257, 1216, 411, 341, 307, 406, 257, 6613, 295, 428, 1623, 12, 1353, 12, 42544, 317, 5909, 13, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 98854, "start": 1009.5, "end": 1012.0, "text": " It doesn't remember that you were mid-jump over a pit.", "tokens": [51413, 467, 1177, 380, 1604, 300, 291, 645, 2062, 12, 73, 1420, 670, 257, 10147, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 98854, "start": 1012.18, "end": 1013.0, "text": " No, it doesn't care.", "tokens": [51547, 883, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 1127, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0978369156519572, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796949252161463e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 101300, "start": 1013.0, "end": 1018.16, "text": " It is a snapshot of the outer scope's accumulated state at an exact instant.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 30163, 295, 264, 10847, 11923, 311, 31346, 1785, 412, 364, 1900, 9836, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11900791755089393, "compression_ratio": 1.5124378109452736, "no_speech_prob": 1.642378615919482e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 101300, "start": 1018.6, "end": 1022.48, "text": " It records the inventory that has been successfully exported from completed levels.", "tokens": [50645, 467, 7724, 264, 14228, 300, 575, 668, 10727, 42055, 490, 7365, 4358, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11900791755089393, "compression_ratio": 1.5124378109452736, "no_speech_prob": 1.642378615919482e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 101300, "start": 1022.62, "end": 1026.78, "text": " So it deliberately ignores whatever is currently happening inside the temporary", "tokens": [50846, 407, 309, 23506, 5335, 2706, 2035, 307, 4362, 2737, 1854, 264, 13413, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11900791755089393, "compression_ratio": 1.5124378109452736, "no_speech_prob": 1.642378615919482e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 101300, "start": 1026.78, "end": 1029.84, "text": " unresolved inner scope of a level you might be halfway through.", "tokens": [51054, 517, 495, 29110, 7284, 11923, 295, 257, 1496, 291, 1062, 312, 15461, 807, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11900791755089393, "compression_ratio": 1.5124378109452736, "no_speech_prob": 1.642378615919482e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 102984, "start": 1029.84, "end": 1032.26, "text": " Exactly. It just discards the unresolved stuff.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 467, 445, 2983, 2287, 264, 517, 495, 29110, 1507, 13, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1573298730348286, "compression_ratio": 1.4422110552763818, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007728775678133e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 102984, "start": 1032.62, "end": 1041.58, "text": " When I hit save, I am closing all the parentheses up to that exact moment and telling the system this is the new baseline reality.", "tokens": [50504, 1133, 286, 2045, 3155, 11, 286, 669, 10377, 439, 264, 34153, 493, 281, 300, 1900, 1623, 293, 3585, 264, 1185, 341, 307, 264, 777, 20518, 4103, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1573298730348286, "compression_ratio": 1.4422110552763818, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007728775678133e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 102984, "start": 1041.78, "end": 1042.76, "text": " That's a great way to put it.", "tokens": [50962, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1573298730348286, "compression_ratio": 1.4422110552763818, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007728775678133e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 102984, "start": 1043.02, "end": 1048.02, "text": " But the paper contrasts Commander Keen with another classic 90s game, Descent.", "tokens": [51024, 583, 264, 3035, 8712, 82, 20857, 3189, 268, 365, 1071, 7230, 4289, 82, 1216, 11, 3885, 2207, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1573298730348286, "compression_ratio": 1.4422110552763818, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007728775678133e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 104802, "start": 1048.02, "end": 1050.3, "text": " How does Descent handle this differently?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 775, 3885, 2207, 4813, 341, 7614, 30, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12265918769088446, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248869875139626e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 104802, "start": 1050.98, "end": 1058.28, "text": " Descent is a brilliant counterexamble because it takes the invisible nested structure and makes it completely visible in three-dimensional space.", "tokens": [50513, 3885, 2207, 307, 257, 10248, 1207, 323, 87, 335, 638, 570, 309, 2516, 264, 14603, 15646, 292, 3877, 293, 1669, 309, 2584, 8974, 294, 1045, 12, 18759, 1901, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12265918769088446, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248869875139626e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 104802, "start": 1058.52, "end": 1059.6, "text": " Okay. Visible how?", "tokens": [50890, 1033, 13, 10410, 964, 577, 30, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12265918769088446, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248869875139626e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 104802, "start": 1059.9, "end": 1063.4, "text": " Well, in Commander Keen, you infer the scope as you go.", "tokens": [50959, 1042, 11, 294, 20857, 3189, 268, 11, 291, 13596, 264, 11923, 382, 291, 352, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12265918769088446, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248869875139626e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 104802, "start": 1063.7, "end": 1066.84, "text": " You have to walk around the map to find the levels and the locked doors.", "tokens": [51149, 509, 362, 281, 1792, 926, 264, 4471, 281, 915, 264, 4358, 293, 264, 9376, 8077, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12265918769088446, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248869875139626e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 104802, "start": 1067.0, "end": 1069.32, "text": " You're kind of blind to the overall structure.", "tokens": [51314, 509, 434, 733, 295, 6865, 281, 264, 4787, 3877, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12265918769088446, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248869875139626e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 104802, "start": 1069.54, "end": 1069.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51441, 1779, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12265918769088446, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248869875139626e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 106976, "start": 1069.76, "end": 1078.2, "text": " But Descent is a 3D spaceship shooter where the player can pull up a wireframe three-dimensional map of the entire mind system at any time.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3885, 2207, 307, 257, 805, 35, 39185, 24680, 689, 264, 4256, 393, 2235, 493, 257, 6234, 17265, 1045, 12, 18759, 4471, 295, 264, 2302, 1575, 1185, 412, 604, 565, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 106976, "start": 1078.48, "end": 1080.9, "text": " Oh, I remember that map. It was super disorienting.", "tokens": [50801, 876, 11, 286, 1604, 300, 4471, 13, 467, 390, 1687, 717, 19521, 278, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 106976, "start": 1081.02, "end": 1081.48, "text": " It was.", "tokens": [50928, 467, 390, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 106976, "start": 1081.92, "end": 1085.8, "text": " But this map shows you exactly where the red, blue, and yellow keys are.", "tokens": [50973, 583, 341, 4471, 3110, 291, 2293, 689, 264, 2182, 11, 3344, 11, 293, 5566, 9317, 366, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 106976, "start": 1086.18, "end": 1091.82, "text": " And it shows you the specific doors they correspond to, all before you've even entered those corridors.", "tokens": [51186, 400, 309, 3110, 291, 264, 2685, 8077, 436, 6805, 281, 11, 439, 949, 291, 600, 754, 9065, 729, 46920, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 106976, "start": 1092.36, "end": 1094.22, "text": " Let me make sure I'm mapping this back to the linguistics.", "tokens": [51495, 961, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 18350, 341, 646, 281, 264, 21766, 6006, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 106976, "start": 1094.34, "end": 1094.78, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [51594, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 106976, "start": 1095.02, "end": 1097.62, "text": " Commander Keen is like listening to a person speak.", "tokens": [51628, 20857, 3189, 268, 307, 411, 4764, 281, 257, 954, 1710, 13, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14162164745908795, "compression_ratio": 1.5961538461538463, "no_speech_prob": 1.478205687195644e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 109762, "start": 1097.62, "end": 1100.58, "text": " You figure out the digression on the fly as it happens.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2573, 484, 264, 2528, 2775, 322, 264, 3603, 382, 309, 2314, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12309651497082832, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 109762, "start": 1101.3999999999999, "end": 1110.1799999999998, "text": " Descent is like being handed a detailed grammatical diagram of every open parenthesis, dash, and subordinate clause before the person even opens their mouth.", "tokens": [50554, 3885, 2207, 307, 411, 885, 16013, 257, 9942, 17570, 267, 804, 10686, 295, 633, 1269, 23350, 9374, 11, 8240, 11, 293, 1422, 37326, 25925, 949, 264, 954, 754, 9870, 641, 4525, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12309651497082832, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 109762, "start": 1110.26, "end": 1112.4199999999998, "text": " You can see the whole nested structure at once.", "tokens": [50997, 509, 393, 536, 264, 1379, 15646, 292, 3877, 412, 1564, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12309651497082832, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 109762, "start": 1112.4399999999998, "end": 1113.54, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [51106, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12309651497082832, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 109762, "start": 1113.76, "end": 1114.9599999999998, "text": " That is the precise distinction.", "tokens": [51172, 663, 307, 264, 13600, 16844, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12309651497082832, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068095425910255e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 111496, "start": 1114.96, "end": 1127.54, "text": " And this exact logic of overworlds and levels of temporary local variables and permanent exported keys isn't just a quirk of retro games.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 1900, 9952, 295, 670, 13217, 82, 293, 4358, 295, 13413, 2654, 9102, 293, 10996, 42055, 9317, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 421, 18610, 295, 18820, 2813, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156561356556567, "compression_ratio": 1.5404255319148936, "no_speech_prob": 1.714111166374599e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 111496, "start": 1127.74, "end": 1128.46, "text": " It's bigger than that.", "tokens": [51004, 467, 311, 3801, 813, 300, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156561356556567, "compression_ratio": 1.5404255319148936, "no_speech_prob": 1.714111166374599e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 111496, "start": 1128.58, "end": 1129.08, "text": " Much bigger.", "tokens": [51046, 12313, 3801, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156561356556567, "compression_ratio": 1.5404255319148936, "no_speech_prob": 1.714111166374599e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 111496, "start": 1129.8, "end": 1134.08, "text": " It is the foundational architecture of computer programming and terminal environments.", "tokens": [51107, 467, 307, 264, 32195, 9482, 295, 3820, 9410, 293, 14709, 12388, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156561356556567, "compression_ratio": 1.5404255319148936, "no_speech_prob": 1.714111166374599e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 111496, "start": 1135.02, "end": 1141.68, "text": " Anyone who has opened a command line interface has physical muscle memory experience of nested scope.", "tokens": [51368, 14643, 567, 575, 5625, 257, 5622, 1622, 9226, 575, 4001, 8679, 4675, 1752, 295, 15646, 292, 11923, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156561356556567, "compression_ratio": 1.5404255319148936, "no_speech_prob": 1.714111166374599e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 114168, "start": 1141.68, "end": 1146.8400000000001, "text": " I use the terminal sometimes to run basic scripts, but honestly, I've never thought of it as a video game map.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 764, 264, 14709, 2171, 281, 1190, 3875, 23294, 11, 457, 6095, 11, 286, 600, 1128, 1194, 295, 309, 382, 257, 960, 1216, 4471, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1154228691915864, "compression_ratio": 1.5150214592274678, "no_speech_prob": 1.4100022148119673e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 114168, "start": 1147.0600000000002, "end": 1148.0, "text": " Most people don't.", "tokens": [50634, 4534, 561, 500, 380, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1154228691915864, "compression_ratio": 1.5150214592274678, "no_speech_prob": 1.4100022148119673e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 114168, "start": 1148.1000000000001, "end": 1151.92, "text": " How does entering a subshell in a terminal map onto the Commando Keen level analogy?", "tokens": [50686, 1012, 775, 11104, 257, 2090, 21288, 294, 257, 14709, 4471, 3911, 264, 3046, 1806, 3189, 268, 1496, 21663, 30, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1154228691915864, "compression_ratio": 1.5150214592274678, "no_speech_prob": 1.4100022148119673e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 114168, "start": 1152.16, "end": 1153.28, "text": " It is a one-to-one mapping.", "tokens": [50889, 467, 307, 257, 472, 12, 1353, 12, 546, 18350, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1154228691915864, "compression_ratio": 1.5150214592274678, "no_speech_prob": 1.4100022148119673e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 114168, "start": 1153.52, "end": 1155.96, "text": " When you open a terminal window, you start in your main shell.", "tokens": [50957, 1133, 291, 1269, 257, 14709, 4910, 11, 291, 722, 294, 428, 2135, 8720, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1154228691915864, "compression_ratio": 1.5150214592274678, "no_speech_prob": 1.4100022148119673e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 114168, "start": 1156.2, "end": 1157.3200000000002, "text": " This is your overworld map.", "tokens": [51091, 639, 307, 428, 670, 13217, 4471, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1154228691915864, "compression_ratio": 1.5150214592274678, "no_speech_prob": 1.4100022148119673e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 114168, "start": 1157.38, "end": 1157.88, "text": " Okay, I'm with you.", "tokens": [51150, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 365, 291, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1154228691915864, "compression_ratio": 1.5150214592274678, "no_speech_prob": 1.4100022148119673e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 115788, "start": 1157.88, "end": 1164.3400000000001, "text": " If you run a script or a program that opens a subshell, you have dropped into an inner scope, a level.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1190, 257, 5755, 420, 257, 1461, 300, 9870, 257, 2090, 21288, 11, 291, 362, 8119, 666, 364, 7284, 11923, 11, 257, 1496, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 115788, "start": 1164.3400000000001, "end": 1165.92, "text": " Oh, not only the side scroller now.", "tokens": [50688, 876, 11, 406, 787, 264, 1252, 11369, 260, 586, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 115788, "start": 1165.98, "end": 1166.3400000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50770, 7587, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 115788, "start": 1166.7, "end": 1173.7600000000002, "text": " If you define a new variable in that subshell, say you set a variable called temptar, that variable is local.", "tokens": [50806, 759, 291, 6964, 257, 777, 7006, 294, 300, 2090, 21288, 11, 584, 291, 992, 257, 7006, 1219, 13794, 289, 11, 300, 7006, 307, 2654, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 115788, "start": 1174.18, "end": 1175.46, "text": " It is trapped in the level.", "tokens": [51180, 467, 307, 14994, 294, 264, 1496, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 115788, "start": 1175.6000000000001, "end": 1178.3600000000001, "text": " So if I close the subshell and return to my main shell.", "tokens": [51251, 407, 498, 286, 1998, 264, 2090, 21288, 293, 2736, 281, 452, 2135, 8720, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 115788, "start": 1178.5200000000002, "end": 1180.2, "text": " Temptar no longer exists.", "tokens": [51397, 314, 4543, 289, 572, 2854, 8198, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 115788, "start": 1180.5400000000002, "end": 1183.6200000000001, "text": " The system wiped it, just like the enemies in Commander Keen.", "tokens": [51498, 440, 1185, 26879, 309, 11, 445, 411, 264, 7805, 294, 20857, 3189, 268, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 115788, "start": 1183.72, "end": 1184.8200000000002, "text": " Unless I export it.", "tokens": [51657, 16581, 286, 10725, 309, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1596221923828125, "compression_ratio": 1.6753731343283582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327278512887842e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 118482, "start": 1184.82, "end": 1188.98, "text": " If I use the export command in the terminal, I am grabbing the red key card.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 764, 264, 10725, 5622, 294, 264, 14709, 11, 286, 669, 23771, 264, 2182, 2141, 2920, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 118482, "start": 1189.34, "end": 1196.2, "text": " Export temptar tells the computer to bring that variable back out to the parent shell so it survives the closing of the inner scope.", "tokens": [50591, 50130, 13794, 289, 5112, 264, 3820, 281, 1565, 300, 7006, 646, 484, 281, 264, 2596, 8720, 370, 309, 46231, 264, 10377, 295, 264, 7284, 11923, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 118482, "start": 1196.28, "end": 1196.74, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50938, 48746, 736, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 118482, "start": 1197.08, "end": 1201.5, "text": " And this localized containment is why complex software doesn't instantly destroy itself.", "tokens": [50978, 400, 341, 44574, 44058, 307, 983, 3997, 4722, 1177, 380, 13518, 5293, 2564, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 118482, "start": 1201.58, "end": 1204.48, "text": " Because the blast radius of any mistake is contained.", "tokens": [51203, 1436, 264, 12035, 15845, 295, 604, 6146, 307, 16212, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 118482, "start": 1204.72, "end": 1204.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51360, 1779, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 118482, "start": 1205.1, "end": 1208.28, "text": " But it also creates cognitive traps for humans interacting with the software.", "tokens": [51379, 583, 309, 611, 7829, 15605, 24173, 337, 6255, 18017, 365, 264, 4722, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 118482, "start": 1208.74, "end": 1209.98, "text": " Look at the text editor Vim.", "tokens": [51561, 2053, 412, 264, 2487, 9839, 691, 332, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 118482, "start": 1210.06, "end": 1211.62, "text": " Oh no, the Vim trap.", "tokens": [51627, 876, 572, 11, 264, 691, 332, 11487, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1322932321517194, "compression_ratio": 1.6116504854368932, "no_speech_prob": 1.6361949772489282e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 121162, "start": 1211.62, "end": 1217.84, "text": " Vim operates on this strict nested logic, which is why it is notoriously terrifying for beginners.", "tokens": [50365, 691, 332, 22577, 322, 341, 10910, 15646, 292, 9952, 11, 597, 307, 983, 309, 307, 46772, 8994, 18106, 337, 26992, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943803099012867, "compression_ratio": 1.536480686695279, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295721282783004e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 121162, "start": 1218.2199999999998, "end": 1228.1, "text": " I think every person who has ever touched code has the shared trauma of opening Vim for the first time, mashing the keyboard, and then having to Google, how do I exit Vim?", "tokens": [50695, 286, 519, 633, 954, 567, 575, 1562, 9828, 3089, 575, 264, 5507, 11407, 295, 5193, 691, 332, 337, 264, 700, 565, 11, 2300, 571, 264, 10186, 11, 293, 550, 1419, 281, 3329, 11, 577, 360, 286, 11043, 691, 332, 30, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943803099012867, "compression_ratio": 1.536480686695279, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295721282783004e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 121162, "start": 1228.2399999999998, "end": 1229.1399999999999, "text": " It's a rite of passage.", "tokens": [51196, 467, 311, 257, 367, 642, 295, 11497, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943803099012867, "compression_ratio": 1.536480686695279, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295721282783004e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 121162, "start": 1229.32, "end": 1229.9799999999998, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51250, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943803099012867, "compression_ratio": 1.536480686695279, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295721282783004e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 121162, "start": 1230.3799999999999, "end": 1233.1599999999999, "text": " Why is it so hard to close a simple text program?", "tokens": [51303, 1545, 307, 309, 370, 1152, 281, 1998, 257, 2199, 2487, 1461, 30, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10943803099012867, "compression_ratio": 1.536480686695279, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295721282783004e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 123316, "start": 1233.16, "end": 1237.66, "text": " Because Vim enforces a strict separation of scopes through modes.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 691, 332, 25495, 887, 257, 10910, 14634, 295, 795, 30545, 807, 14068, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 123316, "start": 1238.0800000000002, "end": 1240.92, "text": " When you open Vim, you are in normal mode.", "tokens": [50611, 1133, 291, 1269, 691, 332, 11, 291, 366, 294, 2710, 4391, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 123316, "start": 1241.26, "end": 1245.66, "text": " This is the outer scope, the overworld, where keystrokes act as navigation commands.", "tokens": [50770, 639, 307, 264, 10847, 11923, 11, 264, 670, 13217, 11, 689, 2141, 27616, 5993, 605, 382, 17346, 16901, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 123316, "start": 1245.72, "end": 1247.92, "text": " So the keys aren't letters, they're movement.", "tokens": [50993, 407, 264, 9317, 3212, 380, 7825, 11, 436, 434, 3963, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 123316, "start": 1248.16, "end": 1248.3400000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51115, 1779, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 123316, "start": 1248.42, "end": 1253.3400000000001, "text": " If you want to type text, you press a specific key, usually I, to drop into insert mode.", "tokens": [51128, 759, 291, 528, 281, 2010, 2487, 11, 291, 1886, 257, 2685, 2141, 11, 2673, 286, 11, 281, 3270, 666, 8969, 4391, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 123316, "start": 1253.94, "end": 1255.46, "text": " This is the inner scope, the level.", "tokens": [51404, 639, 307, 264, 7284, 11923, 11, 264, 1496, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 123316, "start": 1255.6200000000001, "end": 1256.5400000000002, "text": " Okay, so you're in the level.", "tokens": [51488, 1033, 11, 370, 291, 434, 294, 264, 1496, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11899389891788878, "compression_ratio": 1.6434426229508197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141008664539603e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 125654, "start": 1256.54, "end": 1263.5, "text": " New users get trapped because they want to quit the program, and they know the command to quit is colon WQ, right?", "tokens": [50365, 1873, 5022, 483, 14994, 570, 436, 528, 281, 10366, 264, 1461, 11, 293, 436, 458, 264, 5622, 281, 10366, 307, 8255, 343, 48, 11, 558, 30, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11461314414311381, "compression_ratio": 1.7352941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298250726451413e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 125654, "start": 1264.0, "end": 1264.5, "text": " And quit.", "tokens": [50738, 400, 10366, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11461314414311381, "compression_ratio": 1.7352941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298250726451413e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 125654, "start": 1264.6599999999999, "end": 1265.84, "text": " Yeah, that's the famous command.", "tokens": [50771, 865, 11, 300, 311, 264, 4618, 5622, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11461314414311381, "compression_ratio": 1.7352941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298250726451413e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 125654, "start": 1265.96, "end": 1270.34, "text": " But they type colon WQ while they're still inside the inner scope of insert mode.", "tokens": [50836, 583, 436, 2010, 8255, 343, 48, 1339, 436, 434, 920, 1854, 264, 7284, 11923, 295, 8969, 4391, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11461314414311381, "compression_ratio": 1.7352941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298250726451413e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 125654, "start": 1270.98, "end": 1276.68, "text": " So the program just types the literal characters colon WQ into the document.", "tokens": [51087, 407, 264, 1461, 445, 3467, 264, 20411, 4342, 8255, 343, 48, 666, 264, 4166, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11461314414311381, "compression_ratio": 1.7352941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298250726451413e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 125654, "start": 1276.86, "end": 1281.5, "text": " They are trying to use the overworld exit command while they are still trapped inside the level.", "tokens": [51381, 814, 366, 1382, 281, 764, 264, 670, 13217, 11043, 5622, 1339, 436, 366, 920, 14994, 1854, 264, 1496, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11461314414311381, "compression_ratio": 1.7352941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298250726451413e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 128150, "start": 1281.5, "end": 1282.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14872662955467855, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594518527045406e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 128150, "start": 1282.52, "end": 1291.22, "text": " They don't realize they have to press the escape key to close the inner scope, return to normal mode, and then use the colon WQ command to close the outer scope.", "tokens": [50416, 814, 500, 380, 4325, 436, 362, 281, 1886, 264, 7615, 2141, 281, 1998, 264, 7284, 11923, 11, 2736, 281, 2710, 4391, 11, 293, 550, 764, 264, 8255, 343, 48, 5622, 281, 1998, 264, 10847, 11923, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14872662955467855, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594518527045406e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 128150, "start": 1291.36, "end": 1293.16, "text": " They lack the map of the scope boundary.", "tokens": [50858, 814, 5011, 264, 4471, 295, 264, 11923, 12866, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14872662955467855, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594518527045406e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 128150, "start": 1293.26, "end": 1294.04, "text": " That's exactly it.", "tokens": [50953, 663, 311, 2293, 309, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14872662955467855, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594518527045406e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 128150, "start": 1294.16, "end": 1298.48, "text": " The terminal also handles scope suspension beautifully through keyboard shortcuts.", "tokens": [50998, 440, 14709, 611, 18722, 11923, 15771, 16525, 807, 10186, 34620, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14872662955467855, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594518527045406e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 128150, "start": 1298.7, "end": 1300.5, "text": " Oh yeah, the kill and suspend signals.", "tokens": [51225, 876, 1338, 11, 264, 1961, 293, 42546, 12354, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14872662955467855, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594518527045406e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 128150, "start": 1300.7, "end": 1306.5, "text": " If you are running a program in the terminal and you press CAOC, it sends a kill signal.", "tokens": [51325, 759, 291, 366, 2614, 257, 1461, 294, 264, 14709, 293, 291, 1886, 22852, 30087, 11, 309, 14790, 257, 1961, 6358, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14872662955467855, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594518527045406e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 130650, "start": 1306.5, "end": 1311.78, "text": " It forcefully terminates the inner scope entirely and throws you back to the outer shell.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3464, 2277, 10761, 1024, 264, 7284, 11923, 7696, 293, 19251, 291, 646, 281, 264, 10847, 8720, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 130650, "start": 1312.14, "end": 1313.22, "text": " It's the bulldozer method.", "tokens": [50647, 467, 311, 264, 4693, 2595, 4527, 3170, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 130650, "start": 1313.36, "end": 1317.18, "text": " Like the self-correcting sentence that just abandons the original thought.", "tokens": [50708, 1743, 264, 2698, 12, 19558, 2554, 278, 8174, 300, 445, 410, 474, 892, 264, 3380, 1194, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 130650, "start": 1317.28, "end": 1318.24, "text": " We talked about that earlier.", "tokens": [50904, 492, 2825, 466, 300, 3071, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 130650, "start": 1318.38, "end": 1319.3, "text": " Right, it just ends it.", "tokens": [50959, 1779, 11, 309, 445, 5314, 309, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 130650, "start": 1319.58, "end": 1320.8, "text": " But what about CLZ?", "tokens": [51019, 583, 437, 466, 12855, 57, 30, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 130650, "start": 1321.24, "end": 1322.78, "text": " Yeah, what does that do structurally?", "tokens": [51102, 865, 11, 437, 775, 300, 360, 6594, 6512, 30, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 130650, "start": 1323.3, "end": 1325.66, "text": " CLZ does something structurally profound.", "tokens": [51205, 12855, 57, 775, 746, 6594, 6512, 14382, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 130650, "start": 1326.64, "end": 1328.3, "text": " It sends a suspend signal.", "tokens": [51372, 467, 14790, 257, 42546, 6358, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 130650, "start": 1328.9, "end": 1334.3, "text": " It takes the active inner scope, pauses its execution, and pushes it into the background.", "tokens": [51485, 467, 2516, 264, 4967, 7284, 11923, 11, 2502, 8355, 1080, 15058, 11, 293, 21020, 309, 666, 264, 3678, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 130650, "start": 1334.44, "end": 1335.92, "text": " It just freezes it in time.", "tokens": [51762, 467, 445, 1737, 12214, 309, 294, 565, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577919370987836, "compression_ratio": 1.6955017301038062, "no_speech_prob": 1.810849105214618e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 133592, "start": 1335.92, "end": 1343.04, "text": " It returns control to your outer shell, but the inner scope is still sitting there, frozen in memory, holding all its state.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 11247, 1969, 281, 428, 10847, 8720, 11, 457, 264, 7284, 11923, 307, 920, 3798, 456, 11, 12496, 294, 4675, 11, 5061, 439, 1080, 1785, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10183990880062706, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071248285827843e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 133592, "start": 1343.16, "end": 1344.3400000000001, "text": " So it's waiting for you.", "tokens": [50727, 407, 309, 311, 3806, 337, 291, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10183990880062706, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071248285827843e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 133592, "start": 1344.66, "end": 1344.92, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50802, 865, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10183990880062706, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071248285827843e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 133592, "start": 1345.3400000000001, "end": 1356.94, "text": " Later on, you can type FG, which stands for foreground, and the system pulls that frozen inner scope back up, resuming execution at the exact millisecond it was paused.", "tokens": [50836, 11965, 322, 11, 291, 393, 2010, 479, 38, 11, 597, 7382, 337, 32058, 11, 293, 264, 1185, 16982, 300, 12496, 7284, 11923, 646, 493, 11, 725, 24919, 15058, 412, 264, 1900, 27940, 18882, 309, 390, 46860, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10183990880062706, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071248285827843e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 133592, "start": 1357.16, "end": 1359.68, "text": " Let's relate this to something everyone does every day.", "tokens": [51427, 961, 311, 10961, 341, 281, 746, 1518, 775, 633, 786, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10183990880062706, "compression_ratio": 1.5702479338842976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071248285827843e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 135968, "start": 1359.68, "end": 1366.0, "text": " CLZ is the digital equivalent of holding your finger up while a friend is talking so you can answer a phone call.", "tokens": [50365, 12855, 57, 307, 264, 4562, 10344, 295, 5061, 428, 5984, 493, 1339, 257, 1277, 307, 1417, 370, 291, 393, 1867, 257, 2593, 818, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11708402633666992, "compression_ratio": 1.6748971193415638, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362116739623844e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 135968, "start": 1366.24, "end": 1367.22, "text": " That's a perfect parallel.", "tokens": [50693, 663, 311, 257, 2176, 8952, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11708402633666992, "compression_ratio": 1.6748971193415638, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362116739623844e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 135968, "start": 1367.5600000000002, "end": 1370.6000000000001, "text": " And then you turn back to your friend five minutes later and say, okay, where were we?", "tokens": [50759, 400, 550, 291, 1261, 646, 281, 428, 1277, 1732, 2077, 1780, 293, 584, 11, 1392, 11, 689, 645, 321, 30, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11708402633666992, "compression_ratio": 1.6748971193415638, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362116739623844e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 135968, "start": 1370.72, "end": 1372.16, "text": " You didn't kill the conversation.", "tokens": [50917, 509, 994, 380, 1961, 264, 3761, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11708402633666992, "compression_ratio": 1.6748971193415638, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362116739623844e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 135968, "start": 1372.3, "end": 1373.0, "text": " You suspended it.", "tokens": [50996, 509, 23437, 309, 13, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11708402633666992, "compression_ratio": 1.6748971193415638, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362116739623844e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 135968, "start": 1373.0800000000002, "end": 1378.64, "text": " You opened a new scope for the phone call, closed the phone call, and brought the original conversation back to the foreground.", "tokens": [51035, 509, 5625, 257, 777, 11923, 337, 264, 2593, 818, 11, 5395, 264, 2593, 818, 11, 293, 3038, 264, 3380, 3761, 646, 281, 264, 32058, 13, 51313], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11708402633666992, "compression_ratio": 1.6748971193415638, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362116739623844e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 137864, "start": 1378.64, "end": 1386.0400000000002, "text": " But to do that, your brain had to hold the where were we context and memory the entire time the phone call was happening.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 281, 360, 300, 11, 428, 3567, 632, 281, 1797, 264, 689, 645, 321, 4319, 293, 4675, 264, 2302, 565, 264, 2593, 818, 390, 2737, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931222815262644, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.432725574464222e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 137864, "start": 1386.3400000000001, "end": 1386.6000000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50750, 1079, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931222815262644, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.432725574464222e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 137864, "start": 1386.98, "end": 1396.8600000000001, "text": " And if we look at how programmers actually write code, they formalize this process of expectation, interruption, and recovery through structures called try-catch-finally blocks.", "tokens": [50782, 400, 498, 321, 574, 412, 577, 41504, 767, 2464, 3089, 11, 436, 9860, 1125, 341, 1399, 295, 14334, 11, 728, 11266, 11, 293, 8597, 807, 9227, 1219, 853, 12, 66, 852, 12, 5194, 379, 8474, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931222815262644, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.432725574464222e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 137864, "start": 1397.1000000000001, "end": 1401.0, "text": " Break down how a try-catch block works for someone who has never written a line of code.", "tokens": [51288, 16925, 760, 577, 257, 853, 12, 66, 852, 3461, 1985, 337, 1580, 567, 575, 1128, 3720, 257, 1622, 295, 3089, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0931222815262644, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.432725574464222e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 140100, "start": 1401.0, "end": 1402.22, "text": " What is the mechanism there?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 307, 264, 7513, 456, 30, 50426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 140100, "start": 1402.66, "end": 1406.34, "text": " Imagine you are giving a robot a list of nested instructions.", "tokens": [50448, 11739, 291, 366, 2902, 257, 7881, 257, 1329, 295, 15646, 292, 9415, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 140100, "start": 1407.0, "end": 1409.06, "text": " You say, try to go into the kitchen and bake a cake.", "tokens": [50665, 509, 584, 11, 853, 281, 352, 666, 264, 6525, 293, 16562, 257, 5908, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 140100, "start": 1409.44, "end": 1409.68, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50787, 1033, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 140100, "start": 1409.94, "end": 1410.84, "text": " Try to bake a cake.", "tokens": [50812, 6526, 281, 16562, 257, 5908, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 140100, "start": 1410.96, "end": 1413.18, "text": " Opening the try-block is opening a scope.", "tokens": [50863, 41137, 264, 853, 12, 28830, 307, 5193, 257, 11923, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 140100, "start": 1413.28, "end": 1413.5, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50979, 1033, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 140100, "start": 1413.7, "end": 1414.64, "text": " It sets an expectation.", "tokens": [51000, 467, 6352, 364, 14334, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 140100, "start": 1415.1, "end": 1416.7, "text": " The robot starts executing the steps.", "tokens": [51070, 440, 7881, 3719, 32368, 264, 4439, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 140100, "start": 1416.82, "end": 1417.04, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [51156, 2438, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 140100, "start": 1417.86, "end": 1419.36, "text": " But what happens if the oven is broken?", "tokens": [51208, 583, 437, 2314, 498, 264, 9090, 307, 5463, 30, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 140100, "start": 1419.7, "end": 1420.02, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51300, 1779, 13, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 140100, "start": 1420.5, "end": 1430.38, "text": " In a system without scope management, the robot might just crash or stand there forever or burn the house down because it doesn't know how to handle the unexpected failure.", "tokens": [51340, 682, 257, 1185, 1553, 11923, 4592, 11, 264, 7881, 1062, 445, 8252, 420, 1463, 456, 5680, 420, 5064, 264, 1782, 760, 570, 309, 1177, 380, 458, 577, 281, 4813, 264, 13106, 7763, 13, 51834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1742283663303732, "compression_ratio": 1.6491803278688524, "no_speech_prob": 1.604570100920133e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 143038, "start": 1430.38, "end": 1434.72, "text": " It encounters an error and has no instructions for how to bubble that error back up to you.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 26310, 364, 6713, 293, 575, 572, 9415, 337, 577, 281, 12212, 300, 6713, 646, 493, 281, 291, 13, 50582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 143038, "start": 1434.8000000000002, "end": 1435.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50586, 1779, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 143038, "start": 1435.16, "end": 1436.6000000000001, "text": " So programmers add a catch block.", "tokens": [50604, 407, 41504, 909, 257, 3745, 3461, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 143038, "start": 1437.3200000000002, "end": 1446.5800000000002, "text": " The catch block says if an error happens while you are inside the try-scope, stop immediately, contain the damage locally, and run these alternative instructions instead.", "tokens": [50712, 440, 3745, 3461, 1619, 498, 364, 6713, 2314, 1339, 291, 366, 1854, 264, 853, 12, 4417, 1114, 11, 1590, 4258, 11, 5304, 264, 4344, 16143, 11, 293, 1190, 613, 8535, 9415, 2602, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 143038, "start": 1447.0800000000002, "end": 1447.3400000000001, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [51200, 2438, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 143038, "start": 1447.42, "end": 1448.46, "text": " So it has a backup plan.", "tokens": [51217, 407, 309, 575, 257, 14807, 1393, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 143038, "start": 1448.7600000000002, "end": 1452.68, "text": " The robot catches the broken oven error and executes the backup plan.", "tokens": [51284, 440, 7881, 25496, 264, 5463, 9090, 6713, 293, 4454, 1819, 264, 14807, 1393, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 143038, "start": 1453.3400000000001, "end": 1453.94, "text": " Order a pizza.", "tokens": [51513, 16321, 257, 8298, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 143038, "start": 1454.0200000000002, "end": 1454.64, "text": " Order a pizza.", "tokens": [51547, 16321, 257, 8298, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 143038, "start": 1454.7600000000002, "end": 1455.7600000000002, "text": " That's a good catch block.", "tokens": [51584, 663, 311, 257, 665, 3745, 3461, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 143038, "start": 1455.8600000000001, "end": 1456.48, "text": " It's the best one.", "tokens": [51639, 467, 311, 264, 1151, 472, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 143038, "start": 1456.8000000000002, "end": 1459.38, "text": " And then, crucially, there's a finally block.", "tokens": [51686, 400, 550, 11, 5140, 1909, 11, 456, 311, 257, 2721, 3461, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12693693254377458, "compression_ratio": 1.8257839721254356, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671222357306e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 145938, "start": 1459.38, "end": 1461.22, "text": " What does the finally block do?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 775, 264, 2721, 3461, 360, 30, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367894729765335, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760887162029948e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 145938, "start": 1461.4, "end": 1465.44, "text": " The finally block runs no matter what happened, whether the cake succeeded or failed.", "tokens": [50466, 440, 2721, 3461, 6676, 572, 1871, 437, 2011, 11, 1968, 264, 5908, 20263, 420, 7612, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367894729765335, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760887162029948e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 145938, "start": 1465.88, "end": 1468.72, "text": " It says, before you return to the main program, clean up the kitchen.", "tokens": [50690, 467, 1619, 11, 949, 291, 2736, 281, 264, 2135, 1461, 11, 2541, 493, 264, 6525, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367894729765335, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760887162029948e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 145938, "start": 1469.1200000000001, "end": 1469.44, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50852, 3153, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367894729765335, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760887162029948e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 145938, "start": 1470.0, "end": 1479.7600000000002, "text": " It's a formalized contract for how to open a dangerous scope, handle an explosive interruption without destroying the whole system, and guarantee a safe return to the main timeline.", "tokens": [50896, 467, 311, 257, 9860, 1602, 4364, 337, 577, 281, 1269, 257, 5795, 11923, 11, 4813, 364, 24630, 728, 11266, 1553, 19926, 264, 1379, 1185, 11, 293, 10815, 257, 3273, 2736, 281, 264, 2135, 12933, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367894729765335, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760887162029948e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 145938, "start": 1480.64, "end": 1484.1000000000001, "text": " Programmers call this overarching concept lexical scope.", "tokens": [51428, 8338, 18552, 818, 341, 45501, 3410, 476, 87, 804, 11923, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1367894729765335, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760887162029948e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 148410, "start": 1484.1, "end": 1493.02, "text": " But Flexion's profound point is that computer scientists did not invent lexical scope to mimic human linguistics or psychology.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 29208, 313, 311, 14382, 935, 307, 300, 3820, 7708, 630, 406, 7962, 476, 87, 804, 11923, 281, 31075, 1952, 21766, 6006, 420, 15105, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12530731118243674, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393511540260032e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 148410, "start": 1493.3999999999999, "end": 1494.78, "text": " They weren't trying to copy us.", "tokens": [50830, 814, 4999, 380, 1382, 281, 5055, 505, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12530731118243674, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393511540260032e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 148410, "start": 1494.9399999999998, "end": 1495.1999999999998, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50907, 883, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12530731118243674, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393511540260032e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 148410, "start": 1495.3999999999999, "end": 1500.6799999999998, "text": " They independently arrived at it because it solves a universal structural constraint of reality.", "tokens": [50930, 814, 21761, 6678, 412, 309, 570, 309, 39890, 257, 11455, 15067, 25534, 295, 4103, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12530731118243674, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393511540260032e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 148410, "start": 1500.82, "end": 1501.3999999999999, "text": " Which is...", "tokens": [51201, 3013, 307, 485, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12530731118243674, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393511540260032e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 148410, "start": 1501.3999999999999, "end": 1508.58, "text": " How do you allow one part of a highly complex system to interact with another part without losing track of what belongs to whom?", "tokens": [51230, 1012, 360, 291, 2089, 472, 644, 295, 257, 5405, 3997, 1185, 281, 4648, 365, 1071, 644, 1553, 7027, 2837, 295, 437, 12953, 281, 7101, 30, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12530731118243674, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393511540260032e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 150858, "start": 1508.58, "end": 1512.54, "text": " If you don't contain the variables, the complexity spirals to infinity.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 500, 380, 5304, 264, 9102, 11, 264, 14024, 10733, 1124, 281, 13202, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 150858, "start": 1513.02, "end": 1514.28, "text": " Everything touches everything else.", "tokens": [50587, 5471, 17431, 1203, 1646, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 150858, "start": 1514.5, "end": 1516.1999999999998, "text": " I was thinking about this in terms of web browsers.", "tokens": [50661, 286, 390, 1953, 466, 341, 294, 2115, 295, 3670, 36069, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 150858, "start": 1516.6399999999999, "end": 1521.32, "text": " Having 50 browser tabs open is a perfect example of unresolved scope, isn't it?", "tokens": [50768, 10222, 2625, 11185, 20743, 1269, 307, 257, 2176, 1365, 295, 517, 495, 29110, 11923, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 150858, "start": 1521.32, "end": 1522.72, "text": " Oh, it's the ultimate example.", "tokens": [51002, 876, 11, 309, 311, 264, 9705, 1365, 13, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 150858, "start": 1522.8799999999999, "end": 1523.9399999999998, "text": " You start reading an article.", "tokens": [51080, 509, 722, 3760, 364, 7222, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 150858, "start": 1524.5, "end": 1529.04, "text": " You click a link to look up a definition which opens a new tab, and then you click a link in that tab.", "tokens": [51161, 509, 2052, 257, 2113, 281, 574, 493, 257, 7123, 597, 9870, 257, 777, 4421, 11, 293, 550, 291, 2052, 257, 2113, 294, 300, 4421, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 150858, "start": 1529.08, "end": 1529.84, "text": " Down the rabbit hole.", "tokens": [51390, 9506, 264, 19509, 5458, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181072575705391, "compression_ratio": 1.628352490421456, "no_speech_prob": 1.5725284572762344e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 152984, "start": 1529.84, "end": 1534.36, "text": " You have 50 tabs open because you keep dropping into deeper and deeper inner scopes.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 2625, 20743, 1269, 570, 291, 1066, 13601, 666, 7731, 293, 7731, 7284, 795, 30545, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13497509146636388, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 152984, "start": 1534.6, "end": 1539.48, "text": " And you refuse to close them because your brain thinks, I still need to resolve that thread eventually.", "tokens": [50603, 400, 291, 16791, 281, 1998, 552, 570, 428, 3567, 7309, 11, 286, 920, 643, 281, 14151, 300, 7207, 4728, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13497509146636388, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 152984, "start": 1540.02, "end": 1542.86, "text": " It is exhausting just looking at a browser with 50 tabs.", "tokens": [50874, 467, 307, 34076, 445, 1237, 412, 257, 11185, 365, 2625, 20743, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13497509146636388, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 152984, "start": 1543.0, "end": 1543.76, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51023, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13497509146636388, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 152984, "start": 1543.76, "end": 1554.5, "text": " It is exhausting because your brain intuitively understands that each tab represents an unclosed cognitive loop, an unresolved dependency.", "tokens": [51061, 467, 307, 34076, 570, 428, 3567, 46506, 15146, 300, 1184, 4421, 8855, 364, 517, 3474, 1744, 15605, 6367, 11, 364, 517, 495, 29110, 33621, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13497509146636388, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 152984, "start": 1554.8, "end": 1559.28, "text": " Which serves as the perfect transition to the next domain Flexion explores.", "tokens": [51613, 3013, 13451, 382, 264, 2176, 6034, 281, 264, 958, 9274, 29208, 313, 45473, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13497509146636388, "compression_ratio": 1.7426470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 155928, "start": 1559.28, "end": 1561.16, "text": " This is where it gets slightly sinister.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 689, 309, 2170, 4748, 45727, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 155928, "start": 1561.6399999999999, "end": 1562.1399999999999, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50483, 467, 775, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 155928, "start": 1562.78, "end": 1567.22, "text": " We've seen how computers use nested scope to organize logic and keep systems stable.", "tokens": [50540, 492, 600, 1612, 577, 10807, 764, 15646, 292, 11923, 281, 13859, 9952, 293, 1066, 3652, 8351, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 155928, "start": 1567.3999999999999, "end": 1571.58, "text": " But what happens when you deliberately use nested scope to destabilize a system?", "tokens": [50771, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 291, 23506, 764, 15646, 292, 11923, 281, 2677, 5177, 1125, 257, 1185, 30, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 155928, "start": 1571.78, "end": 1571.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50990, 1779, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 155928, "start": 1572.08, "end": 1575.18, "text": " What happens when you use it to intentionally overwhelm a human brain?", "tokens": [51005, 708, 2314, 562, 291, 764, 309, 281, 22062, 9103, 76, 257, 1952, 3567, 30, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 155928, "start": 1575.5, "end": 1581.6399999999999, "text": " This brings us to the world of storytelling, and specifically a highly manipulative application of it, conversational hypnosis.", "tokens": [51176, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 1002, 295, 21479, 11, 293, 4682, 257, 5405, 9258, 22678, 3861, 295, 309, 11, 2615, 1478, 7420, 46080, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 155928, "start": 1581.94, "end": 1582.22, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51498, 1079, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 155928, "start": 1582.3999999999999, "end": 1586.08, "text": " The paper points to the techniques of a hypnotist named Igor Litachowski.", "tokens": [51521, 440, 3035, 2793, 281, 264, 7512, 295, 257, 42944, 468, 4926, 40356, 41841, 608, 21866, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1452414349811833, "compression_ratio": 1.6611295681063123, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044018528286855e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 158608, "start": 1586.08, "end": 1590.24, "text": " How does he use story structure to put someone into a trance?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 775, 415, 764, 1657, 3877, 281, 829, 1580, 666, 257, 504, 719, 30, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 158608, "start": 1590.52, "end": 1592.78, "text": " So Litachowski doesn't use swinging pocket watches.", "tokens": [50587, 407, 41841, 608, 21866, 1177, 380, 764, 29500, 8963, 17062, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 158608, "start": 1592.96, "end": 1593.08, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50709, 1779, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 158608, "start": 1593.1399999999999, "end": 1593.8, "text": " No cliches.", "tokens": [50718, 883, 39190, 279, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 158608, "start": 1594.08, "end": 1595.84, "text": " He uses working memory overload.", "tokens": [50765, 634, 4960, 1364, 4675, 28777, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 158608, "start": 1596.9399999999998, "end": 1602.1999999999998, "text": " His technique involves building hypnotic inductions entirely out of interrupted narratives.", "tokens": [50908, 2812, 6532, 11626, 2390, 42944, 299, 13716, 3916, 7696, 484, 295, 30329, 28016, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 158608, "start": 1602.3999999999999, "end": 1603.28, "text": " Interrupted narratives?", "tokens": [51181, 5751, 5428, 292, 28016, 30, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 158608, "start": 1603.54, "end": 1604.02, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [51238, 1743, 437, 30, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 158608, "start": 1604.5, "end": 1607.32, "text": " He will sit across from you and start telling you a compelling story.", "tokens": [51286, 634, 486, 1394, 2108, 490, 291, 293, 722, 3585, 291, 257, 20050, 1657, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 158608, "start": 1607.4399999999998, "end": 1609.5, "text": " Say, a story about a train ride he took.", "tokens": [51433, 6463, 11, 257, 1657, 466, 257, 3847, 5077, 415, 1890, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 158608, "start": 1609.9399999999998, "end": 1611.34, "text": " You engage with the story.", "tokens": [51558, 509, 4683, 365, 264, 1657, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 158608, "start": 1611.8, "end": 1613.6799999999998, "text": " Your brain maps the outer scope.", "tokens": [51651, 2260, 3567, 11317, 264, 10847, 11923, 13, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557015085608008, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234785868082802e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 161368, "start": 1613.68, "end": 1615.54, "text": " Okay, I'm following the train story.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 3480, 264, 3847, 1657, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1312751104665357, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638467601712e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 161368, "start": 1615.6200000000001, "end": 1620.64, "text": " But right as the story approaches its climax, before he provides a resolution, he digresses.", "tokens": [50462, 583, 558, 382, 264, 1657, 11587, 1080, 41329, 11, 949, 415, 6417, 257, 8669, 11, 415, 2528, 40352, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1312751104665357, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638467601712e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 161368, "start": 1621.28, "end": 1627.28, "text": " He smoothly transitions into a second, completely different story about a conversation he had with a stranger.", "tokens": [50745, 634, 19565, 23767, 666, 257, 1150, 11, 2584, 819, 1657, 466, 257, 3761, 415, 632, 365, 257, 18834, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1312751104665357, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638467601712e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 161368, "start": 1627.52, "end": 1630.28, "text": " He opens an inner scope before closing the outer one.", "tokens": [51057, 634, 9870, 364, 7284, 11923, 949, 10377, 264, 10847, 472, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1312751104665357, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638467601712e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 161368, "start": 1630.3600000000001, "end": 1633.2, "text": " So now my brain is holding two unresolved threads.", "tokens": [51199, 407, 586, 452, 3567, 307, 5061, 732, 517, 495, 29110, 19314, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1312751104665357, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638467601712e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 161368, "start": 1633.3, "end": 1633.66, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51346, 7587, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1312751104665357, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638467601712e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 163366, "start": 1633.66, "end": 1637.94, "text": " And before the second story finishes, he pauses and starts a third story.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 949, 264, 1150, 1657, 23615, 11, 415, 2502, 8355, 293, 3719, 257, 2636, 1657, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13383545914316566, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 163366, "start": 1638.26, "end": 1638.66, "text": " Oh, man.", "tokens": [50595, 876, 11, 587, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13383545914316566, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 163366, "start": 1639.3600000000001, "end": 1642.7, "text": " He is deliberately stacking unresolved scopes in your working memory.", "tokens": [50650, 634, 307, 23506, 41376, 517, 495, 29110, 795, 30545, 294, 428, 1364, 4675, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13383545914316566, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 163366, "start": 1643.16, "end": 1648.1000000000001, "text": " Your conscious mind is desperately trying to keep track of the train ride, the stranger, and the third narrative.", "tokens": [50840, 2260, 6648, 1575, 307, 23726, 1382, 281, 1066, 2837, 295, 264, 3847, 5077, 11, 264, 18834, 11, 293, 264, 2636, 9977, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13383545914316566, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 163366, "start": 1648.42, "end": 1650.98, "text": " Wait, you used the phrase stacking unresolved scopes.", "tokens": [51103, 3802, 11, 291, 1143, 264, 9535, 41376, 517, 495, 29110, 795, 30545, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13383545914316566, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 163366, "start": 1651.1000000000001, "end": 1653.44, "text": " How does a stack actually work in this context?", "tokens": [51237, 1012, 775, 257, 8630, 767, 589, 294, 341, 4319, 30, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13383545914316566, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 163366, "start": 1653.8600000000001, "end": 1661.0400000000002, "text": " In computer science and mathematics, a stack is a specific type of data structure that operates on a last-in, first-out principle.", "tokens": [51375, 682, 3820, 3497, 293, 18666, 11, 257, 8630, 307, 257, 2685, 2010, 295, 1412, 3877, 300, 22577, 322, 257, 1036, 12, 259, 11, 700, 12, 346, 8665, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13383545914316566, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 166104, "start": 1661.84, "end": 1663.12, "text": " Or, leaf-o.", "tokens": [50405, 1610, 11, 10871, 12, 78, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 166104, "start": 1663.26, "end": 1664.34, "text": " Last-in, first-out.", "tokens": [50476, 5264, 12, 259, 11, 700, 12, 346, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 166104, "start": 1664.5, "end": 1666.34, "text": " Think of a stack of cafeteria trays.", "tokens": [50538, 6557, 295, 257, 8630, 295, 42230, 47496, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 166104, "start": 1666.7, "end": 1667.48, "text": " You put a tray down.", "tokens": [50648, 509, 829, 257, 16027, 760, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 166104, "start": 1667.6399999999999, "end": 1668.3999999999999, "text": " That's the first story.", "tokens": [50695, 663, 311, 264, 700, 1657, 13, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 166104, "start": 1668.74, "end": 1670.8, "text": " You put another tray on top of it, the second story.", "tokens": [50750, 509, 829, 1071, 16027, 322, 1192, 295, 309, 11, 264, 1150, 1657, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 166104, "start": 1671.0, "end": 1672.5, "text": " You put a third tray on top.", "tokens": [50863, 509, 829, 257, 2636, 16027, 322, 1192, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 166104, "start": 1672.58, "end": 1673.6599999999999, "text": " Okay, I see the stack.", "tokens": [50942, 1033, 11, 286, 536, 264, 8630, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 166104, "start": 1673.92, "end": 1676.72, "text": " When it's time to remove a tray, you can't grab the bottom one first.", "tokens": [51009, 1133, 309, 311, 565, 281, 4159, 257, 16027, 11, 291, 393, 380, 4444, 264, 2767, 472, 700, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 166104, "start": 1676.74, "end": 1678.18, "text": " Yeah, the whole thing would fall over.", "tokens": [51150, 865, 11, 264, 1379, 551, 576, 2100, 670, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 166104, "start": 1678.28, "end": 1678.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51227, 1779, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 166104, "start": 1678.74, "end": 1680.3, "text": " You have to remove the last one you added.", "tokens": [51250, 509, 362, 281, 4159, 264, 1036, 472, 291, 3869, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 166104, "start": 1680.54, "end": 1683.06, "text": " The innermost story must be resolved first.", "tokens": [51340, 440, 7714, 966, 555, 1657, 1633, 312, 20772, 700, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 166104, "start": 1683.7, "end": 1688.28, "text": " So, to safely close out the hypnotic induction, he has to finish story number three.", "tokens": [51498, 407, 11, 281, 11750, 1998, 484, 264, 42944, 299, 33371, 11, 415, 575, 281, 2413, 1657, 1230, 1045, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 166104, "start": 1688.58, "end": 1690.34, "text": " Which brings you back to story number two.", "tokens": [51742, 3013, 5607, 291, 646, 281, 1657, 1230, 732, 13, 51830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1746721435011479, "compression_ratio": 1.8, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045690167179605e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 169034, "start": 1690.34, "end": 1691.1999999999998, "text": " Finish that one.", "tokens": [50365, 31583, 300, 472, 13, 50408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 169034, "start": 1691.3999999999999, "end": 1693.56, "text": " And finally delivered the punchline of the train ride.", "tokens": [50418, 400, 2721, 10144, 264, 8135, 1889, 295, 264, 3847, 5077, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 169034, "start": 1693.6799999999998, "end": 1694.06, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50532, 1079, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 169034, "start": 1694.78, "end": 1704.6999999999998, "text": " Appendix A of Fliction's paper describes this mathematically as a stack functor, a formal, perfectly balanced sequence of opening and closing brackets.", "tokens": [50587, 3132, 521, 970, 316, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 3035, 15626, 341, 44003, 382, 257, 8630, 1019, 1672, 11, 257, 9860, 11, 6239, 13902, 8310, 295, 5193, 293, 10377, 26179, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 169034, "start": 1704.8799999999999, "end": 1709.84, "text": " But the brilliance of Lidachowski's technique is that the actual content of the stories barely matters.", "tokens": [51092, 583, 264, 8695, 6276, 295, 441, 327, 608, 21866, 311, 6532, 307, 300, 264, 3539, 2701, 295, 264, 3676, 10268, 7001, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 169034, "start": 1710.0, "end": 1711.0, "text": " It's just filler.", "tokens": [51348, 467, 311, 445, 34676, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 169034, "start": 1711.4599999999998, "end": 1713.8999999999999, "text": " The purpose of the stories is purely mechanical.", "tokens": [51421, 440, 4334, 295, 264, 3676, 307, 17491, 12070, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 169034, "start": 1714.52, "end": 1717.6, "text": " The nesting itself absorbs your conscious attention.", "tokens": [51574, 440, 297, 8714, 2564, 40745, 428, 6648, 3202, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1767196308482777, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.1557372897250118e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 171760, "start": 1717.6, "end": 1730.86, "text": " The critical analytical part of your mind, the part that might normally resist hypnotic suggestion, is too busy doing the heavy lifting of holding all those cognitive doors open to notice the suggestions he is slipping in.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4924, 29579, 644, 295, 428, 1575, 11, 264, 644, 300, 1062, 5646, 4597, 42944, 299, 16541, 11, 307, 886, 5856, 884, 264, 4676, 15798, 295, 5061, 439, 729, 15605, 8077, 1269, 281, 3449, 264, 13396, 415, 307, 36779, 294, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07241144710116916, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938735148738557e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 173086, "start": 1730.86, "end": 1736.78, "text": " The critical mind gets so distracted holding the doors open for all these stories that it forgets to guard the house.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4924, 1575, 2170, 370, 21658, 5061, 264, 8077, 1269, 337, 439, 613, 3676, 300, 309, 2870, 82, 281, 6290, 264, 1782, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525391448627818, "compression_ratio": 1.59915611814346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671680533152488e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 173086, "start": 1737.26, "end": 1738.52, "text": " That's a brilliant way to phrase it.", "tokens": [50685, 663, 311, 257, 10248, 636, 281, 9535, 309, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525391448627818, "compression_ratio": 1.59915611814346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671680533152488e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 173086, "start": 1738.6399999999999, "end": 1742.12, "text": " It is quite literally a buffer overflow attack on the human brain.", "tokens": [50754, 467, 307, 1596, 3736, 257, 21762, 37772, 2690, 322, 264, 1952, 3567, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525391448627818, "compression_ratio": 1.59915611814346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671680533152488e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 173086, "start": 1742.56, "end": 1748.76, "text": " You feed the system more open loops than its active memory can handle, and the security protocols just crash.", "tokens": [50950, 509, 3154, 264, 1185, 544, 1269, 16121, 813, 1080, 4967, 4675, 393, 4813, 11, 293, 264, 3825, 20618, 445, 8252, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525391448627818, "compression_ratio": 1.59915611814346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671680533152488e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 173086, "start": 1749.24, "end": 1751.6599999999999, "text": " That is an incredibly accurate way to model it.", "tokens": [51284, 663, 307, 364, 6252, 8559, 636, 281, 2316, 309, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525391448627818, "compression_ratio": 1.59915611814346, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671680533152488e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 175166, "start": 1751.66, "end": 1757.02, "text": " It proves that nested scope is not just an accidental byproduct of real-time speech.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25019, 300, 15646, 292, 11923, 307, 406, 445, 364, 38094, 538, 33244, 295, 957, 12, 3766, 6218, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 175166, "start": 1757.26, "end": 1757.88, "text": " It's a vulnerability.", "tokens": [50645, 467, 311, 257, 24210, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 175166, "start": 1758.38, "end": 1765.18, "text": " It is a fundamental structural vulnerability in human cognition that can be weaponized to bypass critical thought.", "tokens": [50701, 467, 307, 257, 8088, 15067, 24210, 294, 1952, 46905, 300, 393, 312, 7463, 1602, 281, 24996, 4924, 1194, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 175166, "start": 1765.22, "end": 1766.02, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [51043, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 175166, "start": 1766.3000000000002, "end": 1768.9, "text": " But it can also be used to captivate us in beautiful ways, right?", "tokens": [51097, 583, 309, 393, 611, 312, 1143, 281, 40769, 473, 505, 294, 2238, 2098, 11, 558, 30, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 175166, "start": 1768.9, "end": 1769.48, "text": " Oh, totally.", "tokens": [51227, 876, 11, 3879, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 175166, "start": 1769.68, "end": 1773.18, "text": " The ancient collection of tales, the Arabian Nights, relies on this.", "tokens": [51266, 440, 7832, 5765, 295, 27254, 11, 264, 8625, 952, 426, 5761, 11, 30910, 322, 341, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 175166, "start": 1773.2, "end": 1773.48, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51442, 1779, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 175166, "start": 1773.72, "end": 1774.28, "text": " Sheherzad.", "tokens": [51468, 1240, 511, 89, 345, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 175166, "start": 1774.44, "end": 1774.74, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51504, 1079, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1629309570580198, "compression_ratio": 1.5615384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 2.5436634135816982e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 177474, "start": 1774.74, "end": 1781.5, "text": " She survives by telling a story within a story within a story, keeping the king's attention suspended indefinitely.", "tokens": [50365, 1240, 46231, 538, 3585, 257, 1657, 1951, 257, 1657, 1951, 257, 1657, 11, 5145, 264, 4867, 311, 3202, 23437, 24162, 10925, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13507058885362414, "compression_ratio": 1.79182156133829, "no_speech_prob": 1.3725919272705722e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 177474, "start": 1781.96, "end": 1783.52, "text": " Christopher Nolan does this in film.", "tokens": [50726, 20649, 43707, 775, 341, 294, 2007, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13507058885362414, "compression_ratio": 1.79182156133829, "no_speech_prob": 1.3725919272705722e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 177474, "start": 1784.3, "end": 1788.6, "text": " Inception is a literal visual representation of a stack functor.", "tokens": [50843, 682, 7311, 307, 257, 20411, 5056, 10290, 295, 257, 8630, 1019, 1672, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13507058885362414, "compression_ratio": 1.79182156133829, "no_speech_prob": 1.3725919272705722e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 177474, "start": 1788.9, "end": 1791.1, "text": " A dream within a dream within a dream.", "tokens": [51073, 316, 3055, 1951, 257, 3055, 1951, 257, 3055, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13507058885362414, "compression_ratio": 1.79182156133829, "no_speech_prob": 1.3725919272705722e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 177474, "start": 1791.36, "end": 1793.32, "text": " The tension of the movie isn't just the action.", "tokens": [51196, 440, 8980, 295, 264, 3169, 1943, 380, 445, 264, 3069, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13507058885362414, "compression_ratio": 1.79182156133829, "no_speech_prob": 1.3725919272705722e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 177474, "start": 1793.32, "end": 1801.48, "text": " It's the cognitive weight of knowing they have to successfully exit the innermost dream to wake up in the middle dream, to wake up in the outer dream.", "tokens": [51294, 467, 311, 264, 15605, 3364, 295, 5276, 436, 362, 281, 10727, 11043, 264, 7714, 966, 555, 3055, 281, 6634, 493, 294, 264, 2808, 3055, 11, 281, 6634, 493, 294, 264, 10847, 3055, 13, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13507058885362414, "compression_ratio": 1.79182156133829, "no_speech_prob": 1.3725919272705722e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 177474, "start": 1801.58, "end": 1802.72, "text": " It's that stack structure.", "tokens": [51707, 467, 311, 300, 8630, 3877, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13507058885362414, "compression_ratio": 1.79182156133829, "no_speech_prob": 1.3725919272705722e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 180272, "start": 1802.72, "end": 1810.2, "text": " We love the feeling of holding those threads and feeling the immense relief when they finally tie up cleanly at the end.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 959, 264, 2633, 295, 5061, 729, 19314, 293, 2633, 264, 22920, 10915, 562, 436, 2721, 7582, 493, 2541, 356, 412, 264, 917, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 180272, "start": 1810.52, "end": 1816.98, "text": " That feeling of tension and release is paramount, and it leads to a profound question Flixiam poses.", "tokens": [50755, 663, 2633, 295, 8980, 293, 4374, 307, 6220, 792, 11, 293, 309, 6689, 281, 257, 14382, 1168, 3235, 970, 2918, 26059, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 180272, "start": 1817.44, "end": 1818.2, "text": " What's the question?", "tokens": [51101, 708, 311, 264, 1168, 30, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 180272, "start": 1818.42, "end": 1820.32, "text": " What if we remove words entirely?", "tokens": [51150, 708, 498, 321, 4159, 2283, 7696, 30, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 180272, "start": 1821.24, "end": 1823.88, "text": " What if we remove logic, narrative, and code?", "tokens": [51291, 708, 498, 321, 4159, 9952, 11, 9977, 11, 293, 3089, 30, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 180272, "start": 1824.7, "end": 1829.68, "text": " Can we still feel the physical tension of an open scope without any semantic meaning attached to it?", "tokens": [51464, 1664, 321, 920, 841, 264, 4001, 8980, 295, 364, 1269, 11923, 1553, 604, 47982, 3620, 8570, 281, 309, 30, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 180272, "start": 1829.72, "end": 1830.98, "text": " Which brings us to music.", "tokens": [51715, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 1318, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 180272, "start": 1831.2, "end": 1832.44, "text": " The most visceral example.", "tokens": [51789, 440, 881, 1452, 47879, 1365, 13, 51851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436613212197514, "compression_ratio": 1.7246376811594204, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747481223003402e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 183244, "start": 1832.44, "end": 1837.72, "text": " Music is the ultimate proof that our bodies understand scope even when language isn't involved at all.", "tokens": [50365, 7609, 307, 264, 9705, 8177, 300, 527, 7510, 1223, 11923, 754, 562, 2856, 1943, 380, 3288, 412, 439, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15115648786598276, "compression_ratio": 1.6162361623616237, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161598326303815e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 183244, "start": 1838.0800000000002, "end": 1840.4, "text": " The paper uses sonata form to illustrate this.", "tokens": [50647, 440, 3035, 4960, 1872, 3274, 1254, 281, 23221, 341, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15115648786598276, "compression_ratio": 1.6162361623616237, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161598326303815e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 183244, "start": 1840.92, "end": 1843.04, "text": " Break down the mechanics of sonata form for me.", "tokens": [50789, 16925, 760, 264, 12939, 295, 1872, 3274, 1254, 337, 385, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15115648786598276, "compression_ratio": 1.6162361623616237, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161598326303815e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 183244, "start": 1843.24, "end": 1845.3400000000001, "text": " I know the term, but I don't know how it maps to parentheses.", "tokens": [50905, 286, 458, 264, 1433, 11, 457, 286, 500, 380, 458, 577, 309, 11317, 281, 34153, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15115648786598276, "compression_ratio": 1.6162361623616237, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161598326303815e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 183244, "start": 1846.04, "end": 1852.68, "text": " Sonata form has been the dominant architectural structure of Western classical music since the days of Haydn and Mozart.", "tokens": [51045, 5185, 3274, 1254, 575, 668, 264, 15657, 26621, 3877, 295, 8724, 13735, 1318, 1670, 264, 1708, 295, 8721, 67, 77, 293, 42653, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15115648786598276, "compression_ratio": 1.6162361623616237, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161598326303815e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 183244, "start": 1853.46, "end": 1855.1000000000001, "text": " It consists of three main sections.", "tokens": [51416, 467, 14689, 295, 1045, 2135, 10863, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15115648786598276, "compression_ratio": 1.6162361623616237, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161598326303815e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 183244, "start": 1855.22, "end": 1856.02, "text": " Okay, three sections.", "tokens": [51504, 1033, 11, 1045, 10863, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15115648786598276, "compression_ratio": 1.6162361623616237, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161598326303815e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 185602, "start": 1856.02, "end": 1857.18, "text": " First for the exposition.", "tokens": [50365, 2386, 337, 264, 1278, 5830, 13, 50423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17548694610595703, "compression_ratio": 1.1938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 185602, "start": 1857.34, "end": 1862.1, "text": " This is where the composer introduces the main musical theme, usually in a stable home key.", "tokens": [50431, 639, 307, 689, 264, 26003, 31472, 264, 2135, 9165, 6314, 11, 2673, 294, 257, 8351, 1280, 2141, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17548694610595703, "compression_ratio": 1.1938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 186210, "start": 1862.1, "end": 1864.8799999999999, "text": " So this opens the massive outer scope.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 341, 9870, 264, 5994, 10847, 11923, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3001285990079244, "compression_ratio": 1.0512820512820513, "no_speech_prob": 1.701394342253082e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 186210, "start": 1865.02, "end": 1865.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50511, 7587, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3001285990079244, "compression_ratio": 1.0512820512820513, "no_speech_prob": 1.701394342253082e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 186210, "start": 1865.9599999999998, "end": 1867.3799999999999, "text": " Second is the development section.", "tokens": [50558, 5736, 307, 264, 3250, 3541, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3001285990079244, "compression_ratio": 1.0512820512820513, "no_speech_prob": 1.701394342253082e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 186738, "start": 1867.38, "end": 1870.68, "text": " Here, the composer shatters the main theme.", "tokens": [50365, 1692, 11, 264, 26003, 402, 37690, 264, 2135, 6314, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24518648215702601, "compression_ratio": 1.0945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.94322184211837e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 186738, "start": 1870.7600000000002, "end": 1871.72, "text": " Shatters it how?", "tokens": [50534, 1160, 37690, 309, 577, 30, 50582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24518648215702601, "compression_ratio": 1.0945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.94322184211837e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 186738, "start": 1871.8400000000001, "end": 1872.94, "text": " They change the key.", "tokens": [50588, 814, 1319, 264, 2141, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24518648215702601, "compression_ratio": 1.0945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.94322184211837e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 187294, "start": 1872.94, "end": 1874.3200000000002, "text": " They fragment the melody.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 26424, 264, 17997, 13, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.33660914103190104, "compression_ratio": 1.1717171717171717, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 187294, "start": 1874.3200000000002, "end": 1875.64, "text": " They introduce dissonance.", "tokens": [50434, 814, 5366, 717, 3015, 719, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.33660914103190104, "compression_ratio": 1.1717171717171717, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 187294, "start": 1875.76, "end": 1880.54, "text": " And they wander into entirely new, unstable harmonic territory.", "tokens": [50506, 400, 436, 27541, 666, 7696, 777, 11, 23742, 32270, 11360, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.33660914103190104, "compression_ratio": 1.1717171717171717, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484516659684423e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 188054, "start": 1880.54, "end": 1883.5, "text": " The development section is the musical digression.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3250, 3541, 307, 264, 9165, 2528, 2775, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654456839504012, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522555009561128e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 188054, "start": 1883.7, "end": 1885.84, "text": " It's the inner scope where things get chaotic.", "tokens": [50523, 467, 311, 264, 7284, 11923, 689, 721, 483, 27013, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654456839504012, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522555009561128e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 188054, "start": 1885.98, "end": 1887.06, "text": " It's chaos by design.", "tokens": [50637, 467, 311, 14158, 538, 1715, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654456839504012, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522555009561128e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 188054, "start": 1887.36, "end": 1889.48, "text": " But it only works because of what comes next, right?", "tokens": [50706, 583, 309, 787, 1985, 570, 295, 437, 1487, 958, 11, 558, 30, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654456839504012, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522555009561128e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 188054, "start": 1889.48, "end": 1889.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50812, 1779, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654456839504012, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522555009561128e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 188054, "start": 1890.18, "end": 1898.58, "text": " It is permitted to wander so far off course precisely because the rigid structure of sonata form guarantees a recapitulation.", "tokens": [50847, 467, 307, 28658, 281, 27541, 370, 1400, 766, 1164, 13402, 570, 264, 22195, 3877, 295, 1872, 3274, 1254, 32567, 257, 20928, 270, 2776, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654456839504012, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522555009561128e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 188054, "start": 1898.74, "end": 1899.68, "text": " The third section.", "tokens": [51275, 440, 2636, 3541, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1654456839504012, "compression_ratio": 1.528301886792453, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522555009561128e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 189968, "start": 1899.68, "end": 1902.8, "text": " The recapitulation is where the original theme returns in the home key.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 20928, 270, 2776, 307, 689, 264, 3380, 6314, 11247, 294, 264, 1280, 2141, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09797522939484694, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832594125313794e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 189968, "start": 1903.3600000000001, "end": 1909.3600000000001, "text": " The form itself acts as a contract with the listener's brain, guaranteeing a way back from the chaos to the main threat.", "tokens": [50549, 440, 1254, 2564, 10672, 382, 257, 4364, 365, 264, 31569, 311, 3567, 11, 10815, 278, 257, 636, 646, 490, 264, 14158, 281, 264, 2135, 4734, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09797522939484694, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832594125313794e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 189968, "start": 1909.68, "end": 1915.3, "text": " You can tolerate the immense complexity of the inner scope because you trust the outer scope will close.", "tokens": [50865, 509, 393, 25773, 264, 22920, 14024, 295, 264, 7284, 11923, 570, 291, 3361, 264, 10847, 11923, 486, 1998, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09797522939484694, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832594125313794e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 189968, "start": 1915.52, "end": 1917.0, "text": " You feel it intuitively.", "tokens": [51157, 509, 841, 309, 46506, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09797522939484694, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832594125313794e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 189968, "start": 1917.4, "end": 1925.94, "text": " We feel this on a massive architectural level over a 15-minute symphony, but we also feel it on a micro level, like millisecond by millisecond.", "tokens": [51251, 492, 841, 341, 322, 257, 5994, 26621, 1496, 670, 257, 2119, 12, 18256, 6697, 28616, 11, 457, 321, 611, 841, 309, 322, 257, 4532, 1496, 11, 411, 27940, 18882, 538, 27940, 18882, 13, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09797522939484694, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832594125313794e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 189968, "start": 1926.02, "end": 1926.54, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51682, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09797522939484694, "compression_ratio": 1.6620689655172414, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832594125313794e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 192654, "start": 1926.54, "end": 1929.8999999999999, "text": " The paper talks about the concept of a suspension in music.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 6686, 466, 264, 3410, 295, 257, 15771, 294, 1318, 13, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 192654, "start": 1930.42, "end": 1932.56, "text": " What physically happens during a suspension?", "tokens": [50559, 708, 9762, 2314, 1830, 257, 15771, 30, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 192654, "start": 1933.08, "end": 1940.8, "text": " A suspension occurs when a composer holds one note from a previous chord over into a new chord where it doesn't harmonically belong.", "tokens": [50692, 316, 15771, 11843, 562, 257, 26003, 9190, 472, 3637, 490, 257, 3894, 14137, 670, 666, 257, 777, 14137, 689, 309, 1177, 380, 14750, 984, 5784, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 192654, "start": 1940.8999999999999, "end": 1942.32, "text": " Like it overstays its welcome.", "tokens": [51083, 1743, 309, 48834, 3772, 1080, 2928, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 192654, "start": 1942.56, "end": 1942.92, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51166, 7587, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 192654, "start": 1943.7, "end": 1949.54, "text": " Let's say the orchestra moves to a clean, stable C major chord, but the violins refuse to move.", "tokens": [51223, 961, 311, 584, 264, 25280, 6067, 281, 257, 2541, 11, 8351, 383, 2563, 14137, 11, 457, 264, 3448, 1292, 16791, 281, 1286, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 192654, "start": 1949.92, "end": 1952.44, "text": " They hold on to an F from the previous measure.", "tokens": [51534, 814, 1797, 322, 281, 364, 479, 490, 264, 3894, 3481, 13, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 192654, "start": 1952.72, "end": 1953.18, "text": " Ouch!", "tokens": [51674, 27217, 0, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13830555809868705, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591337658749543e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 195318, "start": 1953.18, "end": 1958.42, "text": " Right, the F rubs against the E in the C major chord, creating acoustic dissonance.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 264, 479, 367, 5432, 1970, 264, 462, 294, 264, 383, 2563, 14137, 11, 4084, 26753, 717, 3015, 719, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12658771224643872, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349480142467288e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 195318, "start": 1958.64, "end": 1961.38, "text": " Why does that rubbing sound create tension in the body?", "tokens": [50638, 1545, 775, 300, 29770, 1626, 1884, 8980, 294, 264, 1772, 30, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12658771224643872, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349480142467288e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 195318, "start": 1961.5, "end": 1962.7, "text": " What is the physics of that?", "tokens": [50781, 708, 307, 264, 10649, 295, 300, 30, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12658771224643872, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349480142467288e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 195318, "start": 1962.96, "end": 1964.78, "text": " It comes down to the physics of sound waves.", "tokens": [50854, 467, 1487, 760, 281, 264, 10649, 295, 1626, 9417, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12658771224643872, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349480142467288e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 195318, "start": 1965.44, "end": 1969.74, "text": " Dissonant intervals create complex, overlapping wave frequencies that clash,", "tokens": [50978, 413, 30472, 394, 26651, 1884, 3997, 11, 33535, 5772, 20250, 300, 36508, 11, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12658771224643872, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349480142467288e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 195318, "start": 1970.26, "end": 1974.8, "text": " literally causing the tiny hair cells in your inner ear to fire in conflicting patterns.", "tokens": [51219, 3736, 9853, 264, 5870, 2578, 5438, 294, 428, 7284, 1273, 281, 2610, 294, 43784, 8294, 13, 51446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12658771224643872, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349480142467288e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 197480, "start": 1974.8, "end": 1976.98, "text": " So your ear is physically confused.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 428, 1273, 307, 9762, 9019, 13, 50474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16963704427083334, "compression_ratio": 1.507462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251264877738646e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 197480, "start": 1976.98, "end": 1981.3999999999999, "text": " Your brain interprets this irregular firing as instability or tension.", "tokens": [50474, 2260, 3567, 17489, 1373, 341, 29349, 16045, 382, 34379, 420, 8980, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16963704427083334, "compression_ratio": 1.507462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251264877738646e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 197480, "start": 1982.8799999999999, "end": 1989.98, "text": " By holding that diffident note, the composer is opening a tiny, painful scope and artificially delaying the closure.", "tokens": [50769, 3146, 5061, 300, 7593, 1078, 3637, 11, 264, 26003, 307, 5193, 257, 5870, 11, 11697, 11923, 293, 39905, 2270, 8577, 278, 264, 24653, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16963704427083334, "compression_ratio": 1.507462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251264877738646e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 197480, "start": 1990.52, "end": 1995.1399999999999, "text": " It is the harmonic equivalent of a sentence pausing right before the punchline.", "tokens": [51151, 467, 307, 264, 32270, 10344, 295, 257, 8174, 2502, 7981, 558, 949, 264, 8135, 1889, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16963704427083334, "compression_ratio": 1.507462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251264877738646e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 199514, "start": 1995.14, "end": 1997.8200000000002, "text": " The listener physically crazed the resolution.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 31569, 9762, 2094, 11312, 264, 8669, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13628588552060333, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522518146687263e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 199514, "start": 1998.0, "end": 1998.98, "text": " You feel it in your chest.", "tokens": [50508, 509, 841, 309, 294, 428, 7443, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13628588552060333, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522518146687263e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 199514, "start": 1999.4, "end": 2003.16, "text": " You are waiting for the violins to drop down to the E so the chord can stabilize.", "tokens": [50578, 509, 366, 3806, 337, 264, 3448, 1292, 281, 3270, 760, 281, 264, 462, 370, 264, 14137, 393, 31870, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13628588552060333, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522518146687263e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 199514, "start": 2003.6200000000001, "end": 2006.42, "text": " And when they finally do, the physical relief is palpable.", "tokens": [50789, 400, 562, 436, 2721, 360, 11, 264, 4001, 10915, 307, 3984, 30454, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13628588552060333, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522518146687263e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 199514, "start": 2006.96, "end": 2013.3400000000001, "text": " Appendix D, Affliction's paper, connects this to the psychologist David Huron's research on musical expectation.", "tokens": [50956, 3132, 521, 970, 413, 11, 12840, 75, 4105, 311, 3035, 11, 16967, 341, 281, 264, 29514, 4389, 8598, 266, 311, 2132, 322, 9165, 14334, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13628588552060333, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522518146687263e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 199514, "start": 2013.68, "end": 2014.46, "text": " What does Huron say?", "tokens": [51292, 708, 775, 8598, 266, 584, 30, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13628588552060333, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522518146687263e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 201446, "start": 2014.46, "end": 2019.96, "text": " Huron's ITPRA theory, which models imagination, tension, prediction, reaction, and appraisal,", "tokens": [50365, 8598, 266, 311, 6783, 47, 3750, 5261, 11, 597, 5245, 12938, 11, 8980, 11, 17630, 11, 5480, 11, 293, 724, 20769, 304, 11, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 201446, "start": 2020.42, "end": 2025.88, "text": " shows that the interplay between delayed and fulfilled expectations creates genuine physiological responses.", "tokens": [50663, 3110, 300, 264, 728, 2858, 1296, 20268, 293, 21380, 9843, 7829, 16699, 41234, 13019, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 201446, "start": 2026.04, "end": 2026.38, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [50944, 1743, 437, 30, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 201446, "start": 2026.68, "end": 2027.58, "text": " Heart rates change.", "tokens": [50976, 13569, 6846, 1319, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 201446, "start": 2027.76, "end": 2028.76, "text": " Skin conductance alters.", "tokens": [51030, 26333, 6018, 719, 419, 1559, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 201446, "start": 2028.92, "end": 2031.82, "text": " You are literally feeling the unclosed dash in your nervous system.", "tokens": [51088, 509, 366, 3736, 2633, 264, 517, 3474, 1744, 8240, 294, 428, 6296, 1185, 13, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 201446, "start": 2031.9, "end": 2034.66, "text": " And composers love to hack that biological response.", "tokens": [51237, 400, 43872, 959, 281, 10339, 300, 13910, 4134, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 201446, "start": 2034.8, "end": 2036.04, "text": " Look at the deceptive cadence.", "tokens": [51382, 2053, 412, 264, 368, 1336, 488, 46109, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 201446, "start": 2036.24, "end": 2037.76, "text": " Oh, the deceptive cadence is devious.", "tokens": [51454, 876, 11, 264, 368, 1336, 488, 46109, 307, 368, 1502, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 201446, "start": 2038.1200000000001, "end": 2041.6200000000001, "text": " A cadence is supposed to be the period at the end of a musical sentence.", "tokens": [51548, 316, 46109, 307, 3442, 281, 312, 264, 2896, 412, 264, 917, 295, 257, 9165, 8174, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12683435978780266, "compression_ratio": 1.686084142394822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604540209440136e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 204162, "start": 2041.62, "end": 2045.9799999999998, "text": " The music builds up, signaling a completely clean return to the home chord.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1318, 15182, 493, 11, 38639, 257, 2584, 2541, 2736, 281, 264, 1280, 14137, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707511061922127, "compression_ratio": 1.7201492537313432, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426206098443807e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 204162, "start": 2046.2399999999998, "end": 2047.26, "text": " Everything points to home.", "tokens": [50596, 5471, 2793, 281, 1280, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707511061922127, "compression_ratio": 1.7201492537313432, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426206098443807e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 204162, "start": 2047.52, "end": 2050.16, "text": " The dominant chord is screaming that the tonic is coming.", "tokens": [50660, 440, 15657, 14137, 307, 12636, 300, 264, 2952, 299, 307, 1348, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707511061922127, "compression_ratio": 1.7201492537313432, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426206098443807e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 204162, "start": 2050.3399999999997, "end": 2052.3599999999997, "text": " You think the scope is about to close perfectly.", "tokens": [50801, 509, 519, 264, 11923, 307, 466, 281, 1998, 6239, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707511061922127, "compression_ratio": 1.7201492537313432, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426206098443807e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 204162, "start": 2052.8599999999997, "end": 2058.8599999999997, "text": " And then at the very last millisecond, the composer resolves onto a completely unexpected minor chord.", "tokens": [50927, 400, 550, 412, 264, 588, 1036, 27940, 18882, 11, 264, 26003, 7923, 977, 3911, 257, 2584, 13106, 6696, 14137, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707511061922127, "compression_ratio": 1.7201492537313432, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426206098443807e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 204162, "start": 2059.5, "end": 2062.0, "text": " It violently subverts the expectation of closure.", "tokens": [51259, 467, 46728, 1422, 36999, 264, 14334, 295, 24653, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707511061922127, "compression_ratio": 1.7201492537313432, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426206098443807e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 204162, "start": 2062.24, "end": 2068.0, "text": " It is a scope you fully expected to close that suddenly rips open a door into a new room entirely.", "tokens": [51396, 467, 307, 257, 11923, 291, 4498, 5176, 281, 1998, 300, 5800, 367, 2600, 1269, 257, 2853, 666, 257, 777, 1808, 7696, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707511061922127, "compression_ratio": 1.7201492537313432, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426206098443807e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 206800, "start": 2068.0, "end": 2073.08, "text": " But fliction pushes the complexity even further by bringing up fugues.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 932, 4105, 21020, 264, 14024, 754, 3052, 538, 5062, 493, 31838, 1247, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 206800, "start": 2073.76, "end": 2080.14, "text": " A fugue, like those perfected by Bach, completely destroys the idea that scopes have to be sequential.", "tokens": [50653, 316, 31838, 622, 11, 411, 729, 2176, 292, 538, 30920, 11, 2584, 36714, 264, 1558, 300, 795, 30545, 362, 281, 312, 42881, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 206800, "start": 2080.5, "end": 2084.84, "text": " Explain how a fugue works, because in the hypnosis example, the stories were sequential.", "tokens": [50990, 39574, 577, 257, 31838, 622, 1985, 11, 570, 294, 264, 7420, 46080, 1365, 11, 264, 3676, 645, 42881, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 206800, "start": 2085.06, "end": 2087.0, "text": " Last in, first out, one at a time.", "tokens": [51218, 5264, 294, 11, 700, 484, 11, 472, 412, 257, 565, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 206800, "start": 2087.54, "end": 2088.9, "text": " How does a fugue break that rule?", "tokens": [51342, 1012, 775, 257, 31838, 622, 1821, 300, 4978, 30, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 206800, "start": 2089.14, "end": 2091.62, "text": " In a fugue, you have multiple independent musical voices,", "tokens": [51422, 682, 257, 31838, 622, 11, 291, 362, 3866, 6695, 9165, 9802, 11, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 206800, "start": 2091.98, "end": 2095.08, "text": " say a soprano, an alto, a tenor, and a bass line.", "tokens": [51564, 584, 257, 37375, 3730, 11, 364, 21275, 11, 257, 2064, 284, 11, 293, 257, 10136, 1622, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 206800, "start": 2095.4, "end": 2097.7, "text": " And they track independent scopes concurrently.", "tokens": [51735, 400, 436, 2837, 6695, 795, 30545, 37702, 356, 13, 51850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180364030780215, "compression_ratio": 1.667808219178082, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251296319601648e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 209770, "start": 2098.4199999999996, "end": 2098.64, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50401, 865, 13, 50412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 209770, "start": 2099.48, "end": 2101.8399999999997, "text": " The soprano voice introduces the main subject.", "tokens": [50454, 440, 37375, 3730, 3177, 31472, 264, 2135, 3983, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 209770, "start": 2102.48, "end": 2104.9399999999996, "text": " Then, while the soprano continues with new material,", "tokens": [50604, 1396, 11, 1339, 264, 37375, 3730, 6515, 365, 777, 2527, 11, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 209770, "start": 2105.3599999999997, "end": 2108.12, "text": " the alto enters and plays that exact same subject.", "tokens": [50748, 264, 21275, 18780, 293, 5749, 300, 1900, 912, 3983, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 209770, "start": 2108.7, "end": 2109.52, "text": " Then the tenor enters.", "tokens": [50915, 1396, 264, 2064, 284, 18780, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 209770, "start": 2109.72, "end": 2110.64, "text": " So they're all overlapping.", "tokens": [50966, 407, 436, 434, 439, 33535, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 209770, "start": 2110.9399999999996, "end": 2114.2599999999998, "text": " You have multiple threads operating simultaneously, overlapping,", "tokens": [51027, 509, 362, 3866, 19314, 7447, 16561, 11, 33535, 11, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 209770, "start": 2114.54, "end": 2115.7999999999997, "text": " weaving in and out of each other,", "tokens": [51207, 40028, 294, 293, 484, 295, 1184, 661, 11, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 209770, "start": 2116.46, "end": 2118.08, "text": " without waiting for the prior one to finish.", "tokens": [51303, 1553, 3806, 337, 264, 4059, 472, 281, 2413, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 209770, "start": 2118.18, "end": 2119.24, "text": " It's parallel processing.", "tokens": [51389, 467, 311, 8952, 9007, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24088706183679326, "compression_ratio": 1.6391304347826088, "no_speech_prob": 4.1295656130757585e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 211924, "start": 2119.24, "end": 2122.3399999999997, "text": " You have three or four parentheses open at the exact same time,", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 1045, 420, 1451, 34153, 1269, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 565, 11, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 211924, "start": 2122.3399999999997, "end": 2125.3199999999997, "text": " and they aren't nested neatly inside each other.", "tokens": [50520, 293, 436, 3212, 380, 15646, 292, 36634, 1854, 1184, 661, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 211924, "start": 2125.7799999999997, "end": 2128.16, "text": " They are overlapping like a Venn diagram.", "tokens": [50692, 814, 366, 33535, 411, 257, 691, 1857, 10686, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 211924, "start": 2128.4199999999996, "end": 2131.62, "text": " And somehow the human brain can listen to a Bach for a fugue", "tokens": [50824, 400, 6063, 264, 1952, 3567, 393, 2140, 281, 257, 30920, 337, 257, 31838, 622, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 211924, "start": 2131.62, "end": 2134.4599999999996, "text": " and track all four independent timelines at once.", "tokens": [50984, 293, 2837, 439, 1451, 6695, 45886, 412, 1564, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 211924, "start": 2134.52, "end": 2135.1, "text": " It's incredible.", "tokens": [51129, 467, 311, 4651, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 211924, "start": 2135.3799999999997, "end": 2138.4399999999996, "text": " Appendix A of the paper formally models this phenomenon,", "tokens": [51172, 3132, 521, 970, 316, 295, 264, 3035, 25983, 5245, 341, 14029, 11, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 211924, "start": 2139.16, "end": 2143.4199999999996, "text": " showing that our cognitive tracking is sophisticated enough to handle concurrent readiness.", "tokens": [51361, 4099, 300, 527, 15605, 11603, 307, 16950, 1547, 281, 4813, 37702, 34954, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 211924, "start": 2143.7599999999998, "end": 2144.68, "text": " Concurrent readiness.", "tokens": [51591, 2656, 49827, 34954, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1627750921686855, "compression_ratio": 1.6236559139784945, "no_speech_prob": 1.388142747450749e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 214468, "start": 2144.68, "end": 2146.04, "text": " We don't just process sequences.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 500, 380, 445, 1399, 22978, 13, 50433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17092893030736353, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 2.352555650286803e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 214468, "start": 2146.3999999999996, "end": 2148.52, "text": " We can process parallel states of tension.", "tokens": [50451, 492, 393, 1399, 8952, 4368, 295, 8980, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17092893030736353, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 2.352555650286803e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 214468, "start": 2148.74, "end": 2152.9199999999996, "text": " But here is where we reach the most profound pivot in the entire document.", "tokens": [50568, 583, 510, 307, 689, 321, 2524, 264, 881, 14382, 14538, 294, 264, 2302, 4166, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17092893030736353, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 2.352555650286803e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 214468, "start": 2153.48, "end": 2155.2, "text": " Up to this point in our dupe dive,", "tokens": [50805, 5858, 281, 341, 935, 294, 527, 1581, 494, 9192, 11, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17092893030736353, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 2.352555650286803e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 214468, "start": 2155.54, "end": 2157.3799999999997, "text": " every single example we've discussed,", "tokens": [50908, 633, 2167, 1365, 321, 600, 7152, 11, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17092893030736353, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 2.352555650286803e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 214468, "start": 2157.74, "end": 2162.2, "text": " from conversational digressions to video game save points to musical suspensions,", "tokens": [51018, 490, 2615, 1478, 2528, 735, 626, 281, 960, 1216, 3155, 2793, 281, 9165, 6535, 8302, 11, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17092893030736353, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 2.352555650286803e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 216220, "start": 2162.2, "end": 2164.64, "text": " has been fundamentally about time.", "tokens": [50365, 575, 668, 17879, 466, 565, 13, 50487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 216220, "start": 2164.9399999999996, "end": 2166.8399999999997, "text": " Time is the common denominator, yeah.", "tokens": [50502, 6161, 307, 264, 2689, 20687, 11, 1338, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 216220, "start": 2166.9199999999996, "end": 2167.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50601, 1779, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 216220, "start": 2167.58, "end": 2169.1, "text": " A sentence pauses chronologically.", "tokens": [50634, 316, 8174, 2502, 8355, 19393, 17157, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 216220, "start": 2170.06, "end": 2172.9399999999996, "text": " A video game level is entered and exited sequentially.", "tokens": [50758, 316, 960, 1216, 1496, 307, 9065, 293, 454, 1226, 5123, 3137, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 216220, "start": 2173.6, "end": 2176.0, "text": " A chord is suspended and resolved in time.", "tokens": [50935, 316, 14137, 307, 23437, 293, 20772, 294, 565, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 216220, "start": 2176.4399999999996, "end": 2180.7799999999997, "text": " It is all about when a scope opens and when it closes on a timeline.", "tokens": [51077, 467, 307, 439, 466, 562, 257, 11923, 9870, 293, 562, 309, 24157, 322, 257, 12933, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 216220, "start": 2181.02, "end": 2181.54, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51306, 7587, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 216220, "start": 2181.74, "end": 2184.7, "text": " Affliction points out that time is only one dimension of scope.", "tokens": [51342, 12840, 75, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 565, 307, 787, 472, 10139, 295, 11923, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 216220, "start": 2185.0, "end": 2188.68, "text": " What happens when scope stops being about when something happens", "tokens": [51505, 708, 2314, 562, 11923, 10094, 885, 466, 562, 746, 2314, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 216220, "start": 2188.68, "end": 2191.7999999999997, "text": " and starts being about who is allowed to know about it?", "tokens": [51689, 293, 3719, 885, 466, 567, 307, 4350, 281, 458, 466, 309, 30, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19355769235579695, "compression_ratio": 1.7592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 2.860371011229046e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 219180, "start": 2191.8, "end": 2195.36, "text": " This transition is where the paper moves from cognitive linguistics", "tokens": [50365, 639, 6034, 307, 689, 264, 3035, 6067, 490, 15605, 21766, 6006, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 219180, "start": 2195.36, "end": 2198.82, "text": " into something bordering on topology and information theory.", "tokens": [50543, 666, 746, 25872, 1794, 322, 1192, 1793, 293, 1589, 5261, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 219180, "start": 2198.92, "end": 2200.04, "text": " It gets really conceptual.", "tokens": [50721, 467, 2170, 534, 24106, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 219180, "start": 2200.4, "end": 2200.78, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50795, 467, 775, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 219180, "start": 2201.1400000000003, "end": 2205.28, "text": " The pivot point rests on a highly specific moment analyzed from the stage musical Hamilton.", "tokens": [50832, 440, 14538, 935, 39755, 322, 257, 5405, 2685, 1623, 28181, 490, 264, 3233, 9165, 18484, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 219180, "start": 2206.1800000000003, "end": 2210.84, "text": " Affliction asks us to imagine an actor on stage delivering a vocal aside to the audience.", "tokens": [51084, 12840, 75, 4105, 8962, 505, 281, 3811, 364, 8747, 322, 3233, 14666, 257, 11657, 7359, 281, 264, 4034, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 219180, "start": 2211.2000000000003, "end": 2215.34, "text": " Okay, an actor turns their head, shifts their tone, and speaks directly to the crowd.", "tokens": [51335, 1033, 11, 364, 8747, 4523, 641, 1378, 11, 19201, 641, 8027, 11, 293, 10789, 3838, 281, 264, 6919, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 219180, "start": 2215.5800000000004, "end": 2217.1800000000003, "text": " By changing their tone and cadence,", "tokens": [51554, 3146, 4473, 641, 8027, 293, 46109, 11, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 219180, "start": 2217.4, "end": 2221.38, "text": " the actor is using vocal cues to open a temporal scope, a parenthesis in time.", "tokens": [51645, 264, 8747, 307, 1228, 11657, 32192, 281, 1269, 257, 30881, 11923, 11, 257, 23350, 9374, 294, 565, 13, 51844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13309957814771076, "compression_ratio": 1.6987577639751552, "no_speech_prob": 2.61483976832233e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 222138, "start": 2221.38, "end": 2225.4, "text": " But imagine you are watching a recorded version of this performance on a screen", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3811, 291, 366, 1976, 257, 8287, 3037, 295, 341, 3389, 322, 257, 2568, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1552871348811131, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 3.0093024426525172e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 222138, "start": 2225.4, "end": 2227.56, "text": " and you have the English subtitles turned on.", "tokens": [50566, 293, 291, 362, 264, 3669, 42045, 3574, 322, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1552871348811131, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 3.0093024426525172e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 222138, "start": 2227.6600000000003, "end": 2228.8, "text": " Okay, closed captions are on.", "tokens": [50679, 1033, 11, 5395, 44832, 366, 322, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1552871348811131, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 3.0093024426525172e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 222138, "start": 2229.1, "end": 2235.54, "text": " The person who typed those subtitles decided to place that vocal aside inside written parentheses.", "tokens": [50751, 440, 954, 567, 33941, 729, 42045, 3047, 281, 1081, 300, 11657, 7359, 1854, 3720, 34153, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1552871348811131, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 3.0093024426525172e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 222138, "start": 2235.92, "end": 2238.28, "text": " So you have two completely independent systems.", "tokens": [51092, 407, 291, 362, 732, 2584, 6695, 3652, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1552871348811131, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 3.0093024426525172e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 222138, "start": 2238.52, "end": 2243.08, "text": " You have the biological system of the actor's vocal cords manipulating pitch and time.", "tokens": [51222, 509, 362, 264, 13910, 1185, 295, 264, 8747, 311, 11657, 36302, 40805, 7293, 293, 565, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1552871348811131, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 3.0093024426525172e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 222138, "start": 2243.5, "end": 2247.92, "text": " And you have the typographic system of the subtitle track rendering static symbols.", "tokens": [51471, 400, 291, 362, 264, 2125, 12295, 1185, 295, 264, 30706, 306, 2837, 22407, 13437, 16944, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1552871348811131, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 3.0093024426525172e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 224792, "start": 2247.92, "end": 2253.14, "text": " And both systems arrived at the exact same structural boundary without communicating with each other.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1293, 3652, 6678, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 15067, 12866, 1553, 17559, 365, 1184, 661, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 224792, "start": 2253.42, "end": 2253.94, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50640, 48746, 736, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 224792, "start": 2254.14, "end": 2256.02, "text": " The text and the voice align perfectly.", "tokens": [50676, 440, 2487, 293, 264, 3177, 7975, 6239, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 224792, "start": 2256.44, "end": 2261.38, "text": " But the subtitle track introduces a second, entirely different dimension of scope,", "tokens": [50791, 583, 264, 30706, 306, 2837, 31472, 257, 1150, 11, 7696, 819, 10139, 295, 11923, 11, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 224792, "start": 2261.6, "end": 2264.12, "text": " which Affliction terms recipient scope.", "tokens": [51049, 597, 12840, 75, 4105, 2115, 26216, 11923, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 224792, "start": 2264.28, "end": 2265.16, "text": " Recipient scope.", "tokens": [51183, 1300, 11371, 1196, 11923, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 224792, "start": 2265.28, "end": 2268.66, "text": " To understand this, we have to look at forced subtitles in film.", "tokens": [51233, 1407, 1223, 341, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 7579, 42045, 294, 2007, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 224792, "start": 2269.04, "end": 2270.7200000000003, "text": " Like when an alien language is spoken.", "tokens": [51421, 1743, 562, 364, 12319, 2856, 307, 10759, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 224792, "start": 2270.86, "end": 2271.32, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51512, 7587, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 224792, "start": 2271.7200000000003, "end": 2273.6, "text": " Imagine a scene in a science fiction movie", "tokens": [51555, 11739, 257, 4145, 294, 257, 3497, 13266, 3169, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15895486534188646, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.6453810929999433e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 227360, "start": 2273.6, "end": 2276.68, "text": " where two characters are speaking a fictional alien language.", "tokens": [50365, 689, 732, 4342, 366, 4124, 257, 28911, 12319, 2856, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 227360, "start": 2277.4, "end": 2280.2999999999997, "text": " The characters in the scene occupy one specific scope.", "tokens": [50555, 440, 4342, 294, 264, 4145, 30645, 472, 2685, 11923, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 227360, "start": 2280.8199999999997, "end": 2282.4, "text": " They hear the alien sounds.", "tokens": [50726, 814, 1568, 264, 12319, 3263, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 227360, "start": 2282.6, "end": 2283.5, "text": " They understand the syntax.", "tokens": [50815, 814, 1223, 264, 28431, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 227360, "start": 2284.0, "end": 2286.08, "text": " They exist within the reality of the scene.", "tokens": [50885, 814, 2514, 1951, 264, 4103, 295, 264, 4145, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 227360, "start": 2286.2599999999998, "end": 2289.54, "text": " But the audience watching the movie occupies a completely different scope.", "tokens": [50998, 583, 264, 4034, 1976, 264, 3169, 8073, 530, 257, 2584, 819, 11923, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 227360, "start": 2289.86, "end": 2291.54, "text": " We don't understand the alien language.", "tokens": [51178, 492, 500, 380, 1223, 264, 12319, 2856, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 227360, "start": 2292.04, "end": 2295.3399999999997, "text": " We are reading the English translation forced at the bottom of the screen.", "tokens": [51287, 492, 366, 3760, 264, 3669, 12853, 7579, 412, 264, 2767, 295, 264, 2568, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 227360, "start": 2295.48, "end": 2296.94, "text": " The characters can't see the text.", "tokens": [51459, 440, 4342, 393, 380, 536, 264, 2487, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 227360, "start": 2297.2599999999998, "end": 2299.04, "text": " And we can't understand the audio.", "tokens": [51548, 400, 321, 393, 380, 1223, 264, 6278, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17878966204887997, "compression_ratio": 1.9271255060728745, "no_speech_prob": 3.477233258275536e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 229904, "start": 2299.04, "end": 2300.7799999999997, "text": " And here's the crucial distinction.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 510, 311, 264, 11462, 16844, 13, 50452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 229904, "start": 2301.7799999999997, "end": 2305.58, "text": " Those forced subtitles do not open and close in time.", "tokens": [50502, 3950, 7579, 42045, 360, 406, 1269, 293, 1998, 294, 565, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 229904, "start": 2306.16, "end": 2308.86, "text": " They do not interrupt the temporal flow of the scene.", "tokens": [50721, 814, 360, 406, 12729, 264, 30881, 3095, 295, 264, 4145, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 229904, "start": 2309.0, "end": 2311.16, "text": " The scene just continues to play out sequentially.", "tokens": [50863, 440, 4145, 445, 6515, 281, 862, 484, 5123, 3137, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 229904, "start": 2311.38, "end": 2313.22, "text": " The subtitles run alongside the scene.", "tokens": [50982, 440, 42045, 1190, 12385, 264, 4145, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 229904, "start": 2313.7599999999998, "end": 2317.22, "text": " The boundary separating the character's knowledge from the audience's knowledge", "tokens": [51101, 440, 12866, 29279, 264, 2517, 311, 3601, 490, 264, 4034, 311, 3601, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 229904, "start": 2317.22, "end": 2318.98, "text": " is not a boundary of time.", "tokens": [51274, 307, 406, 257, 12866, 295, 565, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 229904, "start": 2319.4, "end": 2320.56, "text": " It is a boundary of access.", "tokens": [51383, 467, 307, 257, 12866, 295, 2105, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 229904, "start": 2320.82, "end": 2321.1, "text": " Access.", "tokens": [51454, 17166, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 229904, "start": 2321.68, "end": 2325.96, "text": " The scope is partitioning information simultaneously among different audiences.", "tokens": [51497, 440, 11923, 307, 24808, 278, 1589, 16561, 3654, 819, 15479, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 229904, "start": 2326.16, "end": 2326.54, "text": " Hold on.", "tokens": [51721, 6962, 322, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17099194867270334, "compression_ratio": 1.7953667953667953, "no_speech_prob": 2.218983026838761e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 232654, "start": 2326.54, "end": 2328.84, "text": " If this is just about separating who knows what,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 341, 307, 445, 466, 29279, 567, 3255, 437, 11, 50480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 232654, "start": 2329.04, "end": 2331.1, "text": " then this applies to dramatic irony, too.", "tokens": [50490, 550, 341, 13165, 281, 12023, 35365, 11, 886, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 232654, "start": 2331.32, "end": 2332.18, "text": " It absolutely does.", "tokens": [50604, 467, 3122, 775, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 232654, "start": 2332.22, "end": 2333.62, "text": " If I am watching a horror movie,", "tokens": [50649, 759, 286, 669, 1976, 257, 11501, 3169, 11, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 232654, "start": 2334.04, "end": 2337.2, "text": " and the camera pans to show the killer hiding in the closet,", "tokens": [50740, 293, 264, 2799, 32905, 281, 855, 264, 13364, 10596, 294, 264, 16669, 11, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 232654, "start": 2337.82, "end": 2340.5, "text": " I, the audience, know the killer is there.", "tokens": [50929, 286, 11, 264, 4034, 11, 458, 264, 13364, 307, 456, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 232654, "start": 2341.04, "end": 2345.14, "text": " But the main character, who is slowly walking into the bedroom, does not know.", "tokens": [51090, 583, 264, 2135, 2517, 11, 567, 307, 5692, 4494, 666, 264, 11211, 11, 775, 406, 458, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 232654, "start": 2345.38, "end": 2348.24, "text": " The audience has access to a layer of information", "tokens": [51307, 440, 4034, 575, 2105, 281, 257, 4583, 295, 1589, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 232654, "start": 2348.24, "end": 2350.2799999999997, "text": " that is strictly hidden from the character.", "tokens": [51450, 300, 307, 20792, 7633, 490, 264, 2517, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 232654, "start": 2350.66, "end": 2353.14, "text": " Are you telling me that the tension of a horror movie", "tokens": [51571, 2014, 291, 3585, 385, 300, 264, 8980, 295, 257, 11501, 3169, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879176655753715, "compression_ratio": 1.72992700729927, "no_speech_prob": 2.0444429569416167e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 235314, "start": 2353.14, "end": 2357.92, "text": " is mathematically the exact same phenomenon as a bilingual viewer reading a forced subtitle?", "tokens": [50365, 307, 44003, 264, 1900, 912, 14029, 382, 257, 48757, 16767, 3760, 257, 7579, 30706, 306, 30, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10284396409988403, "compression_ratio": 1.15, "no_speech_prob": 1.9432786543122083e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 235792, "start": 2357.92, "end": 2360.58, "text": " That is exactly what Fuchsian argues in the text.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 479, 37503, 952, 38218, 294, 264, 2487, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 235792, "start": 2361.54, "end": 2365.14, "text": " In Appendix B, the paper applies a sheaf-theoretic treatment", "tokens": [50546, 682, 3132, 521, 970, 363, 11, 264, 3035, 13165, 257, 750, 2792, 12, 3322, 26262, 299, 5032, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 235792, "start": 2365.14, "end": 2369.7400000000002, "text": " to prove that dramatic irony, stage-asides, forced subtitles,", "tokens": [50726, 281, 7081, 300, 12023, 35365, 11, 3233, 12, 296, 1875, 11, 7579, 42045, 11, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 235792, "start": 2370.06, "end": 2374.44, "text": " and internal monologues in a novel are all structurally identical.", "tokens": [50972, 293, 6920, 1108, 1132, 1247, 294, 257, 7613, 366, 439, 6594, 6512, 14800, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 235792, "start": 2374.84, "end": 2376.2000000000003, "text": " Whoa, stop right there.", "tokens": [51211, 7521, 11, 1590, 558, 456, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 235792, "start": 2376.38, "end": 2378.7400000000002, "text": " You just dropped sheaf-theoretic treatment,", "tokens": [51288, 509, 445, 8119, 750, 2792, 12, 3322, 26262, 299, 5032, 11, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 235792, "start": 2379.02, "end": 2383.08, "text": " which sounds like something out of an incredibly dense graduate mathematics seminar.", "tokens": [51420, 597, 3263, 411, 746, 484, 295, 364, 6252, 18011, 8080, 18666, 29235, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 235792, "start": 2383.2000000000003, "end": 2384.7000000000003, "text": " It sounds intimidating, I know.", "tokens": [51629, 467, 3263, 29714, 11, 286, 458, 13, 51704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434927156993321, "compression_ratio": 1.593984962406015, "no_speech_prob": 2.125873478989182e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 238470, "start": 2384.7, "end": 2385.98, "text": " You need to break that down for me.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 643, 281, 1821, 300, 760, 337, 385, 13, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 238470, "start": 2386.12, "end": 2389.98, "text": " What on earth is a sheaf, and how does it apply to horror movies and subtitles?", "tokens": [50436, 708, 322, 4120, 307, 257, 750, 2792, 11, 293, 577, 775, 309, 3079, 281, 11501, 6233, 293, 42045, 30, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 238470, "start": 2390.2999999999997, "end": 2392.3199999999997, "text": " It is a concept from algebraic topology,", "tokens": [50645, 467, 307, 257, 3410, 490, 21989, 299, 1192, 1793, 11, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 238470, "start": 2392.8799999999997, "end": 2395.3399999999997, "text": " but the underlying intuition is actually quite elegant.", "tokens": [50774, 457, 264, 14217, 24002, 307, 767, 1596, 21117, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 238470, "start": 2395.6, "end": 2397.5, "text": " Imagine a large patchwork quilt.", "tokens": [50910, 11739, 257, 2416, 9972, 1902, 27566, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 238470, "start": 2397.8999999999996, "end": 2398.8599999999997, "text": " Okay, a quilt.", "tokens": [51025, 1033, 11, 257, 27566, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 238470, "start": 2399.04, "end": 2401.0, "text": " The entire quilt represents global truth,", "tokens": [51082, 440, 2302, 27566, 8855, 4338, 3494, 11, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 238470, "start": 2401.22, "end": 2402.62, "text": " everything that is happening everywhere.", "tokens": [51191, 1203, 300, 307, 2737, 5315, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 238470, "start": 2403.3199999999997, "end": 2406.7, "text": " But you are only allowed to look at one specific square of the quilt at a time.", "tokens": [51296, 583, 291, 366, 787, 4350, 281, 574, 412, 472, 2685, 3732, 295, 264, 27566, 412, 257, 565, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 238470, "start": 2406.74, "end": 2408.12, "text": " I can only see my little square.", "tokens": [51467, 286, 393, 787, 536, 452, 707, 3732, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 238470, "start": 2408.7, "end": 2413.08, "text": " A sheaf is a mathematical tool that tracks how data or information is restricted", "tokens": [51565, 316, 750, 2792, 307, 257, 18894, 2290, 300, 10218, 577, 1412, 420, 1589, 307, 20608, 51784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14116860828260436, "compression_ratio": 1.6625386996904026, "no_speech_prob": 1.6557095321514947e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 241308, "start": 2413.08, "end": 2417.14, "text": " as you move from the global view to a local restricted view.", "tokens": [50365, 382, 291, 1286, 490, 264, 4338, 1910, 281, 257, 2654, 20608, 1910, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 241308, "start": 2417.68, "end": 2422.2, "text": " It formally defines what information is visible based on where you are standing.", "tokens": [50595, 467, 25983, 23122, 437, 1589, 307, 8974, 2361, 322, 689, 291, 366, 4877, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 241308, "start": 2422.2, "end": 2426.6, "text": " So in the horror movie, the global view includes the killer in the closet", "tokens": [50821, 407, 294, 264, 11501, 3169, 11, 264, 4338, 1910, 5974, 264, 13364, 294, 264, 16669, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 241308, "start": 2426.6, "end": 2428.04, "text": " and the character in the room.", "tokens": [51041, 293, 264, 2517, 294, 264, 1808, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 241308, "start": 2428.46, "end": 2429.98, "text": " The audience has the global view.", "tokens": [51134, 440, 4034, 575, 264, 4338, 1910, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 241308, "start": 2430.12, "end": 2430.3199999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51217, 1779, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 241308, "start": 2430.5, "end": 2435.04, "text": " But the character is restricted to a local view that only includes the empty room.", "tokens": [51236, 583, 264, 2517, 307, 20608, 281, 257, 2654, 1910, 300, 787, 5974, 264, 6707, 1808, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 241308, "start": 2435.08, "end": 2435.4, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51465, 7587, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 241308, "start": 2435.64, "end": 2442.58, "text": " Appendix B models the viewers and the characters as a partially ordered set or pose of audiences.", "tokens": [51493, 3132, 521, 970, 363, 5245, 264, 8499, 293, 264, 4342, 382, 257, 18886, 8866, 992, 420, 10774, 295, 15479, 13, 51840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13685040638364596, "compression_ratio": 1.8779527559055118, "no_speech_prob": 1.629592402858926e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 244258, "start": 2442.58, "end": 2444.14, "text": " Like partially ordered set.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 18886, 8866, 992, 13, 50443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 244258, "start": 2444.22, "end": 2446.34, "text": " It just means there is a hierarchy of access.", "tokens": [50447, 467, 445, 1355, 456, 307, 257, 22333, 295, 2105, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 244258, "start": 2447.16, "end": 2452.2, "text": " A bilingual viewer who understands both the alien spoken audio and the English subtitles", "tokens": [50594, 316, 48757, 16767, 567, 15146, 1293, 264, 12319, 10759, 6278, 293, 264, 3669, 42045, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 244258, "start": 2452.2, "end": 2457.8199999999997, "text": " sits at a different point in the hierarchy than a monolingual viewer who only reads the text.", "tokens": [50846, 12696, 412, 257, 819, 935, 294, 264, 22333, 813, 257, 1108, 401, 278, 901, 16767, 567, 787, 15700, 264, 2487, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 244258, "start": 2458.04, "end": 2462.18, "text": " The information the sheaf restricts differently depending on who is looking at it.", "tokens": [51138, 440, 1589, 264, 750, 2792, 7694, 82, 7614, 5413, 322, 567, 307, 1237, 412, 309, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 244258, "start": 2462.36, "end": 2462.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51354, 1779, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 244258, "start": 2462.88, "end": 2465.88, "text": " Temporal scope, like the video game level, is a stack in time.", "tokens": [51380, 8095, 2816, 304, 11923, 11, 411, 264, 960, 1216, 1496, 11, 307, 257, 8630, 294, 565, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 244258, "start": 2466.34, "end": 2469.7599999999998, "text": " Recipient scope is about overlapping local sections of reality.", "tokens": [51553, 1300, 11371, 1196, 11923, 307, 466, 33535, 2654, 10863, 295, 4103, 13, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482446090034816, "compression_ratio": 1.6480836236933798, "no_speech_prob": 1.383019458504886e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 246976, "start": 2469.76, "end": 2471.1200000000003, "text": " It's not a sequence of events.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 257, 8310, 295, 3931, 13, 50433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 246976, "start": 2471.26, "end": 2472.5600000000004, "text": " It's an architecture of access.", "tokens": [50440, 467, 311, 364, 9482, 295, 2105, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 246976, "start": 2472.82, "end": 2474.7200000000003, "text": " This completely blew my mind when I read it.", "tokens": [50518, 639, 2584, 19075, 452, 1575, 562, 286, 1401, 309, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 246976, "start": 2475.1000000000004, "end": 2479.0400000000004, "text": " The paper takes the temporal scope of when things happen and the recipient scope of who", "tokens": [50632, 440, 3035, 2516, 264, 30881, 11923, 295, 562, 721, 1051, 293, 264, 26216, 11923, 295, 567, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 246976, "start": 2479.0400000000004, "end": 2484.5600000000004, "text": " has access to them and combines them to arrive at the grand unification theory of this whole concept.", "tokens": [50829, 575, 2105, 281, 552, 293, 29520, 552, 281, 8881, 412, 264, 2697, 517, 3774, 5261, 295, 341, 1379, 3410, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 246976, "start": 2485.2400000000002, "end": 2491.6600000000003, "text": " And that grand unification theory requires us to completely discard our original understanding", "tokens": [51139, 400, 300, 2697, 517, 3774, 5261, 7029, 505, 281, 2584, 31597, 527, 3380, 3701, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 246976, "start": 2491.6600000000003, "end": 2492.5, "text": " of punctuation.", "tokens": [51460, 295, 27006, 16073, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 246976, "start": 2492.6800000000003, "end": 2494.6200000000003, "text": " All those grammar rules out the window.", "tokens": [51511, 1057, 729, 22317, 4474, 484, 264, 4910, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10978905814034598, "compression_ratio": 1.763779527559055, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129138377482757e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 249462, "start": 2494.62, "end": 2500.8399999999997, "text": " Fliction concludes that a comma, a parenthesis, or an em dash is not the actual phenomenon.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 24643, 300, 257, 22117, 11, 257, 23350, 9374, 11, 420, 364, 846, 8240, 307, 406, 264, 3539, 14029, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 249462, "start": 2501.68, "end": 2506.92, "text": " The ink on the page is just the tiny visible fragment of the true phenomenon that happened", "tokens": [50718, 440, 11276, 322, 264, 3028, 307, 445, 264, 5870, 8974, 26424, 295, 264, 2074, 14029, 300, 2011, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 249462, "start": 2506.92, "end": 2507.7799999999997, "text": " to get written down.", "tokens": [50980, 281, 483, 3720, 760, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 249462, "start": 2508.02, "end": 2509.94, "text": " So what is the true phenomenon?", "tokens": [51035, 407, 437, 307, 264, 2074, 14029, 30, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 249462, "start": 2510.4, "end": 2514.16, "text": " Fundamentally, a scope is simply a mechanism for limiting interaction.", "tokens": [51154, 13493, 2466, 379, 11, 257, 11923, 307, 2935, 257, 7513, 337, 22083, 9285, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 249462, "start": 2514.72, "end": 2516.6, "text": " A mechanism for limiting interaction.", "tokens": [51370, 316, 7513, 337, 22083, 9285, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 249462, "start": 2516.6, "end": 2518.44, "text": " That is so profound.", "tokens": [51464, 663, 307, 370, 14382, 13, 51556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 249462, "start": 2518.72, "end": 2519.64, "text": " It explains everything.", "tokens": [51570, 467, 13948, 1203, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093923195121214, "compression_ratio": 1.7212389380530972, "no_speech_prob": 2.860328727344319e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 251964, "start": 2519.64, "end": 2524.74, "text": " Without a mechanism to limit interaction, everything in the universe affects everything else instantly,", "tokens": [50365, 9129, 257, 7513, 281, 4948, 9285, 11, 1203, 294, 264, 6445, 11807, 1203, 1646, 13518, 11, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 251964, "start": 2524.96, "end": 2526.92, "text": " which results in pure chaos.", "tokens": [50631, 597, 3542, 294, 6075, 14158, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 251964, "start": 2527.0, "end": 2527.52, "text": " Codaloys.", "tokens": [50733, 383, 378, 10334, 749, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 251964, "start": 2527.8599999999997, "end": 2532.2599999999998, "text": " If we didn't have linguistic scope, a digression about a grocery store would bleed into a story", "tokens": [50776, 759, 321, 994, 380, 362, 43002, 11923, 11, 257, 2528, 2775, 466, 257, 14410, 3531, 576, 28385, 666, 257, 1657, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 251964, "start": 2532.2599999999998, "end": 2535.3799999999997, "text": " about a train ride, destroying the grammar of both.", "tokens": [50996, 466, 257, 3847, 5077, 11, 19926, 264, 22317, 295, 1293, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 251964, "start": 2535.72, "end": 2540.68, "text": " If we didn't have programmatic scope, the enemies from level 1 of Commander Keen would follow", "tokens": [51169, 759, 321, 994, 380, 362, 1461, 25915, 11923, 11, 264, 7805, 490, 1496, 502, 295, 20857, 3189, 268, 576, 1524, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 251964, "start": 2540.68, "end": 2541.58, "text": " you into level 2.", "tokens": [51417, 291, 666, 1496, 568, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 251964, "start": 2541.7599999999998, "end": 2546.68, "text": " And every variable in your computer would overwrite every other variable until the machine crashed.", "tokens": [51471, 400, 633, 7006, 294, 428, 3820, 576, 670, 21561, 633, 661, 7006, 1826, 264, 3479, 24190, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179687467672057, "compression_ratio": 1.7191780821917808, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351614494872438e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 254668, "start": 2546.68, "end": 2551.8799999999997, "text": " If we didn't have musical scope, every note would have to resolve instantly, and there", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 994, 380, 362, 9165, 11923, 11, 633, 3637, 576, 362, 281, 14151, 13518, 11, 293, 456, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 254668, "start": 2551.8799999999997, "end": 2555.16, "text": " could be no tension, no development, and no emotional journey.", "tokens": [50625, 727, 312, 572, 8980, 11, 572, 3250, 11, 293, 572, 6863, 4671, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 254668, "start": 2555.44, "end": 2560.6, "text": " Every system that scales must invent scope to create what physicists and computer scientists", "tokens": [50803, 2048, 1185, 300, 17408, 1633, 7962, 11923, 281, 1884, 437, 48716, 293, 3820, 7708, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 254668, "start": 2560.6, "end": 2562.52, "text": " call temporary locality.", "tokens": [51061, 818, 13413, 1628, 1860, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 254668, "start": 2562.7, "end": 2563.74, "text": " Temporary locality.", "tokens": [51166, 8095, 2816, 822, 1628, 1860, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 254668, "start": 2563.8999999999996, "end": 2564.12, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51226, 865, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 254668, "start": 2564.3599999999997, "end": 2569.2999999999997, "text": " It must build a boundary inside which things can happen without immediately mattering everywhere else.", "tokens": [51249, 467, 1633, 1322, 257, 12866, 1854, 597, 721, 393, 1051, 1553, 4258, 1871, 278, 5315, 1646, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 254668, "start": 2569.48, "end": 2574.3999999999996, "text": " It's the exact same fundamental constraint manifesting in different substrates.", "tokens": [51505, 467, 311, 264, 1900, 912, 8088, 25534, 8173, 8714, 294, 819, 4594, 12507, 13, 51751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 254668, "start": 2574.52, "end": 2574.7999999999997, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51757, 467, 307, 13, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10154418434415545, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540663795918455e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 257480, "start": 2574.8, "end": 2576.28, "text": " It reframes everything.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 13334, 1632, 1203, 13, 50439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 257480, "start": 2576.92, "end": 2581.6400000000003, "text": " You aren't just learning arcane grammar rules when you study the dash or syntax when you", "tokens": [50471, 509, 3212, 380, 445, 2539, 10346, 1929, 22317, 4474, 562, 291, 2979, 264, 8240, 420, 28431, 562, 291, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 257480, "start": 2581.6400000000003, "end": 2582.28, "text": " study code.", "tokens": [50707, 2979, 3089, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 257480, "start": 2582.7200000000003, "end": 2587.4, "text": " You are looking at the foundational architecture that makes communication, computation, and", "tokens": [50761, 509, 366, 1237, 412, 264, 32195, 9482, 300, 1669, 6101, 11, 24903, 11, 293, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 257480, "start": 2587.4, "end": 2589.54, "text": " composition entirely possible.", "tokens": [50995, 12686, 7696, 1944, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 257480, "start": 2589.8, "end": 2591.7000000000003, "text": " It is a universal law of organization.", "tokens": [51115, 467, 307, 257, 11455, 2101, 295, 4475, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 257480, "start": 2591.84, "end": 2592.5800000000004, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51217, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 257480, "start": 2592.88, "end": 2597.6800000000003, "text": " Infliction adds a wonderful metal layer to the very end of the text by pointing out that", "tokens": [51269, 682, 3423, 4105, 10860, 257, 3715, 5760, 4583, 281, 264, 588, 917, 295, 264, 2487, 538, 12166, 484, 300, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 257480, "start": 2597.6800000000003, "end": 2601.52, "text": " academic essays themselves operate on this exact architectural principle.", "tokens": [51509, 7778, 35123, 2969, 9651, 322, 341, 1900, 26621, 8665, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 257480, "start": 2601.6800000000003, "end": 2602.94, "text": " Oh, I loved that part.", "tokens": [51709, 876, 11, 286, 4333, 300, 644, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10820169616163823, "compression_ratio": 1.7052631578947368, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349495321297703e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 260294, "start": 2602.94, "end": 2605.62, "text": " An essay is a guided tour through nested scopes.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 16238, 307, 257, 19663, 3512, 807, 15646, 292, 795, 30545, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16823531559535435, "compression_ratio": 1.53551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327304533739982e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 260294, "start": 2606.16, "end": 2608.48, "text": " The introduction opens a massive outer scope.", "tokens": [50526, 440, 9339, 9870, 257, 5994, 10847, 11923, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16823531559535435, "compression_ratio": 1.53551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327304533739982e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 260294, "start": 2609.12, "end": 2611.96, "text": " It establishes a premise and promises to answer a question.", "tokens": [50674, 467, 8327, 279, 257, 22045, 293, 16403, 281, 1867, 257, 1168, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16823531559535435, "compression_ratio": 1.53551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327304533739982e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 260294, "start": 2612.38, "end": 2618.92, "text": " And then the body of the essay drops into inner scopes, digressing into arguments, citing evidence, and", "tokens": [50837, 400, 550, 264, 1772, 295, 264, 16238, 11438, 666, 7284, 795, 30545, 11, 2528, 18605, 666, 12869, 11, 48749, 4467, 11, 293, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16823531559535435, "compression_ratio": 1.53551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327304533739982e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 260294, "start": 2618.92, "end": 2620.16, "text": " exploring subsections.", "tokens": [51164, 12736, 1422, 40329, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16823531559535435, "compression_ratio": 1.53551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327304533739982e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 262016, "start": 2620.16, "end": 2625.56, "text": " And the conclusion finally executes the return marker, closing those inner loops and returning", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 10063, 2721, 4454, 1819, 264, 2736, 15247, 11, 10377, 729, 7284, 16121, 293, 12678, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16271597440125513, "compression_ratio": 1.4860335195530727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493982186322696e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 262016, "start": 2625.56, "end": 2627.2, "text": " you to the main thread where you started.", "tokens": [50635, 291, 281, 264, 2135, 7207, 689, 291, 1409, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16271597440125513, "compression_ratio": 1.4860335195530727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493982186322696e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 262016, "start": 2627.2, "end": 2634.14, "text": " But changed by the journey, which means this very deep dive has operated on that exact principle.", "tokens": [50717, 583, 3105, 538, 264, 4671, 11, 597, 1355, 341, 588, 2452, 9192, 575, 20826, 322, 300, 1900, 8665, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16271597440125513, "compression_ratio": 1.4860335195530727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493982186322696e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 262016, "start": 2634.42, "end": 2635.7999999999997, "text": " We fell right into the pattern.", "tokens": [51078, 492, 5696, 558, 666, 264, 5102, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16271597440125513, "compression_ratio": 1.4860335195530727, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493982186322696e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 263580, "start": 2635.8, "end": 2641.6600000000003, "text": " We opened our outer scope by talking about two simple sentences and a tiny change in punctuation.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 5625, 527, 10847, 11923, 538, 1417, 466, 732, 2199, 16579, 293, 257, 5870, 1319, 294, 27006, 16073, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14185007607064595, "compression_ratio": 1.52863436123348, "no_speech_prob": 1.708050476230405e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 263580, "start": 2642.2200000000003, "end": 2647.7400000000002, "text": " We dropped into inner scopes through 90s video games, terminal windows, conversational hypnosis,", "tokens": [50686, 492, 8119, 666, 7284, 795, 30545, 807, 4289, 82, 960, 2813, 11, 14709, 9309, 11, 2615, 1478, 7420, 46080, 11, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14185007607064595, "compression_ratio": 1.52863436123348, "no_speech_prob": 1.708050476230405e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 263580, "start": 2648.26, "end": 2649.2400000000002, "text": " and Bach fugues.", "tokens": [50988, 293, 30920, 31838, 1247, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14185007607064595, "compression_ratio": 1.52863436123348, "no_speech_prob": 1.708050476230405e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 263580, "start": 2649.34, "end": 2652.6400000000003, "text": " And now we are closing the loop, pulling all those threads back to the starting point.", "tokens": [51042, 400, 586, 321, 366, 10377, 264, 6367, 11, 8407, 439, 729, 19314, 646, 281, 264, 2891, 935, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14185007607064595, "compression_ratio": 1.52863436123348, "no_speech_prob": 1.708050476230405e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 263580, "start": 2652.82, "end": 2655.5600000000004, "text": " We are successfully executing the return marker.", "tokens": [51216, 492, 366, 10727, 32368, 264, 2736, 15247, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14185007607064595, "compression_ratio": 1.52863436123348, "no_speech_prob": 1.708050476230405e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 265556, "start": 2655.56, "end": 2662.14, "text": " Which brings us to one final fascinating scenario from the text that stretches this concept of", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 472, 2572, 10343, 9005, 490, 264, 2487, 300, 29058, 341, 3410, 295, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11962733818934514, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071354537640747e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 265556, "start": 2662.14, "end": 2664.96, "text": " scope to its absolute agonizing limit.", "tokens": [50694, 11923, 281, 1080, 8236, 623, 266, 3319, 4948, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11962733818934514, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071354537640747e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 265556, "start": 2665.4, "end": 2667.2599999999998, "text": " This is something everyone has experienced.", "tokens": [50857, 639, 307, 746, 1518, 575, 6751, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11962733818934514, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071354537640747e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 265556, "start": 2667.42, "end": 2671.42, "text": " I want you to think about picking up an old draft of a novel you were writing, or maybe", "tokens": [50958, 286, 528, 291, 281, 519, 466, 8867, 493, 364, 1331, 11206, 295, 257, 7613, 291, 645, 3579, 11, 420, 1310, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11962733818934514, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071354537640747e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 265556, "start": 2671.42, "end": 2675.1, "text": " a forgotten coding project or a hobby you abandoned a year ago.", "tokens": [51158, 257, 11832, 17720, 1716, 420, 257, 18240, 291, 13732, 257, 1064, 2057, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11962733818934514, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071354537640747e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 265556, "start": 2675.2, "end": 2676.04, "text": " Oh, it's the worst feeling.", "tokens": [51347, 876, 11, 309, 311, 264, 5855, 2633, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11962733818934514, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071354537640747e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 265556, "start": 2676.2599999999998, "end": 2680.2, "text": " Think about what it actually feels like to open that file after 12 months.", "tokens": [51400, 6557, 466, 437, 309, 767, 3417, 411, 281, 1269, 300, 3991, 934, 2272, 2493, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11962733818934514, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071354537640747e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 268020, "start": 2680.2, "end": 2685.7, "text": " According to the mechanics we've discussed today, this is scope re-entry stretched over", "tokens": [50365, 7328, 281, 264, 12939, 321, 600, 7152, 965, 11, 341, 307, 11923, 319, 12, 48766, 23563, 670, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 268020, "start": 2685.7, "end": 2688.14, "text": " a massive, unnatural time scale.", "tokens": [50640, 257, 5994, 11, 43470, 565, 4373, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 268020, "start": 2688.74, "end": 2692.8199999999997, "text": " When you open that old file, the computer loads the text instantly.", "tokens": [50792, 1133, 291, 1269, 300, 1331, 3991, 11, 264, 3820, 12668, 264, 2487, 13518, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 268020, "start": 2693.02, "end": 2693.22, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51006, 865, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 268020, "start": 2693.56, "end": 2694.7799999999997, "text": " But your brain does not.", "tokens": [51033, 583, 428, 3567, 775, 406, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 268020, "start": 2694.98, "end": 2697.9399999999996, "text": " There is no automated save point to load your cognitive state.", "tokens": [51104, 821, 307, 572, 18473, 3155, 935, 281, 3677, 428, 15605, 1785, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 268020, "start": 2698.06, "end": 2703.56, "text": " There is no FG terminal command you can type into your mind to magically bring your past", "tokens": [51258, 821, 307, 572, 479, 38, 14709, 5622, 291, 393, 2010, 666, 428, 1575, 281, 39763, 1565, 428, 1791, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 268020, "start": 2703.56, "end": 2704.8199999999997, "text": " thoughts back to the foreground.", "tokens": [51533, 4598, 646, 281, 264, 32058, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 268020, "start": 2704.8199999999997, "end": 2709.7799999999997, "text": " The inner scopes you left unresolved a year ago have been completely dumped from your working", "tokens": [51596, 440, 7284, 795, 30545, 291, 1411, 517, 495, 29110, 257, 1064, 2057, 362, 668, 2584, 32131, 490, 428, 1364, 51844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12424125356122481, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860165828232575e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 270978, "start": 2709.78, "end": 2710.1400000000003, "text": " memory.", "tokens": [50365, 4675, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07860620205218975, "compression_ratio": 1.775244299674267, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339759386646007e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 270978, "start": 2710.34, "end": 2715.82, "text": " You, the human being, have to do the manual, grueling labor of reconstructing the architecture.", "tokens": [50393, 509, 11, 264, 1952, 885, 11, 362, 281, 360, 264, 9688, 11, 677, 3483, 278, 5938, 295, 31499, 278, 264, 9482, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07860620205218975, "compression_ratio": 1.775244299674267, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339759386646007e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 270978, "start": 2716.0400000000004, "end": 2719.96, "text": " You have to re-read your own draft, sentence by sentence, to figure out what threads had", "tokens": [50678, 509, 362, 281, 319, 12, 2538, 428, 1065, 11206, 11, 8174, 538, 8174, 11, 281, 2573, 484, 437, 19314, 632, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07860620205218975, "compression_ratio": 1.775244299674267, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339759386646007e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 270978, "start": 2719.96, "end": 2723.38, "text": " been resolved, what arguments were left open, and what the dependencies were.", "tokens": [50874, 668, 20772, 11, 437, 12869, 645, 1411, 1269, 11, 293, 437, 264, 36606, 645, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07860620205218975, "compression_ratio": 1.775244299674267, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339759386646007e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 270978, "start": 2723.48, "end": 2727.5600000000004, "text": " And when you feel that friction, that heavy, frustrating brain fog of trying to remember", "tokens": [51050, 400, 562, 291, 841, 300, 17710, 11, 300, 4676, 11, 16522, 3567, 13648, 295, 1382, 281, 1604, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07860620205218975, "compression_ratio": 1.775244299674267, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339759386646007e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 270978, "start": 2727.5600000000004, "end": 2732.3, "text": " what you were doing and why you were doing it, you aren't just being forgetful or lazy.", "tokens": [51254, 437, 291, 645, 884, 293, 983, 291, 645, 884, 309, 11, 291, 3212, 380, 445, 885, 2870, 906, 420, 14847, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07860620205218975, "compression_ratio": 1.775244299674267, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339759386646007e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 270978, "start": 2732.3, "end": 2738.48, "text": " You are feeling the immense, literal cognitive weight of manually restoring a deeply nested scope", "tokens": [51491, 509, 366, 2633, 264, 22920, 11, 20411, 15605, 3364, 295, 16945, 36349, 257, 8760, 15646, 292, 11923, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07860620205218975, "compression_ratio": 1.775244299674267, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339759386646007e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 273848, "start": 2738.48, "end": 2741.2400000000002, "text": " brick by brick back into your working memory.", "tokens": [50365, 16725, 538, 16725, 646, 666, 428, 1364, 4675, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1281431180621506, "compression_ratio": 1.6715867158671587, "