logprob": -0.14251832074897233, "compression_ratio": 1.537117903930131, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617984778030445e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5742, "start": 72.06, "end": 76.46000000000001, "text": " So the question you have to answer before you hit that deploy button is, how do you tell them apart?", "tokens": [51097, 407, 264, 1168, 291, 362, 281, 1867, 949, 291, 2045, 300, 7274, 2960, 307, 11, 577, 360, 291, 980, 552, 4936, 30, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14251832074897233, "compression_ratio": 1.537117903930131, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617984778030445e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 7646, "start": 76.46, "end": 81.03999999999999, "text": " It is a genuinely terrifying scenario for anyone working in technology today, honestly.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 17839, 18106, 9005, 337, 2878, 1364, 294, 2899, 965, 11, 6095, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1412852302430168, "compression_ratio": 1.4293478260869565, "no_speech_prob": 1.825054213658306e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 7646, "start": 81.38, "end": 81.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50611, 1779, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1412852302430168, "compression_ratio": 1.4293478260869565, "no_speech_prob": 1.825054213658306e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 7646, "start": 81.97999999999999, "end": 89.55999999999999, "text": " Largely because, based on everything the tech industry has been taught about testing, auditing, and securing systems, you just can't.", "tokens": [50641, 11569, 70, 736, 570, 11, 2361, 322, 1203, 264, 7553, 3518, 575, 668, 5928, 466, 4997, 11, 2379, 1748, 11, 293, 33640, 3652, 11, 291, 445, 393, 380, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1412852302430168, "compression_ratio": 1.4293478260869565, "no_speech_prob": 1.825054213658306e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 7646, "start": 89.63999999999999, "end": 91.82, "text": " You simply cannot tell them apart.", "tokens": [51024, 509, 2935, 2644, 980, 552, 4936, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1412852302430168, "compression_ratio": 1.4293478260869565, "no_speech_prob": 1.825054213658306e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 9182, "start": 91.82, "end": 102.91999999999999, "text": " Exactly. If your entire auditing philosophy relies on looking at the object that is sitting right in front of you in the present moment, you are entirely blind to the danger hidden inside it.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 759, 428, 2302, 2379, 1748, 10675, 30910, 322, 1237, 412, 264, 2657, 300, 307, 3798, 558, 294, 1868, 295, 291, 294, 264, 1974, 1623, 11, 291, 366, 7696, 6865, 281, 264, 4330, 7633, 1854, 309, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06369753286872111, "compression_ratio": 1.5606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 2.307034554713261e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 9182, "start": 102.97999999999999, "end": 106.88, "text": " Because the math of the present state will tell you both systems are flawless.", "tokens": [50923, 1436, 264, 5221, 295, 264, 1974, 1785, 486, 980, 291, 1293, 3652, 366, 45693, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06369753286872111, "compression_ratio": 1.5606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 2.307034554713261e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 9182, "start": 107.24, "end": 109.33999999999999, "text": " Right. The math says they're the same.", "tokens": [51136, 1779, 13, 440, 5221, 1619, 436, 434, 264, 912, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06369753286872111, "compression_ratio": 1.5606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 2.307034554713261e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 10934, "start": 109.34, "end": 113.56, "text": " And that terrifying blind spot is the core mission of our deep dive today.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 18106, 6865, 4008, 307, 264, 4965, 4447, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 965, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1359656806131011, "compression_ratio": 1.5412186379928314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214538171675398e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 10934, "start": 114.0, "end": 121.34, "text": " We are completely unpacking this brilliant 2026 paper by an independent researcher operating under the name Fliction.", "tokens": [50598, 492, 366, 2584, 26699, 278, 341, 10248, 945, 10880, 3035, 538, 364, 6695, 21751, 7447, 833, 264, 1315, 3235, 4105, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1359656806131011, "compression_ratio": 1.5412186379928314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214538171675398e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 10934, "start": 121.54, "end": 122.58, "text": " Oh, it's such a good paper.", "tokens": [50975, 876, 11, 309, 311, 1270, 257, 665, 3035, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1359656806131011, "compression_ratio": 1.5412186379928314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214538171675398e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10934, "start": 122.58, "end": 129.1, "text": " It really is. It's titled Admissibility Certificates, Trust as a Property of System Histories.", "tokens": [51027, 467, 534, 307, 13, 467, 311, 19841, 46292, 891, 2841, 31036, 1089, 1024, 11, 11580, 382, 257, 48966, 295, 8910, 9038, 2083, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1359656806131011, "compression_ratio": 1.5412186379928314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214538171675398e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10934, "start": 129.74, "end": 136.32, "text": " And let me tell you, this paper fundamentally shatters how we think about the concept of trust in complex systems.", "tokens": [51385, 400, 718, 385, 980, 291, 11, 341, 3035, 17879, 402, 37690, 577, 321, 519, 466, 264, 3410, 295, 3361, 294, 3997, 3652, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1359656806131011, "compression_ratio": 1.5412186379928314, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214538171675398e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 13632, "start": 136.32, "end": 140.32, "text": " It really demands a complete paradigm shift from everyone in the field.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 15107, 257, 3566, 24709, 5513, 490, 1518, 294, 264, 2519, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10685242712497711, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667055547520902e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 13632, "start": 140.42, "end": 146.7, "text": " It does. We have to stop asking, you know, what does the system look like right now and start asking, how exactly did it get here?", "tokens": [50570, 467, 775, 13, 492, 362, 281, 1590, 3365, 11, 291, 458, 11, 437, 775, 264, 1185, 574, 411, 558, 586, 293, 722, 3365, 11, 577, 2293, 630, 309, 483, 510, 30, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10685242712497711, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667055547520902e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 13632, "start": 146.85999999999999, "end": 152.0, "text": " Yeah. And the beauty of Fliction's work is that it transcends just, like, theoretical math.", "tokens": [50892, 865, 13, 400, 264, 6643, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 589, 307, 300, 309, 43800, 2581, 445, 11, 411, 11, 20864, 5221, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10685242712497711, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667055547520902e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 13632, "start": 152.14, "end": 155.62, "text": " I mean, the rigorous formal logic is definitely the foundation.", "tokens": [51156, 286, 914, 11, 264, 29882, 9860, 9952, 307, 2138, 264, 7030, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10685242712497711, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667055547520902e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 13632, "start": 155.74, "end": 157.16, "text": " For sure. The math is dense.", "tokens": [51336, 1171, 988, 13, 440, 5221, 307, 18011, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10685242712497711, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667055547520902e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 13632, "start": 157.92, "end": 163.82, "text": " Right. But it functions more as a universal master key. It unlocks solutions across entirely disparate fields.", "tokens": [51445, 1779, 13, 583, 309, 6828, 544, 382, 257, 11455, 4505, 2141, 13, 467, 517, 34896, 6547, 2108, 7696, 14548, 473, 7909, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10685242712497711, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667055547520902e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 13632, "start": 163.94, "end": 164.6, "text": " It's everywhere.", "tokens": [51746, 467, 311, 5315, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10685242712497711, "compression_ratio": 1.609375, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667055547520902e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 16460, "start": 164.6, "end": 177.4, "text": " It really is. We are going to explore how this single mathematical concept redefines AI security, but also, you know, how it explains biological evolution, the rigorous safety protocols of aviation regulators.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 307, 13, 492, 366, 516, 281, 6839, 577, 341, 2167, 18894, 3410, 38818, 1652, 7318, 3825, 11, 457, 611, 11, 291, 458, 11, 577, 309, 13948, 13910, 9303, 11, 264, 29882, 4514, 20618, 295, 28831, 37311, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08570761458818303, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691398496370021e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 16460, "start": 177.57999999999998, "end": 179.22, "text": " Which is wild to think about.", "tokens": [51014, 3013, 307, 4868, 281, 519, 466, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08570761458818303, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691398496370021e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 16460, "start": 179.28, "end": 183.18, "text": " Yeah. And even the reproducibility crisis currently plaguing scientific research.", "tokens": [51099, 865, 13, 400, 754, 264, 11408, 537, 39802, 5869, 4362, 33756, 9635, 8134, 2132, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08570761458818303, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691398496370021e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 16460, "start": 183.34, "end": 187.07999999999998, "text": " I mean, the applications are just staggering once you understand the underlying mechanism.", "tokens": [51302, 286, 914, 11, 264, 5821, 366, 445, 42974, 1564, 291, 1223, 264, 14217, 7513, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08570761458818303, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691398496370021e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 18708, "start": 187.08, "end": 194.48000000000002, "text": " So, to understand the solution Fliction is proposing, we have to deeply understand the trap we are all currently caught in.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 281, 1223, 264, 3827, 3235, 4105, 307, 29939, 11, 321, 362, 281, 8760, 1223, 264, 11487, 321, 366, 439, 4362, 5415, 294, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560110714970803, "compression_ratio": 1.5970149253731343, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 18708, "start": 195.04000000000002, "end": 198.58, "text": " The paper calls this the identical endpoint problem.", "tokens": [50763, 440, 3035, 5498, 341, 264, 14800, 35795, 1154, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560110714970803, "compression_ratio": 1.5970149253731343, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 18708, "start": 198.66000000000003, "end": 200.14000000000001, "text": " The identical endpoint problem. Yeah.", "tokens": [50944, 440, 14800, 35795, 1154, 13, 865, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560110714970803, "compression_ratio": 1.5970149253731343, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 20014, "start": 200.14, "end": 207.38, "text": " It is the core vulnerability of almost all modern technology. And it really stems from our obsession with present state auditing.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 4965, 24210, 295, 1920, 439, 4363, 2899, 13, 400, 309, 534, 27600, 490, 527, 30521, 365, 1974, 1785, 2379, 1748, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10949065468528053, "compression_ratio": 1.591093117408907, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899417420319305e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 20014, "start": 207.54, "end": 209.44, "text": " Right. Checking things as they are right now.", "tokens": [50735, 1779, 13, 6881, 278, 721, 382, 436, 366, 558, 586, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10949065468528053, "compression_ratio": 1.591093117408907, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899417420319305e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 20014, "start": 209.6, "end": 216.1, "text": " Exactly. We evaluate software, AI models, and even physical machines by checking their current status.", "tokens": [50838, 7587, 13, 492, 13059, 4722, 11, 7318, 5245, 11, 293, 754, 4001, 8379, 538, 8568, 641, 2190, 6558, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10949065468528053, "compression_ratio": 1.591093117408907, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899417420319305e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 20014, "start": 216.44, "end": 222.1, "text": " We look at the model's weights. We measure its current outputs. We check its behavior against a static test suite.", "tokens": [51180, 492, 574, 412, 264, 2316, 311, 17443, 13, 492, 3481, 1080, 2190, 23930, 13, 492, 1520, 1080, 5223, 1970, 257, 13437, 1500, 14205, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10949065468528053, "compression_ratio": 1.591093117408907, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899417420319305e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 22210, "start": 222.1, "end": 227.1, "text": " And the paper argues this entire framing is not just flawed, but actively deceptive.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3035, 38218, 341, 2302, 28971, 307, 406, 445, 38823, 11, 457, 13022, 368, 1336, 488, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276780928688488, "compression_ratio": 1.6229508196721312, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423748212118783e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 22210, "start": 227.9, "end": 235.92, "text": " Actively deceptive. Yeah. Because two complex systems can occupy an identical present state, but have arrived there through wildly different histories.", "tokens": [50655, 3251, 3413, 368, 1336, 488, 13, 865, 13, 1436, 732, 3997, 3652, 393, 30645, 364, 14800, 1974, 1785, 11, 457, 362, 6678, 456, 807, 34731, 819, 30631, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276780928688488, "compression_ratio": 1.6229508196721312, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423748212118783e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 22210, "start": 236.45999999999998, "end": 241.35999999999999, "text": " Yeah. Fliction illustrates this with a really stark contrast between two hypothetical systems.", "tokens": [51083, 865, 13, 3235, 4105, 41718, 341, 365, 257, 534, 17417, 8712, 1296, 732, 33053, 3652, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276780928688488, "compression_ratio": 1.6229508196721312, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423748212118783e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 22210, "start": 241.94, "end": 244.22, "text": " System number one is like the gold standard.", "tokens": [51357, 8910, 1230, 472, 307, 411, 264, 3821, 3832, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276780928688488, "compression_ratio": 1.6229508196721312, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423748212118783e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 22210, "start": 244.38, "end": 245.32, "text": " The perfect system.", "tokens": [51479, 440, 2176, 1185, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276780928688488, "compression_ratio": 1.6229508196721312, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423748212118783e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 24532, "start": 245.32, "end": 254.22, "text": " Right. It was built using authenticated data. Every single experiment run during its development was meticulously documented and totally reproducible.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 467, 390, 3094, 1228, 9214, 3587, 1412, 13, 2048, 2167, 5120, 1190, 1830, 1080, 3250, 390, 41566, 25038, 23007, 293, 3879, 11408, 32128, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11151214710717063, "compression_ratio": 1.6853146853146854, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 24532, "start": 254.62, "end": 256.4, "text": " The engineers actually did their jobs.", "tokens": [50830, 440, 11955, 767, 630, 641, 4782, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11151214710717063, "compression_ratio": 1.6853146853146854, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 24532, "start": 256.58, "end": 263.68, "text": " Exactly. The engineering team maintains strict governance over their feature engineering. It is a clean, defensible process.", "tokens": [50928, 7587, 13, 440, 7043, 1469, 33385, 10910, 17449, 670, 641, 4111, 7043, 13, 467, 307, 257, 2541, 11, 1060, 30633, 1399, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11151214710717063, "compression_ratio": 1.6853146853146854, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 24532, "start": 264.46, "end": 268.76, "text": " System number two, however, was built during a training run that was secretly contaminated.", "tokens": [51322, 8910, 1230, 732, 11, 4461, 11, 390, 3094, 1830, 257, 3097, 1190, 300, 390, 22611, 34492, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11151214710717063, "compression_ratio": 1.6853146853146854, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 24532, "start": 269.0, "end": 270.74, "text": " By a poisoned data set.", "tokens": [51549, 3146, 257, 36677, 1412, 992, 13, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11151214710717063, "compression_ratio": 1.6853146853146854, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 24532, "start": 270.82, "end": 274.03999999999996, "text": " Yes. A poisoned data injected by a malicious actor.", "tokens": [51640, 1079, 13, 316, 36677, 1412, 36967, 538, 257, 33496, 8747, 13, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11151214710717063, "compression_ratio": 1.6853146853146854, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 27404, "start": 274.04, "end": 281.08000000000004, "text": " And then, to cover their tracks, the attacker made an undocumented manual edit to the internal weights of the model.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 550, 11, 281, 2060, 641, 10218, 11, 264, 35871, 1027, 364, 40472, 9688, 8129, 281, 264, 6920, 17443, 295, 264, 2316, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06909249207683812, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3713353329568587e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 27404, "start": 281.16, "end": 282.5, "text": " Right. Which is so sneaky.", "tokens": [50721, 1779, 13, 3013, 307, 370, 39518, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06909249207683812, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3713353329568587e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 27404, "start": 282.84000000000003, "end": 284.34000000000003, "text": " It's brilliant in a dark way.", "tokens": [50805, 467, 311, 10248, 294, 257, 2877, 636, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06909249207683812, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3713353329568587e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 27404, "start": 284.76000000000005, "end": 291.70000000000005, "text": " They specifically designed this edit to mask the anomaly from the exact benchmarks they knew the auditors were going to run.", "tokens": [50901, 814, 4682, 4761, 341, 8129, 281, 6094, 264, 42737, 490, 264, 1900, 43751, 436, 2586, 264, 2379, 9862, 645, 516, 281, 1190, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06909249207683812, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3713353329568587e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 27404, "start": 292.06, "end": 294.92, "text": " They smoothed over the surface so the math looked correct.", "tokens": [51266, 814, 5508, 292, 670, 264, 3753, 370, 264, 5221, 2956, 3006, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06909249207683812, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3713353329568587e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 27404, "start": 295.34000000000003, "end": 300.40000000000003, "text": " Mathematically speaking, the final state of system one and system two are now geometrically identical.", "tokens": [51430, 15776, 40197, 4124, 11, 264, 2572, 1785, 295, 1185, 472, 293, 1185, 732, 366, 586, 12956, 81, 984, 14800, 13, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06909249207683812, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.3713353329568587e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 30040, "start": 300.4, "end": 313.46, "text": " Right. If a security auditor evaluates a predicate, meaning like a formal true or false statement regarding the system's safety based solely on that single moment in time, both systems return true.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 759, 257, 3825, 33970, 6133, 1024, 257, 3852, 8700, 11, 3620, 411, 257, 9860, 2074, 420, 7908, 5629, 8595, 264, 1185, 311, 4514, 2361, 23309, 322, 300, 2167, 1623, 294, 565, 11, 1293, 3652, 2736, 2074, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525149906382841, "compression_ratio": 1.5125628140703518, "no_speech_prob": 1.513260003416228e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 30040, "start": 313.62, "end": 315.5, "text": " They both appear perfectly safe to deploy.", "tokens": [51026, 814, 1293, 4204, 6239, 3273, 281, 7274, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525149906382841, "compression_ratio": 1.5125628140703518, "no_speech_prob": 1.513260003416228e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 30040, "start": 315.84, "end": 319.03999999999996, "text": " But only system one is what the paper defines as admissible.", "tokens": [51137, 583, 787, 1185, 472, 307, 437, 264, 3035, 23122, 382, 5910, 41073, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525149906382841, "compression_ratio": 1.5125628140703518, "no_speech_prob": 1.513260003416228e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 31904, "start": 319.04, "end": 324.90000000000003, "text": " System two is a compromised object that merely mimics the appearance of an admissible one.", "tokens": [50365, 8910, 732, 307, 257, 32463, 2657, 300, 17003, 12247, 1167, 264, 8967, 295, 364, 5910, 41073, 472, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10641640424728394, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105214392323706e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 31904, "start": 325.58000000000004, "end": 338.62, "text": " I was thinking about this for you, the listener, and it's kind of similar to judging the structural integrity of a massive suspension bridge by only looking at its final coat of paint and measuring its cross-section against the blueprint.", "tokens": [50692, 286, 390, 1953, 466, 341, 337, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 293, 309, 311, 733, 295, 2531, 281, 23587, 264, 15067, 16000, 295, 257, 5994, 15771, 7283, 538, 787, 1237, 412, 1080, 2572, 10690, 295, 4225, 293, 13389, 1080, 3278, 12, 11963, 1970, 264, 35868, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10641640424728394, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105214392323706e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 31904, "start": 338.74, "end": 339.66, "text": " Yeah, that's a great analogy.", "tokens": [51350, 865, 11, 300, 311, 257, 869, 21663, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10641640424728394, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105214392323706e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 33966, "start": 339.66, "end": 347.28000000000003, "text": " Right. You can walk out onto the bridge, note that the paint is pristine, the steel looks solid, the measurements are absolutely flawless.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 509, 393, 1792, 484, 3911, 264, 7283, 11, 3637, 300, 264, 4225, 307, 582, 42745, 11, 264, 8269, 1542, 5100, 11, 264, 15383, 366, 3122, 45693, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06540873955036032, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370889240237662e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 33966, "start": 347.94, "end": 351.1, "text": " But you are completely ignoring the unseen history of that bridge.", "tokens": [50779, 583, 291, 366, 2584, 26258, 264, 40608, 2503, 295, 300, 7283, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06540873955036032, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370889240237662e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 33966, "start": 351.24, "end": 356.46000000000004, "text": " Exactly. Like, was it built using counterfeit steel that will just shear under winter temperatures?", "tokens": [50944, 7587, 13, 1743, 11, 390, 309, 3094, 1228, 5682, 37434, 8269, 300, 486, 445, 24082, 833, 6355, 12633, 30, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06540873955036032, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370889240237662e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 33966, "start": 356.6, "end": 360.96000000000004, "text": " Right. Or were the safety inspectors actually on site during the pouring of the concrete?", "tokens": [51212, 1779, 13, 1610, 645, 264, 4514, 15018, 830, 767, 322, 3621, 1830, 264, 20450, 295, 264, 9859, 30, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06540873955036032, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370889240237662e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 33966, "start": 361.48, "end": 367.64000000000004, "text": " Or did the concrete cure at the wrong humidity level, leaving, you know, microscopic stress fractures inside the pylons?", "tokens": [51456, 1610, 630, 264, 9859, 13698, 412, 264, 2085, 24751, 1496, 11, 5012, 11, 291, 458, 11, 47897, 4244, 17948, 1303, 1854, 264, 280, 5088, 892, 30, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06540873955036032, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370889240237662e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 36764, "start": 367.64, "end": 376.14, "text": " Yes. If you only evaluate the final, present endpoint, you entirely miss the structural rot hidden inside the object.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 759, 291, 787, 13059, 264, 2572, 11, 1974, 35795, 11, 291, 7696, 1713, 264, 15067, 4297, 7633, 1854, 264, 2657, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12884440979400238, "compression_ratio": 1.5394736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.741736854569964e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 36764, "start": 376.56, "end": 382.3, "text": " And that bridge analogy captures the exact dynamic of a sophisticated backdoor attack in cybersecurity.", "tokens": [50811, 400, 300, 7283, 21663, 27986, 264, 1900, 8546, 295, 257, 16950, 646, 10441, 2690, 294, 38765, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12884440979400238, "compression_ratio": 1.5394736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.741736854569964e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 36764, "start": 383.59999999999997, "end": 389.21999999999997, "text": " Attackers are not trying to create a system that looks broken or behaves erratically under testing.", "tokens": [51163, 22477, 433, 366, 406, 1382, 281, 1884, 257, 1185, 300, 1542, 5463, 420, 36896, 1189, 4481, 984, 833, 4997, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12884440979400238, "compression_ratio": 1.5394736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.741736854569964e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 36764, "start": 389.32, "end": 390.56, "text": " They want it to look perfect.", "tokens": [51449, 814, 528, 309, 281, 574, 2176, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12884440979400238, "compression_ratio": 1.5394736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.741736854569964e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 39056, "start": 390.56, "end": 398.82, "text": " Exactly. They are highly motivated to reach a state that is behaviorally indistinguishable from a safe one under ordinary inspection.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 814, 366, 5405, 14515, 281, 2524, 257, 1785, 300, 307, 5223, 379, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 490, 257, 3273, 472, 833, 10547, 22085, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08596748716375802, "compression_ratio": 1.5612648221343874, "no_speech_prob": 1.846851230974389e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 39056, "start": 399.72, "end": 403.06, "text": " State-level admissibility checks are just blind to this strategy.", "tokens": [50823, 4533, 12, 12418, 5910, 891, 2841, 13834, 366, 445, 6865, 281, 341, 5206, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08596748716375802, "compression_ratio": 1.5612648221343874, "no_speech_prob": 1.846851230974389e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 39056, "start": 403.26, "end": 406.58, "text": " Because they only examine a single coordinate in time and space.", "tokens": [51000, 1436, 436, 787, 17496, 257, 2167, 15670, 294, 565, 293, 1901, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08596748716375802, "compression_ratio": 1.5612648221343874, "no_speech_prob": 1.846851230974389e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 39056, "start": 406.78, "end": 413.1, "text": " Right. They look at where the system is sitting right now, ignoring the entire trajectory of how it maneuvered into that position.", "tokens": [51176, 1779, 13, 814, 574, 412, 689, 264, 1185, 307, 3798, 558, 586, 11, 26258, 264, 2302, 21512, 295, 577, 309, 25976, 292, 666, 300, 2535, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08596748716375802, "compression_ratio": 1.5612648221343874, "no_speech_prob": 1.846851230974389e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 41310, "start": 413.1, "end": 420.76000000000005, "text": " So, if examining the present state is a trap, we're kind of left staring at a massive void in how we evaluate trust.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 498, 34662, 264, 1974, 1785, 307, 257, 11487, 11, 321, 434, 733, 295, 1411, 18043, 412, 257, 5994, 22009, 294, 577, 321, 13059, 3361, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977849299364751, "compression_ratio": 1.6015325670498084, "no_speech_prob": 1.9729346194957698e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 41310, "start": 420.84000000000003, "end": 422.0, "text": " Like, what do we actually do?", "tokens": [50752, 1743, 11, 437, 360, 321, 767, 360, 30, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977849299364751, "compression_ratio": 1.6015325670498084, "no_speech_prob": 1.9729346194957698e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 41310, "start": 422.08000000000004, "end": 423.48, "text": " We need a completely different lens.", "tokens": [50814, 492, 643, 257, 2584, 819, 6765, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977849299364751, "compression_ratio": 1.6015325670498084, "no_speech_prob": 1.9729346194957698e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 41310, "start": 423.56, "end": 429.6, "text": " And this is where Fliction introduces the core mathematical reformulation of the paper, which they call systems as histories.", "tokens": [50888, 400, 341, 307, 689, 3235, 4105, 31472, 264, 4965, 18894, 8290, 2776, 295, 264, 3035, 11, 597, 436, 818, 3652, 382, 30631, 13, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977849299364751, "compression_ratio": 1.6015325670498084, "no_speech_prob": 1.9729346194957698e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 41310, "start": 429.78000000000003, "end": 430.98, "text": " Systems as histories, yes.", "tokens": [51199, 27059, 382, 30631, 11, 2086, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977849299364751, "compression_ratio": 1.6015325670498084, "no_speech_prob": 1.9729346194957698e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 41310, "start": 431.14000000000004, "end": 434.40000000000003, "text": " Fliction argues we just have to stop defining a system by its current parameters.", "tokens": [51267, 3235, 4105, 38218, 321, 445, 362, 281, 1590, 17827, 257, 1185, 538, 1080, 2190, 9834, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977849299364751, "compression_ratio": 1.6015325670498084, "no_speech_prob": 1.9729346194957698e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 43440, "start": 434.4, "end": 440.08, "text": " Instead, they introduce a new notation, H-sub-sigma, standing for system history.", "tokens": [50365, 7156, 11, 436, 5366, 257, 777, 24657, 11, 389, 12, 30131, 12, 82, 16150, 11, 4877, 337, 1185, 2503, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14037432877913766, "compression_ratio": 1.5574468085106383, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537847038674338e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 43440, "start": 440.46, "end": 449.9, "text": " Right. So, Fliction defines a system at any given time, not as a static object, but as a constantly evolving tuple, basically a mathematical list of interconnected elements.", "tokens": [50668, 1779, 13, 407, 11, 3235, 4105, 23122, 257, 1185, 412, 604, 2212, 565, 11, 406, 382, 257, 13437, 2657, 11, 457, 382, 257, 6460, 21085, 2604, 781, 11, 1936, 257, 18894, 1329, 295, 36611, 4959, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14037432877913766, "compression_ratio": 1.5574468085106383, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537847038674338e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 43440, "start": 450.03999999999996, "end": 450.23999999999995, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51147, 1779, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14037432877913766, "compression_ratio": 1.5574468085106383, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537847038674338e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 43440, "start": 450.56, "end": 456.03999999999996, "text": " And this tuple includes theta-sub-t, which is the current operative parameters or weights of the model.", "tokens": [51173, 400, 341, 2604, 781, 5974, 9725, 12, 30131, 12, 83, 11, 597, 307, 264, 2190, 2208, 1166, 9834, 420, 17443, 295, 264, 2316, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14037432877913766, "compression_ratio": 1.5574468085106383, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537847038674338e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 45604, "start": 456.04, "end": 464.06, "text": " But crucially, it expands outward to include D-sub-t, the data dependencies the system currently relies on.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 5140, 1909, 11, 309, 33706, 26914, 281, 4090, 413, 12, 30131, 12, 83, 11, 264, 1412, 36606, 264, 1185, 4362, 30910, 322, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10128726092251865, "compression_ratio": 1.5904059040590406, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724504168034391e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 45604, "start": 464.66, "end": 466.84000000000003, "text": " It also integrates L-sub-t, its lineage.", "tokens": [50796, 467, 611, 3572, 1024, 441, 12, 30131, 12, 83, 11, 1080, 38257, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10128726092251865, "compression_ratio": 1.5904059040590406, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724504168034391e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 45604, "start": 467.04, "end": 468.62, "text": " Let's unpack lineage real quick.", "tokens": [50915, 961, 311, 26699, 38257, 957, 1702, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10128726092251865, "compression_ratio": 1.5904059040590406, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724504168034391e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 45604, "start": 468.86, "end": 476.5, "text": " Lineage being the cryptographic or documented record of how that specific data and those specific parameters were actually produced, right?", "tokens": [51006, 14670, 609, 885, 264, 9844, 12295, 420, 23007, 2136, 295, 577, 300, 2685, 1412, 293, 729, 2685, 9834, 645, 767, 7126, 11, 558, 30, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10128726092251865, "compression_ratio": 1.5904059040590406, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724504168034391e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 45604, "start": 476.5, "end": 477.0, "text": " Yeah, exactly.", "tokens": [51388, 865, 11, 2293, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10128726092251865, "compression_ratio": 1.5904059040590406, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724504168034391e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 45604, "start": 477.02000000000004, "end": 479.20000000000005, "text": " It's basically the chain of custody for the code.", "tokens": [51414, 467, 311, 1936, 264, 5021, 295, 26976, 337, 264, 3089, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10128726092251865, "compression_ratio": 1.5904059040590406, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724504168034391e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 45604, "start": 479.32000000000005, "end": 481.3, "text": " Yeah, that's the perfect way to describe it.", "tokens": [51529, 865, 11, 300, 311, 264, 2176, 636, 281, 6786, 309, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10128726092251865, "compression_ratio": 1.5904059040590406, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724504168034391e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 48130, "start": 481.3, "end": 493.56, "text": " The tuple also encompasses the pipeline state, the governance protocols, meaning, you know, who actually holds the authority to act on or modify the system at any given time and its recovery capacity.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2604, 781, 611, 49866, 264, 15517, 1785, 11, 264, 17449, 20618, 11, 3620, 11, 291, 458, 11, 567, 767, 9190, 264, 8281, 281, 605, 322, 420, 16927, 264, 1185, 412, 604, 2212, 565, 293, 1080, 8597, 6042, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06427362158491805, "compression_ratio": 1.560747663551402, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956346707992174e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 48130, "start": 494.02000000000004, "end": 496.98, "text": " It fundamentally changed the definition of the object itself.", "tokens": [51001, 467, 17879, 3105, 264, 7123, 295, 264, 2657, 2564, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06427362158491805, "compression_ratio": 1.560747663551402, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956346707992174e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 48130, "start": 497.12, "end": 500.32, "text": " I mean, a car is no longer just the metal box sitting in your driveway.", "tokens": [51156, 286, 914, 11, 257, 1032, 307, 572, 2854, 445, 264, 5760, 2424, 3798, 294, 428, 38276, 13, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06427362158491805, "compression_ratio": 1.560747663551402, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956346707992174e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 50032, "start": 500.32, "end": 518.54, "text": " In this framework, the car is the vehicle, plus the factory that manufactured it, the entire global supply chain that sourced its parts, the maintenance logbook of every mechanic who ever tightened a bolt on it, and the emergency brake system all rolled into one conceptual entity.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 8388, 11, 264, 1032, 307, 264, 5864, 11, 1804, 264, 9265, 300, 25738, 309, 11, 264, 2302, 4338, 5847, 5021, 300, 11006, 1232, 1080, 3166, 11, 264, 11258, 3565, 2939, 295, 633, 23860, 567, 1562, 49673, 257, 13436, 322, 309, 11, 293, 264, 7473, 13997, 1185, 439, 14306, 666, 472, 24106, 13977, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09775196032577686, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179312222255106e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 50032, "start": 518.78, "end": 519.54, "text": " It's massive.", "tokens": [51288, 467, 311, 5994, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09775196032577686, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179312222255106e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 50032, "start": 519.9399999999999, "end": 522.72, "text": " And the most vital component of this concept is order.", "tokens": [51346, 400, 264, 881, 11707, 6542, 295, 341, 3410, 307, 1668, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09775196032577686, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179312222255106e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 50032, "start": 522.98, "end": 523.26, "text": " Order.", "tokens": [51498, 16321, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09775196032577686, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179312222255106e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 50032, "start": 523.48, "end": 524.28, "text": " Okay, explain that.", "tokens": [51523, 1033, 11, 2903, 300, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09775196032577686, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179312222255106e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 52428, "start": 524.28, "end": 529.62, "text": " Well, a system history is not a chaotic bucket of random snapshots just thrown together in a folder.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 257, 1185, 2503, 307, 406, 257, 27013, 13058, 295, 4974, 19206, 27495, 445, 11732, 1214, 294, 257, 10820, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 52428, "start": 529.88, "end": 530.04, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50645, 865, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 52428, "start": 530.04, "end": 533.54, "text": " It is an ordered, sequential trajectory through time.", "tokens": [50653, 467, 307, 364, 8866, 11, 42881, 21512, 807, 565, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 52428, "start": 533.72, "end": 533.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50837, 1779, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 52428, "start": 534.38, "end": 542.6999999999999, "text": " The sequence in which data was acquired, or the precise chronological order in which interventions and updates occurred, is the defining characteristic of the system.", "tokens": [50870, 440, 8310, 294, 597, 1412, 390, 17554, 11, 420, 264, 13600, 19393, 4383, 1668, 294, 597, 20924, 293, 9205, 11068, 11, 307, 264, 17827, 16282, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 52428, "start": 543.42, "end": 547.38, "text": " Affliction explicitly warns against treating history as an unordered set.", "tokens": [51322, 12840, 75, 4105, 20803, 12286, 82, 1970, 15083, 2503, 382, 364, 517, 765, 4073, 992, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 52428, "start": 547.52, "end": 548.8399999999999, "text": " Because the path matters.", "tokens": [51527, 1436, 264, 3100, 7001, 13, 51593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 52428, "start": 549.1, "end": 552.02, "text": " The path the system took dictates its fundamental reality.", "tokens": [51606, 440, 3100, 264, 1185, 1890, 12569, 1024, 1080, 8088, 4103, 13, 51752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15837277864155017, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496192874552394e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 55202, "start": 552.02, "end": 557.76, "text": " You know, order completely changes the outcome of a complex process, even if the ingredients are exactly the same.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 458, 11, 1668, 2584, 2962, 264, 9700, 295, 257, 3997, 1399, 11, 754, 498, 264, 6952, 366, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07814145998190378, "compression_ratio": 1.7747440273037542, "no_speech_prob": 1.70779926658704e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 55202, "start": 557.88, "end": 558.34, "text": " Oh, for sure.", "tokens": [50658, 876, 11, 337, 988, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07814145998190378, "compression_ratio": 1.7747440273037542, "no_speech_prob": 1.70779926658704e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 55202, "start": 558.4, "end": 564.18, "text": " Like, if you are baking, right, and you mix the flour and water before adding the yeast, you get bread.", "tokens": [50684, 1743, 11, 498, 291, 366, 12102, 11, 558, 11, 293, 291, 2890, 264, 7693, 293, 1281, 949, 5127, 264, 21629, 11, 291, 483, 5961, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07814145998190378, "compression_ratio": 1.7747440273037542, "no_speech_prob": 1.70779926658704e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 55202, "start": 564.42, "end": 570.6999999999999, "text": " But if you heat the water to boiling, add the yeast, which kills it, and then add the flour, you get a dense, inedible brick.", "tokens": [50985, 583, 498, 291, 3738, 264, 1281, 281, 16208, 11, 909, 264, 21629, 11, 597, 14563, 309, 11, 293, 550, 909, 264, 7693, 11, 291, 483, 257, 18011, 11, 294, 292, 964, 16725, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07814145998190378, "compression_ratio": 1.7747440273037542, "no_speech_prob": 1.70779926658704e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 55202, "start": 571.14, "end": 574.3199999999999, "text": " The ingredients, the state, are identical in the bowl.", "tokens": [51321, 440, 6952, 11, 264, 1785, 11, 366, 14800, 294, 264, 6571, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07814145998190378, "compression_ratio": 1.7747440273037542, "no_speech_prob": 1.70779926658704e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 55202, "start": 574.4, "end": 575.26, "text": " The state is identical.", "tokens": [51484, 440, 1785, 307, 14800, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07814145998190378, "compression_ratio": 1.7747440273037542, "no_speech_prob": 1.70779926658704e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 55202, "start": 575.52, "end": 580.78, "text": " But the sequence of operations resulted in a fundamentally different final entity.", "tokens": [51540, 583, 264, 8310, 295, 7705, 18753, 294, 257, 17879, 819, 2572, 13977, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07814145998190378, "compression_ratio": 1.7747440273037542, "no_speech_prob": 1.70779926658704e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 58078, "start": 580.78, "end": 582.74, "text": " That's a really clear way to put it.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 257, 534, 1850, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792855580647787, "compression_ratio": 1.5808080808080809, "no_speech_prob": 1.996892234901182e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 58078, "start": 583.16, "end": 592.72, "text": " Fliction is taking the idea of admissibility, which usually just means a single data point satisfies a set of constraints and stretching it across the dimension of time.", "tokens": [50484, 3235, 4105, 307, 1940, 264, 1558, 295, 5910, 891, 2841, 11, 597, 2673, 445, 1355, 257, 2167, 1412, 935, 44271, 257, 992, 295, 18491, 293, 19632, 309, 2108, 264, 10139, 295, 565, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792855580647787, "compression_ratio": 1.5808080808080809, "no_speech_prob": 1.996892234901182e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 58078, "start": 593.0799999999999, "end": 593.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50980, 1779, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792855580647787, "compression_ratio": 1.5808080808080809, "no_speech_prob": 1.996892234901182e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 58078, "start": 593.4399999999999, "end": 599.02, "text": " So an admissible system is one whose entire chronological journey satisfies the safety constraints.", "tokens": [50998, 407, 364, 5910, 41073, 1185, 307, 472, 6104, 2302, 19393, 4383, 4671, 44271, 264, 4514, 18491, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792855580647787, "compression_ratio": 1.5808080808080809, "no_speech_prob": 1.996892234901182e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 59902, "start": 599.02, "end": 604.04, "text": " The paper defines this as A of H-sub-sigma equals one.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 23122, 341, 382, 316, 295, 389, 12, 30131, 12, 82, 16150, 6915, 472, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 59902, "start": 604.8199999999999, "end": 607.78, "text": " The entire history must be verifiably clean.", "tokens": [50655, 440, 2302, 2503, 1633, 312, 1306, 17638, 1188, 2541, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 59902, "start": 608.26, "end": 609.22, "text": " Now, I have to be honest.", "tokens": [50827, 823, 11, 286, 362, 281, 312, 3245, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 59902, "start": 609.34, "end": 612.62, "text": " When I read this, I found myself arguing with the paper at this exact point.", "tokens": [50881, 1133, 286, 1401, 341, 11, 286, 1352, 2059, 19697, 365, 264, 3035, 412, 341, 1900, 935, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 59902, "start": 612.8, "end": 614.52, "text": " Oh, you and every engineer who reads it.", "tokens": [51054, 876, 11, 291, 293, 633, 11403, 567, 15700, 309, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 59902, "start": 614.56, "end": 614.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51142, 1779, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 59902, "start": 614.9399999999999, "end": 619.46, "text": " The demand for a perfectly clean history, it usually triggers an immediate practical objection.", "tokens": [51161, 440, 4733, 337, 257, 6239, 2541, 2503, 11, 309, 2673, 22827, 364, 11629, 8496, 35756, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 59902, "start": 619.86, "end": 623.46, "text": " The concept of evaluating a total history sounds beautiful in theory,", "tokens": [51407, 440, 3410, 295, 27479, 257, 3217, 2503, 3263, 2238, 294, 5261, 11, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1807595699205311, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897466278102292e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 62346, "start": 623.46, "end": 627.22, "text": " but in practice, it feels demanding to the point of absurdity.", "tokens": [50365, 457, 294, 3124, 11, 309, 3417, 19960, 281, 264, 935, 295, 19774, 507, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511439241008994, "compression_ratio": 1.4678899082568808, "no_speech_prob": 2.3704736090701672e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 62346, "start": 627.34, "end": 628.14, "text": " It sounds impossible.", "tokens": [50559, 467, 3263, 6243, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511439241008994, "compression_ratio": 1.4678899082568808, "no_speech_prob": 2.3704736090701672e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 62346, "start": 628.38, "end": 628.6, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50611, 865, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511439241008994, "compression_ratio": 1.4678899082568808, "no_speech_prob": 2.3704736090701672e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 62346, "start": 629.24, "end": 634.94, "text": " We cannot perfectly observe or record every single microsecond of a complex system's past.", "tokens": [50654, 492, 2644, 6239, 11441, 420, 2136, 633, 2167, 3123, 37841, 18882, 295, 257, 3997, 1185, 311, 1791, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511439241008994, "compression_ratio": 1.4678899082568808, "no_speech_prob": 2.3704736090701672e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 62346, "start": 635.36, "end": 642.9000000000001, "text": " A modern deep learning model processes billions of data points across thousands of GPUs over months of training time.", "tokens": [50960, 316, 4363, 2452, 2539, 2316, 7555, 17375, 295, 1412, 2793, 2108, 5383, 295, 18407, 82, 670, 2493, 295, 3097, 565, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511439241008994, "compression_ratio": 1.4678899082568808, "no_speech_prob": 2.3704736090701672e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 62346, "start": 642.94, "end": 643.1600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51339, 1779, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511439241008994, "compression_ratio": 1.4678899082568808, "no_speech_prob": 2.3704736090701672e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 62346, "start": 643.26, "end": 643.7800000000001, "text": " It's immense.", "tokens": [51355, 467, 311, 22920, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14511439241008994, "compression_ratio": 1.4678899082568808, "no_speech_prob": 2.3704736090701672e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 64378, "start": 643.78, "end": 648.3199999999999, "text": " Most of the operational history evaporates the very millisecond it is computed.", "tokens": [50365, 4534, 295, 264, 16607, 2503, 26315, 1024, 264, 588, 27940, 18882, 309, 307, 40610, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 64378, "start": 648.5799999999999, "end": 649.88, "text": " It is just lost to time.", "tokens": [50605, 467, 307, 445, 2731, 281, 565, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 64378, "start": 650.3199999999999, "end": 656.06, "text": " So how can anyone possibly evaluate an entire trajectory that they can no longer physically see?", "tokens": [50692, 407, 577, 393, 2878, 6264, 13059, 364, 2302, 21512, 300, 436, 393, 572, 2854, 9762, 536, 30, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 64378, "start": 656.36, "end": 657.24, "text": " It's a great question.", "tokens": [50994, 467, 311, 257, 869, 1168, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 64378, "start": 657.4399999999999, "end": 662.1, "text": " Infliction actually anticipates that friction and validates the pushback.", "tokens": [51048, 682, 3423, 4105, 767, 10416, 1024, 300, 17710, 293, 7363, 1024, 264, 2944, 3207, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 64378, "start": 662.66, "end": 667.38, "text": " You cannot observe the full past because the history is not directly inspectable at runtime.", "tokens": [51309, 509, 2644, 11441, 264, 1577, 1791, 570, 264, 2503, 307, 406, 3838, 15018, 712, 412, 34474, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 64378, "start": 668.06, "end": 671.78, "text": " An organization really has no choice but to rely on tangible evidence.", "tokens": [51579, 1107, 4475, 534, 575, 572, 3922, 457, 281, 10687, 322, 27094, 4467, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 64378, "start": 671.9, "end": 672.6999999999999, "text": " Tangible evidence.", "tokens": [51771, 22063, 964, 4467, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 64378, "start": 672.8399999999999, "end": 672.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51818, 1779, 13, 51825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1776482812289534, "compression_ratio": 1.6885813148788926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016201173126409e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 67298, "start": 672.98, "end": 678.64, "text": " A system with no lineage records, no monitoring history, and no provenance isn't automatically malicious,", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1185, 365, 572, 38257, 7724, 11, 572, 11028, 2503, 11, 293, 572, 12785, 719, 1943, 380, 6772, 33496, 11, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 67298, "start": 678.88, "end": 680.98, "text": " but its admissibility is fundamentally unverifiable.", "tokens": [50660, 457, 1080, 5910, 891, 2841, 307, 17879, 517, 331, 30876, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 67298, "start": 681.78, "end": 682.82, "text": " You just can't prove it's safe.", "tokens": [50805, 509, 445, 393, 380, 7081, 309, 311, 3273, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 67298, "start": 682.94, "end": 683.4200000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50863, 7587, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 67298, "start": 683.64, "end": 686.78, "text": " The paper states clearly trust cannot attach to a history no one can see.", "tokens": [50898, 440, 3035, 4368, 4448, 3361, 2644, 5085, 281, 257, 2503, 572, 472, 393, 536, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 67298, "start": 687.34, "end": 690.08, "text": " If the history is invisible, trust is a hallucination.", "tokens": [51083, 759, 264, 2503, 307, 14603, 11, 3361, 307, 257, 35212, 2486, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 67298, "start": 690.1800000000001, "end": 691.44, "text": " Trust is a hallucination.", "tokens": [51225, 11580, 307, 257, 35212, 2486, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 67298, "start": 692.02, "end": 692.34, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51317, 3153, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 67298, "start": 692.5, "end": 695.88, "text": " So we need physical, undeniable proof of the invisible past.", "tokens": [51341, 407, 321, 643, 4001, 11, 674, 268, 9364, 8177, 295, 264, 14603, 1791, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 67298, "start": 695.9, "end": 696.16, "text": " That's right.", "tokens": [51511, 663, 311, 558, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 67298, "start": 696.16, "end": 702.64, "text": " But before affliction even dives into the intense theoretical math of how to generate and verify this proof,", "tokens": [51524, 583, 949, 2096, 75, 4105, 754, 274, 1539, 666, 264, 9447, 20864, 5221, 295, 577, 281, 8460, 293, 16888, 341, 8177, 11, 51848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837228502546037, "compression_ratio": 1.702194357366771, "no_speech_prob": 1.935470880787271e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 70298, "start": 702.98, "end": 705.22, "text": " the paper highlights a fascinating reality.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 3035, 14254, 257, 10343, 4103, 13, 50477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19889886695218373, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430435992812134e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 70298, "start": 705.64, "end": 706.96, "text": " This is my favorite part of the paper.", "tokens": [50498, 639, 307, 452, 2954, 644, 295, 264, 3035, 13, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19889886695218373, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430435992812134e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 70298, "start": 707.08, "end": 707.5, "text": " Mine too.", "tokens": [50570, 11620, 886, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19889886695218373, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430435992812134e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 70298, "start": 708.3000000000001, "end": 713.6, "text": " This exact problem of proving an unobservable history was recently solved in the real world.", "tokens": [50631, 639, 1900, 1154, 295, 27221, 364, 8526, 929, 1978, 712, 2503, 390, 3938, 13041, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19889886695218373, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430435992812134e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 70298, "start": 713.74, "end": 714.08, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50903, 1079, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19889886695218373, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430435992812134e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 70298, "start": 714.28, "end": 716.98, "text": " And the person who solved it was not a theoretical mathematician,", "tokens": [50930, 400, 264, 954, 567, 13041, 309, 390, 406, 257, 20864, 48281, 11, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19889886695218373, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430435992812134e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 70298, "start": 717.38, "end": 720.9200000000001, "text": " and they had absolutely no idea they were proving Fliction's theorems.", "tokens": [51085, 293, 436, 632, 3122, 572, 1558, 436, 645, 27221, 3235, 4105, 311, 10299, 2592, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19889886695218373, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430435992812134e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 72092, "start": 720.92, "end": 721.86, "text": " No idea at all.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 1558, 412, 439, 13, 50412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 72092, "start": 722.24, "end": 724.8399999999999, "text": " The paper introduces this deeply compelling case study,", "tokens": [50431, 440, 3035, 31472, 341, 8760, 20050, 1389, 2979, 11, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 72092, "start": 725.2199999999999, "end": 728.86, "text": " an industrial machine learning operations security framework.", "tokens": [50580, 364, 9987, 3479, 2539, 7705, 3825, 8388, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 72092, "start": 728.9599999999999, "end": 729.5799999999999, "text": " M.L. OAPS.", "tokens": [50767, 376, 13, 43, 13, 422, 4715, 50, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 72092, "start": 729.76, "end": 729.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50807, 1779, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 72092, "start": 729.9799999999999, "end": 730.5, "text": " M.L. OAPS.", "tokens": [50818, 376, 13, 43, 13, 422, 4715, 50, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 72092, "start": 730.8199999999999, "end": 733.4, "text": " And this was created by an engineer named Susanna Cox.", "tokens": [50860, 400, 341, 390, 2942, 538, 364, 11403, 4926, 9545, 1795, 41576, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 72092, "start": 734.04, "end": 738.64, "text": " Her framework is titled Securing AML Systems in the Age of Information Warfare.", "tokens": [51021, 3204, 8388, 307, 19841, 3306, 1345, 6475, 43, 27059, 294, 264, 16280, 295, 15357, 3630, 11079, 13, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 72092, "start": 738.86, "end": 740.38, "text": " Such a badass title, by the way.", "tokens": [51262, 9653, 257, 33907, 4876, 11, 538, 264, 636, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 72092, "start": 740.4399999999999, "end": 741.06, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51341, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 72092, "start": 741.42, "end": 745.12, "text": " And Cox was not trying to write a grand unified theory of mathematical trust.", "tokens": [51390, 400, 41576, 390, 406, 1382, 281, 2464, 257, 2697, 26787, 5261, 295, 18894, 3361, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 72092, "start": 745.5, "end": 748.52, "text": " She was entrenched in a gritty, boots-on-the-ground crisis.", "tokens": [51594, 1240, 390, 948, 42388, 294, 257, 677, 10016, 11, 15194, 12, 266, 12, 3322, 12, 2921, 5869, 13, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17977763236837185, "compression_ratio": 1.5855263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417406492775678e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 74852, "start": 748.52, "end": 752.8, "text": " She was trying to figure out how to keep corporate machine learning systems secure", "tokens": [50365, 1240, 390, 1382, 281, 2573, 484, 577, 281, 1066, 10896, 3479, 2539, 3652, 7144, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10861332115085645, "compression_ratio": 1.5992063492063493, "no_speech_prob": 1.579459219663848e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 74852, "start": 752.8, "end": 756.04, "text": " when they're operating in highly adversarial environments,", "tokens": [50579, 562, 436, 434, 7447, 294, 5405, 17641, 44745, 12388, 11, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10861332115085645, "compression_ratio": 1.5992063492063493, "no_speech_prob": 1.579459219663848e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 74852, "start": 756.52, "end": 761.42, "text": " like where nation states and malicious hackers are actively trying to subtly poison the data", "tokens": [50765, 411, 689, 4790, 4368, 293, 33496, 39766, 366, 13022, 1382, 281, 7257, 356, 10836, 264, 1412, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10861332115085645, "compression_ratio": 1.5992063492063493, "no_speech_prob": 1.579459219663848e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 74852, "start": 761.42, "end": 763.16, "text": " feeds those systems rely on.", "tokens": [51010, 23712, 729, 3652, 10687, 322, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10861332115085645, "compression_ratio": 1.5992063492063493, "no_speech_prob": 1.579459219663848e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 74852, "start": 763.26, "end": 763.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51102, 1779, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10861332115085645, "compression_ratio": 1.5992063492063493, "no_speech_prob": 1.579459219663848e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 74852, "start": 763.56, "end": 766.28, "text": " She was dealing with the identical endpoint problem in the wild.", "tokens": [51117, 1240, 390, 6260, 365, 264, 14800, 35795, 1154, 294, 264, 4868, 13, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10861332115085645, "compression_ratio": 1.5992063492063493, "no_speech_prob": 1.579459219663848e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 74852, "start": 767.1, "end": 771.12, "text": " And Fliction maps out this astonishing, almost total correspondence", "tokens": [51294, 400, 3235, 4105, 11317, 484, 341, 35264, 11, 1920, 3217, 38135, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10861332115085645, "compression_ratio": 1.5992063492063493, "no_speech_prob": 1.579459219663848e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 77112, "start": 771.12, "end": 775.5, "text": " between Cox's highly practical, industrially motivated framework", "tokens": [50365, 1296, 41576, 311, 5405, 8496, 11, 49005, 379, 14515, 8388, 50584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14161805753354673, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.81792178966661e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 77112, "start": 775.5, "end": 779.02, "text": " and Flitchian's own abstract theoretical math.", "tokens": [50584, 293, 3235, 1549, 952, 311, 1065, 12649, 20864, 5221, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14161805753354673, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.81792178966661e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 77112, "start": 779.12, "end": 780.92, "text": " It's like they were looking at the same blueprint.", "tokens": [50765, 467, 311, 411, 436, 645, 1237, 412, 264, 912, 35868, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14161805753354673, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.81792178966661e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 77112, "start": 781.66, "end": 787.48, "text": " Cox independently derived nearly every single component of Fliction's complex formal structure", "tokens": [50892, 41576, 21761, 18949, 6217, 633, 2167, 6542, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 3997, 9860, 3877, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14161805753354673, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.81792178966661e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 77112, "start": 787.48, "end": 790.74, "text": " out of pure, desperate, practical necessity.", "tokens": [51183, 484, 295, 6075, 11, 17601, 11, 8496, 24217, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14161805753354673, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.81792178966661e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 77112, "start": 790.96, "end": 793.86, "text": " The overlaps are staggering when you lay them side by side.", "tokens": [51357, 440, 15986, 2382, 366, 42974, 562, 291, 2360, 552, 1252, 538, 1252, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14161805753354673, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.81792178966661e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 79386, "start": 793.86, "end": 795.0, "text": " I mean, let's look at it.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 309, 13, 50422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 79386, "start": 795.3000000000001, "end": 800.7, "text": " Cox's framework relies on establishing what she calls a trusted baseline for a model, right?", "tokens": [50437, 41576, 311, 8388, 30910, 322, 22494, 437, 750, 5498, 257, 16034, 20518, 337, 257, 2316, 11, 558, 30, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 79386, "start": 800.96, "end": 803.0600000000001, "text": " A known good state before deploying it.", "tokens": [50720, 316, 2570, 665, 1785, 949, 34198, 309, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 79386, "start": 803.42, "end": 803.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50843, 1779, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 79386, "start": 803.64, "end": 807.6, "text": " And Fliction points out that this corporate terminology maps perfectly to the mathematical", "tokens": [50854, 400, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 341, 10896, 27575, 11317, 6239, 281, 264, 18894, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 79386, "start": 807.6, "end": 809.78, "text": " concept of an admissible state.", "tokens": [51052, 3410, 295, 364, 5910, 41073, 1785, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 79386, "start": 809.9, "end": 810.4, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51167, 7587, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 79386, "start": 810.72, "end": 816.12, "text": " And Cox uses automated monitoring thresholds to track live inference behavior against that baseline,", "tokens": [51208, 400, 41576, 4960, 18473, 11028, 14678, 82, 281, 2837, 1621, 38253, 5223, 1970, 300, 20518, 11, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 79386, "start": 816.6, "end": 819.1800000000001, "text": " flagging when the model starts acting slightly strangely.", "tokens": [51502, 7166, 3249, 562, 264, 2316, 3719, 6577, 4748, 39851, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 79386, "start": 819.66, "end": 823.32, "text": " And in Fliction's mathematical notation, these are admissibility predicates.", "tokens": [51655, 400, 294, 3235, 4105, 311, 18894, 24657, 11, 613, 366, 5910, 891, 2841, 47336, 1024, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15258696771437122, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747692642427037e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 82332, "start": 823.32, "end": 827.5200000000001, "text": " They're computable surrogates that basically stand in for the history you can no longer see.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 434, 2807, 712, 1022, 6675, 1024, 300, 1936, 1463, 294, 337, 264, 2503, 291, 393, 572, 2854, 536, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 82332, "start": 827.9200000000001, "end": 828.0200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50595, 1779, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 82332, "start": 828.44, "end": 832.1400000000001, "text": " And Cox also places a massive emphasis on lineage tracking.", "tokens": [50621, 400, 41576, 611, 3190, 257, 5994, 16271, 322, 38257, 11603, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 82332, "start": 832.9000000000001, "end": 836.6600000000001, "text": " Her system meticulously tracks exactly where retraining data comes from,", "tokens": [50844, 3204, 1185, 41566, 25038, 10218, 2293, 689, 49356, 1760, 1412, 1487, 490, 11, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 82332, "start": 836.96, "end": 839.12, "text": " what sensors collected it, and who touched it.", "tokens": [51047, 437, 14840, 11087, 309, 11, 293, 567, 9828, 309, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 82332, "start": 839.36, "end": 843.6, "text": " Which Fliction maps directly to the theoretical concept of empirical reachability.", "tokens": [51167, 3013, 3235, 4105, 11317, 3838, 281, 264, 20864, 3410, 295, 31886, 2524, 2310, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 82332, "start": 843.84, "end": 845.2, "text": " It's just one-to-one.", "tokens": [51391, 467, 311, 445, 472, 12, 1353, 12, 546, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 82332, "start": 845.9000000000001, "end": 849.7600000000001, "text": " Furthermore, when the automated thresholds in Cox's system are breached,", "tokens": [51494, 23999, 11, 562, 264, 18473, 14678, 82, 294, 41576, 311, 1185, 366, 1403, 15095, 11, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 82332, "start": 850.2800000000001, "end": 852.7, "text": " her framework doesn't just automatically delete the model.", "tokens": [51713, 720, 8388, 1177, 380, 445, 6772, 12097, 264, 2316, 13, 51834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12955685584775864, "compression_ratio": 1.5975232198142415, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419127121623412e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 85270, "start": 852.7, "end": 853.08, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 85270, "start": 853.1600000000001, "end": 854.36, "text": " It doesn't just auto-resolve.", "tokens": [50388, 467, 1177, 380, 445, 8399, 12, 495, 37361, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 85270, "start": 854.5, "end": 856.88, "text": " It escalates the alert to a human review board.", "tokens": [50455, 467, 17871, 1024, 264, 9615, 281, 257, 1952, 3131, 3150, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 85270, "start": 856.98, "end": 857.26, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50579, 1079, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 85270, "start": 857.9000000000001, "end": 863.24, "text": " And Fliction notes that this human escalation is a tacit, practical acknowledgement of a deep", "tokens": [50625, 400, 3235, 4105, 5570, 300, 341, 1952, 17871, 399, 307, 257, 25018, 270, 11, 8496, 47227, 295, 257, 2452, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 85270, "start": 863.24, "end": 864.26, "text": " mathematical truth.", "tokens": [50892, 18894, 3494, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 85270, "start": 865.2, "end": 868.08, "text": " Admissibility isn't purely mechanically decidable.", "tokens": [50990, 46292, 891, 2841, 1943, 380, 17491, 4236, 984, 21937, 712, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 85270, "start": 868.1600000000001, "end": 870.0400000000001, "text": " We can't just code our way out of it.", "tokens": [51138, 492, 393, 380, 445, 3089, 527, 636, 484, 295, 309, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 85270, "start": 870.1600000000001, "end": 870.62, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51238, 7587, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18263865576850044, "compression_ratio": 1.4682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803836710134e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 87062, "start": 870.62, "end": 881.5, "text": " Sometimes, judging whether a specific sequence of events in a history is trustworthy requires a level of contextual human interpretation that a simple Boolean code check just cannot provide.", "tokens": [50365, 4803, 11, 23587, 1968, 257, 2685, 8310, 295, 3931, 294, 257, 2503, 307, 39714, 7029, 257, 1496, 295, 35526, 1952, 14174, 300, 257, 2199, 23351, 28499, 3089, 1520, 445, 2644, 2893, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128045688975941, "compression_ratio": 1.4550264550264551, "no_speech_prob": 2.815567006972386e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 87062, "start": 881.9, "end": 885.4, "text": " You need human judgment to look at the lineage and decide if the path was corrupted.", "tokens": [50929, 509, 643, 1952, 12216, 281, 574, 412, 264, 38257, 293, 4536, 498, 264, 3100, 390, 39480, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128045688975941, "compression_ratio": 1.4550264550264551, "no_speech_prob": 2.815567006972386e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 88540, "start": 885.4, "end": 903.04, "text": " When two entirely independent fields, I mean abstract formal constraint theory on one side, and practical corporate MLO's defense on the other, arrive at the exact same architectural blueprint to solve a problem, it indicates they have stumbled onto a universal principle.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 732, 7696, 6695, 7909, 11, 286, 914, 12649, 9860, 25534, 5261, 322, 472, 1252, 11, 293, 8496, 10896, 376, 20184, 311, 7654, 322, 264, 661, 11, 8881, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 26621, 35868, 281, 5039, 257, 1154, 11, 309, 16203, 436, 362, 36668, 3911, 257, 11455, 8665, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11123607743461177, "compression_ratio": 1.4863387978142077, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201224811526973e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 90304, "start": 903.04, "end": 903.86, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 50406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2000982165336609, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.981060931618983e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 90304, "start": 904.04, "end": 905.1999999999999, "text": " It is convergent evolution.", "tokens": [50415, 467, 307, 9652, 6930, 9303, 13, 50473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2000982165336609, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.981060931618983e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 90304, "start": 905.3399999999999, "end": 906.54, "text": " Convergent evolution, yeah.", "tokens": [50480, 2656, 331, 6930, 9303, 11, 1338, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2000982165336609, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.981060931618983e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 90304, "start": 907.48, "end": 915.6999999999999, "text": " The crushing pressure of practical necessity forced Susanna Cox to build the very theoretical object Flicksheen was conceptualizing in the abstract.", "tokens": [50587, 440, 31317, 3321, 295, 8496, 24217, 7579, 9545, 1795, 41576, 281, 1322, 264, 588, 20864, 2657, 3235, 618, 9611, 268, 390, 24106, 3319, 294, 264, 12649, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2000982165336609, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.981060931618983e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 90304, "start": 916.0799999999999, "end": 923.0799999999999, "text": " It's kind of reminiscent of Newton and Leibniz both inventing calculus simultaneously in the 17th century.", "tokens": [51017, 467, 311, 733, 295, 44304, 295, 19541, 293, 1456, 897, 77, 590, 1293, 7962, 278, 33400, 16561, 294, 264, 3282, 392, 4901, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2000982165336609, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.981060931618983e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 90304, "start": 923.12, "end": 923.9, "text": " Oh, right, yeah.", "tokens": [51369, 876, 11, 558, 11, 1338, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2000982165336609, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.981060931618983e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 90304, "start": 924.0, "end": 925.0999999999999, "text": " They weren't copying each other.", "tokens": [51413, 814, 4999, 380, 27976, 1184, 661, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2000982165336609, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.981060931618983e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 92510, "start": 925.1, "end": 933.0600000000001, "text": " However, the mathematical universe simply required that specific tool to be invented to understand the physics of motion, so they both found it from different angles.", "tokens": [50365, 2908, 11, 264, 18894, 6445, 2935, 4739, 300, 2685, 2290, 281, 312, 14479, 281, 1223, 264, 10649, 295, 5394, 11, 370, 436, 1293, 1352, 309, 490, 819, 14708, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 92510, "start": 933.36, "end": 934.36, "text": " That's a perfect comparison.", "tokens": [50778, 663, 311, 257, 2176, 9660, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 92510, "start": 934.94, "end": 939.32, "text": " However, Flicksheen doesn't just use Cox's framework as a glowing endorsement of theory.", "tokens": [50857, 2908, 11, 3235, 618, 9611, 268, 1177, 380, 445, 764, 41576, 311, 8388, 382, 257, 27064, 29228, 518, 295, 5261, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 92510, "start": 939.96, "end": 941.02, "text": " The paper pivots.", "tokens": [51108, 440, 3035, 280, 592, 1971, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 92510, "start": 941.16, "end": 941.66, "text": " Oh, yeah.", "tokens": [51168, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 92510, "start": 941.82, "end": 942.72, "text": " It definitely pivots.", "tokens": [51201, 467, 2138, 280, 592, 1971, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 92510, "start": 942.8000000000001, "end": 947.14, "text": " And it identifies one massive, potentially catastrophic blind spot in her framework.", "tokens": [51250, 400, 309, 34597, 472, 5994, 11, 7263, 34915, 6865, 4008, 294, 720, 8388, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 92510, "start": 947.46, "end": 952.0600000000001, "text": " And it's a blind spot shared by almost the entire global tech industry.", "tokens": [51483, 400, 309, 311, 257, 6865, 4008, 5507, 538, 1920, 264, 2302, 4338, 7553, 3518, 13, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14202895284700795, "compression_ratio": 1.6204620462046204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736825904888452e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 95206, "start": 952.06, "end": 958.6199999999999, "text": " It revolves around a fundamental misunderstanding of what it actually means to fix a broken system.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 47934, 926, 257, 8088, 29227, 295, 437, 309, 767, 1355, 281, 3191, 257, 5463, 1185, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 95206, "start": 959.02, "end": 959.2199999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50713, 1079, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 95206, "start": 959.4799999999999, "end": 965.5799999999999, "text": " The tech industry has a really bad habit of using terms like recovery, retraining, and rollback.", "tokens": [50736, 440, 7553, 3518, 575, 257, 534, 1578, 7164, 295, 1228, 2115, 411, 8597, 11, 49356, 1760, 11, 293, 3373, 3207, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 95206, "start": 966.04, "end": 967.18, "text": " Completely interchangeable.", "tokens": [51064, 39978, 30358, 712, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 95206, "start": 967.1999999999999, "end": 967.8399999999999, "text": " Oh, I've done it.", "tokens": [51122, 876, 11, 286, 600, 1096, 309, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 95206, "start": 967.88, "end": 968.66, "text": " We've all done it.", "tokens": [51156, 492, 600, 439, 1096, 309, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 95206, "start": 968.8399999999999, "end": 969.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51204, 1779, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 95206, "start": 969.4799999999999, "end": 976.68, "text": " When a server goes down or a model starts hallucinating, engineers will casually say, let's roll it back or let's trigger a system recovery.", "tokens": [51236, 1133, 257, 7154, 1709, 760, 420, 257, 2316, 3719, 35212, 8205, 11, 11955, 486, 34872, 584, 11, 718, 311, 3373, 309, 646, 420, 718, 311, 7875, 257, 1185, 8597, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 95206, "start": 976.8199999999999, "end": 977.9399999999999, "text": " Like they're the same thing.", "tokens": [51603, 1743, 436, 434, 264, 912, 551, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 95206, "start": 978.06, "end": 978.3599999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51665, 7587, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917440096537273, "compression_ratio": 1.5586206896551724, "no_speech_prob": 1.734688998347722e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 97836, "start": 978.36, "end": 985.92, "text": " But Flicksheen establishes a strict, unforgiving mathematical hierarchy that separates these concepts entirely.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 618, 9611, 268, 8327, 279, 257, 10910, 11, 31411, 15441, 18894, 22333, 300, 34149, 613, 10392, 7696, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12254385794362714, "compression_ratio": 1.6431372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.3349574267199071e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 97836, "start": 986.62, "end": 993.48, "text": " The paper states that rollback is merely a subset of reconstruction, and reconstruction is merely a subset of true repair.", "tokens": [50778, 440, 3035, 4368, 300, 3373, 3207, 307, 17003, 257, 25993, 295, 31565, 11, 293, 31565, 307, 17003, 257, 25993, 295, 2074, 10535, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12254385794362714, "compression_ratio": 1.6431372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.3349574267199071e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 97836, "start": 993.88, "end": 994.1, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51141, 1033, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12254385794362714, "compression_ratio": 1.6431372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.3349574267199071e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 97836, "start": 994.22, "end": 1001.76, "text": " We need to break these three distinct operations down carefully because the distinction changes how we handle every failure in a complex system.", "tokens": [51158, 492, 643, 281, 1821, 613, 1045, 10644, 7705, 760, 7500, 570, 264, 16844, 2962, 577, 321, 4813, 633, 7763, 294, 257, 3997, 1185, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12254385794362714, "compression_ratio": 1.6431372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.3349574267199071e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 97836, "start": 1002.04, "end": 1003.3000000000001, "text": " Let's start with rollback.", "tokens": [51549, 961, 311, 722, 365, 3373, 3207, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12254385794362714, "compression_ratio": 1.6431372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.3349574267199071e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 97836, "start": 1003.54, "end": 1003.82, "text": " Do it.", "tokens": [51624, 1144, 309, 13, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12254385794362714, "compression_ratio": 1.6431372549019607, "no_speech_prob": 1.3349574267199071e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 100382, "start": 1003.82, "end": 1008.36, "text": " In this framework, rollback is the narrowest, most superficial operation.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 8388, 11, 3373, 3207, 307, 264, 9432, 377, 11, 881, 34622, 6916, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11858784397946129, "compression_ratio": 1.5355648535564854, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007729859880305e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 100382, "start": 1008.5200000000001, "end": 1010.08, "text": " It simply restores an artifact.", "tokens": [50600, 467, 2935, 1472, 2706, 364, 34806, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11858784397946129, "compression_ratio": 1.5355648535564854, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007729859880305e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 100382, "start": 1010.7, "end": 1016.74, "text": " You are just fetching old parameter values from a version-controlled repository like GitHub or a server backup.", "tokens": [50709, 509, 366, 445, 23673, 278, 1331, 13075, 4190, 490, 257, 3037, 12, 49344, 25841, 411, 23331, 420, 257, 7154, 14807, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11858784397946129, "compression_ratio": 1.5355648535564854, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007729859880305e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 100382, "start": 1017.2600000000001, "end": 1025.92, "text": " You are taking the current corrupted weights of your AI model and replacing them with the saved weights from last Tuesday before the problem started.", "tokens": [51037, 509, 366, 1940, 264, 2190, 39480, 17443, 295, 428, 7318, 2316, 293, 19139, 552, 365, 264, 6624, 17443, 490, 1036, 10017, 949, 264, 1154, 1409, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11858784397946129, "compression_ratio": 1.5355648535564854, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007729859880305e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 102592, "start": 1025.92, "end": 1026.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072524157437411, "compression_ratio": 1.5341880341880343, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414771881496538e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 102592, "start": 1026.22, "end": 1034.5, "text": " It is fast, it is mechanical, and it requires absolutely no cognitive judgment about why the system actually failed in the first place.", "tokens": [50380, 467, 307, 2370, 11, 309, 307, 12070, 11, 293, 309, 7029, 3122, 572, 15605, 12216, 466, 983, 264, 1185, 767, 7612, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072524157437411, "compression_ratio": 1.5341880341880343, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414771881496538e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 102592, "start": 1034.5600000000002, "end": 1039.5800000000002, "text": " To use a video game analogy for you, the listener, rollback is just loading a saved game.", "tokens": [50797, 1407, 764, 257, 960, 1216, 21663, 337, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 3373, 3207, 307, 445, 15114, 257, 6624, 1216, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072524157437411, "compression_ratio": 1.5341880341880343, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414771881496538e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 102592, "start": 1040.02, "end": 1044.38, "text": " Your character walks into a room, gets instantly eliminated by a trap, and you hit reload.", "tokens": [51070, 2260, 2517, 12896, 666, 257, 1808, 11, 2170, 13518, 20308, 538, 257, 11487, 11, 293, 291, 2045, 25628, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072524157437411, "compression_ratio": 1.5341880341880343, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414771881496538e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 102592, "start": 1044.6200000000001, "end": 1045.72, "text": " You're just back at the checkpoint.", "tokens": [51300, 509, 434, 445, 646, 412, 264, 42269, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12072524157437411, "compression_ratio": 1.5341880341880343, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414771881496538e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 104572, "start": 1045.72, "end": 1046.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 104572, "start": 1046.72, "end": 1048.3, "text": " Back at the checkpoint outside the room.", "tokens": [50415, 5833, 412, 264, 42269, 2380, 264, 1808, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 104572, "start": 1048.72, "end": 1052.72, "text": " You haven't actually learned anything about the mechanics of the trap or why you failed.", "tokens": [50515, 509, 2378, 380, 767, 3264, 1340, 466, 264, 12939, 295, 264, 11487, 420, 983, 291, 7612, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 104572, "start": 1052.98, "end": 1056.14, "text": " You have simply reversed time a few minutes to a previous state.", "tokens": [50728, 509, 362, 2935, 30563, 565, 257, 1326, 2077, 281, 257, 3894, 1785, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 104572, "start": 1056.48, "end": 1057.72, "text": " That's a great way to think about it.", "tokens": [50903, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 519, 466, 309, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 104572, "start": 1057.92, "end": 1060.52, "text": " And moving up the hierarchy, we have reconstruction.", "tokens": [50975, 400, 2684, 493, 264, 22333, 11, 321, 362, 31565, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 104572, "start": 1060.94, "end": 1061.14, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51126, 1033, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 104572, "start": 1061.6200000000001, "end": 1062.1000000000001, "text": " Reconstruction.", "tokens": [51160, 1300, 25279, 3826, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 104572, "start": 1062.6200000000001, "end": 1064.88, "text": " Reconstruction is a much broader operation.", "tokens": [51210, 1300, 25279, 3826, 307, 257, 709, 13227, 6916, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2507734599866365, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381165529264717e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 106488, "start": 1064.88, "end": 1069.42, "text": " It attempts to restore an entire state rather than just fetching an old artifact.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 15257, 281, 15227, 364, 2302, 1785, 2831, 813, 445, 23673, 278, 364, 1331, 34806, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 106488, "start": 1069.8400000000001, "end": 1072.2, "text": " We're not just downloading the old weights.", "tokens": [50613, 492, 434, 406, 445, 32529, 264, 1331, 17443, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 106488, "start": 1072.48, "end": 1082.18, "text": " You are actively retraining the model against the specific historical data and pipeline configuration that originally produced that old artifact.", "tokens": [50745, 509, 366, 13022, 49356, 1760, 264, 2316, 1970, 264, 2685, 8584, 1412, 293, 15517, 11694, 300, 7993, 7126, 300, 1331, 34806, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 106488, "start": 1082.42, "end": 1082.5600000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51242, 1033, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 106488, "start": 1082.64, "end": 1083.68, "text": " So you're re-deriving it.", "tokens": [51253, 407, 291, 434, 319, 12, 1068, 2123, 309, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 106488, "start": 1083.8600000000001, "end": 1084.2, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51314, 7587, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 106488, "start": 1084.3400000000001, "end": 1087.2, "text": " You are re-deriving the state from scratch to prove you can get back there.", "tokens": [51338, 509, 366, 319, 12, 1068, 2123, 264, 1785, 490, 8459, 281, 7081, 291, 393, 483, 646, 456, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 106488, "start": 1087.3400000000001, "end": 1087.5400000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51488, 1033, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 106488, "start": 1087.64, "end": 1092.44, "text": " Returning to the video game analogy, reconstruction is not just loading the save file.", "tokens": [51503, 11495, 10656, 281, 264, 960, 1216, 21663, 11, 31565, 307, 406, 445, 15114, 264, 3155, 3991, 13, 51743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1492947798508864, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.694506622691716e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 109244, "start": 1092.44, "end": 1103.66, "text": " It is replaying the entire level flawlessly up to that exact checkpoint to ensure you possess all the same inventory items, health points, and positional advantages.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 23836, 278, 264, 2302, 1496, 13717, 12048, 493, 281, 300, 1900, 42269, 281, 5586, 291, 17490, 439, 264, 912, 14228, 4754, 11, 1585, 2793, 11, 293, 2535, 304, 14906, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 109244, "start": 1104.04, "end": 1107.18, "text": " You are proving the mechanics of getting there are still viable.", "tokens": [50945, 509, 366, 27221, 264, 12939, 295, 1242, 456, 366, 920, 22024, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 109244, "start": 1107.3400000000001, "end": 1107.7, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51110, 7587, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 109244, "start": 1107.9, "end": 1109.5, "text": " You proved you can walk the path again.", "tokens": [51138, 509, 14617, 291, 393, 1792, 264, 3100, 797, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 109244, "start": 1109.6200000000001, "end": 1109.8200000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51224, 1779, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 109244, "start": 1110.0, "end": 1114.22, "text": " And that brings us to the apex of the hierarchy, the most demanding operation.", "tokens": [51243, 400, 300, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 48115, 295, 264, 22333, 11, 264, 881, 19960, 6916, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 109244, "start": 1114.76, "end": 1115.28, "text": " Repair.", "tokens": [51481, 3696, 1246, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 109244, "start": 1115.5, "end": 1116.3600000000001, "text": " Repair, yes.", "tokens": [51518, 3696, 1246, 11, 2086, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 109244, "start": 1116.4, "end": 1120.78, "text": " Repair is the only operation that restores admissibility to the history itself.", "tokens": [51563, 3696, 1246, 307, 264, 787, 6916, 300, 1472, 2706, 5910, 891, 2841, 281, 264, 2503, 2564, 13, 51782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 109244, "start": 1120.8400000000001, "end": 1121.8, "text": " This is the crucial part.", "tokens": [51785, 639, 307, 264, 11462, 644, 13, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632534057374984, "compression_ratio": 1.696551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671656680704693e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 112180, "start": 1121.8, "end": 1130.1399999999999, "text": " It is a highly constrained transformation that diagnoses and fixes the root compromise while preserving the core structures of the system.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 5405, 38901, 9887, 300, 7234, 4201, 293, 32539, 264, 5593, 18577, 1339, 33173, 264, 4965, 9227, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07750685421037085, "compression_ratio": 1.6902654867256637, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579860736224086e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 112180, "start": 1130.32, "end": 1134.1599999999999, "text": " Repair is not loading a save, and it is not replaying the level.", "tokens": [50791, 3696, 1246, 307, 406, 15114, 257, 3155, 11, 293, 309, 307, 406, 23836, 278, 264, 1496, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07750685421037085, "compression_ratio": 1.6902654867256637, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579860736224086e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 112180, "start": 1134.78, "end": 1143.3799999999999, "text": " Repair is opening the game's actual source code and fixing the underlying software glitch that caused your character to fall through the geometry of the floor in the first place.", "tokens": [51014, 3696, 1246, 307, 5193, 264, 1216, 311, 3539, 4009, 3089, 293, 19442, 264, 14217, 4722, 23552, 300, 7008, 428, 2517, 281, 2100, 807, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 4123, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07750685421037085, "compression_ratio": 1.6902654867256637, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579860736224086e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 114338, "start": 1143.38, "end": 1151.72, "text": " And this is exactly where Cox's blind spot and, really, the wider industry's blind spot becomes incredibly dangerous.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 2293, 689, 41576, 311, 6865, 4008, 293, 11, 534, 11, 264, 11842, 3518, 311, 6865, 4008, 3643, 6252, 5795, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28154001430589326, "compression_ratio": 1.4391891891891893, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803403029265e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 114338, "start": 1151.72, "end": 1153.68, "text": " Because they just reconstruct.", "tokens": [50782, 1436, 436, 445, 31499, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28154001430589326, "compression_ratio": 1.4391891891891893, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803403029265e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 114338, "start": 1154.0600000000002, "end": 1154.24, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50899, 1079, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28154001430589326, "compression_ratio": 1.4391891891891893, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803403029265e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 114338, "start": 1154.7800000000002, "end": 1158.16, "text": " Cox's framework relies heavily on automated reconstruction.", "tokens": [50935, 41576, 311, 8388, 30910, 10950, 322, 18473, 31565, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28154001430589326, "compression_ratio": 1.4391891891891893, "no_speech_prob": 1.89803403029265e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 115816, "start": 1158.16, "end": 1164.1200000000001, "text": " When an anomaly is detected, her system triggers a retraining protocol from a validated baseline.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 364, 42737, 307, 21896, 11, 720, 1185, 22827, 257, 49356, 1760, 10336, 490, 257, 40693, 20518, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17378675020658052, "compression_ratio": 1.2300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740089496006e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 115816, "start": 1164.38, "end": 1165.5, "text": " Which sounds good on paper.", "tokens": [50676, 3013, 3263, 665, 322, 3035, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17378675020658052, "compression_ratio": 1.2300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740089496006e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 115816, "start": 1165.7, "end": 1166.2, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50742, 467, 775, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17378675020658052, "compression_ratio": 1.2300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740089496006e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 115816, "start": 1166.68, "end": 1166.88, "text": " Hmm.", "tokens": [50791, 8239, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17378675020658052, "compression_ratio": 1.2300884955752212, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740089496006e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 116688, "start": 1166.88, "end": 1171.8200000000002, "text": " But consider a scenario where a system is compromised via an active, ongoing pipeline vulnerability.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1949, 257, 9005, 689, 257, 1185, 307, 32463, 5766, 364, 4967, 11, 10452, 15517, 24210, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577737746700163, "compression_ratio": 1.5984555984555984, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980364155374296e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 116688, "start": 1172.5400000000002, "end": 1177.3200000000002, "text": " Like, imagine a malicious data scraper is injected into the data ingestion pipeline.", "tokens": [50648, 1743, 11, 3811, 257, 33496, 1412, 13943, 610, 307, 36967, 666, 264, 1412, 3957, 31342, 15517, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577737746700163, "compression_ratio": 1.5984555984555984, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980364155374296e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 116688, "start": 1177.48, "end": 1177.72, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50895, 1033, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577737746700163, "compression_ratio": 1.5984555984555984, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980364155374296e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 116688, "start": 1177.8400000000001, "end": 1180.8000000000002, "text": " So it's silently feeding poison data into the training pool.", "tokens": [50913, 407, 309, 311, 40087, 12919, 10836, 1412, 666, 264, 3097, 7005, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577737746700163, "compression_ratio": 1.5984555984555984, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980364155374296e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 116688, "start": 1180.92, "end": 1181.22, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51067, 7587, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577737746700163, "compression_ratio": 1.5984555984555984, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980364155374296e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 116688, "start": 1181.22, "end": 1189.3600000000001, "text": " If you simply reconstruct the system by deleting the current model and retraining it from last week's baseline, you have not actually fixed the problem.", "tokens": [51082, 759, 291, 2935, 31499, 264, 1185, 538, 48946, 264, 2190, 2316, 293, 49356, 1760, 309, 490, 1036, 1243, 311, 20518, 11, 291, 362, 406, 767, 6806, 264, 1154, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577737746700163, "compression_ratio": 1.5984555984555984, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980364155374296e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 118936, "start": 1189.36, "end": 1192.86, "text": " You are simply returning the system to the mouth of the exact same trap.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 2935, 12678, 264, 1185, 281, 264, 4525, 295, 264, 1900, 912, 11487, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17088402758587848, "compression_ratio": 1.624, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750118002686887e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 118936, "start": 1193.1999999999998, "end": 1193.4799999999998, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50557, 1079, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17088402758587848, "compression_ratio": 1.624, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750118002686887e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 118936, "start": 1194.1599999999999, "end": 1196.6599999999999, "text": " The malicious data scraper is still running in the background.", "tokens": [50605, 440, 33496, 1412, 13943, 610, 307, 920, 2614, 294, 264, 3678, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17088402758587848, "compression_ratio": 1.624, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750118002686887e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 118936, "start": 1197.7199999999998, "end": 1202.4399999999998, "text": " The history just resumes its forward motion on the exact same compromised path.", "tokens": [50783, 440, 2503, 445, 48068, 1080, 2128, 5394, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 32463, 3100, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17088402758587848, "compression_ratio": 1.624, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750118002686887e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 118936, "start": 1202.74, "end": 1203.1399999999999, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51034, 3153, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17088402758587848, "compression_ratio": 1.624, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750118002686887e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 118936, "start": 1203.4199999999998, "end": 1206.1999999999998, "text": " True repair requires a preservation constraint.", "tokens": [51068, 13587, 10535, 7029, 257, 27257, 25534, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17088402758587848, "compression_ratio": 1.624, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750118002686887e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 118936, "start": 1206.82, "end": 1214.26, "text": " You must ensure the mechanism of departure, the vulnerability that allowed the attacker in, is diagnosed and permanently closed off.", "tokens": [51238, 509, 1633, 5586, 264, 7513, 295, 25866, 11, 264, 24210, 300, 4350, 264, 35871, 294, 11, 307, 16899, 293, 24042, 5395, 766, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17088402758587848, "compression_ratio": 1.624, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750118002686887e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 121426, "start": 1214.26, "end": 1221.44, "text": " If you do not close the mechanism, the forward trajectory of the history becomes inadmissible the second you hit deploy again.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 360, 406, 1998, 264, 7513, 11, 264, 2128, 21512, 295, 264, 2503, 3643, 42148, 76, 41073, 264, 1150, 291, 2045, 7274, 797, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 121426, "start": 1221.54, "end": 1221.96, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50729, 7587, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 121426, "start": 1222.46, "end": 1225.82, "text": " It is a profound shift in perspective regarding incident response.", "tokens": [50775, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 5513, 294, 4585, 8595, 9348, 4134, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 121426, "start": 1225.94, "end": 1226.04, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50949, 865, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 121426, "start": 1226.16, "end": 1233.02, "text": " If you just roll back or reconstruct, your quote unquote fix is nothing more than hitting the reset button on a time bomb.", "tokens": [50960, 759, 291, 445, 3373, 646, 420, 31499, 11, 428, 6513, 37557, 3191, 307, 1825, 544, 813, 8850, 264, 14322, 2960, 322, 257, 565, 7851, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 121426, "start": 1233.04, "end": 1234.78, "text": " A reset button on a time bomb.", "tokens": [51304, 316, 14322, 2960, 322, 257, 565, 7851, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 121426, "start": 1235.0, "end": 1235.22, "text": " Man.", "tokens": [51402, 2458, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 121426, "start": 1235.42, "end": 1238.74, "text": " To truly repair a system, you have to close off the attacker's path.", "tokens": [51423, 1407, 4908, 10535, 257, 1185, 11, 291, 362, 281, 1998, 766, 264, 35871, 311, 3100, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673031378229824, "compression_ratio": 1.6390977443609023, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851490223326556e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 123874, "start": 1238.74, "end": 1244.5, "text": " And this requires us to completely rethink what an attack actually looks like within this historical framework.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 7029, 505, 281, 2584, 34595, 437, 364, 2690, 767, 1542, 411, 1951, 341, 8584, 8388, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 123874, "start": 1244.72, "end": 1245.16, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50664, 467, 775, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 123874, "start": 1245.38, "end": 1248.74, "text": " Flixian shifts the paper into redefining the very nature of hacking.", "tokens": [50697, 3235, 970, 952, 19201, 264, 3035, 666, 38818, 1760, 264, 588, 3687, 295, 31422, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 123874, "start": 1249.36, "end": 1253.68, "text": " Traditionally, security frameworks view attacks as a static Boolean checklist.", "tokens": [50896, 22017, 15899, 11, 3825, 29834, 1910, 8122, 382, 257, 13437, 23351, 28499, 30357, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 123874, "start": 1253.94, "end": 1256.56, "text": " It is a series of strict and or logic baits.", "tokens": [51125, 467, 307, 257, 2638, 295, 10910, 293, 420, 9952, 16865, 82, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 123874, "start": 1256.56, "end": 1256.7, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51256, 1779, 13, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 123874, "start": 1256.72, "end": 1257.72, "text": " Like a literal checklist.", "tokens": [51264, 1743, 257, 20411, 30357, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 123874, "start": 1257.84, "end": 1257.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51320, 1779, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 123874, "start": 1258.22, "end": 1258.7, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51339, 7587, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 123874, "start": 1258.7, "end": 1261.68, "text": " The auditor asks, you know, does the attacker have access?", "tokens": [51363, 440, 33970, 8962, 11, 291, 458, 11, 775, 264, 35871, 362, 2105, 30, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 123874, "start": 1262.4, "end": 1265.1, "text": " And D, do they have the requisite knowledge of the system?", "tokens": [51548, 400, 413, 11, 360, 436, 362, 264, 49878, 642, 3601, 295, 264, 1185, 30, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 123874, "start": 1265.46, "end": 1267.4, "text": " And do they possess the technical capability?", "tokens": [51701, 400, 360, 436, 17490, 264, 6191, 13759, 30, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20188533726023206, "compression_ratio": 1.66984126984127, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683234213195954e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 126740, "start": 1267.4, "end": 1270.24, "text": " And is there a measurable impact?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 307, 456, 257, 43615, 2712, 30, 50507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 126740, "start": 1270.5600000000002, "end": 1274.0600000000002, "text": " It is a static list of conditions that must be satisfied.", "tokens": [50523, 467, 307, 257, 13437, 1329, 295, 4487, 300, 1633, 312, 11239, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 126740, "start": 1274.44, "end": 1276.8400000000001, "text": " Infliction just discards the checklist entirely.", "tokens": [50717, 682, 3423, 4105, 445, 2983, 2287, 264, 30357, 7696, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 126740, "start": 1277.0400000000002, "end": 1277.6000000000001, "text": " Throws it out.", "tokens": [50847, 334, 28251, 309, 484, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 126740, "start": 1277.72, "end": 1277.9, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50881, 865, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 126740, "start": 1278.0, "end": 1280.0400000000002, "text": " And redefines an attack geometrically.", "tokens": [50895, 400, 38818, 1652, 364, 2690, 12956, 81, 984, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 126740, "start": 1280.68, "end": 1285.7, "text": " In the language of system histories, an attack is the successful traversal of a trajectory.", "tokens": [51029, 682, 264, 2856, 295, 1185, 30631, 11, 364, 2690, 307, 264, 4406, 23149, 304, 295, 257, 21512, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 126740, "start": 1285.9, "end": 1286.52, "text": " A trajectory.", "tokens": [51290, 316, 21512, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 126740, "start": 1286.9, "end": 1287.14, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51340, 1079, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 126740, "start": 1287.24, "end": 1292.7800000000002, "text": " It is the movement from an admissible safe history into an inadmissible compromised one.", "tokens": [51357, 467, 307, 264, 3963, 490, 364, 5910, 41073, 3273, 2503, 666, 364, 42148, 76, 41073, 32463, 472, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1915217328954626, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414797902348678e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 129278, "start": 1292.78, "end": 1297.8999999999999, "text": " It is about navigating through a multidimensional space of possibilities over time.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 466, 32054, 807, 257, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 1901, 295, 12178, 670, 565, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1397371706755265, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 2.0402657428114646e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 129278, "start": 1298.04, "end": 1302.94, "text": " To visualize this, I think we have to discard the idea of a hacker trying to pick a single lock on a front door.", "tokens": [50628, 1407, 23273, 341, 11, 286, 519, 321, 362, 281, 31597, 264, 1558, 295, 257, 38155, 1382, 281, 1888, 257, 2167, 4017, 322, 257, 1868, 2853, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1397371706755265, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 2.0402657428114646e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 129278, "start": 1303.06, "end": 1303.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50879, 1779, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1397371706755265, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 2.0402657428114646e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 129278, "start": 1303.28, "end": 1303.8, "text": " That's too simple.", "tokens": [50890, 663, 311, 886, 2199, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1397371706755265, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 2.0402657428114646e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 129278, "start": 1303.94, "end": 1310.62, "text": " Imagine instead an attacker trying to navigate a massive subterranean cave system to reach a vault deep underground.", "tokens": [50923, 11739, 2602, 364, 35871, 1382, 281, 12350, 257, 5994, 1422, 391, 24584, 11730, 1185, 281, 2524, 257, 27134, 2452, 14977, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1397371706755265, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 2.0402657428114646e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 129278, "start": 1311.22, "end": 1313.1399999999999, "text": " The cave system is the network architecture.", "tokens": [51287, 440, 11730, 1185, 307, 264, 3209, 9482, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1397371706755265, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 2.0402657428114646e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 131314, "start": 1313.14, "end": 1317.7, "text": " To understand this navigation, the paper breaks down the concept of reachability.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 1223, 341, 17346, 11, 264, 3035, 9857, 760, 264, 3410, 295, 2524, 2310, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1987734415444983, "compression_ratio": 1.6288209606986899, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547626763106394e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 131314, "start": 1317.8400000000001, "end": 1318.5800000000002, "text": " Reachability, yeah.", "tokens": [50600, 35904, 2310, 11, 1338, 13, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1987734415444983, "compression_ratio": 1.6288209606986899, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547626763106394e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 131314, "start": 1318.6200000000001, "end": 1321.68, "text": " And it separates it into two drastically different categories.", "tokens": [50639, 400, 309, 34149, 309, 666, 732, 29673, 819, 10479, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1987734415444983, "compression_ratio": 1.6288209606986899, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547626763106394e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 131314, "start": 1322.16, "end": 1325.0600000000002, "text": " Nominal reachability and effective reachability.", "tokens": [50816, 31272, 2071, 2524, 2310, 293, 4942, 2524, 2310, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1987734415444983, "compression_ratio": 1.6288209606986899, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547626763106394e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 131314, "start": 1325.3400000000001, "end": 1327.0800000000002, "text": " Let's start with nominal reachability.", "tokens": [50975, 961, 311, 722, 365, 41641, 2524, 2310, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1987734415444983, "compression_ratio": 1.6288209606986899, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547626763106394e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 131314, "start": 1328.0800000000002, "end": 1335.0200000000002, "text": " It encompasses every single trajectory that is technically possible given the attacker's raw access and knowledge.", "tokens": [51112, 467, 49866, 633, 2167, 21512, 300, 307, 12120, 1944, 2212, 264, 35871, 311, 8936, 2105, 293, 3601, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1987734415444983, "compression_ratio": 1.6288209606986899, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547626763106394e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 131314, "start": 1335.22, "end": 1335.5600000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51469, 1033, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1987734415444983, "compression_ratio": 1.6288209606986899, "no_speech_prob": 1.7547626763106394e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 133556, "start": 1335.56, "end": 1344.82, "text": " Looking at a map of the cave system, nominal reachability includes every single tunnel, fissure, and underground river that physically connects the entrance to the vault.", "tokens": [50365, 11053, 412, 257, 4471, 295, 264, 11730, 1185, 11, 41641, 2524, 2310, 5974, 633, 2167, 13186, 11, 283, 891, 540, 11, 293, 14977, 6810, 300, 9762, 16967, 264, 12014, 281, 264, 27134, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783612807591757, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 2.289091008758626e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 133556, "start": 1344.96, "end": 1353.2, "text": " So, if an attacker has stolen administrative credential, nominally, they have the power to instantly delete the entire production database.", "tokens": [50835, 407, 11, 498, 364, 35871, 575, 15900, 17900, 22034, 11, 5369, 19801, 11, 436, 362, 264, 1347, 281, 13518, 12097, 264, 2302, 4265, 8149, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783612807591757, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 2.289091008758626e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 133556, "start": 1353.36, "end": 1354.1599999999999, "text": " Technically, yes.", "tokens": [51255, 42494, 11, 2086, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783612807591757, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 2.289091008758626e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 133556, "start": 1354.46, "end": 1357.78, "text": " But the attacker rarely takes the most direct nominal path.", "tokens": [51310, 583, 264, 35871, 13752, 2516, 264, 881, 2047, 41641, 3100, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783612807591757, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 2.289091008758626e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 133556, "start": 1358.0, "end": 1358.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51487, 1779, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783612807591757, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 2.289091008758626e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 133556, "start": 1358.84, "end": 1360.82, "text": " Because they are constrained by reality.", "tokens": [51529, 1436, 436, 366, 38901, 538, 4103, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12783612807591757, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 2.289091008758626e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 136082, "start": 1360.82, "end": 1373.78, "text": " If they just nuke the database, massive klaxons go off, the security operations center is instantly alerted, their stolen access is revoked within seconds, and the attack is over before they can extract the intellectual property they actually wanted.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 436, 445, 3822, 330, 264, 8149, 11, 5994, 350, 25923, 892, 352, 766, 11, 264, 3825, 7705, 3056, 307, 13518, 9615, 292, 11, 641, 15900, 2105, 307, 3698, 9511, 1951, 3949, 11, 293, 264, 2690, 307, 670, 949, 436, 393, 8947, 264, 12576, 4707, 436, 767, 1415, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1389951505159077, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.734958964688671e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 136082, "start": 1373.8999999999999, "end": 1374.3799999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51019, 7587, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1389951505159077, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.734958964688671e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 136082, "start": 1375.0, "end": 1377.56, "text": " The most direct path is suicidal to their mission.", "tokens": [51074, 440, 881, 2047, 3100, 307, 43243, 281, 641, 4447, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1389951505159077, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.734958964688671e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 136082, "start": 1377.9199999999998, "end": 1378.1399999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51220, 1779, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1389951505159077, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.734958964688671e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 136082, "start": 1378.4199999999998, "end": 1381.08, "text": " And that reality introduces effective reachability.", "tokens": [51245, 400, 300, 4103, 31472, 4942, 2524, 2310, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1389951505159077, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.734958964688671e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 136082, "start": 1381.5, "end": 1383.48, "text": " Denoted in the paper is gamma sub f.", "tokens": [51399, 6458, 23325, 294, 264, 3035, 307, 15546, 1422, 283, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1389951505159077, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.734958964688671e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 138348, "start": 1383.48, "end": 1391.14, "text": " Effective reachability is the heavily restricted subset of paths an attacker can actually take while maintaining their own operational continuity.", "tokens": [50365, 17764, 488, 2524, 2310, 307, 264, 10950, 20608, 25993, 295, 14518, 364, 35871, 393, 767, 747, 1339, 14916, 641, 1065, 16607, 23807, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11181913677014803, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279318167279234e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 138348, "start": 1391.42, "end": 1404.3600000000001, "text": " These are the paths where they do not trigger detection algorithms, they do not lose their initial foothold in the network, and they do not break the very tools or exploits they are relying on to move laterally.", "tokens": [50762, 1981, 366, 264, 14518, 689, 436, 360, 406, 7875, 17784, 14642, 11, 436, 360, 406, 3624, 641, 5883, 726, 900, 2641, 294, 264, 3209, 11, 293, 436, 360, 406, 1821, 264, 588, 3873, 420, 12382, 1208, 436, 366, 24140, 322, 281, 1286, 1780, 379, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11181913677014803, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279318167279234e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 138348, "start": 1404.48, "end": 1409.1, "text": " Because an attacker is severely constrained by their own desperate need to remain hidden.", "tokens": [51415, 1436, 364, 35871, 307, 26271, 38901, 538, 641, 1065, 17601, 643, 281, 6222, 7633, 13, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11181913677014803, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279318167279234e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 138348, "start": 1409.24, "end": 1409.68, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51653, 7587, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11181913677014803, "compression_ratio": 1.6988847583643123, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279318167279234e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 140968, "start": 1409.68, "end": 1423.5600000000002, "text": " Returning to the cave analogy, effective reachability only includes the tunnels that are not flooded, the passages that don't require heavy explosives that would elute the guards on the surface, and the routes that actually have enough oxygen to survive the journey.", "tokens": [50365, 11495, 10656, 281, 264, 11730, 21663, 11, 4942, 2524, 2310, 787, 5974, 264, 30804, 300, 366, 406, 31594, 11, 264, 31589, 300, 500, 380, 3651, 4676, 46421, 300, 576, 806, 1169, 264, 17652, 322, 264, 3753, 11, 293, 264, 18242, 300, 767, 362, 1547, 9169, 281, 7867, 264, 4671, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10832085229654227, "compression_ratio": 1.6927899686520376, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528973908115702e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 140968, "start": 1423.5600000000002, "end": 1425.3600000000001, "text": " That makes so much sense.", "tokens": [51059, 663, 1669, 370, 709, 2020, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10832085229654227, "compression_ratio": 1.6927899686520376, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528973908115702e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 140968, "start": 1425.5800000000002, "end": 1430.3600000000001, "text": " And understanding this geometry completely changes the game for the person defending the system.", "tokens": [51160, 400, 3701, 341, 18426, 2584, 2962, 264, 1216, 337, 264, 954, 21377, 264, 1185, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10832085229654227, "compression_ratio": 1.6927899686520376, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528973908115702e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 140968, "start": 1430.68, "end": 1437.04, "text": " Because if a network defender only looks at nominal reachability, securing a system feels completely impossible.", "tokens": [51415, 1436, 498, 257, 3209, 26537, 787, 1542, 412, 41641, 2524, 2310, 11, 33640, 257, 1185, 3417, 2584, 6243, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10832085229654227, "compression_ratio": 1.6927899686520376, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528973908115702e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 140968, "start": 1437.3600000000001, "end": 1438.3400000000001, "text": " Oh, it's totally overwhelming.", "tokens": [51749, 876, 11, 309, 311, 3879, 13373, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10832085229654227, "compression_ratio": 1.6927899686520376, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528973908115702e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 140968, "start": 1438.5600000000002, "end": 1438.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51809, 1779, 13, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10832085229654227, "compression_ratio": 1.6927899686520376, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528973908115702e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 143878, "start": 1438.78, "end": 1447.1399999999999, "text": " There are millions of technical vulnerabilities, thousands of outdated endpoints, and millions of possible actions an attacker could theoretically take.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 366, 6803, 295, 6191, 37633, 11, 5383, 295, 36313, 917, 20552, 11, 293, 6803, 295, 1944, 5909, 364, 35871, 727, 29400, 747, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 143878, "start": 1447.32, "end": 1451.22, "text": " You cannot patch every single hole in a massive corporate network.", "tokens": [50792, 509, 2644, 9972, 633, 2167, 5458, 294, 257, 5994, 10896, 3209, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 143878, "start": 1451.36, "end": 1452.1399999999999, "text": " You just can't.", "tokens": [50994, 509, 445, 393, 380, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 143878, "start": 1452.28, "end": 1457.0, "text": " And Fliction argues a defender doesn't need to secure every possible nominal vulnerability.", "tokens": [51040, 400, 3235, 4105, 38218, 257, 26537, 1177, 380, 643, 281, 7144, 633, 1944, 41641, 24210, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 143878, "start": 1457.22, "end": 1458.3999999999999, "text": " Okay, this is the big shift.", "tokens": [51287, 1033, 11, 341, 307, 264, 955, 5513, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 143878, "start": 1458.72, "end": 1458.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51362, 1779, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 143878, "start": 1459.66, "end": 1467.12, "text": " The defender's mathematically optimal strategy is simply to eliminate the intersection between effective reachability and impact.", "tokens": [51409, 440, 26537, 311, 44003, 16252, 5206, 307, 2935, 281, 13819, 264, 15236, 1296, 4942, 2524, 2310, 293, 2712, 13, 51782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 143878, "start": 1467.42, "end": 1468.6399999999999, "text": " Eliminate the intersection.", "tokens": [51797, 2699, 4395, 473, 264, 15236, 13, 51858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14014202464710582, "compression_ratio": 1.7366666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.668646340893809e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 146864, "start": 1468.64, "end": 1469.0800000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16558074951171875, "compression_ratio": 1.5809523809523809, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 146864, "start": 1469.0800000000002, "end": 1472.0200000000002, "text": " You don't have to block every single tunnel in the cave.", "tokens": [50387, 509, 500, 380, 362, 281, 3461, 633, 2167, 13186, 294, 264, 11730, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16558074951171875, "compression_ratio": 1.5809523809523809, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 146864, "start": 1472.38, "end": 1482.16, "text": " You only have to collapse the specific, narrow bottlenecks that the attacker must practically travel through to remain undetected while reaching their objective.", "tokens": [50552, 509, 787, 362, 281, 15584, 264, 2685, 11, 9432, 44641, 2761, 300, 264, 35871, 1633, 15667, 3147, 807, 281, 6222, 674, 302, 39963, 1339, 9906, 641, 10024, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16558074951171875, "compression_ratio": 1.5809523809523809, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 146864, "start": 1482.68, "end": 1488.46, "text": " So, if you sever the route that connects their starting point to the inadmissible outcome, you win.", "tokens": [51067, 407, 11, 498, 291, 2802, 264, 7955, 300, 16967, 641, 2891, 935, 281, 264, 42148, 76, 41073, 9700, 11, 291, 1942, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16558074951171875, "compression_ratio": 1.5809523809523809, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 146864, "start": 1488.6200000000001, "end": 1489.1000000000001, "text": " You win.", "tokens": [51364, 509, 1942, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16558074951171875, "compression_ratio": 1.5809523809523809, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 148910, "start": 1489.1, "end": 1496.8999999999999, "text": " You have successfully defended the entire system, even if thousands of other nominal vulnerabilities still exist on the periphery.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 10727, 34135, 264, 2302, 1185, 11, 754, 498, 5383, 295, 661, 41641, 37633, 920, 2514, 322, 264, 26807, 88, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08863261438185169, "compression_ratio": 1.528888888888889, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011421568277618e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 148910, "start": 1496.8999999999999, "end": 1509.74, "text": " It transforms network security from an overwhelming, impossible task of perfectly sealing an infinite fortress into a highly strategic game of simply cutting the specific bridges the enemy actually needs to cross.", "tokens": [50755, 467, 35592, 3209, 3825, 490, 364, 13373, 11, 6243, 5633, 295, 6239, 48678, 364, 13785, 31826, 666, 257, 5405, 10924, 1216, 295, 2935, 6492, 264, 2685, 21114, 264, 5945, 767, 2203, 281, 3278, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08863261438185169, "compression_ratio": 1.528888888888889, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011421568277618e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 150974, "start": 1509.74, "end": 1510.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.194401723688299, "compression_ratio": 1.42, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602957274268308e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 150974, "start": 1510.6, "end": 1512.78, "text": " It's so much more manageable when you look at it that way.", "tokens": [50408, 467, 311, 370, 709, 544, 38798, 562, 291, 574, 412, 309, 300, 636, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.194401723688299, "compression_ratio": 1.42, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602957274268308e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 150974, "start": 1512.82, "end": 1513.48, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50519, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.194401723688299, "compression_ratio": 1.42, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602957274268308e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 150974, "start": 1513.92, "end": 1520.24, "text": " So, we have established that trust is about maintaining an admissible trajectory, and defense is about blocking inadmissible paths.", "tokens": [50574, 407, 11, 321, 362, 7545, 300, 3361, 307, 466, 14916, 364, 5910, 41073, 21512, 11, 293, 7654, 307, 466, 17776, 42148, 76, 41073, 14518, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.194401723688299, "compression_ratio": 1.42, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602957274268308e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 152024, "start": 1520.24, "end": 1520.68, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26034938267299107, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 2.084272207950044e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 152024, "start": 1520.68, "end": 1524.36, "text": " But this circles back to the massive logistical problem we discussed earlier.", "tokens": [50387, 583, 341, 13040, 646, 281, 264, 5994, 3565, 42686, 1154, 321, 7152, 3071, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26034938267299107, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 2.084272207950044e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 152024, "start": 1524.42, "end": 1524.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50574, 1779, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26034938267299107, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 2.084272207950044e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 152024, "start": 1524.68, "end": 1525.86, "text": " The unobservable history.", "tokens": [50587, 440, 8526, 929, 1978, 712, 2503, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26034938267299107, "compression_ratio": 1.1386138613861385, "no_speech_prob": 2.084272207950044e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 152586, "start": 1525.86, "end": 1526.54, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707706942416654, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.721603111806691e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 152586, "start": 1527.1799999999998, "end": 1531.2199999999998, "text": " All of this elegant math relies on knowing the history of the system.", "tokens": [50431, 1057, 295, 341, 21117, 5221, 30910, 322, 5276, 264, 2503, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707706942416654, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.721603111806691e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 152586, "start": 1532.02, "end": 1542.06, "text": " How do you definitively prove to an outside auditor, a government regulator, or a skeptical customer that your invisible, unobservable history is actually clean?", "tokens": [50673, 1012, 360, 291, 28152, 356, 7081, 281, 364, 2380, 33970, 11, 257, 2463, 36250, 11, 420, 257, 28601, 5474, 300, 428, 14603, 11, 8526, 929, 1978, 712, 2503, 307, 767, 2541, 30, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707706942416654, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.721603111806691e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 152586, "start": 1542.56, "end": 1546.8799999999999, "text": " And this brings us to the centerpiece of the paper, the title object itself.", "tokens": [51200, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 3056, 15281, 295, 264, 3035, 11, 264, 4876, 2657, 2564, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707706942416654, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.721603111806691e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 152586, "start": 1547.06, "end": 1548.32, "text": " The admissibility certificate.", "tokens": [51425, 440, 5910, 891, 2841, 15953, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707706942416654, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.721603111806691e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 152586, "start": 1548.4199999999998, "end": 1552.4599999999998, "text": " The admissibility certificate, mathematically denoted as C sub-sigma.", "tokens": [51493, 440, 5910, 891, 2841, 15953, 11, 44003, 1441, 23325, 382, 383, 1422, 12, 82, 16150, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14707706942416654, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.721603111806691e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 155246, "start": 1552.46, "end": 1556.18, "text": " The certificate is a structured, highly versioned body of evidence.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15953, 307, 257, 18519, 11, 5405, 3037, 292, 1772, 295, 4467, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 155246, "start": 1556.3600000000001, "end": 1556.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50560, 1779, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 155246, "start": 1556.78, "end": 1565.0, "text": " It is the definitive proof that the history is admissible without requiring the auditor to literally travel back in time and observe the entire history themselves.", "tokens": [50581, 467, 307, 264, 28152, 8177, 300, 264, 2503, 307, 5910, 41073, 1553, 24165, 264, 33970, 281, 3736, 3147, 646, 294, 565, 293, 11441, 264, 2302, 2503, 2969, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 155246, "start": 1565.58, "end": 1569.28, "text": " It is the physical or digital manifestation of the system's past.", "tokens": [51021, 467, 307, 264, 4001, 420, 4562, 29550, 295, 264, 1185, 311, 1791, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 155246, "start": 1569.54, "end": 1575.16, "text": " And Flitchin provides a minimal decomposition of what this certificate must legally and mathematically include.", "tokens": [51219, 400, 3235, 1549, 259, 6417, 257, 13206, 48356, 295, 437, 341, 15953, 1633, 21106, 293, 44003, 4090, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 155246, "start": 1575.44, "end": 1577.18, "text": " It is a rigorous seven-part structure.", "tokens": [51514, 467, 307, 257, 29882, 3407, 12, 6971, 3877, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 155246, "start": 1577.28, "end": 1578.0, "text": " Should we walk through them?", "tokens": [51606, 6454, 321, 1792, 807, 552, 30, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 155246, "start": 1578.1000000000001, "end": 1578.74, "text": " Yeah, let's do it.", "tokens": [51647, 865, 11, 718, 311, 360, 309, 13, 51679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 155246, "start": 1578.8, "end": 1579.9, "text": " First up is provenance.", "tokens": [51682, 2386, 493, 307, 12785, 719, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13452958278968685, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 2.060284018043368e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 157990, "start": 1579.9, "end": 1584.98, "text": " That's the definitive origin of all raw materials, like training data and foundational code.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 264, 28152, 4957, 295, 439, 8936, 5319, 11, 411, 3097, 1412, 293, 32195, 3089, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 157990, "start": 1585.0800000000002, "end": 1585.22, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50624, 1033, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 157990, "start": 1585.52, "end": 1590.44, "text": " Second is lineage, the exact chronological record of every transformation those materials underwent.", "tokens": [50646, 5736, 307, 38257, 11, 264, 1900, 19393, 4383, 2136, 295, 633, 9887, 729, 5319, 833, 34798, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 157990, "start": 1590.5600000000002, "end": 1590.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50898, 1779, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 157990, "start": 1591.1200000000001, "end": 1593.52, "text": " Third is the anticipated failure decomposition.", "tokens": [50926, 12548, 307, 264, 23267, 7763, 48356, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 157990, "start": 1593.96, "end": 1597.4, "text": " Which details how the engineers expect the system to break under stress.", "tokens": [51068, 3013, 4365, 577, 264, 11955, 2066, 264, 1185, 281, 1821, 833, 4244, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 157990, "start": 1597.6200000000001, "end": 1598.0400000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51251, 7587, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 157990, "start": 1598.6000000000001, "end": 1601.48, "text": " Fourth is empirical adversarial evidence.", "tokens": [51300, 23773, 307, 31886, 17641, 44745, 4467, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 157990, "start": 1602.3400000000001, "end": 1606.5600000000002, "text": " These are the records of the red teaming and stress tests the model was subjected to.", "tokens": [51487, 1981, 366, 264, 7724, 295, 264, 2182, 1469, 278, 293, 4244, 6921, 264, 2316, 390, 32153, 281, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 157990, "start": 1606.8200000000002, "end": 1608.5, "text": " Fifth are the trusted baselines.", "tokens": [51711, 33588, 366, 264, 16034, 987, 9173, 13, 51795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659764574285139, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204095778879715e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 160850, "start": 1608.5, "end": 1611.7, "text": " Sixth are the lies monitoring predicates we discussed earlier.", "tokens": [50365, 11678, 392, 366, 264, 9134, 11028, 47336, 1024, 321, 7152, 3071, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042454865601686, "compression_ratio": 1.6051779935275081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182099706040566e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 160850, "start": 1611.92, "end": 1618.4, "text": " And seventh is a graded recovery record documenting every time the system was rolled back, reconstructed, or fully repaired.", "tokens": [50536, 400, 17875, 307, 257, 2771, 292, 8597, 2136, 42360, 633, 565, 264, 1185, 390, 14306, 646, 11, 31499, 292, 11, 420, 4498, 36551, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042454865601686, "compression_ratio": 1.6051779935275081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182099706040566e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 160850, "start": 1618.66, "end": 1624.66, "text": " And amazingly, this seven-part structure maps perfectly back to Susanna Cox's Emma Loeb's framework.", "tokens": [50873, 400, 31762, 11, 341, 3407, 12, 6971, 3877, 11317, 6239, 646, 281, 9545, 1795, 41576, 311, 17124, 6130, 34727, 311, 8388, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042454865601686, "compression_ratio": 1.6051779935275081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182099706040566e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 160850, "start": 1625.06, "end": 1625.82, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [51193, 467, 534, 775, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042454865601686, "compression_ratio": 1.6051779935275081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182099706040566e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 160850, "start": 1626.32, "end": 1637.26, "text": " Her corporate data sheets, her failure mode and effects analysis documents, her alerting thresholds, those were just early, unformalized, messy versions of these exact certificate components.", "tokens": [51256, 3204, 10896, 1412, 15421, 11, 720, 7763, 4391, 293, 5065, 5215, 8512, 11, 720, 419, 27187, 14678, 82, 11, 729, 645, 445, 2440, 11, 517, 837, 304, 1602, 11, 16191, 9606, 295, 613, 1900, 15953, 6677, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11042454865601686, "compression_ratio": 1.6051779935275081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182099706040566e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 163726, "start": 1637.26, "end": 1643.2, "text": " She was building an admissibility certificate piece by piece without knowing the formal mathematical name for it.", "tokens": [50365, 1240, 390, 2390, 364, 5910, 891, 2841, 15953, 2522, 538, 2522, 1553, 5276, 264, 9860, 18894, 1315, 337, 309, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145473108059023, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251500551324522e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 163726, "start": 1643.26, "end": 1643.68, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50665, 7587, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145473108059023, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251500551324522e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 163726, "start": 1644.26, "end": 1649.02, "text": " The certificate acts as the evidentiary bridge between the unseen history and the present moment.", "tokens": [50715, 440, 15953, 10672, 382, 264, 16371, 29104, 7283, 1296, 264, 40608, 2503, 293, 264, 1974, 1623, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145473108059023, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251500551324522e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 163726, "start": 1649.16, "end": 1654.68, "text": " But, and I know a critical, security-minded listener is likely spotting a massive logical loophole here.", "tokens": [50960, 583, 11, 293, 286, 458, 257, 4924, 11, 3825, 12, 23310, 31569, 307, 3700, 4008, 783, 257, 5994, 14978, 6367, 14094, 510, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145473108059023, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251500551324522e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 163726, "start": 1654.72, "end": 1655.58, "text": " Oh, I'm sure they are.", "tokens": [51238, 876, 11, 286, 478, 988, 436, 366, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145473108059023, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251500551324522e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 165558, "start": 1655.58, "end": 1669.24, "text": " Right, because if an attacker is sophisticated enough to poison the training data, rewrite the model's internal weights, and smoothly mask their tracks from state-of-the-art benchmarks, why couldn't they just forge the certificate?", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 570, 498, 364, 35871, 307, 16950, 1547, 281, 10836, 264, 3097, 1412, 11, 28132, 264, 2316, 311, 6920, 17443, 11, 293, 19565, 6094, 641, 10218, 490, 1785, 12, 2670, 12, 3322, 12, 446, 43751, 11, 983, 2809, 380, 436, 445, 38741, 264, 15953, 30, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08889146774045882, "compression_ratio": 1.425531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802858555715956e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 165558, "start": 1669.36, "end": 1669.76, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51054, 7587, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08889146774045882, "compression_ratio": 1.425531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802858555715956e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 165558, "start": 1669.9199999999998, "end": 1671.1799999999998, "text": " Why not fake the paperwork?", "tokens": [51082, 1545, 406, 7592, 264, 27953, 30, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08889146774045882, "compression_ratio": 1.425531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 2.3802858555715956e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 167118, "start": 1671.18, "end": 1671.7, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1414101774042303, "compression_ratio": 1.8305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620125193976155e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 167118, "start": 1672.18, "end": 1677.52, "text": " If the entire trustworthiness of the system relies on a certificate, who certifies the certificate?", "tokens": [50415, 759, 264, 2302, 3361, 13136, 1324, 295, 264, 1185, 30910, 322, 257, 15953, 11, 567, 5351, 11221, 264, 15953, 30, 50682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1414101774042303, "compression_ratio": 1.8305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620125193976155e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 167118, "start": 1677.96, "end": 1685.3, "text": " If you need a document to prove the system and a document to prove the document, aren't you trapped in an endless loop?", "tokens": [50704, 759, 291, 643, 257, 4166, 281, 7081, 264, 1185, 293, 257, 4166, 281, 7081, 264, 4166, 11, 3212, 380, 291, 14994, 294, 364, 16144, 6367, 30, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1414101774042303, "compression_ratio": 1.8305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620125193976155e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 167118, "start": 1685.5800000000002, "end": 1690.04, "text": " It is the classic problem of an infinite regress of turtles all the way down.", "tokens": [51085, 467, 307, 264, 7230, 1154, 295, 364, 13785, 1121, 735, 295, 32422, 439, 264, 636, 760, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1414101774042303, "compression_ratio": 1.8305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620125193976155e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 167118, "start": 1690.14, "end": 1691.3200000000002, "text": " Turtles all the way down, yeah.", "tokens": [51313, 5712, 23995, 439, 264, 636, 760, 11, 1338, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1414101774042303, "compression_ratio": 1.8305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620125193976155e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 167118, "start": 1691.68, "end": 1698.1200000000001, "text": " Fliction anticipates this exact philosophical trap, which is known in epistemology as the regress problem.", "tokens": [51390, 3235, 4105, 10416, 1024, 341, 1900, 25066, 11487, 11, 597, 307, 2570, 294, 2388, 43958, 1793, 382, 264, 1121, 735, 1154, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1414101774042303, "compression_ratio": 1.8305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620125193976155e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 169812, "start": 1698.12, "end": 1699.2399999999998, "text": " Okay, the regress problem.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 264, 1121, 735, 1154, 13, 50421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309834687606148, "compression_ratio": 1.7323420074349443, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761209591768637e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 169812, "start": 1699.2399999999998, "end": 1705.8799999999999, "text": " And the paper solves it elegantly with a theorem they call Proposition 2, Closure Undercertification.", "tokens": [50421, 400, 264, 3035, 39890, 309, 14459, 3627, 365, 257, 20904, 436, 818, 21944, 5830, 568, 11, 2033, 7641, 2719, 2869, 911, 3774, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309834687606148, "compression_ratio": 1.7323420074349443, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761209591768637e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 169812, "start": 1706.1399999999999, "end": 1708.34, "text": " Closure Undercertification, how does that work?", "tokens": [50766, 2033, 7641, 2719, 2869, 911, 3774, 11, 577, 775, 300, 589, 30, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309834687606148, "compression_ratio": 1.7323420074349443, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761209591768637e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 169812, "start": 1708.54, "end": 1716.28, "text": " Proposition 2 closes the loop without relying on infinite turtles by forcing us to recognize that the certificate itself is an artifact.", "tokens": [50886, 21944, 5830, 568, 24157, 264, 6367, 1553, 24140, 322, 13785, 32422, 538, 19030, 505, 281, 5521, 300, 264, 15953, 2564, 307, 364, 34806, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309834687606148, "compression_ratio": 1.7323420074349443, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761209591768637e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 169812, "start": 1716.54, "end": 1717.8, "text": " Okay, wait, let me make sure I get this.", "tokens": [51286, 1033, 11, 1699, 11, 718, 385, 652, 988, 286, 483, 341, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309834687606148, "compression_ratio": 1.7323420074349443, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761209591768637e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 169812, "start": 1718.06, "end": 1722.3999999999999, "text": " Because the certificate is an artifact generated by a system, it inherently possesses its own history.", "tokens": [51362, 1436, 264, 15953, 307, 364, 34806, 10833, 538, 257, 1185, 11, 309, 27993, 17490, 279, 1080, 1065, 2503, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309834687606148, "compression_ratio": 1.7323420074349443, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761209591768637e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 169812, "start": 1722.7199999999998, "end": 1723.1799999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51595, 7587, 13, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1309834687606148, "compression_ratio": 1.7323420074349443, "no_speech_prob": 2.0761209591768637e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 172318, "start": 1723.18, "end": 1728.66, "text": " The history of the certificate is mathematically denoted as H of C sub-sigma.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2503, 295, 264, 15953, 307, 44003, 1441, 23325, 382, 389, 295, 383, 1422, 12, 82, 16150, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500235438346863, "compression_ratio": 1.6823529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830465836449205e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 172318, "start": 1729.6200000000001, "end": 1739.54, "text": " The exact same rigorous rules of admissibility that apply to the massive AI model also apply to the history of the piece of paper or the digital file certifying it.", "tokens": [50687, 440, 1900, 912, 29882, 4474, 295, 5910, 891, 2841, 300, 3079, 281, 264, 5994, 7318, 2316, 611, 3079, 281, 264, 2503, 295, 264, 2522, 295, 3035, 420, 264, 4562, 3991, 5351, 5489, 309, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500235438346863, "compression_ratio": 1.6823529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830465836449205e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 172318, "start": 1740.0, "end": 1740.66, "text": " Mind blown.", "tokens": [51206, 13719, 16479, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500235438346863, "compression_ratio": 1.6823529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830465836449205e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 172318, "start": 1741.2, "end": 1751.3200000000002, "text": " So the auditor must evaluate how the certificate was compiled, who compiled it, what underlying primary evidence was used, under whose cryptographic authority was it stamped.", "tokens": [51266, 407, 264, 33970, 1633, 13059, 577, 264, 15953, 390, 36548, 11, 567, 36548, 309, 11, 437, 14217, 6194, 4467, 390, 1143, 11, 833, 6104, 9844, 12295, 8281, 390, 309, 39111, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12500235438346863, "compression_ratio": 1.6823529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830465836449205e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 175132, "start": 1751.32, "end": 1757.76, "text": " Right. And you might initially think, this just kicks the can down the road, pushing the verification problem back one step.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 400, 291, 1062, 9105, 519, 11, 341, 445, 21293, 264, 393, 760, 264, 3060, 11, 7380, 264, 30206, 1154, 646, 472, 1823, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700106930423092, "compression_ratio": 1.4922279792746114, "no_speech_prob": 1.404807693783372e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 175132, "start": 1757.8, "end": 1759.1599999999999, "text": " Yeah, that was my first thought.", "tokens": [50689, 865, 11, 300, 390, 452, 700, 1194, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700106930423092, "compression_ratio": 1.4922279792746114, "no_speech_prob": 1.404807693783372e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 175132, "start": 1759.2, "end": 1762.6799999999998, "text": " In reality, it creates a finite, directed acyclic graph.", "tokens": [50759, 682, 4103, 11, 309, 7829, 257, 19362, 11, 12898, 696, 88, 66, 1050, 4295, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700106930423092, "compression_ratio": 1.4922279792746114, "no_speech_prob": 1.404807693783372e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 175132, "start": 1762.8999999999999, "end": 1766.3, "text": " Let's translate directed acyclic graph for a general audience.", "tokens": [50944, 961, 311, 13799, 12898, 696, 88, 66, 1050, 4295, 337, 257, 2674, 4034, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700106930423092, "compression_ratio": 1.4922279792746114, "no_speech_prob": 1.404807693783372e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 175132, "start": 1766.46, "end": 1766.8799999999999, "text": " Good idea.", "tokens": [51122, 2205, 1558, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700106930423092, "compression_ratio": 1.4922279792746114, "no_speech_prob": 1.404807693783372e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 176688, "start": 1766.88, "end": 1772.7, "text": " Imagine a complex map with arrows connecting different points, but the arrows only go one way.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 257, 3997, 4471, 365, 19669, 11015, 819, 2793, 11, 457, 264, 19669, 787, 352, 472, 636, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12621709489330804, "compression_ratio": 1.6983471074380165, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091464078720756e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 176688, "start": 1773.0200000000002, "end": 1777.7, "text": " You can follow the arrows from point to point, but they never loop back on themselves to create a circle.", "tokens": [50672, 509, 393, 1524, 264, 19669, 490, 935, 281, 935, 11, 457, 436, 1128, 6367, 646, 322, 2969, 281, 1884, 257, 6329, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12621709489330804, "compression_ratio": 1.6983471074380165, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091464078720756e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 176688, "start": 1777.98, "end": 1778.1200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50920, 1779, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12621709489330804, "compression_ratio": 1.6983471074380165, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091464078720756e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 176688, "start": 1778.44, "end": 1782.14, "text": " Eventually, if you follow the arrows long enough, they have to stop at a final destination.", "tokens": [50943, 17586, 11, 498, 291, 1524, 264, 19669, 938, 1547, 11, 436, 362, 281, 1590, 412, 257, 2572, 12236, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12621709489330804, "compression_ratio": 1.6983471074380165, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091464078720756e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 176688, "start": 1782.44, "end": 1787.68, "text": " And the destinations where those arrows finally terminate are what Fliction calls trust anchors.", "tokens": [51143, 400, 264, 37787, 689, 729, 19669, 2721, 10761, 473, 366, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 3361, 12723, 830, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12621709489330804, "compression_ratio": 1.6983471074380165, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091464078720756e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 176688, "start": 1787.94, "end": 1788.72, "text": " Trust anchors.", "tokens": [51418, 11580, 12723, 830, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12621709489330804, "compression_ratio": 1.6983471074380165, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091464078720756e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 178872, "start": 1788.72, "end": 1795.16, "text": " These anchors are profoundly important because they exist outside the mathematical framework of the computer system.", "tokens": [50365, 1981, 12723, 830, 366, 39954, 1021, 570, 436, 2514, 2380, 264, 18894, 8388, 295, 264, 3820, 1185, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981403121029038, "compression_ratio": 1.616600790513834, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 178872, "start": 1796.06, "end": 1799.04, "text": " Trust anchors are things rooted in physical reality.", "tokens": [50732, 11580, 12723, 830, 366, 721, 25277, 294, 4001, 4103, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981403121029038, "compression_ratio": 1.616600790513834, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 178872, "start": 1799.16, "end": 1799.68, "text": " Reality.", "tokens": [50887, 33822, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981403121029038, "compression_ratio": 1.616600790513834, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 178872, "start": 1799.84, "end": 1800.0, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50921, 1033, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981403121029038, "compression_ratio": 1.616600790513834, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 178872, "start": 1800.2, "end": 1813.08, "text": " They include cryptographic signatures verified by an offline root key, physical laws measured by calibrated instruments, directly witnessed human observations, or legally binding attestations signed under penalty of perjury.", "tokens": [50939, 814, 4090, 9844, 12295, 32322, 31197, 538, 364, 21857, 5593, 2141, 11, 4001, 6064, 12690, 538, 21583, 5468, 12190, 11, 3838, 21519, 1952, 18163, 11, 420, 21106, 17359, 951, 377, 763, 8175, 833, 16263, 295, 680, 73, 2598, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981403121029038, "compression_ratio": 1.616600790513834, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582751219215933e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 181308, "start": 1813.08, "end": 1817.9199999999998, "text": " So trust cannot be perfectly, infinitely automated.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 3361, 2644, 312, 6239, 11, 36227, 18473, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17561831618800308, "compression_ratio": 1.4189944134078212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014847004612975e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 181308, "start": 1818.04, "end": 1819.62, "text": " It does not flow in a digital vacuum.", "tokens": [50613, 467, 775, 406, 3095, 294, 257, 4562, 14224, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17561831618800308, "compression_ratio": 1.4189944134078212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014847004612975e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 181308, "start": 1819.86, "end": 1819.96, "text": " Yep.", "tokens": [50704, 7010, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17561831618800308, "compression_ratio": 1.4189944134078212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014847004612975e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 181308, "start": 1820.24, "end": 1828.3799999999999, "text": " Ultimately, it must be anchored to reality, to the laws of physics, the strict rules of cryptography, or the heavy weight of human legal institutions.", "tokens": [50723, 23921, 11, 309, 1633, 312, 12723, 2769, 281, 4103, 11, 281, 264, 6064, 295, 10649, 11, 264, 10910, 4474, 295, 9844, 5820, 11, 420, 264, 4676, 3364, 295, 1952, 5089, 8142, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17561831618800308, "compression_ratio": 1.4189944134078212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014847004612975e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 181308, "start": 1828.6399999999999, "end": 1828.9199999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51143, 7587, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17561831618800308, "compression_ratio": 1.4189944134078212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014847004612975e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 182892, "start": 1828.92, "end": 1844.8400000000001, "text": " If a certificate relies on a surged data provenance sheet, the auditor examines the history of that specific sheet, traces its lineage back to the trust anchor, say, the cryptographic signature of the senior engineer who allegedly signed off on it, and discovers the mathematical forgery.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 15953, 30910, 322, 257, 1022, 3004, 1412, 12785, 719, 8193, 11, 264, 33970, 1139, 1652, 264, 2503, 295, 300, 2685, 8193, 11, 26076, 1080, 38257, 646, 281, 264, 3361, 18487, 11, 584, 11, 264, 9844, 12295, 13397, 295, 264, 7965, 11403, 567, 26794, 8175, 766, 322, 309, 11, 293, 44522, 264, 18894, 337, 7337, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08755069029958625, "compression_ratio": 1.5586854460093897, "no_speech_prob": 1.7283502103462856e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 182892, "start": 1845.14, "end": 1846.14, "text": " The regress is finite.", "tokens": [51176, 440, 1121, 735, 307, 19362, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08755069029958625, "compression_ratio": 1.5586854460093897, "no_speech_prob": 1.7283502103462856e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 182892, "start": 1846.42, "end": 1847.26, "text": " It stops at reality.", "tokens": [51240, 467, 10094, 412, 4103, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08755069029958625, "compression_ratio": 1.5586854460093897, "no_speech_prob": 1.7283502103462856e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 184726, "start": 1847.26, "end": 1862.3, "text": " It stops at reality, and realizing that we use documentation to prove an invisible history, and that we trace that documentation back to physical trust anchors, reveals a breathtaking scope to Flixion's work.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 10094, 412, 4103, 11, 293, 16734, 300, 321, 764, 14333, 281, 7081, 364, 14603, 2503, 11, 293, 300, 321, 13508, 300, 14333, 646, 281, 4001, 3361, 12723, 830, 11, 20893, 257, 48393, 11923, 281, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 589, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12056825035496761, "compression_ratio": 1.526829268292683, "no_speech_prob": 1.898043137590899e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 184726, "start": 1862.3799999999999, "end": 1863.02, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [51121, 467, 534, 775, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12056825035496761, "compression_ratio": 1.526829268292683, "no_speech_prob": 1.898043137590899e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 184726, "start": 1863.2, "end": 1867.14, "text": " This is not just a niche concept for securing next-generation AI models.", "tokens": [51162, 639, 307, 406, 445, 257, 19956, 3410, 337, 33640, 958, 12, 30372, 7318, 5245, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12056825035496761, "compression_ratio": 1.526829268292683, "no_speech_prob": 1.898043137590899e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 184726, "start": 1867.22, "end": 1867.82, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [51363, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12056825035496761, "compression_ratio": 1.526829268292683, "no_speech_prob": 1.898043137590899e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 186782, "start": 1867.82, "end": 1880.6399999999999, "text": " Flixion zooms out and introduces the history principle, which states that any adaptive system whose future behavior depends on accumulated information requires admissibility to be defined over histories, not instantaneous states.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 970, 313, 5721, 4785, 484, 293, 31472, 264, 2503, 8665, 11, 597, 4368, 300, 604, 27912, 1185, 6104, 2027, 5223, 5946, 322, 31346, 1589, 7029, 5910, 891, 2841, 281, 312, 7642, 670, 30631, 11, 406, 45596, 4368, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0949144721031189, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192827299948852e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 186782, "start": 1880.76, "end": 1881.7, "text": " The history principle, yes.", "tokens": [51012, 440, 2503, 8665, 11, 2086, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0949144721031189, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192827299948852e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 186782, "start": 1881.74, "end": 1888.52, "text": " When you grasp the history principle, you realize it is the hidden, humming machinery of all human civilization.", "tokens": [51061, 1133, 291, 21743, 264, 2503, 8665, 11, 291, 4325, 309, 307, 264, 7633, 11, 34965, 27302, 295, 439, 1952, 18036, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0949144721031189, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192827299948852e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 186782, "start": 1888.74, "end": 1889.48, "text": " It is everywhere.", "tokens": [51411, 467, 307, 5315, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0949144721031189, "compression_ratio": 1.6724137931034482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192827299948852e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 188948, "start": 1889.48, "end": 1901.08, "text": " Let's take the time to really dissect the examples the paper provides, starting with the foundational bedrock of modern software security, Ken Thompson's legendary 1984 Turing Award lecture.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 747, 264, 565, 281, 534, 48332, 264, 5110, 264, 3035, 6417, 11, 2891, 365, 264, 32195, 2901, 17799, 295, 4363, 4722, 3825, 11, 8273, 23460, 311, 16698, 27127, 314, 1345, 13894, 7991, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1043013924950952, "compression_ratio": 1.597444089456869, "no_speech_prob": 2.280510415925141e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 188948, "start": 1901.22, "end": 1902.16, "text": " Oh, this is a classic.", "tokens": [50952, 876, 11, 341, 307, 257, 7230, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1043013924950952, "compression_ratio": 1.597444089456869, "no_speech_prob": 2.280510415925141e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 188948, "start": 1902.6, "end": 1908.02, "text": " Ken Thompson, one of the pioneers of computer science, described a brilliant and terrifying compiler hack.", "tokens": [51021, 8273, 23460, 11, 472, 295, 264, 47381, 295, 3820, 3497, 11, 7619, 257, 10248, 293, 18106, 31958, 10339, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1043013924950952, "compression_ratio": 1.597444089456869, "no_speech_prob": 2.280510415925141e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 188948, "start": 1908.44, "end": 1917.3, "text": " He modified a C compiler so that whenever it compiled the code for the Unix login command, it silently inserted a backdoor, allowing him secret access.", "tokens": [51313, 634, 15873, 257, 383, 31958, 370, 300, 5699, 309, 36548, 264, 3089, 337, 264, 1156, 970, 24276, 5622, 11, 309, 40087, 27992, 257, 646, 10441, 11, 8293, 796, 4054, 2105, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1043013924950952, "compression_ratio": 1.597444089456869, "no_speech_prob": 2.280510415925141e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 188948, "start": 1917.3, "end": 1918.5, "text": " But he went a step further.", "tokens": [51756, 583, 415, 1437, 257, 1823, 3052, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1043013924950952, "compression_ratio": 1.597444089456869, "no_speech_prob": 2.280510415925141e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 191850, "start": 1918.5, "end": 1927.38, "text": " He also modified the compiler so that when it compiled a new version of the compiler itself, it inserted the backdoor into the new compiler.", "tokens": [50365, 634, 611, 15873, 264, 31958, 370, 300, 562, 309, 36548, 257, 777, 3037, 295, 264, 31958, 2564, 11, 309, 27992, 264, 646, 10441, 666, 264, 777, 31958, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 191850, "start": 1927.64, "end": 1929.3, "text": " Which is just diabolical.", "tokens": [50822, 3013, 307, 445, 1026, 14923, 804, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 191850, "start": 1929.42, "end": 1929.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50911, 1779, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 191850, "start": 1929.9, "end": 1932.82, "text": " And then he removed the backdoor from the human-readable source code.", "tokens": [50935, 400, 550, 415, 7261, 264, 646, 10441, 490, 264, 1952, 12, 2538, 712, 4009, 3089, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 191850, "start": 1932.92, "end": 1937.7, "text": " Okay, so if an auditor looked at the source code of the login program, it was perfectly clean.", "tokens": [51086, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 364, 33970, 2956, 412, 264, 4009, 3089, 295, 264, 24276, 1461, 11, 309, 390, 6239, 2541, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 191850, "start": 1937.84, "end": 1938.5, "text": " Perfectly clean.", "tokens": [51332, 10246, 356, 2541, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 191850, "start": 1938.62, "end": 1941.6, "text": " If they looked at the source code of the compiler, it was perfectly clean.", "tokens": [51371, 759, 436, 2956, 412, 264, 4009, 3089, 295, 264, 31958, 11, 309, 390, 6239, 2541, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 191850, "start": 1941.92, "end": 1945.34, "text": " The current observable state of the software was flawless.", "tokens": [51536, 440, 2190, 9951, 712, 1785, 295, 264, 4722, 390, 45693, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14506540065858423, "compression_ratio": 1.963855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659417323236728e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 194534, "start": 1945.34, "end": 1946.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10784621672196822, "compression_ratio": 1.697211155378486, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522422736896084e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 194534, "start": 1946.82, "end": 1955.9599999999998, "text": " But the compiled binary code running on the machine contained the backdoor, perpetually re-injecting itself generation after generation.", "tokens": [50439, 583, 264, 36548, 17434, 3089, 2614, 322, 264, 3479, 16212, 264, 646, 10441, 11, 16211, 671, 319, 12, 259, 1020, 278, 2564, 5125, 934, 5125, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10784621672196822, "compression_ratio": 1.697211155378486, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522422736896084e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 194534, "start": 1956.22, "end": 1957.6, "text": " The endpoint was an illusion.", "tokens": [50909, 440, 35795, 390, 364, 18854, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10784621672196822, "compression_ratio": 1.697211155378486, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522422736896084e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 194534, "start": 1958.56, "end": 1961.48, "text": " The history of how the compiler was built was fatally compromised.", "tokens": [51026, 440, 2503, 295, 577, 264, 31958, 390, 3094, 390, 4046, 379, 32463, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10784621672196822, "compression_ratio": 1.697211155378486, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522422736896084e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 194534, "start": 1962.36, "end": 1973.32, "text": " Modern software engineering uses reproducible builds, which is a complex process of verifying compilation history entirely to combat this exact manifestation of the history principle.", "tokens": [51216, 19814, 4722, 7043, 4960, 11408, 32128, 15182, 11, 597, 307, 257, 3997, 1399, 295, 1306, 5489, 40261, 2503, 7696, 281, 8361, 341, 1900, 29550, 295, 264, 2503, 8665, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10784621672196822, "compression_ratio": 1.697211155378486, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522422736896084e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 197332, "start": 1973.32, "end": 1976.62, "text": " Right. And we see the exact same mathematical principle governing aviation.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 400, 321, 536, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 8665, 30054, 28831, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09974083900451661, "compression_ratio": 1.4792626728110598, "no_speech_prob": 1.7819044850764243e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 197332, "start": 1976.74, "end": 1977.54, "text": " Yes, the FAA.", "tokens": [50536, 1079, 11, 264, 479, 5265, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09974083900451661, "compression_ratio": 1.4792626728110598, "no_speech_prob": 1.7819044850764243e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 197332, "start": 1977.8, "end": 1984.2, "text": " The Federal Aviation Administration's oversight of a Boeing 747 is essentially applied history verification.", "tokens": [50589, 440, 12380, 40712, 399, 17187, 311, 29146, 295, 257, 30831, 1614, 14060, 307, 4476, 6456, 2503, 30206, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09974083900451661, "compression_ratio": 1.4792626728110598, "no_speech_prob": 1.7819044850764243e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 197332, "start": 1984.9199999999998, "end": 1992.02, "text": " If the FAA inspects an airliner, they don't simply kick the tires, x-ray the wings, and run the engines up to full thrust.", "tokens": [50945, 759, 264, 479, 5265, 15018, 82, 364, 18856, 4564, 11, 436, 500, 380, 2935, 4437, 264, 13885, 11, 2031, 12, 3458, 264, 11405, 11, 293, 1190, 264, 12982, 493, 281, 1577, 24030, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09974083900451661, "compression_ratio": 1.4792626728110598, "no_speech_prob": 1.7819044850764243e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 199202, "start": 1992.02, "end": 1996.46, "text": " Right. A commercial airplane could pass every single physical and diagnostic test.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 316, 6841, 17130, 727, 1320, 633, 2167, 4001, 293, 27897, 1500, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10398387908935547, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396404191656224e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 199202, "start": 1996.84, "end": 2000.22, "text": " It could look brand new and fly perfectly during a physical test run.", "tokens": [50606, 467, 727, 574, 3360, 777, 293, 3603, 6239, 1830, 257, 4001, 1500, 1190, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10398387908935547, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396404191656224e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 199202, "start": 2000.76, "end": 2012.94, "text": " But if the airline loses the maintenance logs, if the paperwork detailing the origin of a specific turbine blade or the chronological history of a hydraulic repair goes missing, that plane is instantly legally grounded.", "tokens": [50802, 583, 498, 264, 29528, 18293, 264, 11258, 20820, 11, 498, 264, 27953, 42459, 264, 4957, 295, 257, 2685, 27536, 10959, 420, 264, 19393, 4383, 2503, 295, 257, 32134, 10535, 1709, 5361, 11, 300, 5720, 307, 13518, 21106, 23535, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10398387908935547, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396404191656224e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 199202, "start": 2013.2, "end": 2014.86, "text": " It is forbidden from carrying passengers.", "tokens": [51424, 467, 307, 25990, 490, 9792, 18436, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10398387908935547, "compression_ratio": 1.6299212598425197, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396404191656224e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 201486, "start": 2014.86, "end": 2022.3799999999999, "text": " Yes. The FAA understands implicitly that physical state is insufficient. The paperwork is the admissibility certificate.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 440, 479, 5265, 15146, 26947, 356, 300, 4001, 1785, 307, 41709, 13, 440, 27953, 307, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 15953, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07665008579919097, "compression_ratio": 1.6918238993710693, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851344940235442e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 201486, "start": 2022.6999999999998, "end": 2033.9199999999998, "text": " Wow. Yes. An airplane with missing logs possesses an unverifiable history. Therefore, its present state is mathematically inadmissible, regardless of how flawlessly the physical metal performs in the present moment.", "tokens": [50757, 3153, 13, 1079, 13, 1107, 17130, 365, 5361, 20820, 17490, 279, 364, 517, 331, 30876, 2503, 13, 7504, 11, 1080, 1974, 1785, 307, 44003, 42148, 76, 41073, 11, 10060, 295, 577, 13717, 12048, 264, 4001, 5760, 26213, 294, 264, 1974, 1623, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07665008579919097, "compression_ratio": 1.6918238993710693, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851344940235442e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 201486, "start": 2034.1, "end": 2042.74, "text": " Exactly. Moving into academia, the history principle perfectly diagnoses the reproducibility crisis, currently devastating fields like social psychology and medicine.", "tokens": [51327, 7587, 13, 14242, 666, 28937, 11, 264, 2503, 8665, 6239, 7234, 4201, 264, 11408, 537, 39802, 5869, 11, 4362, 21280, 7909, 411, 2093, 15105, 293, 7195, 13, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07665008579919097, "compression_ratio": 1.6918238993710693, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851344940235442e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 201486, "start": 2042.9199999999998, "end": 2044.36, "text": " This one really resonated with me.", "tokens": [51768, 639, 472, 534, 47957, 365, 385, 13, 51840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07665008579919097, "compression_ratio": 1.6918238993710693, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851344940235442e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 204436, "start": 2044.36, "end": 2052.8199999999997, "text": " Right. A research team publishes a groundbreaking study. The final p-value, the statistical measure of significance, looks fantastic.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 316, 2132, 1469, 11374, 279, 257, 42491, 2979, 13, 440, 2572, 280, 12, 29155, 11, 264, 22820, 3481, 295, 17687, 11, 1542, 5456, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1118241241297771, "compression_ratio": 1.7279151943462898, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553956335389365e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 204436, "start": 2053.4, "end": 2058.56, "text": " The published paper, representing the final state of the research, appears rigorous and perfect.", "tokens": [50817, 440, 6572, 3035, 11, 13460, 264, 2572, 1785, 295, 264, 2132, 11, 7038, 29882, 293, 2176, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1118241241297771, "compression_ratio": 1.7279151943462898, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553956335389365e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 204436, "start": 2059.2, "end": 2063.52, "text": " But the hidden methodological history reveals a completely different reality.", "tokens": [51107, 583, 264, 7633, 3170, 4383, 2503, 20893, 257, 2584, 819, 4103, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1118241241297771, "compression_ratio": 1.7279151943462898, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553956335389365e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 204436, "start": 2063.7599999999998, "end": 2074.2799999999997, "text": " The history involves p-hacking, running the data through dozens of different statistical models until one produces a positive result, and quietly discarding the models that failed.", "tokens": [51335, 440, 2503, 11626, 280, 12, 71, 14134, 11, 2614, 264, 1412, 807, 18431, 295, 819, 22820, 5245, 1826, 472, 14725, 257, 3353, 1874, 11, 293, 19141, 31597, 278, 264, 5245, 300, 7612, 13, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1118241241297771, "compression_ratio": 1.7279151943462898, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553956335389365e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 207436, "start": 2074.36, "end": 2077.82, "text": " Or it involves excluding inconvenient data points that didn't fit the narrative.", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 309, 11626, 49999, 46196, 1412, 2793, 300, 994, 380, 3318, 264, 9977, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.176756941753885, "compression_ratio": 1.335483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.150420249855123e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 207436, "start": 2077.82, "end": 2085.48, "text": " Right. It is the file drawer effect, where 99 failed experiments are hidden away, and only the one lucky success is published.", "tokens": [50538, 1779, 13, 467, 307, 264, 3991, 24039, 1802, 11, 689, 11803, 7612, 12050, 366, 7633, 1314, 11, 293, 787, 264, 472, 6356, 2245, 307, 6572, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.176756941753885, "compression_ratio": 1.335483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.150420249855123e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 208548, "start": 2085.48, "end": 2094.2, "text": " The final published state is a mathematical illusion, meticulously crafted to mask an inadmissible, deeply flawed scientific history.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2572, 6572, 1785, 307, 257, 18894, 18854, 11, 41566, 25038, 36213, 281, 6094, 364, 42148, 76, 41073, 11, 8760, 38823, 8134, 2503, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16213796252296084, "compression_ratio": 1.3829787234042554, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453935412392045e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 208548, "start": 2094.4, "end": 2097.72, "text": " It is the identical endpoint problem masquerading as science.", "tokens": [50811, 467, 307, 264, 14800, 35795, 1154, 2300, 8035, 8166, 382, 3497, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16213796252296084, "compression_ratio": 1.3829787234042554, "no_speech_prob": 2.2453935412392045e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 209772, "start": 2097.72, "end": 2103.5, "text": " We also see this structure formalize life and death decisions in the legal system through the chain of custody.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 611, 536, 341, 3877, 9860, 1125, 993, 293, 2966, 5327, 294, 264, 5089, 1185, 807, 264, 5021, 295, 26976, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20501139134536556, "compression_ratio": 1.5765765765765767, "no_speech_prob": 2.044461388378549e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 209772, "start": 2103.58, "end": 2104.4399999999996, "text": " Chain of custody, right.", "tokens": [50658, 33252, 295, 26976, 11, 558, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20501139134536556, "compression_ratio": 1.5765765765765767, "no_speech_prob": 2.044461388378549e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 209772, "start": 2104.7999999999997, "end": 2106.9399999999996, "text": " Consider a high-stakes murder trial.", "tokens": [50719, 17416, 257, 1090, 12, 372, 3419, 6568, 7308, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20501139134536556, "compression_ratio": 1.5765765765765767, "no_speech_prob": 2.044461388378549e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 209772, "start": 2107.6, "end": 2111.7799999999997, "text": " The prosecution introduces a bloody knife as the murder weapon.", "tokens": [50859, 440, 37106, 31472, 257, 18938, 7976, 382, 264, 6568, 7463, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20501139134536556, "compression_ratio": 1.5765765765765767, "no_speech_prob": 2.044461388378549e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 209772, "start": 2112.4599999999996, "end": 2118.2999999999997, "text": " The knife has the defendant's fingerprints perfectly preserved on the handle, and the victim's DNA on the blade.", "tokens": [51102, 440, 7976, 575, 264, 34053, 311, 42170, 6239, 22242, 322, 264, 4813, 11, 293, 264, 6760, 311, 8272, 322, 264, 10959, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20501139134536556, "compression_ratio": 1.5765765765765767, "no_speech_prob": 2.044461388378549e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 211830, "start": 2118.3, "end": 2121.9, "text": " The physical state of the evidence is absolutely damning.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4001, 1785, 295, 264, 4467, 307, 3122, 2422, 773, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13288389515672994, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678119369039628e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 211830, "start": 2121.96, "end": 2122.96, "text": " It looks like a slam dunk.", "tokens": [50548, 467, 1542, 411, 257, 25617, 33555, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13288389515672994, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678119369039628e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 211830, "start": 2123.46, "end": 2132.44, "text": " But the defense attorney discovers that the police officers lost track of who held the evidence bag for three unrecorded hours before it arrived at the secure forensic locker.", "tokens": [50623, 583, 264, 7654, 13469, 44522, 300, 264, 3804, 9199, 2731, 2837, 295, 567, 5167, 264, 4467, 3411, 337, 1045, 517, 38500, 292, 2496, 949, 309, 6678, 412, 264, 7144, 39084, 25707, 13, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13288389515672994, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678119369039628e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 211830, "start": 2132.6600000000003, "end": 2134.0800000000004, "text": " The sequence of custody is broken.", "tokens": [51083, 440, 8310, 295, 26976, 307, 5463, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13288389515672994, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678119369039628e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 211830, "start": 2134.44, "end": 2136.1200000000003, "text": " The history is severed.", "tokens": [51172, 440, 2503, 307, 2802, 292, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13288389515672994, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678119369039628e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 211830, "start": 2136.38, "end": 2144.4, "text": " Because the history is unverifiable, the presiding judge will strike the evidence from the record, declaring the weapon inadmissible in court.", "tokens": [51269, 1436, 264, 2503, 307, 517, 331, 30876, 11, 264, 1183, 2819, 6995, 486, 9302, 264, 4467, 490, 264, 2136, 11, 40374, 264, 7463, 42148, 76, 41073, 294, 4753, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13288389515672994, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678119369039628e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 211830, "start": 2144.76, "end": 2147.0600000000004, "text": " The jury is literally instructed to ignore it.", "tokens": [51688, 440, 19516, 307, 3736, 36384, 281, 11200, 309, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13288389515672994, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1678119369039628e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 214706, "start": 2147.06, "end": 2150.12, "text": " And the legal doctrine is literally named admissibility.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 5089, 23290, 307, 3736, 4926, 5910, 891, 2841, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031873026201803, "compression_ratio": 1.5192982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894344840068692e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 214706, "start": 2150.64, "end": 2155.5, "text": " The judge is performing the exact same mathematical operation as Fliction's AI auditor.", "tokens": [50544, 440, 6995, 307, 10205, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 6916, 382, 3235, 4105, 311, 7318, 33970, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031873026201803, "compression_ratio": 1.5192982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894344840068692e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 214706, "start": 2155.7, "end": 2156.44, "text": " That is so true.", "tokens": [50797, 663, 307, 370, 2074, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031873026201803, "compression_ratio": 1.5192982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894344840068692e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 214706, "start": 2157.32, "end": 2163.6, "text": " Even in the realm of decentralized finance, blockchain technology is a pure manifestation of the history principle.", "tokens": [50878, 2754, 294, 264, 15355, 295, 32870, 10719, 11, 17176, 2899, 307, 257, 6075, 29550, 295, 264, 2503, 8665, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031873026201803, "compression_ratio": 1.5192982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894344840068692e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 214706, "start": 2163.68, "end": 2164.08, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51196, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031873026201803, "compression_ratio": 1.5192982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894344840068692e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 214706, "start": 2164.08, "end": 2172.14, "text": " A consensus protocol like Bitcoin does not function by simply looking at a snapshot of your current wallet balance and blindly trusting it.", "tokens": [51216, 316, 19115, 10336, 411, 11414, 775, 406, 2445, 538, 2935, 1237, 412, 257, 30163, 295, 428, 2190, 16599, 4772, 293, 47744, 28235, 309, 13, 51619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15031873026201803, "compression_ratio": 1.5192982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894344840068692e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 217214, "start": 2172.14, "end": 2185.08, "text": " A node on the network verifies the entire continuous reconstructable chain of past transactions, tracing the lineage of every fraction of a coin all the way back to the original Genesis block.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 9984, 322, 264, 3209, 1306, 11221, 264, 2302, 10957, 31499, 712, 5021, 295, 1791, 16856, 11, 25262, 264, 38257, 295, 633, 14135, 295, 257, 11464, 439, 264, 636, 646, 281, 264, 3380, 20587, 3461, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10127409696578979, "compression_ratio": 1.4328358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077931950548741e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 218508, "start": 2185.08, "end": 2204.3199999999997, "text": " So whether you are an FAA inspector scrutinizing metallurgical fatigue logs, a blockchain node verifying a cryptographic ledger, a trial judge ruling on a compromised bloody knife, a scientist demanding replication data, or an MLOps engineer auditing a neural network, you are executing the exact same mathematical function.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1968, 291, 366, 364, 479, 5265, 34564, 28949, 259, 3319, 20866, 46736, 20574, 20820, 11, 257, 17176, 9984, 1306, 5489, 257, 9844, 12295, 4684, 1321, 11, 257, 7308, 6995, 21437, 322, 257, 32463, 18938, 7976, 11, 257, 12662, 19960, 39911, 1412, 11, 420, 364, 376, 20184, 1878, 11403, 2379, 1748, 257, 18161, 3209, 11, 291, 366, 32368, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 2445, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06209764059852151, "compression_ratio": 1.4794520547945205, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918475305271018e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 220432, "start": 2204.32, "end": 2204.6800000000003, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17043205543800635, "compression_ratio": 1.446078431372549, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039928716835017e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 220432, "start": 2204.6800000000003, "end": 2209.1800000000003, "text": " You are looking past the deceptive endpoint to verify the admissibility of a history.", "tokens": [50383, 509, 366, 1237, 1791, 264, 368, 1336, 488, 35795, 281, 16888, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 295, 257, 2503, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17043205543800635, "compression_ratio": 1.446078431372549, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039928716835017e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 220432, "start": 2209.28, "end": 2209.84, "text": " It's universal.", "tokens": [50613, 467, 311, 11455, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17043205543800635, "compression_ratio": 1.446078431372549, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039928716835017e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 220432, "start": 2210.04, "end": 2218.32, "text": " But in all of these powerful examples, the FAA, the judge, the blockchain, it requires an outside auditor, a third party, to look in and check the history.", "tokens": [50651, 583, 294, 439, 295, 613, 4005, 5110, 11, 264, 479, 5265, 11, 264, 6995, 11, 264, 17176, 11, 309, 7029, 364, 2380, 33970, 11, 257, 2636, 3595, 11, 281, 574, 294, 293, 1520, 264, 2503, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17043205543800635, "compression_ratio": 1.446078431372549, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039928716835017e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 220432, "start": 2218.42, "end": 2218.5800000000004, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51070, 1779, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17043205543800635, "compression_ratio": 1.446078431372549, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039928716835017e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 220432, "start": 2218.6400000000003, "end": 2219.6200000000003, "text": " An external verification.", "tokens": [51081, 1107, 8320, 30206, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17043205543800635, "compression_ratio": 1.446078431372549, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039928716835017e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 221962, "start": 2219.62, "end": 2224.18, "text": " Which raises a profound and fascinating question regarding artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 19658, 257, 14382, 293, 10343, 1168, 8595, 11677, 7599, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11918595549348113, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 2.686664692802543e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 221962, "start": 2224.8199999999997, "end": 2230.7, "text": " Can a highly advanced system like a massively capable AI actually prove its history from the inside?", "tokens": [50625, 1664, 257, 5405, 7339, 1185, 411, 257, 29379, 8189, 7318, 767, 7081, 1080, 2503, 490, 264, 1854, 30, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11918595549348113, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 2.686664692802543e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 221962, "start": 2230.94, "end": 2231.98, "text": " Well, this is the big question.", "tokens": [50931, 1042, 11, 341, 307, 264, 955, 1168, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11918595549348113, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 2.686664692802543e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 221962, "start": 2232.2, "end": 2242.3599999999997, "text": " Can it demonstrate that it genuinely understands the complex path it took to arrive at an answer rather than just faking a perfect endpoint through sophisticated pattern matching?", "tokens": [50994, 1664, 309, 11698, 300, 309, 17839, 15146, 264, 3997, 3100, 309, 1890, 281, 8881, 412, 364, 1867, 2831, 813, 445, 283, 2456, 257, 2176, 35795, 807, 16950, 5102, 14324, 30, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11918595549348113, "compression_ratio": 1.5590551181102361, "no_speech_prob": 2.686664692802543e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 224236, "start": 2242.36, "end": 2250.7400000000002, "text": " And this challenge leads to the final and arguably most conceptually mind-bending test introduced in Fliction's paper.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 3430, 6689, 281, 264, 2572, 293, 26771, 881, 3410, 671, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 1500, 7268, 294, 3235, 4105, 311, 3035, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 224236, "start": 2250.88, "end": 2252.2400000000002, "text": " I am so ready for this.", "tokens": [50791, 286, 669, 370, 1919, 337, 341, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 224236, "start": 2252.32, "end": 2257.8, "text": " They call it reflexive reconstruction or alternatively, withheld history reconstruction.", "tokens": [50863, 814, 818, 309, 23802, 488, 31565, 420, 8535, 356, 11, 365, 23504, 2503, 31565, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 224236, "start": 2258.7000000000003, "end": 2263.1, "text": " It is an ingenious method for forcing a system to generate its own adversarial evidence.", "tokens": [51182, 467, 307, 364, 21600, 851, 3170, 337, 19030, 257, 1185, 281, 8460, 1080, 1065, 17641, 44745, 4467, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 224236, "start": 2263.28, "end": 2264.78, "text": " The mechanics of the test are brilliant.", "tokens": [51411, 440, 12939, 295, 264, 1500, 366, 10248, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 224236, "start": 2264.92, "end": 2265.46, "text": " Let me set it up.", "tokens": [51493, 961, 385, 992, 309, 493, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 224236, "start": 2265.76, "end": 2270.32, "text": " You take a highly complex document that possesses a genuine deep revision history.", "tokens": [51535, 509, 747, 257, 5405, 3997, 4166, 300, 17490, 279, 257, 16699, 2452, 34218, 2503, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 224236, "start": 2270.5, "end": 2270.78, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51772, 1033, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1614140873461698, "compression_ratio": 1.5918367346938775, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620024363174114e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 227078, "start": 2270.78, "end": 2280.5600000000004, "text": " Imagine a dense, multi-stage technical essay or a complex mathematical proof where specific derivations are introduced in a highly rigid chronological order.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 257, 18011, 11, 4825, 12, 17882, 6191, 16238, 420, 257, 3997, 18894, 8177, 689, 2685, 10151, 763, 366, 7268, 294, 257, 5405, 22195, 19393, 4383, 1668, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 227078, "start": 2280.6400000000003, "end": 2280.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50858, 1779, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 227078, "start": 2280.9, "end": 2285.6000000000004, "text": " So, step C absolutely relies on the foundation built in step B.", "tokens": [50871, 407, 11, 1823, 383, 3122, 30910, 322, 264, 7030, 3094, 294, 1823, 363, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 227078, "start": 2285.7000000000003, "end": 2287.84, "text": " Which in turn relies entirely on step A.", "tokens": [51111, 3013, 294, 1261, 30910, 7696, 322, 1823, 316, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 227078, "start": 2287.96, "end": 2288.1600000000003, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51224, 1079, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 227078, "start": 2288.32, "end": 2288.94, "text": " Very structured.", "tokens": [51242, 4372, 18519, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 227078, "start": 2289.26, "end": 2294.3, "text": " You provide the AI model only with the final draft, the polished, observable endpoint.", "tokens": [51289, 509, 2893, 264, 7318, 2316, 787, 365, 264, 2572, 11206, 11, 264, 29079, 11, 9951, 712, 35795, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 227078, "start": 2294.86, "end": 2298.6200000000003, "text": " You intentionally withhold all the intermediate drafts and the history of its construction.", "tokens": [51569, 509, 22062, 48867, 439, 264, 19376, 11206, 82, 293, 264, 2503, 295, 1080, 6435, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327369234977512, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.5540275189889217e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 229862, "start": 2298.62, "end": 2304.0, "text": " You then command the model to reconstruct those hidden intermediate drafts from scratch.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 550, 5622, 264, 2316, 281, 31499, 729, 7633, 19376, 11206, 82, 490, 8459, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10926671738320208, "compression_ratio": 1.467455621301775, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051728510771637e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 229862, "start": 2304.8399999999997, "end": 2313.54, "text": " You are essentially demanding that the AI generate the complex historical trajectory it supposedly used to arrive at the conclusion it is currently looking at.", "tokens": [50676, 509, 366, 4476, 19960, 300, 264, 7318, 8460, 264, 3997, 8584, 21512, 309, 20581, 1143, 281, 8881, 412, 264, 10063, 309, 307, 4362, 1237, 412, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10926671738320208, "compression_ratio": 1.467455621301775, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051728510771637e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 231354, "start": 2313.54, "end": 2316.82, "text": " And this is where the trap snaps shut on superficial models.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 11487, 19206, 5309, 322, 34622, 5245, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10487517150672707, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619896648153998e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 231354, "start": 2316.96, "end": 2320.56, "text": " Because there are infinite ways to fake a path to an endpoint, right?", "tokens": [50536, 1436, 456, 366, 13785, 2098, 281, 7592, 257, 3100, 281, 364, 35795, 11, 558, 30, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10487517150672707, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619896648153998e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 231354, "start": 2320.66, "end": 2321.12, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50721, 7587, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10487517150672707, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619896648153998e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 231354, "start": 2321.6, "end": 2332.92, "text": " An AI model that has simply memorized vast amounts of text, or one that uses statistical fluency to pattern match its way to a plausible sounding output, will fail catastrophically.", "tokens": [50768, 1107, 7318, 2316, 300, 575, 2935, 46677, 8369, 11663, 295, 2487, 11, 420, 472, 300, 4960, 22820, 5029, 3020, 281, 5102, 2995, 1080, 636, 281, 257, 39925, 24931, 5598, 11, 486, 3061, 28363, 984, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10487517150672707, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619896648153998e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 233292, "start": 2332.92, "end": 2339.48, "text": " It will generate a history that sounds superficially coherent to a layman, but is logically shattered upon close inspection.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 486, 8460, 257, 2503, 300, 3263, 23881, 2270, 36239, 281, 257, 2360, 1601, 11, 457, 307, 38887, 35209, 3564, 1998, 22085, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10475309768525681, "compression_ratio": 1.7560137457044673, "no_speech_prob": 2.0929850734485722e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 233292, "start": 2339.7000000000003, "end": 2347.32, "text": " A fluent but incompetent model will make profound chronological errors that violate the internal dependency structure of the logic.", "tokens": [50704, 316, 40799, 457, 41602, 317, 2316, 486, 652, 14382, 19393, 4383, 13603, 300, 37478, 264, 6920, 33621, 3877, 295, 264, 9952, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10475309768525681, "compression_ratio": 1.7560137457044673, "no_speech_prob": 2.0929850734485722e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 233292, "start": 2347.98, "end": 2358.86, "text": " It might hallucinate a draft where it places a grand conclusion in draft two, entirely forgetting that the foundational premise required to support that conclusion isn't introduced until draft three.", "tokens": [51118, 467, 1062, 35212, 13923, 257, 11206, 689, 309, 3190, 257, 2697, 10063, 294, 11206, 732, 11, 7696, 25428, 300, 264, 32195, 22045, 4739, 281, 1406, 300, 10063, 1943, 380, 7268, 1826, 11206, 1045, 13, 51662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10475309768525681, "compression_ratio": 1.7560137457044673, "no_speech_prob": 2.0929850734485722e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 233292, "start": 2359.2000000000003, "end": 2361.42, "text": " It will build the roof before it pours the foundation.", "tokens": [51679, 467, 486, 1322, 264, 8418, 949, 309, 2016, 82, 264, 7030, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10475309768525681, "compression_ratio": 1.7560137457044673, "no_speech_prob": 2.0929850734485722e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 236142, "start": 2361.42, "end": 2362.58, "text": " Yes, exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 2293, 13, 50423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11264099321867291, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.876099969821965e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 236142, "start": 2362.78, "end": 2370.78, "text": " It is the exact same dynamic as a stern math teacher demanding that a high school student show their work on a complex calculus exam.", "tokens": [50433, 467, 307, 264, 1900, 912, 8546, 382, 257, 38312, 5221, 5027, 19960, 300, 257, 1090, 1395, 3107, 855, 641, 589, 322, 257, 3997, 33400, 1139, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11264099321867291, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.876099969821965e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 236142, "start": 2370.9, "end": 2371.92, "text": " Oh, perfect analogy.", "tokens": [50839, 876, 11, 2176, 21663, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11264099321867291, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.876099969821965e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 236142, "start": 2371.92, "end": 2382.58, "text": " If the student merely memorized the answer key they stole from the teacher's desk, or if they copied off the genius sitting next to them, they will write down the correct final number at the bottom of the page.", "tokens": [50890, 759, 264, 3107, 17003, 46677, 264, 1867, 2141, 436, 16326, 490, 264, 5027, 311, 10026, 11, 420, 498, 436, 25365, 766, 264, 14017, 3798, 958, 281, 552, 11, 436, 486, 2464, 760, 264, 3006, 2572, 1230, 412, 264, 2767, 295, 264, 3028, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11264099321867291, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.876099969821965e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 236142, "start": 2382.94, "end": 2385.1, "text": " The endpoint is flawless.", "tokens": [51441, 440, 35795, 307, 45693, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11264099321867291, "compression_ratio": 1.594488188976378, "no_speech_prob": 1.876099969821965e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 238510, "start": 2385.1, "end": 2394.2, "text": " But when the teacher demands they reconstruct the steps, the cheating student will write down a sequence of mathematical gibberish that doesn't logically connect.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 264, 5027, 15107, 436, 31499, 264, 4439, 11, 264, 18309, 3107, 486, 2464, 760, 257, 8310, 295, 18894, 4553, 43189, 300, 1177, 380, 38887, 1745, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10661241081025866, "compression_ratio": 1.581896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620038457802356e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 238510, "start": 2394.46, "end": 2398.16, "text": " The internal struggle of the derivation is the actual proof of understanding.", "tokens": [50833, 440, 6920, 7799, 295, 264, 10151, 399, 307, 264, 3539, 8177, 295, 3701, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10661241081025866, "compression_ratio": 1.581896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620038457802356e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 238510, "start": 2398.6, "end": 2398.8199999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51040, 1779, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10661241081025866, "compression_ratio": 1.581896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620038457802356e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 238510, "start": 2398.96, "end": 2405.46, "text": " And in the context of evaluating artificial intelligence, reflexive reconstruction solves a massive structural problem.", "tokens": [51058, 400, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 27479, 11677, 7599, 11, 23802, 488, 31565, 39890, 257, 5994, 15067, 1154, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10661241081025866, "compression_ratio": 1.581896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620038457802356e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 240546, "start": 2405.46, "end": 2412.28, "text": " It provides an empirical selection signal that separates genuine cognition from mere statistical mimicry.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 6417, 364, 31886, 9450, 6358, 300, 34149, 16699, 46905, 490, 8401, 22820, 31075, 627, 13, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1585738415620765, "compression_ratio": 1.379746835443038, "no_speech_prob": 1.483994676275413e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 240546, "start": 2412.28, "end": 2418.44, "text": " So you can rigorously test whether a system has actually internalized the load-bearing logic of a path.", "tokens": [50706, 407, 291, 393, 42191, 5098, 1500, 1968, 257, 1185, 575, 767, 6920, 1602, 264, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 9952, 295, 257, 3100, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1585738415620765, "compression_ratio": 1.379746835443038, "no_speech_prob": 1.483994676275413e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 240546, "start": 2418.56, "end": 2418.92, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51020, 7587, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1585738415620765, "compression_ratio": 1.379746835443038, "no_speech_prob": 1.483994676275413e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 241892, "start": 2418.92, "end": 2429.48, "text": " A model that correctly identifies which intermediate steps are structurally necessary, rather than just generating text that is locally plausible, proves its deep competence from the inside out.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 2316, 300, 8944, 34597, 597, 19376, 4439, 366, 6594, 6512, 4818, 11, 2831, 813, 445, 17746, 2487, 300, 307, 16143, 39925, 11, 25019, 1080, 2452, 39965, 490, 264, 1854, 484, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09948903095873096, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.868602494958793e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 241892, "start": 2429.48, "end": 2433.06, "text": " We have discovered a way to mathematically x-ray the ghost in the machine.", "tokens": [50893, 492, 362, 6941, 257, 636, 281, 44003, 2031, 12, 3458, 264, 8359, 294, 264, 3479, 13, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09948903095873096, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.868602494958793e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 241892, "start": 2433.78, "end": 2440.96, "text": " It changes everything about how we design, audit, and ultimately trust the deeply complex systems that increasingly run our world.", "tokens": [51108, 467, 2962, 1203, 466, 577, 321, 1715, 11, 17748, 11, 293, 6284, 3361, 264, 8760, 3997, 3652, 300, 12980, 1190, 527, 1002, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09948903095873096, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.868602494958793e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 244096, "start": 2440.96, "end": 2453.12, "text": " We have covered an immense amount of conceptual ground today.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 5343, 364, 22920, 2372, 295, 24106, 2727, 965, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837507360121782, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970834881644084e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 244096, "start": 2453.12, "end": 2460.02, "text": " I mean, we started by staring at two identical AI models and discovering that the endpoint alone is a dangerous illusion.", "tokens": [50973, 286, 914, 11, 321, 1409, 538, 18043, 412, 732, 14800, 7318, 5245, 293, 24773, 300, 264, 35795, 3312, 307, 257, 5795, 18854, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837507360121782, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970834881644084e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 244096, "start": 2460.46, "end": 2460.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51340, 1779, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837507360121782, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970834881644084e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 244096, "start": 2460.92, "end": 2465.92, "text": " We learned that true trust is not a static badge or a certificate you earn once and hang on a wall.", "tokens": [51363, 492, 3264, 300, 2074, 3361, 307, 406, 257, 13437, 25797, 420, 257, 15953, 291, 6012, 1564, 293, 3967, 322, 257, 2929, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837507360121782, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970834881644084e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 244096, "start": 2466.2, "end": 2470.94, "text": " It is an active, continuous, deeply mathematical relationship with the system's past.", "tokens": [51627, 467, 307, 364, 4967, 11, 10957, 11, 8760, 18894, 2480, 365, 264, 1185, 311, 1791, 13, 51864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14837507360121782, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970834881644084e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 247096, "start": 2470.96, "end": 2485.84, "text": " And we unpacked the vital structural difference between simply reloading a saved game, merely reconstructing a state, and the heavy burden of true repair, where you must permanently fix the underlying mechanism of compromise so the future history remains safe.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 26699, 292, 264, 11707, 15067, 2649, 1296, 2935, 25628, 278, 257, 6624, 1216, 11, 17003, 31499, 278, 257, 1785, 11, 293, 264, 4676, 12578, 295, 2074, 10535, 11, 689, 291, 1633, 24042, 3191, 264, 14217, 7513, 295, 18577, 370, 264, 2027, 2503, 7023, 3273, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06820746058041287, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760837489587237e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 247096, "start": 2485.92, "end": 2486.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51113, 1079, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06820746058041287, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760837489587237e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 247096, "start": 2486.8, "end": 2498.2, "text": " We geometrically redefined hacking as maneuvering through a maze of effective paths, and we analyzed how admissibility certificates utilize physical trust anchors to prevent an infinite regress of forgery.", "tokens": [51157, 492, 12956, 81, 984, 38818, 2001, 31422, 382, 25976, 278, 807, 257, 33032, 295, 4942, 14518, 11, 293, 321, 28181, 577, 5910, 891, 2841, 32941, 16117, 4001, 3361, 12723, 830, 281, 4871, 364, 13785, 1121, 735, 295, 337, 7337, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06820746058041287, "compression_ratio": 1.6130136986301369, "no_speech_prob": 2.1760837489587237e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 249820, "start": 2498.2, "end": 2501.2799999999997, "text": " We discover that the history principle governs everything.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 4411, 300, 264, 2503, 8665, 1980, 82, 1203, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1173782730102539, "compression_ratio": 1.5198237885462555, "no_speech_prob": 2.4660273822973977e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 249820, "start": 2502.12, "end": 2517.3799999999997, "text": " Whether you are interrogating an AI model's training data, reviewing the maintenance logs of a Boeing 747, demanding the raw data behind a psychological study, or establishing the chain of custody in a murder trial, trust lives in the trajectory.", "tokens": [50561, 8503, 291, 366, 24871, 990, 364, 7318, 2316, 311, 3097, 1412, 11, 19576, 264, 11258, 20820, 295, 257, 30831, 1614, 14060, 11, 19960, 264, 8936, 1412, 2261, 257, 14346, 2979, 11, 420, 22494, 264, 5021, 295, 26976, 294, 257, 6568, 7308, 11, 3361, 2909, 294, 264, 21512, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1173782730102539, "compression_ratio": 1.5198237885462555, "no_speech_prob": 2.4660273822973977e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 249820, "start": 2517.7999999999997, "end": 2519.68, "text": " The math of admissibility is universal.", "tokens": [51345, 440, 5221, 295, 5910, 891, 2841, 307, 11455, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1173782730102539, "compression_ratio": 1.5198237885462555, "no_speech_prob": 2.4660273822973977e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 251968, "start": 2519.68, "end": 2523.8399999999997, "text": " It forces a necessary evolution in how we interact with technology.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5874, 257, 4818, 9303, 294, 577, 321, 4648, 365, 2899, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11146122325550425, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 2.544093841844175e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 251968, "start": 2524.2, "end": 2533.56, "text": " But as we conclude this deep dive, I want to leave you, the listener, with a deeply personal, philosophical application of flictions math to mull over.", "tokens": [50591, 583, 382, 321, 16886, 341, 2452, 9192, 11, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 365, 257, 8760, 2973, 11, 25066, 3861, 295, 932, 15607, 5221, 281, 275, 858, 670, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11146122325550425, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 2.544093841844175e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 251968, "start": 2533.62, "end": 2534.64, "text": " Oh, this is the part I love.", "tokens": [51062, 876, 11, 341, 307, 264, 644, 286, 959, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11146122325550425, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 2.544093841844175e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 251968, "start": 2534.74, "end": 2540.72, "text": " We have spent this entire time talking about AI, airplanes, software compilation, and legal frameworks.", "tokens": [51118, 492, 362, 4418, 341, 2302, 565, 1417, 466, 7318, 11, 32947, 11, 4722, 40261, 11, 293, 5089, 29834, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11146122325550425, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 2.544093841844175e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 251968, "start": 2540.98, "end": 2544.74, "text": " But consider human civilization. Consider your own personal identity.", "tokens": [51430, 583, 1949, 1952, 18036, 13, 17416, 428, 1065, 2973, 6575, 13, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11146122325550425, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 2.544093841844175e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 251968, "start": 2544.8799999999997, "end": 2547.46, "text": " Applying this to the human condition is a profound pivot.", "tokens": [51625, 3132, 7310, 341, 281, 264, 1952, 4188, 307, 257, 14382, 14538, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11146122325550425, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 2.544093841844175e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 254746, "start": 2547.46, "end": 2551.82, "text": " You and I, and everyone listening, are incredibly complex adaptive systems.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 293, 286, 11, 293, 1518, 4764, 11, 366, 6252, 3997, 27912, 3652, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10200227045379909, "compression_ratio": 1.700657894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256817920450866e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 254746, "start": 2552.48, "end": 2560.54, "text": " We are the cumulative sum of our historical adaptations, our accumulated emotional and physical damage, our learned behaviors, and our agonizing repairs.", "tokens": [50616, 492, 366, 264, 38379, 2408, 295, 527, 8584, 44465, 11, 527, 31346, 6863, 293, 4001, 4344, 11, 527, 3264, 15501, 11, 293, 527, 623, 266, 3319, 28823, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10200227045379909, "compression_ratio": 1.700657894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256817920450866e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 254746, "start": 2560.82, "end": 2560.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51033, 1779, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10200227045379909, "compression_ratio": 1.700657894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256817920450866e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 254746, "start": 2561.16, "end": 2568.34, "text": " If human memory, or our current personality, is merely our endpoint, how do we certify the history of how we became who we are?", "tokens": [51050, 759, 1952, 4675, 11, 420, 527, 2190, 9033, 11, 307, 17003, 527, 35795, 11, 577, 360, 321, 5351, 2505, 264, 2503, 295, 577, 321, 3062, 567, 321, 366, 30, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10200227045379909, "compression_ratio": 1.700657894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256817920450866e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 254746, "start": 2568.6, "end": 2576.54, "text": " Our personal provenance and lineage are the stories we tell ourselves, the journals we keep, the deep relationships we maintain that witness our growth.", "tokens": [51422, 2621, 2973, 12785, 719, 293, 38257, 366, 264, 3676, 321, 980, 4175, 11, 264, 29621, 321, 1066, 11, 264, 2452, 6159, 321, 6909, 300, 7286, 527, 4599, 13, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10200227045379909, "compression_ratio": 1.700657894736842, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256817920450866e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 257654, "start": 2576.54, "end": 2579.7, "text": " On a much grander scale, think about society.", "tokens": [50365, 1282, 257, 709, 2697, 260, 4373, 11, 519, 466, 4086, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10089728652790028, "compression_ratio": 1.5956521739130434, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191840840866888e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 257654, "start": 2580.4, "end": 2589.36, "text": " If we as a civilization lose the ability to explain our own history, if we sever our civilizational chain of custody, we are in peril.", "tokens": [50558, 759, 321, 382, 257, 18036, 3624, 264, 3485, 281, 2903, 527, 1065, 2503, 11, 498, 321, 2802, 527, 5605, 590, 1478, 5021, 295, 26976, 11, 321, 366, 294, 46118, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10089728652790028, "compression_ratio": 1.5956521739130434, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191840840866888e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 257654, "start": 2589.48, "end": 2590.12, "text": " We really are.", "tokens": [51012, 492, 534, 366, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10089728652790028, "compression_ratio": 1.5956521739130434, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191840840866888e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 257654, "start": 2590.3, "end": 2599.16, "text": " If we forget the specific, painful reasons why our laws and institutions were built the way they were, do we lose our admissibility as a society?", "tokens": [51053, 759, 321, 2870, 264, 2685, 11, 11697, 4112, 983, 527, 6064, 293, 8142, 645, 3094, 264, 636, 436, 645, 11, 360, 321, 3624, 527, 5910, 891, 2841, 382, 257, 4086, 30, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10089728652790028, "compression_ratio": 1.5956521739130434, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191840840866888e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 257654, "start": 2599.52, "end": 2600.6, "text": " Like a chilling question.", "tokens": [51514, 1743, 257, 31047, 1168, 13, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10089728652790028, "compression_ratio": 1.5956521739130434, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191840840866888e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 260060, "start": 2600.6, "end": 2612.24, "text": " If we only look at the endpoint of where we are today, without deeply understanding the load-bearing historical steps of how we got here, are we simply fluently imitating a civilization without actually understanding how to maintain it?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 787, 574, 412, 264, 35795, 295, 689, 321, 366, 965, 11, 1553, 8760, 3701, 264, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 8584, 4439, 295, 577, 321, 658, 510, 11, 366, 321, 2935, 5029, 2276, 566, 16350, 257, 18036, 1553, 767, 3701, 577, 281, 6909, 309, 30, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07955771750146216, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164202760800334e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 260060, "start": 2612.36, "end": 2612.66, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50953, 3153, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07955771750146216, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164202760800334e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 260060, "start": 2612.7599999999998, "end": 2619.08, "text": " If we cannot reconstruct our own history, we will be entirely incapable of repairing ourselves when we inevitably break.", "tokens": [50973, 759, 321, 2644, 31499, 527, 1065, 2503, 11, 321, 486, 312, 7696, 44174, 295, 46158, 4175, 562, 321, 28171, 1821, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07955771750146216, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164202760800334e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 260060, "start": 2619.3199999999997, "end": 2622.14, "text": " That is a staggering and necessary thought to hold on to.", "tokens": [51301, 663, 307, 257, 42974, 293, 4818, 1194, 281, 1797, 322, 281, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07955771750146216, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164202760800334e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 262214, "start": 2622.14, "end": 2626.14, "text": " Thank you so much for joining us on this intense intellectual journey today.", "tokens": [50365, 1044, 291, 370, 709, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 9447, 12576, 4671, 965, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, 