7, "text": " mind-blowing to me. It really is an incredible experiment. Zhang et al. decided to test a very simple", "tokens": [51056, 1575, 12, 43788, 281, 385, 13, 467, 534, 307, 364, 4651, 5120, 13, 17729, 1030, 419, 13, 3047, 281, 1500, 257, 588, 2199, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07863778970679458, "compression_ratio": 1.595330739299611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338329123123275e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 24360, "start": 264.65999999999997, "end": 273.5, "text": " yet radical hypothesis. So they took a fully pre-trained transformer model, right? Yes. And just so we're all", "tokens": [51418, 1939, 12001, 17291, 13, 407, 436, 1890, 257, 4498, 659, 12, 17227, 2001, 31782, 2316, 11, 558, 30, 1079, 13, 400, 445, 370, 321, 434, 439, 51860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07863778970679458, "compression_ratio": 1.595330739299611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7338329123123275e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 27350, "start": 273.5, "end": 279.52, "text": " on the same page here. Pre-trained means this AI has already read like a massive chunk of the", "tokens": [50365, 322, 264, 912, 3028, 510, 13, 6001, 12, 17227, 2001, 1355, 341, 7318, 575, 1217, 1401, 411, 257, 5994, 16635, 295, 264, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07387228573069853, "compression_ratio": 1.691029900332226, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118305892741217e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 27350, "start": 279.52, "end": 284.08, "text": " entire internet. Right. And it's already spent months just absorbing text. Yeah. It knows grammar. It knows", "tokens": [50666, 2302, 4705, 13, 1779, 13, 400, 309, 311, 1217, 4418, 2493, 445, 38720, 2487, 13, 865, 13, 467, 3255, 22317, 13, 467, 3255, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07387228573069853, "compression_ratio": 1.691029900332226, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118305892741217e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 27350, "start": 284.08, "end": 288.6, "text": " historical facts. It knows how to predict the next word in a sentence perfectly. It is fully functional.", "tokens": [50894, 8584, 9130, 13, 467, 3255, 577, 281, 6069, 264, 958, 1349, 294, 257, 8174, 6239, 13, 467, 307, 4498, 11745, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07387228573069853, "compression_ratio": 1.691029900332226, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118305892741217e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 27350, "start": 288.8, "end": 294.58, "text": " It has a deeply established internal organization. That's the key. So they took this highly capable", "tokens": [51130, 467, 575, 257, 8760, 7545, 6920, 4475, 13, 663, 311, 264, 2141, 13, 407, 436, 1890, 341, 5405, 8189, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07387228573069853, "compression_ratio": 1.691029900332226, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118305892741217e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 27350, "start": 294.58, "end": 300.56, "text": " pre-trained model and they subjected it to reinforcement learning or RL. Okay. Reinforcement learning.", "tokens": [51419, 659, 12, 17227, 2001, 2316, 293, 436, 32153, 309, 281, 29280, 2539, 420, 497, 43, 13, 1033, 13, 42116, 9382, 2539, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07387228573069853, "compression_ratio": 1.691029900332226, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118305892741217e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 30056, "start": 300.56, "end": 304.88, "text": " Let's define that really quick. That is where we stop just having it passively read text and we start", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 6964, 300, 534, 1702, 13, 663, 307, 689, 321, 1590, 445, 1419, 309, 1320, 3413, 1401, 2487, 293, 321, 722, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03333271615873507, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.8378532203044973e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 30056, "start": 304.88, "end": 309.62, "text": " giving it a specific goal, right? Exactly. Like solve this complex math problem. And we give it a", "tokens": [50581, 2902, 309, 257, 2685, 3387, 11, 558, 30, 7587, 13, 1743, 5039, 341, 3997, 5221, 1154, 13, 400, 321, 976, 309, 257, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03333271615873507, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.8378532203044973e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 30056, "start": 309.62, "end": 313.76, "text": " mathematical reward when it gets the right answer. Kind of like giving a dog a treat when it does a", "tokens": [50818, 18894, 7782, 562, 309, 2170, 264, 558, 1867, 13, 9242, 295, 411, 2902, 257, 3000, 257, 2387, 562, 309, 775, 257, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03333271615873507, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.8378532203044973e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 30056, "start": 313.76, "end": 319.92, "text": " trick. That's a perfect analogy. Yeah. You are actively trying to teach it a new specific capability", "tokens": [51025, 4282, 13, 663, 311, 257, 2176, 21663, 13, 865, 13, 509, 366, 13022, 1382, 281, 2924, 309, 257, 777, 2685, 13759, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03333271615873507, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.8378532203044973e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 30056, "start": 319.92, "end": 327.1, "text": " that it didn't have before. Right. Now, usually when you do RL, you let the algorithm adjust all the", "tokens": [51333, 300, 309, 994, 380, 362, 949, 13, 1779, 13, 823, 11, 2673, 562, 291, 360, 497, 43, 11, 291, 718, 264, 9284, 4369, 439, 264, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03333271615873507, "compression_ratio": 1.6589403973509933, "no_speech_prob": 1.8378532203044973e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 32710, "start": 327.1, "end": 331.86, "text": " parameters in the model. You let the whole digital brain adapt to the reward signal. You use your", "tokens": [50365, 9834, 294, 264, 2316, 13, 509, 718, 264, 1379, 4562, 3567, 6231, 281, 264, 7782, 6358, 13, 509, 764, 428, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0780704262551297, "compression_ratio": 1.6147540983606556, "no_speech_prob": 1.3091414887908548e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 32710, "start": 331.86, "end": 340.02000000000004, "text": " nominal freedom. Right. But Zhang et al didn't do that. Instead, they froze almost everything. When", "tokens": [50603, 41641, 5645, 13, 1779, 13, 583, 17729, 1030, 419, 994, 380, 360, 300, 13, 7156, 11, 436, 46077, 1920, 1203, 13, 1133, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0780704262551297, "compression_ratio": 1.6147540983606556, "no_speech_prob": 1.3091414887908548e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 32710, "start": 340.02000000000004, "end": 345.04, "text": " you say froze, you mean they literally locked the math down. Literally locked it down. The entire", "tokens": [51011, 291, 584, 46077, 11, 291, 914, 436, 3736, 9376, 264, 5221, 760, 13, 23768, 9376, 309, 760, 13, 440, 2302, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0780704262551297, "compression_ratio": 1.6147540983606556, "no_speech_prob": 1.3091414887908548e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 32710, "start": 345.04, "end": 350.8, "text": " network, every single parameter was completely rigid except for one single transformer layer. Wow.", "tokens": [51262, 3209, 11, 633, 2167, 13075, 390, 2584, 22195, 3993, 337, 472, 2167, 31782, 4583, 13, 3153, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0780704262551297, "compression_ratio": 1.6147540983606556, "no_speech_prob": 1.3091414887908548e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 35080, "start": 350.8, "end": 356.68, "text": " They only allowed that one specific layer to learn and change its numbers in response to the reward.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 787, 4350, 300, 472, 2685, 4583, 281, 1466, 293, 1319, 1080, 3547, 294, 4134, 281, 264, 7782, 13, 50659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0880045544017445, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.1156460954717118e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 35080, "start": 356.86, "end": 361.08, "text": " So they trained a single layer and froze every other parameter in the whole model.", "tokens": [50668, 407, 436, 8895, 257, 2167, 4583, 293, 46077, 633, 661, 13075, 294, 264, 1379, 2316, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0880045544017445, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.1156460954717118e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 35080, "start": 361.46000000000004, "end": 366.90000000000003, "text": " Out of billions of connections, they only unlocked a tiny, tiny fraction. Exactly. Just a fraction of a", "tokens": [50898, 5925, 295, 17375, 295, 9271, 11, 436, 787, 30180, 257, 5870, 11, 5870, 14135, 13, 7587, 13, 1449, 257, 14135, 295, 257, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0880045544017445, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.1156460954717118e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 35080, "start": 366.90000000000003, "end": 371.12, "text": " percent. And the big reveal here, the shocking result that you really need to internalize,", "tokens": [51170, 3043, 13, 400, 264, 955, 10658, 510, 11, 264, 18776, 1874, 300, 291, 534, 643, 281, 6920, 1125, 11, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0880045544017445, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.1156460954717118e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 35080, "start": 371.28000000000003, "end": 376.1, "text": " is that this single layer training didn't just like barely work. No, it didn't just scrape by.", "tokens": [51389, 307, 300, 341, 2167, 4583, 3097, 994, 380, 445, 411, 10268, 589, 13, 883, 11, 309, 994, 380, 445, 32827, 538, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0880045544017445, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.1156460954717118e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 37610, "start": 376.1, "end": 381.66, "text": " It recovered most of the performance gain that you would get from full parameter training. And in some", "tokens": [50365, 467, 19542, 881, 295, 264, 3389, 6052, 300, 291, 576, 483, 490, 1577, 13075, 3097, 13, 400, 294, 512, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043322696480699766, "compression_ratio": 1.726890756302521, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050152100791857e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 37610, "start": 381.66, "end": 388.5, "text": " cases, and this is the part that gets me training, just that one single layer actually exceeded the", "tokens": [50643, 3331, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 644, 300, 2170, 385, 3097, 11, 445, 300, 472, 2167, 4583, 767, 38026, 264, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043322696480699766, "compression_ratio": 1.726890756302521, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050152100791857e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 37610, "start": 388.5, "end": 393.90000000000003, "text": " performance of full parameter training. Well, I mean, let that sink in for a moment. It's crazy. You have a", "tokens": [50985, 3389, 295, 1577, 13075, 3097, 13, 1042, 11, 286, 914, 11, 718, 300, 9500, 294, 337, 257, 1623, 13, 467, 311, 3219, 13, 509, 362, 257, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043322696480699766, "compression_ratio": 1.726890756302521, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050152100791857e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 37610, "start": 393.90000000000003, "end": 400.70000000000005, "text": " model with billions of parameters distributed across dozens of layers. You hold all but one of those", "tokens": [51255, 2316, 365, 17375, 295, 9834, 12631, 2108, 18431, 295, 7914, 13, 509, 1797, 439, 457, 472, 295, 729, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043322696480699766, "compression_ratio": 1.726890756302521, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050152100791857e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 40070, "start": 400.7, "end": 407.18, "text": " layers completely rigid. You only let a fraction of a percent of the brain adapt. And it still learns", "tokens": [50365, 7914, 2584, 22195, 13, 509, 787, 718, 257, 14135, 295, 257, 3043, 295, 264, 3567, 6231, 13, 400, 309, 920, 27152, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08357247852143787, "compression_ratio": 1.592156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2543537172490793e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 40070, "start": 407.18, "end": 413.14, "text": " the new reinforcement task just as well, and sometimes even better, than if you had let the", "tokens": [50689, 264, 777, 29280, 5633, 445, 382, 731, 11, 293, 2171, 754, 1101, 11, 813, 498, 291, 632, 718, 264, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08357247852143787, "compression_ratio": 1.592156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2543537172490793e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 40070, "start": 413.14, "end": 418.48, "text": " entire brain adapt. Now, you listening might be thinking, okay, well, maybe they just got lucky on", "tokens": [50987, 2302, 3567, 6231, 13, 823, 11, 291, 4764, 1062, 312, 1953, 11, 1392, 11, 731, 11, 1310, 436, 445, 658, 6356, 322, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08357247852143787, "compression_ratio": 1.592156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2543537172490793e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 40070, "start": 418.48, "end": 420.2, "text": " one specific test. Right.", "tokens": [51254, 472, 2685, 1500, 13, 1779, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08357247852143787, "compression_ratio": 1.592156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2543537172490793e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 40070, "start": 420.41999999999996, "end": 421.76, "text": " Like maybe it was a fluke.", "tokens": [51351, 1743, 1310, 309, 390, 257, 5029, 330, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08357247852143787, "compression_ratio": 1.592156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2543537172490793e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 40070, "start": 421.88, "end": 424.65999999999997, "text": " That's always the first question in science. Was it a fluke?", "tokens": [51424, 663, 311, 1009, 264, 700, 1168, 294, 3497, 13, 3027, 309, 257, 5029, 330, 30, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08357247852143787, "compression_ratio": 1.592156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2543537172490793e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 42466, "start": 424.66, "end": 429.16, "text": " But to prove this isn't just some weird anomaly, let's look at the sheer breadth of this finding", "tokens": [50365, 583, 281, 7081, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 512, 3657, 42737, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 23061, 35862, 295, 341, 5006, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11467724877434808, "compression_ratio": 1.618705035971223, "no_speech_prob": 1.2734876087688862e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 42466, "start": 429.16, "end": 434.04, "text": " directly from the source material. The Fliction paper notes that this wasn't just true for one", "tokens": [50590, 3838, 490, 264, 4009, 2527, 13, 440, 3235, 4105, 3035, 5570, 300, 341, 2067, 380, 445, 2074, 337, 472, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11467724877434808, "compression_ratio": 1.618705035971223, "no_speech_prob": 1.2734876087688862e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 42466, "start": 434.04, "end": 436.14000000000004, "text": " isolated model on a random Tuesday.", "tokens": [50834, 14621, 2316, 322, 257, 4974, 10017, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11467724877434808, "compression_ratio": 1.618705035971223, "no_speech_prob": 1.2734876087688862e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 42466, "start": 436.34000000000003, "end": 440.16, "text": " No, the Zhang et al. study was massive. It spanned seven different models.", "tokens": [50949, 883, 11, 264, 17729, 1030, 419, 13, 2979, 390, 5994, 13, 467, 637, 5943, 3407, 819, 5245, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11467724877434808, "compression_ratio": 1.618705035971223, "no_speech_prob": 1.2734876087688862e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 42466, "start": 440.26000000000005, "end": 440.76000000000005, "text": " Seven models.", "tokens": [51145, 14868, 5245, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11467724877434808, "compression_ratio": 1.618705035971223, "no_speech_prob": 1.2734876087688862e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 42466, "start": 441.14000000000004, "end": 447.98, "text": " Seven models across two entirely distinct model families. So it's not just an architectural quirk of", "tokens": [51189, 14868, 5245, 2108, 732, 7696, 10644, 2316, 4466, 13, 407, 309, 311, 406, 445, 364, 26621, 421, 18610, 295, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11467724877434808, "compression_ratio": 1.618705035971223, "no_speech_prob": 1.2734876087688862e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 42466, "start": 447.98, "end": 450.24, "text": " one specific brand of AI. Right.", "tokens": [51531, 472, 2685, 3360, 295, 7318, 13, 1779, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11467724877434808, "compression_ratio": 1.618705035971223, "no_speech_prob": 1.2734876087688862e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 45024, "start": 450.24, "end": 454.76, "text": " Furthermore, they tested this using three different reinforcement learning algorithms.", "tokens": [50365, 23999, 11, 436, 8246, 341, 1228, 1045, 819, 29280, 2539, 14642, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15439930477657834, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381167697669062e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 45024, "start": 455.66, "end": 460.12, "text": " So it is not a quirk of the specific math used to update the weights either.", "tokens": [50636, 407, 309, 307, 406, 257, 421, 18610, 295, 264, 2685, 5221, 1143, 281, 5623, 264, 17443, 2139, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15439930477657834, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381167697669062e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 45024, "start": 460.12, "end": 466.06, "text": " And the tasks they used to test this were really intense. It wasn't just basic text generation,", "tokens": [50859, 400, 264, 9608, 436, 1143, 281, 1500, 341, 645, 534, 9447, 13, 467, 2067, 380, 445, 3875, 2487, 5125, 11, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15439930477657834, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381167697669062e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 45024, "start": 466.28000000000003, "end": 469.16, "text": " like asking it to, you know, write a haiku about a cat.", "tokens": [51167, 411, 3365, 309, 281, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2464, 257, 324, 24320, 466, 257, 3857, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15439930477657834, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381167697669062e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 45024, "start": 469.26, "end": 470.82, "text": " No, they pushed these models hard.", "tokens": [51316, 883, 11, 436, 9152, 613, 5245, 1152, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15439930477657834, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381167697669062e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 45024, "start": 471.0, "end": 476.74, "text": " They tested this on domains ranging from competition-level mathematics to multi-step", "tokens": [51403, 814, 8246, 341, 322, 25514, 25532, 490, 6211, 12, 12418, 18666, 281, 4825, 12, 16792, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15439930477657834, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381167697669062e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 45024, "start": 476.74, "end": 478.34000000000003, "text": " agentic decision-making.", "tokens": [51690, 9461, 299, 3537, 12, 12402, 13, 51770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15439930477657834, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.4381167697669062e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 47834, "start": 478.34, "end": 483.38, "text": " And agentic decision-making, just to clarify, means the AI has to take an action, observe the", "tokens": [50365, 400, 9461, 299, 3537, 12, 12402, 11, 445, 281, 17594, 11, 1355, 264, 7318, 575, 281, 747, 364, 3069, 11, 11441, 264, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635907102222285, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918434105588464e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 47834, "start": 483.38, "end": 488.11999999999995, "text": " environment, see what changed, and then decide on the next action to achieve a long-term goal.", "tokens": [50617, 2823, 11, 536, 437, 3105, 11, 293, 550, 4536, 322, 264, 958, 3069, 281, 4584, 257, 938, 12, 7039, 3387, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635907102222285, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918434105588464e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 47834, "start": 488.23999999999995, "end": 490.79999999999995, "text": " It requires complex, sustained reasoning.", "tokens": [50860, 467, 7029, 3997, 11, 23389, 21577, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635907102222285, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918434105588464e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 47834, "start": 490.96, "end": 495.41999999999996, "text": " Exactly. And across all these variations, different models, different math, different incredibly hard", "tokens": [50996, 7587, 13, 400, 2108, 439, 613, 17840, 11, 819, 5245, 11, 819, 5221, 11, 819, 6252, 1152, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635907102222285, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918434105588464e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 47834, "start": 495.41999999999996, "end": 500.0, "text": " tasks, the exact same pattern held true. One layer was enough.", "tokens": [51219, 9608, 11, 264, 1900, 912, 5102, 5167, 2074, 13, 1485, 4583, 390, 1547, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635907102222285, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918434105588464e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 47834, "start": 500.41999999999996, "end": 505.32, "text": " But then this is the most crucial detail of this empirical finding. It isn't just that any single", "tokens": [51469, 583, 550, 341, 307, 264, 881, 11462, 2607, 295, 341, 31886, 5006, 13, 467, 1943, 380, 445, 300, 604, 2167, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635907102222285, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918434105588464e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 47834, "start": 505.32, "end": 506.05999999999995, "text": " layer is enough.", "tokens": [51714, 4583, 307, 1547, 13, 51751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635907102222285, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918434105588464e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 50606, "start": 506.06, "end": 509.42, "text": " Right. It is very specifically about which single layer is enough.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 467, 307, 588, 4682, 466, 597, 2167, 4583, 307, 1547, 13, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11739090051543846, "compression_ratio": 1.5275590551181102, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754526147883976e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 50606, "start": 509.42, "end": 515.62, "text": " Because these, like, magic layers, the ones capable of absorbing the training signal so effectively,", "tokens": [50533, 1436, 613, 11, 411, 11, 5585, 7914, 11, 264, 2306, 8189, 295, 38720, 264, 3097, 6358, 370, 8659, 11, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11739090051543846, "compression_ratio": 1.5275590551181102, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754526147883976e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 50606, "start": 515.84, "end": 518.52, "text": " they are not randomly distributed throughout the network.", "tokens": [50854, 436, 366, 406, 16979, 12631, 3710, 264, 3209, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11739090051543846, "compression_ratio": 1.5275590551181102, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754526147883976e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 50606, "start": 518.68, "end": 523.66, "text": " No. You don't just roll a die and pick layer 42 out of 100 and hope for the best.", "tokens": [50996, 883, 13, 509, 500, 380, 445, 3373, 257, 978, 293, 1888, 4583, 14034, 484, 295, 2319, 293, 1454, 337, 264, 1151, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11739090051543846, "compression_ratio": 1.5275590551181102, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754526147883976e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 50606, "start": 523.74, "end": 530.02, "text": " They reliably, consistently concentrate in the middle third of the network step.", "tokens": [51249, 814, 49927, 11, 14961, 18089, 294, 264, 2808, 2636, 295, 264, 3209, 1823, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11739090051543846, "compression_ratio": 1.5275590551181102, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754526147883976e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 53002, "start": 530.02, "end": 531.98, "text": " The middle third. Always.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2808, 2636, 13, 11270, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593183187338021, "compression_ratio": 1.7186311787072244, "no_speech_prob": 2.038968169651434e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 53002, "start": 532.38, "end": 537.36, "text": " The layers near the input end, so the very beginning of the model where the raw text first enters,", "tokens": [50483, 440, 7914, 2651, 264, 4846, 917, 11, 370, 264, 588, 2863, 295, 264, 2316, 689, 264, 8936, 2487, 700, 18780, 11, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593183187338021, "compression_ratio": 1.7186311787072244, "no_speech_prob": 2.038968169651434e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 53002, "start": 537.84, "end": 542.22, "text": " and the layers near the output end where the model is formulating its final answer to print on the", "tokens": [50756, 293, 264, 7914, 2651, 264, 5598, 917, 689, 264, 2316, 307, 1254, 12162, 1080, 2572, 1867, 281, 4482, 322, 264, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593183187338021, "compression_ratio": 1.7186311787072244, "no_speech_prob": 2.038968169651434e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 53002, "start": 542.22, "end": 547.1, "text": " screen, they recover substantially less performance when you train them in isolation.", "tokens": [50975, 2568, 11, 436, 8114, 30797, 1570, 3389, 562, 291, 3847, 552, 294, 16001, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593183187338021, "compression_ratio": 1.7186311787072244, "no_speech_prob": 2.038968169651434e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 53002, "start": 547.38, "end": 552.36, "text": " It is this specific depth-stable band right in the middle that does all the heavy lifting.", "tokens": [51233, 467, 307, 341, 2685, 7161, 12, 372, 712, 4116, 558, 294, 264, 2808, 300, 775, 439, 264, 4676, 15798, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593183187338021, "compression_ratio": 1.7186311787072244, "no_speech_prob": 2.038968169651434e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 53002, "start": 552.46, "end": 554.68, "text": " And this concentration is incredibly stable, right?", "tokens": [51487, 400, 341, 9856, 307, 6252, 8351, 11, 558, 30, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593183187338021, "compression_ratio": 1.7186311787072244, "no_speech_prob": 2.038968169651434e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 55468, "start": 554.68, "end": 559.12, "text": " Oh, absolutely. The source material points out that it holds up under three independent tests of", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 440, 4009, 2527, 2793, 484, 300, 309, 9190, 493, 833, 1045, 6695, 6921, 295, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568580155961969, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756348470899686e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 55468, "start": 559.12, "end": 559.8399999999999, "text": " generalization.", "tokens": [50587, 2674, 2144, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568580155961969, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756348470899686e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 55468, "start": 560.04, "end": 560.8199999999999, "text": " Okay. What were those?", "tokens": [50633, 1033, 13, 708, 645, 729, 30, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568580155961969, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756348470899686e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 55468, "start": 561.04, "end": 565.5, "text": " First, it holds across different training data sets within a fixed model and task.", "tokens": [50683, 2386, 11, 309, 9190, 2108, 819, 3097, 1412, 6352, 1951, 257, 6806, 2316, 293, 5633, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568580155961969, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756348470899686e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 55468, "start": 565.78, "end": 570.2399999999999, "text": " Second, it holds across a complete change of task domain, moving from that competition mat", "tokens": [50920, 5736, 11, 309, 9190, 2108, 257, 3566, 1319, 295, 5633, 9274, 11, 2684, 490, 300, 6211, 3803, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568580155961969, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756348470899686e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 55468, "start": 570.2399999999999, "end": 572.54, "text": " to the agentic decision-making we just mentioned.", "tokens": [51143, 281, 264, 9461, 299, 3537, 12, 12402, 321, 445, 2835, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568580155961969, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756348470899686e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 55468, "start": 572.76, "end": 573.0999999999999, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51269, 3153, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1568580155961969, "compression_ratio": 1.5622317596566524, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756348470899686e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 57310, "start": 573.1, "end": 578.82, "text": " And third, it holds across a simultaneous change of both the model family and the optimization", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2636, 11, 309, 9190, 2108, 257, 46218, 1319, 295, 1293, 264, 2316, 1605, 293, 264, 19618, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11272093454996744, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108560882757694e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 57310, "start": 578.82, "end": 586.08, "text": " algorithm. The middle layers are consistently the locus of effective adaptation under this", "tokens": [50651, 9284, 13, 440, 2808, 7914, 366, 14961, 264, 450, 1149, 295, 4942, 21549, 833, 341, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11272093454996744, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108560882757694e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 57310, "start": 586.08, "end": 587.6800000000001, "text": " constrained training regime.", "tokens": [51014, 38901, 3097, 13120, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11272093454996744, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108560882757694e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 57310, "start": 588.0, "end": 593.38, "text": " Okay. Think about it this way. Imagine you were trying to soup up your car's engine to win a", "tokens": [51110, 1033, 13, 6557, 466, 309, 341, 636, 13, 11739, 291, 645, 1382, 281, 7884, 493, 428, 1032, 311, 2848, 281, 1942, 257, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11272093454996744, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108560882757694e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 57310, "start": 593.38, "end": 593.98, "text": " street waste.", "tokens": [51379, 4838, 5964, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11272093454996744, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108560882757694e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 57310, "start": 594.16, "end": 595.12, "text": " Okay. I like this.", "tokens": [51418, 1033, 13, 286, 411, 341, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11272093454996744, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108560882757694e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 57310, "start": 595.26, "end": 600.6, "text": " You bring your car into the shop and you assume you need to rebuild the entire engine block. You think,", "tokens": [51473, 509, 1565, 428, 1032, 666, 264, 3945, 293, 291, 6552, 291, 643, 281, 16877, 264, 2302, 2848, 3461, 13, 509, 519, 11, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11272093454996744, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108560882757694e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 60060, "start": 600.6, "end": 605.64, "text": " I need to bore out the cylinders, change the exhaust, replace the transmission, this massive", "tokens": [50365, 286, 643, 281, 26002, 484, 264, 42166, 11, 1319, 264, 14687, 11, 7406, 264, 11574, 11, 341, 5994, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 60060, "start": 605.64, "end": 608.34, "text": " full system overhaul just to get more speed.", "tokens": [50617, 1577, 1185, 670, 39423, 445, 281, 483, 544, 3073, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 60060, "start": 608.48, "end": 609.82, "text": " That would be full parameter training.", "tokens": [50759, 663, 576, 312, 1577, 13075, 3097, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 60060, "start": 610.02, "end": 614.32, "text": " Exactly. But then your mechanic looks at it and realizes that actually you just need to swap out", "tokens": [50836, 7587, 13, 583, 550, 428, 23860, 1542, 412, 309, 293, 29316, 300, 767, 291, 445, 643, 281, 18135, 484, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 60060, "start": 614.32, "end": 618.66, "text": " one specific valve right in the middle of the fuel injection system.", "tokens": [51051, 472, 2685, 15294, 558, 294, 264, 2808, 295, 264, 6616, 22873, 1185, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 60060, "start": 618.78, "end": 619.5400000000001, "text": " Just one valve.", "tokens": [51274, 1449, 472, 15294, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 60060, "start": 619.66, "end": 625.48, "text": " Just that one valve, leaving everything else completely factory stock. And it gives you the exact same speed", "tokens": [51318, 1449, 300, 472, 15294, 11, 5012, 1203, 1646, 2584, 9265, 4127, 13, 400, 309, 2709, 291, 264, 1900, 912, 3073, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 60060, "start": 625.48, "end": 627.58, "text": " boost as rebuilding the whole engine block.", "tokens": [51609, 9194, 382, 36717, 264, 1379, 2848, 3461, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11506097744672726, "compression_ratio": 1.6699346405228759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349517005341153e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 62758, "start": 627.58, "end": 632.2800000000001, "text": " That is exactly what this middle layer phenomenon feels like. It's incredibly precise.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 341, 2808, 4583, 14029, 3417, 411, 13, 467, 311, 6252, 13600, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 62758, "start": 632.9200000000001, "end": 637.3000000000001, "text": " That analogy perfectly captures the difference between those nominal and effective spaces we were", "tokens": [50632, 663, 21663, 6239, 27986, 264, 2649, 1296, 729, 41641, 293, 4942, 7673, 321, 645, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 62758, "start": 637.3000000000001, "end": 638.1800000000001, "text": " talking about earlier.", "tokens": [50851, 1417, 466, 3071, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 62758, "start": 638.5, "end": 639.2, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [50911, 467, 534, 775, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 62758, "start": 639.32, "end": 639.44, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50952, 865, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 62758, "start": 639.64, "end": 643.84, "text": " Because if you replace the whole engine block, you are exercising your nominal freedom.", "tokens": [50968, 1436, 498, 291, 7406, 264, 1379, 2848, 3461, 11, 291, 366, 27272, 428, 41641, 5645, 13, 51178], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 62758, "start": 644.14, "end": 648.7, "text": " You are changing everything just because you can, and it's expensive and risky.", "tokens": [51193, 509, 366, 4473, 1203, 445, 570, 291, 393, 11, 293, 309, 311, 5124, 293, 21137, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 62758, "start": 648.82, "end": 649.3000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51427, 1779, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14078445019929306, "compression_ratio": 1.578125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370974892209288e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 64930, "start": 649.3, "end": 656.0999999999999, "text": " But swapping that one middle valve represents your effective freedom to improve the system", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1693, 10534, 300, 472, 2808, 15294, 8855, 428, 4942, 5645, 281, 3470, 264, 1185, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713111048159393, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 64930, "start": 656.0999999999999, "end": 658.38, "text": " without unnecessary disruption.", "tokens": [50705, 1553, 19350, 28751, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713111048159393, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 64930, "start": 658.64, "end": 663.64, "text": " However, when we see a result like this where the middle layers are doing all the heavy lifting,", "tokens": [50832, 2908, 11, 562, 321, 536, 257, 1874, 411, 341, 689, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 884, 439, 264, 4676, 15798, 11, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713111048159393, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 64930, "start": 664.24, "end": 668.3, "text": " human intuition immediately reaches for obvious, simple explanations.", "tokens": [51112, 1952, 24002, 4258, 14235, 337, 6322, 11, 2199, 28708, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713111048159393, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 64930, "start": 668.64, "end": 670.5, "text": " Oh, always. We want the simple answer.", "tokens": [51332, 876, 11, 1009, 13, 492, 528, 264, 2199, 1867, 13, 51425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713111048159393, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 64930, "start": 670.7199999999999, "end": 675.3599999999999, "text": " Exactly. If the middle layers are the ones driving all the improvement, the natural assumption is,", "tokens": [51436, 7587, 13, 759, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 264, 2306, 4840, 439, 264, 10444, 11, 264, 3303, 15302, 307, 11, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713111048159393, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 67536, "start": 675.36, "end": 677.2, "text": " oh, they must just be doing more work.", "tokens": [50365, 1954, 11, 436, 1633, 445, 312, 884, 544, 589, 13, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 67536, "start": 677.28, "end": 679.96, "text": " Or they must be moving more during the training process.", "tokens": [50461, 1610, 436, 1633, 312, 2684, 544, 1830, 264, 3097, 1399, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 67536, "start": 680.1, "end": 680.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50602, 1779, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 67536, "start": 680.88, "end": 685.46, "text": " The most deflationary explanation would be that under full parameter training,", "tokens": [50641, 440, 881, 1060, 24278, 822, 10835, 576, 312, 300, 833, 1577, 13075, 3097, 11, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 67536, "start": 685.66, "end": 690.42, "text": " the optimization algorithm just naturally makes larger mathematical updates to the middle layers", "tokens": [50880, 264, 19618, 9284, 445, 8195, 1669, 4833, 18894, 9205, 281, 264, 2808, 7914, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 67536, "start": 690.42, "end": 690.82, "text": " anyway.", "tokens": [51118, 4033, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 67536, "start": 691.0600000000001, "end": 695.02, "text": " Let's explain what we mean by updates or moving parameters, just to keep things grounded for", "tokens": [51150, 961, 311, 2903, 437, 321, 914, 538, 9205, 420, 2684, 9834, 11, 445, 281, 1066, 721, 23535, 337, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 67536, "start": 695.02, "end": 695.6800000000001, "text": " everyone listening.", "tokens": [51348, 1518, 4764, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 67536, "start": 695.92, "end": 697.08, "text": " Yeah, please do.", "tokens": [51393, 865, 11, 1767, 360, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 67536, "start": 697.2, "end": 697.48, "text": " Certainly.", "tokens": [51457, 16628, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16704686482747397, "compression_ratio": 1.6550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5733001923826095e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 69748, "start": 697.48, "end": 703.46, "text": " So a parameter is essentially just a number. It's a weight that determines how strongly one", "tokens": [50365, 407, 257, 13075, 307, 4476, 445, 257, 1230, 13, 467, 311, 257, 3364, 300, 24799, 577, 10613, 472, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211513117740029, "compression_ratio": 1.628787878787879, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349499658106393e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 69748, "start": 703.46, "end": 705.44, "text": " artificial neuron connects to another.", "tokens": [50664, 11677, 34090, 16967, 281, 1071, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211513117740029, "compression_ratio": 1.628787878787879, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349499658106393e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 69748, "start": 705.84, "end": 706.78, "text": " A synapse, basically.", "tokens": [50783, 316, 5451, 11145, 11, 1936, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211513117740029, "compression_ratio": 1.628787878787879, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349499658106393e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 69748, "start": 706.96, "end": 713.0, "text": " Exactly. When the model learns, the reinforcement learning algorithm changes those numbers.", "tokens": [50839, 7587, 13, 1133, 264, 2316, 27152, 11, 264, 29280, 2539, 9284, 2962, 729, 3547, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211513117740029, "compression_ratio": 1.628787878787879, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349499658106393e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 69748, "start": 713.4, "end": 718.4200000000001, "text": " It increases some, it decreases others. We can think of this mathematically as moving the", "tokens": [51161, 467, 8637, 512, 11, 309, 24108, 2357, 13, 492, 393, 519, 295, 341, 44003, 382, 2684, 264, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211513117740029, "compression_ratio": 1.628787878787879, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349499658106393e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 69748, "start": 718.4200000000001, "end": 723.46, "text": " parameters from the original starting point to a new location in a vast multidimensional space.", "tokens": [51412, 9834, 490, 264, 3380, 2891, 935, 281, 257, 777, 4914, 294, 257, 8369, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 1901, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211513117740029, "compression_ratio": 1.628787878787879, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349499658106393e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 72346, "start": 723.46, "end": 728.4200000000001, "text": " So the simple assumption is that the numbers in the middle layers are just changing by larger", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 2199, 15302, 307, 300, 264, 3547, 294, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 445, 4473, 538, 4833, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 72346, "start": 728.4200000000001, "end": 731.0, "text": " amounts than the numbers in the early or late layers.", "tokens": [50613, 11663, 813, 264, 3547, 294, 264, 2440, 420, 3469, 7914, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 72346, "start": 731.1600000000001, "end": 735.24, "text": " Right. If the middle layers are physically moving further in the parameter space,", "tokens": [50750, 1779, 13, 759, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 9762, 2684, 3052, 294, 264, 13075, 1901, 11, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 72346, "start": 735.7800000000001, "end": 740.62, "text": " of course they would account for most of the performance gain. They are simply receiving", "tokens": [50981, 295, 1164, 436, 576, 2696, 337, 881, 295, 264, 3389, 6052, 13, 814, 366, 2935, 10040, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 72346, "start": 740.62, "end": 741.84, "text": " the bulk of the training signal.", "tokens": [51223, 264, 16139, 295, 264, 3097, 6358, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 72346, "start": 741.96, "end": 742.6, "text": " It makes sense.", "tokens": [51290, 467, 1669, 2020, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 72346, "start": 742.84, "end": 749.2800000000001, "text": " But the fliction paper explicitly highlights that Zhang et al ruled this out entirely.", "tokens": [51334, 583, 264, 932, 4105, 3035, 20803, 14254, 300, 17729, 1030, 419, 20077, 341, 484, 7696, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 72346, "start": 749.4200000000001, "end": 752.14, "text": " Oh, they actually measured the magnitude of the parameter changes.", "tokens": [51663, 876, 11, 436, 767, 12690, 264, 15668, 295, 264, 13075, 2962, 13, 51799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10336601323094861, "compression_ratio": 1.8027681660899655, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 75214, "start": 752.14, "end": 755.12, "text": " They did. They measured the literal distance the weights moved.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 630, 13, 814, 12690, 264, 20411, 4560, 264, 17443, 4259, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 75214, "start": 755.78, "end": 759.34, "text": " And when you do full parameter training, the magnitude of the parameter change,", "tokens": [50547, 400, 562, 291, 360, 1577, 13075, 3097, 11, 264, 15668, 295, 264, 13075, 1319, 11, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 75214, "start": 759.46, "end": 763.46, "text": " how much the weights actually shift, is roughly uniform across all the layers.", "tokens": [50731, 577, 709, 264, 17443, 767, 5513, 11, 307, 9810, 9452, 2108, 439, 264, 7914, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 75214, "start": 763.64, "end": 764.16, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [50940, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 75214, "start": 764.4, "end": 768.08, "text": " Yes. The middle layers are not moving any more than the earlier late layers.", "tokens": [50978, 1079, 13, 440, 2808, 7914, 366, 406, 2684, 604, 544, 813, 264, 3071, 3469, 7914, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 75214, "start": 768.5, "end": 770.56, "text": " They all take roughly the same size steps.", "tokens": [51183, 814, 439, 747, 9810, 264, 912, 2744, 4439, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 75214, "start": 770.9, "end": 773.84, "text": " And even more surprising, when you do single layer training,", "tokens": [51303, 400, 754, 544, 8830, 11, 562, 291, 360, 2167, 4583, 3097, 11, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 75214, "start": 774.1, "end": 777.54, "text": " the magnitude of the weight movement is also roughly uniform,", "tokens": [51463, 264, 15668, 295, 264, 3364, 3963, 307, 611, 9810, 9452, 11, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 75214, "start": 778.0, "end": 780.66, "text": " regardless of which single layer you pick to train.", "tokens": [51658, 10060, 295, 597, 2167, 4583, 291, 1888, 281, 3847, 13, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 75214, "start": 780.8, "end": 781.6, "text": " That's the kicker.", "tokens": [51798, 663, 311, 264, 4437, 260, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1167589606660785, "compression_ratio": 1.9097222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815695971089673e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 78160, "start": 781.6, "end": 785.22, "text": " If you freeze everything and only train an early layer,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 15959, 1203, 293, 787, 3847, 364, 2440, 4583, 11, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17631997954979373, "compression_ratio": 1.6796536796536796, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343192854069045e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 78160, "start": 785.72, "end": 789.6, "text": " its parameters change by about the same total mathematical amount", "tokens": [50571, 1080, 9834, 1319, 538, 466, 264, 912, 3217, 18894, 2372, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17631997954979373, "compression_ratio": 1.6796536796536796, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343192854069045e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 78160, "start": 789.6, "end": 793.4, "text": " as a middle layer would if you only trained the middle layer.", "tokens": [50765, 382, 257, 2808, 4583, 576, 498, 291, 787, 8895, 264, 2808, 4583, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17631997954979373, "compression_ratio": 1.6796536796536796, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343192854069045e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 78160, "start": 793.52, "end": 794.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50961, 7587, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17631997954979373, "compression_ratio": 1.6796536796536796, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343192854069045e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 78160, "start": 794.3000000000001, "end": 799.3000000000001, "text": " So it is absolutely not a matter of the middle layers just receiving larger updates.", "tokens": [51000, 407, 309, 307, 3122, 406, 257, 1871, 295, 264, 2808, 7914, 445, 10040, 4833, 9205, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17631997954979373, "compression_ratio": 1.6796536796536796, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343192854069045e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 78160, "start": 799.46, "end": 802.84, "text": " They are moving the exact same mathematical distance,", "tokens": [51258, 814, 366, 2684, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 4560, 11, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17631997954979373, "compression_ratio": 1.6796536796536796, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343192854069045e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 78160, "start": 803.46, "end": 807.48, "text": " but their movement is somehow, well, vastly more useful.", "tokens": [51458, 457, 641, 3963, 307, 6063, 11, 731, 11, 41426, 544, 4420, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17631997954979373, "compression_ratio": 1.6796536796536796, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343192854069045e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 80748, "start": 807.48, "end": 810.72, "text": " Yes. The distance is the same, but the destination is better.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 440, 4560, 307, 264, 912, 11, 457, 264, 12236, 307, 1101, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261723412407768, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 1.88626501571032e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 80748, "start": 810.86, "end": 814.48, "text": " Okay, hold on. I'm stuck on something here. Let me push back for a second. Let's look at this from another angle.", "tokens": [50534, 1033, 11, 1797, 322, 13, 286, 478, 5541, 322, 746, 510, 13, 961, 385, 2944, 646, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 961, 311, 574, 412, 341, 490, 1071, 5802, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261723412407768, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 1.88626501571032e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 80748, "start": 814.5600000000001, "end": 814.66, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50719, 4894, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261723412407768, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 1.88626501571032e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 80748, "start": 815.04, "end": 818.46, "text": " If a layer is absolutely essential for the model to work in the first place,", "tokens": [50743, 759, 257, 4583, 307, 3122, 7115, 337, 264, 2316, 281, 589, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 11, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261723412407768, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 1.88626501571032e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 80748, "start": 818.52, "end": 823.1800000000001, "text": " like if we completely delete it and the model breaks and starts speaking total gibberish.", "tokens": [50917, 411, 498, 321, 2584, 12097, 309, 293, 264, 2316, 9857, 293, 3719, 4124, 3217, 4553, 43189, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261723412407768, "compression_ratio": 1.5330396475770924, "no_speech_prob": 1.88626501571032e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 82318, "start": 823.18, "end": 824.88, "text": " A very necessary layer, yes.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 588, 4818, 4583, 11, 2086, 13, 50450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12584741791682458, "compression_ratio": 1.563953488372093, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893266098865097e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 82318, "start": 825.1999999999999, "end": 831.02, "text": " Shouldn't that incredibly important layer be the absolute best place to train the model to be better?", "tokens": [50466, 34170, 380, 300, 6252, 1021, 4583, 312, 264, 8236, 1151, 1081, 281, 3847, 264, 2316, 281, 312, 1101, 30, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12584741791682458, "compression_ratio": 1.563953488372093, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893266098865097e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 82318, "start": 831.18, "end": 836.3, "text": " I mean, if the middle layers are the most important for the basic functioning of the AI,", "tokens": [50765, 286, 914, 11, 498, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 264, 881, 1021, 337, 264, 3875, 18483, 295, 264, 7318, 11, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12584741791682458, "compression_ratio": 1.563953488372093, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893266098865097e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 82318, "start": 836.56, "end": 838.66, "text": " it makes sense they are the best to train, right?", "tokens": [51034, 309, 1669, 2020, 436, 366, 264, 1151, 281, 3847, 11, 558, 30, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12584741791682458, "compression_ratio": 1.563953488372093, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893266098865097e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 83866, "start": 838.66, "end": 844.04, "text": " That is exactly the assumption that much of the prior work in this field has implicitly made.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 2293, 264, 15302, 300, 709, 295, 264, 4059, 589, 294, 341, 2519, 575, 26947, 356, 1027, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 83866, "start": 844.24, "end": 845.56, "text": " It sounds incredibly logical.", "tokens": [50644, 467, 3263, 6252, 14978, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 83866, "start": 845.66, "end": 846.38, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [50715, 467, 534, 775, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 83866, "start": 846.66, "end": 852.4, "text": " But the Felician paper argues forcefully that this is a complete conflation of two entirely different things.", "tokens": [50765, 583, 264, 13298, 9027, 3035, 38218, 3464, 2277, 300, 341, 307, 257, 3566, 1497, 24278, 295, 732, 7696, 819, 721, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 83866, "start": 852.62, "end": 858.54, "text": " We have to separate what they call representational necessity from adaptive usefulness.", "tokens": [51063, 492, 362, 281, 4994, 437, 436, 818, 2906, 1478, 24217, 490, 27912, 4420, 1287, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 83866, "start": 859.0, "end": 862.42, "text": " Representational necessity versus adaptive usefulness.", "tokens": [51382, 19945, 1478, 24217, 5717, 27912, 4420, 1287, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 83866, "start": 862.4599999999999, "end": 863.6, "text": " Okay, we need to break those down.", "tokens": [51555, 1033, 11, 321, 643, 281, 1821, 729, 760, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 83866, "start": 863.72, "end": 865.6, "text": " What exactly is representational necessity?", "tokens": [51618, 708, 2293, 307, 2906, 1478, 24217, 30, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16330456283857236, "compression_ratio": 1.7773584905660378, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898015546910282e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 86560, "start": 865.6, "end": 869.44, "text": " Representational necessity is what previous ablation studies measured.", "tokens": [50365, 19945, 1478, 24217, 307, 437, 3894, 410, 24278, 5313, 12690, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17642976882609915, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967620053358e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 86560, "start": 869.6, "end": 874.32, "text": " Ablation meaning like removing or destroying a part of something to see what happens, right?", "tokens": [50565, 2847, 24278, 3620, 411, 12720, 420, 19926, 257, 644, 295, 746, 281, 536, 437, 2314, 11, 558, 30, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17642976882609915, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967620053358e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 86560, "start": 874.64, "end": 877.16, "text": " Correct. An ablation study is when you go into a neural network,", "tokens": [50817, 12753, 13, 1107, 410, 24278, 2979, 307, 562, 291, 352, 666, 257, 18161, 3209, 11, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17642976882609915, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967620053358e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 86560, "start": 877.8000000000001, "end": 881.02, "text": " delete or completely zero out a specific layer entirely,", "tokens": [50975, 12097, 420, 2584, 4018, 484, 257, 2685, 4583, 7696, 11, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17642976882609915, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967620053358e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 86560, "start": 881.34, "end": 884.74, "text": " and observe how badly the model's performance collapses.", "tokens": [51152, 293, 11441, 577, 13425, 264, 2316, 311, 3389, 48765, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17642976882609915, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967620053358e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 86560, "start": 885.08, "end": 890.6600000000001, "text": " If it collapses completely and the model can no longer output coherent text at all,", "tokens": [51339, 759, 309, 48765, 2584, 293, 264, 2316, 393, 572, 2854, 5598, 36239, 2487, 412, 439, 11, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17642976882609915, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.635967620053358e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 89066, "start": 890.66, "end": 896.78, "text": " that layer is deemed highly necessary for the current forward pass behavior.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 4583, 307, 27637, 5405, 4818, 337, 264, 2190, 2128, 1320, 5223, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1336036205291748, "compression_ratio": 1.6098484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947606512607294e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 89066, "start": 896.78, "end": 902.78, "text": " And forward pass just means the normal process of the AI taking in a prompt and spitting out an answer.", "tokens": [50671, 400, 2128, 1320, 445, 1355, 264, 2710, 1399, 295, 264, 7318, 1940, 294, 257, 12391, 293, 637, 2414, 484, 364, 1867, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1336036205291748, "compression_ratio": 1.6098484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947606512607294e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 89066, "start": 903.06, "end": 906.12, "text": " Right. So representational necessity answers the question,", "tokens": [50985, 1779, 13, 407, 2906, 1478, 24217, 6338, 264, 1168, 11, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1336036205291748, "compression_ratio": 1.6098484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947606512607294e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 89066, "start": 906.9, "end": 912.62, "text": " which parameters does the model currently depend on just to function at its baseline level?", "tokens": [51177, 597, 9834, 775, 264, 2316, 4362, 5672, 322, 445, 281, 2445, 412, 1080, 20518, 1496, 30, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1336036205291748, "compression_ratio": 1.6098484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947606512607294e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 89066, "start": 912.74, "end": 913.8199999999999, "text": " Okay, so that's necessity.", "tokens": [51469, 1033, 11, 370, 300, 311, 24217, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1336036205291748, "compression_ratio": 1.6098484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947606512607294e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 89066, "start": 914.06, "end": 916.86, "text": " Think of it like a load-bearing wall in a house you're renovating.", "tokens": [51535, 6557, 295, 309, 411, 257, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 2929, 294, 257, 1782, 291, 434, 18845, 990, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1336036205291748, "compression_ratio": 1.6098484848484849, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947606512607294e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 91686, "start": 916.86, "end": 918.74, "text": " I love the house analogies today.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 959, 264, 1782, 16660, 530, 965, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 91686, "start": 918.86, "end": 921.7, "text": " If you knock it down, the roof literally caves in.", "tokens": [50465, 759, 291, 6728, 309, 760, 11, 264, 8418, 3736, 32288, 294, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 91686, "start": 921.88, "end": 924.58, "text": " It is absolutely necessary for the house to just stand upright.", "tokens": [50616, 467, 307, 3122, 4818, 337, 264, 1782, 281, 445, 1463, 27405, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 91686, "start": 924.98, "end": 925.92, "text": " That's a great visualization.", "tokens": [50771, 663, 311, 257, 869, 25801, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 91686, "start": 926.28, "end": 928.32, "text": " Now compare that to adaptive usefulness.", "tokens": [50836, 823, 6794, 300, 281, 27912, 4420, 1287, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 91686, "start": 928.96, "end": 931.44, "text": " Adaptive usefulness answers a completely different question.", "tokens": [50970, 49643, 488, 4420, 1287, 6338, 257, 2584, 819, 1168, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 91686, "start": 931.5600000000001, "end": 932.02, "text": " Which is?", "tokens": [51100, 3013, 307, 30, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 91686, "start": 932.1800000000001, "end": 935.74, "text": " It asks, which parameters, when given the opportunity to change,", "tokens": [51131, 467, 8962, 11, 597, 9834, 11, 562, 2212, 264, 2650, 281, 1319, 11, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 91686, "start": 936.0600000000001, "end": 939.5, "text": " can efficiently absorb a new training signal to alter the system's behavior", "tokens": [51325, 393, 19621, 15631, 257, 777, 3097, 6358, 281, 11337, 264, 1185, 311, 5223, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 91686, "start": 939.5, "end": 942.96, "text": " while preserving the rest of the system's existing capabilities?", "tokens": [51497, 1339, 33173, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 1185, 311, 6741, 10862, 30, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 91686, "start": 943.2, "end": 944.38, "text": " Ah, okay.", "tokens": [51682, 2438, 11, 1392, 13, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15338899243262508, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347670167368936e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 94438, "start": 944.38, "end": 947.62, "text": " So going back to the house renovation, the load-bearing wall is necessary.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 516, 646, 281, 264, 1782, 39973, 11, 264, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 2929, 307, 4818, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14655409240722655, "compression_ratio": 1.7454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617270710492238e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 94438, "start": 948.38, "end": 952.72, "text": " But if my new goal is to make the house warmer, the load-bearing wall is not adaptively usable.", "tokens": [50565, 583, 498, 452, 777, 3387, 307, 281, 652, 264, 1782, 21599, 11, 264, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 2929, 307, 406, 6231, 3413, 29975, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14655409240722655, "compression_ratio": 1.7454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617270710492238e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 94438, "start": 953.1, "end": 953.82, "text": " No, it's not.", "tokens": [50801, 883, 11, 309, 311, 406, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14655409240722655, "compression_ratio": 1.7454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617270710492238e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 94438, "start": 954.16, "end": 957.66, "text": " Modifying the load-bearing wall to be a heater is a terrible idea.", "tokens": [50854, 6583, 5489, 264, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 2929, 281, 312, 257, 30408, 307, 257, 6237, 1558, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14655409240722655, "compression_ratio": 1.7454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617270710492238e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 94438, "start": 958.42, "end": 964.46, "text": " I might accidentally compromise its structural integrity while I'm, like, digging into it to install heating coils.", "tokens": [51067, 286, 1062, 15715, 18577, 1080, 15067, 16000, 1339, 286, 478, 11, 411, 11, 17343, 666, 309, 281, 3625, 15082, 43639, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14655409240722655, "compression_ratio": 1.7454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617270710492238e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 94438, "start": 964.66, "end": 966.32, "text": " Exactly. You risk the whole structure.", "tokens": [51379, 7587, 13, 509, 3148, 264, 1379, 3877, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14655409240722655, "compression_ratio": 1.7454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617270710492238e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 94438, "start": 966.72, "end": 970.92, "text": " The thermostat on the wall, however, might not be structurally necessary.", "tokens": [51482, 440, 8810, 39036, 322, 264, 2929, 11, 4461, 11, 1062, 406, 312, 6594, 6512, 4818, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14655409240722655, "compression_ratio": 1.7454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617270710492238e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 97092, "start": 970.92, "end": 978.36, "text": " The house won't collapse if I unscrew the thermostat, but it is highly adaptively useful for changing the temperature.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1782, 1582, 380, 15584, 498, 286, 42579, 264, 8810, 39036, 11, 457, 309, 307, 5405, 6231, 3413, 4420, 337, 4473, 264, 4292, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16787886986365685, "compression_ratio": 1.5583756345177664, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014867604454252e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 97092, "start": 978.9799999999999, "end": 980.68, "text": " That perfectly captures the distinction.", "tokens": [50768, 663, 6239, 27986, 264, 16844, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16787886986365685, "compression_ratio": 1.5583756345177664, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014867604454252e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 97092, "start": 981.66, "end": 988.6999999999999, "text": " The paper points out that keeping the house standing and making the house warmer are two entirely different optimization problems.", "tokens": [50902, 440, 3035, 2793, 484, 300, 5145, 264, 1782, 4877, 293, 1455, 264, 1782, 21599, 366, 732, 7696, 819, 19618, 2740, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16787886986365685, "compression_ratio": 1.5583756345177664, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014867604454252e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 97092, "start": 988.86, "end": 989.76, "text": " They really are.", "tokens": [51262, 814, 534, 366, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16787886986365685, "compression_ratio": 1.5583756345177664, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014867604454252e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 98976, "start": 989.76, "end": 996.62, "text": " A parameter can be heavily implicated in the current computation, highly necessary, like your load-bearing wall,", "tokens": [50365, 316, 13075, 393, 312, 10950, 8484, 3587, 294, 264, 2190, 24903, 11, 5405, 4818, 11, 411, 428, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 2929, 11, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13992892542193014, "compression_ratio": 1.6228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945001174786811e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 98976, "start": 997.0, "end": 1002.9, "text": " while offering a geometrically terrible direction for improving that computation under a new training signal.", "tokens": [50727, 1339, 8745, 257, 12956, 81, 984, 6237, 3513, 337, 11470, 300, 24903, 833, 257, 777, 3097, 6358, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13992892542193014, "compression_ratio": 1.6228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945001174786811e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 98976, "start": 1003.12, "end": 1006.22, "text": " A geometrically terrible direction, let's unpack that phrase.", "tokens": [51033, 316, 12956, 81, 984, 6237, 3513, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 300, 9535, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13992892542193014, "compression_ratio": 1.6228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945001174786811e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 100622, "start": 1006.22, "end": 1013.58, "text": " That means if you try to adjust the numbers in that necessary layer, you immediately start ruining the things it was already doing well.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 1355, 498, 291, 853, 281, 4369, 264, 3547, 294, 300, 4818, 4583, 11, 291, 4258, 722, 38938, 264, 721, 309, 390, 1217, 884, 731, 13, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557223320007324, "compression_ratio": 1.4832535885167464, "no_speech_prob": 1.5372245577155441e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 100622, "start": 1014.28, "end": 1021.1, "text": " Precisely. Remember, we are trying to add a new capability, like solving complex math without forgetting how to speak English.", "tokens": [50768, 48746, 736, 13, 5459, 11, 321, 366, 1382, 281, 909, 257, 777, 13759, 11, 411, 12606, 3997, 5221, 1553, 25428, 577, 281, 1710, 3669, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557223320007324, "compression_ratio": 1.4832535885167464, "no_speech_prob": 1.5372245577155441e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 100622, "start": 1021.36, "end": 1023.5400000000001, "text": " Right. We don't want it to unlearn its basics.", "tokens": [51122, 1779, 13, 492, 500, 380, 528, 309, 281, 25272, 1083, 1080, 14688, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09557223320007324, "compression_ratio": 1.4832535885167464, "no_speech_prob": 1.5372245577155441e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 102354, "start": 1023.54, "end": 1032.1599999999999, "text": " If a layer is doing the heavy lifting of basic grammar, tweaking its weights to solve algebra might cause catastrophic forgetting of the grammar.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 4583, 307, 884, 264, 4676, 15798, 295, 3875, 22317, 11, 6986, 2456, 1080, 17443, 281, 5039, 21989, 1062, 3082, 34915, 25428, 295, 264, 22317, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10767188279525093, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 102354, "start": 1032.76, "end": 1040.3999999999999, "text": " The gradient, the mathematical path the training algorithm wants to take to improve the algebra score points in a direction that destroys the grammar.", "tokens": [50826, 440, 16235, 11, 264, 18894, 3100, 264, 3097, 9284, 2738, 281, 747, 281, 3470, 264, 21989, 6175, 2793, 294, 257, 3513, 300, 36714, 264, 22317, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10767188279525093, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 102354, "start": 1040.74, "end": 1042.92, "text": " It's pulling in two opposite directions.", "tokens": [51225, 467, 311, 8407, 294, 732, 6182, 11095, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10767188279525093, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 104292, "start": 1042.92, "end": 1055.28, "text": " Yes. And conversely, a parameter that participates only lightly in the current necessary behavior might sit in a geometrically favorable position to absorb a useful update.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 400, 2615, 736, 11, 257, 13075, 300, 3421, 1024, 787, 16695, 294, 264, 2190, 4818, 5223, 1062, 1394, 294, 257, 12956, 81, 984, 29557, 2535, 281, 15631, 257, 4420, 5623, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06600767771402995, "compression_ratio": 1.743801652892562, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 104292, "start": 1055.48, "end": 1058.9, "text": " It has the freedom to change without ruining things.", "tokens": [50993, 467, 575, 264, 5645, 281, 1319, 1553, 38938, 721, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06600767771402995, "compression_ratio": 1.743801652892562, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 104292, "start": 1058.98, "end": 1069.42, "text": " Yes. The set of parameters whose modification is necessary for a system to function is simply not the same set as the parameters whose modification is useful for improving it.", "tokens": [51168, 1079, 13, 440, 992, 295, 9834, 6104, 26747, 307, 4818, 337, 257, 1185, 281, 2445, 307, 2935, 406, 264, 912, 992, 382, 264, 9834, 6104, 26747, 307, 4420, 337, 11470, 309, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06600767771402995, "compression_ratio": 1.743801652892562, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 104292, "start": 1069.44, "end": 1070.72, "text": " That is so profound.", "tokens": [51691, 663, 307, 370, 14382, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06600767771402995, "compression_ratio": 1.743801652892562, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 107072, "start": 1070.72, "end": 1076.48, "text": " Once you grant this distinction, the fact that middle layers are best for adaptation stops looking like a bizarre anomaly.", "tokens": [50365, 3443, 291, 6386, 341, 16844, 11, 264, 1186, 300, 2808, 7914, 366, 1151, 337, 21549, 10094, 1237, 411, 257, 18265, 42737, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12498150931464301, "compression_ratio": 1.5951417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750145107741199e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 107072, "start": 1077.06, "end": 1083.96, "text": " It just looks like the expected outcome of recognizing that uniform trainability across a complex system is a total myth.", "tokens": [50682, 467, 445, 1542, 411, 264, 5176, 9700, 295, 18538, 300, 9452, 3847, 2310, 2108, 257, 3997, 1185, 307, 257, 3217, 9474, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12498150931464301, "compression_ratio": 1.5951417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750145107741199e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 107072, "start": 1084.5, "end": 1086.64, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this. We know what is happening.", "tokens": [51054, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 492, 458, 437, 307, 2737, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12498150931464301, "compression_ratio": 1.5951417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750145107741199e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 107072, "start": 1086.98, "end": 1089.58, "text": " Single layers in the middle can carry the whole training load.", "tokens": [51178, 31248, 7914, 294, 264, 2808, 393, 3985, 264, 1379, 3097, 3677, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12498150931464301, "compression_ratio": 1.5951417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750145107741199e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 107072, "start": 1089.8600000000001, "end": 1091.74, "text": " And we know what isn't causing it.", "tokens": [51322, 400, 321, 458, 437, 1943, 380, 9853, 309, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12498150931464301, "compression_ratio": 1.5951417004048583, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750145107741199e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 109174, "start": 1091.74, "end": 1100.82, "text": " It's not just because they are moving more, and it's not just because those layers are the most structurally necessary for the AI to function.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 445, 570, 436, 366, 2684, 544, 11, 293, 309, 311, 406, 445, 570, 729, 7914, 366, 264, 881, 6594, 6512, 4818, 337, 264, 7318, 281, 2445, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17704459599086217, "compression_ratio": 1.5794871794871794, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555142673402301e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 109174, "start": 1100.92, "end": 1101.9, "text": " Correct on both counts.", "tokens": [50824, 12753, 322, 1293, 14893, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17704459599086217, "compression_ratio": 1.5794871794871794, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555142673402301e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 109174, "start": 1102.08, "end": 1109.68, "text": " So how do these researchers actually define and measure this phenomenon without getting lost in philosophical debates?", "tokens": [50882, 407, 577, 360, 613, 10309, 767, 6964, 293, 3481, 341, 14029, 1553, 1242, 2731, 294, 25066, 24203, 30, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17704459599086217, "compression_ratio": 1.5794871794871794, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555142673402301e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 109174, "start": 1109.68, "end": 1110.74, "text": " Like, what's the math?", "tokens": [51262, 1743, 11, 437, 311, 264, 5221, 30, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17704459599086217, "compression_ratio": 1.5794871794871794, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555142673402301e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 111074, "start": 1110.74, "end": 1119.68, "text": " Well, they introduce a mathematical formalism to give concrete, measurable expression to this idea of adaptive usefulness.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 436, 5366, 257, 18894, 9860, 1434, 281, 976, 9859, 11, 43615, 6114, 281, 341, 1558, 295, 27912, 4420, 1287, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12155146451340508, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546387961695718e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 111074, "start": 1119.92, "end": 1122.08, "text": " They don't want to just talk about it in metaphors.", "tokens": [50824, 814, 500, 380, 528, 281, 445, 751, 466, 309, 294, 30946, 830, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12155146451340508, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546387961695718e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 111074, "start": 1122.16, "end": 1124.22, "text": " They want to define it rigorously.", "tokens": [50936, 814, 528, 281, 6964, 309, 42191, 5098, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12155146451340508, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546387961695718e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 111074, "start": 1124.38, "end": 1125.38, "text": " So what do they call it?", "tokens": [51047, 407, 437, 360, 436, 818, 309, 30, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12155146451340508, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546387961695718e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 111074, "start": 1125.44, "end": 1127.1, "text": " They call it the repair set formalism.", "tokens": [51100, 814, 818, 309, 264, 10535, 992, 9860, 1434, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12155146451340508, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546387961695718e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 111074, "start": 1127.24, "end": 1133.38, "text": " And we really need to clarify the word repair here, because it doesn't mean what you might intuitively think it means.", "tokens": [51190, 400, 321, 534, 643, 281, 17594, 264, 1349, 10535, 510, 11, 570, 309, 1177, 380, 914, 437, 291, 1062, 46506, 519, 309, 1355, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12155146451340508, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546387961695718e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 113338, "start": 1133.38, "end": 1134.7600000000002, "text": " No, it definitely doesn't.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 309, 2138, 1177, 380, 13, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063127803051565, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667034947679625e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 113338, "start": 1134.8400000000001, "end": 1138.64, "text": " Because when I hear repair, I think something is, like, fundamentally broken.", "tokens": [50438, 1436, 562, 286, 1568, 10535, 11, 286, 519, 746, 307, 11, 411, 11, 17879, 5463, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063127803051565, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667034947679625e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 113338, "start": 1138.94, "end": 1145.14, "text": " Like, taking your car to the shop because the bumper fell off, and you were restoring it to the exact state it was in yesterday.", "tokens": [50643, 1743, 11, 1940, 428, 1032, 281, 264, 3945, 570, 264, 23992, 5696, 766, 11, 293, 291, 645, 36349, 309, 281, 264, 1900, 1785, 309, 390, 294, 5186, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063127803051565, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667034947679625e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 113338, "start": 1145.3200000000002, "end": 1146.98, "text": " Right. That is not what they mean in this context.", "tokens": [50962, 1779, 13, 663, 307, 406, 437, 436, 914, 294, 341, 4319, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063127803051565, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667034947679625e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 113338, "start": 1147.0400000000002, "end": 1147.74, "text": " That's just what do they mean?", "tokens": [51048, 663, 311, 445, 437, 360, 436, 914, 30, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063127803051565, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667034947679625e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 113338, "start": 1147.98, "end": 1158.0200000000002, "text": " In this paper, a repair means adding a new capability that the pre-trained model lacked entirely, while leaving the rest of its established organization largely undisturbed.", "tokens": [51095, 682, 341, 3035, 11, 257, 10535, 1355, 5127, 257, 777, 13759, 300, 264, 659, 12, 17227, 2001, 2316, 41481, 7696, 11, 1339, 5012, 264, 1472, 295, 1080, 7545, 4475, 11611, 674, 468, 374, 2883, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063127803051565, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667034947679625e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 113338, "start": 1158.8200000000002, "end": 1159.6200000000001, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51637, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063127803051565, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667034947679625e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 115962, "start": 1159.62, "end": 1163.54, "text": " It is a targeted upgrade that doesn't break the existing system.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 15045, 11484, 300, 1177, 380, 1821, 264, 6741, 1185, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16032804489135744, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671193083847344e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 115962, "start": 1164.04, "end": 1166.04, "text": " So how do they write that out mathematically?", "tokens": [50586, 407, 577, 360, 436, 2464, 300, 484, 44003, 30, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16032804489135744, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671193083847344e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 115962, "start": 1166.32, "end": 1169.56, "text": " How do you put a hard number on an upgrade that doesn't break things?", "tokens": [50700, 1012, 360, 291, 829, 257, 1152, 1230, 322, 364, 11484, 300, 1177, 380, 1821, 721, 30, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16032804489135744, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671193083847344e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 115962, "start": 1169.9799999999998, "end": 1173.4599999999998, "text": " The formalism defines what it calls a local repair set.", "tokens": [50883, 440, 9860, 1434, 23122, 437, 309, 5498, 257, 2654, 10535, 992, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16032804489135744, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671193083847344e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 115962, "start": 1174.34, "end": 1178.9599999999998, "text": " And to be allowed into this set, a proposed modification to the network's parameters.", "tokens": [51101, 400, 281, 312, 4350, 666, 341, 992, 11, 257, 10348, 26747, 281, 264, 3209, 311, 9834, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16032804489135744, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671193083847344e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 115962, "start": 1180.0, "end": 1183.82, "text": " So any tweak to the weights must balance two competing forces.", "tokens": [51384, 407, 604, 29879, 281, 264, 17443, 1633, 4772, 732, 15439, 5874, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16032804489135744, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671193083847344e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 115962, "start": 1184.0, "end": 1185.04, "text": " Two forces. Okay.", "tokens": [51584, 4453, 5874, 13, 1033, 13, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16032804489135744, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671193083847344e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 118504, "start": 1185.04, "end": 1189.84, "text": " First, it must improve the target task performance by at least some tolerance threshold.", "tokens": [50365, 2386, 11, 309, 1633, 3470, 264, 3779, 5633, 3389, 538, 412, 1935, 512, 23368, 14678, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 118504, "start": 1190.22, "end": 1191.96, "text": " They denote this with the Greek letter epsilon.", "tokens": [50624, 814, 45708, 341, 365, 264, 10281, 5063, 17889, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 118504, "start": 1192.3799999999999, "end": 1192.82, "text": " Epsilon.", "tokens": [50732, 462, 16592, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 118504, "start": 1193.1599999999999, "end": 1196.84, "text": " Okay, so epsilon is the hurdle for actually getting better at the new task.", "tokens": [50771, 1033, 11, 370, 17889, 307, 264, 47423, 337, 767, 1242, 1101, 412, 264, 777, 5633, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 118504, "start": 1196.92, "end": 1197.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50959, 7587, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 118504, "start": 1197.44, "end": 1201.1, "text": " Let's say we are trying to teach the AI to write Python code.", "tokens": [50985, 961, 311, 584, 321, 366, 1382, 281, 2924, 264, 7318, 281, 2464, 15329, 3089, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 118504, "start": 1201.56, "end": 1205.54, "text": " Epsilon is the requirement that the code it generates actually runs and solves the prompt.", "tokens": [51191, 462, 16592, 307, 264, 11695, 300, 264, 3089, 309, 23815, 767, 6676, 293, 39890, 264, 12391, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 118504, "start": 1206.04, "end": 1210.44, "text": " If a weight tweak doesn't improve the Python coding by at least epsilon, we just throw it out.", "tokens": [51415, 759, 257, 3364, 29879, 1177, 380, 3470, 264, 15329, 17720, 538, 412, 1935, 17889, 11, 321, 445, 3507, 309, 484, 13, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 118504, "start": 1210.52, "end": 1210.8999999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51639, 7587, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 118504, "start": 1211.12, "end": 1213.92, "text": " That is the improvement requirement, but that's only half the battle.", "tokens": [51669, 663, 307, 264, 10444, 11695, 11, 457, 300, 311, 787, 1922, 264, 4635, 13, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 118504, "start": 1213.96, "end": 1214.82, "text": " What's the second half?", "tokens": [51811, 708, 311, 264, 1150, 1922, 30, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10050636159962621, "compression_ratio": 1.7876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303639873757378e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 121482, "start": 1214.82, "end": 1220.48, "text": " Second, the modification must stay within a preservation budget, denoted by the Greek letter delta.", "tokens": [50365, 5736, 11, 264, 26747, 1633, 1754, 1951, 257, 27257, 4706, 11, 1441, 23325, 538, 264, 10281, 5063, 8289, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 121482, "start": 1220.74, "end": 1221.06, "text": " Delta.", "tokens": [50661, 18183, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 121482, "start": 1221.36, "end": 1221.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50692, 1779, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 121482, "start": 1221.8, "end": 1223.32, "text": " This is measured by a damage function.", "tokens": [50714, 639, 307, 12690, 538, 257, 4344, 2445, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 121482, "start": 1223.82, "end": 1229.1799999999998, "text": " The modification cannot inflict more damage than your budget, your delta, allows on the", "tokens": [50815, 440, 26747, 2644, 38137, 544, 4344, 813, 428, 4706, 11, 428, 8289, 11, 4045, 322, 264, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 121482, "start": 1229.1799999999998, "end": 1232.26, "text": " capabilities and structures that you want to remain stable.", "tokens": [51083, 10862, 293, 9227, 300, 291, 528, 281, 6222, 8351, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 121482, "start": 1232.76, "end": 1232.98, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51262, 1033, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 121482, "start": 1233.1399999999999, "end": 1236.6399999999999, "text": " So delta is your budget for messing up what the model already knows?", "tokens": [51281, 407, 8289, 307, 428, 4706, 337, 23258, 493, 437, 264, 2316, 1217, 3255, 30, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 121482, "start": 1237.1799999999998, "end": 1237.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51483, 1079, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 121482, "start": 1237.6, "end": 1241.62, "text": " So in our Python example, the model already knows how to converse in fluent English.", "tokens": [51504, 407, 294, 527, 15329, 1365, 11, 264, 2316, 1217, 3255, 577, 281, 416, 4308, 294, 40799, 3669, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1497444484544837, "compression_ratio": 1.690909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.249460604424435e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 124162, "start": 1241.62, "end": 1250.12, "text": " If we tweak the weights to make it better at Python, but suddenly it starts, you know, forgetting how to use verbs properly in English, we've inflicted damage.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 29879, 264, 17443, 281, 652, 309, 1101, 412, 15329, 11, 457, 5800, 309, 3719, 11, 291, 458, 11, 25428, 577, 281, 764, 30051, 6108, 294, 3669, 11, 321, 600, 38137, 292, 4344, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09685682027767865, "compression_ratio": 1.2421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232433149368508e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 125012, "start": 1250.12, "end": 1251.62, "text": " You've exceeded your delta budget.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 600, 38026, 428, 8289, 4706, 13, 50440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19092595867994355, "compression_ratio": 1.3360655737704918, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691684705764543e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 125012, "start": 1251.62, "end": 1252.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50440, 1779, 13, 50462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19092595867994355, "compression_ratio": 1.3360655737704918, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691684705764543e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 125012, "start": 1252.06, "end": 1259.2399999999998, "text": " We want epsilon to be high enough that it masters Python and delta to be low enough that it still speaks perfect English.", "tokens": [50462, 492, 528, 17889, 281, 312, 1090, 1547, 300, 309, 19294, 15329, 293, 8289, 281, 312, 2295, 1547, 300, 309, 920, 10789, 2176, 3669, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19092595867994355, "compression_ratio": 1.3360655737704918, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691684705764543e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 125924, "start": 1259.24, "end": 1259.86, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 50396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15566430921139923, "compression_ratio": 1.425, "no_speech_prob": 2.133679084109774e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 125924, "start": 1260.6200000000001, "end": 1273.86, "text": " The repair set, mathematically written as an R with epsilon and delta subscripts, is simply the collection of all possible parameter tweaks, all the possible weight changes that satisfy both conditions simultaneously.", "tokens": [50434, 440, 10535, 992, 11, 44003, 3720, 382, 364, 497, 365, 17889, 293, 8289, 2325, 39280, 11, 307, 2935, 264, 5765, 295, 439, 1944, 13075, 46664, 11, 439, 264, 1944, 3364, 2962, 300, 19319, 1293, 4487, 16561, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15566430921139923, "compression_ratio": 1.425, "no_speech_prob": 2.133679084109774e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 127386, "start": 1273.86, "end": 1280.26, "text": " They improve the target behavior by at least epsilon, and they disturb the existing organization by no more than delta.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 3470, 264, 3779, 5223, 538, 412, 1935, 17889, 11, 293, 436, 18071, 264, 6741, 4475, 538, 572, 544, 813, 8289, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10858113032120925, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610466900187417e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 127386, "start": 1280.4199999999998, "end": 1281.5, "text": " It's the sweet spot.", "tokens": [50693, 467, 311, 264, 3844, 4008, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10858113032120925, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610466900187417e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 127386, "start": 1281.8999999999999, "end": 1283.0, "text": " Yeah, the sweet spot.", "tokens": [50767, 865, 11, 264, 3844, 4008, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10858113032120925, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610466900187417e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 127386, "start": 1283.3, "end": 1291.02, "text": " And when you restrict this search to just a single layer, say, you only look at layer, you get a layer-specific repair set.", "tokens": [50837, 400, 562, 291, 7694, 341, 3164, 281, 445, 257, 2167, 4583, 11, 584, 11, 291, 787, 574, 412, 4583, 11, 291, 483, 257, 4583, 12, 29258, 10535, 992, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10858113032120925, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610466900187417e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 127386, "start": 1291.1999999999998, "end": 1291.3799999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51232, 1779, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10858113032120925, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610466900187417e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 127386, "start": 1291.4799999999998, "end": 1298.1999999999998, "text": " It is the set of admissible repairs you can reach by moving layer K and leaving every other layer firmly locked at zero.", "tokens": [51246, 467, 307, 264, 992, 295, 5910, 41073, 28823, 291, 393, 2524, 538, 2684, 4583, 591, 293, 5012, 633, 661, 4583, 20031, 9376, 412, 4018, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10858113032120925, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610466900187417e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 129820, "start": 1298.2, "end": 1308.7, "text": " And the paper's central empirical claim, translated into this math, is that the density of reachable repairs in this set differs sharply depending on which layer you are actually looking at.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3035, 311, 5777, 31886, 3932, 11, 16805, 666, 341, 5221, 11, 307, 300, 264, 10305, 295, 2524, 712, 28823, 294, 341, 992, 37761, 42893, 5413, 322, 597, 4583, 291, 366, 767, 1237, 412, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09938704661833934, "compression_ratio": 1.6733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.30703065158544e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 129820, "start": 1308.8400000000001, "end": 1309.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50897, 7587, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09938704661833934, "compression_ratio": 1.6733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.30703065158544e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 129820, "start": 1310.02, "end": 1316.04, "text": " Meaning, if you look at a middle layer, there are tons of weight combinations that satisfy both epsilon and delta.", "tokens": [50956, 19948, 11, 498, 291, 574, 412, 257, 2808, 4583, 11, 456, 366, 9131, 295, 3364, 21267, 300, 19319, 1293, 17889, 293, 8289, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09938704661833934, "compression_ratio": 1.6733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.30703065158544e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 129820, "start": 1316.52, "end": 1318.76, "text": " The repair set is huge and dense.", "tokens": [51281, 440, 10535, 992, 307, 2603, 293, 18011, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09938704661833934, "compression_ratio": 1.6733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.30703065158544e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 129820, "start": 1319.1200000000001, "end": 1323.2, "text": " You can easily find a path to learn Python without forgetting English.", "tokens": [51411, 509, 393, 3612, 915, 257, 3100, 281, 1466, 15329, 1553, 25428, 3669, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09938704661833934, "compression_ratio": 1.6733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.30703065158544e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 129820, "start": 1323.3, "end": 1323.52, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51620, 1079, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09938704661833934, "compression_ratio": 1.6733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.30703065158544e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 129820, "start": 1323.8400000000001, "end": 1327.68, "text": " But if you look at an early layer, that repair set might be completely empty.", "tokens": [51647, 583, 498, 291, 574, 412, 364, 2440, 4583, 11, 300, 10535, 992, 1062, 312, 2584, 6707, 13, 51839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09938704661833934, "compression_ratio": 1.6733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.30703065158544e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 132768, "start": 1327.68, "end": 1329.6000000000001, "text": " There might be no mathematical path at all.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 1062, 312, 572, 18894, 3100, 412, 439, 13, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11576817616695116, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191835419856026e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 132768, "start": 1329.78, "end": 1334.98, "text": " And this formalism beautifully explains some of the more confusing results from the original Zhang study.", "tokens": [50470, 400, 341, 9860, 1434, 16525, 13948, 512, 295, 264, 544, 13181, 3542, 490, 264, 3380, 17729, 2979, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11576817616695116, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191835419856026e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 132768, "start": 1335.2, "end": 1340.74, "text": " Because earlier, we mentioned that sometimes training just one layer actually beats full-parameter training.", "tokens": [50741, 1436, 3071, 11, 321, 2835, 300, 2171, 3097, 445, 472, 4583, 767, 16447, 1577, 12, 2181, 335, 2398, 3097, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11576817616695116, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191835419856026e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 132768, "start": 1340.9, "end": 1342.3400000000001, "text": " Right, which sounds crazy at first.", "tokens": [51026, 1779, 11, 597, 3263, 3219, 412, 700, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11576817616695116, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191835419856026e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 132768, "start": 1342.6200000000001, "end": 1345.0800000000002, "text": " It still seems totally paradoxical to me.", "tokens": [51112, 467, 920, 2544, 3879, 26221, 804, 281, 385, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11576817616695116, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191835419856026e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 132768, "start": 1345.54, "end": 1354.42, "text": " If you search a bigger space, if you let all the parameters move, shouldn't the training algorithm always find a better or at least equal solution?", "tokens": [51258, 759, 291, 3164, 257, 3801, 1901, 11, 498, 291, 718, 439, 264, 9834, 1286, 11, 4659, 380, 264, 3097, 9284, 1009, 915, 257, 1101, 420, 412, 1935, 2681, 3827, 30, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11576817616695116, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191835419856026e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 132768, "start": 1354.7, "end": 1356.3600000000001, "text": " It has so much more room to maneuver.", "tokens": [51716, 467, 575, 370, 709, 544, 1808, 281, 25976, 13, 51799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11576817616695116, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191835419856026e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 135636, "start": 1356.36, "end": 1361.06, "text": " You would think so, but only if the larger space is uniformly useful.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 576, 519, 370, 11, 457, 787, 498, 264, 4833, 1901, 307, 48806, 4420, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15847077803178267, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.741742492421261e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 135636, "start": 1361.82, "end": 1365.8, "text": " Let's look at a brilliant negative example from the source material to illustrate this.", "tokens": [50638, 961, 311, 574, 412, 257, 10248, 3671, 1365, 490, 264, 4009, 2527, 281, 23221, 341, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15847077803178267, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.741742492421261e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 135636, "start": 1365.86, "end": 1367.32, "text": " Okay, I love negative examples.", "tokens": [50840, 1033, 11, 286, 959, 3671, 5110, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15847077803178267, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.741742492421261e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 135636, "start": 1367.4599999999998, "end": 1372.34, "text": " They looked at layer 0, so the very first layer of a model called QUIN38B base.", "tokens": [50920, 814, 2956, 412, 4583, 1958, 11, 370, 264, 588, 700, 4583, 295, 257, 2316, 1219, 7246, 1464, 12625, 33, 3096, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15847077803178267, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.741742492421261e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 135636, "start": 1372.74, "end": 1379.9199999999998, "text": " When the researchers tried to train only layer 0 in isolation using reinforcement learning, the performance didn't just fail to improve.", "tokens": [51184, 1133, 264, 10309, 3031, 281, 3847, 787, 4583, 1958, 294, 16001, 1228, 29280, 2539, 11, 264, 3389, 994, 380, 445, 3061, 281, 3470, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15847077803178267, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.741742492421261e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 135636, "start": 1380.1999999999998, "end": 1383.62, "text": " It actually dropped below the performance of the untrained base model.", "tokens": [51557, 467, 767, 8119, 2507, 264, 3389, 295, 264, 1701, 31774, 3096, 2316, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15847077803178267, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.741742492421261e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 138362, "start": 1383.62, "end": 1394.4799999999998, "text": " Wait, wait, wait. So by actively trying to teach layer 0 a new trick and literally rewarding it for getting the trick right, they actually made the whole model stupider than when they started.", "tokens": [50365, 3802, 11, 1699, 11, 1699, 13, 407, 538, 13022, 1382, 281, 2924, 4583, 1958, 257, 777, 4282, 293, 3736, 20063, 309, 337, 1242, 264, 4282, 558, 11, 436, 767, 1027, 264, 1379, 2316, 342, 1010, 1438, 813, 562, 436, 1409, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11114655841480602, "compression_ratio": 1.5027624309392265, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682271883339261e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 138362, "start": 1394.6399999999999, "end": 1398.6799999999998, "text": " They did. And the repair set formalism explains exactly why that happened.", "tokens": [50916, 814, 630, 13, 400, 264, 10535, 992, 9860, 1434, 13948, 2293, 983, 300, 2011, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11114655841480602, "compression_ratio": 1.5027624309392265, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682271883339261e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 138362, "start": 1398.76, "end": 1399.06, "text": " Why?", "tokens": [51122, 1545, 30, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11114655841480602, "compression_ratio": 1.5027624309392265, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682271883339261e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 139906, "start": 1399.06, "end": 1404.9199999999998, "text": " For layer 0, its optimization trajectory fell entirely outside the useful repair set.", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 4583, 1958, 11, 1080, 19618, 21512, 5696, 7696, 2380, 264, 4420, 10535, 992, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15499453758125875, "compression_ratio": 1.4976744186046511, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 139906, "start": 1405.08, "end": 1407.3799999999999, "text": " What does that actually mean in practice?", "tokens": [50666, 708, 775, 300, 767, 914, 294, 3124, 30, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15499453758125875, "compression_ratio": 1.4976744186046511, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 139906, "start": 1407.94, "end": 1414.0, "text": " It means that when the reinforcement learning algorithm pushed layer 0 to improve the immediate task objective,", "tokens": [50809, 467, 1355, 300, 562, 264, 29280, 2539, 9284, 9152, 4583, 1958, 281, 3470, 264, 11629, 5633, 10024, 11, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15499453758125875, "compression_ratio": 1.4976744186046511, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 139906, "start": 1414.44, "end": 1418.78, "text": " so it's trying desperately to hit that epsilon threshold for the new math problem,", "tokens": [51134, 370, 309, 311, 1382, 23726, 281, 2045, 300, 17889, 14678, 337, 264, 777, 5221, 1154, 11, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15499453758125875, "compression_ratio": 1.4976744186046511, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509865968985846e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 141878, "start": 1418.78, "end": 1425.1399999999999, "text": " it could only do so by inflicting massive, catastrophic damage on the model's existing organization.", "tokens": [50365, 309, 727, 787, 360, 370, 538, 1536, 36580, 5994, 11, 34915, 4344, 322, 264, 2316, 311, 6741, 4475, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09449414949159364, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144716635969504e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 141878, "start": 1425.34, "end": 1427.66, "text": " It blew right past the delta budget.", "tokens": [50693, 467, 19075, 558, 1791, 264, 8289, 4706, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09449414949159364, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144716635969504e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 141878, "start": 1427.8799999999999, "end": 1429.08, "text": " It shattered the delta budget.", "tokens": [50820, 467, 35209, 264, 8289, 4706, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09449414949159364, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144716635969504e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 141878, "start": 1429.2, "end": 1437.36, "text": " There was simply no way to move layer 0's weights to solve the math without destroying the foundational text processing that layer 0 is responsible for.", "tokens": [50886, 821, 390, 2935, 572, 636, 281, 1286, 4583, 1958, 311, 17443, 281, 5039, 264, 5221, 1553, 19926, 264, 32195, 2487, 9007, 300, 4583, 1958, 307, 6250, 337, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09449414949159364, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144716635969504e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 141878, "start": 1437.52, "end": 1438.72, "text": " It couldn't balance the two.", "tokens": [51302, 467, 2809, 380, 4772, 264, 732, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09449414949159364, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144716635969504e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 141878, "start": 1438.82, "end": 1444.08, "text": " It was like trying to upgrade your house's heating by, I don't know, setting the living room rug on fire.", "tokens": [51367, 467, 390, 411, 1382, 281, 11484, 428, 1782, 311, 15082, 538, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 11, 3287, 264, 2647, 1808, 18329, 322, 2610, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09449414949159364, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144716635969504e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 141878, "start": 1444.28, "end": 1444.74, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51640, 7587, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09449414949159364, "compression_ratio": 1.6607142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144716635969504e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 144474, "start": 1444.74, "end": 1452.02, "text": " Sure, you hit your epsilon, it gets warmer for a second, but you are blowing past your delta budget by burning down the whole house.", "tokens": [50365, 4894, 11, 291, 2045, 428, 17889, 11, 309, 2170, 21599, 337, 257, 1150, 11, 457, 291, 366, 15068, 1791, 428, 8289, 4706, 538, 9488, 760, 264, 1379, 1782, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611643203581223, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782103492649856e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 144474, "start": 1452.26, "end": 1453.94, "text": " That is a perfect way to picture it.", "tokens": [50741, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 636, 281, 3036, 309, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611643203581223, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782103492649856e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 144474, "start": 1454.32, "end": 1456.88, "text": " And this explains the paradox of full parameter training.", "tokens": [50844, 400, 341, 13948, 264, 26221, 295, 1577, 13075, 3097, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611643203581223, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782103492649856e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 144474, "start": 1457.04, "end": 1460.98, "text": " Oh, because full parameter training searches over the entire space simultaneously.", "tokens": [50980, 876, 11, 570, 1577, 13075, 3097, 26701, 670, 264, 2302, 1901, 16561, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611643203581223, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782103492649856e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 144474, "start": 1461.48, "end": 1461.86, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51202, 1079, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611643203581223, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782103492649856e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 144474, "start": 1462.48, "end": 1467.3, "text": " It allows movement in layer 0, layer 1, the middle layers, the end layers, all at once.", "tokens": [51252, 467, 4045, 3963, 294, 4583, 1958, 11, 4583, 502, 11, 264, 2808, 7914, 11, 264, 917, 7914, 11, 439, 412, 1564, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09611643203581223, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782103492649856e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 146730, "start": 1467.3, "end": 1478.2, "text": " If you permit the optimization algorithm to move parameters in layers that have poor, small, or totally absent repair sets like layer 0,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 13423, 264, 19618, 9284, 281, 1286, 9834, 294, 7914, 300, 362, 4716, 11, 1359, 11, 420, 3879, 25185, 10535, 6352, 411, 4583, 1958, 11, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11265665797863976, "compression_ratio": 1.4945054945054945, "no_speech_prob": 1.513025707326754e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 146730, "start": 1478.76, "end": 1486.0, "text": " those layers will blindly follow the immediate mathematical reward for the task and end up degrading the overall organization.", "tokens": [50938, 729, 7914, 486, 47744, 1524, 264, 11629, 18894, 7782, 337, 264, 5633, 293, 917, 493, 24740, 278, 264, 4787, 4475, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11265665797863976, "compression_ratio": 1.4945054945054945, "no_speech_prob": 1.513025707326754e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 146730, "start": 1486.32, "end": 1486.82, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51316, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11265665797863976, "compression_ratio": 1.4945054945054945, "no_speech_prob": 1.513025707326754e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 148682, "start": 1486.82, "end": 1497.34, "text": " So, because the training algorithm is just blindly following the math for the new task, if you let it touch layer 0, it will happily burn the house down just to get that short-term temperature boost.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 570, 264, 3097, 9284, 307, 445, 47744, 3480, 264, 5221, 337, 264, 777, 5633, 11, 498, 291, 718, 309, 2557, 4583, 1958, 11, 309, 486, 19909, 5064, 264, 1782, 760, 445, 281, 483, 300, 2099, 12, 7039, 4292, 9194, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08916113111707899, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232331234364294e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 148682, "start": 1497.46, "end": 1498.48, "text": " Yes, it doesn't know any better.", "tokens": [50897, 1079, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 458, 604, 1101, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08916113111707899, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232331234364294e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 148682, "start": 1498.6799999999998, "end": 1503.1399999999999, "text": " Giving the system too much freedom to move in the wrong places actually poisons the result.", "tokens": [50958, 28983, 264, 1185, 886, 709, 5645, 281, 1286, 294, 264, 2085, 3190, 767, 714, 23886, 264, 1874, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08916113111707899, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232331234364294e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 148682, "start": 1503.24, "end": 1503.74, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51186, 48746, 736, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08916113111707899, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232331234364294e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 148682, "start": 1504.32, "end": 1512.1, "text": " That is why locking down the fragile layers and only letting the rich middle layers move can result in a strictly superior model.", "tokens": [51240, 663, 307, 983, 23954, 760, 264, 23847, 7914, 293, 787, 8295, 264, 4593, 2808, 7914, 1286, 393, 1874, 294, 257, 20792, 13028, 2316, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08916113111707899, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232331234364294e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 151210, "start": 1512.1, "end": 1517.3999999999999, "text": " The restraint forces the optimization into the dense repair sets of the middle layers.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 49281, 5874, 264, 19618, 666, 264, 18011, 10535, 6352, 295, 264, 2808, 7914, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 151210, "start": 1517.56, "end": 1517.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50638, 7587, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 151210, "start": 1518.08, "end": 1521.7199999999998, "text": " It prevents the early layers from cannibalizing the model's foundational knowledge.", "tokens": [50664, 467, 22367, 264, 2440, 7914, 490, 12361, 34764, 3319, 264, 2316, 311, 32195, 3601, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 151210, "start": 1522.08, "end": 1523.34, "text": " That is just incredible.", "tokens": [50864, 663, 307, 445, 4651, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 151210, "start": 1523.54, "end": 1527.7199999999998, "text": " Imposing severe constraints actually produces better, safer optimization.", "tokens": [50937, 8270, 6110, 8922, 18491, 767, 14725, 1101, 11, 15856, 19618, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 151210, "start": 1528.1999999999998, "end": 1531.9599999999998, "text": " Okay, so we know the middle layers are the promised land for these repairs.", "tokens": [51170, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 458, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 264, 10768, 2117, 337, 613, 28823, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 151210, "start": 1532.24, "end": 1533.5, "text": " They have the dense repair sets.", "tokens": [51372, 814, 362, 264, 18011, 10535, 6352, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 151210, "start": 1533.52, "end": 1533.86, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [51436, 814, 360, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 151210, "start": 1534.12, "end": 1535.78, "text": " But that brings up a huge question.", "tokens": [51466, 583, 300, 5607, 493, 257, 2603, 1168, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 151210, "start": 1536.6, "end": 1540.76, "text": " If one middle layer is great, what happens if we train a few of them?", "tokens": [51590, 759, 472, 2808, 4583, 307, 869, 11, 437, 2314, 498, 321, 3847, 257, 1326, 295, 552, 30, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13983710738253002, "compression_ratio": 1.7552447552447552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747651442744482e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 154076, "start": 1540.76, "end": 1544.9, "text": " Do they stack together seamlessly or do they just, like, trip over each other?", "tokens": [50365, 1144, 436, 8630, 1214, 38083, 420, 360, 436, 445, 11, 411, 11, 4931, 670, 1184, 661, 30, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13877186812753753, "compression_ratio": 1.654434250764526, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043222523035028e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 154076, "start": 1545.02, "end": 1552.18, "text": " This is a crucial question, and it's where the paper moves from analyzing single layers to analyzing composition.", "tokens": [50578, 639, 307, 257, 11462, 1168, 11, 293, 309, 311, 689, 264, 3035, 6067, 490, 23663, 2167, 7914, 281, 23663, 12686, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13877186812753753, "compression_ratio": 1.654434250764526, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043222523035028e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 154076, "start": 1552.32, "end": 1552.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50943, 1779, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13877186812753753, "compression_ratio": 1.654434250764526, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043222523035028e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 154076, "start": 1552.92, "end": 1558.04, "text": " Because the Fliction paper points out that you cannot just assume that two good layers will work well together.", "tokens": [50973, 1436, 264, 3235, 4105, 3035, 2793, 484, 300, 291, 2644, 445, 6552, 300, 732, 665, 7914, 486, 589, 731, 1214, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13877186812753753, "compression_ratio": 1.654434250764526, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043222523035028e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 154076, "start": 1558.34, "end": 1563.68, "text": " And they highlight a truly baffling data point from the original study to illustrate this.", "tokens": [51244, 400, 436, 5078, 257, 4908, 272, 2518, 1688, 1412, 935, 490, 264, 3380, 2979, 281, 23221, 341, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13877186812753753, "compression_ratio": 1.654434250764526, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043222523035028e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 154076, "start": 1563.82, "end": 1566.16, "text": " Ah, the 34% overlap revelation.", "tokens": [51518, 2438, 11, 264, 12790, 4, 19959, 23456, 13, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13877186812753753, "compression_ratio": 1.654434250764526, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043222523035028e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 154076, "start": 1566.16, "end": 1570.56, "text": " I read this part of the source and I literally had to stop and read it twice to make sure I understood it.", "tokens": [51635, 286, 1401, 341, 644, 295, 264, 4009, 293, 286, 3736, 632, 281, 1590, 293, 1401, 309, 6091, 281, 652, 988, 286, 7320, 309, 13, 51855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13877186812753753, "compression_ratio": 1.654434250764526, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043222523035028e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 157056, "start": 1570.56, "end": 1571.3999999999999, "text": " Very surprising.", "tokens": [50365, 4372, 8830, 13, 50407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17665124170988508, "compression_ratio": 1.5851851851851853, "no_speech_prob": 1.299233507237596e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 157056, "start": 1571.6, "end": 1574.62, "text": " So they used an evaluation benchmark called Olympiad Bench.", "tokens": [50417, 407, 436, 1143, 364, 13344, 18927, 1219, 10395, 38069, 3964, 339, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17665124170988508, "compression_ratio": 1.5851851851851853, "no_speech_prob": 1.299233507237596e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 157056, "start": 1574.6799999999998, "end": 1578.3999999999999, "text": " It's a collection of really hard competition-level math and reasoning problems.", "tokens": [50571, 467, 311, 257, 5765, 295, 534, 1152, 6211, 12, 12418, 5221, 293, 21577, 2740, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17665124170988508, "compression_ratio": 1.5851851851851853, "no_speech_prob": 1.299233507237596e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 157056, "start": 1578.6799999999998, "end": 1583.9199999999998, "text": " And they evaluated the QUEN 3 1.7b base model on this benchmark.", "tokens": [50771, 400, 436, 25509, 264, 7246, 2195, 805, 502, 13, 22, 65, 3096, 2316, 322, 341, 18927, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17665124170988508, "compression_ratio": 1.5851851851851853, "no_speech_prob": 1.299233507237596e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 157056, "start": 1584.1599999999999, "end": 1584.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51045, 1779, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17665124170988508, "compression_ratio": 1.5851851851851853, "no_speech_prob": 1.299233507237596e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 157056, "start": 1584.62, "end": 1588.44, "text": " They looked at the seven highest contribution layers, so the seven individual middle layers,", "tokens": [51068, 814, 2956, 412, 264, 3407, 6343, 13150, 7914, 11, 370, 264, 3407, 2609, 2808, 7914, 11, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17665124170988508, "compression_ratio": 1.5851851851851853, "no_speech_prob": 1.299233507237596e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 157056, "start": 1588.44, "end": 1594.52, "text": " that, when trained completely alone, gave the biggest boost to the model's overall score on the math test.", "tokens": [51259, 300, 11, 562, 8895, 2584, 3312, 11, 2729, 264, 3880, 9194, 281, 264, 2316, 311, 4787, 6175, 322, 264, 5221, 1500, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17665124170988508, "compression_ratio": 1.5851851851851853, "no_speech_prob": 1.299233507237596e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 159452, "start": 1594.52, "end": 1601.28, "text": " Now, you might naturally assume that because these seven layers all achieved roughly the same high overall score on the benchmark,", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 291, 1062, 8195, 6552, 300, 570, 613, 3407, 7914, 439, 11042, 9810, 264, 912, 1090, 4787, 6175, 322, 264, 18927, 11, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15992118785907697, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 1.115647071253667e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 159452, "start": 1601.7, "end": 1605.02, "text": " they all learned the exact same underlying solution.", "tokens": [50724, 436, 439, 3264, 264, 1900, 912, 14217, 3827, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15992118785907697, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 1.115647071253667e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 159452, "start": 1605.3799999999999, "end": 1610.4, "text": " Yeah, you would think they all figured out the same generalized method for solving the new math problems,", "tokens": [50908, 865, 11, 291, 576, 519, 436, 439, 8932, 484, 264, 912, 44498, 3170, 337, 12606, 264, 777, 5221, 2740, 11, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15992118785907697, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 1.115647071253667e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 159452, "start": 1610.52, "end": 1612.0, "text": " like they all read the same textbook.", "tokens": [51165, 411, 436, 439, 1401, 264, 912, 25591, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15992118785907697, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 1.115647071253667e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 159452, "start": 1612.28, "end": 1612.94, "text": " But they didn't.", "tokens": [51253, 583, 436, 994, 380, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15992118785907697, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 1.115647071253667e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 161294, "start": 1612.94, "end": 1621.4, "text": " The source notes that when they looked at the specific individual problems that each layer newly solved relative to the untrained base model,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4009, 5570, 300, 562, 436, 2956, 412, 264, 2685, 2609, 2740, 300, 1184, 4583, 15109, 13041, 4972, 281, 264, 1701, 31774, 3096, 2316, 11, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16677963884570932, "compression_ratio": 1.6201923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.196657356539177e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 161294, "start": 1621.72, "end": 1625.3600000000001, "text": " there was only a 34% meme pairwise overlap.", "tokens": [50804, 456, 390, 787, 257, 12790, 4, 21701, 6119, 3711, 19959, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16677963884570932, "compression_ratio": 1.6201923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.196657356539177e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 161294, "start": 1625.6200000000001, "end": 1629.8, "text": " Meaning that if we look at what layer 12 learned versus what layer 13 learned,", "tokens": [50999, 19948, 300, 498, 321, 574, 412, 437, 4583, 2272, 3264, 5717, 437, 4583, 3705, 3264, 11, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16677963884570932, "compression_ratio": 1.6201923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.196657356539177e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 161294, "start": 1630.2, "end": 1633.3400000000001, "text": " they only agreed on about a third of the newly solved problems.", "tokens": [51228, 436, 787, 9166, 322, 466, 257, 2636, 295, 264, 15109, 13041, 2740, 13, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16677963884570932, "compression_ratio": 1.6201923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.196657356539177e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 161294, "start": 1633.46, "end": 1633.92, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51391, 7587, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16677963884570932, "compression_ratio": 1.6201923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.196657356539177e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 163392, "start": 1633.92, "end": 1638.26, "text": " Layer 12 might figure out how to solve a bunch of complex geometry problems.", "tokens": [50365, 35166, 2272, 1062, 2573, 484, 577, 281, 5039, 257, 3840, 295, 3997, 18426, 2740, 13, 50582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541964689890543, "compression_ratio": 1.6626506024096386, "no_speech_prob": 1.755399319826323e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 163392, "start": 1638.6200000000001, "end": 1644.74, "text": " But layer 13, which got the exact same overall score on the test, didn't figure out the geometry at all.", "tokens": [50600, 583, 4583, 3705, 11, 597, 658, 264, 1900, 912, 4787, 6175, 322, 264, 1500, 11, 994, 380, 2573, 484, 264, 18426, 412, 439, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541964689890543, "compression_ratio": 1.6626506024096386, "no_speech_prob": 1.755399319826323e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 163392, "start": 1645.04, "end": 1648.38, "text": " Instead, it figured out a bunch of advanced algebra problems.", "tokens": [50921, 7156, 11, 309, 8932, 484, 257, 3840, 295, 7339, 21989, 2740, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541964689890543, "compression_ratio": 1.6626506024096386, "no_speech_prob": 1.755399319826323e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 163392, "start": 1648.5600000000002, "end": 1653.76, "text": " They achieved comparable aggregate performance, but they did not converge on the same solutions at all.", "tokens": [51097, 814, 11042, 25323, 26118, 3389, 11, 457, 436, 630, 406, 41881, 322, 264, 912, 6547, 412, 439, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541964689890543, "compression_ratio": 1.6626506024096386, "no_speech_prob": 1.755399319826323e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 163392, "start": 1653.94, "end": 1657.16, "text": " Which leads to what the researchers call the ensemble effect.", "tokens": [51366, 3013, 6689, 281, 437, 264, 10309, 818, 264, 19492, 1802, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541964689890543, "compression_ratio": 1.6626506024096386, "no_speech_prob": 1.755399319826323e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 163392, "start": 1657.5600000000002, "end": 1657.92, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51547, 1079, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541964689890543, "compression_ratio": 1.6626506024096386, "no_speech_prob": 1.755399319826323e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 165792, "start": 1657.92, "end": 1663.0800000000002, "text": " Because these individual layers learned to solve different subsets of problems,", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 613, 2609, 7914, 3264, 281, 5039, 819, 2090, 1385, 295, 2740, 11, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20017965547331087, "compression_ratio": 1.7206477732793521, "no_speech_prob": 1.71474238887942e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 165792, "start": 1663.72, "end": 1671.3600000000001, "text": " the researchers could create a majority vote ensemble across these seven individually layer trained models.", "tokens": [50655, 264, 10309, 727, 1884, 257, 6286, 4740, 19492, 2108, 613, 3407, 16652, 4583, 8895, 5245, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20017965547331087, "compression_ratio": 1.7206477732793521, "no_speech_prob": 1.71474238887942e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 165792, "start": 1671.3600000000001, "end": 1676.26, "text": " So they ran the prompt through all seven differently trained versions of the model,", "tokens": [51037, 407, 436, 5872, 264, 12391, 807, 439, 3407, 7614, 8895, 9606, 295, 264, 2316, 11, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20017965547331087, "compression_ratio": 1.7206477732793521, "no_speech_prob": 1.71474238887942e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 165792, "start": 1676.48, "end": 1680.5800000000002, "text": " and whatever answer the majority gave, they took as a final answer.", "tokens": [51293, 293, 2035, 1867, 264, 6286, 2729, 11, 436, 1890, 382, 257, 2572, 1867, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20017965547331087, "compression_ratio": 1.7206477732793521, "no_speech_prob": 1.71474238887942e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 165792, "start": 1680.74, "end": 1680.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51506, 1779, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20017965547331087, "compression_ratio": 1.7206477732793521, "no_speech_prob": 1.71474238887942e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 165792, "start": 1681.3400000000001, "end": 1686.0, "text": " And this ensemble actually outperformed the single best individual layer.", "tokens": [51536, 400, 341, 19492, 767, 484, 610, 22892, 264, 2167, 1151, 2609, 4583, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20017965547331087, "compression_ratio": 1.7206477732793521, "no_speech_prob": 1.71474238887942e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 165792, "start": 1686.18, "end": 1686.68, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51778, 3153, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20017965547331087, "compression_ratio": 1.7206477732793521, "no_speech_prob": 1.71474238887942e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 168668, "start": 1686.68, "end": 1692.38, "text": " Even more impressively, it outperformed a match-size ensemble made of full parameter models.", "tokens": [50365, 2754, 544, 6729, 3413, 11, 309, 484, 610, 22892, 257, 2995, 12, 27553, 19492, 1027, 295, 1577, 13075, 5245, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13848768431564856, "compression_ratio": 1.6602564102564104, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177430890670593e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 168668, "start": 1692.8, "end": 1699.8600000000001, "text": " What's fascinating here is that it proves that the location of useful adaptation is not the same as the content of what gets learned there.", "tokens": [50671, 708, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 300, 309, 25019, 300, 264, 4914, 295, 4420, 21549, 307, 406, 264, 912, 382, 264, 2701, 295, 437, 2170, 3264, 456, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13848768431564856, "compression_ratio": 1.6602564102564104, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177430890670593e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 168668, "start": 1700.04, "end": 1700.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51033, 7587, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13848768431564856, "compression_ratio": 1.6602564102564104, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177430890670593e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 168668, "start": 1700.66, "end": 1707.3600000000001, "text": " Just because the middle layers are structurally the best place to learn doesn't mean they are mathematically predetermined to learn the exact same thing.", "tokens": [51064, 1449, 570, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 6594, 6512, 264, 1151, 1081, 281, 1466, 1177, 380, 914, 436, 366, 44003, 3852, 35344, 2001, 281, 1466, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13848768431564856, "compression_ratio": 1.6602564102564104, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177430890670593e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 168668, "start": 1707.48, "end": 1710.94, "text": " They each found a totally different path through their respective repair sets.", "tokens": [51405, 814, 1184, 1352, 257, 3879, 819, 3100, 807, 641, 23649, 10535, 6352, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13848768431564856, "compression_ratio": 1.6602564102564104, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177430890670593e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 168668, "start": 1711.1200000000001, "end": 1711.42, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51587, 1079, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13848768431564856, "compression_ratio": 1.6602564102564104, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177430890670593e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 168668, "start": 1711.54, "end": 1713.3600000000001, "text": " But this races the composition puzzle.", "tokens": [51608, 583, 341, 15484, 264, 12686, 12805, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13848768431564856, "compression_ratio": 1.6602564102564104, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177430890670593e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 171336, "start": 1713.36, "end": 1720.1799999999998, "text": " If they learn completely different things in isolation, how do they interact if we actually try to crane them together in the same model?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 436, 1466, 2584, 819, 721, 294, 16001, 11, 577, 360, 436, 4648, 498, 321, 767, 853, 281, 36345, 552, 1214, 294, 264, 912, 2316, 30, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13910083770751952, "compression_ratio": 1.280373831775701, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973436103492114e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 172018, "start": 1720.18, "end": 1728.0, "text": " The author, Fliction, proposes a three-level interaction hierarchy to rigorously test how these repairs compose.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 11, 3235, 4105, 11, 2365, 4201, 257, 1045, 12, 12418, 9285, 22333, 281, 42191, 5098, 1500, 577, 613, 28823, 35925, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10040265321731567, "compression_ratio": 1.5940170940170941, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108501894167905e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 172018, "start": 1728.14, "end": 1729.26, "text": " Okay, let's bring this down.", "tokens": [50763, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1565, 341, 760, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10040265321731567, "compression_ratio": 1.5940170940170941, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108501894167905e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 172018, "start": 1729.6000000000001, "end": 1735.78, "text": " Because, as the paper warns, you have to keep these three levels of interaction conceptually separate.", "tokens": [50836, 1436, 11, 382, 264, 3035, 12286, 82, 11, 291, 362, 281, 1066, 613, 1045, 4358, 295, 9285, 3410, 671, 4994, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10040265321731567, "compression_ratio": 1.5940170940170941, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108501894167905e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 172018, "start": 1736.28, "end": 1742.0800000000002, "text": " They're answered by completely different experiments and license entirely different conclusions about how the network functions.", "tokens": [51170, 814, 434, 10103, 538, 2584, 819, 12050, 293, 10476, 7696, 819, 22865, 466, 577, 264, 3209, 6828, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10040265321731567, "compression_ratio": 1.5940170940170941, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108501894167905e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 174208, "start": 1742.08, "end": 1743.58, "text": " Let's break down this hierarchy.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 341, 22333, 13, 50440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1752836648807969, "compression_ratio": 1.5042372881355932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253183253075234e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 174208, "start": 1744.04, "end": 1745.02, "text": " What is level one?", "tokens": [50463, 708, 307, 1496, 472, 30, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1752836648807969, "compression_ratio": 1.5042372881355932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253183253075234e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 174208, "start": 1745.3, "end": 1750.46, "text": " Level one is isolated summation, denoted mathematically as I-ISO.", "tokens": [50526, 16872, 472, 307, 14621, 28811, 11, 1441, 23325, 44003, 382, 286, 12, 2343, 46, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1752836648807969, "compression_ratio": 1.5042372881355932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253183253075234e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 174208, "start": 1751.06, "end": 1754.46, "text": " This asks the absolute simplest question about composition.", "tokens": [50814, 639, 8962, 264, 8236, 22811, 1168, 466, 12686, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1752836648807969, "compression_ratio": 1.5042372881355932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253183253075234e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 174208, "start": 1754.6399999999999, "end": 1755.06, "text": " Which is?", "tokens": [50993, 3013, 307, 30, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1752836648807969, "compression_ratio": 1.5042372881355932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253183253075234e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 174208, "start": 1755.3999999999999, "end": 1761.8, "text": " If we take repairs obtained in complete isolation and just literally add their weight updates together, do they interfere with each other?", "tokens": [51031, 759, 321, 747, 28823, 14879, 294, 3566, 16001, 293, 445, 3736, 909, 641, 3364, 9205, 1214, 11, 360, 436, 23946, 365, 1184, 661, 30, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1752836648807969, "compression_ratio": 1.5042372881355932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253183253075234e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 174208, "start": 1761.8999999999999, "end": 1762.9199999999998, "text": " So let's make this concrete.", "tokens": [51356, 407, 718, 311, 652, 341, 9859, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1752836648807969, "compression_ratio": 1.5042372881355932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253183253075234e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 176292, "start": 1762.92, "end": 1767.04, "text": " I take the base model and I train only layer 12 on the math benchmark.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 747, 264, 3096, 2316, 293, 286, 3847, 787, 4583, 2272, 322, 264, 5221, 18927, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 176292, "start": 1767.52, "end": 1769.88, "text": " I get a set of changes to the weights in layer 12.", "tokens": [50595, 286, 483, 257, 992, 295, 2962, 281, 264, 17443, 294, 4583, 2272, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 176292, "start": 1770.1000000000001, "end": 1772.26, "text": " Let's call that specific set of changes delta A.", "tokens": [50724, 961, 311, 818, 300, 2685, 992, 295, 2962, 8289, 316, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 176292, "start": 1772.66, "end": 1772.9, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50852, 1033, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 176292, "start": 1773.0, "end": 1777.96, "text": " Then I throw that away, reset the model to the base state, and train only layer 14 on the math benchmark.", "tokens": [50869, 1396, 286, 3507, 300, 1314, 11, 14322, 264, 2316, 281, 264, 3096, 1785, 11, 293, 3847, 787, 4583, 3499, 322, 264, 5221, 18927, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 176292, "start": 1778.48, "end": 1780.6000000000001, "text": " I get a different set of changes for layer 14.", "tokens": [51143, 286, 483, 257, 819, 992, 295, 2962, 337, 4583, 3499, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 176292, "start": 1780.74, "end": 1781.68, "text": " Let's call it delta B.", "tokens": [51256, 961, 311, 818, 309, 8289, 363, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 176292, "start": 1781.98, "end": 1782.3400000000001, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51318, 12753, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 176292, "start": 1782.8600000000001, "end": 1787.42, "text": " Both were derived in a universe where the other layer remained frozen at its original state.", "tokens": [51362, 6767, 645, 18949, 294, 257, 6445, 689, 264, 661, 4583, 12780, 12496, 412, 1080, 3380, 1785, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293075995716622, "compression_ratio": 1.8455284552845528, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682417166430374e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 178742, "start": 1787.42, "end": 1797.8400000000001, "text": " So level one is just asking, what happens if I take the original base model and I slap both delta A into layer 12 and delta B into layer 14 at the exact same time?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1496, 472, 307, 445, 3365, 11, 437, 2314, 498, 286, 747, 264, 3380, 3096, 2316, 293, 286, 21075, 1293, 8289, 316, 666, 4583, 2272, 293, 8289, 363, 666, 4583, 3499, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 565, 30, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08168420953265691, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833603316679155e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 178742, "start": 1797.96, "end": 1798.44, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50892, 7587, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08168420953265691, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833603316679155e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 178742, "start": 1798.6000000000001, "end": 1804.46, "text": " And this is very easy to test because you don't even need to run a new expensive reinforcement learning sequence.", "tokens": [50924, 400, 341, 307, 588, 1858, 281, 1500, 570, 291, 500, 380, 754, 643, 281, 1190, 257, 777, 5124, 29280, 2539, 8310, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08168420953265691, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833603316679155e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 178742, "start": 1804.48, "end": 1804.94, "text": " Not really.", "tokens": [51218, 1726, 534, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08168420953265691, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833603316679155e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 178742, "start": 1805.2, "end": 1805.44, "text": " No.", "tokens": [51254, 883, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08168420953265691, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833603316679155e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 178742, "start": 1805.5800000000002, "end": 1816.76, "text": " You just take the existing saved checkpoints, do some simple matrix addition to apply both sets of weight deltas to the base model simultaneously, and evaluate the resulting model on the benchmark.", "tokens": [51273, 509, 445, 747, 264, 6741, 6624, 1520, 20552, 11, 360, 512, 2199, 8141, 4500, 281, 3079, 1293, 6352, 295, 3364, 1103, 83, 296, 281, 264, 3096, 2316, 16561, 11, 293, 13059, 264, 16505, 2316, 322, 264, 18927, 13, 51832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08168420953265691, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833603316679155e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 181676, "start": 1816.76, "end": 1818.8, "text": " And what are we looking for when we do that?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 366, 321, 1237, 337, 562, 321, 360, 300, 30, 50467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 181676, "start": 1819.1, "end": 1827.5, "text": " If the performance of this combined model drops compared to how the individual layers performed on their own, you have a negative I-ISO value.", "tokens": [50482, 759, 264, 3389, 295, 341, 9354, 2316, 11438, 5347, 281, 577, 264, 2609, 7914, 10332, 322, 641, 1065, 11, 291, 362, 257, 3671, 286, 12, 2343, 46, 2158, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 181676, "start": 1827.56, "end": 1828.5, "text": " Meaning they clash.", "tokens": [50905, 19948, 436, 36508, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 181676, "start": 1829.02, "end": 1831.86, "text": " It means the isolated repairs obstruct each other when summed.", "tokens": [50978, 467, 1355, 264, 14621, 28823, 45579, 1184, 661, 562, 2408, 1912, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 181676, "start": 1832.36, "end": 1836.9, "text": " The change in layer 12 relied on layer 14 being in its original state, and vice versa.", "tokens": [51145, 440, 1319, 294, 4583, 2272, 35463, 322, 4583, 3499, 885, 294, 1080, 3380, 1785, 11, 293, 11964, 25650, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 181676, "start": 1837.42, "end": 1839.64, "text": " When you change both, they break each other's assumptions.", "tokens": [51398, 1133, 291, 1319, 1293, 11, 436, 1821, 1184, 661, 311, 17695, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 181676, "start": 1839.72, "end": 1840.32, "text": " Okay, got it.", "tokens": [51513, 1033, 11, 658, 309, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 181676, "start": 1840.34, "end": 1841.68, "text": " That's just slapping the results together.", "tokens": [51544, 663, 311, 445, 8039, 3759, 264, 3542, 1214, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 181676, "start": 1841.8799999999999, "end": 1842.84, "text": " What is level two?", "tokens": [51621, 708, 307, 1496, 732, 30, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 181676, "start": 1842.84, "end": 1846.18, "text": " Level two is the joint optimization path, or I-joint.", "tokens": [51669, 16872, 732, 307, 264, 7225, 19618, 3100, 11, 420, 286, 12, 48613, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12181933266775949, "compression_ratio": 1.6396396396396395, "no_speech_prob": 1.524891974843956e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 184676, "start": 1846.76, "end": 1848.86, "text": " This asks a slightly more dynamic question.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 8962, 257, 4748, 544, 8546, 1168, 13, 50470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11025809248288472, "compression_ratio": 1.3724137931034484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365298009634154e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 184676, "start": 1849.32, "end": 1858.2, "text": " Do the layers obstruct each other during the actual path of joint training, when both are unfrozen, free to move, and reacting to each other at every step?", "tokens": [50493, 1144, 264, 7914, 45579, 1184, 661, 1830, 264, 3539, 3100, 295, 7225, 3097, 11, 562, 1293, 366, 3971, 340, 2904, 11, 1737, 281, 1286, 11, 293, 25817, 281, 1184, 661, 412, 633, 1823, 30, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11025809248288472, "compression_ratio": 1.3724137931034484, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365298009634154e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 185820, "start": 1858.2, "end": 1864.06, "text": " So instead of training them in isolation and slapping the final results together, we go back to the start.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 2602, 295, 3097, 552, 294, 16001, 293, 8039, 3759, 264, 2572, 3542, 1214, 11, 321, 352, 646, 281, 264, 722, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08249251331601824, "compression_ratio": 1.475609756097561, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620055805037116e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 185820, "start": 1864.46, "end": 1873.1200000000001, "text": " We unfreeze both layer 12 and layer 14 at the same time, keep everything else frozen, and let the reinforcement learning algorithm run.", "tokens": [50678, 492, 3971, 701, 1381, 1293, 4583, 2272, 293, 4583, 3499, 412, 264, 912, 565, 11, 1066, 1203, 1646, 12496, 11, 293, 718, 264, 29280, 2539, 9284, 1190, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08249251331601824, "compression_ratio": 1.475609756097561, "no_speech_prob": 1.7620055805037116e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 187312, "start": 1873.12, "end": 1873.56, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [50365, 12753, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18239096520652234, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368530016310333e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 187312, "start": 1873.9799999999998, "end": 1881.76, "text": " In this scenario, at step one, layer 12 updates slightly, which changes the internal representations that layer 14 receives.", "tokens": [50408, 682, 341, 9005, 11, 412, 1823, 472, 11, 4583, 2272, 9205, 4748, 11, 597, 2962, 264, 6920, 33358, 300, 4583, 3499, 20717, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18239096520652234, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368530016310333e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 187312, "start": 1881.82, "end": 1882.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50800, 1779, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18239096520652234, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368530016310333e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 187312, "start": 1882.36, "end": 1888.32, "text": " Layer 14 then updates based on this new reality, which in turn changes the gradient for layer 12 on the next step.", "tokens": [50827, 35166, 3499, 550, 9205, 2361, 322, 341, 777, 4103, 11, 597, 294, 1261, 2962, 264, 16235, 337, 4583, 2272, 322, 264, 958, 1823, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18239096520652234, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368530016310333e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 187312, "start": 1889.02, "end": 1890.5, "text": " They're in a constant feedback loop.", "tokens": [51160, 814, 434, 294, 257, 5754, 5824, 6367, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18239096520652234, "compression_ratio": 1.553191489361702, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368530016310333e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 189050, "start": 1890.5, "end": 1897.26, "text": " So the deltas that arise during this junk training process might look absolutely nothing like the deltas that arose during isolation.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 1103, 83, 296, 300, 20288, 1830, 341, 19109, 3097, 1399, 1062, 574, 3122, 1825, 411, 264, 1103, 83, 296, 300, 37192, 1830, 16001, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1323437819609771, "compression_ratio": 1.7859778597785978, "no_speech_prob": 1.283824392281363e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 189050, "start": 1897.6, "end": 1898.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50720, 7587, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1323437819609771, "compression_ratio": 1.7859778597785978, "no_speech_prob": 1.283824392281363e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 189050, "start": 1898.44, "end": 1904.06, "text": " Level two measures whether as they step through the optimization process together, they're cooperating to find a better solution,", "tokens": [50762, 16872, 732, 8000, 1968, 382, 436, 1823, 807, 264, 19618, 1399, 1214, 11, 436, 434, 13414, 990, 281, 915, 257, 1101, 3827, 11, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1323437819609771, "compression_ratio": 1.7859778597785978, "no_speech_prob": 1.283824392281363e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 189050, "start": 1904.06, "end": 1910.22, "text": " or if they're fighting each other over the gradient, causing the optimization process to stall or fail.", "tokens": [51043, 420, 498, 436, 434, 5237, 1184, 661, 670, 264, 16235, 11, 9853, 264, 19618, 1399, 281, 19633, 420, 3061, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1323437819609771, "compression_ratio": 1.7859778597785978, "no_speech_prob": 1.283824392281363e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 189050, "start": 1910.36, "end": 1911.2, "text": " Okay, that makes sense.", "tokens": [51358, 1033, 11, 300, 1669, 2020, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1323437819609771, "compression_ratio": 1.7859778597785978, "no_speech_prob": 1.283824392281363e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 189050, "start": 1911.32, "end": 1912.96, "text": " And the final level, level three.", "tokens": [51406, 400, 264, 2572, 1496, 11, 1496, 1045, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1323437819609771, "compression_ratio": 1.7859778597785978, "no_speech_prob": 1.283824392281363e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 189050, "start": 1913.22, "end": 1915.24, "text": " Level three is the broadest and deepest question.", "tokens": [51501, 16872, 1045, 307, 264, 4152, 377, 293, 28288, 1168, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1323437819609771, "compression_ratio": 1.7859778597785978, "no_speech_prob": 1.283824392281363e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 191524, "start": 1915.24, "end": 1916.88, "text": " Reachable sets.", "tokens": [50365, 35904, 712, 6352, 13, 50447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19367796374905494, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.319408232842989e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 191524, "start": 1917.54, "end": 1924.54, "text": " This asks whether training layers jointly uncover solutions that are completely mathematically unavailable to isolated searches.", "tokens": [50480, 639, 8962, 1968, 3097, 7914, 46557, 21694, 6547, 300, 366, 2584, 44003, 36541, 32699, 281, 14621, 26701, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19367796374905494, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.319408232842989e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 191524, "start": 1925.1200000000001, "end": 1933.42, "text": " Does the combination of unfreezing layer 12 and layer 14 open up a subspace of parameters that neither layer could ever reach on its own?", "tokens": [50859, 4402, 264, 6562, 295, 3971, 701, 8781, 4583, 2272, 293, 4583, 3499, 1269, 493, 257, 2090, 17940, 295, 9834, 300, 9662, 4583, 727, 1562, 2524, 322, 1080, 1065, 30, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19367796374905494, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.319408232842989e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 191524, "start": 1933.42, "end": 1935.96, "text": " In other words, does one plus one equal three?", "tokens": [51274, 682, 661, 2283, 11, 775, 472, 1804, 472, 2681, 1045, 30, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19367796374905494, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.319408232842989e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 191524, "start": 1936.5, "end": 1940.02, "text": " Does the co-adaptation allow them to find a super solution?", "tokens": [51428, 4402, 264, 598, 12, 345, 2796, 399, 2089, 552, 281, 915, 257, 1687, 3827, 30, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19367796374905494, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.319408232842989e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 191524, "start": 1940.72, "end": 1941.1, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51639, 7587, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19367796374905494, "compression_ratio": 1.611336032388664, "no_speech_prob": 1.319408232842989e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 194110, "start": 1941.1, "end": 1947.28, "text": " And the paper stresses that you cannot answer level three with just simple arithmetic on the weight deltas.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3035, 27732, 300, 291, 2644, 1867, 1496, 1045, 365, 445, 2199, 42973, 322, 264, 3364, 1103, 83, 296, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11546210522921581, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144729646395573e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 194110, "start": 1947.3999999999999, "end": 1948.52, "text": " You can't just add them up.", "tokens": [50680, 509, 393, 380, 445, 909, 552, 493, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11546210522921581, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144729646395573e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 194110, "start": 1948.58, "end": 1948.76, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50739, 883, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11546210522921581, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144729646395573e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 194110, "start": 1948.9599999999998, "end": 1957.5, "text": " You have to actually compare jointly trained models against every possible mathematical interpolation and composition of the isolated repairs.", "tokens": [50758, 509, 362, 281, 767, 6794, 46557, 8895, 5245, 1970, 633, 1944, 18894, 44902, 399, 293, 12686, 295, 264, 14621, 28823, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11546210522921581, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144729646395573e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 194110, "start": 1958.26, "end": 1963.12, "text": " It is a deep question about the fundamental multidimensional geometry of the parameters face.", "tokens": [51223, 467, 307, 257, 2452, 1168, 466, 264, 8088, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 18426, 295, 264, 9834, 1851, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11546210522921581, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144729646395573e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 194110, "start": 1963.28, "end": 1964.6999999999998, "text": " Let's bring this back to Earth for a second.", "tokens": [51474, 961, 311, 1565, 341, 646, 281, 4755, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11546210522921581, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144729646395573e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 194110, "start": 1965.04, "end": 1967.24, "text": " Why should anyone listening care about this hierarchy?", "tokens": [51562, 1545, 820, 2878, 4764, 1127, 466, 341, 22333, 30, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11546210522921581, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144729646395573e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 196724, "start": 1967.24, "end": 1976.28, "text": " Well, because it proves that locating a cognitive function inside an AI isn't just about pointing your finger at a layer and saying, aha, layer 15 is the reasoning layer.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 570, 309, 25019, 300, 1628, 990, 257, 15605, 2445, 1854, 364, 7318, 1943, 380, 445, 466, 12166, 428, 5984, 412, 257, 4583, 293, 1566, 11, 47340, 11, 4583, 2119, 307, 264, 21577, 4583, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914161314447243, "compression_ratio": 1.4915254237288136, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950828118934223e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 196724, "start": 1976.4, "end": 1976.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50823, 1779, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914161314447243, "compression_ratio": 1.4915254237288136, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950828118934223e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 196724, "start": 1976.84, "end": 1980.94, "text": " It is about understanding how isolated improvements interact dynamically.", "tokens": [50845, 467, 307, 466, 3701, 577, 14621, 13797, 4648, 43492, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914161314447243, "compression_ratio": 1.4915254237288136, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950828118934223e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 196724, "start": 1981.34, "end": 1985.72, "text": " Think of it like assembling a team for a massive project at a software company.", "tokens": [51070, 6557, 295, 309, 411, 43867, 257, 1469, 337, 257, 5994, 1716, 412, 257, 4722, 2237, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914161314447243, "compression_ratio": 1.4915254237288136, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950828118934223e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 196724, "start": 1985.86, "end": 1986.58, "text": " Okay, let's hear it.", "tokens": [51296, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914161314447243, "compression_ratio": 1.4915254237288136, "no_speech_prob": 1.4950828118934223e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 198658, "start": 1986.58, "end": 1996.1, "text": " Level one is like taking two developers who are amazing solo workers, putting them in the same room, taking their individual code and just copy pasting it together.", "tokens": [50365, 16872, 472, 307, 411, 1940, 732, 8849, 567, 366, 2243, 6944, 5600, 11, 3372, 552, 294, 264, 912, 1808, 11, 1940, 641, 2609, 3089, 293, 445, 5055, 1791, 278, 309, 1214, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1472565399973016, "compression_ratio": 1.6037735849056605, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368535437321196e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 198658, "start": 1996.32, "end": 1997.46, "text": " A recipe for disaster.", "tokens": [50852, 316, 6782, 337, 11293, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1472565399973016, "compression_ratio": 1.6037735849056605, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368535437321196e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 198658, "start": 1997.6799999999998, "end": 1998.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50920, 7587, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1472565399973016, "compression_ratio": 1.6037735849056605, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368535437321196e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 198658, "start": 1998.6399999999999, "end": 2003.32, "text": " Just because they are great solo doesn't mean their code won't immediately crash when combined.", "tokens": [50968, 1449, 570, 436, 366, 869, 6944, 1177, 380, 914, 641, 3089, 1582, 380, 4258, 8252, 562, 9354, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1472565399973016, "compression_ratio": 1.6037735849056605, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368535437321196e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 198658, "start": 2003.62, "end": 2007.1399999999999, "text": " They might have used the same variable names for completely different things.", "tokens": [51217, 814, 1062, 362, 1143, 264, 912, 7006, 5288, 337, 2584, 819, 721, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1472565399973016, "compression_ratio": 1.6037735849056605, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368535437321196e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 198658, "start": 2007.22, "end": 2009.9199999999998, "text": " A perfect parallel to the isolated deltas interfering.", "tokens": [51397, 316, 2176, 8952, 281, 264, 14621, 1103, 83, 296, 48721, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1472565399973016, "compression_ratio": 1.6037735849056605, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368535437321196e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 200992, "start": 2009.92, "end": 2010.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835978077907189, "compression_ratio": 1.6215277777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691395243763504e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 200992, "start": 2010.92, "end": 2021.1200000000001, "text": " Then level two is asking if those two developers can actually collaborate on a shared GitHub repository in real time without constantly deleting each other's work and fighting over the architecture.", "tokens": [50415, 1396, 1496, 732, 307, 3365, 498, 729, 732, 8849, 393, 767, 18338, 322, 257, 5507, 23331, 25841, 294, 957, 565, 1553, 6460, 48946, 1184, 661, 311, 589, 293, 5237, 670, 264, 9482, 13, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835978077907189, "compression_ratio": 1.6215277777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691395243763504e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 200992, "start": 2021.52, "end": 2023.64, "text": " Can they optimize their joint path?", "tokens": [50945, 1664, 436, 19719, 641, 7225, 3100, 30, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835978077907189, "compression_ratio": 1.6215277777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691395243763504e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 200992, "start": 2023.88, "end": 2024.5, "text": " Yeah, level three.", "tokens": [51063, 865, 11, 1496, 1045, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835978077907189, "compression_ratio": 1.6215277777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691395243763504e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 200992, "start": 2024.76, "end": 2034.14, "text": " Level three is asking if their collaboration produces an entirely new piece of software, like a brilliant idea that neither of them could have ever conceived of or built alone.", "tokens": [51107, 16872, 1045, 307, 3365, 498, 641, 9363, 14725, 364, 7696, 777, 2522, 295, 4722, 11, 411, 257, 10248, 1558, 300, 9662, 295, 552, 727, 362, 1562, 34898, 295, 420, 3094, 3312, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835978077907189, "compression_ratio": 1.6215277777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691395243763504e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 200992, "start": 2034.3600000000001, "end": 2035.48, "text": " That's a great way to put it.", "tokens": [51587, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11835978077907189, "compression_ratio": 1.6215277777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.2691395243763504e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 203548, "start": 2035.48, "end": 2039.28, "text": " The AI's layers operate under the exact same team dynamics.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7318, 311, 7914, 9651, 833, 264, 1900, 912, 1469, 15679, 13, 50555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746195598315166, "compression_ratio": 1.623134328358209, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856365699618014e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 203548, "start": 2039.72, "end": 2043.92, "text": " You can't understand the team just by interviewing the members in complete isolation.", "tokens": [50577, 509, 393, 380, 1223, 264, 1469, 445, 538, 26524, 264, 2679, 294, 3566, 16001, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746195598315166, "compression_ratio": 1.623134328358209, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856365699618014e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 203548, "start": 2044.54, "end": 2048.94, "text": " That is a highly accurate way to visualize the interaction hierarchy.", "tokens": [50818, 663, 307, 257, 5405, 8559, 636, 281, 23273, 264, 9285, 22333, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746195598315166, "compression_ratio": 1.623134328358209, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856365699618014e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 203548, "start": 2049.46, "end": 2056.22, "text": " It forces the field to move away from static anatomy, just pointing at layers, and toward dynamic composition.", "tokens": [51064, 467, 5874, 264, 2519, 281, 1286, 1314, 490, 13437, 31566, 11, 445, 12166, 412, 7914, 11, 293, 7361, 8546, 12686, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746195598315166, "compression_ratio": 1.623134328358209, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856365699618014e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 203548, "start": 2056.48, "end": 2060.5, "text": " We have to understand how these components negotiate their updates.", "tokens": [51415, 492, 362, 281, 1223, 577, 613, 6677, 21713, 641, 9205, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746195598315166, "compression_ratio": 1.623134328358209, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856365699618014e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 203548, "start": 2060.68, "end": 2062.1, "text": " Here's where it gets really interesting.", "tokens": [51625, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746195598315166, "compression_ratio": 1.623134328358209, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856365699618014e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 206210, "start": 2062.1, "end": 2067.94, "text": " Up until now, everything we have talked about has been based on hard, observable data.", "tokens": [50365, 5858, 1826, 586, 11, 1203, 321, 362, 2825, 466, 575, 668, 2361, 322, 1152, 11, 9951, 712, 1412, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 206210, "start": 2068.2, "end": 2069.2, "text": " Yes, empirical facts.", "tokens": [50670, 1079, 11, 31886, 9130, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 206210, "start": 2069.3399999999997, "end": 2070.66, "text": " The researchers froze layers.", "tokens": [50727, 440, 10309, 46077, 7914, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 206210, "start": 2070.8399999999997, "end": 2071.72, "text": " They measured performance.", "tokens": [50802, 814, 12690, 3389, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 206210, "start": 2071.96, "end": 2073.58, "text": " They checked the math on the overlaps.", "tokens": [50858, 814, 10033, 264, 5221, 322, 264, 15986, 2382, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 206210, "start": 2073.88, "end": 2078.94, "text": " But in Section 5 of the paper, Affliction ventures into something incredibly compelling.", "tokens": [50954, 583, 294, 21804, 1025, 295, 264, 3035, 11, 12840, 75, 4105, 6931, 1303, 666, 746, 6252, 20050, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 206210, "start": 2079.2599999999998, "end": 2079.58, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [51223, 814, 360, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 206210, "start": 2079.64, "end": 2085.38, "text": " They propose a hypothesis for WHY this middle layer magic actually happens in the first place.", "tokens": [51242, 814, 17421, 257, 17291, 337, 32720, 341, 2808, 4583, 5585, 767, 2314, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 206210, "start": 2085.68, "end": 2089.48, "text": " Now, before we dive into the WHY, I really need to issue an epistemic warning.", "tokens": [51544, 823, 11, 949, 321, 9192, 666, 264, 32720, 11, 286, 534, 643, 281, 2734, 364, 2388, 468, 3438, 9164, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 206210, "start": 2089.7599999999998, "end": 2090.5, "text": " Epistemic warning.", "tokens": [51748, 9970, 468, 3438, 9164, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 206210, "start": 2090.6, "end": 2091.14, "text": " I love it.", "tokens": [51790, 286, 959, 309, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16306102724003613, "compression_ratio": 1.632258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 2.060289222213796e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 209114, "start": 2091.14, "end": 2094.7799999999997, "text": " And the author of the paper takes great pains to highlight this distinction as well.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3793, 295, 264, 3035, 2516, 869, 29774, 281, 5078, 341, 16844, 382, 731, 13, 50547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112272999503397, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.898267784281038e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 209114, "start": 2095.2599999999998, "end": 2104.2, "text": " If we want to think clearly about AI, we must rigorously distinguish between observed quantities, derived quantities, and latent explanatory quantities.", "tokens": [50571, 759, 321, 528, 281, 519, 4448, 466, 7318, 11, 321, 1633, 42191, 5098, 20206, 1296, 13095, 22927, 11, 18949, 22927, 11, 293, 48994, 9045, 4745, 22927, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112272999503397, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.898267784281038e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 209114, "start": 2104.56, "end": 2107.0, "text": " Okay, we are putting up caution tape around the theory.", "tokens": [51036, 1033, 11, 321, 366, 3372, 493, 23585, 7314, 926, 264, 5261, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112272999503397, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.898267784281038e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 209114, "start": 2107.9, "end": 2113.64, "text": " Explain the difference between those three quantities, because I know interpretability research gets tangled up in this all the time.", "tokens": [51203, 39574, 264, 2649, 1296, 729, 1045, 22927, 11, 570, 286, 458, 7302, 2310, 2132, 2170, 47192, 493, 294, 341, 439, 264, 565, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112272999503397, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.898267784281038e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 211364, "start": 2113.64, "end": 2115.8399999999997, "text": " It is a very common trap to conflate them.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 588, 2689, 11487, 281, 1497, 17593, 552, 13, 50475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22543636266736017, "compression_ratio": 1.4263959390862944, "no_speech_prob": 1.95846832674873e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 211364, "start": 2116.3199999999997, "end": 2120.64, "text": " So, an observed quantity is something like the layer contribution score.", "tokens": [50499, 407, 11, 364, 13095, 11275, 307, 746, 411, 264, 4583, 13150, 6175, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22543636266736017, "compression_ratio": 1.4263959390862944, "no_speech_prob": 1.95846832674873e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 211364, "start": 2121.2599999999998, "end": 2126.24, "text": " Literally, how much the benchmark performance improved when we train layer 15.", "tokens": [50746, 23768, 11, 577, 709, 264, 18927, 3389, 9689, 562, 321, 3847, 4583, 2119, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22543636266736017, "compression_ratio": 1.4263959390862944, "no_speech_prob": 1.95846832674873e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 211364, "start": 2126.3599999999997, "end": 2126.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51001, 1779, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22543636266736017, "compression_ratio": 1.4263959390862944, "no_speech_prob": 1.95846832674873e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 211364, "start": 2126.8799999999997, "end": 2129.22, "text": " The researchers measured that directly with a test score.", "tokens": [51027, 440, 10309, 12690, 300, 3838, 365, 257, 1500, 6175, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22543636266736017, "compression_ratio": 1.4263959390862944, "no_speech_prob": 1.95846832674873e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 211364, "start": 2129.7, "end": 2130.8399999999997, "text": " It is empirical fact.", "tokens": [51168, 467, 307, 31886, 1186, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22543636266736017, "compression_ratio": 1.4263959390862944, "no_speech_prob": 1.95846832674873e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 213084, "start": 2130.84, "end": 2132.1200000000003, "text": " Okay, so that's the hard data.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 300, 311, 264, 1152, 1412, 13, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15875041632004727, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 1.942340168911705e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 213084, "start": 2132.1200000000003, "end": 2136.52, "text": " A derived quantity is the repair set we discussed earlier, the epsilon and delta constraints.", "tokens": [50429, 316, 18949, 11275, 307, 264, 10535, 992, 321, 7152, 3071, 11, 264, 17889, 293, 8289, 18491, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15875041632004727, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 1.942340168911705e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 213084, "start": 2136.94, "end": 2139.34, "text": " You can actually see a repair set in the wild.", "tokens": [50670, 509, 393, 767, 536, 257, 10535, 992, 294, 264, 4868, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15875041632004727, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 1.942340168911705e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 213084, "start": 2139.5, "end": 2139.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50798, 1779, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15875041632004727, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 1.942340168911705e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 213084, "start": 2139.92, "end": 2144.58, "text": " It is a mathematical object we constructed and defined to describe what the observed quantity is doing.", "tokens": [50819, 467, 307, 257, 18894, 2657, 321, 17083, 293, 7642, 281, 6786, 437, 264, 13095, 11275, 307, 884, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15875041632004727, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 1.942340168911705e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 213084, "start": 2144.6800000000003, "end": 2145.56, "text": " It organizes the data.", "tokens": [51057, 467, 4645, 279, 264, 1412, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15875041632004727, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 1.942340168911705e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 213084, "start": 2145.6600000000003, "end": 2146.06, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51106, 7587, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15875041632004727, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 1.942340168911705e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 214606, "start": 2146.06, "end": 2150.92, "text": " But a latent explanatory quantity is a theoretical construct.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 257, 48994, 9045, 4745, 11275, 307, 257, 20864, 7690, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20155021824787572, "compression_ratio": 1.733644859813084, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507368368894886e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 214606, "start": 2151.04, "end": 2151.52, "text": " It's theory.", "tokens": [50614, 467, 311, 5261, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20155021824787572, "compression_ratio": 1.733644859813084, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507368368894886e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 214606, "start": 2151.7599999999998, "end": 2151.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50650, 1079, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20155021824787572, "compression_ratio": 1.733644859813084, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507368368894886e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 214606, "start": 2152.64, "end": 2160.66, "text": " It is a story we invent to account for why the repair set looks the way it does, and why the observed quantities behave the way they do.", "tokens": [50694, 467, 307, 257, 1657, 321, 7962, 281, 2696, 337, 983, 264, 10535, 992, 1542, 264, 636, 309, 775, 11, 293, 983, 264, 13095, 22927, 15158, 264, 636, 436, 360, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20155021824787572, "compression_ratio": 1.733644859813084, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507368368894886e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 214606, "start": 2161.56, "end": 2166.2599999999998, "text": " The why we are about to discuss is strictly a latent theoretical construct.", "tokens": [51140, 440, 983, 321, 366, 466, 281, 2248, 307, 20792, 257, 48994, 20864, 7690, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20155021824787572, "compression_ratio": 1.733644859813084, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507368368894886e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 214606, "start": 2166.88, "end": 2168.38, "text": " It has not yet been directly observed.", "tokens": [51406, 467, 575, 406, 1939, 668, 3838, 13095, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20155021824787572, "compression_ratio": 1.733644859813084, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507368368894886e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 214606, "start": 2168.7999999999997, "end": 2171.34, "text": " It is a conjecture, a model of reality.", "tokens": [51502, 467, 307, 257, 416, 1020, 540, 11, 257, 2316, 295, 4103, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20155021824787572, "compression_ratio": 1.733644859813084, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507368368894886e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 217134, "start": 2171.34, "end": 2176.1800000000003, "text": " Caution tape acknowledged, we are entering theory territory, but the conjecture is brilliant.", "tokens": [50365, 383, 1375, 313, 7314, 27262, 11, 321, 366, 11104, 5261, 11360, 11, 457, 264, 416, 1020, 540, 307, 10248, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1621551146874061, "compression_ratio": 1.6577946768060836, "no_speech_prob": 1.854064428027935e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 217134, "start": 2176.48, "end": 2180.3, "text": " The paper proposes what we are going to call the product hypothesis.", "tokens": [50622, 440, 3035, 2365, 4201, 437, 321, 366, 516, 281, 818, 264, 1674, 17291, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1621551146874061, "compression_ratio": 1.6577946768060836, "no_speech_prob": 1.854064428027935e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 217134, "start": 2180.76, "end": 2188.34, "text": " It suggests that the contribution of any given layer, let's call that contribution C, is driven by the product of two twin pillars.", "tokens": [50836, 467, 13409, 300, 264, 13150, 295, 604, 2212, 4583, 11, 718, 311, 818, 300, 13150, 383, 11, 307, 9555, 538, 264, 1674, 295, 732, 18397, 26729, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1621551146874061, "compression_ratio": 1.6577946768060836, "no_speech_prob": 1.854064428027935e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 217134, "start": 2188.7200000000003, "end": 2192.38, "text": " The formula they propose is a schematic decomposition.", "tokens": [51234, 440, 8513, 436, 17421, 307, 257, 44739, 48356, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1621551146874061, "compression_ratio": 1.6577946768060836, "no_speech_prob": 1.854064428027935e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 217134, "start": 2193.4, "end": 2197.02, "text": " CK is proportional to AK multiplied by P.", "tokens": [51468, 383, 42, 307, 24969, 281, 24789, 17207, 538, 430, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1621551146874061, "compression_ratio": 1.6577946768060836, "no_speech_prob": 1.854064428027935e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 217134, "start": 2197.44, "end": 2199.2200000000003, "text": " Okay, let's translate the math into English.", "tokens": [51670, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 13799, 264, 5221, 666, 3669, 13, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1621551146874061, "compression_ratio": 1.6577946768060836, "no_speech_prob": 1.854064428027935e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 219922, "start": 2199.22, "end": 2202.3199999999997, "text": " CK is the layer contribution at layer K.", "tokens": [50365, 383, 42, 307, 264, 4583, 13150, 412, 4583, 591, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 219922, "start": 2202.54, "end": 2204.8399999999997, "text": " It is proportional to A multiplied by P.", "tokens": [50531, 467, 307, 24969, 281, 316, 17207, 538, 430, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 219922, "start": 2205.3999999999996, "end": 2206.64, "text": " So what are A and P?", "tokens": [50674, 407, 437, 366, 316, 293, 430, 30, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 219922, "start": 2206.7599999999998, "end": 2209.16, "text": " A stands for task abstraction availability.", "tokens": [50742, 316, 7382, 337, 5633, 37765, 17945, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 219922, "start": 2209.4399999999996, "end": 2210.64, "text": " Task abstraction availability.", "tokens": [50876, 30428, 37765, 17945, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 219922, "start": 2211.0, "end": 2211.2, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50954, 865, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 219922, "start": 2211.3999999999996, "end": 2211.9399999999996, "text": " And P?", "tokens": [50974, 400, 430, 30, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 219922, "start": 2212.18, "end": 2215.16, "text": " P stands for preservation compatible plasticity.", "tokens": [51013, 430, 7382, 337, 27257, 18218, 5900, 507, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 219922, "start": 2215.2999999999997, "end": 2217.9199999999996, "text": " Let's take those one at a time because they are dense concepts.", "tokens": [51169, 961, 311, 747, 729, 472, 412, 257, 565, 570, 436, 366, 18011, 10392, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 219922, "start": 2218.04, "end": 2218.1, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51306, 865, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 219922, "start": 2218.3399999999997, "end": 2219.7, "text": " Task abstraction availability.", "tokens": [51321, 30428, 37765, 17945, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 219922, "start": 2220.08, "end": 2221.18, "text": " A, what is that?", "tokens": [51408, 316, 11, 437, 307, 300, 30, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 219922, "start": 2221.3199999999997, "end": 2227.16, "text": " To understand A, we really need to look at how a modern transformer model actually processes data.", "tokens": [51470, 1407, 1223, 316, 11, 321, 534, 643, 281, 574, 412, 577, 257, 4363, 31782, 2316, 767, 7555, 1412, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20597752516831808, "compression_ratio": 1.7674418604651163, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834376332849123e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 222716, "start": 2227.16, "end": 2235.04, "text": " The paper relies heavily on prior work in the field, specifically by researchers like Jastrzewski regarding residual architectures.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 30910, 10950, 322, 4059, 589, 294, 264, 2519, 11, 4682, 538, 10309, 411, 508, 525, 19390, 1023, 18020, 8595, 27980, 6331, 1303, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446840205091111, "compression_ratio": 1.628691983122363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352502697266955e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 222716, "start": 2235.24, "end": 2236.54, "text": " What is a residual architecture?", "tokens": [50769, 708, 307, 257, 27980, 9482, 30, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446840205091111, "compression_ratio": 1.628691983122363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352502697266955e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 222716, "start": 2236.66, "end": 2237.44, "text": " Let's clarify that.", "tokens": [50840, 961, 311, 17594, 300, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446840205091111, "compression_ratio": 1.628691983122363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352502697266955e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 222716, "start": 2237.66, "end": 2242.54, "text": " In an older type of neural network, layer one would process data handed to layer two.", "tokens": [50890, 682, 364, 4906, 2010, 295, 18161, 3209, 11, 4583, 472, 576, 1399, 1412, 16013, 281, 4583, 732, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446840205091111, "compression_ratio": 1.628691983122363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352502697266955e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 222716, "start": 2242.8799999999997, "end": 2246.0, "text": " Layer two would completely transform it and hand it to layer three and so on.", "tokens": [51151, 35166, 732, 576, 2584, 4088, 309, 293, 1011, 309, 281, 4583, 1045, 293, 370, 322, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446840205091111, "compression_ratio": 1.628691983122363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352502697266955e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 222716, "start": 2246.1, "end": 2248.3399999999997, "text": " Like passing a baton in a relay race.", "tokens": [51312, 1743, 8437, 257, 7362, 266, 294, 257, 24214, 4569, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1446840205091111, "compression_ratio": 1.628691983122363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352502697266955e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 224834, "start": 2248.34, "end": 2248.6600000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 224834, "start": 2248.96, "end": 2255.7400000000002, "text": " But in a residual network, which is what modern LLMs use, there is a central pathway called the residual stream.", "tokens": [50396, 583, 294, 257, 27980, 3209, 11, 597, 307, 437, 4363, 441, 43, 26386, 764, 11, 456, 307, 257, 5777, 18590, 1219, 264, 27980, 4309, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 224834, "start": 2256.2000000000003, "end": 2259.1000000000004, "text": " Think of it like a central conveyor belt running through the entire model.", "tokens": [50758, 6557, 295, 309, 411, 257, 5777, 18053, 2454, 10750, 2614, 807, 264, 2302, 2316, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 224834, "start": 2259.2200000000003, "end": 2259.38, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50909, 1033, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 224834, "start": 2259.48, "end": 2260.1400000000003, "text": " A conveyor belt.", "tokens": [50922, 316, 18053, 2454, 10750, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 224834, "start": 2260.2200000000003, "end": 2260.94, "text": " I can picture that.", "tokens": [50959, 286, 393, 3036, 300, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 224834, "start": 2261.08, "end": 2263.32, "text": " Each layer doesn't replace the data on the belt.", "tokens": [51002, 6947, 4583, 1177, 380, 7406, 264, 1412, 322, 264, 10750, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 224834, "start": 2263.88, "end": 2272.1400000000003, "text": " Instead, each layer pulls the data off the belt, reads it, computes a small bounded update, and adds that tiny update back onto the belt.", "tokens": [51142, 7156, 11, 1184, 4583, 16982, 264, 1412, 766, 264, 10750, 11, 15700, 309, 11, 715, 1819, 257, 1359, 37498, 5623, 11, 293, 10860, 300, 5870, 5623, 646, 3911, 264, 10750, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 224834, "start": 2272.3, "end": 2272.98, "text": " So it's cumulative.", "tokens": [51563, 407, 309, 311, 38379, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11863498057215667, "compression_ratio": 1.6629213483146068, "no_speech_prob": 1.66823846403652e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 227298, "start": 2272.98, "end": 2277.2400000000002, "text": " Yes, it is a process of successive iterative refinement.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 309, 307, 257, 1399, 295, 48043, 17138, 1166, 1895, 30229, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1274254872248723, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617298899748723e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 227298, "start": 2278.2, "end": 2282.9, "text": " The representation on the belt gradually evolves as it moves through the depth of the model.", "tokens": [50626, 440, 10290, 322, 264, 10750, 13145, 43737, 382, 309, 6067, 807, 264, 7161, 295, 264, 2316, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1274254872248723, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617298899748723e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 227298, "start": 2283.58, "end": 2289.5, "text": " And the paper also cites interpretability work to prove this, like the logit lens and the tuned lens.", "tokens": [50895, 400, 264, 3035, 611, 269, 3324, 7302, 2310, 589, 281, 7081, 341, 11, 411, 264, 3565, 270, 6765, 293, 264, 10870, 6765, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1274254872248723, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617298899748723e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 227298, "start": 2289.84, "end": 2291.82, "text": " I've seen these terms thrown around on Twitter.", "tokens": [51208, 286, 600, 1612, 613, 2115, 11732, 926, 322, 5794, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1274254872248723, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617298899748723e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 227298, "start": 2292.3, "end": 2294.62, "text": " What do those actually show us about the conveyor belt?", "tokens": [51331, 708, 360, 729, 767, 855, 505, 466, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 30, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1274254872248723, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617298899748723e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 227298, "start": 2294.76, "end": 2297.48, "text": " The logit lens is a fascinating diagnostic tool.", "tokens": [51454, 440, 3565, 270, 6765, 307, 257, 10343, 27897, 2290, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1274254872248723, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617298899748723e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 227298, "start": 2297.92, "end": 2300.76, "text": " Normally, we only see the final output of the model at the very end.", "tokens": [51612, 17424, 11, 321, 787, 536, 264, 2572, 5598, 295, 264, 2316, 412, 264, 588, 917, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1274254872248723, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617298899748723e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 230076, "start": 2300.76, "end": 2304.0400000000004, "text": " But with the logit lens, you peek inside the transformer.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 365, 264, 3565, 270, 6765, 11, 291, 19604, 1854, 264, 31782, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11112838525038499, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.345929335865026e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 230076, "start": 2304.6800000000003, "end": 2311.44, "text": " You take the hidden states, the data currently sitting on the conveyor belt, at an intermediate layer, say, layer 10 out of 30.", "tokens": [50561, 509, 747, 264, 7633, 4368, 11, 264, 1412, 4362, 3798, 322, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 11, 412, 364, 19376, 4583, 11, 584, 11, 4583, 1266, 484, 295, 2217, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11112838525038499, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.345929335865026e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 230076, "start": 2311.78, "end": 2313.26, "text": " You pull the data off early.", "tokens": [50916, 509, 2235, 264, 1412, 766, 2440, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11112838525038499, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.345929335865026e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 230076, "start": 2313.42, "end": 2313.7000000000003, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50998, 1079, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11112838525038499, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.345929335865026e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 230076, "start": 2314.1400000000003, "end": 2324.36, "text": " And you force that intermediate half-baked data through the final decoding mechanism to see what vocabulary word the model would predict if the computation stopped right there at layer 10.", "tokens": [51034, 400, 291, 3464, 300, 19376, 1922, 12, 65, 7301, 1412, 807, 264, 2572, 979, 8616, 7513, 281, 536, 437, 19864, 1349, 264, 2316, 576, 6069, 498, 264, 24903, 5936, 558, 456, 412, 4583, 1266, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11112838525038499, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.345929335865026e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 230076, "start": 2324.6200000000003, "end": 2325.44, "text": " And what happens?", "tokens": [51558, 400, 437, 2314, 30, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11112838525038499, "compression_ratio": 1.6447876447876448, "no_speech_prob": 1.345929335865026e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 232544, "start": 2325.44, "end": 2335.9, "text": " What you find is amazing, as you move deeper into the network, layer by layer, those intermediate states look like increasingly confident partial predictions of the final output.", "tokens": [50365, 708, 291, 915, 307, 2243, 11, 382, 291, 1286, 7731, 666, 264, 3209, 11, 4583, 538, 4583, 11, 729, 19376, 4368, 574, 411, 12980, 6679, 14641, 21264, 295, 264, 2572, 5598, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14101649303825534, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.3300427382720303e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 232544, "start": 2336.2200000000003, "end": 2340.66, "text": " The internal representations evolve coherently and smoothly across depth.", "tokens": [50904, 440, 6920, 33358, 16693, 26528, 2276, 293, 19565, 2108, 7161, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14101649303825534, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.3300427382720303e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 234066, "start": 2340.66, "end": 2344.12, "text": " So, Ali layers might just be recognizing basic syntax.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 12020, 7914, 1062, 445, 312, 18538, 3875, 28431, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 234066, "start": 2344.42, "end": 2346.3399999999997, "text": " They might not know what word is coming next.", "tokens": [50553, 814, 1062, 406, 458, 437, 1349, 307, 1348, 958, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 234066, "start": 2346.3799999999997, "end": 2347.5, "text": " They just know it should be a noun.", "tokens": [50651, 814, 445, 458, 309, 820, 312, 257, 23307, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 234066, "start": 2347.7, "end": 2347.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50717, 1079, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 234066, "start": 2348.14, "end": 2352.2599999999998, "text": " But as you go deeper down the conveyor belt, the model starts forming abstract concepts.", "tokens": [50739, 583, 382, 291, 352, 7731, 760, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 11, 264, 2316, 3719, 15745, 12649, 10392, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 234066, "start": 2352.56, "end": 2357.68, "text": " If it's reading a math problem, layer 15 might finally realize, oh, this is trigonometry.", "tokens": [50960, 759, 309, 311, 3760, 257, 5221, 1154, 11, 4583, 2119, 1062, 2721, 4325, 11, 1954, 11, 341, 307, 35386, 266, 34730, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 234066, "start": 2357.8199999999997, "end": 2358.2599999999998, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51223, 48746, 736, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 234066, "start": 2358.44, "end": 2361.02, "text": " And that realization is task abstraction availability.", "tokens": [51254, 400, 300, 25138, 307, 5633, 37765, 17945, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 234066, "start": 2361.18, "end": 2361.3199999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51391, 1779, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.170614260718936, "compression_ratio": 1.5291828793774318, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013972695989477e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 236132, "start": 2361.32, "end": 2366.6800000000003, "text": " It is how much of the big picture task is actually available and understood at that specific layer.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 577, 709, 295, 264, 955, 3036, 5633, 307, 767, 2435, 293, 7320, 412, 300, 2685, 4583, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 236132, "start": 2367.6200000000003, "end": 2373.82, "text": " Naturally, A starts very low at the beginning of the network because the early layers are just processing raw text.", "tokens": [50680, 34304, 11, 316, 3719, 588, 2295, 412, 264, 2863, 295, 264, 3209, 570, 264, 2440, 7914, 366, 445, 9007, 8936, 2487, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 236132, "start": 2373.96, "end": 2374.1200000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50997, 1779, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 236132, "start": 2374.2000000000003, "end": 2375.7200000000003, "text": " They just see letters and spaces.", "tokens": [51009, 814, 445, 536, 7825, 293, 7673, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 236132, "start": 2376.0, "end": 2381.02, "text": " But A rises steadily as you get deeper, and the model builds a coherent understanding of the prompt.", "tokens": [51099, 583, 316, 21373, 36129, 382, 291, 483, 7731, 11, 293, 264, 2316, 15182, 257, 36239, 3701, 295, 264, 12391, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 236132, "start": 2381.5, "end": 2381.76, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51374, 1033, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 236132, "start": 2381.88, "end": 2384.26, "text": " So A goes up as you go deeper.", "tokens": [51393, 407, 316, 1709, 493, 382, 291, 352, 7731, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 236132, "start": 2384.7000000000003, "end": 2387.52, "text": " What about P, preservation-compatible plasticity?", "tokens": [51534, 708, 466, 430, 11, 27257, 12, 1112, 11584, 964, 5900, 507, 30, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12134090629783836, "compression_ratio": 1.5971223021582734, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170758288807656e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 238752, "start": 2387.52, "end": 2396.9, "text": " This is the extent to which a change made at that specific layer can be absorbed by the rest of the downstream network without destabilizing the inherited organization.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 8396, 281, 597, 257, 1319, 1027, 412, 300, 2685, 4583, 393, 312, 20799, 538, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 30621, 3209, 1553, 2677, 5177, 3319, 264, 27091, 4475, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 238752, "start": 2397.32, "end": 2403.14, "text": " So if you change a weight here, does the rest of the network panic and break, or can it smoothly roll with the punches?", "tokens": [50855, 407, 498, 291, 1319, 257, 3364, 510, 11, 775, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 3209, 14783, 293, 1821, 11, 420, 393, 309, 19565, 3373, 365, 264, 34103, 30, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 238752, "start": 2403.54, "end": 2403.94, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51166, 7587, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 238752, "start": 2404.32, "end": 2406.24, "text": " And how does P behave across the layers?", "tokens": [51205, 400, 577, 775, 430, 15158, 2108, 264, 7914, 30, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 238752, "start": 2406.4, "end": 2408.42, "text": " Well, key behaves inversely to A.", "tokens": [51309, 1042, 11, 2141, 36896, 21378, 736, 281, 316, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 238752, "start": 2409.02, "end": 2409.46, "text": " Inversely.", "tokens": [51440, 682, 840, 736, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 238752, "start": 2409.56, "end": 2409.74, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51467, 1079, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 238752, "start": 2410.28, "end": 2416.36, "text": " Near the very end of the network, the representations on the conveyor belt are highly committed to the final output decoding.", "tokens": [51503, 22200, 264, 588, 917, 295, 264, 3209, 11, 264, 33358, 322, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 366, 5405, 7784, 281, 264, 2572, 5598, 979, 8616, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1271133723221426, "compression_ratio": 1.6742671009771988, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383355617653137e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 241636, "start": 2416.36, "end": 2420.38, "text": " They are tightly bound to specific token-level surface forms.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 21952, 5472, 281, 2685, 14862, 12, 12418, 3753, 6422, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14960722489790482, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856450267387467e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 241636, "start": 2421.02, "end": 2422.98, "text": " Exactly which word is going to be printed on the screen?", "tokens": [50598, 7587, 597, 1349, 307, 516, 281, 312, 13567, 322, 264, 2568, 30, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14960722489790482, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856450267387467e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 241636, "start": 2423.2000000000003, "end": 2424.2000000000003, "text": " They are locked in.", "tokens": [50707, 814, 366, 9376, 294, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14960722489790482, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856450267387467e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 241636, "start": 2424.4, "end": 2433.54, "text": " If you perturb the network there, you are almost guaranteed to damage the fragile output conventions the model relies on to speak coherently.", "tokens": [50767, 759, 291, 40468, 264, 3209, 456, 11, 291, 366, 1920, 18031, 281, 4344, 264, 23847, 5598, 33520, 264, 2316, 30910, 322, 281, 1710, 26528, 2276, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14960722489790482, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856450267387467e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 241636, "start": 2433.7000000000003, "end": 2435.84, "text": " You violate the preservation budget, Volta.", "tokens": [51232, 509, 37478, 264, 27257, 4706, 11, 8911, 1328, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14960722489790482, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856450267387467e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 241636, "start": 2435.94, "end": 2436.34, "text": " Yeah, exactly.", "tokens": [51344, 865, 11, 2293, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14960722489790482, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856450267387467e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 241636, "start": 2436.76, "end": 2443.5, "text": " So plasticity, P, is very high early on because changes have plenty of time to be smoothed out by subsequent layers.", "tokens": [51385, 407, 5900, 507, 11, 430, 11, 307, 588, 1090, 2440, 322, 570, 2962, 362, 7140, 295, 565, 281, 312, 5508, 292, 484, 538, 19962, 7914, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14960722489790482, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856450267387467e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 244350, "start": 2443.5, "end": 2449.48, "text": " But P falls drastically as you get to the final layers and the representations become rigid.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 430, 8804, 29673, 382, 291, 483, 281, 264, 2572, 7914, 293, 264, 33358, 1813, 22195, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563078195620806, "compression_ratio": 1.5192307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980858993237424e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 244350, "start": 2449.72, "end": 2453.72, "text": " Let me pitch an analogy to tie this all together because I think I see the geometry of this now.", "tokens": [50676, 961, 385, 7293, 364, 21663, 281, 7582, 341, 439, 1214, 570, 286, 519, 286, 536, 264, 18426, 295, 341, 586, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563078195620806, "compression_ratio": 1.5192307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980858993237424e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 244350, "start": 2454.06, "end": 2454.46, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [50893, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563078195620806, "compression_ratio": 1.5192307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980858993237424e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 244350, "start": 2454.78, "end": 2459.78, "text": " Think of the AI's internal process like a factory assembly line building a custom car.", "tokens": [50929, 6557, 295, 264, 7318, 311, 6920, 1399, 411, 257, 9265, 12103, 1622, 2390, 257, 2375, 1032, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563078195620806, "compression_ratio": 1.5192307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980858993237424e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 244350, "start": 2460.28, "end": 2461.52, "text": " I think this will work well.", "tokens": [51204, 286, 519, 341, 486, 589, 731, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563078195620806, "compression_ratio": 1.5192307692307692, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980858993237424e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 246152, "start": 2461.52, "end": 2467.32, "text": " At the very beginning of the assembly line, so the earliest layers of the network, the workers are just unpacking raw materials.", "tokens": [50365, 1711, 264, 588, 2863, 295, 264, 12103, 1622, 11, 370, 264, 20573, 7914, 295, 264, 3209, 11, 264, 5600, 366, 445, 26699, 278, 8936, 5319, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 246152, "start": 2467.6, "end": 2470.2, "text": " They are sorting bolts and stamping sheets of steel.", "tokens": [50669, 814, 366, 32411, 18127, 293, 41792, 15421, 295, 8269, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 246152, "start": 2470.64, "end": 2470.68, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50821, 1033, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 246152, "start": 2470.88, "end": 2475.18, "text": " At this stage, task abstraction availability, A, is very low.", "tokens": [50833, 1711, 341, 3233, 11, 5633, 37765, 17945, 11, 316, 11, 307, 588, 2295, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 246152, "start": 2475.44, "end": 2479.12, "text": " You can't walk up to the workers sorting bolts and say, hey, I need you to make the car faster.", "tokens": [51061, 509, 393, 380, 1792, 493, 281, 264, 5600, 32411, 18127, 293, 584, 11, 4177, 11, 286, 643, 291, 281, 652, 264, 1032, 4663, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 246152, "start": 2479.52, "end": 2481.68, "text": " They don't have the abstraction of a car yet.", "tokens": [51265, 814, 500, 380, 362, 264, 37765, 295, 257, 1032, 1939, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 246152, "start": 2481.74, "end": 2482.88, "text": " They just have a bucket of bolts.", "tokens": [51376, 814, 445, 362, 257, 13058, 295, 18127, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 246152, "start": 2482.98, "end": 2485.54, "text": " It's too early to try and customize the final product.", "tokens": [51438, 467, 311, 886, 2440, 281, 853, 293, 19734, 264, 2572, 1674, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 246152, "start": 2485.92, "end": 2486.2599999999998, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51585, 12753, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1108681878378225, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 2.176091338373931e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 248626, "start": 2486.26, "end": 2495.0200000000004, "text": " So even though those early workers have a lot of freedom to change how they sort the bolts, meaning plasticity, P is high,", "tokens": [50365, 407, 754, 1673, 729, 2440, 5600, 362, 257, 688, 295, 5645, 281, 1319, 577, 436, 1333, 264, 18127, 11, 3620, 5900, 507, 11, 430, 307, 1090, 11, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09284051556453526, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610471899504819e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 248626, "start": 2495.36, "end": 2502.96, "text": " they can't effectively contribute to the high-level task of making the car faster because abstraction, A, is low.", "tokens": [50820, 436, 393, 380, 8659, 10586, 281, 264, 1090, 12, 12418, 5633, 295, 1455, 264, 1032, 4663, 570, 37765, 11, 316, 11, 307, 2295, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09284051556453526, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610471899504819e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 248626, "start": 2503.1600000000003, "end": 2506.5400000000004, "text": " Now look at the very end of the assembly line, the final layers.", "tokens": [51210, 823, 574, 412, 264, 588, 917, 295, 264, 12103, 1622, 11, 264, 2572, 7914, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09284051556453526, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610471899504819e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 248626, "start": 2507.0200000000004, "end": 2513.0200000000004, "text": " Here, the car is fully built, painted, the engine is tuned, and they're literally boxing it up in a shipping container.", "tokens": [51403, 1692, 11, 264, 1032, 307, 4498, 3094, 11, 11797, 11, 264, 2848, 307, 10870, 11, 293, 436, 434, 3736, 24424, 309, 493, 294, 257, 14122, 10129, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09284051556453526, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610471899504819e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 248626, "start": 2513.1400000000003, "end": 2513.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51709, 1779, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09284051556453526, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610471899504819e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 251332, "start": 2513.32, "end": 2516.52, "text": " At this point, the workers completely understand what the product is.", "tokens": [50365, 1711, 341, 935, 11, 264, 5600, 2584, 1223, 437, 264, 1674, 307, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 251332, "start": 2516.6200000000003, "end": 2521.1000000000004, "text": " The abstraction, A, is maxed out, but it is way too late to change the design.", "tokens": [50530, 440, 37765, 11, 316, 11, 307, 11469, 292, 484, 11, 457, 309, 307, 636, 886, 3469, 281, 1319, 264, 1715, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 251332, "start": 2521.2000000000003, "end": 2521.28, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50759, 1779, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 251332, "start": 2521.36, "end": 2522.0, "text": " It's boxed up.", "tokens": [50767, 467, 311, 2424, 292, 493, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 251332, "start": 2522.1000000000004, "end": 2527.96, "text": " If you tell them to swap the engine for a faster one now, they have to tear the finished car apart and ruin the shipping container.", "tokens": [50804, 759, 291, 980, 552, 281, 18135, 264, 2848, 337, 257, 4663, 472, 586, 11, 436, 362, 281, 12556, 264, 4335, 1032, 4936, 293, 15514, 264, 14122, 10129, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 251332, "start": 2528.7400000000002, "end": 2531.96, "text": " The plasticity, P, is practically zero.", "tokens": [51136, 440, 5900, 507, 11, 430, 11, 307, 15667, 4018, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 251332, "start": 2532.1400000000003, "end": 2533.96, "text": " High abstraction, low plasticity.", "tokens": [51306, 5229, 37765, 11, 2295, 5900, 507, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 251332, "start": 2534.56, "end": 2537.2400000000002, "text": " A change here violates the preservation budget immediately.", "tokens": [51427, 316, 1319, 510, 3448, 1024, 264, 27257, 4706, 4258, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 251332, "start": 2537.7400000000002, "end": 2538.82, "text": " The repair set is empty.", "tokens": [51586, 440, 10535, 992, 307, 6707, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 251332, "start": 2539.1400000000003, "end": 2541.7400000000002, "text": " But the middle layers, that is where the magic happens.", "tokens": [51656, 583, 264, 2808, 7914, 11, 300, 307, 689, 264, 5585, 2314, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 251332, "start": 2541.8, "end": 2542.02, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51789, 1079, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10885599149879835, "compression_ratio": 1.6677316293929711, "no_speech_prob": 1.472442935808449e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 254202, "start": 2542.02, "end": 2543.6, "text": " The car is halfway down the line.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1032, 307, 15461, 760, 264, 1622, 13, 50444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 254202, "start": 2543.72, "end": 2544.46, "text": " It's on the chassis.", "tokens": [50450, 467, 311, 322, 264, 28262, 13, 50487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 254202, "start": 2544.96, "end": 2546.22, "text": " The engine block is placed.", "tokens": [50512, 440, 2848, 3461, 307, 7074, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 254202, "start": 2546.38, "end": 2548.66, "text": " But the body panels aren't welded on yet.", "tokens": [50583, 583, 264, 1772, 13419, 3212, 380, 49227, 322, 1939, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 254202, "start": 2548.74, "end": 2550.58, "text": " It's like clay that is still on the wheel.", "tokens": [50701, 467, 311, 411, 13517, 300, 307, 920, 322, 264, 5589, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 254202, "start": 2550.8, "end": 2551.58, "text": " I love that image.", "tokens": [50804, 286, 959, 300, 3256, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 254202, "start": 2551.86, "end": 2554.7, "text": " The system has enough shape to understand what it is becoming.", "tokens": [50857, 440, 1185, 575, 1547, 3909, 281, 1223, 437, 309, 307, 5617, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 254202, "start": 2555.36, "end": 2557.54, "text": " So abstraction, A, is high enough.", "tokens": [51032, 407, 37765, 11, 316, 11, 307, 1090, 1547, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 254202, "start": 2557.94, "end": 2561.7599999999998, "text": " But it is still wet enough to mold without breaking the whole system apart.", "tokens": [51161, 583, 309, 307, 920, 6630, 1547, 281, 11102, 1553, 7697, 264, 1379, 1185, 4936, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 254202, "start": 2562.0, "end": 2565.36, "text": " So plasticity, P, is also high enough.", "tokens": [51364, 407, 5900, 507, 11, 430, 11, 307, 611, 1090, 1547, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15231296705163044, "compression_ratio": 1.6906779661016949, "no_speech_prob": 1.920399820068419e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 256536, "start": 2565.36, "end": 2568.1200000000003, "text": " That is the beautiful elegance of the product hypothesis.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 2238, 14459, 719, 295, 264, 1674, 17291, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327995777130127, "compression_ratio": 1.5723684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359642590266232e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 256536, "start": 2568.1200000000003, "end": 2572.26, "text": " You have one quantity, abstraction, A, that is steadily rising with depth.", "tokens": [50503, 509, 362, 472, 11275, 11, 37765, 11, 316, 11, 300, 307, 36129, 11636, 365, 7161, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327995777130127, "compression_ratio": 1.5723684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359642590266232e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 256536, "start": 2572.34, "end": 2575.78, "text": " You have another quantity, plasticity, P, that is steadily falling with depth.", "tokens": [50714, 509, 362, 1071, 11275, 11, 5900, 507, 11, 430, 11, 300, 307, 36129, 7440, 365, 7161, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327995777130127, "compression_ratio": 1.5723684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359642590266232e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 256536, "start": 2575.82, "end": 2576.82, "text": " And when you multiply them?", "tokens": [50888, 400, 562, 291, 12972, 552, 30, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1327995777130127, "compression_ratio": 1.5723684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359642590266232e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 257682, "start": 2576.82, "end": 2583.1800000000003, "text": " If you multiply a rising quantity by a falling quantity, the product will naturally peak somewhere in the middle.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 12972, 257, 11636, 11275, 538, 257, 7440, 11275, 11, 264, 1674, 486, 8195, 10651, 4079, 294, 264, 2808, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12648472914824616, "compression_ratio": 1.642156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2252979663882058e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 257682, "start": 2583.54, "end": 2587.8, "text": " The A times P multiplier mathematically creates that middle layer sweet spot.", "tokens": [50701, 440, 316, 1413, 430, 44106, 44003, 7829, 300, 2808, 4583, 3844, 4008, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12648472914824616, "compression_ratio": 1.642156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2252979663882058e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 257682, "start": 2588.04, "end": 2588.44, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50926, 3153, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12648472914824616, "compression_ratio": 1.642156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2252979663882058e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 257682, "start": 2588.7200000000003, "end": 2592.2400000000002, "text": " Neither quantity peaks in the middle by itself, but their product does.", "tokens": [50960, 23956, 11275, 26897, 294, 264, 2808, 538, 2564, 11, 457, 641, 1674, 775, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12648472914824616, "compression_ratio": 1.642156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2252979663882058e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 257682, "start": 2592.6000000000004, "end": 2595.76, "text": " And that product represents the optimal density of the repair set.", "tokens": [51154, 400, 300, 1674, 8855, 264, 16252, 10305, 295, 264, 10535, 992, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12648472914824616, "compression_ratio": 1.642156862745098, "no_speech_prob": 1.2252979663882058e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 259576, "start": 2595.76, "end": 2598.6200000000003, "text": " It makes so much intuitive sense when you look at it that way.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1669, 370, 709, 21769, 2020, 562, 291, 574, 412, 309, 300, 636, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 259576, "start": 2598.8, "end": 2603.48, "text": " But, as we know, in science, a great theory is just a bedtime story unless you can actually prove it.", "tokens": [50517, 583, 11, 382, 321, 458, 11, 294, 3497, 11, 257, 869, 5261, 307, 445, 257, 45850, 1657, 5969, 291, 393, 767, 7081, 309, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 259576, "start": 2603.5600000000004, "end": 2603.96, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50755, 7587, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 259576, "start": 2604.32, "end": 2605.0400000000004, "text": " You need evidence.", "tokens": [50793, 509, 643, 4467, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 259576, "start": 2605.36, "end": 2611.0200000000004, "text": " How do the researchers propose we actually test this assembly line theory without just pointing to the RL results and saying,", "tokens": [50845, 1012, 360, 264, 10309, 17421, 321, 767, 1500, 341, 12103, 1622, 5261, 1553, 445, 12166, 281, 264, 497, 43, 3542, 293, 1566, 11, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 259576, "start": 2611.1800000000003, "end": 2612.28, "text": " see, it makes sense?", "tokens": [51136, 536, 11, 309, 1669, 2020, 30, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 259576, "start": 2612.46, "end": 2616.2000000000003, "text": " Which brings us to the most critical part of the paper, the falsifiable test.", "tokens": [51200, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 881, 4924, 644, 295, 264, 3035, 11, 264, 16720, 30876, 1500, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 259576, "start": 2616.5200000000004, "end": 2619.6800000000003, "text": " This is perhaps the most elegant part of the entire fliction paper.", "tokens": [51403, 639, 307, 4317, 264, 881, 21117, 644, 295, 264, 2302, 932, 4105, 3035, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 259576, "start": 2620.2000000000003, "end": 2622.6800000000003, "text": " The author doesn't just spin a theoretical story.", "tokens": [51587, 440, 3793, 1177, 380, 445, 6060, 257, 20864, 1657, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1332956997316275, "compression_ratio": 1.6823899371069182, "no_speech_prob": 1.555339407613432e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 262268, "start": 2622.68, "end": 2628.5, "text": " They propose a concrete, falsifiable experiment to test the product hypothesis.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 17421, 257, 9859, 11, 16720, 30876, 5120, 281, 1500, 264, 1674, 17291, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 262268, "start": 2628.8199999999997, "end": 2629.0, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50672, 1033, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 262268, "start": 2629.3199999999997, "end": 2630.2, "text": " What is the experiment?", "tokens": [50697, 708, 307, 264, 5120, 30, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 262268, "start": 2630.46, "end": 2631.08, "text": " And the best part?", "tokens": [50754, 400, 264, 1151, 644, 30, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 262268, "start": 2631.7599999999998, "end": 2638.64, "text": " We can test this hypothesis using only the publicly available pre-trained model before any reinforcement learning even takes place.", "tokens": [50819, 492, 393, 1500, 341, 17291, 1228, 787, 264, 14843, 2435, 659, 12, 17227, 2001, 2316, 949, 604, 29280, 2539, 754, 2516, 1081, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 262268, "start": 2638.72, "end": 2639.14, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [51167, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 262268, "start": 2639.24, "end": 2644.94, "text": " We don't need to run massive server farms for weeks to do reinforcement learning just to see if the theory holds up.", "tokens": [51193, 492, 500, 380, 643, 281, 1190, 5994, 7154, 20366, 337, 3259, 281, 360, 29280, 2539, 445, 281, 536, 498, 264, 5261, 9190, 493, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 262268, "start": 2645.04, "end": 2645.5, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51483, 7587, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13440118376741705, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776584903591905e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 264550, "start": 2645.5, "end": 2652.88, "text": " Because A and P are proposed as structural properties of the network's geometry that exist purely as a result of the initial pre-training,", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 316, 293, 430, 366, 10348, 382, 15067, 7221, 295, 264, 3209, 311, 18426, 300, 2514, 17491, 382, 257, 1874, 295, 264, 5883, 659, 12, 17227, 1760, 11, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 264550, "start": 2653.1, "end": 2656.2, "text": " they should be fully measurable on the base model itself.", "tokens": [50745, 436, 820, 312, 4498, 43615, 322, 264, 3096, 2316, 2564, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 264550, "start": 2656.32, "end": 2660.54, "text": " Oh, because they are properties of the factory floor before the custom order even comes in.", "tokens": [50906, 876, 11, 570, 436, 366, 7221, 295, 264, 9265, 4123, 949, 264, 2375, 1668, 754, 1487, 294, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 264550, "start": 2660.68, "end": 2661.86, "text": " Beautifully put, yes.", "tokens": [51124, 10584, 15386, 829, 11, 2086, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 264550, "start": 2661.98, "end": 2662.24, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51189, 1033, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 264550, "start": 2662.58, "end": 2665.02, "text": " So, how do we operationalize these variables?", "tokens": [51219, 407, 11, 577, 360, 321, 16607, 1125, 613, 9102, 30, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 264550, "start": 2665.68, "end": 2668.4, "text": " How do we measure A and P on a static model?", "tokens": [51374, 1012, 360, 321, 3481, 316, 293, 430, 322, 257, 13437, 2316, 30, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 264550, "start": 2668.88, "end": 2671.86, "text": " Let's start with A, the task abstraction availability.", "tokens": [51534, 961, 311, 722, 365, 316, 11, 264, 5633, 37765, 17945, 13, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11892000560102792, "compression_ratio": 1.6325088339222615, "no_speech_prob": 1.383022494270969e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 267186, "start": 2671.86, "end": 2677.08, "text": " To measure A at layer K, the paper proposes using a technique called a linear probe.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 3481, 316, 412, 4583, 591, 11, 264, 3035, 2365, 4201, 1228, 257, 6532, 1219, 257, 8213, 22715, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384531596921525, "compression_ratio": 1.6692307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551340155547157e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 267186, "start": 2677.2000000000003, "end": 2678.98, "text": " What exactly is a linear probe?", "tokens": [50632, 708, 2293, 307, 257, 8213, 22715, 30, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384531596921525, "compression_ratio": 1.6692307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551340155547157e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 267186, "start": 2679.2400000000002, "end": 2683.7200000000003, "text": " A linear probe is a relatively simple machine learning technique used in interpretability.", "tokens": [50734, 316, 8213, 22715, 307, 257, 7226, 2199, 3479, 2539, 6532, 1143, 294, 7302, 2310, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384531596921525, "compression_ratio": 1.6692307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551340155547157e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 267186, "start": 2684.3, "end": 2690.2400000000002, "text": " You take the untrained base model, feed it data relevant to the task, say a bunch of math problems,", "tokens": [50987, 509, 747, 264, 1701, 31774, 3096, 2316, 11, 3154, 309, 1412, 7340, 281, 264, 5633, 11, 584, 257, 3840, 295, 5221, 2740, 11, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384531596921525, "compression_ratio": 1.6692307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551340155547157e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 267186, "start": 2690.56, "end": 2693.48, "text": " and extract the hidden activation states at layer K.", "tokens": [51300, 293, 8947, 264, 7633, 24433, 4368, 412, 4583, 591, 13, 51446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384531596921525, "compression_ratio": 1.6692307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551340155547157e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 267186, "start": 2693.7200000000003, "end": 2697.0, "text": " You record what the conveyor belt looks like at that exact moment.", "tokens": [51458, 509, 2136, 437, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 1542, 411, 412, 300, 1900, 1623, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384531596921525, "compression_ratio": 1.6692307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551340155547157e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 267186, "start": 2697.34, "end": 2697.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51639, 1779, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384531596921525, "compression_ratio": 1.6692307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551340155547157e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 269758, "start": 2697.58, "end": 2705.56, "text": " Then, you train a very simple, tiny, linear classifier, a separate mini-AI, on just those extracted hidden states.", "tokens": [50365, 1396, 11, 291, 3847, 257, 588, 2199, 11, 5870, 11, 8213, 1508, 9902, 11, 257, 4994, 8382, 12, 48698, 11, 322, 445, 729, 34086, 7633, 4368, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10813109079996745, "compression_ratio": 1.5977859778597785, "no_speech_prob": 1.965947153334535e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 269758, "start": 2706.06, "end": 2710.34, "text": " Its only job is to see if it can decode past relevant variables from that data.", "tokens": [50789, 6953, 787, 1691, 307, 281, 536, 498, 309, 393, 979, 1429, 1791, 7340, 9102, 490, 300, 1412, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10813109079996745, "compression_ratio": 1.5977859778597785, "no_speech_prob": 1.965947153334535e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 269758, "start": 2710.34, "end": 2715.48, "text": " So, if the task is math, you train the mini-AI to look at layer K's conveyor belt", "tokens": [51003, 407, 11, 498, 264, 5633, 307, 5221, 11, 291, 3847, 264, 8382, 12, 48698, 281, 574, 412, 4583, 591, 311, 18053, 2454, 10750, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10813109079996745, "compression_ratio": 1.5977859778597785, "no_speech_prob": 1.965947153334535e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 269758, "start": 2715.48, "end": 2719.98, "text": " and see if it contains the intermediate reasoning steps needed to solve the math problem.", "tokens": [51260, 293, 536, 498, 309, 8306, 264, 19376, 21577, 4439, 2978, 281, 5039, 264, 5221, 1154, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10813109079996745, "compression_ratio": 1.5977859778597785, "no_speech_prob": 1.965947153334535e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 269758, "start": 2720.2799999999997, "end": 2723.42, "text": " You're asking, does this layer know we're doing long division yet?", "tokens": [51500, 509, 434, 3365, 11, 775, 341, 4583, 458, 321, 434, 884, 938, 10044, 1939, 30, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10813109079996745, "compression_ratio": 1.5977859778597785, "no_speech_prob": 1.965947153334535e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 272342, "start": 2723.42, "end": 2729.62, "text": " Correct. If the linear probe achieves high accuracy, it means the abstraction, the concept of long division,", "tokens": [50365, 12753, 13, 759, 264, 8213, 22715, 3538, 977, 1090, 14170, 11, 309, 1355, 264, 37765, 11, 264, 3410, 295, 938, 10044, 11, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 272342, "start": 2729.9, "end": 2733.28, "text": " is readily available and cleanly represented in the data at that layer.", "tokens": [50689, 307, 26336, 2435, 293, 2541, 356, 10379, 294, 264, 1412, 412, 300, 4583, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 272342, "start": 2733.4, "end": 2734.06, "text": " And if it fails?", "tokens": [50864, 400, 498, 309, 18199, 30, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 272342, "start": 2734.32, "end": 2737.62, "text": " If the probe fails, the abstraction isn't there yet. The data is too raw.", "tokens": [50910, 759, 264, 22715, 18199, 11, 264, 37765, 1943, 380, 456, 1939, 13, 440, 1412, 307, 886, 8936, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 272342, "start": 2737.92, "end": 2742.1, "text": " The accuracy of that linear probe gives you a direct numerical value for a cage.", "tokens": [51090, 440, 14170, 295, 300, 8213, 22715, 2709, 291, 257, 2047, 29054, 2158, 337, 257, 17302, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 272342, "start": 2742.26, "end": 2744.48, "text": " Okay, that makes total sense. We can measure abstraction.", "tokens": [51307, 1033, 11, 300, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 492, 393, 3481, 37765, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 272342, "start": 2744.96, "end": 2745.66, "text": " What about P?", "tokens": [51442, 708, 466, 430, 30, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 272342, "start": 2746.16, "end": 2750.6, "text": " How do we measure preservation-compatible plasticity on an untrained model?", "tokens": [51502, 1012, 360, 321, 3481, 27257, 12, 1112, 11584, 964, 5900, 507, 322, 364, 1701, 31774, 2316, 30, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12311011268979027, "compression_ratio": 1.7182130584192439, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983197838159713e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 275060, "start": 2750.6, "end": 2755.08, "text": " To measure P at layer K, the paper suggests a completely different technique,", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 3481, 430, 412, 4583, 591, 11, 264, 3035, 13409, 257, 2584, 819, 6532, 11, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 275060, "start": 2755.74, "end": 2761.24, "text": " injecting a small fixed-norm perturbation directly into the residual stream at layer K.", "tokens": [50622, 10711, 278, 257, 1359, 6806, 12, 13403, 40468, 399, 3838, 666, 264, 27980, 4309, 412, 4583, 591, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 275060, "start": 2761.4, "end": 2763.24, "text": " Let's translate that, a perturbation.", "tokens": [50905, 961, 311, 13799, 300, 11, 257, 40468, 399, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 275060, "start": 2763.42, "end": 2766.98, "text": " You just add a tiny bit of mathematical noise, a small random vector,", "tokens": [51006, 509, 445, 909, 257, 5870, 857, 295, 18894, 5658, 11, 257, 1359, 4974, 8062, 11, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 275060, "start": 2767.44, "end": 2770.3399999999997, "text": " to the activations on the conveyor belt at that specific depth.", "tokens": [51207, 281, 264, 2430, 763, 322, 264, 18053, 2454, 10750, 412, 300, 2685, 7161, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 275060, "start": 2770.88, "end": 2773.38, "text": " You mathematically shake the box as it passes layer K.", "tokens": [51379, 509, 44003, 10283, 264, 2424, 382, 309, 11335, 4583, 591, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 275060, "start": 2773.6, "end": 2774.44, "text": " Okay, shake the box.", "tokens": [51515, 1033, 11, 10283, 264, 2424, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 275060, "start": 2774.6, "end": 2777.64, "text": " Then you let the forward pass continue all the way to the end of the network,", "tokens": [51565, 1396, 291, 718, 264, 2128, 1320, 2354, 439, 264, 636, 281, 264, 917, 295, 264, 3209, 11, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11092582175402137, "compression_ratio": 1.698961937716263, "no_speech_prob": 1.120011743939442e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 277764, "start": 2777.64, "end": 2782.3199999999997, "text": " and you measure how sensitive the final output is to that tiny injection of noise.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 291, 3481, 577, 9477, 264, 2572, 5598, 307, 281, 300, 5870, 22873, 295, 5658, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 277764, "start": 2782.52, "end": 2783.2599999999998, "text": " Ah, I see.", "tokens": [50609, 2438, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 277764, "start": 2783.52, "end": 2786.46, "text": " So if I inject a tiny bit of static into layer 20,", "tokens": [50659, 407, 498, 286, 10711, 257, 5870, 857, 295, 13437, 666, 4583, 945, 11, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 277764, "start": 2786.7599999999998, "end": 2789.46, "text": " and the final output goes completely crazy,", "tokens": [50821, 293, 264, 2572, 5598, 1709, 2584, 3219, 11, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 277764, "start": 2789.98, "end": 2793.6, "text": " the model starts hallucinating or spewing random letters.", "tokens": [50982, 264, 2316, 3719, 35212, 8205, 420, 768, 7904, 4974, 7825, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 277764, "start": 2793.96, "end": 2794.92, "text": " What does that mean?", "tokens": [51181, 708, 775, 300, 914, 30, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 277764, "start": 2795.0, "end": 2797.56, "text": " It means the network is highly sensitive at that layer.", "tokens": [51233, 467, 1355, 264, 3209, 307, 5405, 9477, 412, 300, 4583, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 277764, "start": 2798.04, "end": 2801.7799999999997, "text": " High downstream sensitivity indicates low plasticity in the relevant sense.", "tokens": [51385, 5229, 30621, 19392, 16203, 2295, 5900, 507, 294, 264, 7340, 2020, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 277764, "start": 2801.8199999999997, "end": 2803.0, "text": " Because it can't handle the noise.", "tokens": [51574, 1436, 309, 393, 380, 4813, 264, 5658, 13, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13109039166651734, "compression_ratio": 1.6564885496183206, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984661511092568e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 280300, "start": 2803.0, "end": 2803.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 280300, "start": 2803.88, "end": 2806.0, "text": " It means any update you make during training,", "tokens": [50409, 467, 1355, 604, 5623, 291, 652, 1830, 3097, 11, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 280300, "start": 2806.3, "end": 2808.18, "text": " which is essentially a targeted perturbation,", "tokens": [50530, 597, 307, 4476, 257, 15045, 40468, 399, 11, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 280300, "start": 2808.46, "end": 2811.68, "text": " is likely to violently disrupt the established output conventions.", "tokens": [50638, 307, 3700, 281, 46728, 14124, 264, 7545, 5598, 33520, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 280300, "start": 2812.16, "end": 2813.98, "text": " The system cannot absorb this shock.", "tokens": [50823, 440, 1185, 2644, 15631, 341, 5588, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 280300, "start": 2814.36, "end": 2816.74, "text": " And conversely, if I inject the noise into layer 5,", "tokens": [50933, 400, 2615, 736, 11, 498, 286, 10711, 264, 5658, 666, 4583, 1025, 11, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 280300, "start": 2817.12, "end": 2818.92, "text": " and the final output barely changes,", "tokens": [51071, 293, 264, 2572, 5598, 10268, 2962, 11, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 280300, "start": 2819.24, "end": 2821.16, "text": " that layer has high plasticity.", "tokens": [51177, 300, 4583, 575, 1090, 5900, 507, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 280300, "start": 2821.64, "end": 2824.36, "text": " The downstream layers are able to smooth over the noise", "tokens": [51297, 440, 30621, 7914, 366, 1075, 281, 5508, 670, 264, 5658, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 280300, "start": 2824.36, "end": 2826.2, "text": " and still produce the correct format.", "tokens": [51433, 293, 920, 5258, 264, 3006, 7877, 13, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 280300, "start": 2826.4, "end": 2826.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51535, 7587, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 280300, "start": 2827.06, "end": 2829.98, "text": " The sensitivity gives you an inverse measure of P.", "tokens": [51568, 440, 19392, 2709, 291, 364, 17340, 3481, 295, 430, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951851440688311, "compression_ratio": 1.6114864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.377843802594092e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 282998, "start": 2829.98, "end": 2833.34, "text": " So now you have a way to measure A with a probe", "tokens": [50365, 407, 586, 291, 362, 257, 636, 281, 3481, 316, 365, 257, 22715, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 282998, "start": 2833.34, "end": 2835.68, "text": " and a way to measure P with noise injection", "tokens": [50533, 293, 257, 636, 281, 3481, 430, 365, 5658, 22873, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 282998, "start": 2835.68, "end": 2838.18, "text": " entirely independently of RL training.", "tokens": [50650, 7696, 21761, 295, 497, 43, 3097, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 282998, "start": 2838.4, "end": 2839.66, "text": " We measure A, we measure P,", "tokens": [50786, 492, 3481, 316, 11, 321, 3481, 430, 11, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 282998, "start": 2839.78, "end": 2843.1, "text": " and we multiply the two numbers together for every single layer.", "tokens": [50855, 293, 321, 12972, 264, 732, 3547, 1214, 337, 633, 2167, 4583, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 282998, "start": 2843.3, "end": 2845.5, "text": " That gives us a predicted graph of which layers", "tokens": [51031, 663, 2709, 505, 257, 19147, 4295, 295, 597, 7914, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 282998, "start": 2845.5, "end": 2847.48, "text": " should theoretically be the best to train.", "tokens": [51141, 820, 29400, 312, 264, 1151, 281, 3847, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 282998, "start": 2847.64, "end": 2847.88, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51248, 1079, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 282998, "start": 2848.36, "end": 2850.92, "text": " The predicted ordering derived purely from the base model", "tokens": [51284, 440, 19147, 21739, 18949, 17491, 490, 264, 3096, 2316, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 282998, "start": 2850.92, "end": 2853.34, "text": " would then be compared directly against the actual", "tokens": [51412, 576, 550, 312, 5347, 3838, 1970, 264, 3539, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 282998, "start": 2853.34, "end": 2855.44, "text": " empirical layer contribution scores,", "tokens": [51533, 31886, 4583, 13150, 13444, 11, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 282998, "start": 2855.7400000000002, "end": 2857.82, "text": " the CK values, that Zhang et al.", "tokens": [51653, 264, 383, 42, 4190, 11, 300, 17729, 1030, 419, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390821838378906, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669089731632722e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 285782, "start": 2857.82, "end": 2861.02, "text": " already reported from their expensive reinforcement learning runs.", "tokens": [50365, 1217, 7055, 490, 641, 5124, 29280, 2539, 6676, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 285782, "start": 2861.1400000000003, "end": 2865.1400000000003, "text": " And if the graph of A times P closely matches the graph of CK.", "tokens": [50531, 400, 498, 264, 4295, 295, 316, 1413, 430, 8185, 10676, 264, 4295, 295, 383, 42, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 285782, "start": 2865.38, "end": 2868.7200000000003, "text": " Then it is incredibly strong quantitative evidence", "tokens": [50743, 1396, 309, 307, 6252, 2068, 27778, 4467, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 285782, "start": 2868.7200000000003, "end": 2870.88, "text": " that this structural geometry,", "tokens": [50910, 300, 341, 15067, 18426, 11, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 285782, "start": 2871.28, "end": 2874.06, "text": " the intersection of abstraction and plasticity,", "tokens": [51038, 264, 15236, 295, 37765, 293, 5900, 507, 11, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 285782, "start": 2874.1800000000003, "end": 2876.0, "text": " is what governs effective adaptation.", "tokens": [51183, 307, 437, 1980, 82, 4942, 21549, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 285782, "start": 2876.5800000000004, "end": 2878.52, "text": " It would prove the product hypothesis.", "tokens": [51303, 467, 576, 7081, 264, 1674, 17291, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 285782, "start": 2879.2400000000002, "end": 2879.8, "text": " But hold on.", "tokens": [51436, 583, 1797, 322, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 285782, "start": 2879.88, "end": 2881.38, "text": " What if they run this test tomorrow?", "tokens": [51468, 708, 498, 436, 1190, 341, 1500, 4153, 30, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 285782, "start": 2881.5, "end": 2883.52, "text": " They do the linear probes and the noise injection,", "tokens": [51549, 814, 360, 264, 8213, 1239, 279, 293, 264, 5658, 22873, 11, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 285782, "start": 2883.7000000000003, "end": 2885.1400000000003, "text": " and the data is just a mess.", "tokens": [51659, 293, 264, 1412, 307, 445, 257, 2082, 13, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18824635890492222, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691654348103714e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 288514, "start": 2885.14, "end": 2889.2599999999998, "text": " What if the A times P graph doesn't match the performance graph at all?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 498, 264, 316, 1413, 430, 4295, 1177, 380, 2995, 264, 3389, 4295, 412, 439, 30, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 288514, "start": 2889.3599999999997, "end": 2890.8799999999997, "text": " Is this whole paper useless?", "tokens": [50576, 1119, 341, 1379, 3035, 14115, 30, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 288514, "start": 2891.12, "end": 2893.3399999999997, "text": " That is the beauty of the asymmetry of good science.", "tokens": [50664, 663, 307, 264, 6643, 295, 264, 37277, 9889, 295, 665, 3497, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 288514, "start": 2893.5, "end": 2895.9, "text": " The author is very clear about this in the text.", "tokens": [50783, 440, 3793, 307, 588, 1850, 466, 341, 294, 264, 2487, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 288514, "start": 2896.02, "end": 2896.24, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50909, 1033, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 288514, "start": 2896.56, "end": 2898.2799999999997, "text": " If the empirical test fails,", "tokens": [50936, 759, 264, 31886, 1500, 18199, 11, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 288514, "start": 2898.7, "end": 2901.2999999999997, "text": " it only falsifies this specific mechanism,", "tokens": [51043, 309, 787, 16720, 11221, 341, 2685, 7513, 11, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 288514, "start": 2902.02, "end": 2903.7799999999997, "text": " the A times P assembly line theory.", "tokens": [51209, 264, 316, 1413, 430, 12103, 1622, 5261, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 288514, "start": 2904.16, "end": 2906.3399999999997, "text": " It means the reason the middle layers are better", "tokens": [51316, 467, 1355, 264, 1778, 264, 2808, 7914, 366, 1101, 51425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 288514, "start": 2906.3399999999997, "end": 2907.54, "text": " is something else entirely.", "tokens": [51425, 307, 746, 1646, 7696, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 288514, "start": 2908.24, "end": 2910.3399999999997, "text": " Maybe it's related to the activation norms", "tokens": [51520, 2704, 309, 311, 4077, 281, 264, 24433, 24357, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 288514, "start": 2910.3399999999997, "end": 2912.54, "text": " or the entropy of the attention patterns.", "tokens": [51625, 420, 264, 30867, 295, 264, 3202, 8294, 13, 51735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 288514, "start": 2912.68, "end": 2914.08, "text": " But the core finding remains.", "tokens": [51742, 583, 264, 4965, 5006, 7023, 13, 51812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599437885714653, "compression_ratio": 1.6877076411960132, "no_speech_prob": 1.8724464253411233e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 291408, "start": 2914.08, "end": 2914.64, "text": " Absolutely.", "tokens": [50365, 7021, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 291408, "start": 2915.02, "end": 2915.9, "text": " The underlying math,", "tokens": [50412, 440, 14217, 5221, 11, 50456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 291408, "start": 2916.18, "end": 2917.38, "text": " the repair set formalism,", "tokens": [50470, 264, 10535, 992, 9860, 1434, 11, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 291408, "start": 2917.58, "end": 2919.08, "text": " and the empirical reality", "tokens": [50540, 293, 264, 31886, 4103, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 291408, "start": 2919.08, "end": 2921.36, "text": " that middle layers dominate reinforcement learning", "tokens": [50615, 300, 2808, 7914, 28246, 29280, 2539, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 291408, "start": 2921.36, "end": 2923.06, "text": " remain completely intact.", "tokens": [50729, 6222, 2584, 23493, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 291408, "start": 2923.3199999999997, "end": 2924.36, "text": " The facts don't change.", "tokens": [50827, 440, 9130, 500, 380, 1319, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 291408, "start": 2924.7799999999997, "end": 2925.2, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50900, 7587, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 291408, "start": 2925.86, "end": 2927.84, "text": " The fact that the effective space of improvement", "tokens": [50954, 440, 1186, 300, 264, 4942, 1901, 295, 10444, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 291408, "start": 2927.84, "end": 2929.72, "text": " is narrow and depth concentrated", "tokens": [51053, 307, 9432, 293, 7161, 21321, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 291408, "start": 2929.72, "end": 2931.74, "text": " is a verifiable fact.", "tokens": [51147, 307, 257, 1306, 30876, 1186, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 291408, "start": 2931.86, "end": 2933.7, "text": " We just wouldn't know the exact why yet.", "tokens": [51254, 492, 445, 2759, 380, 458, 264, 1900, 983, 1939, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 291408, "start": 2934.2999999999997, "end": 2935.56, "text": " The repair set formalism", "tokens": [51376, 440, 10535, 992, 9860, 1434, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 291408, "start": 2935.56, "end": 2936.7, "text": " was deliberately constructed", "tokens": [51439, 390, 23506, 17083, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 291408, "start": 2936.7, "end": 2938.96, "text": " to survive independently of the latent mechanism.", "tokens": [51496, 281, 7867, 21761, 295, 264, 48994, 7513, 13, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 291408, "start": 2939.4, "end": 2941.24, "text": " It is a win-win for science.", "tokens": [51631, 467, 307, 257, 1942, 12, 9136, 337, 3497, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17959410245301294, "compression_ratio": 1.673758865248227, "no_speech_prob": 1.890613533783725e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 294124, "start": 2941.24, "end": 2943.3399999999997, "text": " We either discover the mechanism", "tokens": [50365, 492, 2139, 4411, 264, 7513, 50470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 294124, "start": 2943.3399999999997, "end": 2945.4399999999996, "text": " or we cleanly rule one out", "tokens": [50470, 420, 321, 2541, 356, 4978, 472, 484, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 294124, "start": 2945.4399999999996, "end": 2947.3399999999997, "text": " without losing the descriptive framework.", "tokens": [50575, 1553, 7027, 264, 42585, 8388, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 294124, "start": 2947.58, "end": 2947.8799999999997, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50682, 48746, 736, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 294124, "start": 2947.9799999999996, "end": 2949.72, "text": " So what does this all mean for us?", "tokens": [50702, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 505, 30, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 294124, "start": 2950.06, "end": 2951.8399999999997, "text": " We have spent the last while", "tokens": [50806, 492, 362, 4418, 264, 1036, 1339, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 294124, "start": 2951.8399999999997, "end": 2953.18, "text": " deep inside the weeds", "tokens": [50895, 2452, 1854, 264, 26370, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 294124, "start": 2953.18, "end": 2954.4399999999996, "text": " of transformer architecture,", "tokens": [50962, 295, 31782, 9482, 11, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 294124, "start": 2954.72, "end": 2955.56, "text": " residual streams,", "tokens": [51039, 27980, 15842, 11, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 294124, "start": 2955.74, "end": 2957.2799999999997, "text": " and reinforcement learning equations.", "tokens": [51090, 293, 29280, 2539, 11787, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 294124, "start": 2957.7, "end": 2959.3599999999997, "text": " But we promised at the start", "tokens": [51188, 583, 321, 10768, 412, 264, 722, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 294124, "start": 2959.3599999999997, "end": 2961.3199999999997, "text": " that this teaches us something profound", "tokens": [51271, 300, 341, 16876, 505, 746, 14382, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 294124, "start": 2961.3199999999997, "end": 2963.5, "text": " about complex systems everywhere.", "tokens": [51369, 466, 3997, 3652, 5315, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 294124, "start": 2963.7999999999997, "end": 2965.3199999999997, "text": " And this is where the paper's philosophy", "tokens": [51493, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 3035, 311, 10675, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 294124, "start": 2965.3199999999997, "end": 2966.72, "text": " truly shines, I think.", "tokens": [51569, 4908, 28056, 11, 286, 519, 13, 51639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21278383006220278, "compression_ratio": 1.5734265734265733, "no_speech_prob": 2.1933396938955685e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 296672, "start": 2966.72, "end": 2968.48, "text": " The core insight here", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4965, 11269, 510, 50453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 296672, "start": 2968.48, "end": 2969.8399999999997, "text": " is that when you are optimizing", "tokens": [50453, 307, 300, 562, 291, 366, 40425, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 296672, "start": 2969.8399999999997, "end": 2971.7, "text": " or improving a system post-training,", "tokens": [50521, 420, 11470, 257, 1185, 2183, 12, 17227, 1760, 11, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 296672, "start": 2972.14, "end": 2974.14, "text": " you do not begin from a blank slate.", "tokens": [50636, 291, 360, 406, 1841, 490, 257, 8247, 39118, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 296672, "start": 2974.5, "end": 2974.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50754, 1779, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 296672, "start": 2974.8999999999996, "end": 2976.72, "text": " You begin from a pre-trained point", "tokens": [50774, 509, 1841, 490, 257, 659, 12, 17227, 2001, 935, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 296672, "start": 2976.72, "end": 2977.8399999999997, "text": " that already embodies", "tokens": [50865, 300, 1217, 4605, 6087, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 296672, "start": 2977.8399999999997, "end": 2979.98, "text": " a coherent, highly functional organization.", "tokens": [50921, 257, 36239, 11, 5405, 11745, 4475, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 296672, "start": 2980.7, "end": 2982.2, "text": " The system already solves", "tokens": [51064, 440, 1185, 1217, 39890, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 296672, "start": 2982.2, "end": 2984.24, "text": " a great many problems tolerably well.", "tokens": [51139, 257, 869, 867, 2740, 11125, 1188, 731, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 296672, "start": 2984.5, "end": 2985.7599999999998, "text": " Optimization from that point", "tokens": [51254, 35013, 2144, 490, 300, 935, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 296672, "start": 2985.7599999999998, "end": 2986.9199999999996, "text": " is not free exploration.", "tokens": [51317, 307, 406, 1737, 16197, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 296672, "start": 2987.16, "end": 2988.7799999999997, "text": " You aren't building a house from scratch.", "tokens": [51387, 509, 3212, 380, 2390, 257, 1782, 490, 8459, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 296672, "start": 2988.8599999999997, "end": 2990.68, "text": " You are renovating an occupied building.", "tokens": [51472, 509, 366, 18845, 990, 364, 19629, 2390, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17956578634618744, "compression_ratio": 1.6961538461538461, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922317717770307e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 296672, "start": 2990.9199999999996, "end": 2991.22, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51575, 1079, 13, 51